window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES=window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES||{};window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES[10]={"subjects":{"wiskunde":{"id":"wiskunde","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Wiskunde","en":"Mathematics"},"short":{"af":"Wisk","en":"Maths"},"icon":"📐","color":"#2f6df6","intro":{"af":"Graad 10-Wiskunde lê die fondament vir die NSS: algebra, funksies, trigonometrie, meetkunde, finansies, statistiek en waarskynlikheid. Die Novembereksamen bestaan uit twee vraestelle van 100 punte elk (2 uur elk) en dek die hele jaar se werk. Jy mag 'n goedgekeurde wetenskaplike sakrekenaar gebruik, behalwe waar 'n vraag anders sê.","en":"Grade 10 Mathematics lays the foundation for the NSC: algebra, functions, trigonometry, geometry, finance, statistics and probability. The November exam consists of two papers of 100 marks each (2 hours each) and covers the whole year's work. You may use an approved scientific calculator, except where a question says otherwise."},"examTips":[{"af":"Wys ALTYD jou bewerkings. Die memo gee metodepunte vir elke korrekte stap – 'n antwoord sonder bewerkings kan nul kry, selfs al is dit reg.","en":"ALWAYS show your working. The memo gives method marks for every correct step – an answer without working can score zero, even if it is right."},{"af":"Rond af tot twee desimale plekke, tensy die vraag anders sê, en rond eers aan die einde af – nie in die tussenstappe nie.","en":"Round to two decimal places unless the question says otherwise, and only round at the end – not in the middle steps."},{"af":"Leer die spesiale hoeke (0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°) en die eksponentwette uit jou kop – daar is gewoonlik 'n vraag sonder sakrekenaar.","en":"Know the special angles (0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°) and the exponent laws by heart – there is usually a question without a calculator."},{"af":"Skryf by meetkunde ALTYD 'n rede langs elke bewering, bv. (teenoorst. sye van ||m) of (midpt-stelling). Sonder 'n rede verloor jy die punt.","en":"In geometry ALWAYS write a reason next to every statement, e.g. (opp. sides of ||m) or (midpt theorem). Without a reason you lose the mark."},{"af":"Kyk na die punte: 'n 1-punt-vraag vra een stap, 'n 5-punt-vraag vra 'n volledige metode. Bestee ongeveer 1 minuut per punt.","en":"Look at the marks: a 1-mark question needs one step, a 5-mark question needs a full method. Spend about 1 minute per mark."},{"af":"Kontroleer jou antwoorde waar jy kan: vervang jou x terug in die vergelyking, of kyk of jou grafiek die regte afsnitte het.","en":"Check your answers where you can: substitute your x back into the equation, or check that your graph has the right intercepts."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: Alles Wiskunde Graad 10 (Afrikaans)","en":"Siyavula: Everything Maths Grade 10 (Afrikaans)"},"url":"https://wcedeportal.co.za/eresource/76196","note":{"af":"Gratis, volledige CAPS-handboek met uitgewerkte voorbeelde en oefeninge vir elke hoofstuk.","en":"Free, complete CAPS textbook with worked examples and exercises for every chapter."}},{"title":{"af":"Noordwes Onderwysdepartement: vraestelle en memo's","en":"North West Department of Education: papers and memos"},"url":"https://education.nwpg.gov.za/?page_id=4644","note":{"af":"Provinsiale Graad 10-Novembervraestelle met memorandums – goed vir eksamenoefening.","en":"Provincial Grade 10 November papers with memos – good for exam practice."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Wiskunde-eksamen: twee vraestelle\n\n**Vraestel 1 en Vraestel 2: 100 punte elk, 2 uur elk** (*skatting volgens CAPS en Hoërskool Brits se 2024-afbakening – bevestig met die 2026-afbakening*). 'n Goedgekeurde wetenskaplike sakrekenaar mag gebruik word.\n\n| Vraestel 1 | ±Punte | Vraestel 2 | ±Punte |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Algebra, eksponente, vergelykings en ongelykhede | 30 | Trigonometrie (ook grafieke en 2D) | 40 |\n| Funksies en grafieke | 30 | Euklidiese meetkunde en meting | 30 |\n| Getalpatrone | 15 | Analitiese meetkunde | 15 |\n| Waarskynlikheid | 15 | Statistiek | 15 |\n| Finansies en groei | 10 | | |\n\n### Wat word gevra?\n\n- Faktoriseer, vereenvoudig en los vergelykings op – altyd met volledige bewerkings.\n- Skets grafieke met afsnitte, asimptote en draaipunte; bepaal vergelykings uit gegewe inligting.\n- Meetkunde: bewerings **met redes** en kort bewyse.\n- Woordprobleme in konteks: rente, huurkoop, hoogtehoeke, volumes.\n\n### Wenke vir hierdie vraestelle\n\n1. Begin met die vrae wat jy ken – maar nommer jou antwoorde presies soos die vraestel.\n2. Teken 'n rowwe skets by elke trigonometrie- en analitiese-meetkundevraag.\n3. Skryf formules eers neer, dan die vervanging, dan die antwoord.\n4. Los geen vraag oop nie: 'n korrekte eerste stap kry dikwels al 'n punt.","en":"## Mathematics exam: two papers\n\n**Paper 1 and Paper 2: 100 marks each, 2 hours each** (*estimate based on CAPS and Hoërskool Brits's 2024 scope – confirm with the 2026 scope*). An approved scientific calculator may be used.\n\n| Paper 1 | ±Marks | Paper 2 | ±Marks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Algebra, exponents, equations and inequalities | 30 | Trigonometry (incl. graphs and 2D) | 40 |\n| Functions and graphs | 30 | Euclidean geometry and measurement | 30 |\n| Number patterns | 15 | Analytical geometry | 15 |\n| Probability | 15 | Statistics | 15 |\n| Finance and growth | 10 | | |\n\n### What is asked?\n\n- Factorise, simplify and solve equations – always with full working.\n- Sketch graphs with intercepts, asymptotes and turning points; determine equations from given information.\n- Geometry: statements **with reasons** and short proofs.\n- Word problems in context: interest, hire purchase, angles of elevation, volumes.\n\n### Tips for these papers\n\n1. Start with the questions you know – but number your answers exactly as in the paper.\n2. Draw a rough sketch for every trigonometry and analytical geometry question.\n3. Write the formula first, then the substitution, then the answer.\n4. Leave no question blank: a correct first step often already earns a mark."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Algebra, eksponente, patrone en trigonometrie","en":"Algebra, exponents, patterns and trigonometry"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t1-getalle-uitdrukkings","title":{"af":"Getallestelsel en algebraïese uitdrukkings","en":"Number system and algebraic expressions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal reële getalle kan klassifiseer, repeterende desimale getalle as breuke kan skryf, wortelvorme kan skat en afrond, en algebraïese uitdrukkings kan vermenigvuldig en vereenvoudig.","en":"You will be able to classify real numbers, write recurring decimals as fractions, estimate and round off surds, and multiply and simplify algebraic expressions."},"summary":{"af":"## Die reële getallestelsel\n\n| Simbool | Naam | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| N | Natuurlike getalle | {1; 2; 3; …} |\n| N_{0} | Telgetalle | {0; 1; 2; 3; …} |\n| Z | Heelgetalle | {…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} |\n| Q | Rasionale getalle | [[3/4]]; −5; 0,25; 0,333… |\n| Q′ | Irrasionale getalle | π; √2; ∛5; 1,010010001… |\n| R | Reële getalle | al die rasionale én irrasionale getalle |\n\nElke versameling lê binne die volgende een: N ⊂ N_{0} ⊂ Z ⊂ Q ⊂ R. Q en Q′ saam vorm R.\n\n### Rasionaal of irrasionaal?\n\n'n **Rasionale getal** kan geskryf word as [[a/b]], waar a en b heelgetalle is en b ≠ 0. Dit sluit in:\n\n- alle heelgetalle, bv. −7 = [[−7/1]]\n- **eindigende** desimale getalle, bv. 0,125 = [[1/8]]\n- **repeterende** desimale getalle, bv. 0,272727… = [[3/11]]\n\n'n **Irrasionale getal** kan NIE as [[a/b]] geskryf word nie. Die desimale vorm is **nie-eindigend én nie-repeterend**, bv. π = 3,14159… en √2 = 1,41421…\n\nDie vierkantswortel van 'n negatiewe getal, bv. √(−4), is **nie-reëel**. Let wel: ∛(−8) = −2 is wél reëel.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** [[22/7]] is rasionaal – dis net 'n benadering van π. π self is irrasionaal. √9 = 3 en √0,25 = 0,5 is ook rasionaal, want die wortel is presies.\n\n## Repeterende desimale getalle na gewone breuke\n\nHerhalende syfers word met 'n kolletjie of strepie bo-oor aangedui. Metode vir 0,363636… (die 36 herhaal):\n\n1. Stel x gelyk aan die getal: x = 0,363636…\n2. Vermenigvuldig met 10, 100, 1 000 … – een nul vir elke syfer in die herhalende blok: 100x = 36,363636…\n3. Trek af sodat die herhalende deel wegval: 100x − x = 36, dus 99x = 36.\n4. Los op en vereenvoudig: x = [[36/99]] = [[4/11]].\n\nAs net 'n deel herhaal, bv. 0,1666…, maak eers twee vergelykings waarin die herhaling direk ná die komma begin: 10x = 1,666… en 100x = 16,666… Trek af: 90x = 15, dus x = [[15/90]] = [[1/6]].\n\n## Wortelvorme skat\n\n'n **Wortelvorm** soos √30 of ∛20 is irrasionaal as die getal onder die wortelteken nie 'n volkome vierkant (of volkome derdemag) is nie. So skat jy tussen watter twee heelgetalle dit lê:\n\n1. Soek die volkome vierkante net onder en net bo die getal: 25 < 30 < 36.\n2. Neem die wortels: 5 < √30 < 6.\n3. 30 is nader aan 25 as aan 36, dus is √30 nader aan 5 (√30 ≈ 5,48).\n\nVir 'n derdemagswortel gebruik jy derdemagte: 8 < 20 < 27, dus 2 < ∛20 < 3. Ken die volkome vierkante tot 15^{2} = 225 en die derdemagte tot 10^{3} = 1 000.\n\n## Afronding\n\nKyk na die syfer **net ná** die laaste plek wat jy hou: 5 of meer → rond op; 4 of minder → los die syfer soos dit is.\n\n- 3,14159 tot twee desimale plekke: 3,14\n- 2,4651 tot twee desimale plekke: 2,47\n- 7,996 tot twee desimale plekke: 8,00 (skryf die nulle!)\n\n> **Wenk:** Rond slegs aan die **einde** van 'n berekening af, en net een keer – nie in stappe nie. Tensy die vraag anders sê, rond af tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n## Produkte van algebraïese uitdrukkings\n\n**Gelyksoortige terme** het presies dieselfde veranderlikes en eksponente, bv. 3x^{2} en −5x^{2}. Net hulle kan bymekaargetel of afgetrek word.\n\n**Binomium × trinomium:** vermenigvuldig elke term in die eerste hakie met elke term in die tweede hakie (2 × 3 = 6 produkte) en versamel dan die gelyksoortige terme:\n\n(x + 2)(x^{2} − 3x + 4) = x^{3} − 3x^{2} + 4x + 2x^{2} − 6x + 8 = x^{3} − x^{2} − 2x + 8\n\n### Spesiale produkte – ken hulle uit jou kop\n\n- (a + b)^{2} = a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a + b)(a − b) = a^{2} − b^{2} (verskil van twee vierkante)\n- (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} + b^{3} en (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} − b^{3}\n\n> **Algemene fout:** (x + 3)^{2} ≠ x^{2} + 9. Skryf dit uit as (x + 3)(x + 3) = x^{2} + 6x + 9. Die middelterm 2ab word maklik vergeet.\n\n## Vereenvoudig – stap vir stap\n\n1. Maak die hakies oop (gebruik die spesiale produkte waar jy kan).\n2. 'n Minusteken voor 'n hakie verander die teken van **elke** term binne die hakie: −(x^{2} − 9) = −x^{2} + 9.\n3. Versamel gelyksoortige terme en skryf die antwoord in dalende magte van x.","en":"## The real number system\n\n| Symbol | Name | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| N | Natural numbers | {1; 2; 3; …} |\n| N_{0} | Whole numbers | {0; 1; 2; 3; …} |\n| Z | Integers | {…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} |\n| Q | Rational numbers | [[3/4]]; −5; 0.25; 0.333… |\n| Q′ | Irrational numbers | π; √2; ∛5; 1.010010001… |\n| R | Real numbers | all the rational and irrational numbers |\n\nEach set lies inside the next one: N ⊂ N_{0} ⊂ Z ⊂ Q ⊂ R. Q and Q′ together make up R.\n\n### Rational or irrational?\n\nA **rational number** can be written as [[a/b]], where a and b are integers and b ≠ 0. This includes:\n\n- all integers, e.g. −7 = [[−7/1]]\n- **terminating** decimals, e.g. 0.125 = [[1/8]]\n- **recurring** decimals, e.g. 0.272727… = [[3/11]]\n\nAn **irrational number** can NOT be written as [[a/b]]. Its decimal form is **non-terminating and non-recurring**, e.g. π = 3.14159… and √2 = 1.41421…\n\nThe square root of a negative number, e.g. √(−4), is **non-real**. Note: ∛(−8) = −2 IS real.\n\n> **Common mistake:** [[22/7]] is rational – it is only an approximation of π. π itself is irrational. √9 = 3 and √0.25 = 0.5 are also rational, because the root is exact.\n\n## Recurring decimals to common fractions\n\nRecurring digits are shown with a dot or a bar above them. Method for 0.363636… (the 36 repeats):\n\n1. Let x equal the number: x = 0.363636…\n2. Multiply by 10, 100, 1 000 … – one zero for every digit in the repeating block: 100x = 36.363636…\n3. Subtract so that the repeating part falls away: 100x − x = 36, so 99x = 36.\n4. Solve and simplify: x = [[36/99]] = [[4/11]].\n\nIf only part of the decimal repeats, e.g. 0.1666…, first make two equations in which the repetition starts directly after the decimal point: 10x = 1.666… and 100x = 16.666… Subtract: 90x = 15, so x = [[15/90]] = [[1/6]].\n\n## Estimating surds\n\nA **surd** such as √30 or ∛20 is irrational if the number under the root sign is not a perfect square (or perfect cube). To estimate between which two integers it lies:\n\n1. Find the perfect squares just below and just above the number: 25 < 30 < 36.\n2. Take the roots: 5 < √30 < 6.\n3. 30 is closer to 25 than to 36, so √30 is closer to 5 (√30 ≈ 5.48).\n\nFor a cube root, use cubes: 8 < 20 < 27, so 2 < ∛20 < 3. Know the perfect squares up to 15^{2} = 225 and the cubes up to 10^{3} = 1 000.\n\n## Rounding off\n\nLook at the digit **just after** the last place you are keeping: 5 or more → round up; 4 or less → leave the digit as it is.\n\n- 3.14159 to two decimal places: 3.14\n- 2.4651 to two decimal places: 2.47\n- 7.996 to two decimal places: 8.00 (write the zeros!)\n\n> **Tip:** Round off only at the **end** of a calculation, and only once – not in steps. Unless the question says otherwise, round off to two decimal places.\n\n## Products of algebraic expressions\n\n**Like terms** have exactly the same variables and exponents, e.g. 3x^{2} and −5x^{2}. Only like terms can be added or subtracted.\n\n**Binomial × trinomial:** multiply every term in the first bracket by every term in the second bracket (2 × 3 = 6 products), then collect like terms:\n\n(x + 2)(x^{2} − 3x + 4) = x^{3} − 3x^{2} + 4x + 2x^{2} − 6x + 8 = x^{3} − x^{2} − 2x + 8\n\n### Special products – know them by heart\n\n- (a + b)^{2} = a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a + b)(a − b) = a^{2} − b^{2} (difference of two squares)\n- (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} + b^{3} and (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} − b^{3}\n\n> **Common mistake:** (x + 3)^{2} ≠ x^{2} + 9. Write it out as (x + 3)(x + 3) = x^{2} + 6x + 9. The middle term 2ab is easily forgotten.\n\n## Simplifying – step by step\n\n1. Remove the brackets (use the special products where you can).\n2. A minus sign in front of a bracket changes the sign of **every** term inside the bracket: −(x^{2} − 9) = −x^{2} + 9.\n3. Collect like terms and write the answer in descending powers of x."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Rasionale getal","en":"Rational number"},"def":{"af":"'n Getal wat as a/b geskryf kan word, met a en b heelgetalle en b ≠ 0. Heelgetalle, eindigende en repeterende desimale getalle is almal rasionaal.","en":"A number that can be written as a/b, with a and b integers and b ≠ 0. Integers, terminating and recurring decimals are all rational."}},{"term":{"af":"Irrasionale getal","en":"Irrational number"},"def":{"af":"'n Getal wat nie as a/b geskryf kan word nie; die desimale vorm is nie-eindigend en nie-repeterend, bv. π en √2.","en":"A number that cannot be written as a/b; its decimal form is non-terminating and non-recurring, e.g. π and √2."}},{"term":{"af":"Reële getalle (R)","en":"Real numbers (R)"},"def":{"af":"Al die rasionale en irrasionale getalle saam. Die vierkantswortel van 'n negatiewe getal is nie-reëel.","en":"All the rational and irrational numbers together. The square root of a negative number is non-real."}},{"term":{"af":"Repeterende desimale getal","en":"Recurring decimal"},"def":{"af":"'n Desimale getal waarin een of meer syfers eindeloos herhaal, bv. 0,272727…; dit is altyd rasionaal.","en":"A decimal in which one or more digits repeat endlessly, e.g. 0.272727…; it is always rational."}},{"term":{"af":"Wortelvorm","en":"Surd"},"def":{"af":"'n Wortel wat nie presies uitgewerk kan word nie, bv. √5 of ∛10. Dit is irrasionaal.","en":"A root that cannot be worked out exactly, e.g. √5 or ∛10. It is irrational."}},{"term":{"af":"Afronding","en":"Rounding off"},"def":{"af":"Om 'n getal tot 'n sekere aantal desimale plekke te benader: as die volgende syfer 5 of meer is, rond op; 4 of minder, los dit.","en":"Approximating a number to a certain number of decimal places: if the next digit is 5 or more, round up; 4 or less, leave it."}},{"term":{"af":"Binomium en trinomium","en":"Binomial and trinomial"},"def":{"af":"'n Uitdrukking met twee terme (tweeterm, bv. x + 3) en een met drie terme (drieterm, bv. x² − 2x + 5).","en":"An expression with two terms (e.g. x + 3) and one with three terms (e.g. x² − 2x + 5)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gelyksoortige terme","en":"Like terms"},"def":{"af":"Terme met presies dieselfde veranderlikes en eksponente, bv. 4x² en −7x². Net hulle kan bymekaargetel of afgetrek word.","en":"Terms with exactly the same variables and exponents, e.g. 4x² and −7x². Only they can be added or subtracted."}},{"term":{"af":"Spesiale produk","en":"Special product"},"def":{"af":"'n Produk met 'n vaste patroon, bv. (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b² en (a + b)(a − b) = a² − b².","en":"A product with a fixed pattern, e.g. (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b² and (a + b)(a − b) = a² − b²."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Repeterende desimale getal na 'n breuk","en":"Recurring decimal to a fraction"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 0,1555… (net die 5 herhaal) as 'n gewone breuk in sy eenvoudigste vorm.","en":"Write 0.1555… (only the 5 repeats) as a common fraction in its simplest form."},"steps":[{"af":"Stel x = 0,1555… Die herhalende syfer (5) begin eers by die tweede desimale plek.","en":"Let x = 0.1555… The repeating digit (5) only starts at the second decimal place."},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 10 sodat die herhaling direk ná die komma begin: 10x = 1,555…","en":"Multiply by 10 so that the repetition starts directly after the decimal point: 10x = 1.555…"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 100: 100x = 15,555…","en":"Multiply by 100: 100x = 15.555…"},{"af":"Trek af: 100x − 10x = 15,555… − 1,555…, dus 90x = 14","en":"Subtract: 100x − 10x = 15.555… − 1.555…, so 90x = 14"},{"af":"x = [[14/90]] = [[7/45]] (deel teller en noemer deur 2)","en":"x = [[14/90]] = [[7/45]] (divide numerator and denominator by 2)"}],"answer":{"af":"0,1555… = 7/45","en":"0.1555… = 7/45"}},{"title":{"af":"Skat en rond 'n wortelvorm af","en":"Estimate and round off a surd"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Tussen watter twee opeenvolgende heelgetalle lê √52? (b) Is √52 nader aan die kleiner of die groter heelgetal? (c) Gebruik jou sakrekenaar en rond √52 af tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"(a) Between which two consecutive integers does √52 lie? (b) Is √52 closer to the smaller or the larger integer? (c) Use your calculator and round √52 off to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Volkome vierkante naby 52: 7^{2} = 49 en 8^{2} = 64, dus 49 < 52 < 64.","en":"Perfect squares near 52: 7^{2} = 49 and 8^{2} = 64, so 49 < 52 < 64."},{"af":"Neem die vierkantswortel van elke deel: √49 < √52 < √64, dus 7 < √52 < 8.","en":"Take the square root of each part: √49 < √52 < √64, so 7 < √52 < 8."},{"af":"52 − 49 = 3 en 64 − 52 = 12. Omdat 52 baie nader aan 49 is, is √52 nader aan 7.","en":"52 − 49 = 3 and 64 − 52 = 12. Because 52 is much closer to 49, √52 is closer to 7."},{"af":"Sakrekenaar: √52 = 7,2111… Die derde desimale syfer is 1 (minder as 5), dus √52 ≈ 7,21.","en":"Calculator: √52 = 7.2111… The third decimal digit is 1 (less than 5), so √52 ≈ 7.21."}],"answer":{"af":"7 < √52 < 8; nader aan 7; √52 ≈ 7,21","en":"7 < √52 < 8; closer to 7; √52 ≈ 7.21"}},{"title":{"af":"Binomium maal trinomium","en":"Binomial times trinomial"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2x − 3)(x² + 4x − 5)","en":"Simplify: (2x − 3)(x² + 4x − 5)"},"steps":[{"af":"Vermenigvuldig 2x met elke term in die tweede hakie: 2x(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x","en":"Multiply 2x by every term in the second bracket: 2x(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig −3 met elke term (pas op vir die tekens): −3(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = −3x^{2} − 12x + 15","en":"Multiply −3 by every term (watch the signs): −3(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = −3x^{2} − 12x + 15"},{"af":"Skryf al ses produkte saam: 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x − 3x^{2} − 12x + 15","en":"Write all six products together: 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x − 3x^{2} − 12x + 15"},{"af":"Versamel gelyksoortige terme: 8x^{2} − 3x^{2} = 5x^{2} en −10x − 12x = −22x, dus 2x^{3} + 5x^{2} − 22x + 15","en":"Collect like terms: 8x^{2} − 3x^{2} = 5x^{2} and −10x − 12x = −22x, so 2x^{3} + 5x^{2} − 22x + 15"}],"answer":{"af":"2x³ + 5x² − 22x + 15","en":"2x³ + 5x² − 22x + 15"}},{"title":{"af":"Vereenvoudig met spesiale produkte","en":"Simplify using special products"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2x − 5)² − (x + 4)(x − 4)","en":"Simplify: (2x − 5)² − (x + 4)(x − 4)"},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}: (2x − 5)^{2} = (2x)^{2} − 2(2x)(5) + 5^{2} = 4x^{2} − 20x + 25","en":"Use (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}: (2x − 5)^{2} = (2x)^{2} − 2(2x)(5) + 5^{2} = 4x^{2} − 20x + 25"},{"af":"Verskil van twee vierkante: (x + 4)(x − 4) = x^{2} − 16","en":"Difference of two squares: (x + 4)(x − 4) = x^{2} − 16"},{"af":"Hou die tweede produk in hakies: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − (x^{2} − 16)","en":"Keep the second product in brackets: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − (x^{2} − 16)"},{"af":"Die minus voor die hakie verander albei tekens: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − x^{2} + 16","en":"The minus in front of the bracket changes both signs: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − x^{2} + 16"},{"af":"Versamel gelyksoortige terme: 3x^{2} − 20x + 41","en":"Collect like terms: 3x^{2} − 20x + 41"}],"answer":{"af":"3x² − 20x + 41","en":"3x² − 20x + 41"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende getalle is irrasionaal?","en":"Which of the following numbers is irrational?"},"options":[{"af":"22/7","en":"22/7"},{"af":"√16","en":"√16"},{"af":"π","en":"π"},{"af":"0,333…","en":"0.333…"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"π = 3,14159… is nie-eindigend en nie-repeterend, dus irrasionaal. 22/7 is 'n breuk (net 'n benadering van π), √16 = 4 en 0,333… = 1/3 – al drie is rasionaal.","en":"π = 3.14159… is non-terminating and non-recurring, so it is irrational. 22/7 is a fraction (only an approximation of π), √16 = 4 and 0.333… = 1/3 – all three are rational."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Elke heelgetal is ook 'n rasionale getal.","en":"Every integer is also a rational number."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Enige heelgetal kan as 'n breuk met noemer 1 geskryf word, bv. −5 = −5/1. Daarom lê Z binne Q.","en":"True. Any integer can be written as a fraction with denominator 1, e.g. −5 = −5/1. That is why Z lies inside Q."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke simbool by die regte getalleversameling.","en":"Match each symbol to the correct set of numbers."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"N","en":"N"},"r":{"af":"{1; 2; 3; …} – natuurlike getalle","en":"{1; 2; 3; …} – natural numbers"}},{"l":{"af":"N₀","en":"N₀"},"r":{"af":"{0; 1; 2; 3; …} – telgetalle","en":"{0; 1; 2; 3; …} – whole numbers"}},{"l":{"af":"Z","en":"Z"},"r":{"af":"{…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} – heelgetalle","en":"{…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} – integers"}},{"l":{"af":"Q′","en":"Q′"},"r":{"af":"Getalle wat nie as a/b geskryf kan word nie – irrasionale getalle","en":"Numbers that cannot be written as a/b – irrational numbers"}},{"l":{"af":"R","en":"R"},"r":{"af":"Al die rasionale en irrasionale getalle – reële getalle","en":"All the rational and irrational numbers – real numbers"}}],"explain":{"af":"N begin by 1, N₀ sluit 0 in, Z sluit die negatiewe heelgetalle in, Q′ is die irrasionale getalle en R is alles saam.","en":"N starts at 1, N₀ includes 0, Z includes the negative integers, Q′ is the irrational numbers and R is everything together."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende is NIE 'n reële getal nie?","en":"Which of the following is NOT a real number?"},"options":[{"af":"−√9","en":"−√9"},{"af":"∛(−8)","en":"∛(−8)"},{"af":"0","en":"0"},{"af":"√(−9)","en":"√(−9)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"√(−9) is nie-reëel: geen reële getal maal homself gee −9 nie. −√9 = −3, ∛(−8) = −2 (want (−2)³ = −8) en 0 is almal reëel.","en":"√(−9) is non-real: no real number times itself gives −9. −√9 = −3, ∛(−8) = −2 (because (−2)³ = −8) and 0 are all real."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Rond 7,2849 af tot twee desimale plekke: ___","en":"Round 7.2849 off to two decimal places: ___"},"answers":{"af":["7,28","7.28"],"en":["7.28","7,28"]},"explain":{"af":"Kyk net na die derde desimale syfer: 4 is minder as 5, dus bly die 8 soos dit is: 7,28. Moenie in stappe afrond nie (7,2849 → 7,285 → 7,29 is verkeerd).","en":"Look only at the third decimal digit: 4 is less than 5, so the 8 stays as it is: 7.28. Do not round in steps (7.2849 → 7.285 → 7.29 is wrong)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tussen watter twee opeenvolgende heelgetalle lê √40?","en":"Between which two consecutive integers does √40 lie?"},"options":[{"af":"20 en 21","en":"20 and 21"},{"af":"6 en 7","en":"6 and 7"},{"af":"4 en 5","en":"4 and 5"},{"af":"36 en 49","en":"36 and 49"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"36 < 40 < 49, dus √36 < √40 < √49, m.a.w. 6 < √40 < 7 (√40 ≈ 6,32). 20 en 21 kom van halveer, nie van 'n wortel nie; 36 en 49 is die vierkante, nie die wortels nie.","en":"36 < 40 < 49, so √36 < √40 < √49, i.e. 6 < √40 < 7 (√40 ≈ 6.32). 20 and 21 come from halving, not from a root; 36 and 49 are the squares, not the roots."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf 0,777… as 'n gewone breuk in sy eenvoudigste vorm: ___","en":"Write 0.777… as a common fraction in its simplest form: ___"},"answers":{"af":["7/9"],"en":["7/9"]},"explain":{"af":"x = 0,777…; 10x = 7,777…; 10x − x = 7, dus 9x = 7 en x = 7/9.","en":"x = 0.777…; 10x = 7.777…; 10x − x = 7, so 9x = 7 and x = 7/9."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Brei uit: (x − 4)²","en":"Expand: (x − 4)²"},"options":[{"af":"x² − 8x + 16","en":"x² − 8x + 16"},{"af":"x² − 16","en":"x² − 16"},{"af":"x² + 16","en":"x² + 16"},{"af":"x² − 8x − 16","en":"x² − 8x − 16"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"(a − b)² = a² − 2ab + b²: x² − 2(x)(4) + 4² = x² − 8x + 16. x² − 16 vergeet die middelterm, en die laaste term is (−4)² = +16, nie −16 nie.","en":"(a − b)² = a² − 2ab + b²: x² − 2(x)(4) + 4² = x² − 8x + 16. x² − 16 forgets the middle term, and the last term is (−4)² = +16, not −16."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"(3x − 2)² = 9x² − 4","en":"(3x − 2)² = 9x² − 4"},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. (3x − 2)² = 9x² − 12x + 4. Die middelterm −2(3x)(2) = −12x ontbreek, en (−2)² = +4, nie −4 nie.","en":"False. (3x − 2)² = 9x² − 12x + 4. The middle term −2(3x)(2) = −12x is missing, and (−2)² = +4, not −4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (x − 3)(x² + 2x − 1)","en":"Simplify: (x − 3)(x² + 2x − 1)"},"options":[{"af":"x³ + 3","en":"x³ + 3"},{"af":"x³ − x² − 7x − 3","en":"x³ − x² − 7x − 3"},{"af":"x³ + 5x² + 5x + 3","en":"x³ + 5x² + 5x + 3"},{"af":"x³ − x² − 7x + 3","en":"x³ − x² − 7x + 3"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"x(x² + 2x − 1) − 3(x² + 2x − 1) = x³ + 2x² − x − 3x² − 6x + 3 = x³ − x² − 7x + 3. Vermenigvuldig elke term met elke term (nie net die eerste en laaste nie), en onthou (−3)(−1) = +3.","en":"x(x² + 2x − 1) − 3(x² + 2x − 1) = x³ + 2x² − x − 3x² − 6x + 3 = x³ − x² − 7x + 3. Multiply every term by every term (not just the first and last), and remember (−3)(−1) = +3."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf 0,4666… (net die 6 herhaal) as 'n gewone breuk in sy eenvoudigste vorm: ___","en":"Write 0.4666… (only the 6 repeats) as a common fraction in its simplest form: ___"},"answers":{"af":["7/15"],"en":["7/15"]},"explain":{"af":"x = 0,4666…; 10x = 4,666…; 100x = 46,666… Trek af: 100x − 10x = 42, dus 90x = 42 en x = 42/90 = 7/15.","en":"x = 0.4666…; 10x = 4.666…; 100x = 46.666… Subtract: 100x − 10x = 42, so 90x = 42 and x = 42/90 = 7/15."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2x − 1)² − (x + 3)(x − 3)","en":"Simplify: (2x − 1)² − (x + 3)(x − 3)"},"options":[{"af":"3x² − 4x + 10","en":"3x² − 4x + 10"},{"af":"3x² − 4x − 8","en":"3x² − 4x − 8"},{"af":"3x² − 2x + 10","en":"3x² − 2x + 10"},{"af":"3x² + 10","en":"3x² + 10"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"(2x − 1)² = 4x² − 4x + 1 en (x + 3)(x − 3) = x² − 9. Dan 4x² − 4x + 1 − (x² − 9) = 4x² − 4x + 1 − x² + 9 = 3x² − 4x + 10. Die minus voor die hakie maak −9 → +9.","en":"(2x − 1)² = 4x² − 4x + 1 and (x + 3)(x − 3) = x² − 9. Then 4x² − 4x + 1 − (x² − 9) = 4x² − 4x + 1 − x² + 9 = 3x² − 4x + 10. The minus in front of the bracket turns −9 into +9."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As x + 1/x = 5, wat is die waarde van x² + 1/x²? ___","en":"If x + 1/x = 5, what is the value of x² + 1/x²? ___"},"answers":{"af":["23"],"en":["23"]},"explain":{"af":"Kwadreer albei kante: (x + 1/x)² = x² + 2(x)(1/x) + 1/x² = x² + 2 + 1/x². Dus x² + 2 + 1/x² = 25 en x² + 1/x² = 23. (Die middelterm 2ab = 2 is die sleutel.)","en":"Square both sides: (x + 1/x)² = x² + 2(x)(1/x) + 1/x² = x² + 2 + 1/x². So x² + 2 + 1/x² = 25 and x² + 1/x² = 23. (The middle term 2ab = 2 is the key.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Vierkantige stoep by 'n huis in Hartbeespoort het sye van (2x + 3) m. In die middel word 'n vierkantige blombedding met sye van x m uitgesny. Watter uitdrukking gee die oppervlakte van die stoep wat oorbly, in m²?","en":"A square patio at a house in Hartbeespoort has sides of (2x + 3) m. A square flower bed with sides of x m is cut out in the middle. Which expression gives the area of the patio that remains, in m²?"},"options":[{"af":"3x² + 9","en":"3x² + 9"},{"af":"3x² + 6x + 9","en":"3x² + 6x + 9"},{"af":"3x² + 12x + 9","en":"3x² + 12x + 9"},{"af":"x² + 12x + 9","en":"x² + 12x + 9"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Oorblywende oppervlakte = (2x + 3)² − x² = 4x² + 12x + 9 − x² = 3x² + 12x + 9. 3x² + 9 vergeet die middelterm, 3x² + 6x + 9 vergeet om die middelterm te verdubbel, en x² + 12x + 9 skryf (2x)² verkeerd as 2x².","en":"Remaining area = (2x + 3)² − x² = 4x² + 12x + 9 − x² = 3x² + 12x + 9. 3x² + 9 forgets the middle term, 3x² + 6x + 9 forgets to double the middle term, and x² + 12x + 9 wrongly writes (2x)² as 2x²."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-faktorisering","title":{"af":"Faktorisering en algebraïese breuke","en":"Factorisation and algebraic fractions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal enige Graad 10-uitdrukking volledig kan faktoriseer en algebraïese breuke kan vereenvoudig, vermenigvuldig, deel, optel en aftrek – met die regte beperkings.","en":"You will be able to factorise any Grade 10 expression fully and simplify, multiply, divide, add and subtract algebraic fractions – with the correct restrictions."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is faktorisering?\n\nFaktorisering is die omgekeerde van uitbrei: jy skryf 'n uitdrukking as 'n **produk** van faktore. \"Faktoriseer volledig\" beteken dat geen faktor verder gefaktoriseer kan word nie. Kontroleer altyd jou antwoord deur die faktore terug te vermenigvuldig.\n\n### Kontrolelys – werk in hierdie volgorde\n\n1. Haal die **gemeenskaplike faktor (GGF)** uit – altyd eerste!\n2. Tel die terme. **Twee terme:** verskil van twee vierkante, of som/verskil van twee derdemagte. **Drie terme:** drieterm. **Vier terme:** groepering in pare.\n3. Kyk of enige faktor **verder** gefaktoriseer kan word.\n\n## 1. Gemeenskaplike faktor\n\n- 6x^{2}y − 9xy^{2} = 3xy(2x − 3y)\n- **Negatiewe faktor:** −4x − 8 = −4(x + 2). Al die tekens binne die hakie verander.\n- **Binomiese faktor:** a(x − 2) + 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(a + 3)\n- **Omruil van tekens:** 3 − x = −(x − 3), dus 5(x − 3) − y(3 − x) = 5(x − 3) + y(x − 3) = (x − 3)(5 + y)\n\n## 2. Verskil van twee vierkante\n\na^{2} − b^{2} = (a − b)(a + b)\n\n- 9x^{2} − 25 = (3x − 5)(3x + 5)\n- 2x^{2} − 18 = 2(x^{2} − 9) = 2(x − 3)(x + 3)\n- x^{4} − 16 = (x^{2} − 4)(x^{2} + 4) = (x − 2)(x + 2)(x^{2} + 4)\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n **Som** van twee vierkante, soos x^{2} + 9, kan nie gefaktoriseer word nie.\n\n## 3. Drieterme ax^{2} + bx + c\n\n**As a = 1:** soek twee getalle met **produk c** en **som b**. Bv. x^{2} − x − 12: produk −12 en som −1 gee −4 en 3, dus (x − 4)(x + 3).\n\n- c positief → albei getalle het dieselfde teken as b.\n- c negatief → die getalle het verskillende tekens; die groter een kry die teken van b.\n\n**As a ≠ 1 (verdeel die middelterm):**\n\n1. Bereken a × c.\n2. Soek twee getalle met produk ac en som b.\n3. Skryf die middelterm as twee terme en groepeer in pare.\n\nBv. 2x^{2} + 7x + 3: ac = 6, en 6 + 1 = 7. Dus 2x^{2} + 6x + x + 3 = 2x(x + 3) + 1(x + 3) = (x + 3)(2x + 1).\n\n'n **Volkome vierkant** is 'n spesiale drieterm: x^{2} − 10x + 25 = (x − 5)^{2}.\n\n## 4. Groepering in pare (vier terme)\n\nGroepeer twee-twee sodat elke paar 'n gemeenskaplike faktor het, en haal dan die binomiese faktor uit:\n\nax − ay + bx − by = a(x − y) + b(x − y) = (x − y)(a + b)\n\nPas op met 'n minus voor die tweede paar: x^{3} − 2x^{2} − 3x + 6 = x^{2}(x − 2) − 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(x^{2} − 3).\n\n## 5. Som en verskil van twee derdemagte\n\n- a^{3} + b^{3} = (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2})\n- a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2})\n\nTekens: **dieselfde – teenoorgesteld – altyd positief**. Die middelterm van die drieterm is ab (nie 2ab nie), en die drieterm kan nooit verder gefaktoriseer word nie. Ken die derdemagte 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, 216, 343, 512, 729 en 1 000.\n\nBv. 8x^{3} − 27 = (2x)^{3} − 3^{3} = (2x − 3)(4x^{2} + 6x + 9)\n\n## Algebraïese breuke\n\n**Beperkings:** 'n noemer mag nooit 0 wees nie. Stel elke faktor van elke noemer gelyk aan 0 en sluit daardie waardes uit. By deling geld dit ook vir die teller van die breuk waardeur jy deel, want dit word 'n noemer wanneer jy omkeer.\n\n**Vereenvoudig:** faktoriseer teller en noemer volledig en kanselleer gemeenskaplike **faktore**:\n[[x² − 9/x + 3]] = [[(x − 3)(x + 3)/x + 3]] = x − 3, x ≠ −3\n\n- **Vermenigvuldig:** faktoriseer alles, kanselleer, en vermenigvuldig wat oorbly.\n- **Deel:** vermenigvuldig met die omgekeerde (onderstebo) van die tweede breuk.\n- **Tel op of trek af:** faktoriseer die noemers, kry die KGN (kleinste gemene noemer), skryf elke breuk met die KGN as noemer, kombineer die tellers en vereenvoudig.\n\nOnthou: [[x − 2/2 − x]] = −1, want 2 − x = −(x − 2).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** [[x + 3/3]] ≠ x. Jy mag net **faktore** kanselleer, nooit terme nie. 'n Minus voor 'n breuk geld vir die hele teller – sit die teller in hakies.","en":"## What is factorisation?\n\nFactorisation is the reverse of expanding: you write an expression as a **product** of factors. \"Factorise fully\" means that no factor can be factorised any further. Always check your answer by multiplying the factors back out.\n\n### Checklist – work in this order\n\n1. Take out the **common factor (HCF)** – always first!\n2. Count the terms. **Two terms:** difference of two squares, or sum/difference of two cubes. **Three terms:** trinomial. **Four terms:** grouping in pairs.\n3. Check whether any factor can be factorised **further**.\n\n## 1. Common factor\n\n- 6x^{2}y − 9xy^{2} = 3xy(2x − 3y)\n- **Negative factor:** −4x − 8 = −4(x + 2). All the signs inside the bracket change.\n- **Binomial factor:** a(x − 2) + 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(a + 3)\n- **Swapping signs:** 3 − x = −(x − 3), so 5(x − 3) − y(3 − x) = 5(x − 3) + y(x − 3) = (x − 3)(5 + y)\n\n## 2. Difference of two squares\n\na^{2} − b^{2} = (a − b)(a + b)\n\n- 9x^{2} − 25 = (3x − 5)(3x + 5)\n- 2x^{2} − 18 = 2(x^{2} − 9) = 2(x − 3)(x + 3)\n- x^{4} − 16 = (x^{2} − 4)(x^{2} + 4) = (x − 2)(x + 2)(x^{2} + 4)\n\n> **Common mistake:** A **sum** of two squares, such as x^{2} + 9, cannot be factorised.\n\n## 3. Trinomials ax^{2} + bx + c\n\n**If a = 1:** find two numbers with **product c** and **sum b**. E.g. x^{2} − x − 12: product −12 and sum −1 give −4 and 3, so (x − 4)(x + 3).\n\n- c positive → both numbers have the same sign as b.\n- c negative → the numbers have different signs; the bigger one gets the sign of b.\n\n**If a ≠ 1 (split the middle term):**\n\n1. Calculate a × c.\n2. Find two numbers with product ac and sum b.\n3. Write the middle term as two terms and group in pairs.\n\nE.g. 2x^{2} + 7x + 3: ac = 6, and 6 + 1 = 7. So 2x^{2} + 6x + x + 3 = 2x(x + 3) + 1(x + 3) = (x + 3)(2x + 1).\n\nA **perfect square** is a special trinomial: x^{2} − 10x + 25 = (x − 5)^{2}.\n\n## 4. Grouping in pairs (four terms)\n\nGroup two by two so that each pair has a common factor, then take out the binomial factor:\n\nax − ay + bx − by = a(x − y) + b(x − y) = (x − y)(a + b)\n\nWatch out for a minus in front of the second pair: x^{3} − 2x^{2} − 3x + 6 = x^{2}(x − 2) − 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(x^{2} − 3).\n\n## 5. Sum and difference of two cubes\n\n- a^{3} + b^{3} = (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2})\n- a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2})\n\nSigns: **same – opposite – always positive**. The middle term of the trinomial is ab (not 2ab), and the trinomial can never be factorised further. Know the cubes 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, 216, 343, 512, 729 and 1 000.\n\nE.g. 8x^{3} − 27 = (2x)^{3} − 3^{3} = (2x − 3)(4x^{2} + 6x + 9)\n\n## Algebraic fractions\n\n**Restrictions:** a denominator may never be 0. Set every factor of every denominator equal to 0 and exclude those values. With division this also applies to the numerator of the fraction you divide by, because it becomes a denominator when you invert.\n\n**Simplify:** factorise numerator and denominator fully and cancel common **factors**:\n[[x² − 9/x + 3]] = [[(x − 3)(x + 3)/x + 3]] = x − 3, x ≠ −3\n\n- **Multiply:** factorise everything, cancel, and multiply what is left.\n- **Divide:** multiply by the reciprocal (upside down) of the second fraction.\n- **Add or subtract:** factorise the denominators, find the LCD (lowest common denominator), write each fraction with the LCD as denominator, combine the numerators and simplify.\n\nRemember: [[x − 2/2 − x]] = −1, because 2 − x = −(x − 2).\n\n> **Common mistake:** [[x + 3/3]] ≠ x. You may only cancel **factors**, never terms. A minus in front of a fraction applies to the whole numerator – put the numerator in brackets."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Faktoriseer","en":"Factorise"},"def":{"af":"Skryf 'n uitdrukking as 'n produk van faktore – die omgekeerde van uitbrei.","en":"Write an expression as a product of factors – the reverse of expanding."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike faktor (GGF)","en":"Common factor (HCF)"},"def":{"af":"Die grootste faktor wat in elke term voorkom. Dit word altyd eerste uitgehaal en kan negatief of 'n binomium wees.","en":"The highest factor that appears in every term. It is always taken out first and can be negative or a binomial."}},{"term":{"af":"Verskil van twee vierkante","en":"Difference of two squares"},"def":{"af":"a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b). 'n Som van twee vierkante, a² + b², kan nie gefaktoriseer word nie.","en":"a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b). A sum of two squares, a² + b², cannot be factorised."}},{"term":{"af":"Drieterm (trinomium)","en":"Trinomial"},"def":{"af":"'n Uitdrukking met drie terme, bv. ax² + bx + c. Soek twee getalle met produk ac en som b.","en":"An expression with three terms, e.g. ax² + bx + c. Find two numbers with product ac and sum b."}},{"term":{"af":"Groepering in pare","en":"Grouping in pairs"},"def":{"af":"Vier terme word twee-twee gegroepeer sodat 'n gemeenskaplike binomiese faktor uitgehaal kan word.","en":"Four terms are grouped two by two so that a common binomial factor can be taken out."}},{"term":{"af":"Som en verskil van twee derdemagte","en":"Sum and difference of two cubes"},"def":{"af":"a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) en a³ − b³ = (a − b)(a² + ab + b²).","en":"a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) and a³ − b³ = (a − b)(a² + ab + b²)."}},{"term":{"af":"Algebraïese breuk","en":"Algebraic fraction"},"def":{"af":"'n Breuk met 'n algebraïese uitdrukking in die teller en/of die noemer, bv. (x + 1)/(x − 3).","en":"A fraction with an algebraic expression in the numerator and/or denominator, e.g. (x + 1)/(x − 3)."}},{"term":{"af":"Beperking","en":"Restriction"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde wat die veranderlike nie mag aanneem nie, omdat dit 'n noemer gelyk aan 0 maak, bv. x ≠ 3.","en":"A value the variable may not take because it makes a denominator equal to 0, e.g. x ≠ 3."}},{"term":{"af":"KGN","en":"LCD"},"def":{"af":"Die kleinste gemene noemer: die kleinste uitdrukking waarin al die noemers deel. Faktoriseer eers die noemers om dit te kry.","en":"The lowest common denominator: the smallest expression that all the denominators divide into. Factorise the denominators first to find it."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike faktor en verskil van twee vierkante","en":"Common factor and difference of two squares"},"problem":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: 3x³ − 48x","en":"Factorise fully: 3x³ − 48x"},"steps":[{"af":"GGF eerste: 3x is 'n faktor van albei terme, dus 3x^{3} − 48x = 3x(x^{2} − 16)","en":"HCF first: 3x is a factor of both terms, so 3x^{3} − 48x = 3x(x^{2} − 16)"},{"af":"Die hakie x^{2} − 16 = x^{2} − 4^{2} is 'n verskil van twee vierkante.","en":"The bracket x^{2} − 16 = x^{2} − 4^{2} is a difference of two squares."},{"af":"3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x(x − 4)(x + 4)","en":"3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x(x − 4)(x + 4)"},{"af":"Kontroleer: (x − 4)(x + 4) = x^{2} − 16 en 3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x^{3} − 48x ✓","en":"Check: (x − 4)(x + 4) = x^{2} − 16 and 3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x^{3} − 48x ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"3x(x − 4)(x + 4)","en":"3x(x − 4)(x + 4)"}},{"title":{"af":"Drieterm met a ≠ 1","en":"Trinomial with a ≠ 1"},"problem":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 6x² − x − 2","en":"Factorise: 6x² − x − 2"},"steps":[{"af":"Bereken a × c = 6 × (−2) = −12","en":"Calculate a × c = 6 × (−2) = −12"},{"af":"Soek twee getalle met produk −12 en som −1: −4 en 3","en":"Find two numbers with product −12 and sum −1: −4 and 3"},{"af":"Verdeel die middelterm: 6x^{2} − 4x + 3x − 2","en":"Split the middle term: 6x^{2} − 4x + 3x − 2"},{"af":"Groepeer in pare: 2x(3x − 2) + 1(3x − 2)","en":"Group in pairs: 2x(3x − 2) + 1(3x − 2)"},{"af":"Haal die binomiese faktor uit: (3x − 2)(2x + 1)","en":"Take out the binomial factor: (3x − 2)(2x + 1)"},{"af":"Kontroleer: (3x − 2)(2x + 1) = 6x^{2} + 3x − 4x − 2 = 6x^{2} − x − 2 ✓","en":"Check: (3x − 2)(2x + 1) = 6x^{2} + 3x − 4x − 2 = 6x^{2} − x − 2 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"(3x − 2)(2x + 1)","en":"(3x − 2)(2x + 1)"}},{"title":{"af":"Groepering en derdemagte","en":"Grouping and cubes"},"problem":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: (a) x³ + 3x² − 4x − 12 (b) 2y³ − 54","en":"Factorise fully: (a) x³ + 3x² − 4x − 12 (b) 2y³ − 54"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Vier terme, dus groepeer in pare: x^{2}(x + 3) − 4(x + 3)","en":"(a) Four terms, so group in pairs: x^{2}(x + 3) − 4(x + 3)"},{"af":"Haal die binomiese faktor (x + 3) uit: (x + 3)(x^{2} − 4)","en":"Take out the binomial factor (x + 3): (x + 3)(x^{2} − 4)"},{"af":"x^{2} − 4 is 'n verskil van twee vierkante: (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2)","en":"x^{2} − 4 is a difference of two squares: (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2)"},{"af":"(b) GGF eerste: 2y^{3} − 54 = 2(y^{3} − 27)","en":"(b) HCF first: 2y^{3} − 54 = 2(y^{3} − 27)"},{"af":"y^{3} − 27 = y^{3} − 3^{3}. Gebruik a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}): 2(y − 3)(y^{2} + 3y + 9)","en":"y^{3} − 27 = y^{3} − 3^{3}. Use a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}): 2(y − 3)(y^{2} + 3y + 9)"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2) (b) 2(y − 3)(y² + 3y + 9)","en":"(a) (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2) (b) 2(y − 3)(y² + 3y + 9)"}},{"title":{"af":"Algebraïese breuke aftrek","en":"Subtracting algebraic fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig 3/(x − 2) − 12/(x² − 4) en noem die beperkings.","en":"Simplify 3/(x − 2) − 12/(x² − 4) and state the restrictions."},"steps":[{"af":"Faktoriseer die noemers: [[3/x − 2]] − [[12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]","en":"Factorise the denominators: [[3/x − 2]] − [[12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]"},{"af":"Beperkings: x − 2 ≠ 0 en x + 2 ≠ 0, dus x ≠ 2 en x ≠ −2","en":"Restrictions: x − 2 ≠ 0 and x + 2 ≠ 0, so x ≠ 2 and x ≠ −2"},{"af":"KGN = (x − 2)(x + 2): [[3(x + 2) − 12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]","en":"LCD = (x − 2)(x + 2): [[3(x + 2) − 12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]"},{"af":"Vereenvoudig die teller: 3x + 6 − 12 = 3x − 6 = 3(x − 2)","en":"Simplify the numerator: 3x + 6 − 12 = 3x − 6 = 3(x − 2)"},{"af":"Kanselleer die gemeenskaplike faktor (x − 2): [[3(x − 2)/(x − 2)(x + 2)]] = [[3/x + 2]]","en":"Cancel the common factor (x − 2): [[3(x − 2)/(x − 2)(x + 2)]] = [[3/x + 2]]"}],"answer":{"af":"3/(x + 2); x ≠ 2 en x ≠ −2","en":"3/(x + 2); x ≠ 2 and x ≠ −2"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is altyd die eerste stap wanneer jy 'n uitdrukking volledig faktoriseer?","en":"What is always the first step when you factorise an expression fully?"},"options":[{"af":"Tel die aantal terme","en":"Count the number of terms"},{"af":"Soek 'n verskil van twee vierkante","en":"Look for a difference of two squares"},{"af":"Maal die hakies uit","en":"Multiply out the brackets"},{"af":"Haal die gemeenskaplike faktor (GGF) uit","en":"Take out the common factor (HCF)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Haal altyd eers die GGF uit – dit maak die res makliker en jy mis nie faktore nie. Daarna tel jy die terme om die volgende metode te kies.","en":"Always take out the HCF first – it makes the rest easier and you won't miss factors. After that you count the terms to choose the next method."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"x² + 25 kan gefaktoriseer word as (x + 5)(x − 5).","en":"x² + 25 can be factorised as (x + 5)(x − 5)."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. (x + 5)(x − 5) = x² − 25. 'n Som van twee vierkante soos x² + 25 kan nie gefaktoriseer word nie.","en":"False. (x + 5)(x − 5) = x² − 25. A sum of two squares such as x² + 25 cannot be factorised."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke uitdrukking by sy faktorisering.","en":"Match each expression to its factorisation."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"a² − b²","en":"a² − b²"},"r":{"af":"(a − b)(a + b)","en":"(a − b)(a + b)"}},{"l":{"af":"a² − 2ab + b²","en":"a² − 2ab + b²"},"r":{"af":"(a − b)²","en":"(a − b)²"}},{"l":{"af":"a² + 2ab + b²","en":"a² + 2ab + b²"},"r":{"af":"(a + b)²","en":"(a + b)²"}},{"l":{"af":"a³ + b³","en":"a³ + b³"},"r":{"af":"(a + b)(a² − ab + b²)","en":"(a + b)(a² − ab + b²)"}},{"l":{"af":"a³ − b³","en":"a³ − b³"},"r":{"af":"(a − b)(a² + ab + b²)","en":"(a − b)(a² + ab + b²)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ken hierdie vyf patrone uit jou kop. By derdemagte: die binomium het dieselfde teken, die middelterm van die drieterm die teenoorgestelde teken, en die laaste term is altyd positief.","en":"Know these five patterns by heart. For cubes: the binomial has the same sign, the middle term of the trinomial the opposite sign, and the last term is always positive."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: 2x² − 18","en":"Factorise fully: 2x² − 18"},"options":[{"af":"2(x − 3)(x + 3)","en":"2(x − 3)(x + 3)"},{"af":"(x − 3)(x + 3)","en":"(x − 3)(x + 3)"},{"af":"2(x − 9)(x + 9)","en":"2(x − 9)(x + 9)"},{"af":"2(x − 3)²","en":"2(x − 3)²"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"GGF eerste: 2(x² − 9). Dan is x² − 9 'n verskil van twee vierkante: 2(x − 3)(x + 3). Moenie die 2 laat val nie, en √9 = 3, nie 9 nie.","en":"HCF first: 2(x² − 9). Then x² − 9 is a difference of two squares: 2(x − 3)(x + 3). Don't drop the 2, and √9 = 3, not 9."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: x² + 5x − 14 = (x + 7)(x − ___)","en":"Complete: x² + 5x − 14 = (x + 7)(x − ___)"},"answers":{"af":["2"],"en":["2"]},"explain":{"af":"Soek twee getalle met produk −14 en som 5: 7 en −2. Kontroleer: (x + 7)(x − 2) = x² − 2x + 7x − 14 = x² + 5x − 14.","en":"Find two numbers with product −14 and sum 5: 7 and −2. Check: (x + 7)(x − 2) = x² − 2x + 7x − 14 = x² + 5x − 14."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer: x² − 7x + 12","en":"Factorise: x² − 7x + 12"},"options":[{"af":"(x + 3)(x + 4)","en":"(x + 3)(x + 4)"},{"af":"(x − 2)(x − 6)","en":"(x − 2)(x − 6)"},{"af":"(x − 3)(x − 4)","en":"(x − 3)(x − 4)"},{"af":"(x + 3)(x − 4)","en":"(x + 3)(x − 4)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Produk +12 en som −7: −3 en −4. Omdat c positief is, kry albei die teken van b (negatief). (x − 2)(x − 6) gee wel produk 12, maar die som is −8.","en":"Product +12 and sum −7: −3 and −4. Because c is positive, both get the sign of b (negative). (x − 2)(x − 6) does give product 12, but the sum is −8."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vir x ≠ 5 is (x − 5)/(5 − x) = −1.","en":"For x ≠ 5, (x − 5)/(5 − x) = −1."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 5 − x = −(x − 5), dus (x − 5)/(−(x − 5)) = −1.","en":"True. 5 − x = −(x − 5), so (x − 5)/(−(x − 5)) = −1."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 3x² − 5x − 2","en":"Factorise: 3x² − 5x − 2"},"options":[{"af":"(3x − 1)(x + 2)","en":"(3x − 1)(x + 2)"},{"af":"(3x + 1)(x − 2)","en":"(3x + 1)(x − 2)"},{"af":"(3x + 2)(x − 1)","en":"(3x + 2)(x − 1)"},{"af":"(3x − 2)(x + 1)","en":"(3x − 2)(x + 1)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"ac = 3 × (−2) = −6; getalle met produk −6 en som −5: −6 en 1. 3x² − 6x + x − 2 = 3x(x − 2) + 1(x − 2) = (3x + 1)(x − 2). Kontroleer altyd deur uit te maal – (3x − 1)(x + 2) gee +5x.","en":"ac = 3 × (−2) = −6; numbers with product −6 and sum −5: −6 and 1. 3x² − 6x + x − 2 = 3x(x − 2) + 1(x − 2) = (3x + 1)(x − 2). Always check by multiplying out – (3x − 1)(x + 2) gives +5x."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 5(x − 2) − y(2 − x)","en":"Factorise: 5(x − 2) − y(2 − x)"},"options":[{"af":"(x − 2)(5 − y)","en":"(x − 2)(5 − y)"},{"af":"(x − 2)(y − 5)","en":"(x − 2)(y − 5)"},{"af":"5y(x − 2)","en":"5y(x − 2)"},{"af":"(x − 2)(5 + y)","en":"(x − 2)(5 + y)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Skryf 2 − x = −(x − 2): 5(x − 2) − y(−(x − 2)) = 5(x − 2) + y(x − 2) = (x − 2)(5 + y). Minus maal minus word plus – dis waarom (x − 2)(5 − y) verkeerd is.","en":"Write 2 − x = −(x − 2): 5(x − 2) − y(−(x − 2)) = 5(x − 2) + y(x − 2) = (x − 2)(5 + y). Minus times minus becomes plus – that is why (x − 2)(5 − y) is wrong."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: 27a³ − 8 = (3a − 2)(9a² + ___a + 4)","en":"Complete: 27a³ − 8 = (3a − 2)(9a² + ___a + 4)"},"answers":{"af":["6"],"en":["6"]},"explain":{"af":"27a³ = (3a)³ en 8 = 2³. Die middelterm van die drieterm is (3a)(2) = 6a, met die teenoorgestelde teken van die binomium, dus +6a.","en":"27a³ = (3a)³ and 8 = 2³. The middle term of the trinomial is (3a)(2) = 6a, with the opposite sign to the binomial, so +6a."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: 8x³ + 27","en":"Factorise fully: 8x³ + 27"},"options":[{"af":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9)","en":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9)"},{"af":"(2x + 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)","en":"(2x + 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)"},{"af":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 12x + 9)","en":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 12x + 9)"},{"af":"(2x − 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)","en":"(2x − 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"8x³ = (2x)³ en 27 = 3³. a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) gee (2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9). Die middelterm is ab = 6x (nie 2ab = 12x nie) en het 'n negatiewe teken.","en":"8x³ = (2x)³ and 27 = 3³. a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) gives (2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9). The middle term is ab = 6x (not 2ab = 12x) and has a negative sign."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig (x ≠ 3): x/(x − 3) + 3/(3 − x) = ___","en":"Simplify (x ≠ 3): x/(x − 3) + 3/(3 − x) = ___"},"answers":{"af":["1"],"en":["1"]},"explain":{"af":"3 − x = −(x − 3), dus 3/(3 − x) = −3/(x − 3). Dan x/(x − 3) − 3/(x − 3) = (x − 3)/(x − 3) = 1.","en":"3 − x = −(x − 3), so 3/(3 − x) = −3/(x − 3). Then x/(x − 3) − 3/(x − 3) = (x − 3)/(x − 3) = 1."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: [(2x² − 8)/(x² + x − 6)] ÷ [(x + 2)/(x + 3)] = ___","en":"Simplify: [(2x² − 8)/(x² + x − 6)] ÷ [(x + 2)/(x + 3)] = ___"},"answers":{"af":["2"],"en":["2"]},"explain":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 2x² − 8 = 2(x − 2)(x + 2) en x² + x − 6 = (x + 3)(x − 2). Deel = maal met die omgekeerde: [2(x − 2)(x + 2)]/[(x + 3)(x − 2)] × (x + 3)/(x + 2). Alles kanselleer behalwe 2 (x ≠ −3; 2; −2).","en":"Factorise: 2x² − 8 = 2(x − 2)(x + 2) and x² + x − 6 = (x + 3)(x − 2). Divide = multiply by the reciprocal: [2(x − 2)(x + 2)]/[(x + 3)(x − 2)] × (x + 3)/(x + 2). Everything cancels except 2 (x ≠ −3; 2; −2)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vir watter waardes van x is [(x + 1)/(x − 3)] ÷ [(x + 5)/(x − 2)] ongedefinieerd?","en":"For which values of x is [(x + 1)/(x − 3)] ÷ [(x + 5)/(x − 2)] undefined?"},"options":[{"af":"x = 3 en x = 2","en":"x = 3 and x = 2"},{"af":"x = −1, x = 3, x = −5 en x = 2","en":"x = −1, x = 3, x = −5 and x = 2"},{"af":"x = 3, x = 2 en x = −5","en":"x = 3, x = 2 and x = −5"},{"af":"x = −3 en x = −2","en":"x = −3 and x = −2"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die noemers x − 3 en x − 2 mag nie 0 wees nie: x ≠ 3 en x ≠ 2. By deling keer jy (x + 5)/(x − 2) om na (x − 2)/(x + 5), dus is x + 5 ook 'n noemer: x ≠ −5. Die teller x + 1 = 0 gee net 'n antwoord van 0, wat wel gedefinieer is.","en":"The denominators x − 3 and x − 2 may not be 0: x ≠ 3 and x ≠ 2. With division you invert (x + 5)/(x − 2) to (x − 2)/(x + 5), so x + 5 is also a denominator: x ≠ −5. The numerator x + 1 = 0 only gives an answer of 0, which is defined."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-eksponente","title":{"af":"Eksponente","en":"Exponents"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die eksponentwette (ook nul- en negatiewe eksponente) kan toepas, uitdrukkings met die priemfaktor-metode kan vereenvoudig en eenvoudige eksponensiële vergelykings kan oplos.","en":"You will be able to apply the laws of exponents (including zero and negative exponents), simplify expressions with the prime factor method and solve simple exponential equations."},"summary":{"af":"## Basiese begrippe\n\nIn a^{n} is a die **grondtal** en n die **eksponent**: a^{n} = a × a × … × a (n faktore). Bv. 2^{5} = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 32. In Graad 10 is die eksponente heelgetalle: positief, nul of negatief.\n\n## Die eksponentwette\n\nVir a, b ≠ 0 en m, n heelgetalle:\n\n| Wet | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| a^{m} × a^{n} = a^{m+n} | 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7} |\n| a^{m} ÷ a^{n} = a^{m−n} | x^{9} ÷ x^{4} = x^{5} |\n| (a^{m})^{n} = a^{mn} | (x^{3})^{4} = x^{12} |\n| (ab)^{n} = a^{n}b^{n} | (3x)^{2} = 9x^{2} |\n| ([[a/b]])^{n} = [[aⁿ/bⁿ]] | ([[2/3]])^{3} = [[8/27]] |\n| a^{0} = 1 | 7^{0} = 1 |\n| a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]] | 2^{−3} = [[1/8]] |\n\n**Negatiewe eksponent:** a^{−n} beteken \"een gedeel deur a^{n}\" – dit maak die getal **nie** negatief nie. Om 'n negatiewe eksponent positief te maak, skuif jy die faktor oor die breukstreep: [[1/a⁻ⁿ]] = a^{n}, [[x⁻²/y⁻³]] = [[y³/x²]] en ([[a/b]])^{−n} = ([[b/a]])^{n}.\n\n### Hoekom is a^{0} = 1 en a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]]?\n\nVolgens die deelwet is a^{3} ÷ a^{3} = a^{3−3} = a^{0}. Maar enige getal (behalwe 0) gedeel deur homself is 1, dus a^{0} = 1. Net so is a^{2} ÷ a^{5} = a^{2−5} = a^{−3}. As jy dit uitskryf, kanselleer twee a's en bly daar drie a's onder die breukstreep oor: [[1/a³]]. Daarom is a^{−3} = [[1/a³]].\n\n### Stappe om te vereenvoudig\n\n1. Verwyder hakies met die mag-van-'n-produk-wet.\n2. Skryf verskillende grondtalle as priemfaktore.\n3. Versamel magte van dieselfde grondtal: tel die eksponente op by ×, trek af by ÷.\n4. Skryf die finale antwoord met positiewe eksponente.\n\n### Algemene foute\n\n- 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7}, **nie** 4^{7} nie – die grondtal bly dieselfde.\n- 3x^{0} = 3 × 1 = 3, maar (3x)^{0} = 1.\n- −3^{2} = −9, maar (−3)^{2} = 9.\n- Die wette werk net vir **produkte en kwosiënte**, nie vir somme nie: 2^{3} + 2^{4} ≠ 2^{7}, en (a + b)^{2} ≠ a^{2} + b^{2}.\n- 5^{x} + 5^{x} = 2 × 5^{x} (nie 10^{x} of 5^{2x} nie).\n\n## Die priemfaktor-metode\n\nAs die grondtalle verskil, skryf elke grondtal as 'n produk van **priemfaktore** en pas dan die wette op elke priemgetal apart toe.\n\n- 4 = 2^{2}; 8 = 2^{3}; 9 = 3^{2}; 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 27 = 3^{3}; 36 = 2^{2} × 3^{2}\n- 6^{x} = (2 × 3)^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{x}\n- 9^{x+1} = (3^{2})^{x+1} = 3^{2x+2} – vermenigvuldig die **hele** eksponent met 2.\n\nBv. (6^{x} × 4^{x+1}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = (2^{x} × 3^{x} × 2^{2x+2}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = 2^{3x+2−3x} × 3^{x−x} = 2^{2} = 4\n\n## Uitdrukkings met + of −\n\nAs 'n teller of noemer uit terme bestaan, mag jy nie die wette direk gebruik nie. Haal eers 'n gemeenskaplike faktor uit – gewoonlik die mag met die **kleinste** eksponent. Onthou dat 2^{x+2} = 2^{x} × 2^{2}:\n\n(2^{x+2} − 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 2^{x}(2^{2} − 1) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = (3 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 1\n\n## Eksponensiële vergelykings\n\nIn 'n **eksponensiële vergelyking** is die onbekende in die eksponent. Metode:\n\n1. Skryf albei kante as 'n mag van dieselfde (priem)grondtal.\n2. As a^{x} = a^{y} (a > 0, a ≠ 1), dan is x = y – stel die eksponente gelyk.\n3. Los die lineêre vergelyking op en kontroleer deur terug te vervang.\n\n- 2^{x} = 32 → 2^{x} = 2^{5} → x = 5\n- 3^{x+1} = [[1/27]] → 3^{x+1} = 3^{−3} → x + 1 = −3 → x = −4\n- 5^{2x−1} = 125 → 5^{2x−1} = 5^{3} → 2x − 1 = 3 → x = 2\n- 7^{x} = 1 → 7^{x} = 7^{0} → x = 0\n- 2^{x+1} + 2^{x} = 24 → 2^{x}(2 + 1) = 24 → 2^{x} = 8 → x = 3 (haal eers die gemeenskaplike faktor uit)\n\n> **Onthou!** As a > 0, is a^{x} altyd positief. 'n Vergelyking soos 2^{x} = −8 het dus **geen oplossing** nie.\n\n> **Wenk:** Ken die magte van 2 (tot 2^{10} = 1 024), van 3 (tot 3^{5} = 243) en van 5 (tot 5^{4} = 625) uit jou kop – dan sien jy dadelik watter grondtal om te gebruik.","en":"## Basic concepts\n\nIn a^{n}, a is the **base** and n is the **exponent**: a^{n} = a × a × … × a (n factors). E.g. 2^{5} = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 32. In Grade 10 the exponents are integers: positive, zero or negative.\n\n## The laws of exponents\n\nFor a, b ≠ 0 and m, n integers:\n\n| Law | Example |\n|---|---|\n| a^{m} × a^{n} = a^{m+n} | 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7} |\n| a^{m} ÷ a^{n} = a^{m−n} | x^{9} ÷ x^{4} = x^{5} |\n| (a^{m})^{n} = a^{mn} | (x^{3})^{4} = x^{12} |\n| (ab)^{n} = a^{n}b^{n} | (3x)^{2} = 9x^{2} |\n| ([[a/b]])^{n} = [[aⁿ/bⁿ]] | ([[2/3]])^{3} = [[8/27]] |\n| a^{0} = 1 | 7^{0} = 1 |\n| a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]] | 2^{−3} = [[1/8]] |\n\n**Negative exponent:** a^{−n} means \"one divided by a^{n}\" – it does **not** make the number negative. To make a negative exponent positive, move the factor across the fraction line: [[1/a⁻ⁿ]] = a^{n}, [[x⁻²/y⁻³]] = [[y³/x²]] and ([[a/b]])^{−n} = ([[b/a]])^{n}.\n\n### Why is a^{0} = 1 and a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]]?\n\nBy the division law, a^{3} ÷ a^{3} = a^{3−3} = a^{0}. But any number (except 0) divided by itself is 1, so a^{0} = 1. In the same way, a^{2} ÷ a^{5} = a^{2−5} = a^{−3}. If you write it out, two a's cancel and three a's are left below the fraction line: [[1/a³]]. That is why a^{−3} = [[1/a³]].\n\n### Steps to simplify\n\n1. Remove brackets with the power-of-a-product law.\n2. Write different bases as prime factors.\n3. Collect powers of the same base: add the exponents for ×, subtract for ÷.\n4. Write the final answer with positive exponents.\n\n### Common mistakes\n\n- 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7}, **not** 4^{7} – the base stays the same.\n- 3x^{0} = 3 × 1 = 3, but (3x)^{0} = 1.\n- −3^{2} = −9, but (−3)^{2} = 9.\n- The laws only work for **products and quotients**, not for sums: 2^{3} + 2^{4} ≠ 2^{7}, and (a + b)^{2} ≠ a^{2} + b^{2}.\n- 5^{x} + 5^{x} = 2 × 5^{x} (not 10^{x} or 5^{2x}).\n\n## The prime factor method\n\nIf the bases are different, write every base as a product of **prime factors** and then apply the laws to each prime separately.\n\n- 4 = 2^{2}; 8 = 2^{3}; 9 = 3^{2}; 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 27 = 3^{3}; 36 = 2^{2} × 3^{2}\n- 6^{x} = (2 × 3)^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{x}\n- 9^{x+1} = (3^{2})^{x+1} = 3^{2x+2} – multiply the **whole** exponent by 2.\n\nE.g. (6^{x} × 4^{x+1}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = (2^{x} × 3^{x} × 2^{2x+2}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = 2^{3x+2−3x} × 3^{x−x} = 2^{2} = 4\n\n## Expressions with + or −\n\nIf a numerator or denominator consists of terms, you may not use the laws directly. First take out a common factor – usually the power with the **smallest** exponent. Remember that 2^{x+2} = 2^{x} × 2^{2}:\n\n(2^{x+2} − 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 2^{x}(2^{2} − 1) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = (3 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 1\n\n## Exponential equations\n\nIn an **exponential equation** the unknown is in the exponent. Method:\n\n1. Write both sides as a power of the same (prime) base.\n2. If a^{x} = a^{y} (a > 0, a ≠ 1), then x = y – equate the exponents.\n3. Solve the linear equation and check by substituting back.\n\n- 2^{x} = 32 → 2^{x} = 2^{5} → x = 5\n- 3^{x+1} = [[1/27]] → 3^{x+1} = 3^{−3} → x + 1 = −3 → x = −4\n- 5^{2x−1} = 125 → 5^{2x−1} = 5^{3} → 2x − 1 = 3 → x = 2\n- 7^{x} = 1 → 7^{x} = 7^{0} → x = 0\n- 2^{x+1} + 2^{x} = 24 → 2^{x}(2 + 1) = 24 → 2^{x} = 8 → x = 3 (take out the common factor first)\n\n> **Remember!** If a > 0, a^{x} is always positive. An equation such as 2^{x} = −8 therefore has **no solution**.\n\n> **Tip:** Know the powers of 2 (up to 2^{10} = 1 024), of 3 (up to 3^{5} = 243) and of 5 (up to 5^{4} = 625) by heart – then you immediately see which base to use."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Grondtal","en":"Base"},"def":{"af":"Die getal wat herhaaldelik met homself vermenigvuldig word; in aⁿ is a die grondtal.","en":"The number that is multiplied by itself repeatedly; in aⁿ, a is the base."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponent","en":"Exponent"},"def":{"af":"Die getal bo regs wat aandui hoeveel keer die grondtal as faktor voorkom; in aⁿ is n die eksponent.","en":"The number at the top right that shows how many times the base appears as a factor; in aⁿ, n is the exponent."}},{"term":{"af":"Mag","en":"Power"},"def":{"af":"'n Uitdrukking in die vorm aⁿ, bv. 2⁵ = 32 is die vyfde mag van 2.","en":"An expression of the form aⁿ, e.g. 2⁵ = 32 is the fifth power of 2."}},{"term":{"af":"Nul-eksponent","en":"Zero exponent"},"def":{"af":"Enige grondtal behalwe 0 tot die mag 0 is 1: a⁰ = 1. Let op: 3x⁰ = 3, maar (3x)⁰ = 1.","en":"Any base except 0 to the power 0 is 1: a⁰ = 1. Note: 3x⁰ = 3, but (3x)⁰ = 1."}},{"term":{"af":"Negatiewe eksponent","en":"Negative exponent"},"def":{"af":"a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ. Dit beteken 'een gedeel deur' en maak die getal nie negatief nie, bv. 2⁻³ = 1/8.","en":"a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ. It means 'one divided by' and does not make the number negative, e.g. 2⁻³ = 1/8."}},{"term":{"af":"Priemfaktor-metode","en":"Prime factor method"},"def":{"af":"Skryf elke grondtal as 'n produk van priemfaktore (bv. 12 = 2² × 3) sodat die eksponentwette op elke priemgetal toegepas kan word.","en":"Write every base as a product of prime factors (e.g. 12 = 2² × 3) so that the laws of exponents can be applied to each prime."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponensiële vergelyking","en":"Exponential equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking waarin die onbekende in die eksponent is, bv. 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/27. Maak die grondtalle gelyk en stel die eksponente gelyk.","en":"An equation in which the unknown is in the exponent, e.g. 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/27. Make the bases equal and equate the exponents."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vereenvoudig met die eksponentwette","en":"Simplify with the laws of exponents"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig en skryf die antwoord met positiewe eksponente: (2x³y⁻²)³ ÷ (4x⁵y⁻⁴)","en":"Simplify and write the answer with positive exponents: (2x³y⁻²)³ ÷ (4x⁵y⁻⁴)"},"steps":[{"af":"Mag van 'n produk – verhef elke faktor tot die mag 3: (2x^{3}y^{−2})^{3} = 2^{3}x^{9}y^{−6} = 8x^{9}y^{−6}","en":"Power of a product – raise every factor to the power 3: (2x^{3}y^{−2})^{3} = 2^{3}x^{9}y^{−6} = 8x^{9}y^{−6}"},{"af":"Deel nou 8x^{9}y^{−6} ÷ 4x^{5}y^{−4}: deel die koëffisiënte en trek die eksponente van dieselfde grondtal af.","en":"Now divide 8x^{9}y^{−6} ÷ 4x^{5}y^{−4}: divide the coefficients and subtract the exponents of the same base."},{"af":"8 ÷ 4 = 2; x^{9−5} = x^{4}; y^{−6−(−4)} = y^{−6+4} = y^{−2}","en":"8 ÷ 4 = 2; x^{9−5} = x^{4}; y^{−6−(−4)} = y^{−6+4} = y^{−2}"},{"af":"Skryf met 'n positiewe eksponent: 2x^{4}y^{−2} = [[2x⁴/y²]]","en":"Write with a positive exponent: 2x^{4}y^{−2} = [[2x⁴/y²]]"}],"answer":{"af":"2x⁴/y²","en":"2x⁴/y²"}},{"title":{"af":"Die priemfaktor-metode","en":"The prime factor method"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (12ˣ × 9ˣ⁻¹) ÷ (18ˣ × 6ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (12ˣ × 9ˣ⁻¹) ÷ (18ˣ × 6ˣ)"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf elke grondtal in priemfaktore: 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 9 = 3^{2}; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 6 = 2 × 3","en":"Write every base in prime factors: 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 9 = 3^{2}; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 6 = 2 × 3"},{"af":"Teller: 12^{x} × 9^{x−1} = 2^{2x} × 3^{x} × 3^{2x−2} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x−2}","en":"Numerator: 12^{x} × 9^{x−1} = 2^{2x} × 3^{x} × 3^{2x−2} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x−2}"},{"af":"Noemer: 18^{x} × 6^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{2x} × 2^{x} × 3^{x} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x}","en":"Denominator: 18^{x} × 6^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{2x} × 2^{x} × 3^{x} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x}"},{"af":"Trek die eksponente af: 2^{2x−2x} × 3^{(3x−2)−3x} = 2^{0} × 3^{−2}","en":"Subtract the exponents: 2^{2x−2x} × 3^{(3x−2)−3x} = 2^{0} × 3^{−2}"},{"af":"= 1 × [[1/3²]] = [[1/9]]","en":"= 1 × [[1/3²]] = [[1/9]]"}],"answer":{"af":"1/9","en":"1/9"}},{"title":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike faktor by eksponente","en":"Common factor with exponents"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2ˣ⁺³ − 2ˣ⁺¹) ÷ (3 × 2ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (2ˣ⁺³ − 2ˣ⁺¹) ÷ (3 × 2ˣ)"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf elke mag as 2^{x} maal 'n getal: 2^{x+3} = 2^{x} × 2^{3} = 8 × 2^{x} en 2^{x+1} = 2^{x} × 2 = 2 × 2^{x}","en":"Write every power as 2^{x} times a number: 2^{x+3} = 2^{x} × 2^{3} = 8 × 2^{x} and 2^{x+1} = 2^{x} × 2 = 2 × 2^{x}"},{"af":"Haal die gemeenskaplike faktor 2^{x} in die teller uit: 2^{x}(8 − 2) = 6 × 2^{x}","en":"Take out the common factor 2^{x} in the numerator: 2^{x}(8 − 2) = 6 × 2^{x}"},{"af":"Die uitdrukking word (6 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x})","en":"The expression becomes (6 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x})"},{"af":"Kanselleer die faktor 2^{x}: 6 ÷ 3 = 2","en":"Cancel the factor 2^{x}: 6 ÷ 3 = 2"}],"answer":{"af":"2","en":"2"}},{"title":{"af":"Eksponensiële vergelykings","en":"Exponential equations"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x: (a) 2ˣ⁻³ = 1/16 (b) 4ˣ⁺¹ = 8ˣ","en":"Solve for x: (a) 2ˣ⁻³ = 1/16 (b) 4ˣ⁺¹ = 8ˣ"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 16 = 2^{4}, dus [[1/16]] = 2^{−4}. Die vergelyking word 2^{x−3} = 2^{−4}","en":"(a) 16 = 2^{4}, so [[1/16]] = 2^{−4}. The equation becomes 2^{x−3} = 2^{−4}"},{"af":"Stel die eksponente gelyk: x − 3 = −4, dus x = −1","en":"Equate the exponents: x − 3 = −4, so x = −1"},{"af":"(b) Skryf albei kante met grondtal 2: 4^{x+1} = (2^{2})^{x+1} = 2^{2x+2} en 8^{x} = (2^{3})^{x} = 2^{3x}","en":"(b) Write both sides with base 2: 4^{x+1} = (2^{2})^{x+1} = 2^{2x+2} and 8^{x} = (2^{3})^{x} = 2^{3x}"},{"af":"2^{2x+2} = 2^{3x}, dus 2x + 2 = 3x en x = 2","en":"2^{2x+2} = 2^{3x}, so 2x + 2 = 3x and x = 2"},{"af":"Kontroleer (b): 4^{3} = 64 en 8^{2} = 64 ✓","en":"Check (b): 4^{3} = 64 and 8^{2} = 64 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) x = −1 (b) x = 2","en":"(a) x = −1 (b) x = 2"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: 3⁴ × 3⁵","en":"Simplify: 3⁴ × 3⁵"},"options":[{"af":"3²⁰","en":"3²⁰"},{"af":"9⁹","en":"9⁹"},{"af":"3⁹","en":"3⁹"},{"af":"9²⁰","en":"9²⁰"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Met dieselfde grondtal tel jy die eksponente op: 3⁴⁺⁵ = 3⁹. Die grondtal bly 3 – moenie die grondtalle of die eksponente vermenigvuldig nie.","en":"With the same base you add the exponents: 3⁴⁺⁵ = 3⁹. The base stays 3 – do not multiply the bases or the exponents."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"2⁻³ = −8","en":"2⁻³ = −8"},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Negatiewe eksponent beteken 'een gedeel deur': 2⁻³ = 1/2³ = 1/8. Die antwoord is positief.","en":"False. A negative exponent means 'one divided by': 2⁻³ = 1/2³ = 1/8. The answer is positive."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke uitdrukking by sy waarde.","en":"Match each expression to its value."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"7⁰","en":"7⁰"},"r":{"af":"1","en":"1"}},{"l":{"af":"2⁻²","en":"2⁻²"},"r":{"af":"1/4","en":"1/4"}},{"l":{"af":"(−3)²","en":"(−3)²"},"r":{"af":"9","en":"9"}},{"l":{"af":"−3²","en":"−3²"},"r":{"af":"−9","en":"−9"}},{"l":{"af":"(1/2)⁻³","en":"(1/2)⁻³"},"r":{"af":"8","en":"8"}}],"explain":{"af":"7⁰ = 1; 2⁻² = 1/2² = 1/4; (−3)² = (−3)(−3) = 9; −3² = −(3²) = −9 omdat net die 3 gekwadreer word; (1/2)⁻³ = 2³ = 8.","en":"7⁰ = 1; 2⁻² = 1/2² = 1/4; (−3)² = (−3)(−3) = 9; −3² = −(3²) = −9 because only the 3 is squared; (1/2)⁻³ = 2³ = 8."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: 3x⁰ + (3x)⁰","en":"Simplify: 3x⁰ + (3x)⁰"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"3x + 1","en":"3x + 1"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In 3x⁰ is net die x tot die mag 0: 3 × 1 = 3. In (3x)⁰ is die hele hakie tot die mag 0: 1. Dus 3 + 1 = 4.","en":"In 3x⁰ only the x is to the power 0: 3 × 1 = 3. In (3x)⁰ the whole bracket is to the power 0: 1. So 3 + 1 = 4."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 2ˣ = 64. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 2ˣ = 64. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["6","x = 6"],"en":["6","x = 6"]},"explain":{"af":"64 = 2⁶, dus 2ˣ = 2⁶ en x = 6.","en":"64 = 2⁶, so 2ˣ = 2⁶ and x = 6."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2a³)⁴","en":"Simplify: (2a³)⁴"},"options":[{"af":"8a¹²","en":"8a¹²"},{"af":"2a¹²","en":"2a¹²"},{"af":"16a⁷","en":"16a⁷"},{"af":"16a¹²","en":"16a¹²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"(ab)ⁿ = aⁿbⁿ: 2⁴ × (a³)⁴ = 16a¹². Die 2 moet ook tot die mag 4 verhef word (2⁴ = 16, nie 2 × 4 = 8 nie), en by 'n mag van 'n mag vermenigvuldig jy die eksponente.","en":"(ab)ⁿ = aⁿbⁿ: 2⁴ × (a³)⁴ = 16a¹². The 2 must also be raised to the power 4 (2⁴ = 16, not 2 × 4 = 8), and for a power of a power you multiply the exponents."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 3ˣ⁺² = 81. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 3ˣ⁺² = 81. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["2","x = 2"],"en":["2","x = 2"]},"explain":{"af":"81 = 3⁴, dus 3ˣ⁺² = 3⁴. Stel die eksponente gelyk: x + 2 = 4, dus x = 2.","en":"81 = 3⁴, so 3ˣ⁺² = 3⁴. Equate the exponents: x + 2 = 4, so x = 2."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig en skryf met positiewe eksponente: (x⁻³y²)/(x²y⁻¹)","en":"Simplify and write with positive exponents: (x⁻³y²)/(x²y⁻¹)"},"options":[{"af":"y³/x⁵","en":"y³/x⁵"},{"af":"x⁵y³","en":"x⁵y³"},{"af":"y/x⁵","en":"y/x⁵"},{"af":"y³/x","en":"y³/x"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Trek die eksponente af: x⁻³⁻² = x⁻⁵ en y²⁻⁽⁻¹⁾ = y³. Dus x⁻⁵y³ = y³/x⁵. Let op: 2 − (−1) = 3, nie 1 nie.","en":"Subtract the exponents: x⁻³⁻² = x⁻⁵ and y²⁻⁽⁻¹⁾ = y³. So x⁻⁵y³ = y³/x⁵. Note: 2 − (−1) = 3, not 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die vergelyking 2ˣ = −8 het geen reële oplossing nie.","en":"The equation 2ˣ = −8 has no real solution."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 2ˣ is altyd positief, watter waarde x ook al het (selfs 2⁻³ = 1/8 is positief). Dit kan dus nooit −8 wees nie.","en":"True. 2ˣ is always positive, whatever the value of x (even 2⁻³ = 1/8 is positive). So it can never be −8."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/9. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/9. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","x = -3","x = −3"],"en":["-3","−3","x = -3","x = −3"]},"explain":{"af":"1/9 = 1/3² = 3⁻², dus x + 1 = −2 en x = −3.","en":"1/9 = 1/3² = 3⁻², so x + 1 = −2 and x = −3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (6ˣ × 9ˣ⁺¹)/(2ˣ × 27ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (6ˣ × 9ˣ⁺¹)/(2ˣ × 27ˣ)"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"1/9","en":"1/9"},{"af":"3ˣ⁺²","en":"3ˣ⁺²"},{"af":"9","en":"9"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Priemfaktore: 6ˣ = 2ˣ × 3ˣ, 9ˣ⁺¹ = 3²ˣ⁺² en 27ˣ = 3³ˣ. Teller: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ⁺²; noemer: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ. Antwoord: 3² = 9. As jy 9ˣ⁺¹ as 3²ˣ⁺¹ skryf, kry jy 3 – vermenigvuldig die hele eksponent met 2.","en":"Prime factors: 6ˣ = 2ˣ × 3ˣ, 9ˣ⁺¹ = 3²ˣ⁺² and 27ˣ = 3³ˣ. Numerator: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ⁺²; denominator: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ. Answer: 3² = 9. If you write 9ˣ⁺¹ as 3²ˣ⁺¹ you get 3 – multiply the whole exponent by 2."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ)"},"options":[{"af":"9/10","en":"9/10"},{"af":"1","en":"1"},{"af":"3ˣ⁺²/10","en":"3ˣ⁺²/10"},{"af":"10","en":"10"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Haal 3ˣ in die teller uit: 3ˣ(3² + 1) = 10 × 3ˣ. Dan (10 × 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ) = 1. Jy mag nie 3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ as een mag skryf nie, en die tweede term 3ˣ val nie weg nie.","en":"Take out 3ˣ in the numerator: 3ˣ(3² + 1) = 10 × 3ˣ. Then (10 × 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ) = 1. You may not write 3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ as one power, and the second term 3ˣ does not disappear."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 9ˣ⁻¹ = 27ˣ⁻³. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 9ˣ⁻¹ = 27ˣ⁻³. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["7","x = 7"],"en":["7","x = 7"]},"explain":{"af":"Skryf albei kante as magte van 3: (3²)ˣ⁻¹ = (3³)ˣ⁻³, dus 3²ˣ⁻² = 3³ˣ⁻⁹. Stel gelyk: 2x − 2 = 3x − 9, dus x = 7.","en":"Write both sides as powers of 3: (3²)ˣ⁻¹ = (3³)ˣ⁻³, so 3²ˣ⁻² = 3³ˣ⁻⁹. Equate: 2x − 2 = 3x − 9, so x = 7."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Video van Hoërskool Brits se wendrie word op WhatsApp gedeel. Die aantal mense wat dit gesien het, verdubbel elke 10 minute. Om 18:00 het 3 mense dit gesien. Hoeveel minute ná 18:00 het 96 mense dit gesien?","en":"A video of Hoërskool Brits's winning try is shared on WhatsApp. The number of people who have seen it doubles every 10 minutes. At 18:00, 3 people had seen it. How many minutes after 18:00 had 96 people seen it?"},"options":[{"af":"50 minute","en":"50 minutes"},{"af":"5 minute","en":"5 minutes"},{"af":"60 minute","en":"60 minutes"},{"af":"320 minute","en":"320 minutes"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ná n periodes van 10 minute het 3 × 2ⁿ mense dit gesien. 3 × 2ⁿ = 96, dus 2ⁿ = 32 = 2⁵ en n = 5. Vyf periodes × 10 minute = 50 minute. (3 → 6 → 12 → 24 → 48 → 96 is vyf verdubbelings, nie ses nie; en n = 5 is die aantal periodes, nie minute nie.)","en":"After n periods of 10 minutes, 3 × 2ⁿ people have seen it. 3 × 2ⁿ = 96, so 2ⁿ = 32 = 2⁵ and n = 5. Five periods × 10 minutes = 50 minutes. (3 → 6 → 12 → 24 → 48 → 96 is five doublings, not six; and n = 5 is the number of periods, not minutes.)"}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-getalpatrone","title":{"af":"Getalpatrone","en":"Number patterns"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die konstante verskil van 'n lineêre getalpatroon kan vind, die algemene term kan opstel en dit gebruik om enige term of die posisie van 'n term te bereken.","en":"You will be able to find the constant difference of a linear number pattern, set up the general term and use it to calculate any term or the position of a term."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n getalpatroon?\n\n'n **Getalpatroon** (of **ry**) is 'n lys getalle wat 'n vaste reël volg, bv. 3; 7; 11; 15; … Elke getal in die patroon is 'n **term**, en ons skryf kommapunte tussen die terme.\n\n- T_{1} is die eerste term, T_{2} die tweede term, ensovoorts.\n- **n** is die **posisie** van 'n term. n is altyd 'n natuurlike getal: n = 1; 2; 3; …\n- **T_{n}** is die **waarde** van die term in posisie n.\n\n> **Onthou!** n sê *waar* die term staan; T_{n} sê *wat* die term is. In 3; 7; 11; 15 is n = 3 en T_{3} = 11.\n\n## Konstante verskil en lineêre patrone\n\nTrek elke term van die **volgende** term af: d = T_{2} − T_{1} = T_{3} − T_{2} = T_{4} − T_{3}\n\nAs die verskil elke keer dieselfde is, het die patroon 'n **konstante verskil d** en is dit 'n **lineêre patroon**.\n\n| Ry | Verskille | Lineêr? |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3; 7; 11; 15; … | 4; 4; 4 | Ja, d = 4 |\n| 20; 17; 14; 11; … | −3; −3; −3 | Ja, d = −3 |\n| 2; 4; 8; 16; … | 2; 4; 8 | Nee, elke term verdubbel |\n| 1; 4; 9; 16; … | 3; 5; 7 | Nee, dit is kwadrate |\n\n- d > 0: die terme word groter (**stygende** patroon).\n- d < 0: die terme word kleiner (**dalende** patroon).\n- d kan ook 'n breuk of desimaal wees: 1; 2,5; 4; 5,5 het d = 1,5.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** d = T_{1} − T_{2} uitwerk. Dit gee die verkeerde teken. Werk altyd *latere term min vorige term*.\n\n## Die algemene term T_{n} = dn + c\n\nElke keer as n met 1 groter word, word d bygetel. Daarom is elke term d keer sy posisie plus 'n vaste getal c:\n\n**T_{n} = dn + c**\n\n1. Bereken d en kontroleer dat dit konstant is.\n2. Vind c: as n = 1, is T_{1} = d + c, dus **c = T_{1} − d**. Dink aan c as die \"nulde term\": die getal wat voor T_{1} sou kom.\n3. Skryf T_{n} = dn + c neer.\n4. Kontroleer met T_{2} of T_{3}.\n\nVir 3; 7; 11; 15; … is d = 4 en c = 3 − 4 = −1, dus T_{n} = 4n − 1. Kontrole: T_{3} = 4(3) − 1 = 11 ✓\n\nJy sal ook die vorm T_{n} = T_{1} + (n − 1)d sien. Dit gee presies dieselfde formule: 3 + (n − 1)(4) = 4n − 1.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** T_{n} = 4n + 3 skryf, m.a.w. die eerste term as c gebruik. Toets dit: 4(1) + 3 = 7, nie 3 nie!\n\n## Gebruik die algemene term\n\n**'n Term vind:** vervang n. Vir T_{n} = 4n − 1 is T_{50} = 4(50) − 1 = 199.\n\n**Die posisie vind:** stel T_{n} gelyk aan die gegewe waarde en los op vir n. Watter term is 143? 4n − 1 = 143, dus 4n = 144 en n = 36. Dit is T_{36}.\n\n**Is 'n getal 'n term?** Los T_{n} = getal op. Die getal is net 'n term as n 'n **natuurlike getal** is. Is 100 'n term? 4n − 1 = 100 gee n = 25,25, dus **nee**.\n\n**Eerste term groter as 'n waarde:** los die ongelykheid op en rond **op** na die volgende natuurlike getal. 4n − 1 > 100 gee n > 25,25, dus n = 26 en T_{26} = 103.\n\n**'n Ontbrekende term:** as a; b; c opeenvolgende terme van 'n lineêre patroon is, is b − a = c − b. Vir 5; x; 17 is x − 5 = 17 − x, dus x = 11.\n\n## Woordprobleme en patrone met figure\n\nIn woordprobleme is n die nommer van die figuur, week, ry of dag, en T_{n} die hoeveelheid (vuurhoutjies, stoele, rand). Skryf die eerste paar terme as 'n ry neer en werk dan soos hierbo.\n\nByvoorbeeld: vierkante van vuurhoutjies in 'n ry. Een vierkant het 4 vuurhoutjies nodig, twee vierkante 7 en drie vierkante 10. Die ry 4; 7; 10; … het d = 3, want elke nuwe vierkant deel een sy met die vorige een. Dus is T_{n} = 3n + 1 en 25 vierkante het 3(25) + 1 = 76 vuurhoutjies nodig.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** dink die patroon is direk eweredig: \"1 vierkant = 4, dus 25 vierkante = 100\". Dit werk net as c = 0.\n\n> **Wenk:** Antwoord altyd in die konteks, bv. \"Patroon 25 het 76 vuurhoutjies nodig\". As n 'n aantal mense, tafels of weke is, moet n 'n natuurlike getal wees.","en":"## What is a number pattern?\n\nA **number pattern** (or **sequence**) is a list of numbers that follows a fixed rule, e.g. 3; 7; 11; 15; … Each number in the pattern is a **term**, and we write semicolons between the terms.\n\n- T_{1} is the first term, T_{2} the second term, and so on.\n- **n** is the **position** of a term. n is always a natural number: n = 1; 2; 3; …\n- **T_{n}** is the **value** of the term in position n.\n\n> **Remember!** n tells you *where* the term is; T_{n} tells you *what* the term is. In 3; 7; 11; 15, n = 3 and T_{3} = 11.\n\n## Constant difference and linear patterns\n\nSubtract each term from the **next** term: d = T_{2} − T_{1} = T_{3} − T_{2} = T_{4} − T_{3}\n\nIf the difference is the same every time, the pattern has a **constant (common) difference d** and it is a **linear pattern**.\n\n| Sequence | Differences | Linear? |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3; 7; 11; 15; … | 4; 4; 4 | Yes, d = 4 |\n| 20; 17; 14; 11; … | −3; −3; −3 | Yes, d = −3 |\n| 2; 4; 8; 16; … | 2; 4; 8 | No, each term doubles |\n| 1; 4; 9; 16; … | 3; 5; 7 | No, these are squares |\n\n- d > 0: the terms get bigger (**increasing** pattern).\n- d < 0: the terms get smaller (**decreasing** pattern).\n- d can also be a fraction or decimal: 1; 2.5; 4; 5.5 has d = 1.5.\n\n> **Common mistake:** working out d = T_{1} − T_{2}. That gives the wrong sign. Always use *later term minus previous term*.\n\n## The general term T_{n} = dn + c\n\nEvery time n increases by 1, d is added. That is why every term is d times its position plus a fixed number c:\n\n**T_{n} = dn + c**\n\n1. Calculate d and check that it is constant.\n2. Find c: when n = 1, T_{1} = d + c, so **c = T_{1} − d**. Think of c as the \"zeroth term\": the number that would come before T_{1}.\n3. Write down T_{n} = dn + c.\n4. Check with T_{2} or T_{3}.\n\nFor 3; 7; 11; 15; … d = 4 and c = 3 − 4 = −1, so T_{n} = 4n − 1. Check: T_{3} = 4(3) − 1 = 11 ✓\n\nYou will also see the form T_{n} = T_{1} + (n − 1)d. It gives exactly the same formula: 3 + (n − 1)(4) = 4n − 1.\n\n> **Common mistake:** writing T_{n} = 4n + 3, i.e. using the first term as c. Test it: 4(1) + 3 = 7, not 3!\n\n## Using the general term\n\n**Finding a term:** substitute n. For T_{n} = 4n − 1, T_{50} = 4(50) − 1 = 199.\n\n**Finding the position:** set T_{n} equal to the given value and solve for n. Which term is 143? 4n − 1 = 143, so 4n = 144 and n = 36. It is T_{36}.\n\n**Is a number a term?** Solve T_{n} = number. The number is only a term if n is a **natural number**. Is 100 a term? 4n − 1 = 100 gives n = 25.25, so **no**.\n\n**First term greater than a value:** solve the inequality and round **up** to the next natural number. 4n − 1 > 100 gives n > 25.25, so n = 26 and T_{26} = 103.\n\n**A missing term:** if a; b; c are consecutive terms of a linear pattern, then b − a = c − b. For 5; x; 17, x − 5 = 17 − x, so x = 11.\n\n## Word problems and patterns with figures\n\nIn word problems n is the number of the figure, week, row or day, and T_{n} is the quantity (matches, chairs, rand). Write the first few terms as a sequence and then work as above.\n\nFor example: squares made of matches in a row. One square needs 4 matches, two squares need 7 and three squares need 10. The sequence 4; 7; 10; … has d = 3, because each new square shares one side with the previous one. So T_{n} = 3n + 1 and 25 squares need 3(25) + 1 = 76 matches.\n\n> **Common mistake:** thinking the pattern is directly proportional: \"1 square = 4, so 25 squares = 100\". That only works if c = 0.\n\n> **Tip:** Always answer in context, e.g. \"Pattern 25 needs 76 matches\". If n is a number of people, tables or weeks, n must be a natural number."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Getalpatroon (ry)","en":"Number pattern (sequence)"},"def":{"af":"'n Lys getalle wat 'n vaste reël volg, bv. 3; 7; 11; 15; …","en":"A list of numbers that follows a fixed rule, e.g. 3; 7; 11; 15; …"}},{"term":{"af":"Term","en":"Term"},"def":{"af":"Elke getal in 'n getalpatroon. T₁ is die eerste term, T₂ die tweede, ensovoorts.","en":"Each number in a number pattern. T₁ is the first term, T₂ the second, and so on."}},{"term":{"af":"Posisie (n)","en":"Position (n)"},"def":{"af":"Die plek van 'n term in die ry. n is altyd 'n natuurlike getal: 1; 2; 3; …","en":"The place of a term in the sequence. n is always a natural number: 1; 2; 3; …"}},{"term":{"af":"Konstante verskil (d)","en":"Constant difference (d)"},"def":{"af":"Die vaste getal wat elke keer bygetel word: d = T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂.","en":"The fixed number that is added each time: d = T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂."}},{"term":{"af":"Lineêre patroon","en":"Linear pattern"},"def":{"af":"'n Patroon met 'n konstante verskil tussen opeenvolgende terme. Die algemene term het die vorm Tₙ = dn + c.","en":"A pattern with a constant difference between consecutive terms. The general term has the form Tₙ = dn + c."}},{"term":{"af":"Algemene term (Tₙ)","en":"General term (Tₙ)"},"def":{"af":"'n Formule in terme van n waarmee jy enige term van die patroon kan bereken, bv. Tₙ = 4n − 1.","en":"A formula in terms of n with which you can calculate any term of the pattern, e.g. Tₙ = 4n − 1."}},{"term":{"af":"Opeenvolgende terme","en":"Consecutive terms"},"def":{"af":"Terme wat direk na mekaar in die ry volg, bv. T₃ en T₄.","en":"Terms that follow directly after each other in the sequence, e.g. T₃ and T₄."}},{"term":{"af":"Stygende en dalende patroon","en":"Increasing and decreasing pattern"},"def":{"af":"Stygend: die terme word groter (d > 0). Dalend: die terme word kleiner (d < 0).","en":"Increasing: the terms get bigger (d > 0). Decreasing: the terms get smaller (d < 0)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die algemene term en T₅₀","en":"The general term and T₅₀"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee die getalpatroon 5; 9; 13; 17; … (a) Bepaal die algemene term Tₙ. (b) Bereken T₅₀.","en":"Given the number pattern 5; 9; 13; 17; … (a) Determine the general term Tₙ. (b) Calculate T₅₀."},"steps":[{"af":"Bereken die verskille: 9 − 5 = 4; 13 − 9 = 4; 17 − 13 = 4. Die konstante verskil is d = 4, dus is die patroon lineêr.","en":"Calculate the differences: 9 − 5 = 4; 13 − 9 = 4; 17 − 13 = 4. The constant difference is d = 4, so the pattern is linear."},{"af":"Vind c: c = T_{1} − d = 5 − 4 = 1","en":"Find c: c = T_{1} − d = 5 − 4 = 1"},{"af":"(a) T_{n} = 4n + 1. Kontrole: T_{2} = 4(2) + 1 = 9 ✓","en":"(a) T_{n} = 4n + 1. Check: T_{2} = 4(2) + 1 = 9 ✓"},{"af":"(b) T_{50} = 4(50) + 1 = 200 + 1 = 201","en":"(b) T_{50} = 4(50) + 1 = 200 + 1 = 201"}],"answer":{"af":"Tₙ = 4n + 1; T₅₀ = 201","en":"Tₙ = 4n + 1; T₅₀ = 201"}},{"title":{"af":"Dalende patroon: vind die posisie","en":"Decreasing pattern: find the position"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee die getalpatroon 23; 17; 11; 5; … Bepaal die algemene term en bepaal watter term gelyk is aan −151.","en":"Given the number pattern 23; 17; 11; 5; … Determine the general term and determine which term is equal to −151."},"steps":[{"af":"d = 17 − 23 = −6 (kontroleer: 11 − 17 = −6 ✓). Die patroon daal, dus is d negatief.","en":"d = 17 − 23 = −6 (check: 11 − 17 = −6 ✓). The pattern decreases, so d is negative."},{"af":"c = T_{1} − d = 23 − (−6) = 29, dus T_{n} = −6n + 29","en":"c = T_{1} − d = 23 − (−6) = 29, so T_{n} = −6n + 29"},{"af":"Stel T_{n} = −151: −6n + 29 = −151","en":"Set T_{n} = −151: −6n + 29 = −151"},{"af":"−6n = −180, dus n = 30","en":"−6n = −180, so n = 30"},{"af":"Kontrole: T_{30} = −6(30) + 29 = −180 + 29 = −151 ✓","en":"Check: T_{30} = −6(30) + 29 = −180 + 29 = −151 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"Tₙ = −6n + 29; −151 is die 30ste term (T₃₀).","en":"Tₙ = −6n + 29; −151 is the 30th term (T₃₀)."}},{"title":{"af":"Is 100 'n term?","en":"Is 100 a term?"},"problem":{"af":"Is 100 'n term van die patroon 4; 11; 18; 25; …? Indien nie, bepaal die eerste term wat groter as 100 is.","en":"Is 100 a term of the pattern 4; 11; 18; 25; …? If not, determine the first term that is greater than 100."},"steps":[{"af":"d = 11 − 4 = 7 en c = 4 − 7 = −3, dus T_{n} = 7n − 3","en":"d = 11 − 4 = 7 and c = 4 − 7 = −3, so T_{n} = 7n − 3"},{"af":"Stel 7n − 3 = 100: 7n = 103, dus n = [[103/7]] ≈ 14,71","en":"Set 7n − 3 = 100: 7n = 103, so n = [[103/7]] ≈ 14.71"},{"af":"n is nie 'n natuurlike getal nie, dus is 100 NIE 'n term nie.","en":"n is not a natural number, so 100 is NOT a term."},{"af":"Vir T_{n} > 100: 7n − 3 > 100, dus n > 14,71. Die kleinste natuurlike getal is n = 15.","en":"For T_{n} > 100: 7n − 3 > 100, so n > 14.71. The smallest natural number is n = 15."},{"af":"T_{15} = 7(15) − 3 = 102. (Kontrole: T_{14} = 95 is nog kleiner as 100.)","en":"T_{15} = 7(15) − 3 = 102. (Check: T_{14} = 95 is still less than 100.)"}],"answer":{"af":"100 is nie 'n term nie; die eerste term groter as 100 is T₁₅ = 102.","en":"100 is not a term; the first term greater than 100 is T₁₅ = 102."}},{"title":{"af":"Woordprobleem: tafels by 'n braai","en":"Word problem: tables at a braai"},"problem":{"af":"By 'n braai by Hartbeespoortdam word vierkantige tafels in 'n lang ry teen mekaar geskuif. Een tafel sit 4 mense, twee tafels sit 6 mense en drie tafels sit 8 mense. (a) Bepaal 'n formule vir die aantal mense wat by n tafels kan sit. (b) Hoeveel mense kan by 25 tafels sit? (c) Hoeveel tafels is nodig vir presies 40 gaste?","en":"At a braai at Hartbeespoort Dam square tables are pushed together in a long row. One table seats 4 people, two tables seat 6 people and three tables seat 8 people. (a) Determine a formula for the number of people who can sit at n tables. (b) How many people can sit at 25 tables? (c) How many tables are needed for exactly 40 guests?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die ry is 4; 6; 8; … met d = 2. Elke ekstra tafel voeg net 2 plekke by, want waar twee tafels raak, kan niemand sit nie.","en":"The sequence is 4; 6; 8; … with d = 2. Each extra table only adds 2 places, because nobody can sit where two tables touch."},{"af":"(a) c = T_{1} − d = 4 − 2 = 2, dus T_{n} = 2n + 2","en":"(a) c = T_{1} − d = 4 − 2 = 2, so T_{n} = 2n + 2"},{"af":"(b) T_{25} = 2(25) + 2 = 52 mense","en":"(b) T_{25} = 2(25) + 2 = 52 people"},{"af":"(c) 2n + 2 = 40, dus 2n = 38 en n = 19 tafels","en":"(c) 2n + 2 = 40, so 2n = 38 and n = 19 tables"},{"af":"Kontrole: 2(19) + 2 = 40 ✓","en":"Check: 2(19) + 2 = 40 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"Tₙ = 2n + 2; 25 tafels sit 52 mense; 40 gaste het 19 tafels nodig.","en":"Tₙ = 2n + 2; 25 tables seat 52 people; 40 guests need 19 tables."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die ry 2; 4; 8; 16; … is 'n lineêre getalpatroon.","en":"The sequence 2; 4; 8; 16; … is a linear number pattern."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die verskille is 2; 4; 8 – nie konstant nie. Elke term word verdubbel, dus is die patroon nie lineêr nie.","en":"False. The differences are 2; 4; 8 – not constant. Each term is doubled, so the pattern is not linear."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die konstante verskil van die ry 7; 12; 17; 22; …?","en":"What is the constant difference of the sequence 7; 12; 17; 22; …?"},"options":[{"af":"−5","en":"−5"},{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"2","en":"2"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"d = 12 − 7 = 5 (en 17 − 12 = 5). −5 kry jy as jy die vorige term min die volgende term doen, 7 is die eerste term en 2 is c in Tₙ = 5n + 2.","en":"d = 12 − 7 = 5 (and 17 − 12 = 5). You get −5 if you do the previous term minus the next term, 7 is the first term and 2 is c in Tₙ = 5n + 2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die volgende term van die ry 31; 27; 23; 19; … neer: ___","en":"Write down the next term of the sequence 31; 27; 23; 19; …: ___"},"answers":{"af":["15","T5 = 15","T₅ = 15"],"en":["15","T5 = 15","T₅ = 15"]},"explain":{"af":"Die konstante verskil is d = 27 − 31 = −4, dus is die volgende term 19 − 4 = 15.","en":"The constant difference is d = 27 − 31 = −4, so the next term is 19 − 4 = 15."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke simbool in Tₙ = dn + c by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each symbol in Tₙ = dn + c to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"n","en":"n"},"r":{"af":"die posisie van die term (1; 2; 3; …)","en":"the position of the term (1; 2; 3; …)"}},{"l":{"af":"Tₙ","en":"Tₙ"},"r":{"af":"die waarde van die term in posisie n","en":"the value of the term in position n"}},{"l":{"af":"d","en":"d"},"r":{"af":"die konstante verskil, T₂ − T₁","en":"the constant difference, T₂ − T₁"}},{"l":{"af":"c","en":"c"},"r":{"af":"T₁ − d, die \"nulde term\"","en":"T₁ − d, the \"zeroth term\""}}],"explain":{"af":"n is waar die term staan, Tₙ is wat die term is, d word elke keer bygetel en c = T₁ − d.","en":"n is where the term is, Tₙ is what the term is, d is added every time and c = T₁ − d."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die algemene term van die ry 5; 8; 11; 14; …?","en":"What is the general term of the sequence 5; 8; 11; 14; …?"},"options":[{"af":"Tₙ = 3n + 5","en":"Tₙ = 3n + 5"},{"af":"Tₙ = 2n + 3","en":"Tₙ = 2n + 3"},{"af":"Tₙ = 3n − 2","en":"Tₙ = 3n − 2"},{"af":"Tₙ = 3n + 2","en":"Tₙ = 3n + 2"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"d = 3 en c = T₁ − d = 5 − 3 = 2, dus Tₙ = 3n + 2. Kontrole: T₁ = 3 + 2 = 5 ✓. Tₙ = 3n + 5 gebruik die eerste term as c (dan is T₁ = 8), en 3n − 2 het die teken van c verkeerd.","en":"d = 3 and c = T₁ − d = 5 − 3 = 2, so Tₙ = 3n + 2. Check: T₁ = 3 + 2 = 5 ✓. Tₙ = 3n + 5 uses the first term as c (then T₁ = 8), and 3n − 2 has the wrong sign for c."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gegee Tₙ = 4n − 7. Bereken T₂₀ = ___","en":"Given Tₙ = 4n − 7. Calculate T₂₀ = ___"},"answers":{"af":["73","T20 = 73","T₂₀ = 73"],"en":["73","T20 = 73","T₂₀ = 73"]},"explain":{"af":"Vervang n = 20: T₂₀ = 4(20) − 7 = 80 − 7 = 73.","en":"Substitute n = 20: T₂₀ = 4(20) − 7 = 80 − 7 = 73."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die algemene term van 'n patroon is Tₙ = −3n + 20. Wat is die eerste drie terme?","en":"The general term of a pattern is Tₙ = −3n + 20. What are the first three terms?"},"options":[{"af":"17; 14; 11","en":"17; 14; 11"},{"af":"20; 17; 14","en":"20; 17; 14"},{"af":"23; 26; 29","en":"23; 26; 29"},{"af":"−3; −6; −9","en":"−3; −6; −9"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vervang n = 1; 2; 3: −3(1) + 20 = 17, −3(2) + 20 = 14, −3(3) + 20 = 11. 20; 17; 14 begin by n = 0, maar n begin altyd by 1.","en":"Substitute n = 1; 2; 3: −3(1) + 20 = 17, −3(2) + 20 = 14, −3(3) + 20 = 11. 20; 17; 14 starts at n = 0, but n always starts at 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"100 is 'n term van die ry 2; 9; 16; 23; …","en":"100 is a term of the sequence 2; 9; 16; 23; …"},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. d = 7 en c = 2 − 7 = −5, dus Tₙ = 7n − 5. 7n − 5 = 100 gee 7n = 105 en n = 15 – 'n natuurlike getal. 100 is T₁₅.","en":"True. d = 7 and c = 2 − 7 = −5, so Tₙ = 7n − 5. 7n − 5 = 100 gives 7n = 105 and n = 15 – a natural number. 100 is T₁₅."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter term van die ry 6; 10; 14; 18; … is gelyk aan 126?","en":"Which term of the sequence 6; 10; 14; 18; … is equal to 126?"},"options":[{"af":"T₃₀","en":"T₃₀"},{"af":"T₃₁","en":"T₃₁"},{"af":"T₃₂","en":"T₃₂"},{"af":"T₁₂₄","en":"T₁₂₄"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Tₙ = 4n + 2. Stel 4n + 2 = 126: 4n = 124 en n = 31. T₃₀ kom van Tₙ = 4n + 6 (eerste term as c), T₃₂ van 'n tekenfout in c, en T₁₂₄ as jy vergeet om deur 4 te deel.","en":"Tₙ = 4n + 2. Set 4n + 2 = 126: 4n = 124 and n = 31. T₃₀ comes from Tₙ = 4n + 6 (first term as c), T₃₂ from a sign error in c, and T₁₂₄ if you forget to divide by 4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken T₂₅ van die ry −8; −5; −2; 1; …","en":"Calculate T₂₅ of the sequence −8; −5; −2; 1; …"},"options":[{"af":"67","en":"67"},{"af":"−80","en":"−80"},{"af":"64","en":"64"},{"af":"70","en":"70"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"d = −5 − (−8) = 3 en c = −8 − 3 = −11, dus Tₙ = 3n − 11 en T₂₅ = 75 − 11 = 64. 67 gebruik −8 as c, 70 het −8 + 3 = −5 as c, en −80 het d = −3 (verkeerde volgorde van aftrek).","en":"d = −5 − (−8) = 3 and c = −8 − 3 = −11, so Tₙ = 3n − 11 and T₂₅ = 75 − 11 = 64. 67 uses −8 as c, 70 has −8 + 3 = −5 as c, and −80 has d = −3 (subtracting in the wrong order)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die eerste term van die ry 3; 10; 17; 24; … wat groter as 200 is?","en":"What is the first term of the sequence 3; 10; 17; 24; … that is greater than 200?"},"options":[{"af":"199","en":"199"},{"af":"203","en":"203"},{"af":"213","en":"213"},{"af":"206","en":"206"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Tₙ = 7n − 4. 7n − 4 > 200 gee n > 29,14, dus n = 30 en T₃₀ = 7(30) − 4 = 206. 199 is T₂₉ (nog kleiner as 200), en 203 = 7 × 29 sonder die c.","en":"Tₙ = 7n − 4. 7n − 4 > 200 gives n > 29.14, so n = 30 and T₃₀ = 7(30) − 4 = 206. 199 is T₂₉ (still less than 200), and 203 = 7 × 29 without the c."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"2x + 1; 5x − 2 en 6x + 3 is die eerste drie terme van 'n lineêre getalpatroon. Bepaal x. x = ___","en":"2x + 1; 5x − 2 and 6x + 3 are the first three terms of a linear number pattern. Determine x. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["4","x = 4"],"en":["4","x = 4"]},"explain":{"af":"In 'n lineêre patroon is T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂: (5x − 2) − (2x + 1) = (6x + 3) − (5x − 2), dus 3x − 3 = x + 5, 2x = 8 en x = 4. Die terme is 9; 18; 27 met d = 9 ✓.","en":"In a linear pattern T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂: (5x − 2) − (2x + 1) = (6x + 3) − (5x − 2), so 3x − 3 = x + 5, 2x = 8 and x = 4. The terms are 9; 18; 27 with d = 9 ✓."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Seshoeke word van vuurhoutjies in 'n ry gebou, en elke nuwe seshoek deel een sy met die vorige een. Patroon 1 (een seshoek) het 6 vuurhoutjies, patroon 2 het 11 en patroon 3 het 16. Hoeveel vuurhoutjies het patroon 40 nodig?","en":"Hexagons are built from matches in a row, and each new hexagon shares one side with the previous one. Pattern 1 (one hexagon) has 6 matches, pattern 2 has 11 and pattern 3 has 16. How many matches does pattern 40 need?"},"options":[{"af":"240","en":"240"},{"af":"201","en":"201"},{"af":"206","en":"206"},{"af":"200","en":"200"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die ry 6; 11; 16; … het d = 5 en c = 6 − 5 = 1, dus Tₙ = 5n + 1 en T₄₀ = 201. 240 = 6 × 40 neem aan die patroon is eweredig (maar seshoeke deel sye), en 206 gebruik die eerste term as c.","en":"The sequence 6; 11; 16; … has d = 5 and c = 6 − 5 = 1, so Tₙ = 5n + 1 and T₄₀ = 201. 240 = 6 × 40 assumes the pattern is proportional (but hexagons share sides), and 206 uses the first term as c."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sipho het aan die einde van week 1 R5 in sy spaarpot en sit elke week R4 by. Anja het aan die einde van week 1 R96, maar spandeer elke week R3 aan selfoondata. Aan die einde van watter week het hulle presies ewe veel geld? Week ___","en":"Sipho has R5 in his money box at the end of week 1 and adds R4 every week. Anja has R96 at the end of week 1, but spends R3 on cellphone data every week. At the end of which week do they have exactly the same amount of money? Week ___"},"answers":{"af":["14","week 14","n = 14","T14"],"en":["14","week 14","n = 14","T14"]},"explain":{"af":"Sipho: 5; 9; 13; … dus Tₙ = 4n + 1. Anja: 96; 93; 90; … dus Tₙ = −3n + 99. Stel gelyk: 4n + 1 = −3n + 99, dus 7n = 98 en n = 14. In week 14 het albei R57.","en":"Sipho: 5; 9; 13; … so Tₙ = 4n + 1. Anja: 96; 93; 90; … so Tₙ = −3n + 99. Set equal: 4n + 1 = −3n + 99, so 7n = 98 and n = 14. In week 14 both have R57."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-vergelykings","title":{"af":"Vergelykings","en":"Equations"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal lineêre vergelykings (ook met breuke), kwadratiese vergelykings, letterlike vergelykings en gelyktydige vergelykings kan oplos en dit in woordprobleme kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to solve linear equations (including fractions), quadratic equations, literal equations and simultaneous equations, and use them in word problems."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat beteken \"los op\"?\n\n'n **Vergelyking** sê dat twee uitdrukkings gelyk is, bv. 3x − 4 = 11. Om dit **op te los**, vind jy die waarde(s) van die veranderlike wat die **linkerkant (LK)** gelyk maak aan die **regterkant (RK)**. Die goue reël: **wat jy aan die een kant doen, doen jy ook aan die ander kant.** Kontroleer jou antwoord deur dit in die oorspronklike vergelyking te vervang.\n\n## Lineêre vergelykings\n\nDie hoogste mag van x is 1, dus is daar **een** oplossing.\n\n1. Verwyder hakies. Pas op vir 'n minus voor 'n hakie: −3(x − 1) = −3x + 3.\n2. Verwyder breuke: vermenigvuldig **elke term** aan **albei** kante met die **KGV** van die noemers.\n3. Bring die x-terme na een kant en die getalle na die ander kant.\n4. Deel deur die koëffisiënt van x.\n\nVoorbeeld: [[x/2]] + [[x−1/3]] = 3. Die KGV is 6: 3x + 2(x − 1) = 18, dus 5x − 2 = 18, 5x = 20 en x = 4.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** net die breuke met die KGV vermenigvuldig en die RK vergeet. *Elke* term, ook die getal aan die ander kant, word vermenigvuldig.\n\n**Veranderlike in die noemer:** skryf eers die **beperking** neer, want 'n noemer mag nooit 0 wees nie. Vir [[3/x−2]] = 1 is x ≠ 2. Vermenigvuldig met (x − 2): 3 = x − 2, dus x = 5. As jou antwoord 'n beperkte waarde is, is daar **geen oplossing** nie.\n\n## Kwadratiese vergelykings\n\nDie hoogste mag van x is 2, dus is daar **hoogstens twee** oplossings. Ons los dit op deur te faktoriseer.\n\n1. Skryf in **standaardvorm** ax^{2} + bx + c = 0. Een kant **moet 0** wees.\n2. Faktoriseer: gemene faktor, verskil van twee vierkante of drieterm.\n3. Gebruik die **nulproduk-reël**: as A × B = 0, dan is A = 0 **of** B = 0.\n4. Los elke faktor op.\n\nVoorbeeld: x^{2} − x − 12 = 0, dus (x − 4)(x + 3) = 0 en x = 4 of x = −3.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** x^{2} = 5x deur x deel. Dan verloor jy die oplossing x = 0! Skryf eerder x^{2} − 5x = 0, dus x(x − 5) = 0 en x = 0 of x = 5.\n\n- x^{2} = 9 gee x = **±3** (x = 3 of x = −3), want (−3)^{2} = 9 ook.\n- (x − 2)(x + 1) = 4 beteken **nie** x − 2 = 4 nie. Die nulproduk-reël werk net as die een kant 0 is. Vermenigvuldig uit en maak een kant 0: x^{2} − x − 6 = 0, dus (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 en x = 3 of x = −2.\n\n## Letterlike vergelykings\n\n'n **Letterlike vergelyking** bevat meer as een letter, soos 'n formule. \"Maak a die **onderwerp**\" beteken: kry a alleen aan een kant van die gelykaanteken. Gebruik presies dieselfde stappe as vir 'n gewone vergelyking.\n\n- v = u + at, dus v − u = at en a = [[v−u/t]]\n- As die onderwerp **twee keer** voorkom, bring albei terme na een kant en **haal dit as gemene faktor uit**: ax + 3 = bx + 7, dus ax − bx = 4, x(a − b) = 4 en x = [[4/a−b]] (a ≠ b).\n\n## Gelyktydige vergelykings\n\nTwee vergelykings met twee onbekendes, x en y. Die oplossing is die **paar** (x; y) wat **albei** vergelykings waar maak.\n\n**Vervangingsmetode:** maak een veranderlike die onderwerp van een vergelyking en vervang dit in die ander. Vir y = 2x − 1 en 3x + y = 9: 3x + (2x − 1) = 9, dus 5x = 10, x = 2 en y = 2(2) − 1 = 3.\n\n**Eliminasiemetode:** maak die koëffisiënte van een veranderlike dieselfde (of teenoorgesteld) en trek die vergelykings van mekaar af (of tel hulle op). Vir x + y = 10 en x − y = 4: tel op, 2x = 14, dus x = 7 en y = 3.\n\n**Grafiese idee:** elke lineêre vergelyking is 'n reguit lyn. Die oplossing is die **snypunt** van die twee lyne. Ewewydige lyne (dieselfde gradiënt, ander y-afsnit) sny nooit nie, dus is daar dan **geen oplossing** nie.\n\n> **Wenk:** Kontroleer (x; y) in **albei** oorspronklike vergelykings, nie net in die een wat jy laaste gebruik het nie.\n\n## Woordprobleme\n\n1. Definieer die onbekende(s), bv. \"Laat x = die breedte in meter\".\n2. Vertaal die woorde in 'n vergelyking: \"is\" beteken =, \"3 meer as\" beteken + 3, \"twee keer so oud\" beteken × 2.\n3. Los op.\n4. Antwoord in 'n volsin met eenhede en kyk of dit sin maak. 'n Lengte, ouderdom of aantal kan nie negatief wees nie, dus word 'n negatiewe oplossing **verwerp**.\n\nAlgemene tipes: ouderdomme, opeenvolgende getalle (x; x + 1; x + 2), kaartjies en geld (gelyktydige vergelykings), en die oppervlakte van 'n reghoek (gee dikwels 'n kwadratiese vergelyking).","en":"## What does \"solve\" mean?\n\nAn **equation** says that two expressions are equal, e.g. 3x − 4 = 11. To **solve** it, you find the value(s) of the variable that make the **left-hand side (LHS)** equal to the **right-hand side (RHS)**. The golden rule: **whatever you do to one side, you also do to the other side.** Check your answer by substituting it into the original equation.\n\n## Linear equations\n\nThe highest power of x is 1, so there is **one** solution.\n\n1. Remove brackets. Watch out for a minus in front of a bracket: −3(x − 1) = −3x + 3.\n2. Remove fractions: multiply **every term** on **both** sides by the **LCM** of the denominators.\n3. Bring the x-terms to one side and the numbers to the other side.\n4. Divide by the coefficient of x.\n\nExample: [[x/2]] + [[x−1/3]] = 3. The LCM is 6: 3x + 2(x − 1) = 18, so 5x − 2 = 18, 5x = 20 and x = 4.\n\n> **Common mistake:** multiplying only the fractions by the LCM and forgetting the RHS. *Every* term, including the number on the other side, is multiplied.\n\n**Variable in the denominator:** first write down the **restriction**, because a denominator may never be 0. For [[3/x−2]] = 1, x ≠ 2. Multiply by (x − 2): 3 = x − 2, so x = 5. If your answer is a restricted value, there is **no solution**.\n\n## Quadratic equations\n\nThe highest power of x is 2, so there are **at most two** solutions. We solve them by factorising.\n\n1. Write in **standard form** ax^{2} + bx + c = 0. One side **must be 0**.\n2. Factorise: common factor, difference of two squares or trinomial.\n3. Use the **zero product rule**: if A × B = 0, then A = 0 **or** B = 0.\n4. Solve each factor.\n\nExample: x^{2} − x − 12 = 0, so (x − 4)(x + 3) = 0 and x = 4 or x = −3.\n\n> **Common mistake:** dividing x^{2} = 5x by x. Then you lose the solution x = 0! Rather write x^{2} − 5x = 0, so x(x − 5) = 0 and x = 0 or x = 5.\n\n- x^{2} = 9 gives x = **±3** (x = 3 or x = −3), because (−3)^{2} = 9 too.\n- (x − 2)(x + 1) = 4 does **not** mean x − 2 = 4. The zero product rule only works when one side is 0. Multiply out and make one side 0: x^{2} − x − 6 = 0, so (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 and x = 3 or x = −2.\n\n## Literal equations\n\nA **literal equation** contains more than one letter, like a formula. \"Make a the **subject**\" means: get a on its own on one side of the equals sign. Use exactly the same steps as for an ordinary equation.\n\n- v = u + at, so v − u = at and a = [[v−u/t]]\n- If the subject appears **twice**, bring both terms to one side and **take it out as a common factor**: ax + 3 = bx + 7, so ax − bx = 4, x(a − b) = 4 and x = [[4/a−b]] (a ≠ b).\n\n## Simultaneous equations\n\nTwo equations with two unknowns, x and y. The solution is the **pair** (x; y) that makes **both** equations true.\n\n**Substitution method:** make one variable the subject of one equation and substitute it into the other. For y = 2x − 1 and 3x + y = 9: 3x + (2x − 1) = 9, so 5x = 10, x = 2 and y = 2(2) − 1 = 3.\n\n**Elimination method:** make the coefficients of one variable the same (or opposite) and subtract the equations (or add them). For x + y = 10 and x − y = 4: add, 2x = 14, so x = 7 and y = 3.\n\n**Graphical idea:** every linear equation is a straight line. The solution is the **point of intersection** of the two lines. Parallel lines (same gradient, different y-intercept) never intersect, so then there is **no solution**.\n\n> **Tip:** Check (x; y) in **both** original equations, not just in the one you used last.\n\n## Word problems\n\n1. Define the unknown(s), e.g. \"Let x = the width in metres\".\n2. Translate the words into an equation: \"is\" means =, \"3 more than\" means + 3, \"twice as old\" means × 2.\n3. Solve.\n4. Answer in a full sentence with units and check that it makes sense. A length, age or number of items cannot be negative, so a negative solution is **rejected**.\n\nCommon types: ages, consecutive numbers (x; x + 1; x + 2), tickets and money (simultaneous equations), and the area of a rectangle (often gives a quadratic equation)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Vergelyking","en":"Equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Wiskundige sin wat sê dat twee uitdrukkings gelyk is, bv. 3x − 4 = 11.","en":"A mathematical sentence that says two expressions are equal, e.g. 3x − 4 = 11."}},{"term":{"af":"Oplossing (wortel)","en":"Solution (root)"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde van die veranderlike wat die LK gelyk maak aan die RK.","en":"A value of the variable that makes the LHS equal to the RHS."}},{"term":{"af":"Lineêre vergelyking","en":"Linear equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking waarin die hoogste mag van die veranderlike 1 is. Dit het een oplossing.","en":"An equation in which the highest power of the variable is 1. It has one solution."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwadratiese vergelyking","en":"Quadratic equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking waarin die hoogste mag van die veranderlike 2 is, bv. x² − 5x + 6 = 0. Dit het hoogstens twee oplossings.","en":"An equation in which the highest power of the variable is 2, e.g. x² − 5x + 6 = 0. It has at most two solutions."}},{"term":{"af":"Nulproduk-reël","en":"Zero product rule"},"def":{"af":"As A × B = 0, dan is A = 0 of B = 0. Werk net as een kant van die vergelyking 0 is.","en":"If A × B = 0, then A = 0 or B = 0. Only works if one side of the equation is 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Letterlike vergelyking","en":"Literal equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking of formule met meer as een letter, bv. v = u + at.","en":"An equation or formula with more than one letter, e.g. v = u + at."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp van 'n formule","en":"Subject of a formula"},"def":{"af":"Die veranderlike wat alleen aan een kant van die gelykaanteken staan, bv. a in a = (v − u)/t.","en":"The variable that stands alone on one side of the equals sign, e.g. a in a = (v − u)/t."}},{"term":{"af":"Gelyktydige vergelykings","en":"Simultaneous equations"},"def":{"af":"Twee vergelykings met dieselfde twee onbekendes wat terselfdertyd waar moet wees. Die oplossing is 'n paar (x; y).","en":"Two equations with the same two unknowns that must be true at the same time. The solution is a pair (x; y)."}},{"term":{"af":"Beperking","en":"Restriction"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde wat die veranderlike nie mag hê nie, omdat 'n noemer dan 0 sou wees, bv. x ≠ 2.","en":"A value the variable may not take, because a denominator would then be 0, e.g. x ≠ 2."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lineêre vergelyking met breuke","en":"Linear equation with fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x: (x + 2)/3 − (x − 1)/4 = 2","en":"Solve for x: (x + 2)/3 − (x − 1)/4 = 2"},"steps":[{"af":"Die KGV van 3 en 4 is 12. Vermenigvuldig elke term met 12: 12 × [[x+2/3]] − 12 × [[x−1/4]] = 12 × 2","en":"The LCM of 3 and 4 is 12. Multiply every term by 12: 12 × [[x+2/3]] − 12 × [[x−1/4]] = 12 × 2"},{"af":"4(x + 2) − 3(x − 1) = 24","en":"4(x + 2) − 3(x − 1) = 24"},{"af":"Verwyder hakies – pas op vir die minus voor die tweede hakie: 4x + 8 − 3x + 3 = 24","en":"Remove brackets – watch the minus in front of the second bracket: 4x + 8 − 3x + 3 = 24"},{"af":"x + 11 = 24, dus x = 13","en":"x + 11 = 24, so x = 13"},{"af":"Kontrole: LK = [[15/3]] − [[12/4]] = 5 − 3 = 2 = RK ✓","en":"Check: LHS = [[15/3]] − [[12/4]] = 5 − 3 = 2 = RHS ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"x = 13","en":"x = 13"}},{"title":{"af":"Kwadratiese vergelyking deur faktorisering","en":"Quadratic equation by factorisation"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x: 2x² − 5x = 3","en":"Solve for x: 2x² − 5x = 3"},"steps":[{"af":"Maak een kant 0: 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 = 0","en":"Make one side 0: 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 = 0"},{"af":"Faktoriseer die drieterm: (2x + 1)(x − 3) = 0. Kontrole: 2x^{2} − 6x + x − 3 = 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 ✓","en":"Factorise the trinomial: (2x + 1)(x − 3) = 0. Check: 2x^{2} − 6x + x − 3 = 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 ✓"},{"af":"Nulproduk-reël: 2x + 1 = 0 of x − 3 = 0","en":"Zero product rule: 2x + 1 = 0 or x − 3 = 0"},{"af":"x = −[[1/2]] of x = 3","en":"x = −[[1/2]] or x = 3"}],"answer":{"af":"x = −½ of x = 3","en":"x = −½ or x = 3"}},{"title":{"af":"Letterlike vergelyking: verander die onderwerp","en":"Literal equation: change the subject"},"problem":{"af":"Maak i die onderwerp van die formule A = P(1 + in).","en":"Make i the subject of the formula A = P(1 + in)."},"steps":[{"af":"Vermenigvuldig uit: A = P + Pin","en":"Multiply out: A = P + Pin"},{"af":"Trek P aan albei kante af: A − P = Pin","en":"Subtract P on both sides: A − P = Pin"},{"af":"Deel albei kante deur Pn: i = [[A−P/Pn]]","en":"Divide both sides by Pn: i = [[A−P/Pn]]"},{"af":"Kontrole met getalle: as P = 1 000, n = 2 en i = 0,1, is A = 1 000(1 + 0,2) = 1 200. Dan is A − P = 200 en Pn = 2 000, dus i = [[200/2 000]] = 0,1 ✓","en":"Check with numbers: if P = 1 000, n = 2 and i = 0.1, then A = 1 000(1 + 0.2) = 1 200. Then A − P = 200 and Pn = 2 000, so i = [[200/2 000]] = 0.1 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"i = (A − P)/(Pn)","en":"i = (A − P)/(Pn)"}},{"title":{"af":"Gelyktydige vergelykings: rugbykaartjies","en":"Simultaneous equations: rugby tickets"},"problem":{"af":"By 'n rugbywedstryd op Brits kos 'n kaartjie vir 'n volwassene R x en vir 'n kind R y. Die Botha-gesin betaal R190 vir 3 volwassene- en 2 kinderkaartjies. Die Mokoena-gesin betaal R180 vir 2 volwassene- en 4 kinderkaartjies. Bepaal die prys van elke soort kaartjie.","en":"At a rugby match in Brits a ticket costs R x for an adult and R y for a child. The Botha family pays R190 for 3 adult and 2 child tickets. The Mokoena family pays R180 for 2 adult and 4 child tickets. Determine the price of each type of ticket."},"steps":[{"af":"Stel die vergelykings op: 3x + 2y = 190 … (1) en 2x + 4y = 180 … (2)","en":"Set up the equations: 3x + 2y = 190 … (1) and 2x + 4y = 180 … (2)"},{"af":"Deel (2) deur 2: x + 2y = 90 … (3)","en":"Divide (2) by 2: x + 2y = 90 … (3)"},{"af":"Eliminasie, (1) − (3): 2x = 100, dus x = 50","en":"Elimination, (1) − (3): 2x = 100, so x = 50"},{"af":"Vervang in (3): 50 + 2y = 90, dus 2y = 40 en y = 20","en":"Substitute into (3): 50 + 2y = 90, so 2y = 40 and y = 20"},{"af":"Kontrole in (2): 2(50) + 4(20) = 100 + 80 = 180 ✓. Grafies sou die twee lyne by (50; 20) sny.","en":"Check in (2): 2(50) + 4(20) = 100 + 80 = 180 ✓. Graphically the two lines would intersect at (50; 20)."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Volwassene se kaartjie kos R50 en 'n kind s'n R20.","en":"An adult ticket costs R50 and a child ticket R20."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die oplossing van x² = 25 is slegs x = 5.","en":"The solution of x² = 25 is only x = 5."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. x² − 25 = 0 gee (x − 5)(x + 5) = 0, dus x = 5 of x = −5, want (−5)² = 25 ook.","en":"False. x² − 25 = 0 gives (x − 5)(x + 5) = 0, so x = 5 or x = −5, because (−5)² = 25 too."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelsel vergelykings het GEEN oplossing nie?","en":"Which system of equations has NO solution?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 2x + 1 en y = −2x + 1","en":"y = 2x + 1 and y = −2x + 1"},{"af":"y = 2x + 1 en y = 2x − 3","en":"y = 2x + 1 and y = 2x − 3"},{"af":"y = x en y = −x","en":"y = x and y = −x"},{"af":"y = 3x − 1 en y = x + 3","en":"y = 3x − 1 and y = x + 3"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"y = 2x + 1 en y = 2x − 3 het dieselfde gradiënt (2) maar verskillende y-afsnitte, dus is die lyne ewewydig en sny nooit nie. Lyne met verskillende gradiënte sny altyd presies een keer.","en":"y = 2x + 1 and y = 2x − 3 have the same gradient (2) but different y-intercepts, so the lines are parallel and never intersect. Lines with different gradients always intersect exactly once."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"As (x − 3)(x + 5) = 0, dan is …","en":"If (x − 3)(x + 5) = 0, then …"},"options":[{"af":"x = 3 of x = −5","en":"x = 3 or x = −5"},{"af":"x = −3 of x = 5","en":"x = −3 or x = 5"},{"af":"x = 3 of x = 5","en":"x = 3 or x = 5"},{"af":"x = −15","en":"x = −15"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Nulproduk-reël: x − 3 = 0 of x + 5 = 0, dus x = 3 of x = −5. Die oplossing het die teenoorgestelde teken van die getal in die hakie.","en":"Zero product rule: x − 3 = 0 or x + 5 = 0, so x = 3 or x = −5. The solution has the opposite sign of the number in the bracket."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: 5x − 7 = 2x + 8. x = ___","en":"Solve: 5x − 7 = 2x + 8. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","x = 5"],"en":["5","x = 5"]},"explain":{"af":"5x − 2x = 8 + 7, dus 3x = 15 en x = 5. Kontrole: 25 − 7 = 18 en 10 + 8 = 18 ✓","en":"5x − 2x = 8 + 7, so 3x = 15 and x = 5. Check: 25 − 7 = 18 and 10 + 8 = 18 ✓"}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vergelyking by die tipe en metode.","en":"Match each equation to its type and method."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"4(x − 1) = 2x + 6","en":"4(x − 1) = 2x + 6"},"r":{"af":"Lineêr: verwyder hakies en isoleer x","en":"Linear: remove brackets and isolate x"}},{"l":{"af":"x² + 2x − 15 = 0","en":"x² + 2x − 15 = 0"},"r":{"af":"Kwadraties: faktoriseer en gebruik die nulproduk-reël","en":"Quadratic: factorise and use the zero product rule"}},{"l":{"af":"v = u + at (maak a die onderwerp)","en":"v = u + at (make a the subject)"},"r":{"af":"Letterlike vergelyking","en":"Literal equation"}},{"l":{"af":"x + y = 7 en x − y = 1","en":"x + y = 7 and x − y = 1"},"r":{"af":"Gelyktydig: eliminasie of vervanging","en":"Simultaneous: elimination or substitution"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die hoogste mag (1 of 2), die aantal onbekendes en of jy 'n formule herrangskik, bepaal die metode.","en":"The highest power (1 or 2), the number of unknowns and whether you are rearranging a formula determine the method."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: (2x + 1)/3 − (x − 2)/2 = 2","en":"Solve: (2x + 1)/3 − (x − 2)/2 = 2"},"options":[{"af":"x = 16","en":"x = 16"},{"af":"x = −6","en":"x = −6"},{"af":"x = 6","en":"x = 6"},{"af":"x = 4","en":"x = 4"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"KGV = 6: 2(2x + 1) − 3(x − 2) = 12, dus 4x + 2 − 3x + 6 = 12, x + 8 = 12 en x = 4. x = 16 kom van −3(x − 2) = −3x − 6 (tekenfout), en x = −6 as jy vergeet om die RK met 6 te vermenigvuldig.","en":"LCM = 6: 2(2x + 1) − 3(x − 2) = 12, so 4x + 2 − 3x + 6 = 12, x + 8 = 12 and x = 4. x = 16 comes from −3(x − 2) = −3x − 6 (sign error), and x = −6 if you forget to multiply the RHS by 6."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: x² − 7x + 12 = 0. Die kleinste oplossing is x = ___","en":"Solve: x² − 7x + 12 = 0. The smallest solution is x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["3","x = 3"],"en":["3","x = 3"]},"explain":{"af":"Soek twee getalle met produk 12 en som −7: −3 en −4. (x − 3)(x − 4) = 0, dus x = 3 of x = 4. Die kleinste is 3.","en":"Look for two numbers with product 12 and sum −7: −3 and −4. (x − 3)(x − 4) = 0, so x = 3 or x = 4. The smallest is 3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: x² = 6x","en":"Solve: x² = 6x"},"options":[{"af":"x = 6","en":"x = 6"},{"af":"x = 0 of x = 6","en":"x = 0 or x = 6"},{"af":"x = 0 of x = −6","en":"x = 0 or x = −6"},{"af":"x = ±√6","en":"x = ±√6"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"x² − 6x = 0, dus x(x − 6) = 0 en x = 0 of x = 6. As jy deur x deel, kry jy net x = 6 en verloor jy x = 0.","en":"x² − 6x = 0, so x(x − 6) = 0 and x = 0 or x = 6. If you divide by x you only get x = 6 and lose x = 0."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy y die onderwerp van 4x − 2y = 10 maak, kry jy y = 2x − 5.","en":"If you make y the subject of 4x − 2y = 10, you get y = 2x − 5."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. −2y = 10 − 4x. Deel elke term deur −2: y = −5 + 2x = 2x − 5.","en":"True. −2y = 10 − 4x. Divide every term by −2: y = −5 + 2x = 2x − 5."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los gelyktydig op: x + y = 9 en 2x − y = 3","en":"Solve simultaneously: x + y = 9 and 2x − y = 3"},"options":[{"af":"x = 5 en y = 4","en":"x = 5 and y = 4"},{"af":"x = 12 en y = −3","en":"x = 12 and y = −3"},{"af":"x = 4 en y = 5","en":"x = 4 and y = 5"},{"af":"x = 4 en y = −5","en":"x = 4 and y = −5"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Tel die vergelykings op: 3x = 12, dus x = 4. Dan 4 + y = 9, dus y = 5. Kontrole: 2(4) − 5 = 3 ✓. x = 12 vergeet om deur 3 te deel; y = −5 is 'n tekenfout in 8 − y = 3.","en":"Add the equations: 3x = 12, so x = 4. Then 4 + y = 9, so y = 5. Check: 2(4) − 5 = 3 ✓. x = 12 forgets to divide by 3; y = −5 is a sign error in 8 − y = 3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Maak x die onderwerp van ax − b = cx + d.","en":"Make x the subject of ax − b = cx + d."},"options":[{"af":"x = (b + d)/(a − c)","en":"x = (b + d)/(a − c)"},{"af":"x = (d − b)/(a − c)","en":"x = (d − b)/(a − c)"},{"af":"x = (b + d)/(a + c)","en":"x = (b + d)/(a + c)"},{"af":"x = (b + d)/(c − a)","en":"x = (b + d)/(c − a)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Bring die x-terme na links en die res na regs: ax − cx = d + b. Haal x uit as gemene faktor: x(a − c) = b + d, dus x = (b + d)/(a − c). Die ander opsies het 'n tekenfout wanneer 'n term oorgebring word.","en":"Bring the x-terms to the left and the rest to the right: ax − cx = d + b. Take x out as a common factor: x(a − c) = b + d, so x = (b + d)/(a − c). The other options have a sign error when a term is moved across."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die lengte van 'n reghoekige braai-area is 3 m meer as die breedte. Die oppervlakte is 28 m². Hoe breed is die braai-area? ___ m","en":"The length of a rectangular braai area is 3 m more than its width. The area is 28 m². How wide is the braai area? ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["4","4 m","x = 4"],"en":["4","4 m","x = 4"]},"explain":{"af":"Laat die breedte x wees. x(x + 3) = 28, dus x² + 3x − 28 = 0 en (x + 7)(x − 4) = 0. x = −7 word verwerp ('n breedte kan nie negatief wees nie), dus is die breedte 4 m (en die lengte 7 m).","en":"Let the width be x. x(x + 3) = 28, so x² + 3x − 28 = 0 and (x + 7)(x − 4) = 0. x = −7 is rejected (a width cannot be negative), so the width is 4 m (and the length 7 m)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Ma is nou drie keer so oud as haar seun. Oor 12 jaar sal sy twee keer so oud as hy wees. Hoe oud is die seun nou? ___ jaar","en":"A mother is now three times as old as her son. In 12 years she will be twice as old as he is. How old is the son now? ___ years"},"answers":{"af":["12","12 jaar"],"en":["12","12 years"]},"explain":{"af":"Laat die seun nou x jaar oud wees; ma is 3x. Oor 12 jaar: 3x + 12 = 2(x + 12), dus 3x + 12 = 2x + 24 en x = 12. Die seun is 12 en ma 36 (oor 12 jaar: 48 = 2 × 24 ✓).","en":"Let the son now be x years old; the mother is 3x. In 12 years: 3x + 12 = 2(x + 12), so 3x + 12 = 2x + 24 and x = 12. The son is 12 and the mother 36 (in 12 years: 48 = 2 × 24 ✓)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By 'n kerkbasaar op Brits word koeksisters teen R5 elk en pannekoeke teen R8 elk verkoop. Altesaam 120 items word verkoop vir R816. Hoeveel pannekoeke is verkoop?","en":"At a church fête in Brits koeksisters are sold at R5 each and pancakes at R8 each. Altogether 120 items are sold for R816. How many pancakes were sold?"},"options":[{"af":"48","en":"48"},{"af":"60","en":"60"},{"af":"72","en":"72"},{"af":"102","en":"102"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Laat k = koeksisters en p = pannekoeke. k + p = 120 en 5k + 8p = 816. Vervang k = 120 − p: 600 − 5p + 8p = 816, dus 3p = 216 en p = 72 (en k = 48). 48 is die aantal koeksisters, 60 is net 120 ÷ 2, en 102 = 816 ÷ 8 ignoreer die koeksisters.","en":"Let k = koeksisters and p = pancakes. k + p = 120 and 5k + 8p = 816. Substitute k = 120 − p: 600 − 5p + 8p = 816, so 3p = 216 and p = 72 (and k = 48). 48 is the number of koeksisters, 60 is just 120 ÷ 2, and 102 = 816 ÷ 8 ignores the koeksisters."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-ongelykhede","title":{"af":"Lineêre ongelykhede","en":"Linear inequalities"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal lineêre en saamgestelde ongelykhede kan oplos, weet wanneer om die teken om te draai, en die oplossing op 'n getallelyn en in intervalnotasie kan voorstel.","en":"You will be able to solve linear and compound inequalities, know when to reverse the sign, and represent the solution on a number line and in interval notation."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n ongelykheid?\n\n'n **Ongelykheid** vergelyk twee uitdrukkings met een van die simbole hieronder. 'n **Lineêre ongelykheid** het x tot die mag 1, bv. 3x − 2 > 7. Die oplossing is gewoonlik 'n **interval** (oneindig baie getalle), nie net een getal nie.\n\n| Simbool | Betekenis | Woorde in vrae |\n|---|---|---|\n| < | kleiner as | minder as |\n| > | groter as | meer as |\n| ≤ | kleiner as of gelyk aan | hoogstens, nie meer as nie |\n| ≥ | groter as of gelyk aan | minstens, ten minste, nie minder as nie |\n\n## Los 'n lineêre ongelykheid op\n\nWerk presies soos met 'n vergelyking: verwyder hakies en breuke, bring die x-terme na een kant en die getalle na die ander kant, en deel deur die koëffisiënt van x. Daar is net **een** groot verskil:\n\n> **Onthou!** As jy albei kante met 'n **negatiewe** getal **vermenigvuldig of deel**, moet jy die ongelykheidsteken **omdraai**.\n\n**Hoekom?** 2 < 5 is waar. Vermenigvuldig albei kante met −1 en jy kry −2 en −5. Op die getallelyn lê −2 regs van −5, dus is −2 > −5. Die volgorde het omgedraai.\n\n- **Optel of aftrek** (selfs van 'n negatiewe getal): **moenie** omdraai nie. x − 5 > −2 gee x > 3.\n- **Vermenigvuldig of deel met 'n positiewe getal:** **moenie** omdraai nie.\n- **Ruil die twee kante om:** dan draai die teken ook om. 4 > x beteken dieselfde as x < 4.\n\nVoorbeeld: 5 − 2x > 11, dus −2x > 6. Deel deur −2 en draai om: x < −3.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** die teken omdraai net omdat daar 'n negatiewe getal in die ongelykheid staan. Jy draai slegs om as jy met 'n negatiewe getal **vermenigvuldig of deel**.\n\n## Getallelyn\n\n- **Oop kolletjie (○):** die getal is **nie ingesluit** nie (> of <).\n- **Ingekleurde kolletjie (●):** die getal **is ingesluit** (≤ of ≥).\n- Die pyl wys na **regs** vir \"groter as\" en na **links** vir \"kleiner as\". By 'n saamgestelde ongelykheid trek jy 'n dik lyn tussen die twee kolletjies.\n\n## Intervalnotasie\n\n- **Ronde hakie ( ):** die eindpunt is **nie** ingesluit nie (> of <).\n- **Vierkantige hakie [ ]:** die eindpunt **is** ingesluit (≤ of ≥).\n- By ∞ of −∞ staan **altyd** 'n ronde hakie, want oneindig is nie 'n getal wat jy kan bereik nie.\n- Skryf die kleinste getal eerste, met 'n kommapunt tussenin.\n\n| Ongelykheid | Getallelyn | Intervalnotasie |\n|---|---|---|\n| *x* > 3 | ○ by 3, pyl na regs | (3 ; ∞) |\n| *x* ≤ −1 | ● by −1, pyl na links | (−∞ ; −1] |\n| −2 ≤ *x* < 4 | ● by −2, ○ by 4 | [−2 ; 4) |\n| 1 < *x* ≤ 6 | ○ by 1, ● by 6 | (1 ; 6] |\n\n## Saamgestelde ongelykhede\n\n'n **Saamgestelde ongelykheid** soos −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7 het drie dele. Doen elke bewerking aan **al drie** dele:\n\n- Trek 1 af: −4 ≤ 2x < 6\n- Deel deur 2: −2 ≤ x < 3, dus x ∈ [−2 ; 3)\n\nAs jy deur 'n negatiewe getal deel, draai **albei** tekens om en herskryf dan sodat die kleinste getal links staan:\n\n−7 < 5 − 3x ≤ 11 → trek 5 af: −12 < −3x ≤ 6 → deel deur −3: 4 > x ≥ −2 → herskryf: −2 ≤ x < 4, dus x ∈ [−2 ; 4)\n\n> **Algemene fout:** net een van die twee tekens omdraai, of net die middelste deel deur −3 deel. Al drie dele kry dieselfde bewerking en albei tekens draai om.\n\n## Heelgetal-oplossings\n\nAs die vraag sê x ∈ ℤ (heelgetalle) of x ∈ ℕ (natuurlike getalle), lys jy net daardie getalle in die interval. Kyk mooi na die eindpunte: die eindpunt is ingesluit by ≤ en ≥, maar uitgesluit by > en <.\n\nVir −2 ≤ x < 3 en x ∈ ℤ is x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2. Dit is vyf heelgetalle, want 3 is nie ingesluit nie.\n\n## Breuke en woordprobleme\n\n- **Breuke:** vermenigvuldig elke term met die KGV van die noemers. Die KGV is positief, dus bly die teken dieselfde.\n- **Woordprobleme:** definieer die onbekende, kies die regte simbool (minstens → ≥, hoogstens → ≤), los op en **rond logies af**. Met hoogstens R200 vir items van R30 elk is 30x ≤ 200, dus x ≤ 6,67 en jy kan hoogstens **6** koop (rond af). As jy minstens 'n sekere bedrag moet insamel, rond jy **op**.\n\n> **Wenk:** Toets jou antwoord met 'n getal binne die interval (dit moet werk) en een buite die interval (dit moet nie werk nie).","en":"## What is an inequality?\n\nAn **inequality** compares two expressions using one of the symbols below. A **linear inequality** has x to the power 1, e.g. 3x − 2 > 7. The solution is usually an **interval** (infinitely many numbers), not just one number.\n\n| Symbol | Meaning | Words in questions |\n|---|---|---|\n| < | less than | fewer than |\n| > | greater than | more than |\n| ≤ | less than or equal to | at most, not more than |\n| ≥ | greater than or equal to | at least, no less than |\n\n## Solving a linear inequality\n\nWork exactly as with an equation: remove brackets and fractions, bring the x-terms to one side and the numbers to the other side, and divide by the coefficient of x. There is only **one** big difference:\n\n> **Remember!** If you **multiply or divide** both sides by a **negative** number, you must **reverse** the inequality sign.\n\n**Why?** 2 < 5 is true. Multiply both sides by −1 and you get −2 and −5. On the number line −2 lies to the right of −5, so −2 > −5. The order has reversed.\n\n- **Adding or subtracting** (even a negative number): do **not** reverse.\n- **Multiplying or dividing by a positive number:** do **not** reverse.\n- **Swapping the two sides:** the sign also turns around. 4 > x means the same as x < 4.\n\nFor example, x − 5 > −2 gives x > 3 (no reversing). And 5 − 2x > 11 gives −2x > 6. Divide by −2 and reverse: x < −3.\n\n> **Common mistake:** reversing the sign just because there is a negative number in the inequality. You only reverse when you **multiply or divide** by a negative number.\n\n## Number line\n\n- **Open dot (○):** the number is **not included** (> or <).\n- **Closed (shaded) dot (●):** the number **is included** (≤ or ≥).\n- The arrow points **right** for \"greater than\" and **left** for \"less than\". For a compound inequality you draw a thick line between the two dots.\n\n## Interval notation\n\n- **Round bracket ( ):** the endpoint is **not** included (> or <).\n- **Square bracket [ ]:** the endpoint **is** included (≤ or ≥).\n- At ∞ or −∞ there is **always** a round bracket, because infinity is not a number you can reach.\n- Write the smallest number first, with a semicolon in between.\n\n| Inequality | Number line | Interval notation |\n|---|---|---|\n| *x* > 3 | ○ at 3, arrow right | (3 ; ∞) |\n| *x* ≤ −1 | ● at −1, arrow left | (−∞ ; −1] |\n| −2 ≤ *x* < 4 | ● at −2, ○ at 4 | [−2 ; 4) |\n| 1 < *x* ≤ 6 | ○ at 1, ● at 6 | (1 ; 6] |\n\n## Compound inequalities\n\nA **compound inequality** such as −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7 has three parts. Do every operation to **all three** parts:\n\n- Subtract 1: −4 ≤ 2x < 6\n- Divide by 2: −2 ≤ x < 3, so x ∈ [−2 ; 3)\n\nIf you divide by a negative number, reverse **both** signs and then rewrite so that the smallest number is on the left:\n\n−7 < 5 − 3x ≤ 11 → subtract 5: −12 < −3x ≤ 6 → divide by −3: 4 > x ≥ −2 → rewrite: −2 ≤ x < 4, so x ∈ [−2 ; 4)\n\n> **Common mistake:** reversing only one of the two signs, or dividing only the middle part by −3. All three parts get the same operation and both signs reverse.\n\n## Integer solutions\n\nIf the question says x ∈ ℤ (integers) or x ∈ ℕ (natural numbers), you list only those numbers in the interval. Look carefully at the endpoints: the endpoint is included with ≤ and ≥, but excluded with > and <.\n\nFor −2 ≤ x < 3 and x ∈ ℤ, x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2. That is five integers, because 3 is not included.\n\n## Fractions and word problems\n\n- **Fractions:** multiply every term by the LCM of the denominators. The LCM is positive, so the sign stays the same.\n- **Word problems:** define the unknown, choose the correct symbol (at least → ≥, at most → ≤), solve and **round logically**. With at most R200 for items of R30 each, 30x ≤ 200, so x ≤ 6.67 and you can buy at most **6** (round down). If you must raise at least a certain amount, you round **up**.\n\n> **Tip:** Test your answer with a number inside the interval (it must work) and one outside the interval (it must not work)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Ongelykheid","en":"Inequality"},"def":{"af":"'n Wiskundige sin wat twee uitdrukkings met <, >, ≤ of ≥ vergelyk.","en":"A mathematical sentence that compares two expressions using <, >, ≤ or ≥."}},{"term":{"af":"Lineêre ongelykheid","en":"Linear inequality"},"def":{"af":"'n Ongelykheid waarin die hoogste mag van die veranderlike 1 is, bv. 3x − 2 > 7.","en":"An inequality in which the highest power of the variable is 1, e.g. 3x − 2 > 7."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde ongelykheid","en":"Compound inequality"},"def":{"af":"'n Ongelykheid met twee ongelykheidstekens en drie dele, bv. −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7.","en":"An inequality with two inequality signs and three parts, e.g. −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7."}},{"term":{"af":"Intervalnotasie","en":"Interval notation"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort manier om 'n versameling reële getalle met hakies te skryf, bv. [−2 ; 3). Ronde hakie: nie ingesluit; vierkantige hakie: ingesluit.","en":"A short way of writing a set of real numbers with brackets, e.g. [−2 ; 3). Round bracket: not included; square bracket: included."}},{"term":{"af":"Getallelyn","en":"Number line"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn waarop die oplossing van 'n ongelykheid met kolletjies en 'n pyl of lyn gewys word.","en":"A line on which the solution of an inequality is shown with dots and an arrow or line."}},{"term":{"af":"Oop en ingekleurde kolletjie","en":"Open and closed dot"},"def":{"af":"Oop kolletjie (○): die getal is nie ingesluit nie (< of >). Ingekleurde kolletjie (●): die getal is ingesluit (≤ of ≥).","en":"Open dot (○): the number is not included (< or >). Closed dot (●): the number is included (≤ or ≥)."}},{"term":{"af":"Oneindig (∞)","en":"Infinity (∞)"},"def":{"af":"Wys dat die interval sonder einde aangaan. Kry altyd 'n ronde hakie, bv. (3 ; ∞).","en":"Shows that the interval goes on without end. Always gets a round bracket, e.g. (3 ; ∞)."}},{"term":{"af":"Heelgetalle (ℤ)","en":"Integers (ℤ)"},"def":{"af":"Die getalle …; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; … sonder breuke of desimale.","en":"The numbers …; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; … without fractions or decimals."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Deel deur 'n negatiewe getal","en":"Dividing by a negative number"},"problem":{"af":"Los op: 3 − 2x ≥ 11. Gee die oplossing in intervalnotasie en beskryf dit op 'n getallelyn.","en":"Solve: 3 − 2x ≥ 11. Give the solution in interval notation and describe it on a number line."},"steps":[{"af":"Trek 3 aan albei kante af: −2x ≥ 8","en":"Subtract 3 on both sides: −2x ≥ 8"},{"af":"Deel albei kante deur −2. Ons deel deur 'n negatiewe getal, dus draai die teken om: x ≤ −4","en":"Divide both sides by −2. We are dividing by a negative number, so the sign reverses: x ≤ −4"},{"af":"Intervalnotasie: x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. Die vierkantige hakie wys dat −4 ingesluit is; by −∞ is daar altyd 'n ronde hakie.","en":"Interval notation: x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. The square bracket shows that −4 is included; at −∞ there is always a round bracket."},{"af":"Getallelyn: 'n ingekleurde kolletjie (●) by −4 en 'n pyl na links.","en":"Number line: a closed dot (●) at −4 and an arrow to the left."},{"af":"Kontrole met x = −5: 3 − 2(−5) = 13 en 13 ≥ 11 ✓","en":"Check with x = −5: 3 − 2(−5) = 13 and 13 ≥ 11 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"x ≤ −4, d.w.s. x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]","en":"x ≤ −4, i.e. x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]"}},{"title":{"af":"Ongelykheid met breuke","en":"Inequality with fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Los op: (x − 1)/3 − (x + 2)/2 < 1","en":"Solve: (x − 1)/3 − (x + 2)/2 < 1"},"steps":[{"af":"Die KGV is 6 (positief, dus bly die teken dieselfde): 6 × [[x−1/3]] − 6 × [[x+2/2]] < 6 × 1","en":"The LCM is 6 (positive, so the sign stays the same): 6 × [[x−1/3]] − 6 × [[x+2/2]] < 6 × 1"},{"af":"2(x − 1) − 3(x + 2) < 6","en":"2(x − 1) − 3(x + 2) < 6"},{"af":"2x − 2 − 3x − 6 < 6, dus −x − 8 < 6","en":"2x − 2 − 3x − 6 < 6, so −x − 8 < 6"},{"af":"Tel 8 by: −x < 14","en":"Add 8: −x < 14"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met −1 en draai die teken om: x > −14, dus x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)","en":"Multiply by −1 and reverse the sign: x > −14, so x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)"}],"answer":{"af":"x > −14, d.w.s. x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)","en":"x > −14, i.e. x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)"}},{"title":{"af":"Saamgestelde ongelykheid en heelgetalle","en":"Compound inequality and integers"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Los op: 1 ≤ 7 − 2x < 13 en gee die antwoord in intervalnotasie. (b) Lys die heelgetalle wat aan die ongelykheid voldoen.","en":"(a) Solve: 1 ≤ 7 − 2x < 13 and give the answer in interval notation. (b) List the integers that satisfy the inequality."},"steps":[{"af":"Trek 7 van al drie dele af: −6 ≤ −2x < 6","en":"Subtract 7 from all three parts: −6 ≤ −2x < 6"},{"af":"Deel al drie dele deur −2 en draai albei tekens om: 3 ≥ x > −3","en":"Divide all three parts by −2 and reverse both signs: 3 ≥ x > −3"},{"af":"Herskryf met die kleinste getal links: −3 < x ≤ 3, dus x ∈ (−3 ; 3]","en":"Rewrite with the smallest number on the left: −3 < x ≤ 3, so x ∈ (−3 ; 3]"},{"af":"(b) −3 is nie ingesluit nie, maar 3 wel: x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3","en":"(b) −3 is not included, but 3 is: x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3"}],"answer":{"af":"x ∈ (−3 ; 3]; heelgetalle: −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3","en":"x ∈ (−3 ; 3]; integers: −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3"}},{"title":{"af":"Woordprobleem: hoeveel kan jy koop?","en":"Word problem: how many can you buy?"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho het R350. Hy koop 'n kaartjie vir 'n rugbywedstryd op Loftus in Pretoria vir R89 en wil met die res sakkies biltong teen R27 elk koop. Hoeveel sakkies kan hy hoogstens koop?","en":"Sipho has R350. He buys a ticket for a rugby match at Loftus in Pretoria for R89 and wants to buy packets of biltong at R27 each with the rest. What is the greatest number of packets he can buy?"},"steps":[{"af":"Laat b die aantal sakkies wees. Die totale koste mag hoogstens R350 wees: 89 + 27b ≤ 350","en":"Let b be the number of packets. The total cost may be at most R350: 89 + 27b ≤ 350"},{"af":"Trek 89 af: 27b ≤ 261","en":"Subtract 89: 27b ≤ 261"},{"af":"Deel deur 27 (positief, dus geen omdraai nie): b ≤ 9,67","en":"Divide by 27 (positive, so no reversing): b ≤ 9.67"},{"af":"b moet 'n heelgetal wees, dus rond ons AF: b = 9. Kontrole: 89 + 27(9) = R332 ≤ R350 ✓, maar 89 + 27(10) = R359 is te veel.","en":"b must be a whole number, so we round DOWN: b = 9. Check: 89 + 27(9) = R332 ≤ R350 ✓, but 89 + 27(10) = R359 is too much."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy kan hoogstens 9 sakkies biltong koop.","en":"He can buy at most 9 packets of biltong."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter intervalnotasie stel x ≥ 4 voor?","en":"Which interval notation represents x ≥ 4?"},"options":[{"af":"(4 ; ∞)","en":"(4 ; ∞)"},{"af":"[4 ; ∞)","en":"[4 ; ∞)"},{"af":"[4 ; ∞]","en":"[4 ; ∞]"},{"af":"(−∞ ; 4]","en":"(−∞ ; 4]"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"4 is ingesluit (≥), dus 'n vierkantige hakie by 4. By ∞ is daar altyd 'n ronde hakie. (−∞ ; 4] sou x ≤ 4 wees.","en":"4 is included (≥), so a square bracket at 4. At ∞ there is always a round bracket. (−∞ ; 4] would be x ≤ 4."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy albei kante van 'n ongelykheid met −3 vermenigvuldig, moet jy die ongelykheidsteken omdraai.","en":"If you multiply both sides of an inequality by −3, you must reverse the inequality sign."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Vermenigvuldig of deel jy met 'n negatiewe getal, draai die teken om, bv. 2 < 5 maar −6 > −15.","en":"True. When you multiply or divide by a negative number, the sign reverses, e.g. 2 < 5 but −6 > −15."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die oplossing van 'n ongelykheid word op 'n getallelyn gewys met 'n oop kolletjie by −1 en 'n pyl na regs. Watter ongelykheid is dit?","en":"The solution of an inequality is shown on a number line with an open dot at −1 and an arrow to the right. Which inequality is it?"},"options":[{"af":"x ≥ −1","en":"x ≥ −1"},{"af":"x < −1","en":"x < −1"},{"af":"x ≤ −1","en":"x ≤ −1"},{"af":"x > −1","en":"x > −1"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Oop kolletjie beteken −1 is nie ingesluit nie (> of <), en 'n pyl na regs beteken groter as. Dus x > −1. 'n Ingekleurde kolletjie sou ≥ wees.","en":"An open dot means −1 is not included (> or <), and an arrow to the right means greater than. So x > −1. A closed dot would be ≥."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke ongelykheid by die regte intervalnotasie.","en":"Match each inequality to the correct interval notation."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"−2 < x ≤ 5","en":"−2 < x ≤ 5"},"r":{"af":"(−2 ; 5]","en":"(−2 ; 5]"}},{"l":{"af":"−2 ≤ x < 5","en":"−2 ≤ x < 5"},"r":{"af":"[−2 ; 5)","en":"[−2 ; 5)"}},{"l":{"af":"x < 5","en":"x < 5"},"r":{"af":"(−∞ ; 5)","en":"(−∞ ; 5)"}},{"l":{"af":"x ≥ −2","en":"x ≥ −2"},"r":{"af":"[−2 ; ∞)","en":"[−2 ; ∞)"}}],"explain":{"af":"< en > kry ronde hakies, ≤ en ≥ kry vierkantige hakies, en ∞ kry altyd 'n ronde hakie.","en":"< and > get round brackets, ≤ and ≥ get square brackets, and ∞ always gets a round bracket."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: x − 7 > −3","en":"Solve: x − 7 > −3"},"options":[{"af":"x > 4","en":"x > 4"},{"af":"x < 4","en":"x < 4"},{"af":"x > −10","en":"x > −10"},{"af":"x > 10","en":"x > 10"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Tel 7 aan albei kante by: x > −3 + 7 = 4. Jy het nie met 'n negatiewe getal vermenigvuldig of gedeel nie, dus draai die teken NIE om nie.","en":"Add 7 on both sides: x > −3 + 7 = 4. You did not multiply or divide by a negative number, so the sign does NOT reverse."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: 2x + 5 ≤ 17. Die grootste waarde wat x kan hê, is ___","en":"Solve: 2x + 5 ≤ 17. The greatest value x can have is ___"},"answers":{"af":["6","x = 6"],"en":["6","x = 6"]},"explain":{"af":"2x ≤ 12, dus x ≤ 6. Omdat dit ≤ is, is 6 self ingesluit, dus is 6 die grootste waarde.","en":"2x ≤ 12, so x ≤ 6. Because it is ≤, 6 itself is included, so 6 is the greatest value."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: 4 − 3x < 10","en":"Solve: 4 − 3x < 10"},"options":[{"af":"x < −2","en":"x < −2"},{"af":"x > 2","en":"x > 2"},{"af":"x > −2","en":"x > −2"},{"af":"x < 2","en":"x < 2"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"−3x < 6. Deel deur −3 en draai die teken om: x > −2. x < −2 is die antwoord as jy vergeet om om te draai.","en":"−3x < 6. Divide by −3 and reverse the sign: x > −2. x < −2 is the answer if you forget to reverse."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die oplossing van −2x ≥ 8 is x ∈ [−4 ; ∞).","en":"The solution of −2x ≥ 8 is x ∈ [−4 ; ∞)."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Deel deur −2 en draai om: x ≤ −4, dus x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. Die stelling het vergeet om die teken om te draai.","en":"False. Divide by −2 and reverse: x ≤ −4, so x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. The statement forgot to reverse the sign."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel heelgetalle voldoen aan −1 < 3x + 2 ≤ 14? ___","en":"How many integers satisfy −1 < 3x + 2 ≤ 14? ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five"]},"explain":{"af":"Trek 2 af: −3 < 3x ≤ 12. Deel deur 3: −1 < x ≤ 4. −1 is nie ingesluit nie, 4 wel: 0; 1; 2; 3; 4 – dit is 5 heelgetalle.","en":"Subtract 2: −3 < 3x ≤ 12. Divide by 3: −1 < x ≤ 4. −1 is not included, 4 is: 0; 1; 2; 3; 4 – that is 5 integers."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: −4 ≤ 2x − 6 < 8","en":"Solve: −4 ≤ 2x − 6 < 8"},"options":[{"af":"−5 ≤ x < 1","en":"−5 ≤ x < 1"},{"af":"1 < x ≤ 7","en":"1 < x ≤ 7"},{"af":"2 ≤ x < 14","en":"2 ≤ x < 14"},{"af":"1 ≤ x < 7","en":"1 ≤ x < 7"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Tel 6 by al drie dele: 2 ≤ 2x < 14. Deel deur 2: 1 ≤ x < 7. −5 ≤ x < 1 trek 6 af in plaas daarvan om by te tel, 2 ≤ x < 14 vergeet om deur 2 te deel, en 1 < x ≤ 7 het die tekens omgeruil.","en":"Add 6 to all three parts: 2 ≤ 2x < 14. Divide by 2: 1 ≤ x < 7. −5 ≤ x < 1 subtracts 6 instead of adding, 2 ≤ x < 14 forgets to divide by 2, and 1 < x ≤ 7 swaps the signs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: (x + 3)/2 − (x − 1)/5 ≥ 2","en":"Solve: (x + 3)/2 − (x − 1)/5 ≥ 2"},"options":[{"af":"x ≥ 1","en":"x ≥ 1"},{"af":"x ≤ 1","en":"x ≤ 1"},{"af":"x ≥ −5","en":"x ≥ −5"},{"af":"x ≥ 7/3","en":"x ≥ 7/3"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"KGV = 10: 5(x + 3) − 2(x − 1) ≥ 20, dus 5x + 15 − 2x + 2 ≥ 20, 3x ≥ 3 en x ≥ 1. x ≥ 7/3 kom van −2(x − 1) = −2x − 2 (tekenfout), en x ≥ −5 as jy vergeet om die RK met 10 te vermenigvuldig.","en":"LCM = 10: 5(x + 3) − 2(x − 1) ≥ 20, so 5x + 15 − 2x + 2 ≥ 20, 3x ≥ 3 and x ≥ 1. x ≥ 7/3 comes from −2(x − 1) = −2x − 2 (sign error), and x ≥ −5 if you forget to multiply the RHS by 10."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: 2 < 5 − 3x ≤ 14. Wat is die kleinste heelgetal wat aan die ongelykheid voldoen? ___","en":"Solve: 2 < 5 − 3x ≤ 14. What is the smallest integer that satisfies the inequality? ___"},"answers":{"af":["−3","-3","x = −3","x = -3"],"en":["−3","-3","x = −3","x = -3"]},"explain":{"af":"Trek 5 af: −3 < −3x ≤ 9. Deel deur −3 en draai albei tekens om: 1 > x ≥ −3, dus −3 ≤ x < 1. −3 is ingesluit, dus is die kleinste heelgetal −3.","en":"Subtract 5: −3 < −3x ≤ 9. Divide by −3 and reverse both signs: 1 > x ≥ −3, so −3 ≤ x < 1. −3 is included, so the smallest integer is −3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vir watter waardes van x is 3x − 2 > 7 EN 2x + 1 ≤ 15 albei waar?","en":"For which values of x are 3x − 2 > 7 AND 2x + 1 ≤ 15 both true?"},"options":[{"af":"[3 ; 7)","en":"[3 ; 7)"},{"af":"(3 ; 7]","en":"(3 ; 7]"},{"af":"(3 ; 7)","en":"(3 ; 7)"},{"af":"[3 ; 7]","en":"[3 ; 7]"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"3x > 9 gee x > 3 (3 nie ingesluit nie), en 2x ≤ 14 gee x ≤ 7 (7 ingesluit). Albei saam: 3 < x ≤ 7, dus (3 ; 7].","en":"3x > 9 gives x > 3 (3 not included), and 2x ≤ 14 gives x ≤ 7 (7 included). Both together: 3 < x ≤ 7, so (3 ; 7]."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Taxi-eienaar op Brits het elke dag R480 se koste (brandstof en die bestuurder se loon). Elke passasier betaal R26 vir 'n rit Pretoria toe. Wat is die minste aantal passasiers wat hy per dag moet vervoer om 'n wins te maak? ___","en":"A taxi owner in Brits has R480 in costs every day (fuel and the driver's wage). Each passenger pays R26 for a trip to Pretoria. What is the least number of passengers he must transport per day to make a profit? ___"},"answers":{"af":["19","19 passasiers"],"en":["19","19 passengers"]},"explain":{"af":"Wins beteken inkomste > koste: 26p > 480, dus p > 18,46. Passasiers is heelgetalle, dus rond jy OP: 19. Kontrole: 18 × R26 = R468 (verlies), 19 × R26 = R494 (wins).","en":"Profit means income > costs: 26p > 480, so p > 18.46. Passengers are whole numbers, so you round UP: 19. Check: 18 × R26 = R468 (loss), 19 × R26 = R494 (profit)."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-trigonometrie","title":{"af":"Trigonometrie: verhoudings en spesiale hoeke","en":"Trigonometry: ratios and special angles"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sin, cos, tan en hul resiproke in reghoekige driehoeke en op die Cartesiese vlak kan gebruik, spesiale hoeke sonder 'n sakrekenaar kan uitwerk en eenvoudige trigonometriese vergelykings kan oplos.","en":"You will be able to use sin, cos, tan and their reciprocals in right-angled triangles and on the Cartesian plane, work out special angles without a calculator and solve simple trigonometric equations."},"summary":{"af":"## Die drie trigonometriese verhoudings\n\nIn 'n **reghoekige driehoek** benoem ons die sye **relatief tot 'n skerp hoek θ**:\n\n- **Skuinssy:** die sy oorkant die 90°-hoek. Dit is altyd die langste sy en dit verander nooit.\n- **Teenoorstaande sy:** die sy oorkant θ.\n- **Aangrensende sy:** die sy wat aan θ raak en nie die skuinssy is nie.\n\n| Verhouding | Definisie |\n|---|---|\n| sin θ | [[teenoorstaande/skuinssy]] |\n| cos θ | [[aangrensende/skuinssy]] |\n| tan θ | [[teenoorstaande/aangrensende]] |\n\n**Hoekom werk dit?** Alle reghoekige driehoeke met dieselfde hoek θ is **gelykvormig**. Die verhouding tussen twee sye is dus dieselfde, hoe groot die driehoek ook al is: dit hang net van die hoek af.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** As jy na die ander skerp hoek kyk, ruil die teenoorstaande en aangrensende sy om. Benoem die sye altyd opnuut vir die hoek in die vraag.\n\n## Resiproke verhoudings\n\n| Verhouding | Definisie |\n|---|---|\n| cosec θ = [[1/sin θ]] | [[skuinssy/teenoorstaande]] |\n| sec θ = [[1/cos θ]] | [[skuinssy/aangrensende]] |\n| cot θ = [[1/tan θ]] | [[aangrensende/teenoorstaande]] |\n\nOp die sakrekenaar: cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1,56.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** sin^{−1} is **nie** cosec nie. sin^{−1}(0,5) = 30° gee 'n **hoek**; cosec 30° = [[1/sin 30°]] = 2 gee 'n **getal**.\n\n**Notasie:** sin^{2} θ beteken (sin θ)^{2}, en 2 sin θ ≠ sin 2θ. Op die sakrekenaar is 4 sin 20° = 4 × sin 20° = 1,37, maar sin(4 × 20°) = sin 80° = 0,98.\n\n> **Wenk:** Maak seker jou sakrekenaar is in **grade** (DEG of D op die skerm), nie RAD of GRAD nie.\n\n## Verhoudings op die Cartesiese vlak\n\nKies 'n punt P(x; y). Die hoek θ word vanaf die **positiewe x-as antikloksgewys** tot by die lyn OP gemeet. Met r = OP gee Pythagoras r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}. **r is altyd positief.**\n\n- sin θ = [[y/r]]\n- cos θ = [[x/r]]\n- tan θ = [[y/x]]\n\nDie tekens van x en y bepaal die teken van elke verhouding (CAST-diagram):\n\n| Kwadrant | Hoeke | Positief |\n|---|---|---|\n| I | 0° < θ < 90° | **A**lles |\n| II | 90° < θ < 180° | **S**in (en cosec) |\n| III | 180° < θ < 270° | **T**an (en cot) |\n| IV | 270° < θ < 360° | **C**os (en sec) |\n\n**Metode (sonder sakrekenaar):**\n\n1. Maak die verhouding die onderwerp, bv. 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 → sin θ = [[−3/5]].\n2. Bepaal die kwadrant uit die gegewe tekens.\n3. Skets die punt en skryf x, y en r neer met die regte tekens.\n4. Bereken die ontbrekende koördinaat met r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}; die kwadrant bepaal sy teken.\n5. Vervang in die gevraagde uitdrukking.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die minusteken op r te sit. By sin θ = [[−3/5]] hoort die minus by y, want r is altyd positief.\n\n## Spesiale hoeke (sonder 'n sakrekenaar)\n\nLeer twee driehoeke:\n\n- **45°-driehoek:** reghoekig en gelykbenig, met sye 1 en 1 en skuinssy √2.\n- **30°–60°-driehoek:** die helfte van 'n gelyksydige driehoek met sy 2. Die sye is 1 (oorkant 30°), √3 (oorkant 60°) en skuinssy 2.\n\nVir 0° en 90° gebruik jy die punte (1; 0) en (0; 1) met r = 1.\n\n| | 0° | 30° | 45° | 60° | 90° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin | 0 | [[1/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[√3/2]] | 1 |\n| cos | 1 | [[√3/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[1/2]] | 0 |\n| tan | 0 | [[1/√3]] | 1 | √3 | ongedefinieerd |\n\nLet op: [[1/√2]] = [[√2/2]] en [[1/√3]] = [[√3/3]]. tan 90° is ongedefinieerd, want [[y/x]] = [[1/0]].\n\n> **Wenk:** As 'n vraag sê \"sonder 'n sakrekenaar\", vervang elke verhouding met sy breuk of wortel, vereenvoudig en laat die antwoord in wortelvorm, bv. sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]].\n\n## Sye en hoeke in 'n reghoekige driehoek\n\n**'n Sy bereken:**\n\n1. Benoem die sye relatief tot die gegewe hoek.\n2. Kies die verhouding wat die bekende en die onbekende sy bevat.\n3. Stel 'n vergelyking op en los op. Staan die onbekende onder die breukstreep, ruil om: cos 52° = [[8/PR]] → PR = [[8/cos 52°]].\n\n**'n Hoek bereken:**\n\n1. Kies die verhouding met die twee bekende sye.\n2. Gebruik die inverse: θ = sin^{−1}(…), cos^{−1}(…) of tan^{−1}(…).\n3. Rond eers aan die einde af tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n## Eenvoudige trigonometriese vergelykings\n\nIn vergelykings noem ons die onbekende hoek gewoonlik x (moenie dit met die x-koördinaat verwar nie). Vir skerp hoeke:\n\n1. Kry die verhouding alleen: 2 sin x = 1,3 → sin x = 0,65.\n2. Gebruik die inverse: x = sin^{−1}(0,65) = 40,54°.\n3. Is die hoek saamgestel, los eers die hele hoek op: tan(x + 10°) = 1 → x + 10° = 45° → x = 35°. Net so: cos 2x = 0,3 → 2x = 72,54° → x = 36,27°.\n4. By cosec, sec of cot draai jy eers om: sec x = 2 → cos x = [[1/2]] → x = 60°.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** By 2 sin x = 1,3 moet jy **eers deur 2 deel** en dan sin^{−1} gebruik. Onthou ook: sin x en cos x lê altyd tussen −1 en 1, dus het sin x = 1,3 **geen oplossing** nie.","en":"## The three trigonometric ratios\n\nIn a **right-angled triangle** we name the sides **relative to an acute angle θ**:\n\n- **Hypotenuse:** the side opposite the 90° angle. It is always the longest side and it never changes.\n- **Opposite side:** the side opposite θ.\n- **Adjacent side:** the side that touches θ and is not the hypotenuse.\n\n| Ratio | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| sin θ | [[opposite/hypotenuse]] |\n| cos θ | [[adjacent/hypotenuse]] |\n| tan θ | [[opposite/adjacent]] |\n\n**Why does it work?** All right-angled triangles with the same angle θ are **similar**. So the ratio of two sides is the same however big the triangle is: it depends only on the angle.\n\n> **Common mistake:** If you look at the other acute angle, the opposite and adjacent sides swap. Always label the sides again for the angle in the question.\n\n## Reciprocal ratios\n\n| Ratio | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| cosec θ = [[1/sin θ]] | [[hypotenuse/opposite]] |\n| sec θ = [[1/cos θ]] | [[hypotenuse/adjacent]] |\n| cot θ = [[1/tan θ]] | [[adjacent/opposite]] |\n\nOn the calculator: cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1.56.\n\n> **Common mistake:** sin^{−1} is **not** cosec. sin^{−1}(0.5) = 30° gives an **angle**; cosec 30° = [[1/sin 30°]] = 2 gives a **number**.\n\n**Notation:** sin^{2} θ means (sin θ)^{2}, and 2 sin θ ≠ sin 2θ. On the calculator 4 sin 20° = 4 × sin 20° = 1.37, but sin(4 × 20°) = sin 80° = 0.98.\n\n> **Tip:** Make sure your calculator is in **degrees** (DEG or D on the screen), not RAD or GRAD.\n\n## Ratios on the Cartesian plane\n\nChoose a point P(x; y). The angle θ is measured **anticlockwise from the positive x-axis** to the line OP. With r = OP, Pythagoras gives r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}. **r is always positive.**\n\n- sin θ = [[y/r]]\n- cos θ = [[x/r]]\n- tan θ = [[y/x]]\n\nThe signs of x and y decide the sign of each ratio (CAST diagram):\n\n| Quadrant | Angles | Positive |\n|---|---|---|\n| I | 0° < θ < 90° | **A**ll |\n| II | 90° < θ < 180° | **S**in (and cosec) |\n| III | 180° < θ < 270° | **T**an (and cot) |\n| IV | 270° < θ < 360° | **C**os (and sec) |\n\n**Method (without a calculator):**\n\n1. Make the ratio the subject, e.g. 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 → sin θ = [[−3/5]].\n2. Decide on the quadrant from the given signs.\n3. Sketch the point and write down x, y and r with the correct signs.\n4. Calculate the missing coordinate with r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}; the quadrant decides its sign.\n5. Substitute into the required expression.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Putting the minus sign on r. In sin θ = [[−3/5]] the minus belongs to y, because r is always positive.\n\n## Special angles (without a calculator)\n\nLearn two triangles:\n\n- **45° triangle:** right-angled and isosceles, with sides 1 and 1 and hypotenuse √2.\n- **30°–60° triangle:** half of an equilateral triangle with side 2. The sides are 1 (opposite 30°), √3 (opposite 60°) and hypotenuse 2.\n\nFor 0° and 90° use the points (1; 0) and (0; 1) with r = 1.\n\n| | 0° | 30° | 45° | 60° | 90° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin | 0 | [[1/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[√3/2]] | 1 |\n| cos | 1 | [[√3/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[1/2]] | 0 |\n| tan | 0 | [[1/√3]] | 1 | √3 | undefined |\n\nNote: [[1/√2]] = [[√2/2]] and [[1/√3]] = [[√3/3]]. tan 90° is undefined, because [[y/x]] = [[1/0]].\n\n> **Tip:** When a question says \"without a calculator\", replace each ratio with its fraction or surd, simplify, and leave the answer in surd form, e.g. sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]].\n\n## Sides and angles in a right-angled triangle\n\n**Finding a side:**\n\n1. Label the sides relative to the given angle.\n2. Choose the ratio that contains the known side and the unknown side.\n3. Set up an equation and solve. If the unknown is in the denominator, swap it over: cos 52° = [[8/PR]] → PR = [[8/cos 52°]].\n\n**Finding an angle:**\n\n1. Choose the ratio with the two known sides.\n2. Use the inverse: θ = sin^{−1}(…), cos^{−1}(…) or tan^{−1}(…).\n3. Round to two decimal places only at the end.\n\n## Simple trigonometric equations\n\nIn equations the unknown angle is usually called x (do not confuse it with the x-coordinate). For acute angles:\n\n1. Get the ratio on its own: 2 sin x = 1.3 → sin x = 0.65.\n2. Use the inverse: x = sin^{−1}(0.65) = 40.54°.\n3. If the angle is compound, first solve for the whole angle: tan(x + 10°) = 1 → x + 10° = 45° → x = 35°. In the same way: cos 2x = 0.3 → 2x = 72.54° → x = 36.27°.\n4. With cosec, sec or cot, invert first: sec x = 2 → cos x = [[1/2]] → x = 60°.\n\n> **Common mistake:** In 2 sin x = 1.3 you must **divide by 2 first** and then use sin^{−1}. Remember too: sin x and cos x always lie between −1 and 1, so sin x = 1.3 has **no solution**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Skuinssy","en":"Hypotenuse"},"def":{"af":"Die langste sy van 'n reghoekige driehoek; dit lê oorkant die 90°-hoek.","en":"The longest side of a right-angled triangle; it lies opposite the 90° angle."}},{"term":{"af":"Teenoorstaande sy","en":"Opposite side"},"def":{"af":"Die sy oorkant die hoek waarmee jy werk.","en":"The side opposite the angle you are working with."}},{"term":{"af":"Aangrensende sy","en":"Adjacent side"},"def":{"af":"Die sy wat aan die hoek raak waarmee jy werk en nie die skuinssy is nie.","en":"The side that touches the angle you are working with and is not the hypotenuse."}},{"term":{"af":"Trigonometriese verhouding","en":"Trigonometric ratio"},"def":{"af":"'n Verhouding tussen twee sye van 'n reghoekige driehoek (sin, cos, tan) wat net van die grootte van die hoek afhang.","en":"A ratio of two sides of a right-angled triangle (sin, cos, tan) that depends only on the size of the angle."}},{"term":{"af":"Resiproke verhoudings","en":"Reciprocal ratios"},"def":{"af":"cosec θ = 1/sin θ, sec θ = 1/cos θ en cot θ = 1/tan θ.","en":"cosec θ = 1/sin θ, sec θ = 1/cos θ and cot θ = 1/tan θ."}},{"term":{"af":"Inverse (sin⁻¹, cos⁻¹, tan⁻¹)","en":"Inverse (sin⁻¹, cos⁻¹, tan⁻¹)"},"def":{"af":"Die sakrekenaarfunksie wat die hoek gee as jy die waarde van die verhouding ken, bv. sin⁻¹(0,5) = 30°.","en":"The calculator function that gives the angle when you know the value of the ratio, e.g. sin⁻¹(0.5) = 30°."}},{"term":{"af":"Spesiale hoeke","en":"Special angles"},"def":{"af":"0°, 30°, 45°, 60° en 90°: hul verhoudings word sonder 'n sakrekenaar uit twee driehoeke bepaal.","en":"0°, 30°, 45°, 60° and 90°: their ratios are found without a calculator from two triangles."}},{"term":{"af":"CAST-diagram","en":"CAST diagram"},"def":{"af":"Wys watter verhoudings in elke kwadrant positief is: I alles, II sin, III tan, IV cos.","en":"Shows which ratios are positive in each quadrant: I all, II sin, III tan, IV cos."}},{"term":{"af":"Wortelvorm","en":"Surd form"},"def":{"af":"'n Eksakte antwoord met 'n wortelteken, bv. √3/2, in plaas van 'n afgeronde desimale getal.","en":"An exact answer with a root sign, e.g. √3/2, instead of a rounded decimal number."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bereken sye in 'n reghoekige driehoek","en":"Calculate sides in a right-angled triangle"},"problem":{"af":"In △PQR is ∠Q = 90°, ∠P = 52° en PQ = 8 cm. Bereken, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: (a) QR (b) PR.","en":"In △PQR, ∠Q = 90°, ∠P = 52° and PQ = 8 cm. Calculate, rounded to two decimal places: (a) QR (b) PR."},"steps":[{"af":"Benoem die sye relatief tot ∠P = 52°: QR is teenoorstaande, PQ = 8 cm is aangrensende en PR is die skuinssy (oorkant ∠Q = 90°).","en":"Label the sides relative to ∠P = 52°: QR is opposite, PQ = 8 cm is adjacent and PR is the hypotenuse (opposite ∠Q = 90°)."},{"af":"(a) Teenoorstaande en aangrensende sy → tan: tan 52° = [[QR/8]]","en":"(a) Opposite and adjacent side → tan: tan 52° = [[QR/8]]"},{"af":"QR = 8 tan 52° = 10,24 cm","en":"QR = 8 tan 52° = 10.24 cm"},{"af":"(b) Aangrensende sy en skuinssy → cos: cos 52° = [[8/PR]]","en":"(b) Adjacent side and hypotenuse → cos: cos 52° = [[8/PR]]"},{"af":"PR staan onder die breukstreep, dus ruil om: PR = [[8/cos 52°]] = 12,99 cm. Kontrole: 12,99 cm is die langste sy, soos 'n skuinssy moet wees.","en":"PR is in the denominator, so swap it over: PR = [[8/cos 52°]] = 12.99 cm. Check: 12.99 cm is the longest side, as a hypotenuse should be."}],"answer":{"af":"QR = 10,24 cm; PR = 12,99 cm","en":"QR = 10.24 cm; PR = 12.99 cm"}},{"title":{"af":"Los trigonometriese vergelykings op","en":"Solve trigonometric equations"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x, as x 'n skerp hoek is. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke. (a) 2 sin x = 1,3 (b) 4 cos(x + 15°) = 3","en":"Solve for x if x is an acute angle. Round to two decimal places. (a) 2 sin x = 1.3 (b) 4 cos(x + 15°) = 3"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Deel eers deur 2 sodat sin x alleen staan: sin x = 0,65","en":"(a) First divide by 2 so that sin x stands alone: sin x = 0.65"},{"af":"x = sin^{−1}(0,65) = 40,54°","en":"x = sin^{−1}(0.65) = 40.54°"},{"af":"(b) Deel deur 4: cos(x + 15°) = [[3/4]] = 0,75","en":"(b) Divide by 4: cos(x + 15°) = [[3/4]] = 0.75"},{"af":"Los eers die hele hoek op: x + 15° = cos^{−1}(0,75) = 41,41°","en":"First solve for the whole angle: x + 15° = cos^{−1}(0.75) = 41.41°"},{"af":"x = 41,41° − 15° = 26,41°","en":"x = 41.41° − 15° = 26.41°"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) x = 40,54° (b) x = 26,41°","en":"(a) x = 40.54° (b) x = 26.41°"}},{"title":{"af":"Verhoudings op die Cartesiese vlak","en":"Ratios on the Cartesian plane"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee: 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 en tan θ > 0. Bepaal sonder 'n sakrekenaar die waarde van: (a) cos θ (b) tan θ + sec θ","en":"Given: 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 and tan θ > 0. Without a calculator, determine the value of: (a) cos θ (b) tan θ + sec θ"},"steps":[{"af":"sin θ = [[−3/5]] = [[y/r]], dus y = −3 en r = 5 (r is altyd positief).","en":"sin θ = [[−3/5]] = [[y/r]], so y = −3 and r = 5 (r is always positive)."},{"af":"sin θ < 0 en tan θ > 0 geld net in kwadrant III (T in CAST). Daar is x en y albei negatief.","en":"sin θ < 0 and tan θ > 0 only in quadrant III (T in CAST). There x and y are both negative."},{"af":"Pythagoras: x^{2} = r^{2} − y^{2} = 25 − 9 = 16, dus x = −4 (kwadrant III).","en":"Pythagoras: x^{2} = r^{2} − y^{2} = 25 − 9 = 16, so x = −4 (quadrant III)."},{"af":"(a) cos θ = [[x/r]] = [[−4/5]]","en":"(a) cos θ = [[x/r]] = [[−4/5]]"},{"af":"(b) tan θ + sec θ = [[y/x]] + [[r/x]] = [[−3/−4]] + [[5/−4]] = [[3/4]] − [[5/4]] = −[[1/2]]","en":"(b) tan θ + sec θ = [[y/x]] + [[r/x]] = [[−3/−4]] + [[5/−4]] = [[3/4]] − [[5/4]] = −[[1/2]]"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) cos θ = −4/5 (b) tan θ + sec θ = −1/2","en":"(a) cos θ = −4/5 (b) tan θ + sec θ = −1/2"}},{"title":{"af":"Spesiale hoeke sonder 'n sakrekenaar","en":"Special angles without a calculator"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken sonder 'n sakrekenaar: (tan 60° × cos 30°) ÷ sin² 45°","en":"Calculate without a calculator: (tan 60° × cos 30°) ÷ sin² 45°"},"steps":[{"af":"Vervang die spesiale hoeke: tan 60° = √3, cos 30° = [[√3/2]] en sin 45° = [[1/√2]]","en":"Replace the special angles: tan 60° = √3, cos 30° = [[√3/2]] and sin 45° = [[1/√2]]"},{"af":"Teller: √3 × [[√3/2]] = [[3/2]]","en":"Numerator: √3 × [[√3/2]] = [[3/2]]"},{"af":"Noemer: sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]]","en":"Denominator: sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]]"},{"af":"[[3/2]] ÷ [[1/2]] = [[3/2]] × 2 = 3","en":"[[3/2]] ÷ [[1/2]] = [[3/2]] × 2 = 3"}],"answer":{"af":"3","en":"3"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke verhouding by sy definisie in 'n reghoekige driehoek.","en":"Match each ratio to its definition in a right-angled triangle."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"sin θ","en":"sin θ"},"r":{"af":"teenoorstaande / skuinssy","en":"opposite / hypotenuse"}},{"l":{"af":"cos θ","en":"cos θ"},"r":{"af":"aangrensende / skuinssy","en":"adjacent / hypotenuse"}},{"l":{"af":"tan θ","en":"tan θ"},"r":{"af":"teenoorstaande / aangrensende","en":"opposite / adjacent"}},{"l":{"af":"cosec θ","en":"cosec θ"},"r":{"af":"skuinssy / teenoorstaande","en":"hypotenuse / opposite"}}],"explain":{"af":"sin = teenoorstaande/skuinssy, cos = aangrensende/skuinssy en tan = teenoorstaande/aangrensende. cosec is die omgekeerde van sin, dus skuinssy/teenoorstaande.","en":"sin = opposite/hypotenuse, cos = adjacent/hypotenuse and tan = opposite/adjacent. cosec is the reciprocal of sin, so hypotenuse/opposite."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In △ABC is ∠B = 90°. Watter sy is die skuinssy?","en":"In △ABC, ∠B = 90°. Which side is the hypotenuse?"},"options":[{"af":"AB","en":"AB"},{"af":"BC","en":"BC"},{"af":"AC","en":"AC"},{"af":"Dit hang af van watter skerp hoek jy gebruik","en":"It depends on which acute angle you use"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die skuinssy lê oorkant die regte hoek. ∠B = 90°, dus is AC die skuinssy. Die skuinssy verander nooit; net die teenoorstaande en aangrensende sy hang van die hoek af.","en":"The hypotenuse lies opposite the right angle. ∠B = 90°, so AC is the hypotenuse. The hypotenuse never changes; only the opposite and adjacent sides depend on the angle."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om cosec 40° op jou sakrekenaar te bereken, druk jy sin⁻¹ 40.","en":"To calculate cosec 40° on your calculator, you press sin⁻¹ 40."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1,56. sin⁻¹ werk andersom: dit gee 'n hoek as jy 'n verhouding invoer. sin⁻¹ 40 gee selfs 'n fout, want sin lê altyd tussen −1 en 1.","en":"False. cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1.56. sin⁻¹ works the other way round: it gives an angle when you enter a ratio. sin⁻¹ 40 even gives an error, because sin always lies between −1 and 1."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sonder 'n sakrekenaar: tan 60° = ?","en":"Without a calculator: tan 60° = ?"},"options":[{"af":"1/√3","en":"1/√3"},{"af":"√3/2","en":"√3/2"},{"af":"1/2","en":"1/2"},{"af":"√3","en":"√3"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In die 30°–60°-driehoek is die sy oorkant 60° √3 en die aangrensende sy 1, dus tan 60° = √3/1 = √3. 1/√3 is tan 30°, √3/2 is sin 60° en 1/2 is cos 60°.","en":"In the 30°–60° triangle the side opposite 60° is √3 and the adjacent side is 1, so tan 60° = √3/1 = √3. 1/√3 is tan 30°, √3/2 is sin 60° and 1/2 is cos 60°."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In △PQR is ∠Q = 90°, PQ = 5, QR = 12 en PR = 13. Skryf sin P as 'n breuk: sin P = ___","en":"In △PQR, ∠Q = 90°, PQ = 5, QR = 12 and PR = 13. Write sin P as a fraction: sin P = ___"},"answers":{"af":["12/13","sin P = 12/13","sinP=12/13"],"en":["12/13","sin P = 12/13","sinP=12/13"]},"explain":{"af":"Relatief tot ∠P is QR = 12 die teenoorstaande sy en PR = 13 die skuinssy (oorkant ∠Q = 90°). sin P = 12/13. (5/13 sou cos P wees.)","en":"Relative to ∠P, QR = 12 is the opposite side and PR = 13 is the hypotenuse (opposite ∠Q = 90°). sin P = 12/13. (5/13 would be cos P.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 3 cos 40°, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"Calculate 3 cos 40°, rounded to two decimal places."},"options":[{"af":"2,30","en":"2.30"},{"af":"−0,50","en":"−0.50"},{"af":"0,77","en":"0.77"},{"af":"−2,00","en":"−2.00"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"3 cos 40° = 3 × cos 40° = 3 × 0,766… = 2,30. −0,50 is cos 120° (jy het die hoek met 3 vermenigvuldig), 0,77 is net cos 40°, en −2,00 kry jy as die sakrekenaar in RAD is.","en":"3 cos 40° = 3 × cos 40° = 3 × 0.766… = 2.30. −0.50 is cos 120° (you multiplied the angle by 3), 0.77 is only cos 40°, and −2.00 is what you get with the calculator in RAD."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x (x is skerp), afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: 3 cos x = 2,1. x = ___°","en":"Solve for x (x is acute), rounded to two decimal places: 3 cos x = 2.1. x = ___°"},"answers":{"af":["45,57","45.57","45,57°","45.57°","x = 45,57","x = 45.57","x = 45,57°","x = 45.57°","x=45,57","x=45.57","x=45,57°","x=45.57°"],"en":["45,57","45.57","45,57°","45.57°","x = 45,57","x = 45.57","x = 45,57°","x = 45.57°","x=45,57","x=45.57","x=45,57°","x=45.57°"]},"explain":{"af":"Deel eers deur 3: cos x = 0,7. Dan is x = cos⁻¹(0,7) = 45,57°.","en":"First divide by 3: cos x = 0.7. Then x = cos⁻¹(0.7) = 45.57°."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In △ABC is ∠C = 90°, ∠A = 32° en AB = 15 cm. Bereken BC, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"In △ABC, ∠C = 90°, ∠A = 32° and AB = 15 cm. Calculate BC, rounded to two decimal places."},"options":[{"af":"12,72 cm","en":"12.72 cm"},{"af":"7,95 cm","en":"7.95 cm"},{"af":"28,31 cm","en":"28.31 cm"},{"af":"9,37 cm","en":"9.37 cm"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Relatief tot ∠A is BC die teenoorstaande sy en AB die skuinssy, dus sin 32° = BC/15 en BC = 15 sin 32° = 7,95 cm. 12,72 cm gebruik cos (verkeerde sy), 28,31 cm is 15 ÷ sin 32° (breuk omgekeer) en 9,37 cm gebruik tan.","en":"Relative to ∠A, BC is the opposite side and AB the hypotenuse, so sin 32° = BC/15 and BC = 15 sin 32° = 7.95 cm. 12.72 cm uses cos (wrong side), 28.31 cm is 15 ÷ sin 32° (fraction upside down) and 9.37 cm uses tan."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As tan θ > 0 en cos θ < 0, dan lê θ in die derde kwadrant.","en":"If tan θ > 0 and cos θ < 0, then θ lies in the third quadrant."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. cos θ < 0 in kwadrant II en III. tan θ > 0 in kwadrant I en III. Albei geld net in kwadrant III (T in CAST).","en":"True. cos θ < 0 in quadrants II and III. tan θ > 0 in quadrants I and III. Both hold only in quadrant III (T in CAST)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"O is die oorsprong en P(−5; 12). Die hoek θ word vanaf die positiewe x-as tot by OP gemeet. Wat is cos θ?","en":"O is the origin and P(−5; 12). The angle θ is measured from the positive x-axis to OP. What is cos θ?"},"options":[{"af":"5/13","en":"5/13"},{"af":"−12/13","en":"−12/13"},{"af":"−5/13","en":"−5/13"},{"af":"−5/12","en":"−5/12"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"r² = (−5)² + 12² = 169, dus r = 13. cos θ = x/r = −5/13. 5/13 vergeet die teken van x, −12/13 gebruik y in plaas van x, en −5/12 is x/y.","en":"r² = (−5)² + 12² = 169, so r = 13. cos θ = x/r = −5/13. 5/13 forgets the sign of x, −12/13 uses y instead of x, and −5/12 is x/y."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken sonder 'n sakrekenaar: tan² 60° − 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = ___","en":"Calculate without a calculator: tan² 60° − 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = ___"},"answers":{"af":["2"],"en":["2"]},"explain":{"af":"tan² 60° = (√3)² = 3 en 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = 4 × 1/2 × 1/2 = 1. Dus 3 − 1 = 2.","en":"tan² 60° = (√3)² = 3 and 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = 4 × 1/2 × 1/2 = 1. So 3 − 1 = 2."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op vir x sonder 'n sakrekenaar, as x 'n skerp hoek is: 2 cos(x − 15°) = √3","en":"Solve for x without a calculator, if x is an acute angle: 2 cos(x − 15°) = √3"},"options":[{"af":"45°","en":"45°"},{"af":"15°","en":"15°"},{"af":"75°","en":"75°"},{"af":"30°","en":"30°"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"cos(x − 15°) = √3/2 en cos 30° = √3/2, dus x − 15° = 30° en x = 45°. 30° vergeet om 15° by te tel, 15° trek af in plaas van bytel, en 75° kom van die fout cos 60° = √3/2.","en":"cos(x − 15°) = √3/2 and cos 30° = √3/2, so x − 15° = 30° and x = 45°. 30° forgets to add 15°, 15° subtracts instead of adding, and 75° comes from the mistake cos 60° = √3/2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x (2x is 'n skerp hoek), afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: sec 2x = 2,5. x = ___°","en":"Solve for x (2x is an acute angle), rounded to two decimal places: sec 2x = 2.5. x = ___°"},"answers":{"af":["33,21","33.21","33,21°","33.21°","x = 33,21","x = 33.21","x = 33,21°","x = 33.21°","x=33,21","x=33.21","x=33,21°","x=33.21°"],"en":["33,21","33.21","33,21°","33.21°","x = 33,21","x = 33.21","x = 33,21°","x = 33.21°","x=33,21","x=33.21","x=33,21°","x=33.21°"]},"explain":{"af":"sec 2x = 2,5 beteken cos 2x = 1 ÷ 2,5 = 0,4. Dan is 2x = cos⁻¹(0,4) = 66,42°, dus x = 33,21°. Moenie cos⁻¹(2,5) probeer nie (dit gee 'n fout), en onthou om aan die einde deur 2 te deel.","en":"sec 2x = 2.5 means cos 2x = 1 ÷ 2.5 = 0.4. Then 2x = cos⁻¹(0.4) = 66.42°, so x = 33.21°. Do not try cos⁻¹(2.5) (it gives an error), and remember to divide by 2 at the end."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gegee: 13 sin θ + 5 = 0 en cos θ < 0. Bepaal sonder 'n sakrekenaar die waarde van 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ.","en":"Given: 13 sin θ + 5 = 0 and cos θ < 0. Without a calculator, determine the value of 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ."},"options":[{"af":"17","en":"17"},{"af":"−7","en":"−7"},{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"−17","en":"−17"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"sin θ = −5/13, dus y = −5 en r = 13. sin θ < 0 en cos θ < 0 → kwadrant III, dus x = −12 (x² = 169 − 25 = 144). 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ = 13(−12/13) − 12(−5/−12) = −12 − 5 = −17. Die ander opsies kom van tekenfoute: x positief gee 17, y positief gee −7, en albei positief gee 7.","en":"sin θ = −5/13, so y = −5 and r = 13. sin θ < 0 and cos θ < 0 → quadrant III, so x = −12 (x² = 169 − 25 = 144). 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ = 13(−12/13) − 12(−5/−12) = −12 − 5 = −17. The other options come from sign errors: x positive gives 17, y positive gives −7, and both positive gives 7."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Funksies, trigonometriese grafieke en Euklidiese meetkunde","en":"Functions, trigonometric graphs and Euclidean geometry"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t2-funksies-lyn-parabool","title":{"af":"Funksies: reguit lyn en parabool","en":"Functions: straight line and parabola"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal reguit lyne en parabole kan skets, hul definisie- en waardeversameling kan gee en hul vergelykings uit gegewe punte kan bepaal.","en":"You will be able to sketch straight lines and parabolas, give their domain and range, and determine their equations from given points."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n funksie?\n\n'n **Funksie** is 'n reël wat elke invoerwaarde (x) aan **presies een** uitvoerwaarde (y) koppel. Ons skryf y = 2x + 1 of f(x) = 2x + 1. Die notasie f(3) beteken: vervang x met 3. Dus f(3) = 2(3) + 1 = 7, en die punt (3; 7) lê op die grafiek.\n\n- **Vertikale-lyn-toets:** 'n grafiek is 'n funksie as elke vertikale lyn dit hoogstens een keer sny. 'n Vertikale lyn x = k is self **nie** 'n funksie nie.\n- **Definisieversameling:** al die x-waardes wat jy mag invul. Lees dit van links na regs op die x-as.\n- **Waardeversameling:** al die y-waardes wat die grafiek bereik. Lees dit van onder na bo op die y-as.\n- **Notasie:** x ∈ ℝ beteken \"x is enige reële getal\". Skryf 'n waardeversameling as 'n ongelykheid (y ≥ −3) of in intervalnotasie (y ∈ [−3; ∞)). 'n Vierkantige hakie sluit die grenswaarde in, 'n ronde hakie sluit dit uit, en ∞ kry altyd 'n ronde hakie.\n\n## Die reguit lyn: y = ax + q\n\nDit is dieselfde as y = mx + c: **a is die gradiënt** en **q is die y-afsnit**.\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | lyn styg van links na regs (toenemend) |\n| a < 0 | lyn daal van links na regs (afnemend) |\n| a = 0 | horisontale lyn y = q |\n| groter numeriese waarde van a | steiler lyn |\n| q | skuif die lyn q eenhede op (q > 0) of af (q < 0) |\n\n- **Gradiënt deur twee punte:** a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]]. Trek bo en onder in dieselfde volgorde af.\n- **y-afsnit:** stel x = 0 → (0; q).\n- **x-afsnit:** stel y = 0 en los x op.\n- Vir 'n skuins lyn is die definisieversameling x ∈ ℝ en die waardeversameling y ∈ ℝ.\n- **Afsnitmetode (dubbel-afsnitmetode):** bereken albei afsnitte, plot hulle en trek 'n reguit lyn deur die twee punte.\n\n## Die parabool: y = ax^{2} + q\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | \"glimlag\" ∪ met 'n **minimum** draaipunt |\n| a < 0 | \"frons\" ∩ met 'n **maksimum** draaipunt |\n| groter numeriese waarde van a | smaller (nouer) parabool |\n| a naby 0 | wyer parabool |\n| q | skuif die parabool op of af |\n\n- **Draaipunt:** (0; q). Dit is ook die **y-afsnit**.\n- **Simmetrie-as:** x = 0 (die y-as). Die linker- en regterkant is spieëlbeelde van mekaar.\n- **x-afsnitte:** stel y = 0: ax^{2} + q = 0 → x^{2} = [[−q/a]] → x = ±√([[−q/a]]). Daar is net x-afsnitte as a en q **teenoorgestelde tekens** het (of as q = 0).\n- **Definisieversameling:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Waardeversameling:** as a > 0 is y ≥ q, d.w.s. y ∈ [q; ∞). As a < 0 is y ≤ q, d.w.s. y ∈ (−∞; q].\n- **Toenemend en afnemend:** vir a > 0 is die parabool afnemend vir x < 0 en toenemend vir x > 0. Vir a < 0 is dit andersom.\n\n> **Onthou!** Die draaipunt is deel van die grafiek, daarom gebruik die waardeversameling van 'n parabool ≥ of ≤ (nie > of <).\n\n## Hoe om 'n grafiek te skets\n\n1. Bepaal die vorm uit die teken van a.\n2. Bereken die y-afsnit (stel x = 0).\n3. Bereken die x-afsnit(te) (stel y = 0).\n4. Vir 'n parabool: skryf die draaipunt en die simmetrie-as neer.\n5. Plot die punte, trek 'n reguit lyn of 'n gladde kurwe, en benoem die afsnitte, die draaipunt en die vergelyking.\n\n## Die vergelyking bepaal\n\n- **Lyn:** bereken a met die gradiëntformule. Vervang dan een punt in y = ax + q om q te kry. Kontroleer met die ander punt.\n- **Parabool:** q is die y-koördinaat van die draaipunt (0; q). Vervang dan nog 'n punt op die grafiek in y = ax^{2} + q en los a op.\n\n## Snypunte en grafieke lees\n\n- Twee grafieke sny waar hul y-waardes gelyk is: stel f(x) = g(x). Vir 'n lyn en 'n parabool kry jy 'n kwadratiese vergelyking: maak een kant nul, faktoriseer en kry dan die y-waardes.\n- f(x) > g(x) vra: waar lê f se grafiek **bo** g s'n? Lees die x-waardes tussen of buite die snypunte af.\n- f(x) ≥ 0 vra: waar lê die grafiek **op of bo** die x-as?\n\n> **Wenk:** Moet nie net 'n getal neerskryf nie. Toon die vergelyking wat jy oplos, want die memo gee punte vir die metode.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Die definisieversameling en die waardeversameling omruil.\n- Die ± vergeet wanneer jy x^{2} = 9 oplos (x = 3 **of** x = −3).\n- By 2y = 4x + 6 vergeet om eers deur 2 te deel: die gradiënt is 2, nie 4 nie.\n- Die y-koördinaat van enige gegewe punt as q gebruik. q is net die y-afsnit, waar x = 0.\n- Koördinate met 'n komma skryf. In Suid-Afrika skryf ons (2; 3).","en":"## What is a function?\n\nA **function** is a rule that links every input value (x) to **exactly one** output value (y). We write y = 2x + 1 or f(x) = 2x + 1. The notation f(3) means: replace x with 3. So f(3) = 2(3) + 1 = 7, and the point (3; 7) lies on the graph.\n\n- **Vertical line test:** a graph is a function if every vertical line cuts it at most once. A vertical line x = k is itself **not** a function.\n- **Domain:** all the x-values you may substitute. Read it from left to right on the x-axis.\n- **Range:** all the y-values the graph reaches. Read it from bottom to top on the y-axis.\n- **Notation:** x ∈ ℝ means \"x is any real number\". Write a range as an inequality (y ≥ −3) or in interval notation (y ∈ [−3; ∞)). A square bracket includes the end value, a round bracket excludes it, and ∞ always gets a round bracket.\n\n## The straight line: y = ax + q\n\nThis is the same as y = mx + c: **a is the gradient** and **q is the y-intercept**.\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | line rises from left to right (increasing) |\n| a < 0 | line falls from left to right (decreasing) |\n| a = 0 | horizontal line y = q |\n| larger numerical value of a | steeper line |\n| q | shifts the line q units up (q > 0) or down (q < 0) |\n\n- **Gradient through two points:** a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]]. Subtract in the same order at the top and the bottom.\n- **y-intercept:** let x = 0 → (0; q).\n- **x-intercept:** let y = 0 and solve for x.\n- For a slanted line the domain is x ∈ ℝ and the range is y ∈ ℝ.\n- **Dual-intercept method:** calculate both intercepts, plot them and draw a straight line through the two points.\n\n## The parabola: y = ax^{2} + q\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | \"smile\" ∪ with a **minimum** turning point |\n| a < 0 | \"frown\" ∩ with a **maximum** turning point |\n| larger numerical value of a | narrower parabola |\n| a close to 0 | wider parabola |\n| q | shifts the parabola up or down |\n\n- **Turning point:** (0; q). This is also the **y-intercept**.\n- **Axis of symmetry:** x = 0 (the y-axis). The left and right sides are mirror images.\n- **x-intercepts:** let y = 0: ax^{2} + q = 0 → x^{2} = [[−q/a]] → x = ±√([[−q/a]]). There are only x-intercepts if a and q have **opposite signs** (or if q = 0).\n- **Domain:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Range:** if a > 0 then y ≥ q, i.e. y ∈ [q; ∞). If a < 0 then y ≤ q, i.e. y ∈ (−∞; q].\n- **Increasing and decreasing:** for a > 0 the parabola is decreasing for x < 0 and increasing for x > 0. For a < 0 it is the other way round.\n\n> **Remember!** The turning point is part of the graph, so the range of a parabola uses ≥ or ≤, not > or <.\n\n## How to sketch a graph\n\n1. Decide on the shape from the sign of a.\n2. Calculate the y-intercept (let x = 0).\n3. Calculate the x-intercept(s) (let y = 0).\n4. For a parabola: write down the turning point and the axis of symmetry.\n5. Plot the points, draw a straight line or a smooth curve, and label the intercepts, the turning point and the equation.\n\n## Determining the equation\n\n- **Line:** calculate a with the gradient formula. Then substitute one point into y = ax + q to find q. Check with the other point.\n- **Parabola:** q is the y-coordinate of the turning point (0; q). Then substitute another point on the graph into y = ax^{2} + q and solve for a.\n\n## Points of intersection and reading graphs\n\n- Two graphs intersect where their y-values are equal: set f(x) = g(x). For a line and a parabola you get a quadratic equation: make one side zero, factorise and then find the y-values.\n- f(x) > g(x) asks: where is the graph of f **above** the graph of g? Read off the x-values between or outside the points of intersection.\n- f(x) ≥ 0 asks: where is the graph **on or above** the x-axis?\n\n> **Tip:** Never write down only a number. Show the equation you are solving, because the memo gives marks for the method.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Swapping the domain and the range.\n- Forgetting the ± when you solve x^{2} = 9 (x = 3 **or** x = −3).\n- With 2y = 4x + 6, forgetting to divide by 2 first: the gradient is 2, not 4.\n- Using the y-coordinate of any given point as q. q is only the y-intercept, where x = 0.\n- Writing coordinates with a comma. In South Africa we write (2; 3)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Funksie","en":"Function"},"def":{"af":"'n Reël wat elke invoerwaarde (x) aan presies een uitvoerwaarde (y) koppel.","en":"A rule that links every input value (x) to exactly one output value (y)."}},{"term":{"af":"Definisieversameling","en":"Domain"},"def":{"af":"Die versameling van al die x-waardes (invoerwaardes) waarvoor die funksie gedefinieer is.","en":"The set of all x-values (inputs) for which the function is defined."}},{"term":{"af":"Waardeversameling","en":"Range"},"def":{"af":"Die versameling van al die y-waardes (uitvoerwaardes) wat die funksie aanneem.","en":"The set of all y-values (outputs) that the function takes on."}},{"term":{"af":"Gradiënt","en":"Gradient"},"def":{"af":"Die steilheid van 'n reguit lyn: die verandering in y gedeel deur die verandering in x. In y = ax + q is dit a.","en":"The steepness of a straight line: the change in y divided by the change in x. In y = ax + q it is a."}},{"term":{"af":"Afsnit","en":"Intercept"},"def":{"af":"Die punt waar 'n grafiek 'n as sny. By die y-afsnit is x = 0; by die x-afsnit is y = 0.","en":"The point where a graph cuts an axis. At the y-intercept x = 0; at the x-intercept y = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Parabool","en":"Parabola"},"def":{"af":"Die U-vormige grafiek van 'n kwadratiese funksie soos y = ax² + q.","en":"The U-shaped graph of a quadratic function such as y = ax² + q."}},{"term":{"af":"Draaipunt","en":"Turning point"},"def":{"af":"Die laagste (minimum) of hoogste (maksimum) punt van 'n parabool. Vir y = ax² + q is dit (0; q).","en":"The lowest (minimum) or highest (maximum) point of a parabola. For y = ax² + q it is (0; q)."}},{"term":{"af":"Simmetrie-as","en":"Axis of symmetry"},"def":{"af":"Die vertikale lyn deur die draaipunt wat die parabool in twee spieëlbeelde verdeel. Vir y = ax² + q is dit x = 0.","en":"The vertical line through the turning point that divides the parabola into two mirror images. For y = ax² + q it is x = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Toenemend en afnemend","en":"Increasing and decreasing"},"def":{"af":"'n Grafiek is toenemend waar y groter word soos x groter word (styg na regs), en afnemend waar y kleiner word (daal na regs).","en":"A graph is increasing where y gets bigger as x gets bigger (rises to the right), and decreasing where y gets smaller (falls to the right)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skets 'n reguit lyn met die afsnitmetode","en":"Sketch a straight line with the dual-intercept method"},"problem":{"af":"Skets die grafiek van g(x) = −2x + 4 met die afsnitmetode. Gee die gradiënt, die definisieversameling en die waardeversameling.","en":"Sketch the graph of g(x) = −2x + 4 using the dual-intercept method. Give the gradient, the domain and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"Vorm: a = −2 < 0, dus daal die lyn van links na regs (afnemend). Die gradiënt is −2.","en":"Shape: a = −2 < 0, so the line falls from left to right (decreasing). The gradient is −2."},{"af":"y-afsnit: stel x = 0: g(0) = −2(0) + 4 = 4 → (0; 4)","en":"y-intercept: let x = 0: g(0) = −2(0) + 4 = 4 → (0; 4)"},{"af":"x-afsnit: stel y = 0: 0 = −2x + 4 → 2x = 4 → x = 2 → (2; 0)","en":"x-intercept: let y = 0: 0 = −2x + 4 → 2x = 4 → x = 2 → (2; 0)"},{"af":"Plot (0; 4) en (2; 0), trek 'n reguit lyn deur albei punte en benoem dit g(x) = −2x + 4.","en":"Plot (0; 4) and (2; 0), draw a straight line through both points and label it g(x) = −2x + 4."},{"af":"Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ. Waardeversameling: y ∈ ℝ (die lyn gaan oneindig op en af).","en":"Domain: x ∈ ℝ. Range: y ∈ ℝ (the line goes on forever up and down)."}],"answer":{"af":"Lyn deur (0; 4) en (2; 0); gradiënt −2; x ∈ ℝ; y ∈ ℝ","en":"Line through (0; 4) and (2; 0); gradient −2; x ∈ ℝ; y ∈ ℝ"}},{"title":{"af":"Eienskappe van 'n parabool","en":"Features of a parabola"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 2x² − 8. Bepaal die vorm, die draaipunt, die simmetrie-as, die afsnitte, die definisie- en waardeversameling, en waar f afnemend is.","en":"Given f(x) = 2x² − 8. Determine the shape, the turning point, the axis of symmetry, the intercepts, the domain and range, and where f is decreasing."},"steps":[{"af":"a = 2 > 0, dus is die grafiek 'n \"glimlag\" met 'n minimum draaipunt.","en":"a = 2 > 0, so the graph is a \"smile\" with a minimum turning point."},{"af":"q = −8, dus is die draaipunt (0; −8) en die simmetrie-as x = 0. Die y-afsnit is ook (0; −8).","en":"q = −8, so the turning point is (0; −8) and the axis of symmetry is x = 0. The y-intercept is also (0; −8)."},{"af":"x-afsnitte: 2x^{2} − 8 = 0 → 2x^{2} = 8 → x^{2} = 4 → x = ±2. Die punte is (−2; 0) en (2; 0).","en":"x-intercepts: 2x^{2} − 8 = 0 → 2x^{2} = 8 → x^{2} = 4 → x = ±2. The points are (−2; 0) and (2; 0)."},{"af":"Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ. Waardeversameling: y ≥ −8, d.w.s. y ∈ [−8; ∞).","en":"Domain: x ∈ ℝ. Range: y ≥ −8, i.e. y ∈ [−8; ∞)."},{"af":"Die grafiek daal tot by die draaipunt en styg daarna: f is afnemend vir x < 0 (en toenemend vir x > 0).","en":"The graph falls down to the turning point and rises after it: f is decreasing for x < 0 (and increasing for x > 0)."}],"answer":{"af":"Draaipunt (0; −8); x-afsnitte (−2; 0) en (2; 0); y ∈ [−8; ∞); afnemend vir x < 0","en":"Turning point (0; −8); x-intercepts (−2; 0) and (2; 0); y ∈ [−8; ∞); decreasing for x < 0"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyking van 'n lyn deur twee punte","en":"Equation of a line through two points"},"problem":{"af":"'n Reguit lyn h gaan deur die punte (−1; 5) en (3; −3). Bepaal die vergelyking van h in die vorm y = ax + q.","en":"A straight line h passes through the points (−1; 5) and (3; −3). Determine the equation of h in the form y = ax + q."},"steps":[{"af":"Gradiënt: a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] = [[−3 − 5/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2","en":"Gradient: a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] = [[−3 − 5/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2"},{"af":"Dus is y = −2x + q. Vervang die punt (−1; 5): 5 = −2(−1) + q","en":"So y = −2x + q. Substitute the point (−1; 5): 5 = −2(−1) + q"},{"af":"5 = 2 + q → q = 3","en":"5 = 2 + q → q = 3"},{"af":"Kontroleer met die ander punt (3; −3): −2(3) + 3 = −3 ✓","en":"Check with the other point (3; −3): −2(3) + 3 = −3 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"h(x) = −2x + 3","en":"h(x) = −2x + 3"}},{"title":{"af":"Parabool, lyn en snypunte","en":"Parabola, line and points of intersection"},"problem":{"af":"Die parabool f(x) = ax² + q het 'n draaipunt by (0; −4) en gaan deur die punt (3; 5). Die lyn g(x) = x + 2 sny f by A en B. (a) Bepaal die vergelyking van f. (b) Bepaal die koördinate van A en B. (c) Vir watter waardes van x is f(x) < g(x)?","en":"The parabola f(x) = ax² + q has a turning point at (0; −4) and passes through the point (3; 5). The line g(x) = x + 2 cuts f at A and B. (a) Determine the equation of f. (b) Determine the coordinates of A and B. (c) For which values of x is f(x) < g(x)?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die draaipunt is (0; −4), dus q = −4 en f(x) = ax^{2} − 4.","en":"(a) The turning point is (0; −4), so q = −4 and f(x) = ax^{2} − 4."},{"af":"Vervang (3; 5): 5 = a(3)^{2} − 4 → 9a = 9 → a = 1. Dus f(x) = x^{2} − 4.","en":"Substitute (3; 5): 5 = a(3)^{2} − 4 → 9a = 9 → a = 1. So f(x) = x^{2} − 4."},{"af":"(b) Stel f(x) = g(x): x^{2} − 4 = x + 2 → x^{2} − x − 6 = 0","en":"(b) Set f(x) = g(x): x^{2} − 4 = x + 2 → x^{2} − x − 6 = 0"},{"af":"Faktoriseer: (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 → x = 3 of x = −2","en":"Factorise: (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 → x = 3 or x = −2"},{"af":"Kry die y-waardes uit die lyn: g(−2) = −2 + 2 = 0 en g(3) = 3 + 2 = 5. Dus A(−2; 0) en B(3; 5).","en":"Find the y-values from the line: g(−2) = −2 + 2 = 0 and g(3) = 3 + 2 = 5. So A(−2; 0) and B(3; 5)."},{"af":"(c) f(x) < g(x) waar die parabool ONDER die lyn lê, dit is tussen die snypunte: −2 < x < 3.","en":"(c) f(x) < g(x) where the parabola lies BELOW the line, which is between the points of intersection: −2 < x < 3."}],"answer":{"af":"f(x) = x² − 4; A(−2; 0) en B(3; 5); −2 < x < 3","en":"f(x) = x² − 4; A(−2; 0) and B(3; 5); −2 < x < 3"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die definisieversameling van 'n funksie?","en":"What is the domain of a function?"},"options":[{"af":"Al die moontlike y-waardes (uitvoerwaardes)","en":"All the possible y-values (outputs)"},{"af":"Al die moontlike x-waardes (invoerwaardes)","en":"All the possible x-values (inputs)"},{"af":"Die punt waar die grafiek die y-as sny","en":"The point where the graph cuts the y-axis"},{"af":"Die hoogste of laagste punt van die grafiek","en":"The highest or lowest point of the graph"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die definisieversameling is al die x-waardes wat jy mag invul. Al die y-waardes vorm die waardeversameling. Moenie die twee omruil nie.","en":"The domain is all the x-values you may substitute. All the y-values form the range. Don't swap the two."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = −4x² + 1 het 'n maksimum draaipunt.","en":"The graph of y = −4x² + 1 has a maximum turning point."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. a = −4 < 0, dus is die parabool 'n \"frons\" (∩) en die draaipunt (0; 1) is die hoogste punt: 'n maksimum.","en":"True. a = −4 < 0, so the parabola is a \"frown\" (∩) and the turning point (0; 1) is the highest point: a maximum."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke beskrywing by die regte effek op die grafiek.","en":"Match each description to the correct effect on the graph."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"a > 0 in y = ax + q","en":"a > 0 in y = ax + q"},"r":{"af":"Die lyn styg van links na regs","en":"The line rises from left to right"}},{"l":{"af":"a < 0 in y = ax² + q","en":"a < 0 in y = ax² + q"},"r":{"af":"Die parabool het 'n maksimum draaipunt","en":"The parabola has a maximum turning point"}},{"l":{"af":"q in y = ax² + q","en":"q in y = ax² + q"},"r":{"af":"Die y-koördinaat van die draaipunt","en":"The y-coordinate of the turning point"}},{"l":{"af":"a = 0 in y = ax + q","en":"a = 0 in y = ax + q"},"r":{"af":"'n Horisontale lyn y = q","en":"A horizontal line y = q"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die teken van a bepaal die rigting (lyn) of vorm (parabool). q skuif die grafiek op of af: by die parabool is (0; q) die draaipunt. As a = 0 verdwyn die x-term en bly y = q oor.","en":"The sign of a decides the direction (line) or shape (parabola). q shifts the graph up or down: for the parabola (0; q) is the turning point. If a = 0 the x-term disappears and y = q remains."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt en die y-afsnit van die lyn 2y = −6x + 8?","en":"What are the gradient and the y-intercept of the line 2y = −6x + 8?"},"options":[{"af":"Gradiënt −6; y-afsnit 8","en":"Gradient −6; y-intercept 8"},{"af":"Gradiënt 3; y-afsnit −4","en":"Gradient 3; y-intercept −4"},{"af":"Gradiënt −3; y-afsnit 8","en":"Gradient −3; y-intercept 8"},{"af":"Gradiënt −3; y-afsnit 4","en":"Gradient −3; y-intercept 4"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Maak eers y die onderwerp: deel elke term deur 2, dan y = −3x + 4. Dus a = −3 en q = 4. Die algemeenste fout is om net een term (of geen term) deur 2 te deel.","en":"First make y the subject: divide every term by 2, then y = −3x + 4. So a = −3 and q = 4. The most common mistake is to divide only one term (or no term) by 2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = 2x − 6 sny die x-as by x = ___.","en":"The graph of y = 2x − 6 cuts the x-axis at x = ___."},"answers":{"af":["3","x = 3","x=3","(3; 0)","(3;0)","(3,0)"],"en":["3","x = 3","x=3","(3; 0)","(3;0)","(3,0)"]},"explain":{"af":"By die x-afsnit is y = 0: 0 = 2x − 6 → 2x = 6 → x = 3. Die punt is (3; 0).","en":"At the x-intercept y = 0: 0 = 2x − 6 → 2x = 6 → x = 3. The point is (3; 0)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die waardeversameling van f(x) = −2x² + 5?","en":"What is the range of f(x) = −2x² + 5?"},"options":[{"af":"y ≥ 5","en":"y ≥ 5"},{"af":"y < 5","en":"y < 5"},{"af":"y ≤ 5","en":"y ≤ 5"},{"af":"y ∈ ℝ","en":"y ∈ ℝ"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"a = −2 < 0, dus is dit 'n frons met 'n maksimum draaipunt (0; 5). Die hoogste y-waarde is 5 en dit word bereik, dus y ≤ 5, of y ∈ (−∞; 5]. \"y < 5\" laat die draaipunt uit en \"y ≥ 5\" ignoreer die teken van a.","en":"a = −2 < 0, so it is a frown with a maximum turning point (0; 5). The highest y-value is 5 and it is reached, so y ≤ 5, or y ∈ (−∞; 5]. \"y < 5\" leaves out the turning point and \"y ≥ 5\" ignores the sign of a."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 2x² − 50. Die positiewe x-afsnit van f is x = ___.","en":"Given f(x) = 2x² − 50. The positive x-intercept of f is x = ___."},"answers":{"af":["5","x = 5","x=5","(5; 0)","(5;0)","(5,0)"],"en":["5","x = 5","x=5","(5; 0)","(5;0)","(5,0)"]},"explain":{"af":"Stel f(x) = 0: 2x² − 50 = 0 → x² = 25 → x = ±5. Die positiewe afsnit is x = 5. Deel eers deur 2: √50 is verkeerd.","en":"Let f(x) = 0: 2x² − 50 = 0 → x² = 25 → x = ±5. The positive intercept is x = 5. Divide by 2 first: √50 is wrong."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt van die lyn deur (−2; 7) en (4; −5)?","en":"What is the gradient of the line through (−2; 7) and (4; −5)?"},"options":[{"af":"−2","en":"−2"},{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"−½","en":"−½"},{"af":"−6","en":"−6"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"a = (−5 − 7)/(4 − (−2)) = −12/6 = −2. As jy die y's en die x's in verskillende volgordes aftrek, kry jy 2. As jy Δx/Δy bereken, kry jy −½. −6 kom van 4 − 2 in plaas van 4 − (−2).","en":"a = (−5 − 7)/(4 − (−2)) = −12/6 = −2. If you subtract the y's and the x's in different orders you get 2. If you calculate Δx/Δy you get −½. −6 comes from 4 − 2 instead of 4 − (−2)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van f(x) = x² + 4 het twee x-afsnitte.","en":"The graph of f(x) = x² + 4 has two x-intercepts."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. x² + 4 = 0 gee x² = −4, en geen reële getal se kwadraat is negatief nie. Die parabool is 'n glimlag met sy minimum draaipunt (0; 4) bo die x-as, dus sny dit nooit die x-as nie. a en q het dieselfde teken.","en":"False. x² + 4 = 0 gives x² = −4, and no real number squared is negative. The parabola is a smile with its minimum turning point (0; 4) above the x-axis, so it never cuts the x-axis. a and q have the same sign."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vir watter waardes van x is f(x) = −x² + 4 toenemend?","en":"For which values of x is f(x) = −x² + 4 increasing?"},"options":[{"af":"x > 0","en":"x > 0"},{"af":"x < 0","en":"x < 0"},{"af":"y < 4","en":"y < 4"},{"af":"−2 < x < 2","en":"−2 < x < 2"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"a < 0, dus 'n frons met 'n maksimum by (0; 4). Van links af styg die grafiek tot by die draaipunt, dus is f toenemend vir x < 0 en afnemend vir x > 0. \"y < 4\" gee y-waardes, nie x-waardes nie, en −2 < x < 2 is waar f(x) > 0.","en":"a < 0, so a frown with a maximum at (0; 4). From the left the graph rises up to the turning point, so f is increasing for x < 0 and decreasing for x > 0. \"y < 4\" gives y-values, not x-values, and −2 < x < 2 is where f(x) > 0."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Reguit lyn gaan deur (−1; 5) en (2; −4). Wat is die vergelyking van die lyn?","en":"A straight line passes through (−1; 5) and (2; −4). What is the equation of the line?"},"options":[{"af":"y = −3x + 8","en":"y = −3x + 8"},{"af":"y = 3x + 8","en":"y = 3x + 8"},{"af":"y = −3x + 5","en":"y = −3x + 5"},{"af":"y = −3x + 2","en":"y = −3x + 2"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"a = (−4 − 5)/(2 − (−1)) = −9/3 = −3. Vervang (−1; 5): 5 = −3(−1) + q → 5 = 3 + q → q = 2. Kontroleer: −3(2) + 2 = −4 ✓. y = −3x + 8 kom van 'n tekenfout met −3 × −1, en y = −3x + 5 gebruik die y-waarde van 'n punt as q, maar q is net die y-afsnit (x = 0).","en":"a = (−4 − 5)/(2 − (−1)) = −9/3 = −3. Substitute (−1; 5): 5 = −3(−1) + q → 5 = 3 + q → q = 2. Check: −3(2) + 2 = −4 ✓. y = −3x + 8 comes from a sign error with −3 × −1, and y = −3x + 5 uses the y-value of a point as q, but q is only the y-intercept (x = 0)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die parabool y = ax² + q het 'n draaipunt by (0; 5) en gaan deur die punt (2; −7). Bepaal a. a = ___","en":"The parabola y = ax² + q has a turning point at (0; 5) and passes through the point (2; −7). Determine a. a = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","a = -3","a=-3","a = −3","a=−3"],"en":["-3","−3","a = -3","a=-3","a = −3","a=−3"]},"explain":{"af":"q = 5 (die y-koördinaat van die draaipunt). Vervang (2; −7): −7 = a(2)² + 5 → 4a = −12 → a = −3. Dit maak sin: die grafiek daal van 5 na −7, dus is dit 'n frons (a < 0).","en":"q = 5 (the y-coordinate of the turning point). Substitute (2; −7): −7 = a(2)² + 5 → 4a = −12 → a = −3. This makes sense: the graph drops from 5 to −7, so it is a frown (a < 0)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = x² − 1 en g(x) = x + 1. By watter punte sny die twee grafieke mekaar?","en":"Given f(x) = x² − 1 and g(x) = x + 1. At which points do the two graphs intersect?"},"options":[{"af":"(−1; 0) en (2; 3)","en":"(−1; 0) and (2; 3)"},{"af":"(1; 2) en (−2; −1)","en":"(1; 2) and (−2; −1)"},{"af":"(−1; 0) en (1; 0)","en":"(−1; 0) and (1; 0)"},{"af":"(0; −1) en (0; 1)","en":"(0; −1) and (0; 1)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Stel f(x) = g(x): x² − 1 = x + 1 → x² − x − 2 = 0 → (x − 2)(x + 1) = 0 → x = 2 of x = −1. Dan is g(2) = 3 en g(−1) = 0. (1; 2) en (−2; −1) kom van 'n tekenfout in die faktore, (−1; 0) en (1; 0) is net f se x-afsnitte, en (0; −1) en (0; 1) is die twee y-afsnitte.","en":"Set f(x) = g(x): x² − 1 = x + 1 → x² − x − 2 = 0 → (x − 2)(x + 1) = 0 → x = 2 or x = −1. Then g(2) = 3 and g(−1) = 0. (1; 2) and (−2; −1) come from a sign error in the factors, (−1; 0) and (1; 0) are only the x-intercepts of f, and (0; −1) and (0; 1) are the two y-intercepts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Boog oor die ingang van 'n vakansieoord by Hartbeespoortdam het die vorm y = −½x² + 8, met x en y in meter en die grond langs die x-as. Hoe wyd is die boog op grondvlak? ___ m","en":"An arch over the entrance of a holiday resort at Hartbeespoort Dam has the shape y = −½x² + 8, with x and y in metres and the ground along the x-axis. How wide is the arch at ground level? ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["8","8 m","8m"],"en":["8","8 m","8m"]},"explain":{"af":"Die boog raak die grond waar y = 0: −½x² + 8 = 0 → x² = 16 → x = ±4. Die boog strek van x = −4 tot x = 4, dus is dit 4 − (−4) = 8 m wyd. (Dit is ook 8 m hoog by die draaipunt (0; 8).)","en":"The arch touches the ground where y = 0: −½x² + 8 = 0 → x² = 16 → x = ±4. The arch stretches from x = −4 to x = 4, so it is 4 − (−4) = 8 m wide. (It is also 8 m high at the turning point (0; 8).)"}}]},{"id":"w10-t2-funksies-hiperbool-eksponensieel","title":{"af":"Funksies: hiperbool en eksponensiële grafiek","en":"Functions: hyperbola and exponential graph"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hiperbole en eksponensiële grafieke kan skets, hul asimptote, afsnitte en definisie- en waardeversameling kan gee, en hul vergelykings en snypunte kan bepaal.","en":"You will be able to sketch hyperbolas and exponential graphs, give their asymptotes, intercepts, domain and range, and determine their equations and points of intersection."},"summary":{"af":"## Die hiperbool: y = [[a/x]] + q\n\nDie basiese grafiek y = [[1/x]] bestaan uit **twee takke** wat nie aan mekaar raak nie. Jy mag nie deur 0 deel nie, daarom het die grafiek geen punt by x = 0 nie.\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | takke in die 1ste en 3de kwadrant (relatief tot die asimptote); elke tak is afnemend |\n| a < 0 | takke in die 2de en 4de kwadrant; elke tak is toenemend |\n| groter numeriese waarde van a | takke lê verder van die asimptote af |\n| q | skuif die grafiek q eenhede op (q > 0) of af (q < 0) |\n\n- **Asimptoot:** 'n lyn waarna die grafiek al hoe nader kom, maar wat dit nooit raak nie. Die hiperbool het 'n **vertikale asimptoot x = 0** (die y-as) en 'n **horisontale asimptoot y = q**. Teken asimptote as stippellyne.\n- **Definisieversameling:** x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0.\n- **Waardeversameling:** y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ q.\n- **y-afsnit:** **geen**, want x = 0 word nie toegelaat nie.\n- **x-afsnit:** stel y = 0: [[a/x]] + q = 0 → x = [[−a/q]]. As q = 0 is daar geen x-afsnit nie.\n- **Simmetrie-asse:** y = x + q en y = −x + q. Albei gaan deur (0; q), waar die asimptote mekaar sny.\n\n## Die eksponensiële grafiek: y = a · b^{x} + q\n\nHier is b > 0 en b ≠ 1, en die veranderlike x staan in die **eksponent**. Die getal b is die **grondtal**.\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| b > 1 (met a > 0) | toenemend: eksponensiële groei, bv. y = 2^{x} |\n| b tussen 0 en 1 (met a > 0) | afnemend: eksponensiële verval, bv. y = ([[1/2]])^{x} |\n| a > 0 | grafiek lê bo die asimptoot |\n| a < 0 | grafiek lê onder die asimptoot; dit is 'n spieëlbeeld, dus draai toenemend en afnemend om |\n| q | horisontale asimptoot y = q |\n\n- **Asimptoot:** y = q. Daar is geen vertikale asimptoot nie.\n- **Definisieversameling:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Waardeversameling:** as a > 0 is y > q, d.w.s. y ∈ (q; ∞). As a < 0 is y ∈ (−∞; q). Gebruik ronde hakies, want die asimptoot word nooit bereik nie.\n- **y-afsnit:** stel x = 0. Omdat b^{0} = 1, is die y-afsnit (0; a + q).\n- **x-afsnit:** stel y = 0: a · b^{x} = −q → b^{x} = [[−q/a]]. Skryf albei kante met dieselfde grondtal en stel die eksponente gelyk, bv. 2^{x} = 8 = 2^{3} → x = 3. As [[−q/a]] nul of negatief is, is daar **geen** x-afsnit nie.\n- b^{−x} = ([[1/b]])^{x}, dus is y = 2^{−x} dieselfde grafiek as y = ([[1/2]])^{x}.\n- **Volgorde van bewerkings:** in 3 · 2^{x} bereken jy eers 2^{x} en vermenigvuldig dan met 3. By x = 2 is dit 3 · 4 = 12, nie 6^{2} = 36 nie. En −2^{x} beteken −(2^{x}), nie (−2)^{x} nie.\n\n## Skets: stappe\n\n1. Teken die asimptoot (of asimptote) as stippellyne.\n2. Bereken die afsnitte met die asse.\n3. Bereken nog een of twee punte, bv. by x = 1 en x = −1.\n4. Bepaal die vorm uit die tekens van a (en b) en trek 'n gladde kurwe wat die asimptote nader, maar nooit raak nie.\n5. Benoem die afsnitte, die asimptote en die vergelyking.\n\n## Die vergelyking uit 'n grafiek bepaal\n\n- **Hiperbool y = [[a/x]] + q:** lees q van die horisontale asimptoot af. Vervang dan 'n punt op die grafiek en los a op.\n- **Eksponensieel y = a · b^{x} + q:** lees q van die asimptoot af. Gebruik die y-afsnit (0; a + q) om a te kry, of vervang 'n ander punt om b te kry. b moet positief wees, dus verwerp 'n negatiewe waarde van b.\n\n## Snypunte en grafieke lees\n\n- Stel f(x) = g(x) en los op. Met 'n hiperbool: vermenigvuldig albei kante met x (x ≠ 0) om 'n kwadratiese vergelyking te kry, en faktoriseer.\n- Vervang elke x-waarde terug in die eenvoudigste vergelyking om die y-waarde te kry.\n- f(x) > g(x) vra: waar lê f se grafiek **bo** g s'n? By 'n hiperbool moet jy die asimptoot x = 0 in ag neem: die antwoord bestaan dikwels uit twee intervalle.\n- Om 'n waarde van 'n grafiek af te lees, vervang die x-waarde in die vergelyking, bv. f(2).\n\n> **Wenk:** Maak altyd seker jou antwoord pas by die skets. 'n Punt op 'n hiperbool met a > 0 en q = 0 moet in die 1ste of 3de kwadrant lê.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Sê dat 'n hiperbool 'n y-afsnit het.\n- Vergeet x ≠ 0 in die definisieversameling van 'n hiperbool.\n- Skryf y ≥ q vir 'n eksponensiële grafiek (dit moet y > q wees as a > 0).\n- Verwar a · b^{x} met (ab)^{x}.\n- Neem die asimptoot as y = a in plaas van y = q.\n- Behou 'n negatiewe b, of x = 0, as antwoord, al word dit nie toegelaat nie.","en":"## The hyperbola: y = [[a/x]] + q\n\nThe basic graph y = [[1/x]] consists of **two branches** that do not touch each other. You may not divide by 0, so the graph has no point at x = 0.\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | branches in the 1st and 3rd quadrants (relative to the asymptotes); each branch is decreasing |\n| a < 0 | branches in the 2nd and 4th quadrants; each branch is increasing |\n| larger numerical value of a | branches lie further away from the asymptotes |\n| q | shifts the graph q units up (q > 0) or down (q < 0) |\n\n- **Asymptote:** a line that the graph gets closer and closer to, but never touches. The hyperbola has a **vertical asymptote x = 0** (the y-axis) and a **horizontal asymptote y = q**. Draw asymptotes as dotted lines.\n- **Domain:** x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0.\n- **Range:** y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ q.\n- **y-intercept:** **none**, because x = 0 is not allowed.\n- **x-intercept:** let y = 0: [[a/x]] + q = 0 → x = [[−a/q]]. If q = 0 there is no x-intercept.\n- **Axes of symmetry:** y = x + q and y = −x + q. Both pass through (0; q), where the asymptotes intersect.\n\n## The exponential graph: y = a · b^{x} + q\n\nHere b > 0 and b ≠ 1, and the variable x is in the **exponent**. The number b is the **base**.\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| b > 1 (with a > 0) | increasing: exponential growth, e.g. y = 2^{x} |\n| b between 0 and 1 (with a > 0) | decreasing: exponential decay, e.g. y = ([[1/2]])^{x} |\n| a > 0 | graph lies above the asymptote |\n| a < 0 | graph lies below the asymptote; it is a mirror image, so increasing and decreasing swap |\n| q | horizontal asymptote y = q |\n\n- **Asymptote:** y = q. There is no vertical asymptote.\n- **Domain:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Range:** if a > 0 then y > q, i.e. y ∈ (q; ∞). If a < 0 then y ∈ (−∞; q). Use round brackets, because the asymptote is never reached.\n- **y-intercept:** let x = 0. Because b^{0} = 1, the y-intercept is (0; a + q).\n- **x-intercept:** let y = 0: a · b^{x} = −q → b^{x} = [[−q/a]]. Write both sides with the same base and set the exponents equal, e.g. 2^{x} = 8 = 2^{3} → x = 3. If [[−q/a]] is zero or negative, there is **no** x-intercept.\n- b^{−x} = ([[1/b]])^{x}, so y = 2^{−x} is the same graph as y = ([[1/2]])^{x}.\n- **Order of operations:** in 3 · 2^{x} you first calculate 2^{x} and then multiply by 3. At x = 2 it is 3 · 4 = 12, not 6^{2} = 36. And −2^{x} means −(2^{x}), not (−2)^{x}.\n\n## Sketching: steps\n\n1. Draw the asymptote (or asymptotes) as dotted lines.\n2. Calculate the intercepts with the axes.\n3. Calculate one or two more points, e.g. at x = 1 and x = −1.\n4. Decide on the shape from the signs of a (and b) and draw a smooth curve that approaches the asymptotes but never touches them.\n5. Label the intercepts, the asymptotes and the equation.\n\n## Determining the equation from a graph\n\n- **Hyperbola y = [[a/x]] + q:** read q from the horizontal asymptote. Then substitute a point on the graph and solve for a.\n- **Exponential y = a · b^{x} + q:** read q from the asymptote. Use the y-intercept (0; a + q) to find a, or substitute another point to find b. b must be positive, so reject a negative value of b.\n\n## Points of intersection and reading graphs\n\n- Set f(x) = g(x) and solve. With a hyperbola: multiply both sides by x (x ≠ 0) to get a quadratic equation, and factorise.\n- Substitute each x-value back into the simplest equation to get the y-value.\n- f(x) > g(x) asks: where is the graph of f **above** the graph of g? With a hyperbola you must take the asymptote x = 0 into account: the answer often consists of two intervals.\n- To read a value from a graph, substitute the x-value into the equation, e.g. f(2).\n\n> **Tip:** Always check that your answer fits the sketch. A point on a hyperbola with a > 0 and q = 0 must lie in the 1st or 3rd quadrant.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Saying that a hyperbola has a y-intercept.\n- Forgetting x ≠ 0 in the domain of a hyperbola.\n- Writing y ≥ q for an exponential graph (it must be y > q if a > 0).\n- Confusing a · b^{x} with (ab)^{x}.\n- Taking the asymptote as y = a instead of y = q.\n- Keeping a negative b, or x = 0, as an answer even though it is not allowed."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hiperbool","en":"Hyperbola"},"def":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a/x + q: twee afsonderlike takke wat twee asimptote nader.","en":"The graph of y = a/x + q: two separate branches that approach two asymptotes."}},{"term":{"af":"Asimptoot","en":"Asymptote"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn waarna 'n grafiek al hoe nader kom, maar wat dit nooit raak nie.","en":"A line that a graph gets closer and closer to, but never touches."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertikale asimptoot","en":"Vertical asymptote"},"def":{"af":"By y = a/x + q is dit die lyn x = 0, want jy kan nie deur 0 deel nie.","en":"For y = a/x + q it is the line x = 0, because you cannot divide by 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Horisontale asimptoot","en":"Horizontal asymptote"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn y = q by y = a/x + q en by y = a · bˣ + q.","en":"The line y = q for y = a/x + q and for y = a · bˣ + q."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponensiële funksie","en":"Exponential function"},"def":{"af":"'n Funksie van die vorm y = a · bˣ + q (b > 0, b ≠ 1) waarin die veranderlike in die eksponent staan.","en":"A function of the form y = a · bˣ + q (b > 0, b ≠ 1) in which the variable is in the exponent."}},{"term":{"af":"Grondtal","en":"Base"},"def":{"af":"Die getal b in y = a · bˣ + q. Dit moet positief wees en mag nie 1 wees nie.","en":"The number b in y = a · bˣ + q. It must be positive and may not be 1."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponensiële groei en verval","en":"Exponential growth and decay"},"def":{"af":"Groei: die waardes word al vinniger groter (b > 1). Verval: die waardes neem af na die asimptoot toe (b tussen 0 en 1).","en":"Growth: the values increase faster and faster (b > 1). Decay: the values decrease towards the asymptote (b between 0 and 1)."}},{"term":{"af":"Snypunt","en":"Point of intersection"},"def":{"af":"'n Punt wat op albei grafieke lê. Jy vind dit deur f(x) = g(x) op te los.","en":"A point that lies on both graphs. You find it by solving f(x) = g(x)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Eienskappe van 'n hiperbool","en":"Features of a hyperbola"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 6/x − 2. Bepaal die asimptote, die afsnitte, die definisie- en waardeversameling, en twee ekstra punte vir die skets.","en":"Given f(x) = 6/x − 2. Determine the asymptotes, the intercepts, the domain and range, and two extra points for the sketch."},"steps":[{"af":"Asimptote: vertikaal x = 0 en horisontaal y = q = −2.","en":"Asymptotes: vertical x = 0 and horizontal y = q = −2."},{"af":"y-afsnit: geen, want x = 0 word nie toegelaat nie.","en":"y-intercept: none, because x = 0 is not allowed."},{"af":"x-afsnit: 0 = [[6/x]] − 2 → [[6/x]] = 2 → 6 = 2x → x = 3. Die punt is (3; 0).","en":"x-intercept: 0 = [[6/x]] − 2 → [[6/x]] = 2 → 6 = 2x → x = 3. The point is (3; 0)."},{"af":"a = 6 > 0, dus lê die takke in die 1ste en 3de kwadrant relatief tot die asimptote. Ekstra punte: f(1) = 6 − 2 = 4 → (1; 4) en f(−3) = −2 − 2 = −4 → (−3; −4).","en":"a = 6 > 0, so the branches lie in the 1st and 3rd quadrants relative to the asymptotes. Extra points: f(1) = 6 − 2 = 4 → (1; 4) and f(−3) = −2 − 2 = −4 → (−3; −4)."},{"af":"Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0. Waardeversameling: y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −2.","en":"Domain: x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0. Range: y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −2."}],"answer":{"af":"Asimptote x = 0 en y = −2; x-afsnit (3; 0); geen y-afsnit; x ≠ 0; y ≠ −2","en":"Asymptotes x = 0 and y = −2; x-intercept (3; 0); no y-intercept; x ≠ 0; y ≠ −2"}},{"title":{"af":"Eksponensiële grafiek met a < 0","en":"Exponential graph with a < 0"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee g(x) = −2ˣ + 4. Bepaal die asimptoot, die afsnitte, die definisie- en waardeversameling, en of g toenemend of afnemend is.","en":"Given g(x) = −2ˣ + 4. Determine the asymptote, the intercepts, the domain and range, and whether g is increasing or decreasing."},"steps":[{"af":"Hier is a = −1, b = 2 en q = 4. Let op: −2^{x} beteken −(2^{x}).","en":"Here a = −1, b = 2 and q = 4. Note: −2^{x} means −(2^{x})."},{"af":"Asimptoot: y = 4.","en":"Asymptote: y = 4."},{"af":"y-afsnit: g(0) = −2^{0} + 4 = −1 + 4 = 3 → (0; 3)","en":"y-intercept: g(0) = −2^{0} + 4 = −1 + 4 = 3 → (0; 3)"},{"af":"x-afsnit: 0 = −2^{x} + 4 → 2^{x} = 4 = 2^{2} → x = 2 → (2; 0)","en":"x-intercept: 0 = −2^{x} + 4 → 2^{x} = 4 = 2^{2} → x = 2 → (2; 0)"},{"af":"a < 0, dus lê die grafiek onder die asimptoot. Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ. Waardeversameling: y < 4, d.w.s. y ∈ (−∞; 4).","en":"a < 0, so the graph lies below the asymptote. Domain: x ∈ ℝ. Range: y < 4, i.e. y ∈ (−∞; 4)."},{"af":"b > 1 maar a < 0, dus is die grafiek omgekeer: g is afnemend (dit daal van links na regs).","en":"b > 1 but a < 0, so the graph is flipped: g is decreasing (it falls from left to right)."}],"answer":{"af":"Asimptoot y = 4; afsnitte (0; 3) en (2; 0); y ∈ (−∞; 4); afnemend","en":"Asymptote y = 4; intercepts (0; 3) and (2; 0); y ∈ (−∞; 4); decreasing"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelykings uit grafiekkenmerke","en":"Equations from graph features"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Die hiperbool h(x) = a/x + q het 'n horisontale asimptoot y = 3 en gaan deur (2; 1). Bepaal h(x). (b) Die grafiek van k(x) = bˣ + q het 'n asimptoot y = −1 en gaan deur (2; 8). Bepaal k(x).","en":"(a) The hyperbola h(x) = a/x + q has a horizontal asymptote y = 3 and passes through (2; 1). Determine h(x). (b) The graph of k(x) = bˣ + q has an asymptote y = −1 and passes through (2; 8). Determine k(x)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die horisontale asimptoot is y = 3, dus q = 3 en h(x) = [[a/x]] + 3.","en":"(a) The horizontal asymptote is y = 3, so q = 3 and h(x) = [[a/x]] + 3."},{"af":"Vervang (2; 1): 1 = [[a/2]] + 3 → [[a/2]] = −2 → a = −4. Dus h(x) = [[−4/x]] + 3.","en":"Substitute (2; 1): 1 = [[a/2]] + 3 → [[a/2]] = −2 → a = −4. So h(x) = [[−4/x]] + 3."},{"af":"(b) Die asimptoot is y = −1, dus q = −1 en k(x) = b^{x} − 1.","en":"(b) The asymptote is y = −1, so q = −1 and k(x) = b^{x} − 1."},{"af":"Vervang (2; 8): 8 = b^{2} − 1 → b^{2} = 9 → b = 3 of b = −3","en":"Substitute (2; 8): 8 = b^{2} − 1 → b^{2} = 9 → b = 3 or b = −3"},{"af":"Die grondtal moet positief wees, dus b = 3 en k(x) = 3^{x} − 1. Kontroleer: 3^{2} − 1 = 8 ✓","en":"The base must be positive, so b = 3 and k(x) = 3^{x} − 1. Check: 3^{2} − 1 = 8 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"h(x) = −4/x + 3; k(x) = 3ˣ − 1","en":"h(x) = −4/x + 3; k(x) = 3ˣ − 1"}},{"title":{"af":"Snypunte van 'n hiperbool en 'n lyn","en":"Points of intersection of a hyperbola and a line"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 4/x en g(x) = x + 3. (a) Bepaal die koördinate van die snypunte van f en g. (b) Vir watter waardes van x is f(x) > g(x)?","en":"Given f(x) = 4/x and g(x) = x + 3. (a) Determine the coordinates of the points of intersection of f and g. (b) For which values of x is f(x) > g(x)?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Stel f(x) = g(x): [[4/x]] = x + 3","en":"(a) Set f(x) = g(x): [[4/x]] = x + 3"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met x (x ≠ 0): 4 = x^{2} + 3x → x^{2} + 3x − 4 = 0","en":"Multiply by x (x ≠ 0): 4 = x^{2} + 3x → x^{2} + 3x − 4 = 0"},{"af":"Faktoriseer: (x + 4)(x − 1) = 0 → x = −4 of x = 1","en":"Factorise: (x + 4)(x − 1) = 0 → x = −4 or x = 1"},{"af":"y-waardes uit g: g(−4) = −1 en g(1) = 4. Die snypunte is (−4; −1) en (1; 4).","en":"y-values from g: g(−4) = −1 and g(1) = 4. The points of intersection are (−4; −1) and (1; 4)."},{"af":"(b) Die hiperbool lê bo die lyn links van x = −4, en tussen die asimptoot x = 0 en x = 1. Toets: f(−5) = −0,8 > g(−5) = −2 ✓ en f(0,5) = 8 > g(0,5) = 3,5 ✓","en":"(b) The hyperbola lies above the line to the left of x = −4, and between the asymptote x = 0 and x = 1. Test: f(−5) = −0.8 > g(−5) = −2 ✓ and f(0.5) = 8 > g(0.5) = 3.5 ✓"},{"af":"Antwoord: x < −4 of 0 < x < 1. x = 0 is uitgesluit, want f bestaan nie daar nie.","en":"Answer: x < −4 or 0 < x < 1. x = 0 is excluded, because f does not exist there."}],"answer":{"af":"(−4; −1) en (1; 4); x < −4 of 0 < x < 1","en":"(−4; −1) and (1; 4); x < −4 or 0 < x < 1"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n eksponensiële funksie?","en":"Which one of the following is an exponential function?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 3x²","en":"y = 3x²"},{"af":"y = 3/x","en":"y = 3/x"},{"af":"y = 3 · 2ˣ","en":"y = 3 · 2ˣ"},{"af":"y = 3x + 2","en":"y = 3x + 2"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"By 'n eksponensiële funksie staan die veranderlike x in die eksponent: y = a · bˣ + q. y = 3x² is 'n parabool, y = 3/x 'n hiperbool en y = 3x + 2 'n reguit lyn.","en":"In an exponential function the variable x is in the exponent: y = a · bˣ + q. y = 3x² is a parabola, y = 3/x a hyperbola and y = 3x + 2 a straight line."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die waardeversameling van y = 2ˣ + 3 is y ≥ 3.","en":"The range of y = 2ˣ + 3 is y ≥ 3."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. y = 3 is 'n asimptoot: die grafiek kom al hoe nader, maar raak dit nooit. Omdat a > 0 is die waardeversameling y > 3, d.w.s. y ∈ (3; ∞).","en":"False. y = 3 is an asymptote: the graph gets closer and closer but never touches it. Because a > 0 the range is y > 3, i.e. y ∈ (3; ∞)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vergelyking by die beskrywing van sy grafiek.","en":"Match each equation to the description of its graph."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"y = 2ˣ","en":"y = 2ˣ"},"r":{"af":"Toenemend; gaan deur (0; 1)","en":"Increasing; passes through (0; 1)"}},{"l":{"af":"y = (½)ˣ","en":"y = (½)ˣ"},"r":{"af":"Afnemend; gaan deur (0; 1)","en":"Decreasing; passes through (0; 1)"}},{"l":{"af":"y = 2/x","en":"y = 2/x"},"r":{"af":"Takke in die 1ste en 3de kwadrant","en":"Branches in the 1st and 3rd quadrants"}},{"l":{"af":"y = −2/x","en":"y = −2/x"},"r":{"af":"Takke in die 2de en 4de kwadrant","en":"Branches in the 2nd and 4th quadrants"}}],"explain":{"af":"By y = bˣ is die y-afsnit altyd (0; 1), want b⁰ = 1. b > 1 gee groei en b tussen 0 en 1 gee verval. By y = a/x bepaal die teken van a die kwadrante: a > 0 gee 1ste en 3de, a < 0 gee 2de en 4de.","en":"For y = bˣ the y-intercept is always (0; 1), because b⁰ = 1. b > 1 gives growth and b between 0 and 1 gives decay. For y = a/x the sign of a decides the quadrants: a > 0 gives 1st and 3rd, a < 0 gives 2nd and 4th."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die definisieversameling van y = 3/x − 1?","en":"What is the domain of y = 3/x − 1?"},"options":[{"af":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0","en":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0"},{"af":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ −1","en":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ −1"},{"af":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −1","en":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −1"},{"af":"x ∈ ℝ","en":"x ∈ ℝ"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Jy mag nie deur 0 deel nie, dus x ≠ 0. Die −1 (dit is q) beïnvloed die waardeversameling (y ≠ −1), nie die definisieversameling nie.","en":"You may not divide by 0, so x ≠ 0. The −1 (that is q) affects the range (y ≠ −1), not the domain."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die asimptote van y = −4/x + 2?","en":"What are the asymptotes of y = −4/x + 2?"},"options":[{"af":"x = 2 en y = 0","en":"x = 2 and y = 0"},{"af":"x = 0 en y = −4","en":"x = 0 and y = −4"},{"af":"x = −4 en y = 2","en":"x = −4 and y = 2"},{"af":"x = 0 en y = 2","en":"x = 0 and y = 2"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By y = a/x + q is die vertikale asimptoot altyd x = 0 en die horisontale asimptoot y = q = 2. Die a-waarde (−4) bepaal net die kwadrante en die vorm, nie die asimptote nie.","en":"For y = a/x + q the vertical asymptote is always x = 0 and the horizontal asymptote is y = q = 2. The a-value (−4) only decides the quadrants and the shape, not the asymptotes."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die y-afsnit van y = 3 · 2ˣ − 5 is (0; ___).","en":"The y-intercept of y = 3 · 2ˣ − 5 is (0; ___)."},"answers":{"af":["-2","−2","y = -2","y=-2","y = −2","y=−2","(0;-2)","(0;−2)"],"en":["-2","−2","y = -2","y=-2","y = −2","y=−2","(0;-2)","(0;−2)"]},"explain":{"af":"Stel x = 0: 2⁰ = 1, dus y = 3(1) − 5 = −2. Die y-afsnit is (0; −2). Kortpad: die y-afsnit is a + q = 3 + (−5).","en":"Let x = 0: 2⁰ = 1, so y = 3(1) − 5 = −2. The y-intercept is (0; −2). Shortcut: the y-intercept is a + q = 3 + (−5)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hiperbool y = 6/x + 2 sny die x-as by x = ___.","en":"The hyperbola y = 6/x + 2 cuts the x-axis at x = ___."},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","x = -3","x=-3","x = −3","x=−3","(-3;0)","(−3;0)","(-3,0)","(−3,0)"],"en":["-3","−3","x = -3","x=-3","x = −3","x=−3","(-3;0)","(−3;0)","(-3,0)","(−3,0)"]},"explain":{"af":"Stel y = 0: 6/x + 2 = 0 → 6/x = −2 → 6 = −2x → x = −3. Die x-afsnit is (−3; 0).","en":"Let y = 0: 6/x + 2 = 0 → 6/x = −2 → 6 = −2x → x = −3. The x-intercept is (−3; 0)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = 5 · (0,4)ˣ is afnemend (dalend).","en":"The graph of y = 5 · (0.4)ˣ is decreasing."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die grondtal 0,4 lê tussen 0 en 1 en a = 5 > 0, dus word die y-waardes kleiner soos x groter word: eksponensiële verval.","en":"True. The base 0.4 lies between 0 and 1 and a = 5 > 0, so the y-values get smaller as x gets bigger: exponential decay."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die waardeversameling van f(x) = −2 · 3ˣ + 4?","en":"What is the range of f(x) = −2 · 3ˣ + 4?"},"options":[{"af":"y > 4","en":"y > 4"},{"af":"y < 4","en":"y < 4"},{"af":"y ≤ 4","en":"y ≤ 4"},{"af":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ 4","en":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ 4"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die asimptoot is y = 4. a = −2 < 0, dus lê die grafiek onder die asimptoot: y < 4. Gebruik < en nie ≤ nie, want die asimptoot word nooit bereik nie. \"y ≠ 4\" is die soort waardeversameling wat 'n hiperbool het.","en":"The asymptote is y = 4. a = −2 < 0, so the graph lies below the asymptote: y < 4. Use < and not ≤, because the asymptote is never reached. \"y ≠ 4\" is the kind of range a hyperbola has."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die x-afsnit van g(x) = 2ˣ − 8?","en":"What is the x-intercept of g(x) = 2ˣ − 8?"},"options":[{"af":"(3; 0)","en":"(3; 0)"},{"af":"(4; 0)","en":"(4; 0)"},{"af":"(0; −7)","en":"(0; −7)"},{"af":"(−3; 0)","en":"(−3; 0)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Stel g(x) = 0: 2ˣ = 8 = 2³, dus x = 3. (4; 0) kom van 8 ÷ 2, maar 2ˣ beteken nie 2 × x nie. (0; −7) is die y-afsnit.","en":"Let g(x) = 0: 2ˣ = 8 = 2³, so x = 3. (4; 0) comes from 8 ÷ 2, but 2ˣ does not mean 2 × x. (0; −7) is the y-intercept."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die hiperbool y = a/x + q het 'n horisontale asimptoot y = −1 en gaan deur die punt (2; 3). Wat is die vergelyking van die hiperbool?","en":"The hyperbola y = a/x + q has a horizontal asymptote y = −1 and passes through the point (2; 3). What is the equation of the hyperbola?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 4/x − 1","en":"y = 4/x − 1"},{"af":"y = 8/x + 1","en":"y = 8/x + 1"},{"af":"y = 8/x − 1","en":"y = 8/x − 1"},{"af":"y = 2/x − 1","en":"y = 2/x − 1"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"q = −1. Vervang (2; 3): 3 = a/2 − 1 → a/2 = 4 → a = 8. Dus y = 8/x − 1. y = 4/x − 1 vergeet om met 2 te vermenigvuldig, y = 2/x − 1 deel in plaas daarvan, en y = 8/x + 1 het die verkeerde teken vir q.","en":"q = −1. Substitute (2; 3): 3 = a/2 − 1 → a/2 = 4 → a = 8. So y = 8/x − 1. y = 4/x − 1 forgets to multiply by 2, y = 2/x − 1 divides instead, and y = 8/x + 1 has the wrong sign for q."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = bˣ − 4 gaan deur die punt (2; 21). Bepaal b. b = ___","en":"The graph of y = bˣ − 4 passes through the point (2; 21). Determine b. b = ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","b = 5","b=5"],"en":["5","b = 5","b=5"]},"explain":{"af":"21 = b² − 4 → b² = 25 → b = ±5. By 'n eksponensiële funksie moet die grondtal positief wees, dus b = 5 (verwerp −5).","en":"21 = b² − 4 → b² = 25 → b = ±5. In an exponential function the base must be positive, so b = 5 (reject −5)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 6/x en g(x) = x + 1. Wat is die snypunte van f en g?","en":"Given f(x) = 6/x and g(x) = x + 1. What are the points of intersection of f and g?"},"options":[{"af":"(−2; −3) en (3; 2)","en":"(−2; −3) and (3; 2)"},{"af":"(2; 3) en (−3; −2)","en":"(2; 3) and (−3; −2)"},{"af":"(0; 1) en (−1; 0)","en":"(0; 1) and (−1; 0)"},{"af":"Slegs (2; 3)","en":"Only (2; 3)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"6/x = x + 1 → 6 = x² + x → x² + x − 6 = 0 → (x + 3)(x − 2) = 0 → x = −3 of x = 2. g(−3) = −2 en g(2) = 3. Die hiperbool het twee takke, dus moenie die negatiewe oplossing weggooi nie. (−2; −3) en (3; 2) kom van 'n tekenfout in die faktore, en (0; 1) en (−1; 0) is net g se afsnitte.","en":"6/x = x + 1 → 6 = x² + x → x² + x − 6 = 0 → (x + 3)(x − 2) = 0 → x = −3 or x = 2. g(−3) = −2 and g(2) = 3. The hyperbola has two branches, so don't throw away the negative solution. (−2; −3) and (3; 2) come from a sign error in the factors, and (0; 1) and (−1; 0) are only the intercepts of g."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die aantal bakterieë in 'n watermonster uit die Hartbeespoortdam word gegee deur N = 200 · 2ᵗ, met t die tyd in ure. Na hoeveel uur is daar 3 200 bakterieë? ___ uur","en":"The number of bacteria in a water sample from Hartbeespoort Dam is given by N = 200 · 2ᵗ, with t the time in hours. After how many hours are there 3 200 bacteria? ___ hours"},"answers":{"af":["4","4 uur","t = 4","t=4","4 h","4h"],"en":["4","4 hours","t = 4","t=4","4 h","4h"]},"explain":{"af":"3 200 = 200 · 2ᵗ → deel albei kante deur 200: 2ᵗ = 16 = 2⁴ → t = 4 uur. Moenie eers 200 · 2 = 400 uitwerk nie: die eksponent behoort net by die 2.","en":"3 200 = 200 · 2ᵗ → divide both sides by 200: 2ᵗ = 16 = 2⁴ → t = 4 hours. Don't work out 200 · 2 = 400 first: the exponent belongs only to the 2."}}]},{"id":"w10-t2-trig-grafieke","title":{"af":"Trigonometriese grafieke","en":"Trigonometric graphs"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die grafieke van y = a sin θ + q, y = a cos θ + q en y = a tan θ + q kan skets, hul eienskappe kan neerskryf, a en q uit 'n grafiek kan bepaal en grafieke kan lees.","en":"You will be able to sketch the graphs of y = a sin θ + q, y = a cos θ + q and y = a tan θ + q, write down their properties, determine a and q from a graph and read graphs."},"summary":{"af":"## Die basiese grafieke vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°\n\nLeer hierdie sleutelpunte. Elke skets begin hier.\n\n| θ | 0° | 90° | 180° | 270° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin θ | 0 | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 |\n| cos θ | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 | 1 |\n\n| θ | 0° | 45° | 90° | 135° | 180° | 225° | 270° | 315° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| tan θ | 0 | 1 | ongedefinieerd | −1 | 0 | 1 | ongedefinieerd | −1 | 0 |\n\n| Eienskap | y = sin θ | y = cos θ | y = tan θ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Periode | 360° | 360° | 180° |\n| Amplitude | 1 | 1 | geen |\n| Maksimum | 1 by θ = 90° | 1 by θ = 0° en 360° | geen |\n| Minimum | −1 by θ = 270° | −1 by θ = 180° | geen |\n| Waardeversameling | [−1; 1] | [−1; 1] | y ∈ ℝ |\n| Asimptote | geen | geen | θ = 90° en θ = 270° |\n| Snypunte met die θ-as | 0°, 180°, 360° | 90°, 270° | 0°, 180°, 360° |\n\n- **Periode:** die horisontale lengte van een volledige siklus (een golf) voordat die patroon herhaal.\n- **Amplitude:** die helfte van die verskil tussen die maksimum- en minimumwaarde: amplitude = [[maks − min/2]]. Dit is altyd positief.\n- **Definisieversameling:** in Gr 10 altyd 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. By 90° en 270° is tan θ ongedefinieerd. Daar is **vertikale asimptote** (stippellyne) wat die grafiek nooit raak nie.\n\n## Die effek van a: y = a sin θ, y = a cos θ, y = a tan θ\n\n- Elke y-waarde word met a vermenigvuldig. Die **amplitude word |a|**: y = 3 sin θ wissel tussen −3 en 3.\n- As a < 0, word die grafiek in die x-as **gereflekteer** (onderstebo gedraai). y = −2 cos θ begin dus by (0°; −2).\n- By tan verander a die steilheid: die punt (45°; 1) skuif na (45°; a).\n- a verander **nie** die periode of die asimptote nie.\n\n## Die effek van q: y = a sin θ + q, ens.\n\n- Die hele grafiek skuif **vertikaal** met q eenhede: op as q > 0 en af as q < 0.\n- Die golf beweeg nou op en af om die lyn y = q.\n- Maksimum = q + |a| en minimum = q − |a|, dus is die waardeversameling [q − |a|; q + |a|].\n- q verander **nie** die amplitude, die periode of tan se asimptote nie. Vir y = a tan θ + q bly die waardeversameling y ∈ ℝ.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** By y = 2 cos θ − 1 is die amplitude 2, nie 1 of 3 nie. q skuif die grafiek net op of af.\n\n## Hoe om te skets\n\n1. Identifiseer die basiese grafiek, a en q.\n2. Maak 'n tabel met die sleutelpunte: vermenigvuldig die basiese y-waardes met a en tel dan q by.\n3. Stip die punte en trek 'n gladde kromme. Golwe het ronde draaipunte, nie skerp punte nie.\n4. Benoem die grafiek, die y-afsnit, die draaipunte en die eindpunte. By tan trek jy die asimptote θ = 90° en θ = 270° as stippellyne.\n\nVoorbeeld: y = 2 sin θ + 1 gaan deur (0°; 1), (90°; 3), (180°; 1), (270°; −1) en (360°; 1). Die amplitude is 2 en die waardeversameling [−1; 3].\n\n## Bepaal a en q uit 'n grafiek\n\n**sin en cos:** q = [[maks + min/2]] en |a| = [[maks − min/2]].\n\n- **Teken van a:** As y = a sin θ + q vanaf (0°; q) eers **afgaan**, is a < 0. As y = a cos θ + q by θ = 0° 'n **minimum** het, is a < 0.\n- Of vervang twee punte en los gelyktydig op. Bv. y = a cos θ + q gaan deur (0°; 5) en (180°; 1): a + q = 5 en −a + q = 1, dus q = 3 en a = 2.\n\n**tan:** By θ = 0° is tan θ = 0, dus lê (0°; q) op die grafiek. By θ = 45° is tan θ = 1, dus lê (45°; a + q) op die grafiek.\n\n## Lees van grafieke\n\n- **Snypunte van f en g:** waar f(θ) = g(θ). Bv. y = sin θ en y = cos θ sny by θ = 45° en θ = 225°.\n- **f(θ) > g(θ):** waar die grafiek van f bó dié van g lê. Gebruik streng ongelykhede (die tekens > en <), want by die snypunte is f(θ) = g(θ). Die tekens ≥ en ≤ sluit die snypunte in.\n- **f(θ) × g(θ) < 0:** waar een grafiek bo en die ander onder die θ-as lê (teenoorgestelde tekens).\n- **Toenemend en afnemend:** y = sin θ neem toe vir 0° < θ < 90° en 270° < θ < 360°; y = cos θ neem af vir 0° < θ < 180°.\n- **Aantal oplossings:** Die vergelyking f(θ) = k het soveel oplossings as wat die horisontale lyn y = k die grafiek sny.\n\n> **Wenk:** Skryf 'n waardeversameling as [min; maks] of as min ≤ y ≤ maks. Vierkantige hakies sluit die eindpunte in.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** tan θ het geen amplitude, maksimum of minimum nie. Die punt (45°; 1) is net 'n punt op die kromme, nie 'n draaipunt nie.","en":"## The basic graphs for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°\n\nLearn these key points. Every sketch starts here.\n\n| θ | 0° | 90° | 180° | 270° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin θ | 0 | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 |\n| cos θ | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 | 1 |\n\n| θ | 0° | 45° | 90° | 135° | 180° | 225° | 270° | 315° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| tan θ | 0 | 1 | undefined | −1 | 0 | 1 | undefined | −1 | 0 |\n\n| Property | y = sin θ | y = cos θ | y = tan θ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Period | 360° | 360° | 180° |\n| Amplitude | 1 | 1 | none |\n| Maximum | 1 at θ = 90° | 1 at θ = 0° and 360° | none |\n| Minimum | −1 at θ = 270° | −1 at θ = 180° | none |\n| Range | [−1; 1] | [−1; 1] | y ∈ ℝ |\n| Asymptotes | none | none | θ = 90° and θ = 270° |\n| Intercepts with the θ-axis | 0°, 180°, 360° | 90°, 270° | 0°, 180°, 360° |\n\n- **Period:** the horizontal length of one complete cycle (one wave) before the pattern repeats.\n- **Amplitude:** half the difference between the maximum and minimum values: amplitude = [[max − min/2]]. It is always positive.\n- **Domain:** in Gr 10 always 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. At 90° and 270° tan θ is undefined. There are **vertical asymptotes** (dotted lines) that the graph never touches.\n\n## The effect of a: y = a sin θ, y = a cos θ, y = a tan θ\n\n- Every y-value is multiplied by a. The **amplitude becomes |a|**: y = 3 sin θ varies between −3 and 3.\n- If a < 0, the graph is **reflected** in the x-axis (turned upside down). So y = −2 cos θ starts at (0°; −2).\n- For tan, a changes the steepness: the point (45°; 1) moves to (45°; a).\n- a does **not** change the period or the asymptotes.\n\n## The effect of q: y = a sin θ + q, etc.\n\n- The whole graph shifts **vertically** by q units: up if q > 0 and down if q < 0.\n- The wave now moves up and down around the line y = q.\n- Maximum = q + |a| and minimum = q − |a|, so the range is [q − |a|; q + |a|].\n- q does **not** change the amplitude, the period or the asymptotes of tan. For y = a tan θ + q the range stays y ∈ ℝ.\n\n> **Common mistake:** For y = 2 cos θ − 1 the amplitude is 2, not 1 or 3. q only moves the graph up or down.\n\n## How to sketch\n\n1. Identify the basic graph, a and q.\n2. Make a table of the key points: multiply the basic y-values by a and then add q.\n3. Plot the points and draw a smooth curve. Waves have rounded turning points, not sharp points.\n4. Label the graph, the y-intercept, the turning points and the end points. For tan, draw the asymptotes θ = 90° and θ = 270° as dotted lines.\n\nExample: y = 2 sin θ + 1 passes through (0°; 1), (90°; 3), (180°; 1), (270°; −1) and (360°; 1). The amplitude is 2 and the range [−1; 3].\n\n## Determining a and q from a graph\n\n**sin and cos:** q = [[max + min/2]] and |a| = [[max − min/2]].\n\n- **Sign of a:** If y = a sin θ + q first goes **down** from (0°; q), then a < 0. If y = a cos θ + q has a **minimum** at θ = 0°, then a < 0.\n- Or substitute two points and solve simultaneously. E.g. y = a cos θ + q passes through (0°; 5) and (180°; 1): a + q = 5 and −a + q = 1, so q = 3 and a = 2.\n\n**tan:** At θ = 0°, tan θ = 0, so (0°; q) lies on the graph. At θ = 45°, tan θ = 1, so (45°; a + q) lies on the graph.\n\n## Reading graphs\n\n- **Points of intersection of f and g:** where f(θ) = g(θ). E.g. y = sin θ and y = cos θ intersect at θ = 45° and θ = 225°.\n- **f(θ) > g(θ):** where the graph of f lies above that of g. Use strict inequalities (the signs > and <), because at the points of intersection f(θ) = g(θ). The signs ≥ and ≤ include the points of intersection.\n- **f(θ) × g(θ) < 0:** where one graph lies above and the other below the θ-axis (opposite signs).\n- **Increasing and decreasing:** y = sin θ increases for 0° < θ < 90° and 270° < θ < 360°; y = cos θ decreases for 0° < θ < 180°.\n- **Number of solutions:** The equation f(θ) = k has as many solutions as the number of times the horizontal line y = k cuts the graph.\n\n> **Tip:** Write a range as [min; max] or as min ≤ y ≤ max. Square brackets include the end points.\n\n> **Common mistake:** tan θ has no amplitude, maximum or minimum. The point (45°; 1) is just a point on the curve, not a turning point."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Periode","en":"Period"},"def":{"af":"Die horisontale lengte van een volledige siklus van die grafiek: 360° vir sin en cos, 180° vir tan.","en":"The horizontal length of one complete cycle of the graph: 360° for sin and cos, 180° for tan."}},{"term":{"af":"Amplitude","en":"Amplitude"},"def":{"af":"Die helfte van die verskil tussen die maksimum- en minimumwaarde van 'n sin- of cos-grafiek; vir y = a sin θ + q is dit |a|.","en":"Half the difference between the maximum and minimum values of a sin or cos graph; for y = a sin θ + q it is |a|."}},{"term":{"af":"Waardeversameling","en":"Range"},"def":{"af":"Al die y-waardes wat die grafiek aanneem, bv. [q − |a|; q + |a|] vir sin en cos.","en":"All the y-values the graph takes on, e.g. [q − |a|; q + |a|] for sin and cos."}},{"term":{"af":"Definisieversameling","en":"Domain"},"def":{"af":"Al die θ-waardes waarvoor die grafiek geskets word; in Gr 10 is dit 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°.","en":"All the θ-values for which the graph is sketched; in Gr 10 it is 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°."}},{"term":{"af":"Asimptoot","en":"Asymptote"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn wat die grafiek nader maar nooit raak nie; y = tan θ het vertikale asimptote by θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"A line that the graph approaches but never touches; y = tan θ has vertical asymptotes at θ = 90° and θ = 270°."}},{"term":{"af":"Maksimum- en minimumwaarde","en":"Maximum and minimum value"},"def":{"af":"Die grootste en kleinste y-waarde van die grafiek: q + |a| en q − |a| vir sin en cos.","en":"The greatest and smallest y-value of the graph: q + |a| and q − |a| for sin and cos."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertikale skuif","en":"Vertical shift"},"def":{"af":"Die effek van q: die hele grafiek skuif q eenhede op (q > 0) of af (q < 0).","en":"The effect of q: the whole graph moves q units up (q > 0) or down (q < 0)."}},{"term":{"af":"Refleksie in die x-as","en":"Reflection in the x-axis"},"def":{"af":"Die effek van a < 0: die grafiek word onderstebo gedraai, sodat maksimums minimums word.","en":"The effect of a < 0: the graph is turned upside down, so maximums become minimums."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Eienskappe van y = a cos θ + q","en":"Properties of y = a cos θ + q"},"problem":{"af":"Beskou f(θ) = 3 cos θ + 1 vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. (a) Bepaal die sleutelpunte vir 'n skets. (b) Skryf die amplitude, periode, maksimum- en minimumwaarde en die waardeversameling neer.","en":"Consider f(θ) = 3 cos θ + 1 for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. (a) Determine the key points for a sketch. (b) Write down the amplitude, period, maximum and minimum value and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"Basiese cos-waardes by θ = 0°; 90°; 180°; 270°; 360° is 1; 0; −1; 0; 1.","en":"Basic cos values at θ = 0°; 90°; 180°; 270°; 360° are 1; 0; −1; 0; 1."},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 3 en tel 1 by: 3(1) + 1 = 4; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(−1) + 1 = −2; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(1) + 1 = 4","en":"Multiply by 3 and add 1: 3(1) + 1 = 4; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(−1) + 1 = −2; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(1) + 1 = 4"},{"af":"(a) Sleutelpunte: (0°; 4), (90°; 1), (180°; −2), (270°; 1), (360°; 4). Stip hulle en trek 'n gladde kromme.","en":"(a) Key points: (0°; 4), (90°; 1), (180°; −2), (270°; 1), (360°; 4). Plot them and draw a smooth curve."},{"af":"(b) Amplitude = |a| = 3 (kontrole: [[4 − (−2)/2]] = 3). Periode = 360°, want a en q verander nie die periode nie.","en":"(b) Amplitude = |a| = 3 (check: [[4 − (−2)/2]] = 3). Period = 360°, because a and q do not change the period."},{"af":"Maksimum = q + |a| = 4 by θ = 0° en 360°; minimum = q − |a| = −2 by θ = 180°. Waardeversameling: [−2; 4], of −2 ≤ y ≤ 4.","en":"Maximum = q + |a| = 4 at θ = 0° and 360°; minimum = q − |a| = −2 at θ = 180°. Range: [−2; 4], or −2 ≤ y ≤ 4."}],"answer":{"af":"Amplitude 3; periode 360°; maksimum 4; minimum −2; waardeversameling [−2; 4]","en":"Amplitude 3; period 360°; maximum 4; minimum −2; range [−2; 4]"}},{"title":{"af":"Die tan-grafiek met a en q","en":"The tan graph with a and q"},"problem":{"af":"Beskou g(θ) = 2 tan θ − 1 vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. Bepaal (a) die vergelykings van die asimptote, (b) die punte by θ = 0°, 45°, 135° en 180°, (c) die periode en die waardeversameling.","en":"Consider g(θ) = 2 tan θ − 1 for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. Determine (a) the equations of the asymptotes, (b) the points at θ = 0°, 45°, 135° and 180°, (c) the period and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) a en q skuif nie die asimptote nie: θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"(a) a and q do not move the asymptotes: θ = 90° and θ = 270°."},{"af":"(b) Basiese tan-waardes by 0°; 45°; 135°; 180° is 0; 1; −1; 0.","en":"(b) Basic tan values at 0°; 45°; 135°; 180° are 0; 1; −1; 0."},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 2 en trek 1 af: (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1).","en":"Multiply by 2 and subtract 1: (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1)."},{"af":"(c) Periode = 180°: die patroon herhaal elke 180°. Waardeversameling: y ∈ ℝ, want 'n tan-grafiek het geen maksimum of minimum nie.","en":"(c) Period = 180°: the pattern repeats every 180°. Range: y ∈ ℝ, because a tan graph has no maximum or minimum."}],"answer":{"af":"Asimptote θ = 90° en θ = 270°; (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1); periode 180°; y ∈ ℝ","en":"Asymptotes θ = 90° and θ = 270°; (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1); period 180°; y ∈ ℝ"}},{"title":{"af":"Bepaal a en q uit die maksimum en minimum","en":"Determine a and q from the maximum and minimum"},"problem":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a sin θ + q het 'n minimum van −5 by θ = 90° en 'n maksimum van 1 by θ = 270°. Bepaal a en q, en skryf die y-afsnit en die waardeversameling neer.","en":"The graph of y = a sin θ + q has a minimum of −5 at θ = 90° and a maximum of 1 at θ = 270°. Determine a and q, and write down the y-intercept and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"q = [[maks + min/2]] = [[1 + (−5)/2]] = −2","en":"q = [[max + min/2]] = [[1 + (−5)/2]] = −2"},{"af":"|a| = [[maks − min/2]] = [[1 − (−5)/2]] = 3","en":"|a| = [[max − min/2]] = [[1 − (−5)/2]] = 3"},{"af":"'n Gewone sin-grafiek het sy maksimum by 90°. Hierdie een het 'n minimum by 90°, dus is dit gereflekteer: a = −3.","en":"An ordinary sin graph has its maximum at 90°. This one has a minimum at 90°, so it is reflected: a = −3."},{"af":"Kontrole: θ = 90°: y = −3(1) − 2 = −5 ✓ en θ = 270°: y = −3(−1) − 2 = 1 ✓","en":"Check: θ = 90°: y = −3(1) − 2 = −5 ✓ and θ = 270°: y = −3(−1) − 2 = 1 ✓"},{"af":"y-afsnit: by θ = 0° is y = −3(0) − 2 = −2, dus (0°; −2). Waardeversameling: [−5; 1].","en":"y-intercept: at θ = 0°, y = −3(0) − 2 = −2, so (0°; −2). Range: [−5; 1]."}],"answer":{"af":"a = −3 en q = −2, dus y = −3 sin θ − 2; y-afsnit (0°; −2); waardeversameling [−5; 1]","en":"a = −3 and q = −2, so y = −3 sin θ − 2; y-intercept (0°; −2); range [−5; 1]"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees twee grafieke saam","en":"Reading two graphs together"},"problem":{"af":"f(θ) = 2 sin θ en g(θ) = −2 cos θ vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. Die grafieke sny by θ = 135° en θ = 315°. Bepaal: (a) waar f(θ) > g(θ); (b) waar f(θ) × g(θ) < 0; (c) die waardeversameling van h(θ) = g(θ) + 3.","en":"f(θ) = 2 sin θ and g(θ) = −2 cos θ for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. The graphs intersect at θ = 135° and θ = 315°. Determine: (a) where f(θ) > g(θ); (b) where f(θ) × g(θ) < 0; (c) the range of h(θ) = g(θ) + 3."},"steps":[{"af":"Sleutelpunte. f: (0°; 0), (90°; 2), (180°; 0), (270°; −2), (360°; 0). g is die grafiek van 2 cos θ, gereflekteer in die x-as: (0°; −2), (90°; 0), (180°; 2), (270°; 0), (360°; −2).","en":"Key points. f: (0°; 0), (90°; 2), (180°; 0), (270°; −2), (360°; 0). g is the graph of 2 cos θ, reflected in the x-axis: (0°; −2), (90°; 0), (180°; 2), (270°; 0), (360°; −2)."},{"af":"(a) By θ = 0° is f = 0 en g = −2, dus begin f bó g. Tussen die snypunte 135° en 315° lê g bo f (bv. by 180°: f = 0 en g = 2). Na 315° is f weer bo.","en":"(a) At θ = 0°, f = 0 and g = −2, so f starts above g. Between the intersections 135° and 315°, g lies above f (e.g. at 180°: f = 0 and g = 2). After 315°, f is above again."},{"af":"f(θ) > g(θ) vir 0° ≤ θ < 135° of 315° < θ ≤ 360°","en":"f(θ) > g(θ) for 0° ≤ θ < 135° or 315° < θ ≤ 360°"},{"af":"(b) Die produk is negatief as f en g teenoorgestelde tekens het. f > 0 vir 0° < θ < 180°, en g > 0 vir 90° < θ < 270°.","en":"(b) The product is negative when f and g have opposite signs. f > 0 for 0° < θ < 180°, and g > 0 for 90° < θ < 270°."},{"af":"Teenoorgestelde tekens: 0° < θ < 90° (f positief, g negatief) of 180° < θ < 270° (f negatief, g positief).","en":"Opposite signs: 0° < θ < 90° (f positive, g negative) or 180° < θ < 270° (f negative, g positive)."},{"af":"(c) h(θ) = −2 cos θ + 3: maksimum = 3 + 2 = 5 en minimum = 3 − 2 = 1. Waardeversameling [1; 5].","en":"(c) h(θ) = −2 cos θ + 3: maximum = 3 + 2 = 5 and minimum = 3 − 2 = 1. Range [1; 5]."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0° ≤ θ < 135° of 315° < θ ≤ 360°; (b) 0° < θ < 90° of 180° < θ < 270°; (c) [1; 5]","en":"(a) 0° ≤ θ < 135° or 315° < θ ≤ 360°; (b) 0° < θ < 90° or 180° < θ < 270°; (c) [1; 5]"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die periode van y = tan θ?","en":"What is the period of y = tan θ?"},"options":[{"af":"360°","en":"360°"},{"af":"90°","en":"90°"},{"af":"180°","en":"180°"},{"af":"Dit het geen periode nie","en":"It has no period"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"tan θ herhaal elke 180°: van (0°; 0) tot (180°; 0) is een volledige siklus. 360° is die periode van sin en cos, en 90° is net die afstand van 'n afsnit tot 'n asimptoot.","en":"tan θ repeats every 180°: from (0°; 0) to (180°; 0) is one complete cycle. 360° is the period of sin and cos, and 90° is only the distance from an intercept to an asymptote."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke eienskap by die regte waarde.","en":"Match each property to the correct value."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Amplitude van y = 3 sin θ","en":"Amplitude of y = 3 sin θ"},"r":{"af":"3","en":"3"}},{"l":{"af":"Periode van y = cos θ","en":"Period of y = cos θ"},"r":{"af":"360°","en":"360°"}},{"l":{"af":"Asimptote van y = tan θ","en":"Asymptotes of y = tan θ"},"r":{"af":"θ = 90° en θ = 270°","en":"θ = 90° and θ = 270°"}},{"l":{"af":"Waardeversameling van y = sin θ","en":"Range of y = sin θ"},"r":{"af":"[−1; 1]","en":"[−1; 1]"}}],"explain":{"af":"Amplitude = |a| = 3. sin en cos herhaal elke 360°. tan θ is ongedefinieerd by 90° en 270°. sin θ wissel tussen −1 en 1.","en":"Amplitude = |a| = 3. sin and cos repeat every 360°. tan θ is undefined at 90° and 270°. sin θ varies between −1 and 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = tan θ het 'n amplitude van 1.","en":"The graph of y = tan θ has an amplitude of 1."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. tan θ het geen maksimum of minimum nie (die waardeversameling is ℝ), dus het dit geen amplitude nie. Die punt (45°; 1) is nie 'n draaipunt nie.","en":"False. tan θ has no maximum or minimum (the range is ℝ), so it has no amplitude. The point (45°; 1) is not a turning point."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By watter waarde van θ het y = cos θ sy minimum vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°?","en":"At which value of θ does y = cos θ have its minimum for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°?"},"options":[{"af":"90°","en":"90°"},{"af":"270°","en":"270°"},{"af":"0°","en":"0°"},{"af":"180°","en":"180°"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"cos θ begin by 1 (θ = 0°), sak tot −1 by θ = 180° en klim terug tot 1 by 360°. By 270° het sin θ sy minimum, en by 90° is cos θ = 0.","en":"cos θ starts at 1 (θ = 0°), drops to −1 at θ = 180° and climbs back to 1 at 360°. At 270° sin θ has its minimum, and at 90° cos θ = 0."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wat is die amplitude van y = −4 sin θ + 2? Amplitude = ___","en":"What is the amplitude of y = −4 sin θ + 2? Amplitude = ___"},"answers":{"af":["4"],"en":["4"]},"explain":{"af":"Amplitude = |a| = |−4| = 4. 'n Amplitude is altyd positief, en q = 2 verander dit nie. (Kontrole: maksimum 6, minimum −2, en (6 − (−2)) ÷ 2 = 4.)","en":"Amplitude = |a| = |−4| = 4. An amplitude is always positive, and q = 2 does not change it. (Check: maximum 6, minimum −2, and (6 − (−2)) ÷ 2 = 4.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die waardeversameling van y = 3 cos θ − 1?","en":"What is the range of y = 3 cos θ − 1?"},"options":[{"af":"[−3; 3]","en":"[−3; 3]"},{"af":"[−4; 2]","en":"[−4; 2]"},{"af":"[−2; 4]","en":"[−2; 4]"},{"af":"[−2; 2]","en":"[−2; 2]"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Maksimum = q + |a| = −1 + 3 = 2 en minimum = q − |a| = −1 − 3 = −4, dus [−4; 2]. [−3; 3] ignoreer q, [−2; 4] skuif op in plaas van af, en [−2; 2] verwar a + q met die amplitude.","en":"Maximum = q + |a| = −1 + 3 = 2 and minimum = q − |a| = −1 − 3 = −4, so [−4; 2]. [−3; 3] ignores q, [−2; 4] shifts up instead of down, and [−2; 2] confuses a + q with the amplitude."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wat is die maksimumwaarde van y = 2 sin θ + 3? Maksimum = ___","en":"What is the maximum value of y = 2 sin θ + 3? Maximum = ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","y = 5","y=5"],"en":["5","y = 5","y=5"]},"explain":{"af":"Maksimum = q + |a| = 3 + 2 = 5. Dit gebeur by θ = 90°, waar sin θ = 1.","en":"Maximum = q + |a| = 3 + 2 = 5. It happens at θ = 90°, where sin θ = 1."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Grafiek vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360° het 'n y-afsnit by (0°; 3), 'n maksimum van 3, 'n minimum van −1 en 'n periode van 360°. Watter vergelyking pas?","en":"A graph for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360° has a y-intercept at (0°; 3), a maximum of 3, a minimum of −1 and a period of 360°. Which equation fits?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 2 sin θ + 1","en":"y = 2 sin θ + 1"},{"af":"y = 3 cos θ","en":"y = 3 cos θ"},{"af":"y = 2 cos θ + 1","en":"y = 2 cos θ + 1"},{"af":"y = 2 cos θ + 3","en":"y = 2 cos θ + 3"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"q = (3 + (−1)) ÷ 2 = 1 en |a| = (3 − (−1)) ÷ 2 = 2. Die maksimum lê op die y-as (θ = 0°), wat by 'n cos-grafiek met a > 0 gebeur. Dus y = 2 cos θ + 1. y = 2 sin θ + 1 gaan deur (0°; 1), y = 3 cos θ het 'n minimum van −3, en y = 2 cos θ + 3 neem q verkeerdelik as die y-afsnit.","en":"q = (3 + (−1)) ÷ 2 = 1 and |a| = (3 − (−1)) ÷ 2 = 2. The maximum lies on the y-axis (θ = 0°), which happens for a cos graph with a > 0. So y = 2 cos θ + 1. y = 2 sin θ + 1 passes through (0°; 1), y = 3 cos θ has a minimum of −3, and y = 2 cos θ + 3 wrongly takes q as the y-intercept."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die asimptote van y = −3 tan θ + 2 is θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"The asymptotes of y = −3 tan θ + 2 are θ = 90° and θ = 270°."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. a rek en reflekteer die grafiek en q skuif dit op of af, maar die asimptote is vertikale lyne. Hulle bly by θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"True. a stretches and reflects the graph and q moves it up or down, but the asymptotes are vertical lines. They stay at θ = 90° and θ = 270°."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a tan θ + q gaan deur (0°; −2) en (45°; 1). Bepaal a en q.","en":"The graph of y = a tan θ + q passes through (0°; −2) and (45°; 1). Determine a and q."},"options":[{"af":"a = 3; q = −2","en":"a = 3; q = −2"},{"af":"a = 1; q = −2","en":"a = 1; q = −2"},{"af":"a = −2; q = 3","en":"a = −2; q = 3"},{"af":"a = −3; q = −2","en":"a = −3; q = −2"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By θ = 0° is tan 0° = 0, dus y = q = −2. By θ = 45° is tan 45° = 1: a(1) − 2 = 1, dus a = 3. Moenie a gelyk stel aan die y-waarde by 45° nie; trek eers q af.","en":"At θ = 0°, tan 0° = 0, so y = q = −2. At θ = 45°, tan 45° = 1: a(1) − 2 = 1, so a = 3. Do not set a equal to the y-value at 45°; subtract q first."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a cos θ + q gaan deur (0°; −1) en (180°; 5). Wat is die waarde van a? a = ___","en":"The graph of y = a cos θ + q passes through (0°; −1) and (180°; 5). What is the value of a? a = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","a = -3","a = −3","a=-3","a=−3"],"en":["-3","−3","a = -3","a = −3","a=-3","a=−3"]},"explain":{"af":"θ = 0°: a(1) + q = −1. θ = 180°: a(−1) + q = 5. Trek af: 2a = −6, dus a = −3 (en q = 2). a is negatief, want die grafiek het 'n minimum by θ = 0°.","en":"θ = 0°: a(1) + q = −1. θ = 180°: a(−1) + q = 5. Subtract: 2a = −6, so a = −3 (and q = 2). a is negative, because the graph has a minimum at θ = 0°."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"f(θ) = sin θ en g(θ) = cos θ sny by θ = 45° en θ = 225° (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). Vir watter waardes van θ is f(θ) > g(θ)?","en":"f(θ) = sin θ and g(θ) = cos θ intersect at θ = 45° and θ = 225° (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). For which values of θ is f(θ) > g(θ)?"},"options":[{"af":"0° ≤ θ < 45° of 225° < θ ≤ 360°","en":"0° ≤ θ < 45° or 225° < θ ≤ 360°"},{"af":"45° ≤ θ ≤ 225°","en":"45° ≤ θ ≤ 225°"},{"af":"90° < θ < 270°","en":"90° < θ < 270°"},{"af":"45° < θ < 225°","en":"45° < θ < 225°"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By θ = 90° is sin θ = 1 en cos θ = 0, dus lê f tussen die snypunte bó g: 45° < θ < 225°. Gebruik streng ongelykhede, want by 45° en 225° is f(θ) = g(θ). Die eerste opsie is waar g bo f lê.","en":"At θ = 90°, sin θ = 1 and cos θ = 0, so between the intersections f lies above g: 45° < θ < 225°. Use strict inequalities, because at 45° and 225° f(θ) = g(θ). The first option is where g lies above f."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vir watter waarde van k (k > 0) het die vergelyking 3 sin θ + 1 = k presies een oplossing vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°? k = ___","en":"For which value of k (k > 0) does the equation 3 sin θ + 1 = k have exactly one solution for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°? k = ___"},"answers":{"af":["4","k = 4","k=4"],"en":["4","k = 4","k=4"]},"explain":{"af":"Die horisontale lyn y = k sny y = 3 sin θ + 1 net een keer by die maksimum (90°; 4) of die minimum (270°; −2). Omdat k > 0, is k = 4. Vir enige k tussen −2 en 4 is daar twee of drie snypunte.","en":"The horizontal line y = k cuts y = 3 sin θ + 1 only once at the maximum (90°; 4) or the minimum (270°; −2). Because k > 0, k = 4. For any k between −2 and 4 there are two or three points of intersection."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die hoogte h (in meter) bo die grond van 'n sitplek op 'n reuse-wiel (Ferriswiel) by 'n kermis in Pretoria word gegee deur h = −15 cos θ + 17, waar θ die hoek is waardeur die wiel gedraai het (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). Wat is die deursnee van die wiel?","en":"The height h (in metres) above the ground of a seat on a Ferris wheel at a fair in Pretoria is given by h = −15 cos θ + 17, where θ is the angle through which the wheel has turned (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). What is the diameter of the wheel?"},"options":[{"af":"15 m","en":"15 m"},{"af":"30 m","en":"30 m"},{"af":"32 m","en":"32 m"},{"af":"17 m","en":"17 m"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die amplitude is |−15| = 15 m: die sitplek gaan 15 m bo en 15 m onder die as van die wiel. Dit is die radius, dus is die deursnee 2 × 15 = 30 m. (Hoogste punt 17 + 15 = 32 m, laagste punt 17 − 15 = 2 m, en 32 − 2 = 30 m.) 17 m is die hoogte van die as.","en":"The amplitude is |−15| = 15 m: the seat goes 15 m above and 15 m below the axle of the wheel. That is the radius, so the diameter is 2 × 15 = 30 m. (Highest point 17 + 15 = 32 m, lowest point 17 − 15 = 2 m, and 32 − 2 = 30 m.) 17 m is the height of the axle."}}]},{"id":"w10-t2-euklidiese-meetkunde","title":{"af":"Euklidiese meetkunde: vierhoeke en middelpuntstelling","en":"Euclidean geometry: quadrilaterals and midpoint theorem"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die eienskappe van vierhoeke en die middelpuntstelling kan gebruik om hoeke en lengtes te bereken en kort bewyse met korrekte redes te skryf.","en":"You will be able to use the properties of quadrilaterals and the midpoint theorem to calculate angles and lengths and write short proofs with correct reasons."},"summary":{"af":"## Hersiening: lyne, hoeke en driehoeke\n\nIn meetkunde kry elke bewering 'n **rede** tussen hakies. 'n Korrekte antwoord sonder 'n rede kos jou punte.\n\n- Hoeke op 'n reguit lyn tel op tot 180°. *(hoeke op 'n reguit lyn)*\n- Regoorstaande hoeke is gelyk. *(regoorst. ∠e)*\n- Hoeke om 'n punt tel op tot 360°. *(∠e om 'n punt)*\n- As AB || CD: ooreenkomstige hoeke is gelyk *(ooreenk. ∠e; AB || CD)*, verwisselende hoeke is gelyk *(verwiss. ∠e; AB || CD)* en ko-binnehoeke tel op tot 180° *(ko-binne ∠e; AB || CD)*.\n- Die binnehoeke van 'n driehoek tel op tot 180°. *(som ∠e van Δ)*\n- 'n Buitehoek van 'n driehoek is gelyk aan die som van die twee teenoorstaande binnehoeke. *(buite ∠ van Δ)*\n- In 'n gelykbenige driehoek is die hoeke teenoor die gelyke sye gelyk. *(∠e teenoor gelyke sye)*\n- In 'n reghoekige driehoek is skuinssy^{2} = die som van die kwadrate van die ander twee sye. *(Pyth.)*\n- Kongruente driehoeke (≡) bewys jy met SSS, SHS, HHS of 90°, skuinssy, sy.\n- Die binnehoeke van enige vierhoek tel op tot 360°.\n\n## Eienskappe van vierhoeke\n\n| Vierhoek | Sye | Hoeke | Hoeklyne |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | albei pare teenoorstaande sye ewewydig en gelyk | teenoorstaande hoeke gelyk | halveer mekaar |\n| Reghoek | soos 'n parallelogram | al vier hoeke 90° | halveer mekaar en is **ewe lank** |\n| Ruit | al vier sye gelyk; teenoorstaande sye ewewydig | teenoorstaande hoeke gelyk | halveer mekaar **loodreg** en halveer die hoeke van die ruit |\n| Vierkant | al vier sye gelyk; teenoorstaande sye ewewydig | al vier hoeke 90° | ewe lank, halveer mekaar loodreg en halveer die hoeke (45°) |\n| Trapesium | een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig | ko-binnehoeke tussen die ewewydige sye tel op tot 180° | geen spesiale eienskap nie |\n| Vlieër | twee pare **aangrensende** sye gelyk | die twee hoeke tussen die ongelyke sye is gelyk | sny mekaar loodreg; die hoeklyn deur die hoekpunte waar die gelyke sye ontmoet (die simmetrie-as) halveer die ander hoeklyn en die hoeke by sy eindpunte |\n\n**Families:** 'n Vierkant is 'n spesiale reghoek én 'n spesiale ruit, en reghoeke en ruite is spesiale parallelogramme. Alle eienskappe van 'n parallelogram geld dus ook vir 'n reghoek, ruit en vierkant – maar nie andersom nie.\n\nAs jy reeds wéét dit is 'n parallelogram, gebruik jy die redes *(teenoorst. sye van ||m)*, *(teenoorst. ∠e van ||m)* en *(hoekl. van ||m)*. Vir 'n ruit skryf jy *(hoekl. van ruit)* en vir 'n reghoek *(hoekl. van reghoek)*.\n\n## Bewys dat 'n vierhoek 'n parallelogram is\n\n'n Vierhoek is 'n parallelogram as **enige een** van hierdie vyf toetse waar is:\n\n1. Albei pare teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig (die definisie). *(teenoorst. sye ||)*\n2. Albei pare teenoorstaande sye is gelyk. *(teenoorst. sye =)*\n3. Albei pare teenoorstaande hoeke is gelyk. *(teenoorst. ∠e =)*\n4. Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar. *(hoekl. halveer mekaar)*\n5. Een paar teenoorstaande sye is gelyk **en** ewewydig. *(een paar teenoorst. sye = en ||)*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"Een paar teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig en die ander paar is gelyk\" is NIE 'n toets nie. 'n Gelykbenige trapesium het ook dié eienskap.\n\n**Stappe vir 'n kort bewys:** (1) skryf neer wat gegee is; (2) kies die toets wat by die gegewe inligting pas; (3) skryf elke bewering met sy rede; (4) sluit af met \"∴ ABCD is 'n parallelogram\" en die rede.\n\n## Die middelpuntstelling\n\nIn ΔABC is D die middelpunt van AB en E die middelpunt van AC. Dan is:\n\n- DE || BC **en**\n- DE = [[1/2]]BC *(midpt-stelling)*\n\n**Omgekeerde:** As D die middelpunt van AB is en DE || BC (met E op AC), dan is E die middelpunt van AC. *(lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy)*\n\n**Waarom dit werk:** Verleng DE tot by F sodat DE = EF. In vierhoek ADCF halveer die hoeklyne AC en DF mekaar by E, dus is ADCF 'n parallelogram. Dan is CF = AD = DB en CF || DB, dus is DBCF 'n parallelogram (een paar teenoorst. sye = en ||). Daarom is DF || BC en DF = BC, en DE = [[1/2]]DF = [[1/2]]BC.\n\n> **Wenk:** As jy die middelpunte van die vier sye van *enige* vierhoek verbind, kry jy 'n parallelogram. Elke sy van die nuwe vierhoek is ewewydig aan een van die oorspronklike hoeklyne en die helfte daarvan lank (midpt-stelling in twee driehoeke).\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Om te sê die hoeklyne van 'n ruit is ewe lank. Dit geld net vir 'n reghoek en 'n vierkant.\n- Om die midpt-stelling te gebruik as net **een** middelpunt gegee is. Dan het jy die omgekeerde nodig, en dit werk net as die lyn ewewydig aan die tweede sy is.\n- Om DE = 2BC te skryf in plaas van BC = 2DE.\n- Om die ewewydige lyne in die rede te vergeet: skryf *(ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC)*, nie net *(ooreenk. ∠e)* nie.","en":"## Revision: lines, angles and triangles\n\nIn geometry every statement gets a **reason** in brackets. A correct answer without a reason costs you marks.\n\n- Angles on a straight line add up to 180°. *(∠s on a str line)*\n- Vertically opposite angles are equal. *(vert opp ∠s)*\n- Angles around a point add up to 360°. *(∠s round a pt)*\n- If AB || CD: corresponding angles are equal *(corresp ∠s; AB || CD)*, alternate angles are equal *(alt ∠s; AB || CD)* and co-interior angles add up to 180° *(co-int ∠s; AB || CD)*.\n- The interior angles of a triangle add up to 180°. *(sum of ∠s in Δ)*\n- An exterior angle of a triangle equals the sum of the two opposite interior angles. *(ext ∠ of Δ)*\n- In an isosceles triangle the angles opposite the equal sides are equal. *(∠s opp equal sides)*\n- In a right-angled triangle hypotenuse^{2} = the sum of the squares of the other two sides. *(Pyth)*\n- You prove triangles congruent (≡) with SSS, SAS, AAS or RHS.\n- The interior angles of any quadrilateral add up to 360°.\n\n## Properties of quadrilaterals\n\n| Quadrilateral | Sides | Angles | Diagonals |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | both pairs of opposite sides parallel and equal | opposite angles equal | bisect each other |\n| Rectangle | as for a parallelogram | all four angles 90° | bisect each other and are **equal in length** |\n| Rhombus | all four sides equal; opposite sides parallel | opposite angles equal | bisect each other **at right angles** and bisect the angles of the rhombus |\n| Square | all four sides equal; opposite sides parallel | all four angles 90° | equal, bisect each other at right angles and bisect the angles (45°) |\n| Trapezium | one pair of opposite sides parallel | co-interior angles between the parallel sides add up to 180° | no special property |\n| Kite | two pairs of **adjacent** sides equal | the two angles between the unequal sides are equal | cut at right angles; the diagonal through the vertices where the equal sides meet (the axis of symmetry) bisects the other diagonal and the angles at its ends |\n\n**Families:** A square is a special rectangle and a special rhombus, and rectangles and rhombuses are special parallelograms. So every property of a parallelogram also holds for a rectangle, rhombus and square – but not the other way round.\n\nIf you already know it is a parallelogram, use the reasons *(opp sides of ||m)*, *(opp ∠s of ||m)* and *(diags of ||m)*. For a rhombus write *(diags of rhombus)* and for a rectangle *(diags of rectangle)*.\n\n## Proving that a quadrilateral is a parallelogram\n\nA quadrilateral is a parallelogram if **any one** of these five tests is true:\n\n1. Both pairs of opposite sides are parallel (the definition). *(opp sides ||)*\n2. Both pairs of opposite sides are equal. *(opp sides =)*\n3. Both pairs of opposite angles are equal. *(opp ∠s =)*\n4. The diagonals bisect each other. *(diags bisect each other)*\n5. One pair of opposite sides is equal **and** parallel. *(one pair opp sides = and ||)*\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"One pair of opposite sides is parallel and the other pair is equal\" is NOT a test. An isosceles trapezium also has this property.\n\n**Steps for a short proof:** (1) write down what is given; (2) choose the test that matches the given information; (3) write every statement with its reason; (4) conclude with \"∴ ABCD is a parallelogram\" and the reason.\n\n## The midpoint theorem\n\nIn ΔABC, D is the midpoint of AB and E is the midpoint of AC. Then:\n\n- DE || BC **and**\n- DE = [[1/2]]BC *(midpt theorem)*\n\n**Converse:** If D is the midpoint of AB and DE || BC (with E on AC), then E is the midpoint of AC. *(line through midpt || to 2nd side)*\n\n**Why it works:** Extend DE to F so that DE = EF. In quadrilateral ADCF the diagonals AC and DF bisect each other at E, so ADCF is a parallelogram. Then CF = AD = DB and CF || DB, so DBCF is a parallelogram (one pair opp sides = and ||). Therefore DF || BC and DF = BC, and DE = [[1/2]]DF = [[1/2]]BC.\n\n> **Tip:** If you join the midpoints of the four sides of *any* quadrilateral, you get a parallelogram. Each side of the new quadrilateral is parallel to one of the original diagonals and half as long (midpoint theorem in two triangles).\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Saying the diagonals of a rhombus are equal. That is only true for a rectangle and a square.\n- Using the midpoint theorem when only **one** midpoint is given. Then you need the converse, and it only works if the line is parallel to the second side.\n- Writing DE = 2BC instead of BC = 2DE.\n- Leaving the parallel lines out of the reason: write *(corresp ∠s; DE || BC)*, not just *(corresp ∠s)*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Parallelogram","en":"Parallelogram"},"def":{"af":"'n Vierhoek met albei pare teenoorstaande sye ewewydig.","en":"A quadrilateral with both pairs of opposite sides parallel."}},{"term":{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},"def":{"af":"'n Parallelogram met al vier hoeke 90°; sy hoeklyne is ewe lank.","en":"A parallelogram with all four angles 90°; its diagonals are equal in length."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruit","en":"Rhombus"},"def":{"af":"'n Parallelogram met al vier sye ewe lank; sy hoeklyne halveer mekaar loodreg.","en":"A parallelogram with all four sides equal; its diagonals bisect each other at right angles."}},{"term":{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},"def":{"af":"'n Reghoek met al vier sye gelyk – dit is ook 'n ruit met 90°-hoeke.","en":"A rectangle with all four sides equal – it is also a rhombus with 90° angles."}},{"term":{"af":"Trapesium","en":"Trapezium"},"def":{"af":"'n Vierhoek met een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig.","en":"A quadrilateral with one pair of opposite sides parallel."}},{"term":{"af":"Vlieër","en":"Kite"},"def":{"af":"'n Vierhoek met twee pare aangrensende sye gelyk; sy hoeklyne sny mekaar loodreg.","en":"A quadrilateral with two pairs of adjacent sides equal; its diagonals cut at right angles."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoeklyn","en":"Diagonal"},"def":{"af":"'n Lynstuk wat twee teenoorstaande hoekpunte van 'n vierhoek verbind.","en":"A line segment joining two opposite vertices of a quadrilateral."}},{"term":{"af":"Middelpuntstelling","en":"Midpoint theorem"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn wat die middelpunte van twee sye van 'n driehoek verbind, is ewewydig aan die derde sy en die helfte daarvan lank.","en":"The line joining the midpoints of two sides of a triangle is parallel to the third side and half as long."}},{"term":{"af":"Omgekeerde van die middelpuntstelling","en":"Converse of the midpoint theorem"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn deur die middelpunt van een sy van 'n driehoek, ewewydig aan 'n tweede sy, halveer die derde sy.","en":"A line through the midpoint of one side of a triangle, parallel to a second side, bisects the third side."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoeke in 'n parallelogram","en":"Angles in a parallelogram"},"problem":{"af":"In parallelogram ABCD is ∠A = 3x + 10° en ∠C = 5x − 30°. Bereken x, ∠A en ∠B.","en":"In parallelogram ABCD, ∠A = 3x + 10° and ∠C = 5x − 30°. Calculate x, ∠A and ∠B."},"steps":[{"af":"∠A = ∠C (teenoorst. ∠e van ||m), dus 3x + 10° = 5x − 30°","en":"∠A = ∠C (opp ∠s of ||m), so 3x + 10° = 5x − 30°"},{"af":"10° + 30° = 5x − 3x, dus 40° = 2x en x = 20°","en":"10° + 30° = 5x − 3x, so 40° = 2x and x = 20°"},{"af":"∠A = 3(20°) + 10° = 70°. Kontroleer: ∠C = 5(20°) − 30° = 70° ✓","en":"∠A = 3(20°) + 10° = 70°. Check: ∠C = 5(20°) − 30° = 70° ✓"},{"af":"∠A + ∠B = 180° (ko-binne ∠e; AD || BC), dus ∠B = 180° − 70° = 110°","en":"∠A + ∠B = 180° (co-int ∠s; AD || BC), so ∠B = 180° − 70° = 110°"}],"answer":{"af":"x = 20°; ∠A = 70°; ∠B = 110°","en":"x = 20°; ∠A = 70°; ∠B = 110°"}},{"title":{"af":"Sylengte van 'n ruit","en":"Side length of a rhombus"},"problem":{"af":"PQRS is 'n ruit. Die hoeklyne PR = 16 cm en QS = 12 cm sny by T. Bereken ∠PTQ, die lengte van PQ en die omtrek van die ruit.","en":"PQRS is a rhombus. The diagonals PR = 16 cm and QS = 12 cm intersect at T. Calculate ∠PTQ, the length of PQ and the perimeter of the rhombus."},"steps":[{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n ruit halveer mekaar loodreg: ∠PTQ = 90°, PT = 8 cm en QT = 6 cm (hoekl. van ruit)","en":"The diagonals of a rhombus bisect each other at right angles: ∠PTQ = 90°, PT = 8 cm and QT = 6 cm (diags of rhombus)"},{"af":"In ΔPTQ: PQ^{2} = PT^{2} + QT^{2} = 8^{2} + 6^{2} = 64 + 36 = 100 (Pyth.)","en":"In ΔPTQ: PQ^{2} = PT^{2} + QT^{2} = 8^{2} + 6^{2} = 64 + 36 = 100 (Pyth)"},{"af":"PQ = √100 = 10 cm","en":"PQ = √100 = 10 cm"},{"af":"Al vier sye van 'n ruit is gelyk: omtrek = 4 × 10 = 40 cm","en":"All four sides of a rhombus are equal: perimeter = 4 × 10 = 40 cm"}],"answer":{"af":"∠PTQ = 90°; PQ = 10 cm; omtrek = 40 cm","en":"∠PTQ = 90°; PQ = 10 cm; perimeter = 40 cm"}},{"title":{"af":"Middelpuntstelling en die omgekeerde","en":"Midpoint theorem and its converse"},"problem":{"af":"In ΔABC is AB = 14 cm, BC = 18 cm en ∠ABC = 64°. D is die middelpunt van AB en E is die middelpunt van AC. Die lyn deur E ewewydig aan AB sny BC by F. Bereken DE, ∠ADE, BF en EF.","en":"In ΔABC, AB = 14 cm, BC = 18 cm and ∠ABC = 64°. D is the midpoint of AB and E is the midpoint of AC. The line through E parallel to AB cuts BC at F. Calculate DE, ∠ADE, BF and EF."},"steps":[{"af":"D en E is middelpunte van AB en AC, dus DE || BC en DE = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm (midpt-stelling)","en":"D and E are the midpoints of AB and AC, so DE || BC and DE = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm (midpt theorem)"},{"af":"∠ADE = ∠ABC = 64° (ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC)","en":"∠ADE = ∠ABC = 64° (corresp ∠s; DE || BC)"},{"af":"In ΔCAB is E die middelpunt van AC en EF || AB, dus is F die middelpunt van BC (lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy)","en":"In ΔCAB, E is the midpoint of AC and EF || AB, so F is the midpoint of BC (line through midpt || to 2nd side)"},{"af":"BF = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm","en":"BF = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm"},{"af":"E en F is nou middelpunte van CA en CB, dus EF = [[1/2]]AB = [[1/2]] × 14 = 7 cm (midpt-stelling)","en":"E and F are now the midpoints of CA and CB, so EF = [[1/2]]AB = [[1/2]] × 14 = 7 cm (midpt theorem)"}],"answer":{"af":"DE = 9 cm; ∠ADE = 64°; BF = 9 cm; EF = 7 cm","en":"DE = 9 cm; ∠ADE = 64°; BF = 9 cm; EF = 7 cm"}},{"title":{"af":"Bewys dat 'n vierhoek 'n parallelogram is","en":"Prove that a quadrilateral is a parallelogram"},"problem":{"af":"ABCD is 'n parallelogram en sy hoeklyne sny by O. E en F is punte op AC, met E tussen A en O en F tussen O en C, sodat AE = CF. Bewys dat BEDF 'n parallelogram is.","en":"ABCD is a parallelogram and its diagonals intersect at O. E and F are points on AC, with E between A and O and F between O and C, so that AE = CF. Prove that BEDF is a parallelogram."},"steps":[{"af":"AO = OC en BO = OD (hoekl. van ||m)","en":"AO = OC and BO = OD (diags of ||m)"},{"af":"AE = CF (gegee)","en":"AE = CF (given)"},{"af":"EO = AO − AE en OF = OC − CF. Gelyke lengtes minus gelyke lengtes, dus EO = OF","en":"EO = AO − AE and OF = OC − CF. Equal lengths minus equal lengths, so EO = OF"},{"af":"In vierhoek BEDF sny die hoeklyne BD en EF by O, met BO = OD en EO = OF","en":"In quadrilateral BEDF the diagonals BD and EF meet at O, with BO = OD and EO = OF"},{"af":"∴ BEDF is 'n parallelogram (hoekl. halveer mekaar)","en":"∴ BEDF is a parallelogram (diags bisect each other)"}],"answer":{"af":"BEDF is 'n parallelogram, want sy hoeklyne halveer mekaar.","en":"BEDF is a parallelogram, because its diagonals bisect each other."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter eienskap geld vir elke ruit, maar NIE vir elke parallelogram nie?","en":"Which property holds for every rhombus, but NOT for every parallelogram?"},"options":[{"af":"Teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig","en":"Opposite sides are parallel"},{"af":"Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar","en":"The diagonals bisect each other"},{"af":"Die hoeklyne sny mekaar loodreg","en":"The diagonals cut each other at right angles"},{"af":"Teenoorstaande hoeke is gelyk","en":"Opposite angles are equal"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die ander drie eienskappe geld vir álle parallelogramme. Net in 'n ruit (en vierkant) sny die hoeklyne mekaar loodreg.","en":"The other three properties hold for all parallelograms. Only in a rhombus (and square) do the diagonals cut at right angles."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vierhoek by 'n eienskap wat dit definieer.","en":"Match each quadrilateral to a property that defines it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},"r":{"af":"Parallelogram met al vier hoeke 90°","en":"Parallelogram with all four angles 90°"}},{"l":{"af":"Ruit","en":"Rhombus"},"r":{"af":"Parallelogram met al vier sye gelyk","en":"Parallelogram with all four sides equal"}},{"l":{"af":"Trapesium","en":"Trapezium"},"r":{"af":"Een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig","en":"One pair of opposite sides parallel"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlieër","en":"Kite"},"r":{"af":"Twee pare aangrensende sye gelyk","en":"Two pairs of adjacent sides equal"}},{"l":{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},"r":{"af":"Al vier sye gelyk en al vier hoeke 90°","en":"All four sides equal and all four angles 90°"}}],"explain":{"af":"Let op: 'n vlieër se gelyke sye is aangrensend (langs mekaar), 'n parallelogram s'n is teenoorstaande. 'n Vierkant is reghoek én ruit.","en":"Note: a kite's equal sides are adjacent (next to each other), a parallelogram's are opposite. A square is both a rectangle and a rhombus."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van elke ruit is ewe lank.","en":"The diagonals of every rhombus are equal in length."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Ruit se hoeklyne halveer mekaar loodreg, maar hulle is net ewe lank as die ruit 'n vierkant is. Ewe lange hoeklyne is 'n eienskap van 'n reghoek.","en":"False. A rhombus's diagonals bisect each other at right angles, but they are only equal if the rhombus is a square. Equal diagonals are a property of a rectangle."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In ΔABC is D die middelpunt van AB en E die middelpunt van AC. Watter rede gebruik jy om te sê dat DE || BC?","en":"In ΔABC, D is the midpoint of AB and E is the midpoint of AC. Which reason do you use to say that DE || BC?"},"options":[{"af":"(lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy)","en":"(line through midpt || to 2nd side)"},{"af":"(ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC)","en":"(corresp ∠s; DE || BC)"},{"af":"(teenoorst. sye van ||m)","en":"(opp sides of ||m)"},{"af":"(midpt-stelling)","en":"(midpt theorem)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Albei middelpunte is gegee, dus gebruik jy die middelpuntstelling: DE || BC en DE = ½BC. Die omgekeerde gebruik jy net as een middelpunt en 'n ewewydige lyn gegee is. (ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC) is sirkelredenasie – jy kan nie DE || BC gebruik om DE || BC te bewys nie.","en":"Both midpoints are given, so you use the midpoint theorem: DE || BC and DE = ½BC. You use the converse only when one midpoint and a parallel line are given. (corresp ∠s; DE || BC) is circular – you cannot use DE || BC to prove DE || BC."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In parallelogram ABCD is ∠A = 68°. Dan is ∠B = ___°.","en":"In parallelogram ABCD, ∠A = 68°. Then ∠B = ___°."},"answers":{"af":["112","112°"],"en":["112","112°"]},"explain":{"af":"∠A en ∠B is ko-binnehoeke tussen AD || BC, dus ∠B = 180° − 68° = 112° (ko-binne ∠e; AD || BC). Die hoek teenoor ∠A (∠C) is 68°.","en":"∠A and ∠B are co-interior angles between AD || BC, so ∠B = 180° − 68° = 112° (co-int ∠s; AD || BC). The angle opposite ∠A (∠C) is 68°."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ΔPQR is S die middelpunt van PQ en T die middelpunt van PR. QR = 15 cm. Dan is ST = ___ cm.","en":"In ΔPQR, S is the midpoint of PQ and T is the midpoint of PR. QR = 15 cm. Then ST = ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["7,5","7.5","7,5 cm","7.5 cm","15/2"],"en":["7.5","7,5","7.5 cm","7,5 cm","15/2"]},"explain":{"af":"ST = ½QR = ½ × 15 = 7,5 cm (midpt-stelling). Moenie verdubbel nie – die lyn tussen die middelpunte is die korter een.","en":"ST = ½QR = ½ × 15 = 7.5 cm (midpt theorem). Do not double – the line between the midpoints is the shorter one."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is NIE genoeg om te bewys dat vierhoek ABCD 'n parallelogram is nie?","en":"Which one of the following is NOT enough to prove that quadrilateral ABCD is a parallelogram?"},"options":[{"af":"Albei pare teenoorstaande sye is gelyk","en":"Both pairs of opposite sides are equal"},{"af":"Een paar teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig en die ander paar is gelyk","en":"One pair of opposite sides is parallel and the other pair is equal"},{"af":"Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar","en":"The diagonals bisect each other"},{"af":"Een paar teenoorstaande sye is gelyk en ewewydig","en":"One pair of opposite sides is equal and parallel"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Gelykbenige trapesium het een paar ewewydige sye en die ander paar gelyk, maar dit is nie 'n parallelogram nie. Die ander drie is van die vyf geldige toetse.","en":"An isosceles trapezium has one pair of parallel sides and the other pair equal, but it is not a parallelogram. The other three are among the five valid tests."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In parallelogram PQRS is ∠P = 4x − 15° en ∠R = 2x + 25°. Wat is die grootte van ∠Q?","en":"In parallelogram PQRS, ∠P = 4x − 15° and ∠R = 2x + 25°. What is the size of ∠Q?"},"options":[{"af":"115°","en":"115°"},{"af":"65°","en":"65°"},{"af":"81,67°","en":"81.67°"},{"af":"20°","en":"20°"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"∠P = ∠R (teenoorst. ∠e van ||m): 4x − 15° = 2x + 25°, dus 2x = 40° en x = 20°. ∠P = 4(20°) − 15° = 65°. ∠Q = 180° − 65° = 115° (ko-binne ∠e; PS || QR). 65° is ∠P self, 20° is net x, en 81,67° kry jy as jy teenoorstaande hoeke verkeerdelik as supplementêr behandel.","en":"∠P = ∠R (opp ∠s of ||m): 4x − 15° = 2x + 25°, so 2x = 40° and x = 20°. ∠P = 4(20°) − 15° = 65°. ∠Q = 180° − 65° = 115° (co-int ∠s; PS || QR). 65° is ∠P itself, 20° is just x, and 81.67° comes from wrongly treating opposite angles as supplementary."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n ruit is 10 cm en 24 cm lank. Die lengte van een sy van die ruit is ___ cm.","en":"The diagonals of a rhombus are 10 cm and 24 cm long. The length of one side of the rhombus is ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["13","13 cm"],"en":["13","13 cm"]},"explain":{"af":"Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar loodreg, dus vorm die halwe hoeklyne (5 cm en 12 cm) 'n reghoekige driehoek met die sy as skuinssy: sy² = 5² + 12² = 169, sy = 13 cm (Pyth.).","en":"The diagonals bisect each other at right angles, so the half-diagonals (5 cm and 12 cm) form a right-angled triangle with the side as hypotenuse: side² = 5² + 12² = 169, side = 13 cm (Pyth)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"ABCD is 'n vlieër met AB = AD en CB = CD. ∠BAD = 80° en ∠BCD = 50°. Wat is die grootte van ∠ABC?","en":"ABCD is a kite with AB = AD and CB = CD. ∠BAD = 80° and ∠BCD = 50°. What is the size of ∠ABC?"},"options":[{"af":"50°","en":"50°"},{"af":"230°","en":"230°"},{"af":"115°","en":"115°"},{"af":"80°","en":"80°"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In 'n vlieër is die hoeke tussen die ongelyke sye gelyk: ∠ABC = ∠ADC. Die hoeke van 'n vierhoek tel op tot 360°: 2∠ABC = 360° − 80° − 50° = 230°, dus ∠ABC = 115°. 230° vergeet om deur 2 te deel.","en":"In a kite the angles between the unequal sides are equal: ∠ABC = ∠ADC. The angles of a quadrilateral add up to 360°: 2∠ABC = 360° − 80° − 50° = 230°, so ∠ABC = 115°. 230° forgets to divide by 2."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ΔABC is D die middelpunt van AB, en E is 'n punt op AC sodat DE || BC. Dan is E die middelpunt van AC.","en":"In ΔABC, D is the midpoint of AB, and E is a point on AC such that DE || BC. Then E is the midpoint of AC."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is die omgekeerde van die middelpuntstelling: 'n lyn deur die middelpunt van een sy, ewewydig aan 'n tweede sy, halveer die derde sy (lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy).","en":"True. This is the converse of the midpoint theorem: a line through the midpoint of one side, parallel to a second side, bisects the third side (line through midpt || to 2nd side)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ΔKLM is KL = 18 cm en KM = 22 cm. N is die middelpunt van KL, en P lê op KM sodat NP || LM. NP = 8 cm. Die omtrek van trapesium NLMP is ___ cm.","en":"In ΔKLM, KL = 18 cm and KM = 22 cm. N is the midpoint of KL, and P lies on KM such that NP || LM. NP = 8 cm. The perimeter of trapezium NLMP is ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["44","44 cm"],"en":["44","44 cm"]},"explain":{"af":"P is die middelpunt van KM (lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy), dus PM = 11 cm. Nou is N en P middelpunte, dus LM = 2 × NP = 16 cm (midpt-stelling). NL = 9 cm. Omtrek = 9 + 16 + 11 + 8 = 44 cm.","en":"P is the midpoint of KM (line through midpt || to 2nd side), so PM = 11 cm. Now N and P are midpoints, so LM = 2 × NP = 16 cm (midpt theorem). NL = 9 cm. Perimeter = 9 + 16 + 11 + 8 = 44 cm."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"ABCD is 'n reghoek en sy hoeklyne sny by O. ∠OAB = 35°. Wat is die grootte van ∠AOD?","en":"ABCD is a rectangle and its diagonals intersect at O. ∠OAB = 35°. What is the size of ∠AOD?"},"options":[{"af":"70°","en":"70°"},{"af":"110°","en":"110°"},{"af":"35°","en":"35°"},{"af":"55°","en":"55°"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n reghoek is ewe lank en halveer mekaar, dus OA = OB. Dan is ∠OBA = 35° (∠e teenoor gelyke sye) en ∠AOB = 180° − 70° = 110° (som ∠e van Δ). ∠AOD = 180° − 110° = 70° (hoeke op 'n reguit lyn). 110° is ∠AOB, en 55° is ∠OAD.","en":"The diagonals of a rectangle are equal and bisect each other, so OA = OB. Then ∠OBA = 35° (∠s opp equal sides) and ∠AOB = 180° − 70° = 110° (sum of ∠s in Δ). ∠AOD = 180° − 110° = 70° (∠s on a str line). 110° is ∠AOB, and 55° is ∠OAD."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"P, Q, R en S is die middelpunte van die sye AB, BC, CD en DA van vierhoek ABCD. Die hoeklyne is AC = 20 cm en BD = 14 cm. Wat is die omtrek van PQRS?","en":"P, Q, R and S are the midpoints of the sides AB, BC, CD and DA of quadrilateral ABCD. The diagonals are AC = 20 cm and BD = 14 cm. What is the perimeter of PQRS?"},"options":[{"af":"17 cm","en":"17 cm"},{"af":"34 cm","en":"34 cm"},{"af":"48 cm","en":"48 cm"},{"af":"68 cm","en":"68 cm"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In ΔABC: PQ = ½AC = 10 cm, en in ΔADC: SR = ½AC = 10 cm. In ΔABD: PS = ½BD = 7 cm, en in ΔCBD: QR = ½BD = 7 cm (midpt-stelling). Omtrek = 10 + 7 + 10 + 7 = 34 cm. 68 cm vergeet om te halveer, en 48 cm halveer net een hoeklyn.","en":"In ΔABC: PQ = ½AC = 10 cm, and in ΔADC: SR = ½AC = 10 cm. In ΔABD: PS = ½BD = 7 cm, and in ΔCBD: QR = ½BD = 7 cm (midpt theorem). Perimeter = 10 + 7 + 10 + 7 = 34 cm. 68 cm forgets to halve, and 48 cm halves only one diagonal."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Analitiese meetkunde, finansies, statistiek en trigonometrie","en":"Analytical geometry, finance, statistics and trigonometry"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t3-analitiese-meetkunde","title":{"af":"Analitiese meetkunde","en":"Analytical geometry"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal afstand, middelpunt en gradiënt tussen punte kan bereken, die vergelyking van 'n lyn kan bepaal, en met koördinate kan bewys watter soort vierhoek gegee is.","en":"You will be able to calculate the distance, midpoint and gradient between points, determine the equation of a line, and use coordinates to prove what kind of quadrilateral is given."},"summary":{"af":"## Die drie basiese formules\n\nVir twee punte A(x_{1}; y_{1}) en B(x_{2}; y_{2}):\n\n| Wat | Formule |\n|---|---|\n| Afstand (lengte van AB) | AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] |\n| Middelpunt M van AB | M([[x_{1} + x_{2}/2]] ; [[y_{1} + y_{2}/2]]) |\n| Gradiënt van AB | m_{AB} = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] |\n\n> **Wenk:** Maak altyd eers 'n rowwe skets van die punte. Dan sien jy gou of jou antwoord sin maak.\n\n### Afstand\n\nDie afstandsformule is net **Pythagoras**: die horisontale verskil en die vertikale verskil is die twee reghoeksye, en AB is die skuinssy. Omdat die verskille gekwadreer word, maak die volgorde van die punte nie saak nie, en 'n afstand is altyd positief. Los die antwoord in wortelvorm (bv. √45 = 3√5) of rond af tot twee desimale plekke, soos die vraag vra.\n\n### Middelpunt\n\nDie middelpunt is die **gemiddeld** van die x-koördinate en die gemiddeld van die y-koördinate. As die middelpunt M en een eindpunt A gegee is, kry jy die ander eindpunt met x_{B} = 2x_{M} − x_{A} en y_{B} = 2y_{M} − y_{A}.\n\n### Gradiënt\n\nDie gradiënt meet hoe steil 'n lyn is: [[verandering in y/verandering in x]].\n\n- m > 0: die lyn styg na regs. m < 0: die lyn daal na regs.\n- Horisontale lyn (y = k): m = 0.\n- Vertikale lyn (x = k): m is **ongedefinieerd**, want jy sal deur 0 moet deel.\n\n## Ewewydige en loodregte lyne\n\n- **Ewewydig (∥):** m_{1} = m_{2}.\n- **Loodreg (⊥):** m_{1} × m_{2} = −1. Die loodregte gradiënt is die **negatiewe resiprook**: draai die breuk om en verander die teken. Bv. m = [[2/3]] → m_{⊥} = −[[3/2]].\n- Uitsondering: 'n horisontale en 'n vertikale lyn is loodreg, al kan jy nie m_{1} × m_{2} bereken nie.\n\n## Saamlynige punte\n\nPunte A, B en C is **saamlynig** as hulle op dieselfde reguit lyn lê. Bewys dit met m_{AB} = m_{BC}. Omdat die twee lynstukke die punt B deel en ewe steil is, vorm hulle een reguit lyn.\n\n## Vergelyking van 'n reguit lyn: y = mx + c\n\n1. Bereken m uit twee punte, of neem dit van 'n ewewydige of loodregte lyn.\n2. Vervang een bekende punt (x; y) in y = mx + c en los c op.\n3. Skryf die vergelyking in die vorm y = mx + c.\n\nJy mag ook y − y_{1} = m(x − x_{1}) gebruik; dit gee dieselfde antwoord.\n\n## Vierhoeke bewys met koördinate\n\n| Vierhoek | Wys dat ... |\n|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | albei pare teenoorstaande sye ewewydig is (gelyke gradiënte), **of** die hoeklyne mekaar halveer (dieselfde middelpunt), **of** een paar teenoorstaande sye gelyk en ewewydig is |\n| Reghoek | dit 'n parallelogram is met een regte hoek (m_{1} × m_{2} = −1), of met gelyke hoeklyne |\n| Ruit | dit 'n parallelogram is met twee aangrensende sye gelyk, of met hoeklyne wat loodreg op mekaar is |\n| Vierkant | dit 'n ruit is met een regte hoek, of 'n reghoek met twee aangrensende sye gelyk |\n| Trapesium | een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig is |\n| Vlieër | twee pare aangrensende sye gelyk is |\n\nVir driehoeke: 'n driehoek is **reghoekig** as twee sye loodreg is (of as Pythagoras klop), en **gelykbenig** as twee sye ewe lank is.\n\n> **Onthou!** Gee altyd die rede in woorde, bv. \"AB = BC, dus is die parallelogram 'n ruit\". Die berekening alleen is nie 'n bewys nie.\n\n## Ontbrekende koördinaat\n\nSkryf die gegewe inligting as 'n vergelyking met die onbekende en los dit op:\n\n- **Gegewe gradiënt:** stel [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] gelyk aan die gegewe waarde en kruisvermenigvuldig.\n- **Gegewe afstand:** kwadreer albei kante. Jy kry dikwels **twee** antwoorde (±), en albei kan geldig wees.\n- **Gegewe middelpunt:** stel elke koördinaat se gemiddeld gelyk aan die middelpunt se koördinaat.\n- **Saamlynig, ewewydig of loodreg:** stel die gradiënte gelyk, of stel hul produk gelyk aan −1.\n- **Vierde hoekpunt van 'n parallelogram:** die hoeklyne het dieselfde middelpunt.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Tekenfoute met negatiewe getalle: 3 − (−2) = 5, en (−4)^{2} = 16, nie −16 nie.\n- Die volgorde in die gradiëntformule meng: as jy bo met y_{2} begin, moet jy onder met x_{2} begin.\n- Vergeet om deur 2 te deel by die middelpunt.\n- Vergeet die wortel by die afstand.\n- Dink loodreg beteken net \"verander die teken\". Jy moet die breuk ook omdraai.\n- Wys net dat al die sye gelyk is en noem die vorm 'n vierkant. Kontroleer ook vir 'n regte hoek.","en":"## The three basic formulas\n\nFor two points A(x_{1}; y_{1}) and B(x_{2}; y_{2}):\n\n| What | Formula |\n|---|---|\n| Distance (length of AB) | AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] |\n| Midpoint M of AB | M([[x_{1} + x_{2}/2]] ; [[y_{1} + y_{2}/2]]) |\n| Gradient of AB | m_{AB} = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] |\n\n> **Tip:** Always make a rough sketch of the points first. Then you quickly see whether your answer makes sense.\n\n### Distance\n\nThe distance formula is just **Pythagoras**: the horizontal difference and the vertical difference are the two shorter sides, and AB is the hypotenuse. Because the differences are squared, the order of the points does not matter, and a distance is always positive. Leave the answer in surd form (e.g. √45 = 3√5) or round off to two decimal places, as the question asks.\n\n### Midpoint\n\nThe midpoint is the **average** of the x-coordinates and the average of the y-coordinates. If the midpoint M and one endpoint A are given, you find the other endpoint with x_{B} = 2x_{M} − x_{A} and y_{B} = 2y_{M} − y_{A}.\n\n### Gradient\n\nThe gradient measures how steep a line is: [[change in y/change in x]].\n\n- m > 0: the line rises to the right. m < 0: the line falls to the right.\n- Horizontal line (y = k): m = 0.\n- Vertical line (x = k): m is **undefined**, because you would have to divide by 0.\n\n## Parallel and perpendicular lines\n\n- **Parallel (∥):** m_{1} = m_{2}.\n- **Perpendicular (⊥):** m_{1} × m_{2} = −1. The perpendicular gradient is the **negative reciprocal**: flip the fraction and change the sign. E.g. m = [[2/3]] → m_{⊥} = −[[3/2]].\n- Exception: a horizontal and a vertical line are perpendicular, even though you cannot calculate m_{1} × m_{2}.\n\n## Collinear points\n\nPoints A, B and C are **collinear** if they lie on the same straight line. Prove it with m_{AB} = m_{BC}. Because the two line segments share the point B and are equally steep, they form one straight line.\n\n## Equation of a straight line: y = mx + c\n\n1. Calculate m from two points, or take it from a parallel or perpendicular line.\n2. Substitute one known point (x; y) into y = mx + c and solve for c.\n3. Write the equation in the form y = mx + c.\n\nYou may also use y − y_{1} = m(x − x_{1}); it gives the same answer.\n\n## Proving quadrilaterals with coordinates\n\n| Quadrilateral | Show that ... |\n|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | both pairs of opposite sides are parallel (equal gradients), **or** the diagonals bisect each other (same midpoint), **or** one pair of opposite sides is equal and parallel |\n| Rectangle | it is a parallelogram with one right angle (m_{1} × m_{2} = −1), or with equal diagonals |\n| Rhombus | it is a parallelogram with two adjacent sides equal, or with diagonals that are perpendicular to each other |\n| Square | it is a rhombus with one right angle, or a rectangle with two adjacent sides equal |\n| Trapezium | one pair of opposite sides is parallel |\n| Kite | two pairs of adjacent sides are equal |\n\nFor triangles: a triangle is **right-angled** if two sides are perpendicular (or if Pythagoras works), and **isosceles** if two sides are equally long.\n\n> **Remember!** Always give the reason in words, e.g. \"AB = BC, so the parallelogram is a rhombus\". The calculation alone is not a proof.\n\n## Missing coordinate\n\nWrite the given information as an equation with the unknown and solve it:\n\n- **Given gradient:** set [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] equal to the given value and cross-multiply.\n- **Given distance:** square both sides. You often get **two** answers (±), and both can be valid.\n- **Given midpoint:** set the average of each coordinate equal to the midpoint's coordinate.\n- **Collinear, parallel or perpendicular:** set the gradients equal, or set their product equal to −1.\n- **Fourth vertex of a parallelogram:** the diagonals have the same midpoint.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Sign errors with negative numbers: 3 − (−2) = 5, and (−4)^{2} = 16, not −16.\n- Mixing up the order in the gradient formula: if you start with y_{2} at the top, you must start with x_{2} at the bottom.\n- Forgetting to divide by 2 for the midpoint.\n- Forgetting the square root for the distance.\n- Thinking perpendicular only means \"change the sign\". You must also flip the fraction.\n- Showing only that all the sides are equal and calling the shape a square. Also check for a right angle."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Afstandsformule","en":"Distance formula"},"def":{"af":"AB = √[(x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²]. Dit gee die lengte van die lynstuk tussen twee punte en is gebaseer op Pythagoras.","en":"AB = √[(x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²]. It gives the length of the line segment between two points and is based on Pythagoras."}},{"term":{"af":"Middelpunt","en":"Midpoint"},"def":{"af":"Die punt presies halfpad tussen twee punte: M((x₁ + x₂)/2; (y₁ + y₂)/2).","en":"The point exactly halfway between two points: M((x₁ + x₂)/2; (y₁ + y₂)/2)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gradiënt","en":"Gradient"},"def":{"af":"Die steilheid van 'n lyn: m = (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁), die verandering in y gedeel deur die verandering in x.","en":"The steepness of a line: m = (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁), the change in y divided by the change in x."}},{"term":{"af":"Ewewydige lyne","en":"Parallel lines"},"def":{"af":"Lyne wat nooit sny nie. Hulle het gelyke gradiënte: m₁ = m₂.","en":"Lines that never meet. They have equal gradients: m₁ = m₂."}},{"term":{"af":"Loodregte lyne","en":"Perpendicular lines"},"def":{"af":"Lyne wat mekaar teen 90° sny. Die produk van hul gradiënte is −1: m₁ × m₂ = −1.","en":"Lines that cut each other at 90°. The product of their gradients is −1: m₁ × m₂ = −1."}},{"term":{"af":"Negatiewe resiprook","en":"Negative reciprocal"},"def":{"af":"Die breuk omgedraai en die teken verander, bv. ⅔ → −3/2. Dit gee die gradiënt van 'n loodregte lyn.","en":"The fraction flipped and the sign changed, e.g. ⅔ → −3/2. It gives the gradient of a perpendicular line."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamlynige punte","en":"Collinear points"},"def":{"af":"Drie of meer punte wat op dieselfde reguit lyn lê, bv. as m_AB = m_BC.","en":"Three or more points that lie on the same straight line, e.g. if m_AB = m_BC."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoeklyn","en":"Diagonal"},"def":{"af":"'n Lynstuk wat twee teenoorstaande hoekpunte van 'n vierhoek verbind. As die hoeklyne mekaar halveer, is die vierhoek 'n parallelogram.","en":"A line segment that joins two opposite vertices of a quadrilateral. If the diagonals bisect each other, the quadrilateral is a parallelogram."}},{"term":{"af":"Ongedefinieerde gradiënt","en":"Undefined gradient"},"def":{"af":"Die gradiënt van 'n vertikale lyn x = k: die verandering in x is 0 en jy kan nie deur 0 deel nie.","en":"The gradient of a vertical line x = k: the change in x is 0 and you cannot divide by 0."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Afstand, middelpunt en gradiënt","en":"Distance, midpoint and gradient"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee A(−2; 5) en B(4; −3). Bereken (a) die lengte van AB, (b) die koördinate van M, die middelpunt van AB, en (c) die gradiënt van AB.","en":"Given A(−2; 5) and B(4; −3). Calculate (a) the length of AB, (b) the coordinates of M, the midpoint of AB, and (c) the gradient of AB."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] = √[(4 − (−2))^{2} + (−3 − 5)^{2}]","en":"(a) AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] = √[(4 − (−2))^{2} + (−3 − 5)^{2}]"},{"af":"= √[6^{2} + (−8)^{2}] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 eenhede","en":"= √[6^{2} + (−8)^{2}] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 units"},{"af":"(b) M = ([[−2 + 4/2]] ; [[5 + (−3)/2]]) = ([[2/2]] ; [[2/2]]) = (1; 1)","en":"(b) M = ([[−2 + 4/2]] ; [[5 + (−3)/2]]) = ([[2/2]] ; [[2/2]]) = (1; 1)"},{"af":"(c) m_{AB} = [[−3 − 5/4 − (−2)]] = [[−8/6]] = −[[4/3]]","en":"(c) m_{AB} = [[−3 − 5/4 − (−2)]] = [[−8/6]] = −[[4/3]]"}],"answer":{"af":"AB = 10 eenhede; M(1; 1); m_AB = −4/3","en":"AB = 10 units; M(1; 1); m_AB = −4/3"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyking van 'n lyn en 'n loodregte lyn","en":"Equation of a line and a perpendicular line"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee C(−1; 4) en D(3; −4). (a) Bepaal die vergelyking van die lyn CD. (b) Bepaal die vergelyking van die lyn deur E(4; 1) wat loodreg op CD is.","en":"Given C(−1; 4) and D(3; −4). (a) Determine the equation of the line CD. (b) Determine the equation of the line through E(4; 1) that is perpendicular to CD."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) m_{CD} = [[−4 − 4/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2","en":"(a) m_{CD} = [[−4 − 4/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2"},{"af":"Vervang C(−1; 4) in y = −2x + c: 4 = −2(−1) + c → 4 = 2 + c → c = 2. Dus CD: y = −2x + 2.","en":"Substitute C(−1; 4) into y = −2x + c: 4 = −2(−1) + c → 4 = 2 + c → c = 2. So CD: y = −2x + 2."},{"af":"(b) Loodreg: m × (−2) = −1 → m = [[1/2]] (die negatiewe resiprook van −2).","en":"(b) Perpendicular: m × (−2) = −1 → m = [[1/2]] (the negative reciprocal of −2)."},{"af":"Vervang E(4; 1) in y = [[1/2]]x + c: 1 = [[1/2]](4) + c → 1 = 2 + c → c = −1","en":"Substitute E(4; 1) into y = [[1/2]]x + c: 1 = [[1/2]](4) + c → 1 = 2 + c → c = −1"},{"af":"Die loodregte lyn is y = [[1/2]]x − 1.","en":"The perpendicular line is y = [[1/2]]x − 1."}],"answer":{"af":"CD: y = −2x + 2; loodregte lyn: y = ½x − 1","en":"CD: y = −2x + 2; perpendicular line: y = ½x − 1"}},{"title":{"af":"Bewys dat 'n vierhoek 'n ruit is","en":"Prove that a quadrilateral is a rhombus"},"problem":{"af":"Die hoekpunte van vierhoek ABCD is A(1; 2), B(4; 6), C(9; 6) en D(6; 2). (a) Bewys dat ABCD 'n parallelogram is. (b) Bewys dat ABCD 'n ruit is. (c) Is ABCD 'n vierkant? Gee 'n rede.","en":"The vertices of quadrilateral ABCD are A(1; 2), B(4; 6), C(9; 6) and D(6; 2). (a) Prove that ABCD is a parallelogram. (b) Prove that ABCD is a rhombus. (c) Is ABCD a square? Give a reason."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Middelpunt van AC = ([[1 + 9/2]] ; [[2 + 6/2]]) = (5; 4). Middelpunt van BD = ([[4 + 6/2]] ; [[6 + 2/2]]) = (5; 4).","en":"(a) Midpoint of AC = ([[1 + 9/2]] ; [[2 + 6/2]]) = (5; 4). Midpoint of BD = ([[4 + 6/2]] ; [[6 + 2/2]]) = (5; 4)."},{"af":"Die hoeklyne het dieselfde middelpunt, dus halveer hulle mekaar. ABCD is 'n parallelogram.","en":"The diagonals have the same midpoint, so they bisect each other. ABCD is a parallelogram."},{"af":"(b) AB = √[(4 − 1)^{2} + (6 − 2)^{2}] = √(9 + 16) = 5 en BC = √[(9 − 4)^{2} + (6 − 6)^{2}] = √25 = 5","en":"(b) AB = √[(4 − 1)^{2} + (6 − 2)^{2}] = √(9 + 16) = 5 and BC = √[(9 − 4)^{2} + (6 − 6)^{2}] = √25 = 5"},{"af":"ABCD is 'n parallelogram met twee aangrensende sye gelyk (AB = BC), dus is dit 'n ruit.","en":"ABCD is a parallelogram with two adjacent sides equal (AB = BC), so it is a rhombus."},{"af":"(c) m_{AB} = [[6 − 2/4 − 1]] = [[4/3]] en m_{BC} = [[6 − 6/9 − 4]] = 0. Omdat [[4/3]] × 0 = 0 ≠ −1, is ∠ABC nie 90° nie, dus is ABCD nie 'n vierkant nie.","en":"(c) m_{AB} = [[6 − 2/4 − 1]] = [[4/3]] and m_{BC} = [[6 − 6/9 − 4]] = 0. Because [[4/3]] × 0 = 0 ≠ −1, ∠ABC is not 90°, so ABCD is not a square."}],"answer":{"af":"Parallelogram (hoeklyne halveer mekaar); ruit (AB = BC = 5); nie 'n vierkant nie (geen regte hoek)","en":"Parallelogram (diagonals bisect each other); rhombus (AB = BC = 5); not a square (no right angle)"}},{"title":{"af":"Ontbrekende koördinaat: saamlynige punte","en":"Missing coordinate: collinear points"},"problem":{"af":"Op 'n kaart van 'n sitrusplaas naby Brits staan drie besproeiingskrane by A(2; −1), B(5; 3) en C(k; 11). Hulle lê op een reguit pyplyn. Bepaal k en die lengte van die pyplyn AC as een eenheid 10 m is.","en":"On a map of a citrus farm near Brits, three irrigation taps stand at A(2; −1), B(5; 3) and C(k; 11). They lie on one straight pipeline. Determine k and the length of the pipeline AC if one unit is 10 m."},"steps":[{"af":"Die punte is saamlynig, dus m_{AB} = m_{BC}.","en":"The points are collinear, so m_{AB} = m_{BC}."},{"af":"m_{AB} = [[3 − (−1)/5 − 2]] = [[4/3]]","en":"m_{AB} = [[3 − (−1)/5 − 2]] = [[4/3]]"},{"af":"m_{BC} = [[11 − 3/k − 5]] = [[8/k − 5]]. Stel gelyk: [[8/k − 5]] = [[4/3]]","en":"m_{BC} = [[11 − 3/k − 5]] = [[8/k − 5]]. Set equal: [[8/k − 5]] = [[4/3]]"},{"af":"Kruisvermenigvuldig: 4(k − 5) = 24 → k − 5 = 6 → k = 11. Kontroleer: m_{AC} = [[12/9]] = [[4/3]] ✓","en":"Cross-multiply: 4(k − 5) = 24 → k − 5 = 6 → k = 11. Check: m_{AC} = [[12/9]] = [[4/3]] ✓"},{"af":"AC = √[(11 − 2)^{2} + (11 − (−1))^{2}] = √(81 + 144) = √225 = 15 eenhede = 15 × 10 m = 150 m","en":"AC = √[(11 − 2)^{2} + (11 − (−1))^{2}] = √(81 + 144) = √225 = 15 units = 15 × 10 m = 150 m"}],"answer":{"af":"k = 11; AC = 150 m","en":"k = 11; AC = 150 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter formule gee die gradiënt van die lyn deur (x₁; y₁) en (x₂; y₂)?","en":"Which formula gives the gradient of the line through (x₁; y₁) and (x₂; y₂)?"},"options":[{"af":"(x₂ − x₁)/(y₂ − y₁)","en":"(x₂ − x₁)/(y₂ − y₁)"},{"af":"(y₂ + y₁)/(x₂ + x₁)","en":"(y₂ + y₁)/(x₂ + x₁)"},{"af":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁)","en":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁)"},{"af":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₁ − x₂)","en":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₁ − x₂)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Gradiënt = verandering in y gedeel deur verandering in x, met dieselfde volgorde bo en onder. Die eerste opsie is omgekeer, die tweede lyk na die middelpuntformule en die laaste meng die volgorde (dit gee die verkeerde teken).","en":"Gradient = change in y divided by change in x, with the same order at the top and the bottom. The first option is upside down, the second looks like the midpoint formula and the last mixes the order (it gives the wrong sign)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As twee lyne loodreg op mekaar is, is hul gradiënte gelyk.","en":"If two lines are perpendicular to each other, their gradients are equal."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. Gelyke gradiënte beteken die lyne is ewewydig. Vir loodregte lyne is m₁ × m₂ = −1, bv. 2 en −½.","en":"False. Equal gradients mean the lines are parallel. For perpendicular lines m₁ × m₂ = −1, e.g. 2 and −½."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke gradiënt-eienskap by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each gradient property to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"m₁ = m₂","en":"m₁ = m₂"},"r":{"af":"Ewewydige lyne","en":"Parallel lines"}},{"l":{"af":"m₁ × m₂ = −1","en":"m₁ × m₂ = −1"},"r":{"af":"Loodregte lyne","en":"Perpendicular lines"}},{"l":{"af":"m = 0","en":"m = 0"},"r":{"af":"Horisontale lyn","en":"Horizontal line"}},{"l":{"af":"m is ongedefinieerd","en":"m is undefined"},"r":{"af":"Vertikale lyn","en":"Vertical line"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ewewydige lyne is ewe steil. By loodregte lyne is die gradiënte negatiewe resiproke. 'n Horisontale lyn het geen styging nie (m = 0), en by 'n vertikale lyn is die verandering in x nul, dus is m ongedefinieerd.","en":"Parallel lines are equally steep. For perpendicular lines the gradients are negative reciprocals. A horizontal line has no rise (m = 0), and for a vertical line the change in x is zero, so m is undefined."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die middelpunt van A(−3; 7) en B(5; −1)?","en":"What is the midpoint of A(−3; 7) and B(5; −1)?"},"options":[{"af":"(1; 3)","en":"(1; 3)"},{"af":"(4; −4)","en":"(4; −4)"},{"af":"(2; 6)","en":"(2; 6)"},{"af":"(8; −8)","en":"(8; −8)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"M = ((−3 + 5)/2; (7 + (−1))/2) = (2/2; 6/2) = (1; 3). (2; 6) vergeet om deur 2 te deel, (4; −4) trek af in plaas daarvan om bymekaar te tel, en (8; −8) trek af sonder om te halveer.","en":"M = ((−3 + 5)/2; (7 + (−1))/2) = (2/2; 6/2) = (1; 3). (2; 6) forgets to divide by 2, (4; −4) subtracts instead of adding, and (8; −8) subtracts without halving."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op 'n kaart van Brits (eenhede in km) is die taxistaanplek by P(1; −2) en die skool by Q(7; 6). Hoe ver is dit in 'n reguit lyn van P na Q?","en":"On a map of Brits (units in km) the taxi rank is at P(1; −2) and the school is at Q(7; 6). How far is it in a straight line from P to Q?"},"options":[{"af":"√52 ≈ 7,21 km","en":"√52 ≈ 7.21 km"},{"af":"14 km","en":"14 km"},{"af":"100 km","en":"100 km"},{"af":"10 km","en":"10 km"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"PQ = √[(7 − 1)² + (6 − (−2))²] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 km. √52 kom van 6 − 2 in plaas van 6 − (−2), 14 tel net die verskille bymekaar, en 100 vergeet die wortel.","en":"PQ = √[(7 − 1)² + (6 − (−2))²] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 km. √52 comes from 6 − 2 instead of 6 − (−2), 14 just adds the differences, and 100 forgets the square root."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt van die lyn deur (−1; 4) en (3; −8)?","en":"What is the gradient of the line through (−1; 4) and (3; −8)?"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"−3","en":"−3"},{"af":"−⅓","en":"−⅓"},{"af":"−6","en":"−6"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"m = (−8 − 4)/(3 − (−1)) = −12/4 = −3. Die lyn daal na regs, dus moet m negatief wees. −⅓ is Δx/Δy (omgekeer) en −6 kom van 3 − 1 = 2 in die noemer.","en":"m = (−8 − 4)/(3 − (−1)) = −12/4 = −3. The line falls to the right, so m must be negative. −⅓ is Δx/Δy (upside down) and −6 comes from 3 − 1 = 2 in the denominator."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt van 'n lyn wat loodreg is op y = ⅔x − 1? m = ___","en":"What is the gradient of a line that is perpendicular to y = ⅔x − 1? m = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3/2","−3/2","-1,5","−1,5","m = -3/2","m=-3/2","m = −3/2","m=−3/2","m = -1,5","m=-1,5"],"en":["-3/2","−3/2","-1.5","−1.5","m = -3/2","m=-3/2","m = −3/2","m=−3/2","m = -1.5","m=-1.5"]},"explain":{"af":"Die gegewe lyn se gradiënt is ⅔. Loodreg: ⅔ × m = −1 → m = −3/2 = −1,5. Draai die breuk om EN verander die teken.","en":"The given line's gradient is ⅔. Perpendicular: ⅔ × m = −1 → m = −3/2 = −1.5. Flip the fraction AND change the sign."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die punte A(0; 1), B(2; 5) en C(4; 9) is saamlynig.","en":"The points A(0; 1), B(2; 5) and C(4; 9) are collinear."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. m_AB = (5 − 1)/(2 − 0) = 2 en m_BC = (9 − 5)/(4 − 2) = 2. Die gradiënte is gelyk en B is 'n gemeenskaplike punt, dus lê al drie punte op dieselfde lyn.","en":"True. m_AB = (5 − 1)/(2 − 0) = 2 and m_BC = (9 − 5)/(4 − 2) = 2. The gradients are equal and B is a common point, so all three points lie on the same line."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"M(2; −1) is die middelpunt van lynstuk AB, met A(−1; 3). Die y-koördinaat van B is ___.","en":"M(2; −1) is the midpoint of line segment AB, with A(−1; 3). The y-coordinate of B is ___."},"answers":{"af":["-5","−5","y = -5","y=-5","y = −5","y=−5"],"en":["-5","−5","y = -5","y=-5","y = −5","y=−5"]},"explain":{"af":"(3 + y)/2 = −1 → 3 + y = −2 → y = −5. Net so: (−1 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 5, dus B(5; −5). Kortpad: y_B = 2(−1) − 3 = −5.","en":"(3 + y)/2 = −1 → 3 + y = −2 → y = −5. In the same way: (−1 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 5, so B(5; −5). Shortcut: y_B = 2(−1) − 3 = −5."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die vergelyking van die lyn deur (2; 1) wat ewewydig is aan y = 3x − 4?","en":"What is the equation of the line through (2; 1) that is parallel to y = 3x − 4?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 3x − 4","en":"y = 3x − 4"},{"af":"y = 3x + 7","en":"y = 3x + 7"},{"af":"y = −3x + 7","en":"y = −3x + 7"},{"af":"y = 3x − 5","en":"y = 3x − 5"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ewewydig, dus m = 3. Vervang (2; 1): 1 = 3(2) + c → c = 1 − 6 = −5. Dus y = 3x − 5. y = 3x − 4 is die gegewe lyn self (dit gaan nie deur (2; 1) nie), y = 3x + 7 het 'n tekenfout by c, en y = −3x + 7 het die verkeerde gradiënt.","en":"Parallel, so m = 3. Substitute (2; 1): 1 = 3(2) + c → c = 1 − 6 = −5. So y = 3x − 5. y = 3x − 4 is the given line itself (it does not pass through (2; 1)), y = 3x + 7 has a sign error in c, and y = −3x + 7 has the wrong gradient."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die afstand tussen P(1; t) en Q(4; 2) is 5 eenhede. Bepaal t.","en":"The distance between P(1; t) and Q(4; 2) is 5 units. Determine t."},"options":[{"af":"t = −2 of t = 6","en":"t = −2 or t = 6"},{"af":"t = 6","en":"t = 6"},{"af":"t = 2 of t = −6","en":"t = 2 or t = −6"},{"af":"t = 7","en":"t = 7"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"(4 − 1)² + (2 − t)² = 25 → 9 + (2 − t)² = 25 → (2 − t)² = 16 → 2 − t = ±4 → t = −2 of t = 6. Albei punte lê 5 eenhede van Q af: een bo en een onder. \"t = 6\" vergeet die negatiewe wortel.","en":"(4 − 1)² + (2 − t)² = 25 → 9 + (2 − t)² = 25 → (2 − t)² = 16 → 2 − t = ±4 → t = −2 or t = 6. Both points lie 5 units from Q: one above and one below. \"t = 6\" forgets the negative root."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die punte A(−1; −3), B(1; 1) en C(4; k) is saamlynig. k = ___","en":"The points A(−1; −3), B(1; 1) and C(4; k) are collinear. k = ___"},"answers":{"af":["7","k = 7","k=7"],"en":["7","k = 7","k=7"]},"explain":{"af":"m_AB = (1 − (−3))/(1 − (−1)) = 4/2 = 2. Stel m_BC = 2: (k − 1)/(4 − 1) = 2 → k − 1 = 6 → k = 7.","en":"m_AB = (1 − (−3))/(1 − (−1)) = 4/2 = 2. Set m_BC = 2: (k − 1)/(4 − 1) = 2 → k − 1 = 6 → k = 7."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die hoekpunte van vierhoek PQRS is P(−2; 1), Q(1; 4), R(4; 1) en S(1; −2). Wat is die mees spesifieke naam vir PQRS?","en":"The vertices of quadrilateral PQRS are P(−2; 1), Q(1; 4), R(4; 1) and S(1; −2). What is the most specific name for PQRS?"},"options":[{"af":"Ruit","en":"Rhombus"},{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},{"af":"Vlieër","en":"Kite"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Al vier sye is √18 lank (bv. PQ = √(3² + 3²)), dus is PQRS ten minste 'n ruit. m_PQ = 3/3 = 1 en m_QR = −3/3 = −1, en 1 × (−1) = −1, dus is ∠Q = 90°. 'n Ruit met 'n regte hoek is 'n vierkant. (Die hoeklyne PR en QS is ook albei 6 eenhede lank.)","en":"All four sides are √18 long (e.g. PQ = √(3² + 3²)), so PQRS is at least a rhombus. m_PQ = 3/3 = 1 and m_QR = −3/3 = −1, and 1 × (−1) = −1, so ∠Q = 90°. A rhombus with a right angle is a square. (The diagonals PR and QS are also both 6 units long.)"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"A(−2; 3), B(4; 5) en C(6; −1) is drie hoekpunte van parallelogram ABCD. Bepaal die koördinate van D. D = ___","en":"A(−2; 3), B(4; 5) and C(6; −1) are three vertices of parallelogram ABCD. Determine the coordinates of D. D = ___"},"answers":{"af":["(0; −3)","(0;-3)","(0;−3)","0;-3","0;−3","(0,-3)","(0,−3)","D(0;-3)","D(0;−3)","D(0; −3)"],"en":["(0; −3)","(0;-3)","(0;−3)","0;-3","0;−3","(0,-3)","(0,−3)","D(0;-3)","D(0;−3)","D(0; −3)"]},"explain":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n parallelogram halveer mekaar, dus het AC en BD dieselfde middelpunt. Middelpunt van AC = ((−2 + 6)/2; (3 + (−1))/2) = (2; 1). Vir BD: (4 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 0 en (5 + y)/2 = 1 → y = −3. Dus D(0; −3).","en":"The diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other, so AC and BD have the same midpoint. Midpoint of AC = ((−2 + 6)/2; (3 + (−1))/2) = (2; 1). For BD: (4 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 0 and (5 + y)/2 = 1 → y = −3. So D(0; −3)."}}]},{"id":"w10-t3-finansies","title":{"af":"Finansies en groei","en":"Finance and growth"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal enkelvoudige en saamgestelde rente, huurkoop, inflasie, bevolkingsgroei en wisselkoerse kan bereken en verduidelik watter formule wanneer gebruik word.","en":"You will be able to calculate simple and compound interest, hire purchase, inflation, population growth and exchange rates, and explain which formula to use when."},"summary":{"af":"## Die simbole wat jy moet ken\n\n| Simbool | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| P | **hoofsom**: die beginbedrag wat jy belê of leen |\n| A | **opgehoopte bedrag**: die eindbedrag ná n jaar |\n| i | **rentekoers** per jaar as 'n desimaal: 8% → i = [[8/100]] = 0,08 |\n| n | **tydperk** in jare (of die aantal saamstellingsperiodes) |\n\nDie rente wat jy verdien (of betaal) is **A − P**. Geldbedrae word afgerond tot die naaste sent, dus **twee desimale plekke**, en in Afrikaans so geskryf: R12 345,67.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om i = 8 in plaas van i = 0,08 in te vervang. Deel die persentasie altyd eers deur 100.\n\n## Enkelvoudige rente\n\n**A = P(1 + in)**\n\nDie rente word elke jaar net op die **oorspronklike hoofsom** bereken, so jy kry elke jaar presies dieselfde bedrag rente. Daarom is die groei **lineêr**: die grafiek van A teenoor n is 'n reguit lyn.\n\n- Tyd in maande? Skakel om na jare: 18 maande → n = [[18/12]] = 1,5.\n- Jy kan ook P, i of n bereken: vervang die bekende waardes en los die vergelyking op. Bv. R6 000 groei teen 8% p.j. enkelvoudige rente tot R8 400: 8 400 = 6 000(1 + 0,08n) → 1,4 = 1 + 0,08n → n = 5 jaar.\n\n## Saamgestelde rente\n\n**A = P(1 + i)^{n}**\n\nHier word rente bereken op die hoofsom **plus die rente wat reeds bygetel is**: rente op rente. Die groei is **eksponensieel**: die grafiek is 'n kromme wat al hoe steiler word. Ná die eerste jaar gee saamgestelde rente altyd meer as enkelvoudige rente teen dieselfde koers.\n\nOm die hoofsom te kry as die eindbedrag gegee is (\"Hoeveel moet ek nou belê?\"): **P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}**.\n\n### Saamstellingsperiodes\n\nAs rente meer as een keer per jaar bygetel word, pas jy i **én** n aan:\n\n| Saamgestel | Koers per periode | Aantal periodes |\n|---|---|---|\n| jaarliks | i | n |\n| halfjaarliks | [[i/2]] | 2n |\n| kwartaalliks | [[i/4]] | 4n |\n| maandeliks | [[i/12]] | 12n |\n\nBv. 8% p.j., kwartaalliks saamgestel vir 5 jaar: A = P(1 + [[0,08/4]])^{20}.\n\n> **Wenk:** Tik die hele berekening in een keer op jou sakrekenaar. As jy tussenin afrond (bv. 1,00875 → 1,01), sal jou antwoord verkeerd wees. Rond net die finale antwoord af.\n\n## Huurkoop\n\nMet **huurkoop** neem jy die item nou en betaal dit in maandelikse paaiemente af. Die rente is **enkelvoudige rente op die uitstaande bedrag** (die balans ná die deposito).\n\n1. Deposito = persentasie × kontantprys.\n2. Uitstaande bedrag: P = kontantprys − deposito.\n3. A = P(1 + in): die totaal wat jy oor die tydperk terugbetaal.\n4. Maandelikse paaiement = A ÷ aantal maande. Tel maandelikse versekering by as dit gegee word.\n5. Totale koste = deposito + A (+ alle versekering).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om rente op die volle kontantprys te bereken, of om te vergeet om die deposito eers af te trek.\n\n## Inflasie\n\n**Inflasie** is die algemene styging in pryse oor tyd. Dit werk presies soos saamgestelde rente: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, waar i die inflasiekoers is. Om 'n vroeëre prys te kry, deel jy: P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}.\n\n## Bevolkingsgroei\n\n'n Bevolking groei ook saamgesteld: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, met P die huidige bevolking en i die groeikoers per jaar. Rond die antwoord af tot 'n **heelgetal**, want daar is nie 0,4 van 'n mens nie.\n\n## Wisselkoerse\n\n'n **Wisselkoers** sê hoeveel een geldeenheid in 'n ander werd is, bv. $1 = R18,40.\n\n- Buitelandse geld → rand: **vermenigvuldig** met die koers: $150 × 18,40 = R2 760,00.\n- Rand → buitelandse geld: **deel** deur die koers: R2 000 ÷ 18,40 = $108,70.\n- Die rand **verswak** as jy meer rand vir een dollar moet betaal (bv. R18,40 → R19,10). Ingevoerde goedere soos selfone en petrol word duurder, maar uitvoerders, soos die sitrusboere by Brits, kry meer rand vir elke dollar.\n- Die rand **versterk** as een dollar minder rand kos. Dan word invoere goedkoper.\n\n> **Onthou!** Gesonde-verstand-toets: een dollar (of euro of pond) is meer werd as een rand, dus moet die getal rand altyd **groter** wees as die getal dollar.\n\n## Stappe vir enige finansiesom\n\n1. Besluit watter tipe dit is: enkelvoudig, saamgesteld, huurkoop, inflasie, bevolking of wisselkoers.\n2. Skryf die formule neer.\n3. Skryf P, i en n neer, en pas i en n aan vir die saamstellingsperiode.\n4. Vervang en bereken in een stap.\n5. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke en skryf die eenheid (R, $, € of £).","en":"## The symbols you must know\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| P | **principal**: the starting amount you invest or borrow |\n| A | **accumulated amount**: the final amount after n years |\n| i | **interest rate** per year as a decimal: 8% → i = [[8/100]] = 0.08 |\n| n | **time period** in years (or the number of compounding periods) |\n\nThe interest you earn (or pay) is **A − P**. Money is rounded to the nearest cent, so **two decimal places**, e.g. R12 345.67.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Substituting i = 8 instead of i = 0.08. Always divide the percentage by 100 first.\n\n## Simple interest\n\n**A = P(1 + in)**\n\nInterest is calculated each year only on the **original principal**, so you get exactly the same amount of interest every year. That is why the growth is **linear**: the graph of A against n is a straight line.\n\n- Time in months? Convert to years: 18 months → n = [[18/12]] = 1.5.\n- You can also calculate P, i or n: substitute the known values and solve the equation. E.g. R6 000 grows at 8% p.a. simple interest to R8 400: 8 400 = 6 000(1 + 0.08n) → 1.4 = 1 + 0.08n → n = 5 years.\n\n## Compound interest\n\n**A = P(1 + i)^{n}**\n\nHere interest is calculated on the principal **plus the interest already added**: interest on interest. The growth is **exponential**: the graph is a curve that gets steeper and steeper. After the first year compound interest always gives more than simple interest at the same rate.\n\nTo find the principal when the final amount is given (\"How much must I invest now?\"): **P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}**.\n\n### Compounding periods\n\nIf interest is added more than once a year, adjust **both** i and n:\n\n| Compounded | Rate per period | Number of periods |\n|---|---|---|\n| annually | i | n |\n| half-yearly | [[i/2]] | 2n |\n| quarterly | [[i/4]] | 4n |\n| monthly | [[i/12]] | 12n |\n\nE.g. 8% p.a. compounded quarterly for 5 years: A = P(1 + [[0.08/4]])^{20}.\n\n> **Tip:** Type the whole calculation into your calculator in one go. If you round in between (e.g. 1.00875 → 1.01), your answer will be wrong. Only round the final answer.\n\n## Hire purchase\n\nWith **hire purchase** you take the item now and pay it off in monthly instalments. The interest is **simple interest on the outstanding amount** (the balance after the deposit).\n\n1. Deposit = percentage × cash price.\n2. Outstanding amount: P = cash price − deposit.\n3. A = P(1 + in): the total you pay back over the period.\n4. Monthly instalment = A ÷ number of months. Add monthly insurance if it is given.\n5. Total cost = deposit + A (+ all insurance).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Calculating interest on the full cash price, or forgetting to subtract the deposit first.\n\n## Inflation\n\n**Inflation** is the general rise in prices over time. It works exactly like compound interest: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, where i is the inflation rate. To find an earlier price, divide: P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}.\n\n## Population growth\n\nA population also grows in a compound way: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, with P the current population and i the growth rate per year. Round the answer to a **whole number**, because there is no such thing as 0.4 of a person.\n\n## Exchange rates\n\nAn **exchange rate** tells you how much one currency is worth in another, e.g. $1 = R18.40.\n\n- Foreign currency → rand: **multiply** by the rate: $150 × 18.40 = R2 760.00.\n- Rand → foreign currency: **divide** by the rate: R2 000 ÷ 18.40 = $108.70.\n- The rand **weakens** when you have to pay more rand for one dollar (e.g. R18.40 → R19.10). Imported goods such as cellphones and petrol become more expensive, but exporters, such as the citrus farmers near Brits, get more rand for every dollar.\n- The rand **strengthens** when one dollar costs fewer rand. Then imports become cheaper.\n\n> **Remember!** Common-sense check: one dollar (or euro or pound) is worth more than one rand, so the number of rand must always be **bigger** than the number of dollars.\n\n## Steps for any finance question\n\n1. Decide what type it is: simple, compound, hire purchase, inflation, population or exchange rate.\n2. Write down the formula.\n3. Write down P, i and n, and adjust i and n for the compounding period.\n4. Substitute and calculate in one step.\n5. Round to two decimal places and write the unit (R, $, € or £)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoofsom (P)","en":"Principal (P)"},"def":{"af":"Die beginbedrag wat belê of geleen word.","en":"The starting amount that is invested or borrowed."}},{"term":{"af":"Opgehoopte bedrag (A)","en":"Accumulated amount (A)"},"def":{"af":"Die totale bedrag (hoofsom plus rente) aan die einde van die tydperk.","en":"The total amount (principal plus interest) at the end of the period."}},{"term":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente","en":"Simple interest"},"def":{"af":"Rente wat elke jaar net op die oorspronklike hoofsom bereken word: A = P(1 + in). Die groei is lineêr.","en":"Interest calculated each year only on the original principal: A = P(1 + in). The growth is linear."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde rente","en":"Compound interest"},"def":{"af":"Rente wat op die hoofsom plus die reeds bygetelde rente bereken word: A = P(1 + i)ⁿ. Die groei is eksponensieel.","en":"Interest calculated on the principal plus the interest already added: A = P(1 + i)ⁿ. The growth is exponential."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamstellingsperiode","en":"Compounding period"},"def":{"af":"Hoe gereeld rente bygetel word (jaarliks, halfjaarliks, kwartaalliks of maandeliks). Dit verander die waardes van i en n.","en":"How often interest is added (annually, half-yearly, quarterly or monthly). It changes the values of i and n."}},{"term":{"af":"Huurkoop","en":"Hire purchase"},"def":{"af":"Koop op krediet: jy betaal 'n deposito en dan maandelikse paaiemente, met enkelvoudige rente op die uitstaande bedrag.","en":"Buying on credit: you pay a deposit and then monthly instalments, with simple interest on the outstanding amount."}},{"term":{"af":"Paaiement","en":"Instalment"},"def":{"af":"Die vaste bedrag wat elke maand betaal word om 'n skuld af te betaal.","en":"The fixed amount paid every month to pay off a debt."}},{"term":{"af":"Inflasie","en":"Inflation"},"def":{"af":"Die algemene styging in die pryse van goedere en dienste oor tyd; dit word met saamgestelde groei bereken.","en":"The general rise in the prices of goods and services over time; it is calculated with compound growth."}},{"term":{"af":"Wisselkoers","en":"Exchange rate"},"def":{"af":"Die waarde van een geldeenheid uitgedruk in 'n ander, bv. $1 = R18,40.","en":"The value of one currency expressed in another, e.g. $1 = R18.40."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Enkelvoudige teenoor saamgestelde rente","en":"Simple versus compound interest"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato belê R8 000 vir 5 jaar teen 7,5% p.j. Bereken die opgehoopte bedrag as die rente (a) enkelvoudig is en (b) jaarliks saamgestel word. (c) Hoeveel meer lewer die saamgestelde belegging op?","en":"Lerato invests R8 000 for 5 years at 7.5% p.a. Calculate the accumulated amount if the interest is (a) simple and (b) compounded annually. (c) How much more does the compound investment give?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf die waardes neer: P = 8 000; i = [[7,5/100]] = 0,075; n = 5.","en":"Write down the values: P = 8 000; i = [[7.5/100]] = 0.075; n = 5."},{"af":"(a) A = P(1 + in) = 8 000(1 + 0,075 × 5) = 8 000 × 1,375","en":"(a) A = P(1 + in) = 8 000(1 + 0.075 × 5) = 8 000 × 1.375"},{"af":"A = R11 000,00","en":"A = R11 000.00"},{"af":"(b) A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 8 000(1 + 0,075)^{5} = 8 000(1,075)^{5} = R11 485,03 (tik dit in een keer in)","en":"(b) A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 8 000(1 + 0.075)^{5} = 8 000(1.075)^{5} = R11 485.03 (type it in one go)"},{"af":"(c) Verskil = 11 485,03 − 11 000,00 = R485,03","en":"(c) Difference = 11 485.03 − 11 000.00 = R485.03"},{"af":"Saamgestelde rente lewer meer op, want elke jaar word rente ook op die vorige jare se rente verdien.","en":"Compound interest gives more, because each year interest is also earned on the previous years' interest."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R11 000,00  (b) R11 485,03  (c) R485,03 meer","en":"(a) R11 000.00  (b) R11 485.03  (c) R485.03 more"}},{"title":{"af":"Maandeliks saamgestelde rente","en":"Interest compounded monthly"},"problem":{"af":"Johan belê R15 000 in 'n spaarrekening by 'n bank in Pretoria teen 10,5% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel. Hoeveel is in die rekening ná 4 jaar, en hoeveel rente het hy verdien?","en":"Johan invests R15 000 in a savings account at a bank in Pretoria at 10.5% p.a., compounded monthly. How much is in the account after 4 years, and how much interest did he earn?"},"steps":[{"af":"Maandeliks: deel die koers deur 12 en vermenigvuldig die jare met 12. i = [[0,105/12]] = 0,00875 per maand; n = 4 × 12 = 48 maande.","en":"Monthly: divide the rate by 12 and multiply the years by 12. i = [[0.105/12]] = 0.00875 per month; n = 4 × 12 = 48 months."},{"af":"A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 15 000(1 + [[0,105/12]])^{48}","en":"A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 15 000(1 + [[0.105/12]])^{48}"},{"af":"A = R22 787,76 (moenie 1,00875 afrond voordat jy die mag bereken nie)","en":"A = R22 787.76 (do not round 1.00875 before you work out the power)"},{"af":"Rente = A − P = 22 787,76 − 15 000 = R7 787,76","en":"Interest = A − P = 22 787.76 − 15 000 = R7 787.76"}],"answer":{"af":"A = R22 787,76; rente = R7 787,76","en":"A = R22 787.76; interest = R7 787.76"}},{"title":{"af":"Huurkoop","en":"Hire purchase"},"problem":{"af":"Thandi koop 'n yskas met 'n kontantprys van R12 000 op huurkoop by 'n meubelwinkel in Brits. Sy betaal 10% deposito en die balans oor 2 jaar teen 15% p.j. enkelvoudige rente. Bereken (a) haar maandelikse paaiement en (b) die totale bedrag wat sy vir die yskas betaal.","en":"Thandi buys a fridge with a cash price of R12 000 on hire purchase at a furniture store in Brits. She pays a 10% deposit and the balance over 2 years at 15% p.a. simple interest. Calculate (a) her monthly instalment and (b) the total amount she pays for the fridge."},"steps":[{"af":"Deposito = 10% × 12 000 = 0,1 × 12 000 = R1 200,00","en":"Deposit = 10% × 12 000 = 0.1 × 12 000 = R1 200.00"},{"af":"Uitstaande bedrag: P = 12 000 − 1 200 = R10 800,00. Die rente word net hierop bereken.","en":"Outstanding amount: P = 12 000 − 1 200 = R10 800.00. Interest is charged only on this."},{"af":"A = P(1 + in) = 10 800(1 + 0,15 × 2) = 10 800 × 1,3 = R14 040,00","en":"A = P(1 + in) = 10 800(1 + 0.15 × 2) = 10 800 × 1.3 = R14 040.00"},{"af":"(a) 2 jaar = 24 maande. Paaiement = 14 040 ÷ 24 = R585,00 per maand","en":"(a) 2 years = 24 months. Instalment = 14 040 ÷ 24 = R585.00 per month"},{"af":"(b) Totaal = deposito + A = 1 200 + 14 040 = R15 240,00. Dit is R3 240,00 meer as die kontantprys.","en":"(b) Total = deposit + A = 1 200 + 14 040 = R15 240.00. That is R3 240.00 more than the cash price."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R585,00 per maand  (b) R15 240,00","en":"(a) R585.00 per month  (b) R15 240.00"}},{"title":{"af":"Wisselkoerse en 'n swakker rand","en":"Exchange rates and a weaker rand"},"problem":{"af":"'n Sitrusboer naby Brits voer lemoene na Europa uit en ontvang €18 000. (a) Hoeveel rand is dit as €1 = R20,15? (b) Die rand verswak na €1 = R20,90. Hoeveel meer rand kry die boer nou vir dieselfde €18 000? (c) Is 'n swakker rand goed of sleg vir 'n gesin wat 'n vakansie in Europa beplan?","en":"A citrus farmer near Brits exports oranges to Europe and receives €18 000. (a) How many rand is that if €1 = R20.15? (b) The rand weakens to €1 = R20.90. How many more rand does the farmer now get for the same €18 000? (c) Is a weaker rand good or bad for a family planning a holiday in Europe?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Euro → rand: vermenigvuldig met die koers. 18 000 × 20,15 = R362 700,00","en":"(a) Euro → rand: multiply by the rate. 18 000 × 20.15 = R362 700.00"},{"af":"(b) Teen die nuwe koers: 18 000 × 20,90 = R376 200,00","en":"(b) At the new rate: 18 000 × 20.90 = R376 200.00"},{"af":"Verskil = 376 200 − 362 700 = R13 500,00 meer vir die boer","en":"Difference = 376 200 − 362 700 = R13 500.00 more for the farmer"},{"af":"(c) Sleg: die rand het verswak, so die gesin moet nou meer rand betaal vir elke euro wat hulle in Europa spandeer. Wat goed is vir uitvoerders, is sleg vir invoerders en reisigers.","en":"(c) Bad: the rand has weakened, so the family must now pay more rand for every euro they spend in Europe. What is good for exporters is bad for importers and travellers."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R362 700,00  (b) R13 500,00 meer  (c) sleg vir die gesin","en":"(a) R362 700.00  (b) R13 500.00 more  (c) bad for the family"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die formule A = P(1 + in) staan P vir …","en":"In the formula A = P(1 + in), P stands for …"},"options":[{"af":"die opgehoopte bedrag ná n jaar","en":"the accumulated amount after n years"},{"af":"die rentekoers per jaar","en":"the interest rate per year"},{"af":"die hoofsom (die beginbedrag)","en":"the principal (the starting amount)"},{"af":"die rente wat verdien is","en":"the interest earned"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"P is die hoofsom: die bedrag waarmee jy begin. A is die eindbedrag, i die rentekoers en die rente self is A − P.","en":"P is the principal: the amount you start with. A is the final amount, i is the interest rate and the interest itself is A − P."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"By enkelvoudige rente is die grafiek van die opgehoopte bedrag teenoor die tyd 'n kromme wat al hoe steiler word.","en":"With simple interest the graph of the accumulated amount against time is a curve that gets steeper and steeper."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Enkelvoudige rente gee elke jaar dieselfde bedrag rente, so die groei is lineêr: 'n reguit lyn. Die kromme hoort by saamgestelde rente (eksponensiële groei).","en":"False. Simple interest gives the same amount of interest every year, so the growth is linear: a straight line. The curve belongs to compound interest (exponential growth)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing of formule.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description or formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente","en":"Simple interest"},"r":{"af":"A = P(1 + in)","en":"A = P(1 + in)"}},{"l":{"af":"Saamgestelde rente","en":"Compound interest"},"r":{"af":"A = P(1 + i)ⁿ","en":"A = P(1 + i)ⁿ"}},{"l":{"af":"Huurkoop","en":"Hire purchase"},"r":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente op die balans ná die deposito","en":"Simple interest on the balance after the deposit"}},{"l":{"af":"Inflasie","en":"Inflation"},"r":{"af":"Die algemene styging in pryse oor tyd","en":"The general rise in prices over time"}},{"l":{"af":"Wisselkoers","en":"Exchange rate"},"r":{"af":"Die waarde van een geldeenheid in 'n ander","en":"The value of one currency in another"}}],"explain":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente: rente net op P (lineêr). Saamgestelde rente: rente op rente (eksponensieel). Huurkoop gebruik enkelvoudige rente op die uitstaande bedrag. Inflasie is prysstyging en word met saamgestelde groei bereken. 'n Wisselkoers skakel tussen geldeenhede om.","en":"Simple interest: interest only on P (linear). Compound interest: interest on interest (exponential). Hire purchase uses simple interest on the outstanding amount. Inflation is rising prices and is calculated with compound growth. An exchange rate converts between currencies."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Belegging verdien 12% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel, vir 3 jaar. Watter waardes van i en n gebruik jy in A = P(1 + i)ⁿ?","en":"An investment earns 12% p.a., compounded monthly, for 3 years. Which values of i and n do you use in A = P(1 + i)ⁿ?"},"options":[{"af":"i = 0,12 en n = 3","en":"i = 0.12 and n = 3"},{"af":"i = 0,01 en n = 36","en":"i = 0.01 and n = 36"},{"af":"i = 0,12 en n = 36","en":"i = 0.12 and n = 36"},{"af":"i = 0,01 en n = 3","en":"i = 0.01 and n = 3"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Maandeliks: i = 0,12 ÷ 12 = 0,01 per maand en n = 3 × 12 = 36 maande. Jy moet albei aanpas; as jy net een verander, is die antwoord verkeerd.","en":"Monthly: i = 0.12 ÷ 12 = 0.01 per month and n = 3 × 12 = 36 months. You must adjust both; if you change only one, the answer is wrong."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sipho belê R4 000 teen 6% p.j. enkelvoudige rente vir 3 jaar. Die opgehoopte bedrag is R___.","en":"Sipho invests R4 000 at 6% p.a. simple interest for 3 years. The accumulated amount is R___."},"answers":{"af":["4 720,00","R4 720,00","R 4 720,00","4 720","R4 720","R 4 720","4720,00","R4720,00","R 4720,00","4720","R4720","R 4720","4 720.00","R4 720.00","R 4 720.00","4720.00","R4720.00","R 4720.00"],"en":["4 720,00","R4 720,00","R 4 720,00","4 720","R4 720","R 4 720","4720,00","R4720,00","R 4720,00","4720","R4720","R 4720","4 720.00","R4 720.00","R 4 720.00","4720.00","R4720.00","R 4720.00"]},"explain":{"af":"A = P(1 + in) = 4 000(1 + 0,06 × 3) = 4 000 × 1,18 = R4 720,00.","en":"A = P(1 + in) = 4 000(1 + 0.06 × 3) = 4 000 × 1.18 = R4 720.00."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"R5 000 word vir 4 jaar belê teen 8% p.j., jaarliks saamgestel. Wat is die opgehoopte bedrag?","en":"R5 000 is invested for 4 years at 8% p.a., compounded annually. What is the accumulated amount?"},"options":[{"af":"R6 600,00","en":"R6 600.00"},{"af":"R1 802,44","en":"R1 802.44"},{"af":"R21 600,00","en":"R21 600.00"},{"af":"R6 802,44","en":"R6 802.44"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"A = 5 000(1,08)⁴ = R6 802,44. R6 600,00 is enkelvoudige rente, R1 802,44 is net die rente, en R21 600,00 kom van 5 000 × 1,08 × 4 (maal 4 in plaas van tot die mag 4).","en":"A = 5 000(1.08)⁴ = R6 802.44. R6 600.00 is simple interest, R1 802.44 is only the interest, and R21 600.00 comes from 5 000 × 1.08 × 4 (times 4 instead of to the power 4)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die wisselkoers verander van $1 = R17,80 na $1 = R18,90. Dit beteken die rand het verswak, en ingevoerde goedere soos selfone word duurder in rand.","en":"The exchange rate changes from $1 = R17.80 to $1 = R18.90. This means the rand has weakened, and imported goods such as cellphones become more expensive in rand."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jy moet nou meer rand (R18,90 in plaas van R17,80) vir een dollar betaal, so die rand is swakker en alles wat in dollar gekoop word, kos meer rand.","en":"True. You now have to pay more rand (R18.90 instead of R17.80) for one dollar, so the rand is weaker and everything bought in dollars costs more rand."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die wisselkoers is $1 = R18,40. Hoeveel dollar kry jy vir R5 000? Rond af tot 2 desimale plekke: $___","en":"The exchange rate is $1 = R18.40. How many dollars do you get for R5 000? Round to 2 decimal places: $___"},"answers":{"af":["271,74","$271,74","$ 271,74","271.74","$271.74","$ 271.74"],"en":["271,74","$271,74","$ 271,74","271.74","$271.74","$ 271.74"]},"explain":{"af":"Rand → dollar: deel deur die koers. 5 000 ÷ 18,40 = $271,74. Gesonde-verstand-toets: die getal dollar moet kleiner as die getal rand wees.","en":"Rand → dollar: divide by the rate. 5 000 ÷ 18.40 = $271.74. Common-sense check: the number of dollars must be smaller than the number of rand."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Brood kos vandag R20,00. As die inflasiekoers 6% p.j. bly, wat sal 'n brood oor 5 jaar kos?","en":"A loaf of bread costs R20.00 today. If the inflation rate stays at 6% p.a., what will a loaf cost in 5 years?"},"options":[{"af":"R26,76","en":"R26.76"},{"af":"R26,00","en":"R26.00"},{"af":"R14,68","en":"R14.68"},{"af":"R6,76","en":"R6.76"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Inflasie is saamgestelde groei: A = 20(1,06)⁵ = R26,76. R26,00 is enkelvoudige groei, R14,68 kom van (1 − 0,06) en R6,76 is net die prysstyging.","en":"Inflation is compound growth: A = 20(1.06)⁵ = R26.76. R26.00 is simple growth, R14.68 comes from (1 − 0.06) and R6.76 is only the price increase."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"R10 000 word belê teen 9% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel. Wat is die waarde van die belegging ná 3 jaar?","en":"R10 000 is invested at 9% p.a., compounded monthly. What is the value of the investment after 3 years?"},"options":[{"af":"R12 950,29","en":"R12 950.29"},{"af":"R10 226,69","en":"R10 226.69"},{"af":"R13 086,45","en":"R13 086.45"},{"af":"R222 512,25","en":"R222 512.25"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"i = 0,09 ÷ 12 = 0,0075 en n = 3 × 12 = 36: A = 10 000(1,0075)³⁶ = R13 086,45. R12 950,29 is jaarliks saamgestel, R10 226,69 gebruik n = 3 en R222 512,25 gebruik i = 0,09 met n = 36.","en":"i = 0.09 ÷ 12 = 0.0075 and n = 3 × 12 = 36: A = 10 000(1.0075)³⁶ = R13 086.45. R12 950.29 is compounded annually, R10 226.69 uses n = 3 and R222 512.25 uses i = 0.09 with n = 36."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Televisie het 'n kontantprys van R8 400. Lindiwe koop dit op huurkoop: sy betaal 10% deposito en die balans oor 2 jaar teen 16% p.j. enkelvoudige rente. Daar is ook R25 versekering per maand. Wat is haar totale maandelikse betaling? R___","en":"A television has a cash price of R8 400. Lindiwe buys it on hire purchase: she pays a 10% deposit and the balance over 2 years at 16% p.a. simple interest. There is also R25 insurance per month. What is her total monthly payment? R___"},"answers":{"af":["440,80","R440,80","R 440,80","440,8","R440,8","R 440,8","440.80","R440.80","R 440.80","440.8","R440.8","R 440.8"],"en":["440,80","R440,80","R 440,80","440,8","R440,8","R 440,8","440.80","R440.80","R 440.80","440.8","R440.8","R 440.8"]},"explain":{"af":"Deposito = 0,1 × 8 400 = R840,00. Balans = R7 560,00. A = 7 560(1 + 0,16 × 2) = R9 979,20. Paaiement = 9 979,20 ÷ 24 = R415,80. Plus versekering: 415,80 + 25 = R440,80.","en":"Deposit = 0.1 × 8 400 = R840.00. Balance = R7 560.00. A = 7 560(1 + 0.16 × 2) = R9 979.20. Instalment = 9 979.20 ÷ 24 = R415.80. Plus insurance: 415.80 + 25 = R440.80."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gestel 'n dorp in Madibeng het 120 000 inwoners en die bevolking groei teen 2,4% p.j. Wat sal die bevolking ná 6 jaar wees (afgerond tot 'n heelgetal)?","en":"Suppose a town in Madibeng has 120 000 inhabitants and the population grows at 2.4% p.a. What will the population be after 6 years (rounded to a whole number)?"},"options":[{"af":"137 280","en":"137 280"},{"af":"138 351","en":"138 351"},{"af":"436 226","en":"436 226"},{"af":"737 280","en":"737 280"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Bevolkingsgroei is saamgesteld: A = 120 000(1,024)⁶ = 138 350,58 ≈ 138 351. 137 280 is enkelvoudige groei, 436 226 gebruik i = 0,24 en 737 280 vermenigvuldig met 6 in plaas van tot die mag 6.","en":"Population growth is compound: A = 120 000(1.024)⁶ = 138 350.58 ≈ 138 351. 137 280 is simple growth, 436 226 uses i = 0.24 and 737 280 multiplies by 6 instead of raising to the power 6."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Anika wil oor 4 jaar R20 000 hê vir haar eerste motor. Hoeveel moet sy nou belê teen 7% p.j., jaarliks saamgestel? Rond af tot 2 desimale plekke: R___","en":"Anika wants R20 000 in 4 years for her first car. How much must she invest now at 7% p.a., compounded annually? Round to 2 decimal places: R___"},"answers":{"af":["15 257,90","R15 257,90","R 15 257,90","15 257,9","R15 257,9","R 15 257,9","15257,90","R15257,90","R 15257,90","15257,9","R15257,9","R 15257,9","15 257.90","R15 257.90","R 15 257.90","15 257.9","R15 257.9","R 15 257.9","15257.90","R15257.90","R 15257.90","15257.9","R15257.9","R 15257.9"],"en":["15 257,90","R15 257,90","R 15 257,90","15 257,9","R15 257,9","R 15 257,9","15257,90","R15257,90","R 15257,90","15257,9","R15257,9","R 15257,9","15 257.90","R15 257.90","R 15 257.90","15 257.9","R15 257.9","R 15 257.9","15257.90","R15257.90","R 15257.90","15257.9","R15257.9","R 15257.9"]},"explain":{"af":"Hier is A = 20 000 gegee en jy soek P. P = A ÷ (1 + i)ⁿ = 20 000 ÷ (1,07)⁴ = R15 257,90. Kontroleer: 15 257,90 × (1,07)⁴ ≈ 20 000.","en":"Here A = 20 000 is given and you need P. P = A ÷ (1 + i)ⁿ = 20 000 ÷ (1.07)⁴ = R15 257.90. Check: 15 257.90 × (1.07)⁴ ≈ 20 000."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter wil R12 000 vir 5 jaar belê. Bank A bied 10% p.j. enkelvoudige rente. Bank B bied 9% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel. Watter bank gee die meeste geld ná 5 jaar?","en":"Pieter wants to invest R12 000 for 5 years. Bank A offers 10% p.a. simple interest. Bank B offers 9% p.a., compounded monthly. Which bank gives the most money after 5 years?"},"options":[{"af":"Bank B: R18 788,17 teenoor Bank A se R18 000,00","en":"Bank B: R18 788.17 against Bank A's R18 000.00"},{"af":"Bank A, want 10% is 'n hoër koers as 9%","en":"Bank A, because 10% is a higher rate than 9%"},{"af":"Bank B: R18 463,49 teenoor Bank A se R18 000,00","en":"Bank B: R18 463.49 against Bank A's R18 000.00"},{"af":"Bank A: R18 000,00 teenoor Bank B se R17 400,00","en":"Bank A: R18 000.00 against Bank B's R17 400.00"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Bank A: 12 000(1 + 0,10 × 5) = R18 000,00. Bank B: 12 000(1 + 0,09 ÷ 12)⁶⁰ = R18 788,17. Bank B gee R788,17 meer, al is sy koers laer, want maandelikse saamstelling gee rente op rente. R18 463,49 sou jaarlikse saamstelling wees en R17 400,00 enkelvoudige rente teen 9%.","en":"Bank A: 12 000(1 + 0.10 × 5) = R18 000.00. Bank B: 12 000(1 + 0.09 ÷ 12)⁶⁰ = R18 788.17. Bank B gives R788.17 more, even though its rate is lower, because monthly compounding gives interest on interest. R18 463.49 would be annual compounding and R17 400.00 simple interest at 9%."}}]},{"id":"w10-t3-statistiek","title":{"af":"Statistiek","en":"Statistics"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die gemiddelde, mediaan, modus, kwartiele, IKO en persentiele kan bereken, 'n vyfgetalopsomming en mond-en-snor-diagram kan opstel, en gegroepeerde data kan ontleed.","en":"You will be able to calculate the mean, median, mode, quartiles, IQR and percentiles, set up a five-number summary and box-and-whisker plot, and analyse grouped data."},"summary":{"af":"## Sentrale neiging: gemiddelde, mediaan en modus\n\n**Ongegroepeerde data** is 'n lys van die werklike waardes. Die drie maatstawwe van sentrale neiging beskryf die \"tipiese\" waarde:\n\n| Maatstaf | Hoe om dit te kry |\n|---|---|\n| **Gemiddelde** (x̄) | x̄ = [[som van die waardes/aantal waardes]] = [[Σx/n]] |\n| **Mediaan** | Rangskik die data eers van klein na groot. Die mediaan is die middelste waarde, by posisie [[n + 1/2]]. As n ewe is, is dit die gemiddelde van die twee middelste waardes. |\n| **Modus** | Die waarde wat die meeste voorkom. Data kan twee modusse hê (bimodaal) of geen modus nie. |\n\nAs die gemiddelde gegee is, kry jy die som so: **som = x̄ × n**. Bv. vyf getalle met 'n gemiddelde van 14 het 'n som van 70. So bereken jy 'n ontbrekende waarde of 'n nuwe gemiddelde.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die middelste getal in die lys te kies sonder om die data eers te rangskik.\n\n### Watter maatstaf pas die beste?\n\n- **Gemiddelde:** gebruik al die waardes, maar word maklik deur uitskieters getrek.\n- **Mediaan:** die beste keuse as daar uitskieters is of as die data skeef is, bv. huispryse en salarisse.\n- **Modus:** die enigste keuse vir kategoriese data, bv. die gewildste skoengrootte.\n\n## Verspreiding: omvang, kwartiele en persentiele\n\n- **Omvang** = grootste waarde − kleinste waarde.\n- **Kwartiele** verdeel die gerangskikte data in vier dele met ewe veel waardes. Q_{2} is die mediaan.\n- **Q_{1}** (onderste kwartiel) is die mediaan van die onderste helfte van die data, en **Q_{3}** (boonste kwartiel) is die mediaan van die boonste helfte.\n- As n onewe is, laat jy die mediaan self uit wanneer jy die twee helftes vorm.\n- **Interkwartielomvang (IKO)** = Q_{3} − Q_{1}. Dit is die omvang van die middelste 50% van die data, en uitskieters raak dit nie.\n- **Semi-interkwartielomvang** = [[1/2]](Q_{3} − Q_{1}).\n- **Persentiele** verdeel die data in 100 dele. Die p-de persentiel is die waarde waaronder ongeveer p% van die data lê. Q_{1} is die 25ste, die mediaan die 50ste en Q_{3} die 75ste persentiel.\n\n> **Wenk:** As jou punt op die 90ste persentiel is, het ongeveer 90% van die groep laer as jy gekry. Dit is NIE 'n punt van 90% nie!\n\n## Vyfgetalopsomming en mond-en-snor-diagram\n\nDie **vyfgetalopsomming** is: minimum; Q_{1}; mediaan; Q_{3}; maksimum.\n\nOm 'n **mond-en-snor-diagram** te teken:\n\n1. Teken 'n getallelyn met 'n eweredige skaal van die minimum tot die maksimum.\n2. Teken 'n reghoek (die \"mond\") van Q_{1} tot Q_{3}.\n3. Trek 'n lyn dwarsdeur die mond by die mediaan.\n4. Trek die \"snorre\": van Q_{1} tot by die minimum en van Q_{3} tot by die maksimum.\n\nElke snor en elke helfte van die mond bevat ongeveer 25% van die data. 'n Lang snor of 'n breë deel van die mond wys dat die data daar meer uitgesprei is; 'n smal mond wys dat die middelste 50% dig bymekaar lê.\n\n## Uitskieters\n\n'n **Uitskieter** is 'n waarde wat baie groter of baie kleiner as die res van die data is, bv. 'n tikfout of een baie hoë salaris. Dit trek die gemiddelde en die omvang sterk, maar die mediaan en die IKO skaars. Op 'n mond-en-snor-diagram sien jy dit as 'n baie lang snor. (In graad 11 leer jy 'n formele reël vir uitskieters.)\n\n## Gegroepeerde data\n\nAs data in **klasintervalle** soos 10 ≤ x < 20 gegee word, ken jy nie die presiese waardes nie, dus **beraam** jy.\n\n- **Modale klas:** die klas met die grootste frekwensie.\n- **Klas wat die mediaan bevat:** bereken die posisie [[n + 1/2]], tel die frekwensies van bo af op (kumulatiewe frekwensie) en kyk in watter klas daardie posisie val.\n- **Beraamde gemiddelde:** gebruik die **middelpunt** van elke klas as die waarde vir al die data in daardie klas.\n\n1. Middelpunt = [[ondergrens + bogrens/2]], bv. 10 ≤ x < 20 → 15.\n2. Vermenigvuldig elke middelpunt met sy frekwensie: f × x.\n3. Beraamde gemiddelde = [[Σ(f × x)/Σf]] = [[som van al die f × x/totale frekwensie]].\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om deur die aantal klasse te deel in plaas van deur die totale frekwensie, of om net die middelpunte op te tel sonder om met f te vermenigvuldig.\n\n## Effek van veranderinge op die data\n\n- Tel 'n getal k by elke waarde: die gemiddelde, mediaan, modus en kwartiele styg almal met k, maar die omvang en IKO bly dieselfde, want die hele datastel skuif net op.\n- Vermenigvuldig elke waarde met 'n positiewe getal k: al die maatstawwe, ook die omvang en IKO, word met k vermenigvuldig.","en":"## Central tendency: mean, median and mode\n\n**Ungrouped data** is a list of the actual values. The three measures of central tendency describe the \"typical\" value:\n\n| Measure | How to find it |\n|---|---|\n| **Mean** (x̄) | x̄ = [[sum of the values/number of values]] = [[Σx/n]] |\n| **Median** | First arrange the data from smallest to largest. The median is the middle value, at position [[n + 1/2]]. If n is even, it is the mean of the two middle values. |\n| **Mode** | The value that occurs most often. Data can have two modes (bimodal) or no mode. |\n\nIf the mean is given, you find the sum like this: **sum = x̄ × n**. E.g. five numbers with a mean of 14 have a sum of 70. This is how you calculate a missing value or a new mean.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Choosing the middle number in the list without first arranging the data in order.\n\n### Which measure fits best?\n\n- **Mean:** uses all the values, but is easily pulled by outliers.\n- **Median:** the best choice if there are outliers or the data is skewed, e.g. house prices and salaries.\n- **Mode:** the only choice for categorical data, e.g. the most popular shoe size.\n\n## Spread: range, quartiles and percentiles\n\n- **Range** = largest value − smallest value.\n- **Quartiles** divide the ordered data into four parts with equally many values. Q_{2} is the median.\n- **Q_{1}** (lower quartile) is the median of the lower half of the data, and **Q_{3}** (upper quartile) is the median of the upper half.\n- If n is odd, leave out the median itself when you form the two halves.\n- **Interquartile range (IQR)** = Q_{3} − Q_{1}. It is the range of the middle 50% of the data, and outliers do not affect it.\n- **Semi-interquartile range** = [[1/2]](Q_{3} − Q_{1}).\n- **Percentiles** divide the data into 100 parts. The p-th percentile is the value below which about p% of the data lies. Q_{1} is the 25th, the median the 50th and Q_{3} the 75th percentile.\n\n> **Tip:** If your mark is at the 90th percentile, about 90% of the group scored lower than you. It is NOT a mark of 90%!\n\n## Five-number summary and box-and-whisker plot\n\nThe **five-number summary** is: minimum; Q_{1}; median; Q_{3}; maximum.\n\nTo draw a **box-and-whisker plot**:\n\n1. Draw a number line with an even scale from the minimum to the maximum.\n2. Draw a rectangle (the \"box\") from Q_{1} to Q_{3}.\n3. Draw a line across the box at the median.\n4. Draw the \"whiskers\": from Q_{1} to the minimum and from Q_{3} to the maximum.\n\nEach whisker and each half of the box contains about 25% of the data. A long whisker or a wide part of the box shows that the data is more spread out there; a narrow box shows that the middle 50% lies close together.\n\n## Outliers\n\nAn **outlier** is a value that is much bigger or much smaller than the rest of the data, e.g. a typing error or one very high salary. It pulls the mean and the range strongly, but hardly affects the median and the IQR. On a box-and-whisker plot you see it as a very long whisker. (In Grade 11 you learn a formal rule for outliers.)\n\n## Grouped data\n\nIf data is given in **class intervals** such as 10 ≤ x < 20, you do not know the exact values, so you **estimate**.\n\n- **Modal class:** the class with the highest frequency.\n- **Class containing the median:** work out the position [[n + 1/2]], add up the frequencies from the top (cumulative frequency) and see in which class that position falls.\n- **Estimated mean:** use the **midpoint** of each class as the value for all the data in that class.\n\n1. Midpoint = [[lower limit + upper limit/2]], e.g. 10 ≤ x < 20 → 15.\n2. Multiply each midpoint by its frequency: f × x.\n3. Estimated mean = [[Σ(f × x)/Σf]] = [[sum of all the f × x/total frequency]].\n\n> **Common mistake:** Dividing by the number of classes instead of by the total frequency, or just adding the midpoints without multiplying by f.\n\n## Effect of changes to the data\n\n- Add a number k to every value: the mean, median, mode and quartiles all increase by k, but the range and IQR stay the same, because the whole data set just shifts up.\n- Multiply every value by a positive number k: all the measures, including the range and IQR, are multiplied by k."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Gemiddelde (x̄)","en":"Mean (x̄)"},"def":{"af":"Die som van al die waardes gedeel deur die aantal waardes.","en":"The sum of all the values divided by the number of values."}},{"term":{"af":"Mediaan","en":"Median"},"def":{"af":"Die middelste waarde wanneer die data van klein na groot gerangskik is (Q₂, die 50ste persentiel).","en":"The middle value when the data is arranged from smallest to largest (Q₂, the 50th percentile)."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwartiele","en":"Quartiles"},"def":{"af":"Die drie waardes Q₁, Q₂ en Q₃ wat gerangskikte data in vier dele met ewe veel waardes verdeel.","en":"The three values Q₁, Q₂ and Q₃ that divide ordered data into four parts with equally many values."}},{"term":{"af":"Interkwartielomvang (IKO)","en":"Interquartile range (IQR)"},"def":{"af":"Q₃ − Q₁: die omvang van die middelste 50% van die data. Die semi-interkwartielomvang is die helfte daarvan.","en":"Q₃ − Q₁: the range of the middle 50% of the data. The semi-interquartile range is half of it."}},{"term":{"af":"Persentiel","en":"Percentile"},"def":{"af":"Die p-de persentiel is die waarde waaronder ongeveer p% van die data lê.","en":"The p-th percentile is the value below which about p% of the data lies."}},{"term":{"af":"Vyfgetalopsomming","en":"Five-number summary"},"def":{"af":"Minimum; Q₁; mediaan; Q₃; maksimum.","en":"Minimum; Q₁; median; Q₃; maximum."}},{"term":{"af":"Mond-en-snor-diagram","en":"Box-and-whisker plot"},"def":{"af":"'n Diagram van die vyfgetalopsomming: 'n mond van Q₁ tot Q₃ met 'n lyn by die mediaan, en snorre tot by die minimum en maksimum.","en":"A diagram of the five-number summary: a box from Q₁ to Q₃ with a line at the median, and whiskers to the minimum and maximum."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitskieter","en":"Outlier"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde wat baie groter of baie kleiner as die res van die data is; dit beïnvloed die gemiddelde en omvang sterk.","en":"A value that is much bigger or much smaller than the rest of the data; it strongly affects the mean and range."}},{"term":{"af":"Modale klas","en":"Modal class"},"def":{"af":"By gegroepeerde data: die klasinterval met die grootste frekwensie.","en":"For grouped data: the class interval with the highest frequency."}},{"term":{"af":"Beraamde gemiddelde","en":"Estimated mean"},"def":{"af":"Die gemiddelde van gegroepeerde data, bereken met die klasmiddelpunte: Σ(f × x) ÷ Σf.","en":"The mean of grouped data, calculated with the class midpoints: Σ(f × x) ÷ Σf."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gemiddelde, mediaan, modus en omvang","en":"Mean, median, mode and range"},"problem":{"af":"'n Skool in Brits se o.16-rugbyspan het in 10 wedstryde die volgende punte aangeteken: 24; 17; 31; 12; 24; 38; 9; 24; 15; 26. Bereken die gemiddelde, mediaan, modus en omvang.","en":"A Brits school's U16 rugby team scored the following points in 10 matches: 24, 17, 31, 12, 24, 38, 9, 24, 15, 26. Calculate the mean, median, mode and range."},"steps":[{"af":"Gemiddelde: som = 220 en n = 10, dus x̄ = [[220/10]] = 22 punte.","en":"Mean: sum = 220 and n = 10, so x̄ = [[220/10]] = 22 points."},{"af":"Rangskik eers: 9; 12; 15; 17; 24; 24; 24; 26; 31; 38.","en":"First arrange in order: 9, 12, 15, 17, 24, 24, 24, 26, 31, 38."},{"af":"Mediaan: n = 10 is ewe, dus lê die mediaan tussen die 5de en 6de waardes: [[24 + 24/2]] = 24 punte.","en":"Median: n = 10 is even, so the median lies between the 5th and 6th values: [[24 + 24/2]] = 24 points."},{"af":"Modus: 24 kom drie keer voor, meer as enige ander waarde, dus is die modus 24 punte.","en":"Mode: 24 occurs three times, more than any other value, so the mode is 24 points."},{"af":"Omvang = 38 − 9 = 29 punte.","en":"Range = 38 − 9 = 29 points."}],"answer":{"af":"x̄ = 22; mediaan = 24; modus = 24; omvang = 29","en":"x̄ = 22; median = 24; mode = 24; range = 29"}},{"title":{"af":"Kwartiele, IKO en die vyfgetalopsomming","en":"Quartiles, IQR and the five-number summary"},"problem":{"af":"Die aantal minute wat 15 leerders op 'n Saterdag op sosiale media spandeer, is: 45; 30; 120; 20; 60; 35; 15; 55; 30; 85; 40; 60; 25; 70; 50. (a) Gee die vyfgetalopsomming. (b) Bereken die IKO en die semi-interkwartielomvang. (c) Beskryf die mond-en-snor-diagram en lewer kommentaar.","en":"The number of minutes 15 learners spend on social media on a Saturday is: 45, 30, 120, 20, 60, 35, 15, 55, 30, 85, 40, 60, 25, 70, 50. (a) Give the five-number summary. (b) Calculate the IQR and the semi-interquartile range. (c) Describe the box-and-whisker plot and comment."},"steps":[{"af":"Rangskik: 15; 20; 25; 30; 30; 35; 40; 45; 50; 55; 60; 60; 70; 85; 120. n = 15.","en":"Arrange in order: 15, 20, 25, 30, 30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 55, 60, 60, 70, 85, 120. n = 15."},{"af":"Mediaan by posisie [[15 + 1/2]] = 8: die 8ste waarde is 45 min.","en":"Median at position [[15 + 1/2]] = 8: the 8th value is 45 min."},{"af":"Onderste helfte (die 7 waardes vóór die mediaan): 15; 20; 25; 30; 30; 35; 40, dus Q_{1} = 30. Boonste helfte: 50; 55; 60; 60; 70; 85; 120, dus Q_{3} = 60.","en":"Lower half (the 7 values before the median): 15, 20, 25, 30, 30, 35, 40, so Q_{1} = 30. Upper half: 50, 55, 60, 60, 70, 85, 120, so Q_{3} = 60."},{"af":"(a) Vyfgetalopsomming: minimum 15; Q_{1} = 30; mediaan 45; Q_{3} = 60; maksimum 120.","en":"(a) Five-number summary: minimum 15; Q_{1} = 30; median 45; Q_{3} = 60; maximum 120."},{"af":"(b) IKO = Q_{3} − Q_{1} = 60 − 30 = 30 min; semi-interkwartielomvang = [[30/2]] = 15 min.","en":"(b) IQR = Q_{3} − Q_{1} = 60 − 30 = 30 min; semi-interquartile range = [[30/2]] = 15 min."},{"af":"(c) Die mond strek van 30 tot 60 met 'n lyn by 45; die linkersnor gaan tot 15 en die regtersnor tot 120. Die regtersnor (60 tot 120) is baie langer as die linkersnor (15 tot 30), dus lyk 120 na 'n uitskieter.","en":"(c) The box runs from 30 to 60 with a line at 45; the left whisker goes to 15 and the right whisker to 120. The right whisker (60 to 120) is much longer than the left whisker (15 to 30), so 120 looks like an outlier."}],"answer":{"af":"Vyfgetalopsomming: 15; 30; 45; 60; 120. IKO = 30 min; semi-IKO = 15 min.","en":"Five-number summary: 15; 30; 45; 60; 120. IQR = 30 min; semi-IQR = 15 min."}},{"title":{"af":"Gegroepeerde data","en":"Grouped data"},"problem":{"af":"Die afstand (in km) wat 40 werkers van 'n myn naby Brits elke dag werk toe reis: 0 ≤ x < 10: 6 werkers; 10 ≤ x < 20: 12; 20 ≤ x < 30: 11; 30 ≤ x < 40: 8; 40 ≤ x < 50: 3. Bepaal (a) die modale klas, (b) die klas wat die mediaan bevat en (c) die beraamde gemiddelde afstand.","en":"The distance (in km) that 40 workers at a mine near Brits travel to work each day: 0 ≤ x < 10: 6 workers; 10 ≤ x < 20: 12; 20 ≤ x < 30: 11; 30 ≤ x < 40: 8; 40 ≤ x < 50: 3. Determine (a) the modal class, (b) the class containing the median and (c) the estimated mean distance."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die grootste frekwensie is 12, dus is die modale klas 10 ≤ x < 20.","en":"(a) The highest frequency is 12, so the modal class is 10 ≤ x < 20."},{"af":"(b) Mediaan by posisie [[40 + 1/2]] = 20,5. Kumulatiewe frekwensies: 6; 18; 29; 37; 40. Die 20ste en 21ste waardes lê in 20 ≤ x < 30.","en":"(b) Median at position [[40 + 1/2]] = 20.5. Cumulative frequencies: 6, 18, 29, 37, 40. The 20th and 21st values lie in 20 ≤ x < 30."},{"af":"(c) Middelpunte: 5; 15; 25; 35; 45.","en":"(c) Midpoints: 5, 15, 25, 35, 45."},{"af":"f × x: 6 × 5 = 30; 12 × 15 = 180; 11 × 25 = 275; 8 × 35 = 280; 3 × 45 = 135. Σ(f × x) = 900.","en":"f × x: 6 × 5 = 30; 12 × 15 = 180; 11 × 25 = 275; 8 × 35 = 280; 3 × 45 = 135. Σ(f × x) = 900."},{"af":"Beraamde gemiddelde = [[900/40]] = 22,5 km. Dit is 'n beraming, want ons gebruik middelpunte en nie die werklike afstande nie.","en":"Estimated mean = [[900/40]] = 22.5 km. It is an estimate, because we use midpoints and not the actual distances."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 10 ≤ x < 20  (b) 20 ≤ x < 30  (c) 22,5 km","en":"(a) 10 ≤ x < 20  (b) 20 ≤ x < 30  (c) 22.5 km"}},{"title":{"af":"'n Uitskieter en die beste maatstaf","en":"An outlier and the best measure"},"problem":{"af":"'n Klein besigheid in Brits het ses werknemers. Hulle maandelikse salarisse is R8 500; R9 200; R9 200; R10 400; R11 700 en die eienaar s'n is R65 000. (a) Bereken die gemiddelde en die mediaan. (b) Watter maatstaf beskryf die tipiese salaris die beste? Verduidelik.","en":"A small business in Brits has six employees. Their monthly salaries are R8 500, R9 200, R9 200, R10 400, R11 700 and the owner's is R65 000. (a) Calculate the mean and the median. (b) Which measure describes the typical salary best? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Som = 8 500 + 9 200 + 9 200 + 10 400 + 11 700 + 65 000 = R114 000","en":"Sum = 8 500 + 9 200 + 9 200 + 10 400 + 11 700 + 65 000 = R114 000"},{"af":"Gemiddelde = [[114 000/6]] = R19 000","en":"Mean = [[114 000/6]] = R19 000"},{"af":"Die data is reeds gerangskik en n = 6 is ewe, dus is die mediaan die gemiddelde van die 3de en 4de waardes: [[9 200 + 10 400/2]] = R9 800.","en":"The data is already in order and n = 6 is even, so the median is the mean of the 3rd and 4th values: [[9 200 + 10 400/2]] = R9 800."},{"af":"R65 000 is 'n uitskieter. Dit trek die gemiddelde op tot R19 000, meer as wat 5 van die 6 werknemers verdien.","en":"R65 000 is an outlier. It pulls the mean up to R19 000, more than 5 of the 6 employees earn."},{"af":"(b) Die mediaan (R9 800) beskryf die tipiese salaris die beste, want 'n uitskieter beïnvloed die mediaan skaars.","en":"(b) The median (R9 800) describes the typical salary best, because an outlier hardly affects the median."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Gemiddelde = R19 000; mediaan = R9 800  (b) die mediaan","en":"(a) Mean = R19 000; median = R9 800  (b) the median"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter maatstaf is die middelste waarde wanneer die data van klein na groot gerangskik is?","en":"Which measure is the middle value when the data is arranged from smallest to largest?"},"options":[{"af":"Die gemiddelde","en":"The mean"},{"af":"Die modus","en":"The mode"},{"af":"Die mediaan","en":"The median"},{"af":"Die omvang","en":"The range"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die mediaan is die middelste waarde van gerangskikte data. Die gemiddelde is die som ÷ n, die modus die waarde wat die meeste voorkom en die omvang is grootste − kleinste.","en":"The median is the middle value of ordered data. The mean is the sum ÷ n, the mode is the value that occurs most often and the range is largest − smallest."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Uitskieter (baie groot of baie klein waarde) beïnvloed die gemiddelde baie meer as die mediaan.","en":"An outlier (a very large or very small value) affects the mean much more than the median."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die gemiddelde gebruik die grootte van elke waarde, so een uiterste waarde trek dit weg. Die mediaan hang net af van die middelste posisie en verander skaars.","en":"True. The mean uses the size of every value, so one extreme value pulls it away. The median only depends on the middle position and hardly changes."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke maatstaf by die regte beskrywing of formule.","en":"Match each measure to the correct description or formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Omvang","en":"Range"},"r":{"af":"Grootste waarde − kleinste waarde","en":"Largest value − smallest value"}},{"l":{"af":"Interkwartielomvang","en":"Interquartile range"},"r":{"af":"Q₃ − Q₁","en":"Q₃ − Q₁"}},{"l":{"af":"Semi-interkwartielomvang","en":"Semi-interquartile range"},"r":{"af":"½(Q₃ − Q₁)","en":"½(Q₃ − Q₁)"}},{"l":{"af":"75ste persentiel","en":"75th percentile"},"r":{"af":"Q₃, die boonste kwartiel","en":"Q₃, the upper quartile"}},{"l":{"af":"Modus","en":"Mode"},"r":{"af":"Die waarde wat die meeste voorkom","en":"The value that occurs most often"}}],"explain":{"af":"Omvang = maks − min. IKO = Q₃ − Q₁ (middelste 50%). Die semi-IKO is die helfte van die IKO. Q₃ is die 75ste persentiel. Die modus is die waarde wat die meeste voorkom.","en":"Range = max − min. IQR = Q₃ − Q₁ (middle 50%). The semi-IQR is half of the IQR. Q₃ is the 75th percentile. The mode is the value that occurs most often."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken die gemiddelde van hierdie data: 7; 12; 9; 15; 12; 8; 14. x̄ = ___","en":"Calculate the mean of this data: 7, 12, 9, 15, 12, 8, 14. x̄ = ___"},"answers":{"af":["11","11,0","11.0","x̄ = 11","x̄=11"],"en":["11","11.0","11,0","x̄ = 11","x̄=11"]},"explain":{"af":"Som = 7 + 12 + 9 + 15 + 12 + 8 + 14 = 77 en n = 7, dus x̄ = 77 ÷ 7 = 11.","en":"Sum = 7 + 12 + 9 + 15 + 12 + 8 + 14 = 77 and n = 7, so x̄ = 77 ÷ 7 = 11."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die mediaan van 14; 9; 21; 17; 11; 25?","en":"What is the median of 14, 9, 21, 17, 11, 25?"},"options":[{"af":"19","en":"19"},{"af":"15,5","en":"15.5"},{"af":"16,17","en":"16.17"},{"af":"17","en":"17"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rangskik eers: 9; 11; 14; 17; 21; 25. n = 6 is ewe, dus mediaan = (14 + 17) ÷ 2 = 15,5. 19 kom van die middelste twee getalle in die ongerangskikte lys, 16,17 is die gemiddelde en 17 is net een van die twee middelste waardes.","en":"First arrange in order: 9, 11, 14, 17, 21, 25. n = 6 is even, so median = (14 + 17) ÷ 2 = 15.5. 19 comes from the middle two numbers in the unordered list, 16.17 is the mean and 17 is only one of the two middle values."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n graad met 200 leerders lê Lerato se wiskundepunt op die 85ste persentiel. Ongeveer hoeveel leerders het 'n laer punt as sy gekry? ___","en":"In a grade of 200 learners, Lerato's maths mark is at the 85th percentile. About how many learners got a lower mark than she did? ___"},"answers":{"af":["170","170 leerders"],"en":["170","170 learners"]},"explain":{"af":"Die 85ste persentiel beteken ongeveer 85% van die data lê daaronder: 0,85 × 200 = 170 leerders. Dit sê niks oor haar persentasie nie.","en":"The 85th percentile means about 85% of the data lies below it: 0.85 × 200 = 170 learners. It says nothing about her percentage."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy 5 by elke waarde in 'n datastel tel, neem die omvang ook met 5 toe.","en":"If you add 5 to every value in a data set, the range also increases by 5."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die grootste én kleinste waardes styg albei met 5, so die verskil (omvang) bly dieselfde. Die gemiddelde, mediaan en kwartiele styg wel met 5.","en":"False. The largest and the smallest values both increase by 5, so the difference (range) stays the same. The mean, median and quartiles do increase by 5."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bepaal die interkwartielomvang (IKO) van hierdie data: 12; 18; 3; 20; 8; 13; 22; 5; 18; 10; 8.","en":"Determine the interquartile range (IQR) of this data: 12, 18, 3, 20, 8, 13, 22, 5, 18, 10, 8."},"options":[{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"19","en":"19"},{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"12","en":"12"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Gerangskik: 3; 5; 8; 8; 10; 12; 13; 18; 18; 20; 22 (n = 11). Mediaan = 12 (6de waarde). Onderste helfte 3; 5; 8; 8; 10 gee Q₁ = 8; boonste helfte 13; 18; 18; 20; 22 gee Q₃ = 18. IKO = 18 − 8 = 10. 19 is die omvang, 5 die semi-IKO en 12 die mediaan.","en":"Ordered: 3, 5, 8, 8, 10, 12, 13, 18, 18, 20, 22 (n = 11). Median = 12 (6th value). Lower half 3, 5, 8, 8, 10 gives Q₁ = 8; upper half 13, 18, 18, 20, 22 gives Q₃ = 18. IQR = 18 − 8 = 10. 19 is the range, 5 the semi-IQR and 12 the median."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vyfgetalopsomming van 'n klas se toetspunte is: minimum 12; Q₁ = 18; mediaan 25; Q₃ = 31; maksimum 44. Wat is die semi-interkwartielomvang? ___","en":"The five-number summary of a class's test marks is: minimum 12; Q₁ = 18; median 25; Q₃ = 31; maximum 44. What is the semi-interquartile range? ___"},"answers":{"af":["6,5","6.5","6,50","6.50","13/2"],"en":["6.5","6,5","6.50","6,50","13/2"]},"explain":{"af":"Semi-IKO = ½(Q₃ − Q₁) = ½(31 − 18) = 13 ÷ 2 = 6,5. Moenie vergeet om te halveer nie: 13 is die IKO.","en":"Semi-IQR = ½(Q₃ − Q₁) = ½(31 − 18) = 13 ÷ 2 = 6.5. Do not forget to halve: 13 is the IQR."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die mobiele data (in GB) wat 40 leerders in Brits in 'n maand gebruik, is so gegroepeer (klas: frekwensie): 0 ≤ x < 2: 6; 2 ≤ x < 4: 13; 4 ≤ x < 6: 11; 6 ≤ x < 8: 7; 8 ≤ x < 10: 3. Wat is die modale klas?","en":"The mobile data (in GB) that 40 learners in Brits use in a month is grouped like this (class: frequency): 0 ≤ x < 2: 6; 2 ≤ x < 4: 13; 4 ≤ x < 6: 11; 6 ≤ x < 8: 7; 8 ≤ x < 10: 3. What is the modal class?"},"options":[{"af":"4 ≤ x < 6","en":"4 ≤ x < 6"},{"af":"2 ≤ x < 4","en":"2 ≤ x < 4"},{"af":"13","en":"13"},{"af":"8 ≤ x < 10","en":"8 ≤ x < 10"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die modale klas is die klas met die grootste frekwensie: 13, dus 2 ≤ x < 4. Die antwoord is 'n klas, nie die frekwensie 13 nie. 4 ≤ x < 6 is die klas wat die mediaan bevat, en 8 ≤ x < 10 het net die grootste waardes.","en":"The modal class is the class with the highest frequency: 13, so 2 ≤ x < 4. The answer is a class, not the frequency 13. 4 ≤ x < 6 is the class containing the median, and 8 ≤ x < 10 only has the largest values."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die gemiddelde punt van 30 leerders in 'n toets is 62%. 'n Nuwe leerder skryf die toets later en kry 93%. Wat is die nuwe gemiddelde van al 31 leerders? ___%","en":"The mean mark of 30 learners in a test is 62%. A new learner writes the test later and gets 93%. What is the new mean of all 31 learners? ___%"},"answers":{"af":["63","63%","63,0","63.0"],"en":["63","63%","63.0","63,0"]},"explain":{"af":"Som van die 30 punte = 62 × 30 = 1 860. Nuwe som = 1 860 + 93 = 1 953. Nuwe gemiddelde = 1 953 ÷ 31 = 63%. Jy kan nie net (62 + 93) ÷ 2 doen nie, want 62 verteenwoordig 30 leerders.","en":"Sum of the 30 marks = 62 × 30 = 1 860. New sum = 1 860 + 93 = 1 953. New mean = 1 953 ÷ 31 = 63%. You cannot just work out (62 + 93) ÷ 2, because 62 represents 30 learners."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die massa (in g) van 50 suurlemoene van 'n sitrusplaas by Brits is so gegroepeer (klas: frekwensie): 80 ≤ m < 100: 6; 100 ≤ m < 120: 15; 120 ≤ m < 140: 18; 140 ≤ m < 160: 8; 160 ≤ m < 180: 3. Wat is die beraamde gemiddelde massa?","en":"The mass (in g) of 50 lemons from a citrus farm near Brits is grouped like this (class: frequency): 80 ≤ m < 100: 6; 100 ≤ m < 120: 15; 120 ≤ m < 140: 18; 140 ≤ m < 160: 8; 160 ≤ m < 180: 3. What is the estimated mean mass?"},"options":[{"af":"130 g","en":"130 g"},{"af":"1 248 g","en":"1 248 g"},{"af":"134,8 g","en":"134.8 g"},{"af":"124,8 g","en":"124.8 g"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Middelpunte: 90; 110; 130; 150; 170. Σ(f × x) = 6 × 90 + 15 × 110 + 18 × 130 + 8 × 150 + 3 × 170 = 6 240. Beraamde gemiddelde = 6 240 ÷ 50 = 124,8 g. 130 g is net die gemiddelde van die middelpunte, 1 248 g kom van ÷ 5 klasse en 134,8 g gebruik die bogrense in plaas van die middelpunte.","en":"Midpoints: 90, 110, 130, 150, 170. Σ(f × x) = 6 × 90 + 15 × 110 + 18 × 130 + 8 × 150 + 3 × 170 = 6 240. Estimated mean = 6 240 ÷ 50 = 124.8 g. 130 g is just the mean of the midpoints, 1 248 g comes from ÷ 5 classes and 134.8 g uses the upper limits instead of the midpoints."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die wagtyd (in minute) van 45 pendelaars by 'n taxistaanplek in Brits is so gegroepeer (klas: frekwensie): 0 ≤ t < 5: 18; 5 ≤ t < 10: 12; 10 ≤ t < 15: 8; 15 ≤ t < 20: 5; 20 ≤ t < 25: 2. In watter klas lê die mediaan?","en":"The waiting time (in minutes) of 45 commuters at a taxi rank in Brits is grouped like this (class: frequency): 0 ≤ t < 5: 18; 5 ≤ t < 10: 12; 10 ≤ t < 15: 8; 15 ≤ t < 20: 5; 20 ≤ t < 25: 2. In which class does the median lie?"},"options":[{"af":"0 ≤ t < 5","en":"0 ≤ t < 5"},{"af":"10 ≤ t < 15","en":"10 ≤ t < 15"},{"af":"5 ≤ t < 10","en":"5 ≤ t < 10"},{"af":"20 ≤ t < 25","en":"20 ≤ t < 25"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die mediaan is die 23ste waarde ((45 + 1) ÷ 2 = 23). Kumulatiewe frekwensies: 18; 30; … Die 19de tot 30ste waardes lê in 5 ≤ t < 10, dus ook die 23ste. 0 ≤ t < 5 is die modale klas, 10 ≤ t < 15 is net die middelste ry van die tabel, en 20 ≤ t < 25 behandel die posisie 23 asof dit 'n wagtyd van 23 minute is.","en":"The median is the 23rd value ((45 + 1) ÷ 2 = 23). Cumulative frequencies: 18, 30, … The 19th to 30th values lie in 5 ≤ t < 10, so the 23rd does too. 0 ≤ t < 5 is the modal class, 10 ≤ t < 15 is just the middle row of the table, and 20 ≤ t < 25 treats the position 23 as if it were a waiting time of 23 minutes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die vyfgetalopsommings van twee graad 10-klasse se wiskundepunte (in %) is: Klas A: minimum 35; Q₁ = 52; mediaan 60; Q₃ = 71; maksimum 88. Klas B: minimum 41; Q₁ = 55; mediaan 63; Q₃ = 68; maksimum 79. Watter stelling is korrek?","en":"The five-number summaries of two Grade 10 classes' maths marks (in %) are: Class A: minimum 35; Q₁ = 52; median 60; Q₃ = 71; maximum 88. Class B: minimum 41; Q₁ = 55; median 63; Q₃ = 68; maximum 79. Which statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Klas B het beter en meer konsekwent presteer: sy mediaan is hoër, en sy IKO (13) en omvang (38) is kleiner as dié van Klas A.","en":"Class B performed better and more consistently: its median is higher, and its IQR (13) and range (38) are smaller than those of Class A."},{"af":"Klas A het beter presteer, want sy hoogste punt (88%) is hoër as dié van Klas B.","en":"Class A performed better, because its highest mark (88%) is higher than that of Class B."},{"af":"Ongeveer 75% van die leerders in Klas A het meer as 71% gekry.","en":"About 75% of the learners in Class A scored more than 71%."},{"af":"Die twee klasse se punte is ewe veel versprei, want hulle mediane verskil met net 3.","en":"The two classes' marks are equally spread out, because their medians differ by only 3."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Klas A: IKO = 71 − 52 = 19, omvang = 88 − 35 = 53. Klas B: IKO = 68 − 55 = 13, omvang = 79 − 41 = 38, en mediaan 63 > 60. Een hoë punt sê niks oor die hele klas nie; bo Q₃ lê net ongeveer 25% van die data, nie 75% nie; en die mediaan meet die middel, nie die verspreiding nie.","en":"Class A: IQR = 71 − 52 = 19, range = 88 − 35 = 53. Class B: IQR = 68 − 55 = 13, range = 79 − 41 = 38, and median 63 > 60. One high mark says nothing about the whole class; only about 25% of the data lies above Q₃, not 75%; and the median measures the centre, not the spread."}}]},{"id":"w10-t3-trig-2d","title":{"af":"Trigonometrie: probleme in twee dimensies","en":"Trigonometry: problems in two dimensions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hoogte- en dieptehoeke korrek kan gebruik en 2D-probleme met een of twee reghoekige driehoeke in konteks kan oplos, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"You will be able to use angles of elevation and depression correctly and solve 2D problems with one or two right-angled triangles in context, rounded to two decimal places."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoogtehoek en dieptehoek\n\n- Die **hoogtehoek** is die hoek tussen die **horisontaal** en die **siglyn** as jy **op** na 'n voorwerp kyk.\n- Die **dieptehoek** is die hoek tussen die **horisontaal** en die siglyn as jy **af** na 'n voorwerp kyk.\n- Albei word **altyd vanaf die horisontaal** gemeet, nooit vanaf die vertikaal ('n muur of toring) nie.\n\nDie horisontale lyne by die waarnemer en by die voorwerp is ewewydig. Daarom is die **hoogtehoek van A na B gelyk aan die dieptehoek van B na A** (verwisselende hoeke).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die dieptehoek word binne-in die driehoek teen die muur geplaas. Die hoek tussen die siglyn en die vertikale muur is 90° − dieptehoek. Skuif eerder die dieptehoek met verwisselende hoeke na onder, waar dit 'n hoogtehoek binne die driehoek word.\n\n## Metode vir enige 2D-probleem\n\n1. **Skets** 'n netjiese diagram. Merk regte hoeke, horisontale lyne, gegewe lengtes en hoeke, en die onbekende (h, x, d of θ).\n2. Soek 'n **reghoekige driehoek** wat die onbekende bevat en genoeg gegewe inligting het.\n3. Benoem die sye relatief tot die bekende hoek: teenoorstaande, aangrensende en skuinssy.\n4. Kies die verhouding (sin, cos of tan) wat die bekende en die onbekende sy verbind.\n5. Los op. Hou die volle waarde in die sakrekenaar en rond **eers aan die einde** af tot twee desimale plekke. Skryf die eenheid by.\n6. Kontroleer: die skuinssy is die langste sy, en 'n groter hoek lê oorkant 'n groter sy.\n\nOm 'n **hoek** te bereken, kies jy die verhouding met die twee bekende sye en gebruik sin^{−1}, cos^{−1} of tan^{−1}.\n\n## Algemene situasies\n\n| Situasie | Skuinssy | Hoek en sye |\n|---|---|---|\n| Leer teen 'n muur | die leer | hoek met die grond; hoogte teen die muur = teenoorstaande |\n| Skaduwee | die sonstraal | hoogtehoek van die son; skaduwee = aangrensende |\n| Vlieër | die tou | hoek tussen tou en horisontaal; hoogte = teenoorstaande |\n| Kabelkar | die kabel | hellingshoek; styging = teenoorstaande |\n| Oprit of pad | die skuins oppervlak | hellingshoek; horisontale afstand = aangrensende |\n\n- As 'n hoogtehoek vanaf iemand se **oë** (of hand) gemeet word, tel die **ooghoogte** (of handhoogte) by die berekende hoogte.\n- Maak seker al die lengtes het **dieselfde eenheid** (m of km) voordat jy bereken.\n\n## Probleme met twee driehoeke\n\nBaie eksamenvrae het twee reghoekige driehoeke met 'n **gemeenskaplike sy**. Bereken eers die gemeenskaplike sy in die driehoek waar jy genoeg inligting het, en gebruik dit dan in die tweede driehoek.\n\n**Tipe 1: Van een gebou na 'n ander.** Vanaf die dak van 'n gebou kyk jy op na die bopunt van 'n toring (hoogtehoek α) en af na die voet daarvan (dieptehoek β). 'n Horisontale lyn vanaf die dak verdeel die figuur in twee driehoeke met die afstand d tussen die geboue as gemeenskaplike sy.\n\n- Onderste driehoek: d = [[hoogte van gebou/tan β]]\n- Boonste driehoek: hoogte bo die dak = d × tan α\n- Toring = hoogte van gebou + d × tan α\n\n**Tipe 2: Twee waarnemers aan dieselfde kant, hoogte bekend.** Bereken elke horisontale afstand apart, bv. [[h/tan 25°]] en [[h/tan 40°]], en trek af. Moenie die hoeke van mekaar aftrek nie.\n\n**Tipe 3: Twee waarnemers, hoogte onbekend.** Laat die onbekende afstand x wees en skryf h op twee maniere, bv. h = x tan 50° en h = (x + 20) tan 30°. Stel gelyk, los op vir x en bereken dan h = x tan 50°.\n\n**Tipe 4: Een waarnemer, twee hoogtes.** Kyk jy vanaf dieselfde punt na die onderkant en die bokant van iets (bv. 'n vlagpaal op 'n toring), is die horisontale afstand die gemeenskaplike sy. Bereken albei hoogtes en trek af.\n\n> **Wenk:** Skryf by elke stap watter driehoek jy gebruik, bv. \"In △ABC:\". So kan die nasiener jou werk volg, en jy kry steeds metodepunte al is 'n getal later verkeerd.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om tussenantwoorde af te rond en dan verder te werk. Dit kan die laaste desimaal van jou finale antwoord verander. Stoor tussenantwoorde in die sakrekenaar se geheue.","en":"## Angle of elevation and angle of depression\n\n- The **angle of elevation** is the angle between the **horizontal** and the **line of sight** when you look **up** at an object.\n- The **angle of depression** is the angle between the **horizontal** and the line of sight when you look **down** at an object.\n- Both are **always measured from the horizontal**, never from the vertical (a wall or tower).\n\nThe horizontal lines at the observer and at the object are parallel. That is why the **angle of elevation from A to B equals the angle of depression from B to A** (alternate angles).\n\n> **Common mistake:** The angle of depression is placed inside the triangle against the wall. The angle between the line of sight and the vertical wall is 90° − angle of depression. Rather move the angle of depression down with alternate angles, where it becomes an angle of elevation inside the triangle.\n\n## Method for any 2D problem\n\n1. **Sketch** a neat diagram. Mark right angles, horizontal lines, given lengths and angles, and the unknown (h, x, d or θ).\n2. Find a **right-angled triangle** that contains the unknown and has enough given information.\n3. Label the sides relative to the known angle: opposite, adjacent and hypotenuse.\n4. Choose the ratio (sin, cos or tan) that links the known and the unknown side.\n5. Solve. Keep the full value in the calculator and round to two decimal places **only at the end**. Write the unit.\n6. Check: the hypotenuse is the longest side, and a bigger angle lies opposite a bigger side.\n\nTo calculate an **angle**, choose the ratio with the two known sides and use sin^{−1}, cos^{−1} or tan^{−1}.\n\n## Common situations\n\n| Situation | Hypotenuse | Angle and sides |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ladder against a wall | the ladder | angle with the ground; height up the wall = opposite |\n| Shadow | the sun ray | angle of elevation of the sun; shadow = adjacent |\n| Kite | the string | angle between string and horizontal; height = opposite |\n| Cable car | the cable | angle of inclination; rise = opposite |\n| Ramp or road | the sloping surface | angle of inclination; horizontal distance = adjacent |\n\n- If an angle of elevation is measured from someone's **eyes** (or hand), add the **eye height** (or hand height) to the calculated height.\n- Make sure all lengths are in the **same unit** (m or km) before you calculate.\n\n## Problems with two triangles\n\nMany exam questions have two right-angled triangles with a **common side**. First calculate the common side in the triangle where you have enough information, then use it in the second triangle.\n\n**Type 1: From one building to another.** From the roof of a building you look up to the top of a tower (angle of elevation α) and down to its foot (angle of depression β). A horizontal line from the roof splits the figure into two triangles with the distance d between the buildings as the common side.\n\n- Lower triangle: d = [[height of building/tan β]]\n- Upper triangle: height above the roof = d × tan α\n- Tower = height of building + d × tan α\n\n**Type 2: Two observers on the same side, height known.** Calculate each horizontal distance separately, e.g. [[h/tan 25°]] and [[h/tan 40°]], and subtract. Do not subtract the angles from each other.\n\n**Type 3: Two observers, height unknown.** Let the unknown distance be x and write h in two ways, e.g. h = x tan 50° and h = (x + 20) tan 30°. Set them equal, solve for x and then calculate h = x tan 50°.\n\n**Type 4: One observer, two heights.** If you look from the same point at the bottom and the top of something (e.g. a flagpole on a tower), the horizontal distance is the common side. Calculate both heights and subtract.\n\n> **Tip:** At every step, write which triangle you are using, e.g. \"In △ABC:\". That way the marker can follow your work, and you still earn method marks even if a number goes wrong later.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Rounding intermediate answers and then working on. It can change the last decimal of your final answer. Store intermediate answers in the calculator's memory."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoogtehoek","en":"Angle of elevation"},"def":{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as 'n waarnemer óp na 'n voorwerp kyk.","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when an observer looks up at an object."}},{"term":{"af":"Dieptehoek","en":"Angle of depression"},"def":{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as 'n waarnemer áf na 'n voorwerp kyk.","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when an observer looks down at an object."}},{"term":{"af":"Siglyn","en":"Line of sight"},"def":{"af":"Die reguit lyn van die waarnemer se oog na die voorwerp.","en":"The straight line from the observer's eye to the object."}},{"term":{"af":"Horisontaal","en":"Horizontal"},"def":{"af":"'n Plat lyn ewewydig aan gelyk grond of die wateroppervlak; hoogte- en dieptehoeke word daarvandaan gemeet.","en":"A flat line parallel to level ground or the water surface; angles of elevation and depression are measured from it."}},{"term":{"af":"Hellingshoek","en":"Angle of inclination"},"def":{"af":"Die hoek tussen 'n skuins oppervlak (pad, oprit, kabel) en die horisontaal.","en":"The angle between a sloping surface (road, ramp, cable) and the horizontal."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike sy","en":"Common side"},"def":{"af":"'n Sy wat twee driehoeke deel; bereken dit in die een driehoek en gebruik dit in die ander.","en":"A side shared by two triangles; calculate it in one triangle and use it in the other."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwisselende hoeke","en":"Alternate angles"},"def":{"af":"Gelyke hoeke tussen ewewydige lyne; daarom is die dieptehoek van B na A gelyk aan die hoogtehoek van A na B.","en":"Equal angles between parallel lines; that is why the angle of depression from B to A equals the angle of elevation from A to B."}},{"term":{"af":"Ooghoogte","en":"Eye height"},"def":{"af":"Die hoogte van die waarnemer se oë bo die grond; tel dit by die berekende hoogte as die hoek vanaf die oë gemeet is.","en":"The height of the observer's eyes above the ground; add it to the calculated height if the angle was measured from the eyes."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoogtehoek met ooghoogte","en":"Angle of elevation with eye height"},"problem":{"af":"Mpho staan op gelyk grond 40 m van die voet van 'n selfoontoring in Brits. Die hoogtehoek vanaf sy oë na die bopunt van die toring is 38°. Sy oë is 1,6 m bo die grond. Bereken die hoogte van die toring, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"Mpho stands on level ground 40 m from the foot of a cellphone tower in Brits. The angle of elevation from his eyes to the top of the tower is 38°. His eyes are 1.6 m above the ground. Calculate the height of the tower, rounded to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Skets: trek 'n horisontale lyn van 40 m vanaf Mpho se oë tot by die toring. Die vertikale sy h van die driehoek is die deel van die toring bó sy oë.","en":"Sketch: draw a horizontal line of 40 m from Mpho's eyes to the tower. The vertical side h of the triangle is the part of the tower above his eyes."},{"af":"Relatief tot 38° is h teenoorstaande en 40 m aangrensende, dus tan 38° = [[h/40]]","en":"Relative to 38°, h is opposite and 40 m is adjacent, so tan 38° = [[h/40]]"},{"af":"h = 40 tan 38° = 31,25 m (hou die volle waarde in die sakrekenaar)","en":"h = 40 tan 38° = 31.25 m (keep the full value in the calculator)"},{"af":"Tel die ooghoogte by: hoogte van toring = 31,25… + 1,6 = 32,85 m","en":"Add the eye height: height of tower = 31.25… + 1.6 = 32.85 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Die toring is 32,85 m hoog.","en":"The tower is 32.85 m high."}},{"title":{"af":"Dieptehoek vanaf 'n krans","en":"Angle of depression from a cliff"},"problem":{"af":"Vanaf die bopunt van 'n 65 m hoë krans langs die Hartbeespoortdam is die dieptehoek na 'n boot op die water 23°. Hoe ver is die boot van die voet van die krans? Rond af tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"From the top of a 65 m high cliff next to the Hartbeespoort Dam, the angle of depression to a boat on the water is 23°. How far is the boat from the foot of the cliff? Round to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Die dieptehoek lê by die bopunt, tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn na die boot. Die horisontaal is ewewydig aan die wateroppervlak.","en":"The angle of depression is at the top, between the horizontal and the line of sight to the boat. The horizontal is parallel to the water surface."},{"af":"Verwisselende hoeke: die hoogtehoek vanaf die boot na die bopunt is ook 23°. Dit is die hoek binne die driehoek by die boot.","en":"Alternate angles: the angle of elevation from the boat to the top is also 23°. This is the angle inside the triangle at the boat."},{"af":"Relatief tot 23° by die boot is 65 m teenoorstaande en die afstand d aangrensende: tan 23° = [[65/d]]","en":"Relative to 23° at the boat, 65 m is opposite and the distance d is adjacent: tan 23° = [[65/d]]"},{"af":"d staan onder die breukstreep, dus ruil om: d = [[65/tan 23°]] = 153,13 m","en":"d is in the denominator, so swap it over: d = [[65/tan 23°]] = 153.13 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Die boot is 153,13 m van die voet van die krans.","en":"The boat is 153.13 m from the foot of the cliff."}},{"title":{"af":"Twee driehoeke: van een gebou na 'n ander","en":"Two triangles: from one building to another"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato staan op die plat dak van 'n 20 m hoë woonstelblok in Pretoria. Die hoogtehoek na die bopunt van 'n kantoortoring oorkant die straat is 25° en die dieptehoek na die voet van die toring is 35°. Bereken die hoogte van die kantoortoring, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke (ignoreer Lerato se lengte).","en":"Lerato stands on the flat roof of a 20 m high block of flats in Pretoria. The angle of elevation to the top of an office tower across the street is 25° and the angle of depression to the foot of the tower is 35°. Calculate the height of the office tower, rounded to two decimal places (ignore Lerato's height)."},"steps":[{"af":"Trek 'n horisontale lyn vanaf die dak tot by die toring. Dit verdeel die figuur in twee reghoekige driehoeke met die horisontale afstand d as gemeenskaplike sy.","en":"Draw a horizontal line from the roof to the tower. It splits the figure into two right-angled triangles with the horizontal distance d as the common side."},{"af":"Onderste driehoek (dieptehoek 35°; die teenoorstaande sy is 20 m): tan 35° = [[20/d]], dus d = [[20/tan 35°]] = 28,56 m","en":"Lower triangle (angle of depression 35°; the opposite side is 20 m): tan 35° = [[20/d]], so d = [[20/tan 35°]] = 28.56 m"},{"af":"Boonste driehoek (hoogtehoek 25°): tan 25° = [[x/d]], dus x = d × tan 25° = 13,32 m (gebruik die volle waarde van d)","en":"Upper triangle (angle of elevation 25°): tan 25° = [[x/d]], so x = d × tan 25° = 13.32 m (use the full value of d)"},{"af":"Hoogte van toring = 20 + x = 20 + 13,32 = 33,32 m","en":"Height of tower = 20 + x = 20 + 13.32 = 33.32 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Die kantoortoring is 33,32 m hoog.","en":"The office tower is 33.32 m high."}},{"title":{"af":"Twee waarnemers, hoogte onbekend","en":"Two observers, height unknown"},"problem":{"af":"P en Q lê op gelyk grond in 'n reguit lyn met die voet T van 'n watertoring op 'n sitrusplaas naby Brits. PQ = 20 m en Q is nader aan die toring. Die hoogtehoek na die bopunt B van die toring is 30° vanaf P en 50° vanaf Q. Bereken die hoogte BT, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"P and Q lie on level ground in a straight line with the foot T of a water tower on a citrus farm near Brits. PQ = 20 m and Q is closer to the tower. The angle of elevation to the top B of the tower is 30° from P and 50° from Q. Calculate the height BT, rounded to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Laat QT = x en BT = h. Dan is PT = x + 20.","en":"Let QT = x and BT = h. Then PT = x + 20."},{"af":"In △BQT: tan 50° = [[h/x]], dus h = x tan 50°","en":"In △BQT: tan 50° = [[h/x]], so h = x tan 50°"},{"af":"In △BPT: tan 30° = [[h/x + 20]], dus h = (x + 20) tan 30°","en":"In △BPT: tan 30° = [[h/x + 20]], so h = (x + 20) tan 30°"},{"af":"Stel gelyk: x tan 50° = x tan 30° + 20 tan 30°, dus x(tan 50° − tan 30°) = 20 tan 30°","en":"Set equal: x tan 50° = x tan 30° + 20 tan 30°, so x(tan 50° − tan 30°) = 20 tan 30°"},{"af":"x = [[20 tan 30°/tan 50° − tan 30°]] = 18,79 m","en":"x = [[20 tan 30°/tan 50° − tan 30°]] = 18.79 m"},{"af":"h = x tan 50° = 18,794… × tan 50° = 22,40 m (gebruik die volle waarde van x)","en":"h = x tan 50° = 18.794… × tan 50° = 22.40 m (use the full value of x)"}],"answer":{"af":"BT = 22,40 m","en":"BT = 22.40 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n hoogtehoek?","en":"What is an angle of elevation?"},"options":[{"af":"Die hoek tussen die vertikaal en die siglyn as jy opkyk","en":"The angle between the vertical and the line of sight when you look up"},{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as jy afkyk","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when you look down"},{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as jy opkyk","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when you look up"},{"af":"Die hoek tussen die siglyn en die skaduwee van die voorwerp","en":"The angle between the line of sight and the shadow of the object"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Hoogtehoek word altyd vanaf die horisontaal gemeet, met die siglyn bó die horisontaal (jy kyk op). As jy afkyk, is dit 'n dieptehoek. Die vertikaal word nooit as verwysing gebruik nie.","en":"An angle of elevation is always measured from the horizontal, with the line of sight above the horizontal (you look up). When you look down, it is an angle of depression. The vertical is never used as the reference."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die hoogtehoek vanaf 'n boot na die bopunt van 'n krans is gelyk aan die dieptehoek vanaf die bopunt van die krans na die boot.","en":"The angle of elevation from a boat to the top of a cliff equals the angle of depression from the top of the cliff to the boat."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die horisontale lyne by die boot en by die bopunt is ewewydig, dus is die twee hoeke verwisselende hoeke en ewe groot.","en":"True. The horizontal lines at the boat and at the top are parallel, so the two angles are alternate angles and equal."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by sy beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to its description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Hoogtehoek","en":"Angle of elevation"},"r":{"af":"Bo die horisontaal gemeet; jy kyk op","en":"Measured above the horizontal; you look up"}},{"l":{"af":"Dieptehoek","en":"Angle of depression"},"r":{"af":"Onder die horisontaal gemeet; jy kyk af","en":"Measured below the horizontal; you look down"}},{"l":{"af":"Siglyn","en":"Line of sight"},"r":{"af":"Die reguit lyn van die oog na die voorwerp","en":"The straight line from the eye to the object"}},{"l":{"af":"Hellingshoek","en":"Angle of inclination"},"r":{"af":"Die hoek tussen 'n skuins pad of oprit en die horisontaal","en":"The angle between a sloping road or ramp and the horizontal"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hoogte- en dieptehoeke word albei vanaf die horisontaal gemeet: bo (opkyk) of onder (afkyk). Die siglyn is die lyn waarlangs jy kyk, en 'n hellingshoek beskryf hoe steil 'n oppervlak is.","en":"Angles of elevation and depression are both measured from the horizontal: above (look up) or below (look down). The line of sight is the line along which you look, and an angle of inclination describes how steep a surface is."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vanaf die bopunt van 'n gebou is die dieptehoek na 'n motor 40°. Watter hoek maak die siglyn met die vertikale muur van die gebou?","en":"From the top of a building the angle of depression to a car is 40°. What angle does the line of sight make with the vertical wall of the building?"},"options":[{"af":"40°","en":"40°"},{"af":"50°","en":"50°"},{"af":"140°","en":"140°"},{"af":"90°","en":"90°"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die horisontaal en die vertikale muur maak 90° met mekaar. Die siglyn lê 40° onder die horisontaal, dus maak dit 90° − 40° = 50° met die muur. Moenie die 40° teen die muur plaas nie.","en":"The horizontal and the vertical wall make 90° with each other. The line of sight lies 40° below the horizontal, so it makes 90° − 40° = 50° with the wall. Do not place the 40° against the wall."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Leer van 5 m leun teen 'n vertikale muur en maak 'n hoek van 70° met die horisontale grond. Hoe hoog teen die muur reik die leer? Rond af tot twee desimale plekke. ___ m","en":"A 5 m ladder leans against a vertical wall and makes an angle of 70° with the horizontal ground. How high up the wall does the ladder reach? Round to two decimal places. ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["4,7","4.7","4,70","4.70","4,7 m","4.7 m","4,70 m","4.70 m"],"en":["4,7","4.7","4,70","4.70","4,7 m","4.7 m","4,70 m","4.70 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Die leer is die skuinssy en die hoogte lê oorkant die 70°-hoek: sin 70° = h/5, dus h = 5 sin 70° = 4,70 m.","en":"The ladder is the hypotenuse and the height lies opposite the 70° angle: sin 70° = h/5, so h = 5 sin 70° = 4.70 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die son se hoogtehoek is 35°. Hoe lank is die skaduwee van 'n 6 m hoë lamppaal op gelyk grond?","en":"The angle of elevation of the sun is 35°. How long is the shadow of a 6 m high lamp post on level ground?"},"options":[{"af":"4,20 m","en":"4.20 m"},{"af":"10,46 m","en":"10.46 m"},{"af":"8,57 m","en":"8.57 m"},{"af":"4,91 m","en":"4.91 m"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Relatief tot 35° is die paal (6 m) teenoorstaande en die skaduwee s aangrensende: tan 35° = 6/s, dus s = 6 ÷ tan 35° = 8,57 m. 4,20 m is 6 × tan 35° (omgekeer), 10,46 m is die sonstraal (6 ÷ sin 35°) en 4,91 m gebruik cos.","en":"Relative to 35°, the post (6 m) is opposite and the shadow s is adjacent: tan 35° = 6/s, so s = 6 ÷ tan 35° = 8.57 m. 4.20 m is 6 × tan 35° (upside down), 10.46 m is the sun ray (6 ÷ sin 35°) and 4.91 m uses cos."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Oprit by 'n skool in Madibeng styg 0,8 m oor 'n horisontale afstand van 9,6 m. Bereken die hellingshoek van die oprit, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke. ___°","en":"A ramp at a school in Madibeng rises 0.8 m over a horizontal distance of 9.6 m. Calculate the angle of inclination of the ramp, rounded to two decimal places. ___°"},"answers":{"af":["4,76","4.76","4,76°","4.76°","θ = 4,76","θ = 4.76","θ = 4,76°","θ = 4.76°","θ=4,76","θ=4.76","θ=4,76°","θ=4.76°"],"en":["4,76","4.76","4,76°","4.76°","θ = 4,76","θ = 4.76","θ = 4,76°","θ = 4.76°","θ=4,76","θ=4.76","θ=4,76°","θ=4.76°"]},"explain":{"af":"Die styging (0,8 m) is teenoorstaande en die horisontale afstand (9,6 m) aangrensende: tan θ = 0,8 ÷ 9,6, dus θ = tan⁻¹(0,8 ÷ 9,6) = 4,76°.","en":"The rise (0.8 m) is opposite and the horizontal distance (9.6 m) is adjacent: tan θ = 0.8 ÷ 9.6, so θ = tan⁻¹(0.8 ÷ 9.6) = 4.76°."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vanaf 'n venster 12 m bo die grond is die dieptehoek na 'n taxi op die straat 28°. Hoe ver is die taxi horisontaal van die gebou?","en":"From a window 12 m above the ground the angle of depression to a taxi in the street is 28°. How far is the taxi horizontally from the building?"},"options":[{"af":"6,38 m","en":"6.38 m"},{"af":"25,56 m","en":"25.56 m"},{"af":"13,59 m","en":"13.59 m"},{"af":"22,57 m","en":"22.57 m"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Verwisselende hoeke: die hoogtehoek vanaf die taxi na die venster is 28°. tan 28° = 12/d, dus d = 12 ÷ tan 28° = 22,57 m. 6,38 m is 12 × tan 28°, 25,56 m is die lengte van die siglyn (12 ÷ sin 28°) en 13,59 m gebruik cos.","en":"Alternate angles: the angle of elevation from the taxi to the window is 28°. tan 28° = 12/d, so d = 12 ÷ tan 28° = 22.57 m. 6.38 m is 12 × tan 28°, 25.56 m is the length of the line of sight (12 ÷ sin 28°) and 13.59 m uses cos."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vir 'n akkurate antwoord moet jy elke tussenantwoord tot twee desimale plekke afrond voordat jy verder bereken.","en":"For an accurate answer you must round every intermediate answer to two decimal places before you calculate further."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. Hou die volle waarde in die sakrekenaar (of sy geheue) en rond net die finale antwoord af. Vroeë afronding kan die laaste desimaal van die antwoord verander.","en":"False. Keep the full value in the calculator (or its memory) and round only the final answer. Rounding early can change the last decimal of the answer."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho vlieg 'n vlieër op 'n rugbyveld in Brits. Die tou is 50 m lank, styf getrek, en maak 'n hoek van 52° met die horisontaal. Hy hou die tou 1,2 m bo die grond vas. Hoe hoog is die vlieër bo die grond?","en":"Sipho flies a kite on a rugby field in Brits. The string is 50 m long, pulled tight, and makes an angle of 52° with the horizontal. He holds the string 1.2 m above the ground. How high is the kite above the ground?"},"options":[{"af":"40,60 m","en":"40.60 m"},{"af":"39,40 m","en":"39.40 m"},{"af":"31,98 m","en":"31.98 m"},{"af":"65,20 m","en":"65.20 m"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die tou is die skuinssy: hoogte bo sy hand = 50 sin 52° = 39,40 m. Tel die 1,2 m by: 39,40 + 1,2 = 40,60 m. 39,40 m vergeet die hand se hoogte, 31,98 m gebruik cos en 65,20 m gebruik tan.","en":"The string is the hypotenuse: height above his hand = 50 sin 52° = 39.40 m. Add the 1.2 m: 39.40 + 1.2 = 40.60 m. 39.40 m forgets the height of the hand, 31.98 m uses cos and 65.20 m uses tan."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vanaf die bopunt van 'n 15 m hoë gebou is die dieptehoek na die voet van 'n toring oorkant die straat 40° en die hoogtehoek na die bopunt van die toring 30°. Bereken die hoogte van die toring, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke. ___ m","en":"From the top of a 15 m high building the angle of depression to the foot of a tower across the street is 40° and the angle of elevation to the top of the tower is 30°. Calculate the height of the tower, rounded to two decimal places. ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["25,32","25.32","25,32 m","25.32 m"],"en":["25,32","25.32","25,32 m","25.32 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Onderste driehoek: d = 15 ÷ tan 40° = 17,88 m. Boonste driehoek: x = d × tan 30° = 10,32 m. Toring = 15 + 10,32 = 25,32 m.","en":"Lower triangle: d = 15 ÷ tan 40° = 17.88 m. Upper triangle: x = d × tan 30° = 10.32 m. Tower = 15 + 10.32 = 25.32 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die skagtoring van 'n myn naby Brits is 60 m hoog. Vanaf punt A op gelyk grond is die hoogtehoek na die bopunt 25°. Thabo stap reguit na die skagtoring tot by B, waar die hoogtehoek 40° is. Hoe ver het hy gestap?","en":"The headgear (shaft tower) of a mine near Brits is 60 m high. From point A on level ground the angle of elevation to the top is 25°. Thabo walks straight towards the headgear to B, where the angle of elevation is 40°. How far did he walk?"},"options":[{"af":"22,37 m","en":"22.37 m"},{"af":"57,17 m","en":"57.17 m"},{"af":"48,63 m","en":"48.63 m"},{"af":"223,92 m","en":"223.92 m"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike sy: die hoogte van 60 m. Afstand vanaf A = 60 ÷ tan 25° = 128,670… m en vanaf B = 60 ÷ tan 40° = 71,505… m. AB = 128,670… − 71,505… = 57,17 m (met die afgeronde waardes 128,67 − 71,51 kry jy 57,16 m, wat verkeerd is). 22,37 m gebruik 60 × tan (omgekeer), 48,63 m gebruik sin, en 223,92 m trek die hoeke af (40° − 25° = 15°), wat nie mag nie.","en":"Common side: the height of 60 m. Distance from A = 60 ÷ tan 25° = 128.670… m and from B = 60 ÷ tan 40° = 71.505… m. AB = 128.670… − 71.505… = 57.17 m (with the rounded values 128.67 − 71.51 you get 57.16 m, which is wrong). 22.37 m uses 60 × tan (upside down), 48.63 m uses sin, and 223.92 m subtracts the angles (40° − 25° = 15°), which is not allowed."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Punt A is 50 m van die voet T van 'n toring op gelyk grond. Die hoogtehoek vanaf A na die bopunt van die toring is 32°. Bo-op die toring staan 'n vlagpaal, en die hoogtehoek vanaf A na die bopunt van die vlagpaal is 36°. Bereken die lengte van die vlagpaal, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke. ___ m","en":"Point A is 50 m from the foot T of a tower on level ground. The angle of elevation from A to the top of the tower is 32°. A flagpole stands on top of the tower, and the angle of elevation from A to the top of the flagpole is 36°. Calculate the length of the flagpole, rounded to two decimal places. ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["5,08","5.08","5,08 m","5.08 m"],"en":["5,08","5.08","5,08 m","5.08 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike sy AT = 50 m. Toring + vlagpaal = 50 tan 36° = 36,327… m en toring = 50 tan 32° = 31,243… m. Vlagpaal = 50(tan 36° − tan 32°) = 5,08 m. As jy eers afrond, kry jy 36,33 − 31,24 = 5,09 m, wat verkeerd is. 50 tan 4° = 3,50 m is ook verkeerd: hoeke mag nie afgetrek word nie.","en":"Common side AT = 50 m. Tower + flagpole = 50 tan 36° = 36.327… m and tower = 50 tan 32° = 31.243… m. Flagpole = 50(tan 36° − tan 32°) = 5.08 m. If you round first, you get 36.33 − 31.24 = 5.09 m, which is wrong. 50 tan 4° = 3.50 m is also wrong: angles may not be subtracted."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Uitkyktoring staan op gelyk grond langs die Hartbeespoortdam. Vanaf punt P is die hoogtehoek na die bopunt van die toring 35°. Jy stap 30 m reguit na die toring tot by Q, waar die hoogtehoek 55° is. Wat is die hoogte van die toring?","en":"A lookout tower stands on level ground next to the Hartbeespoort Dam. From point P the angle of elevation to the top of the tower is 35°. You walk 30 m straight towards the tower to Q, where the angle of elevation is 55°. What is the height of the tower?"},"options":[{"af":"42,84 m","en":"42.84 m"},{"af":"21,01 m","en":"21.01 m"},{"af":"10,92 m","en":"10.92 m"},{"af":"41,21 m","en":"41.21 m"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Laat QT = x. Dan is h = x tan 55° en h = (x + 30) tan 35°. Stel gelyk: x(tan 55° − tan 35°) = 30 tan 35°, dus x = 28,857… m en h = x tan 55° = 41,21 m (gebruik die volle waarde van x). 42,84 m en 21,01 m behandel 30 m asof dit die afstand tot by die toring is, en 10,92 m trek die hoeke af.","en":"Let QT = x. Then h = x tan 55° and h = (x + 30) tan 35°. Set equal: x(tan 55° − tan 35°) = 30 tan 35°, so x = 28.857… m and h = x tan 55° = 41.21 m (use the full value of x). 42.84 m and 21.01 m treat 30 m as if it were the distance to the tower, and 10.92 m subtracts the angles."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Meting en waarskynlikheid","en":"Measurement and probability"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t4-meting","title":{"af":"Meting: oppervlakte en volume","en":"Measurement: surface area and volume"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die buiteoppervlakte en volume van prismas, silinders, piramides, keëls, sfere en saamgestelde voorwerpe kan bereken, en weet wat gebeur as afmetings met k vermenigvuldig word.","en":"You will be able to calculate the surface area and volume of prisms, cylinders, pyramids, cones, spheres and combined objects, and know what happens when dimensions are multiplied by k."},"summary":{"af":"## Eenhede en omskakelings\n\n- **Lengte:** 1 cm = 10 mm; 1 m = 100 cm\n- **Oppervlakte** (kwadreer die faktor): 1 cm^{2} = 100 mm^{2}; 1 m^{2} = 10 000 cm^{2}\n- **Volume** (kubeer die faktor): 1 cm^{3} = 1 000 mm^{3}; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 000 cm^{3}\n- **Kapasiteit:** 1 cm^{3} = 1 mℓ; **1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ**; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 ℓ = 1 kℓ\n\n> **Onthou!** Maak al die afmetings eers dieselfde eenheid voordat jy in 'n formule vervang. Buiteoppervlakte is in vierkante eenhede (cm^{2}, m^{2}) en volume in kubieke eenhede (cm^{3}, m^{3}).\n\n## Regte prismas en silinders\n\n'n **Regte prisma** het twee kongruente, ewewydige basisse, en sy syvlakke is reghoeke wat loodreg op die basisse staan. 'n **Silinder** werk dieselfde, maar sy basis is 'n sirkel.\n\n- Volume = oppervlakte van die basis × loodregte hoogte (H)\n- Buiteoppervlakte = 2 × oppervlakte van die basis + omtrek van die basis × H\n\n| Voorwerp | Buiteoppervlakte | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Reghoekige prisma (l, b, h) | 2(lb + lh + bh) | l × b × h |\n| Kubus (sy s) | 6s^{2} | s^{3} |\n| Driehoekige prisma | 2 × ([[1/2]] × b × h) + (som van die driehoek se sye) × H | [[1/2]] × b × h × H |\n| Silinder (radius r) | 2πr^{2} + 2πrH | πr^{2}H |\n\nBy die driehoekige prisma is b en h die basis en hoogte van die driehoek, en H is die lengte van die prisma.\n\n**Hoekom 2πrH?** As jy die kromme oppervlak van 'n silinder oopsny en platlê, kry jy 'n reghoek. Sy lengte is die omtrek van die sirkel (2πr) en sy breedte is H.\n\n## Piramides, keëls en sfere\n\nDie volume van 'n piramide of keël is presies [[1/3]] van die prisma of silinder met dieselfde basis en loodregte hoogte:\n\n- Volume = [[1/3]] × oppervlakte van die basis × H\n\nVir die buiteoppervlakte gebruik jy die **skuinshoogte** h_{s}: die hoogte van 'n skuins driehoekige vlak van 'n piramide, of die afstand van die punt van 'n keël tot by die rand van sy basis.\n\n| Voorwerp | Buiteoppervlakte | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Vierkantige piramide (sy b) | b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} | [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H |\n| Keël (radius r) | πr^{2} + πrh_{s} | [[1/3]]πr^{2}H |\n| Sfeer (radius r) | 4πr^{2} | [[4/3]]πr^{3} |\n| Halfsfeer (radius r) | 2πr^{2} (kromme deel) + πr^{2} (plat deel) | [[2/3]]πr^{3} |\n\n**Skuinshoogte met Pythagoras:**\n\n- Keël: h_{s}^{2} = r^{2} + H^{2}\n- Vierkantige piramide: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2}\n\n> **Algemene fout:** H (loodregte hoogte) en h_{s} (skuinshoogte) word verwar. Volume gebruik altyd H; die skuins vlakke van piramides en keëls gebruik h_{s}.\n\n## Saamgestelde voorwerpe\n\n- **Volume:** tel die volumes van die dele bymekaar (of trek af as 'n deel uitgehol is).\n- **Buiteoppervlakte:** tel net die vlakke wat aan die buitekant sigbaar is. Waar twee dele aan mekaar vas is, val daardie vlakke weg. Vir 'n graansilo (silinder met 'n halfsfeer bo-op) is dit die kromme oppervlak van die silinder + 2πr^{2} van die halfsfeer, plus die vloer πr^{2} net as die vraag dit vra.\n\n## Vermenigvuldig afmetings met 'n faktor k\n\n| Verandering | Volume | Buiteoppervlakte |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Een** afmeting × k (bv. net die hoogte) | × k | verander, maar nie met 'n vaste faktor nie – bereken weer |\n| **Alle** afmetings × k | × k^{3} | × k^{2} |\n\nKyk na die formule om te sien wat gebeur. In V = πr^{2}H staan r **gekwadreer**: as net r verdubbel, word V met 2^{2} = 4 vermenigvuldig. As net H verdubbel, verdubbel V.\n\n**Voorbeeld:** 'n Bal se radius word verdriedubbel. Die nuwe volume is 3^{3} = 27 keer die oorspronklike volume, en die nuwe buiteoppervlakte is 3^{2} = 9 keer die oorspronklike buiteoppervlakte.\n\n## Stappe vir enige vraag\n\n1. Skryf die formule neer.\n2. Maak die eenhede dieselfde en vervang. Gebruik die **radius**, nie die middellyn nie.\n3. Hou π in die sakrekenaar en rond eers aan die einde af tot twee desimale plekke.\n4. Skryf die eenheid by (cm^{2} of cm^{3}) en skakel om na ℓ as die vraag dit vra.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** die [[1/3]] by piramides en keëls vergeet; die middellyn as radius gebruik; vergeet om cm^{3} na ℓ om te skakel (÷ 1 000); dink dat die volume net verdubbel as alle afmetings verdubbel (dit word 2^{3} = 8 keer groter).","en":"## Units and conversions\n\n- **Length:** 1 cm = 10 mm; 1 m = 100 cm\n- **Area** (square the factor): 1 cm^{2} = 100 mm^{2}; 1 m^{2} = 10 000 cm^{2}\n- **Volume** (cube the factor): 1 cm^{3} = 1 000 mm^{3}; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 000 cm^{3}\n- **Capacity:** 1 cm^{3} = 1 mℓ; **1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ**; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 ℓ = 1 kℓ\n\n> **Remember!** Make all the dimensions the same unit before you substitute into a formula. Surface area is in square units (cm^{2}, m^{2}) and volume in cubic units (cm^{3}, m^{3}).\n\n## Right prisms and cylinders\n\nA **right prism** has two congruent, parallel bases, and its side faces are rectangles perpendicular to the bases. A **cylinder** works the same way, but its base is a circle.\n\n- Volume = area of the base × perpendicular height (H)\n- Surface area = 2 × area of the base + perimeter of the base × H\n\n| Object | Surface area | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rectangular prism (l, b, h) | 2(lb + lh + bh) | l × b × h |\n| Cube (side s) | 6s^{2} | s^{3} |\n| Triangular prism | 2 × ([[1/2]] × b × h) + (sum of the triangle's sides) × H | [[1/2]] × b × h × H |\n| Cylinder (radius r) | 2πr^{2} + 2πrH | πr^{2}H |\n\nFor the triangular prism, b and h are the base and height of the triangle, and H is the length of the prism.\n\n**Why 2πrH?** If you cut open the curved surface of a cylinder and lay it flat, you get a rectangle. Its length is the circumference of the circle (2πr) and its breadth is H.\n\n## Pyramids, cones and spheres\n\nThe volume of a pyramid or cone is exactly [[1/3]] of the prism or cylinder with the same base and perpendicular height:\n\n- Volume = [[1/3]] × area of the base × H\n\nFor the surface area you use the **slant height** h_{s}: the height of a sloping triangular face of a pyramid, or the distance from the tip of a cone to the edge of its base.\n\n| Object | Surface area | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Square pyramid (side b) | b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} | [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H |\n| Cone (radius r) | πr^{2} + πrh_{s} | [[1/3]]πr^{2}H |\n| Sphere (radius r) | 4πr^{2} | [[4/3]]πr^{3} |\n| Hemisphere (radius r) | 2πr^{2} (curved part) + πr^{2} (flat part) | [[2/3]]πr^{3} |\n\n**Slant height with Pythagoras:**\n\n- Cone: h_{s}^{2} = r^{2} + H^{2}\n- Square pyramid: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2}\n\n> **Common mistake:** mixing up H (perpendicular height) and h_{s} (slant height). Volume always uses H; the sloping faces of pyramids and cones use h_{s}.\n\n## Combined objects\n\n- **Volume:** add the volumes of the parts (or subtract if a part is hollowed out).\n- **Surface area:** only add the faces that are visible on the outside. Where two parts are joined, those faces fall away. For a grain silo (cylinder with a hemisphere on top) it is the curved surface of the cylinder + 2πr^{2} of the hemisphere, plus the floor πr^{2} only if the question asks for it.\n\n## Multiplying dimensions by a factor k\n\n| Change | Volume | Surface area |\n|---|---|---|\n| **One** dimension × k (e.g. only the height) | × k | changes, but not by a fixed factor – recalculate |\n| **All** dimensions × k | × k^{3} | × k^{2} |\n\nLook at the formula to see what happens. In V = πr^{2}H, r is **squared**: if only r doubles, V is multiplied by 2^{2} = 4. If only H doubles, V doubles.\n\n**Example:** A ball's radius is tripled. The new volume is 3^{3} = 27 times the original volume, and the new surface area is 3^{2} = 9 times the original surface area.\n\n## Steps for any question\n\n1. Write down the formula.\n2. Make the units the same and substitute. Use the **radius**, not the diameter.\n3. Keep π in the calculator and only round to two decimal places at the end.\n4. Write the unit (cm^{2} or cm^{3}) and convert to ℓ if the question asks for it.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** forgetting the [[1/3]] for pyramids and cones; using the diameter as the radius; forgetting to convert cm^{3} to ℓ (÷ 1 000); thinking the volume only doubles when all dimensions double (it becomes 2^{3} = 8 times bigger)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Regte prisma","en":"Right prism"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp met twee kongruente, ewewydige basisse en reghoekige syvlakke wat loodreg op die basisse staan.","en":"An object with two congruent, parallel bases and rectangular side faces perpendicular to the bases."}},{"term":{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte","en":"Surface area"},"def":{"af":"Die som van die oppervlaktes van al die buitevlakke van 'n voorwerp, in vierkante eenhede.","en":"The sum of the areas of all the outer faces of an object, in square units."}},{"term":{"af":"Volume","en":"Volume"},"def":{"af":"Die hoeveelheid ruimte wat 'n voorwerp beslaan, in kubieke eenhede (cm³, m³).","en":"The amount of space an object takes up, in cubic units (cm³, m³)."}},{"term":{"af":"Kapasiteit","en":"Capacity"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel 'n houer kan hou, gemeet in mℓ, ℓ of kℓ; 1 000 cm³ = 1 ℓ.","en":"How much a container can hold, measured in mℓ, ℓ or kℓ; 1 000 cm³ = 1 ℓ."}},{"term":{"af":"Loodregte hoogte (H)","en":"Perpendicular height (H)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand van die basis tot die top, gemeet teen 90° met die basis.","en":"The distance from the base to the top, measured at 90° to the base."}},{"term":{"af":"Skuinshoogte","en":"Slant height"},"def":{"af":"Die hoogte langs die skuins vlak van 'n piramide of keël; dit word vir buiteoppervlakte gebruik.","en":"The height along the sloping face of a pyramid or cone; it is used for surface area."}},{"term":{"af":"Sfeer","en":"Sphere"},"def":{"af":"'n Perfek ronde voorwerp waarvan elke punt op die oppervlak dieselfde afstand (r) van die middelpunt is.","en":"A perfectly round object where every point on the surface is the same distance (r) from the centre."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde voorwerp","en":"Combined object"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp wat uit twee of meer eenvoudige voorwerpe bestaan, bv. 'n silinder met 'n halfsfeer bo-op.","en":"An object made up of two or more simple objects, e.g. a cylinder with a hemisphere on top."}},{"term":{"af":"Skaalfaktor k","en":"Scale factor k"},"def":{"af":"Die getal waarmee afmetings vermenigvuldig word; as alle afmetings × k, word oppervlakte × k² en volume × k³.","en":"The number by which dimensions are multiplied; if all dimensions × k, area becomes × k² and volume × k³."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Silinder: buiteoppervlakte, volume en liter","en":"Cylinder: surface area, volume and litres"},"problem":{"af":"'n Silindriese blik vir ingelegde perskes het 'n radius van 5 cm en 'n hoogte van 12 cm. Bereken (a) die totale buiteoppervlakte, (b) die volume en (c) hoeveel liter die blik hou. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"A cylindrical tin for canned peaches has a radius of 5 cm and a height of 12 cm. Calculate (a) the total surface area, (b) the volume and (c) how many litres the tin holds. Round to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Buiteoppervlakte = 2πr^{2} + 2πrH = 2π(5)^{2} + 2π(5)(12)","en":"(a) Surface area = 2πr^{2} + 2πrH = 2π(5)^{2} + 2π(5)(12)"},{"af":"= 50π + 120π = 170π = 534,07 cm^{2}","en":"= 50π + 120π = 170π = 534.07 cm^{2}"},{"af":"(b) Volume = πr^{2}H = π(5)^{2}(12) = 300π = 942,48 cm^{3}","en":"(b) Volume = πr^{2}H = π(5)^{2}(12) = 300π = 942.48 cm^{3}"},{"af":"(c) 1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ, dus 942,48 ÷ 1 000 = 0,94 ℓ","en":"(c) 1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ, so 942.48 ÷ 1 000 = 0.94 ℓ"}],"answer":{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte = 534,07 cm²; volume = 942,48 cm³ ≈ 0,94 ℓ","en":"Surface area = 534.07 cm²; volume = 942.48 cm³ ≈ 0.94 ℓ"}},{"title":{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"},"problem":{"af":"'n Vierkantige piramide het 'n basis met sye van 10 cm en 'n loodregte hoogte van 12 cm. Bereken die skuinshoogte, die totale buiteoppervlakte en die volume.","en":"A square pyramid has a base with sides of 10 cm and a perpendicular height of 12 cm. Calculate the slant height, the total surface area and the volume."},"steps":[{"af":"Skuinshoogte: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2} = 12^{2} + 5^{2} = 144 + 25 = 169 (Pyth.)","en":"Slant height: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2} = 12^{2} + 5^{2} = 144 + 25 = 169 (Pyth)"},{"af":"h_{s} = √169 = 13 cm","en":"h_{s} = √169 = 13 cm"},{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte = b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} = 10^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × 10 × 13","en":"Surface area = b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} = 10^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × 10 × 13"},{"af":"= 100 + 260 = 360 cm^{2}","en":"= 100 + 260 = 360 cm^{2}"},{"af":"Volume = [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H = [[1/3]] × 100 × 12 = 400 cm^{3} (gebruik H, nie h_{s} nie)","en":"Volume = [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H = [[1/3]] × 100 × 12 = 400 cm^{3} (use H, not h_{s})"}],"answer":{"af":"Skuinshoogte = 13 cm; buiteoppervlakte = 360 cm²; volume = 400 cm³","en":"Slant height = 13 cm; surface area = 360 cm²; volume = 400 cm³"}},{"title":{"af":"Saamgestelde voorwerp: 'n graansilo","en":"Combined object: a grain silo"},"problem":{"af":"'n Graansilo op 'n plaas naby Brits bestaan uit 'n silinder met radius 3 m en hoogte 10 m, met 'n halfsfeer (radius 3 m) as dak. Bereken (a) die volume van die silo en (b) die buiteoppervlakte wat geverf moet word (mure en dak, nie die vloer nie).","en":"A grain silo on a farm near Brits consists of a cylinder with radius 3 m and height 10 m, with a hemisphere (radius 3 m) as roof. Calculate (a) the volume of the silo and (b) the outside area that must be painted (walls and roof, not the floor)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Silinder: V = πr^{2}H = π(3)^{2}(10) = 90π","en":"(a) Cylinder: V = πr^{2}H = π(3)^{2}(10) = 90π"},{"af":"Halfsfeer: V = [[2/3]]πr^{3} = [[2/3]]π(3)^{3} = 18π","en":"Hemisphere: V = [[2/3]]πr^{3} = [[2/3]]π(3)^{3} = 18π"},{"af":"Totale volume = 90π + 18π = 108π = 339,29 m^{3}","en":"Total volume = 90π + 18π = 108π = 339.29 m^{3}"},{"af":"(b) Mure (kromme silinder): 2πrH = 2π(3)(10) = 60π. Dak (kromme halfsfeer): 2πr^{2} = 2π(3)^{2} = 18π","en":"(b) Walls (curved cylinder): 2πrH = 2π(3)(10) = 60π. Roof (curved hemisphere): 2πr^{2} = 2π(3)^{2} = 18π"},{"af":"Die sirkel waar die dak op die silinder sit, en die vloer, word nie geverf nie. Oppervlakte = 60π + 18π = 78π = 245,04 m^{2}","en":"The circle where the roof sits on the cylinder, and the floor, are not painted. Area = 60π + 18π = 78π = 245.04 m^{2}"}],"answer":{"af":"Volume = 339,29 m³; oppervlakte om te verf = 245,04 m²","en":"Volume = 339.29 m³; area to paint = 245.04 m²"}},{"title":{"af":"Die effek van 'n skaalfaktor","en":"The effect of a scale factor"},"problem":{"af":"'n Reghoekige doos is 4 cm × 3 cm × 2 cm. (a) Al drie afmetings word met 3 vermenigvuldig. Bereken die nuwe volume en buiteoppervlakte. (b) Wat gebeur as net die hoogte met 3 vermenigvuldig word?","en":"A rectangular box is 4 cm × 3 cm × 2 cm. (a) All three dimensions are multiplied by 3. Calculate the new volume and surface area. (b) What happens if only the height is multiplied by 3?"},"steps":[{"af":"Oorspronklik: V = 4 × 3 × 2 = 24 cm^{3}; A = 2(4 × 3 + 4 × 2 + 3 × 2) = 2(12 + 8 + 6) = 52 cm^{2}","en":"Original: V = 4 × 3 × 2 = 24 cm^{3}; A = 2(4 × 3 + 4 × 2 + 3 × 2) = 2(12 + 8 + 6) = 52 cm^{2}"},{"af":"(a) Alle afmetings × 3, dus volume × 3^{3} = 27: V = 24 × 27 = 648 cm^{3}","en":"(a) All dimensions × 3, so volume × 3^{3} = 27: V = 24 × 27 = 648 cm^{3}"},{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte × 3^{2} = 9: A = 52 × 9 = 468 cm^{2}","en":"Surface area × 3^{2} = 9: A = 52 × 9 = 468 cm^{2}"},{"af":"Kontroleer met die nuwe doos 12 × 9 × 6: V = 648 cm^{3} ✓ en A = 2(108 + 72 + 54) = 468 cm^{2} ✓","en":"Check with the new box 12 × 9 × 6: V = 648 cm^{3} ✓ and A = 2(108 + 72 + 54) = 468 cm^{2} ✓"},{"af":"(b) Net die hoogte × 3 (4 × 3 × 6): V = 72 cm^{3} = 3 × 24, maar A = 2(12 + 24 + 18) = 108 cm^{2}, wat nie 'n eenvoudige veelvoud van 52 is nie","en":"(b) Only the height × 3 (4 × 3 × 6): V = 72 cm^{3} = 3 × 24, but A = 2(12 + 24 + 18) = 108 cm^{2}, which is not a simple multiple of 52"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) V = 648 cm³ (× 27); A = 468 cm² (× 9). (b) V = 72 cm³ (× 3); A = 108 cm²","en":"(a) V = 648 cm³ (× 27); A = 468 cm² (× 9). (b) V = 72 cm³ (× 3); A = 108 cm²"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter formule gee die volume van 'n keël met radius r en loodregte hoogte H?","en":"Which formula gives the volume of a cone with radius r and perpendicular height H?"},"options":[{"af":"πr²H","en":"πr²H"},{"af":"⅓πr²H","en":"⅓πr²H"},{"af":"πr² + πr × skuinshoogte","en":"πr² + πr × slant height"},{"af":"(4/3)πr³","en":"(4/3)πr³"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Keël is ⅓ van die silinder met dieselfde basis en hoogte: V = ⅓πr²H. πr²H is die silinder, πr² + πr × skuinshoogte is die keël se buiteoppervlakte, en (4/3)πr³ is 'n sfeer.","en":"A cone is ⅓ of the cylinder with the same base and height: V = ⅓πr²H. πr²H is the cylinder, πr² + πr × slant height is the cone's surface area, and (4/3)πr³ is a sphere."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Houer met 'n volume van 1 000 cm³ hou presies 1 ℓ.","en":"A container with a volume of 1 000 cm³ holds exactly 1 ℓ."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 1 cm³ = 1 mℓ, dus 1 000 cm³ = 1 000 mℓ = 1 ℓ. Om cm³ na ℓ om te skakel, deel jy deur 1 000.","en":"True. 1 cm³ = 1 mℓ, so 1 000 cm³ = 1 000 mℓ = 1 ℓ. To convert cm³ to ℓ, divide by 1 000."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voorwerp by sy volumeformule.","en":"Match each object to its volume formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Silinder","en":"Cylinder"},"r":{"af":"πr²H","en":"πr²H"}},{"l":{"af":"Keël","en":"Cone"},"r":{"af":"⅓πr²H","en":"⅓πr²H"}},{"l":{"af":"Sfeer","en":"Sphere"},"r":{"af":"(4/3)πr³","en":"(4/3)πr³"}},{"l":{"af":"Reghoekige prisma","en":"Rectangular prism"},"r":{"af":"l × b × h","en":"l × b × h"}},{"l":{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"},"r":{"af":"⅓ × b² × H","en":"⅓ × b² × H"}}],"explain":{"af":"Prismas en silinders: basis × hoogte. Piramides en keëls: ⅓ × basis × hoogte. Sfeer: (4/3)πr³.","en":"Prisms and cylinders: base × height. Pyramids and cones: ⅓ × base × height. Sphere: (4/3)πr³."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As al die afmetings van 'n voorwerp met k vermenigvuldig word, word die volume met ___ vermenigvuldig.","en":"If all the dimensions of an object are multiplied by k, the volume is multiplied by ___."},"answers":{"af":["k³","k^3","k^{3}","k3","k×k×k","k*k*k","kkk"],"en":["k³","k^3","k^{3}","k3","k×k×k","k*k*k","kkk"]},"explain":{"af":"Volume het drie afmetings (lengte × breedte × hoogte), dus word dit met k × k × k = k³ vermenigvuldig. Buiteoppervlakte het twee afmetings en word met k² vermenigvuldig.","en":"Volume has three dimensions (length × breadth × height), so it is multiplied by k × k × k = k³. Surface area has two dimensions and is multiplied by k²."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Silinder het 'n radius van 7 cm en 'n hoogte van 10 cm. Die volume is ___ cm³ (rond af tot twee desimale plekke).","en":"A cylinder has a radius of 7 cm and a height of 10 cm. The volume is ___ cm³ (round to two decimal places)."},"answers":{"af":["1539,38","1 539,38","1539.38","1539,38 cm³","1539,38cm3"],"en":["1539.38","1 539.38","1539,38","1539.38 cm³","1539.38cm3"]},"explain":{"af":"V = πr²H = π × 7² × 10 = 490π = 1 539,38 cm³.","en":"V = πr²H = π × 7² × 10 = 490π = 1 539.38 cm³."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Bal het 'n middellyn van 12 cm. Wat is die buiteoppervlakte van die bal?","en":"A ball has a diameter of 12 cm. What is the surface area of the ball?"},"options":[{"af":"113,10 cm²","en":"113.10 cm²"},{"af":"904,78 cm²","en":"904.78 cm²"},{"af":"1 809,56 cm²","en":"1 809.56 cm²"},{"af":"452,39 cm²","en":"452.39 cm²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"r = 12 ÷ 2 = 6 cm. Buiteoppervlakte = 4πr² = 4π × 36 = 144π = 452,39 cm². 1 809,56 gebruik die middellyn as radius, 113,10 vergeet die 4, en 904,78 is die volume (4/3)πr³.","en":"r = 12 ÷ 2 = 6 cm. Surface area = 4πr² = 4π × 36 = 144π = 452.39 cm². 1 809.56 uses the diameter as the radius, 113.10 forgets the 4, and 904.78 is the volume (4/3)πr³."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Watertenk op 'n plaas by Hartbeespoortdam het 'n volume van 2,4 m³. Hoeveel liter water hou dit?","en":"A water tank on a farm at Hartbeespoort Dam has a volume of 2.4 m³. How many litres of water does it hold?"},"options":[{"af":"240 ℓ","en":"240 ℓ"},{"af":"2 400 ℓ","en":"2 400 ℓ"},{"af":"24 000 ℓ","en":"24 000 ℓ"},{"af":"2 400 000 ℓ","en":"2 400 000 ℓ"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"1 m³ = 1 000 ℓ, dus 2,4 × 1 000 = 2 400 ℓ. (Of: 2,4 m³ = 2 400 000 cm³, en ÷ 1 000 gee 2 400 ℓ. 2 400 000 vergeet die ÷ 1 000.)","en":"1 m³ = 1 000 ℓ, so 2.4 × 1 000 = 2 400 ℓ. (Or: 2.4 m³ = 2 400 000 cm³, and ÷ 1 000 gives 2 400 ℓ. 2 400 000 forgets the ÷ 1 000.)"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Keël het 'n radius van 3 cm en 'n loodregte hoogte van 4 cm. Die totale buiteoppervlakte is ___ cm² (rond af tot twee desimale plekke).","en":"A cone has a radius of 3 cm and a perpendicular height of 4 cm. The total surface area is ___ cm² (round to two decimal places)."},"answers":{"af":["75,40","75,4","75.40","75.4","75,40 cm²","24π"],"en":["75.40","75.4","75,40","75,4","75.40 cm²","24π"]},"explain":{"af":"Skuinshoogte² = 3² + 4² = 25, dus is die skuinshoogte 5 cm. Buiteoppervlakte = πr² + πr × skuinshoogte = 9π + 15π = 24π = 75,40 cm². Moenie H = 4 in die buiteoppervlakte gebruik nie.","en":"Slant height² = 3² + 4² = 25, so the slant height is 5 cm. Surface area = πr² + πr × slant height = 9π + 15π = 24π = 75.40 cm². Do not use H = 4 in the surface area."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Driehoekige prisma het 'n reghoekige driehoek as basis met reghoeksye 6 cm en 8 cm (skuinssy 10 cm). Die prisma is 15 cm lank. Wat is die volume?","en":"A triangular prism has a right-angled triangle as base with legs 6 cm and 8 cm (hypotenuse 10 cm). The prism is 15 cm long. What is the volume?"},"options":[{"af":"360 cm³","en":"360 cm³"},{"af":"720 cm³","en":"720 cm³"},{"af":"120 cm³","en":"120 cm³"},{"af":"408 cm³","en":"408 cm³"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"V = oppervlakte van die driehoek × lengte = (½ × 6 × 8) × 15 = 24 × 15 = 360 cm³. 720 vergeet die ½, 120 deel verkeerdelik deur 3 (dis nie 'n piramide nie), en 408 is die buiteoppervlakte se getal.","en":"V = area of the triangle × length = (½ × 6 × 8) × 15 = 24 × 15 = 360 cm³. 720 forgets the ½, 120 wrongly divides by 3 (it is not a pyramid), and 408 is the surface area's number."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy net die radius van 'n silinder verdubbel (die hoogte bly dieselfde), verdubbel die volume ook.","en":"If you double only the radius of a cylinder (the height stays the same), the volume also doubles."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. In V = πr²H is r gekwadreer, dus word die volume met 2² = 4 vermenigvuldig. Net as die hoogte verdubbel, verdubbel die volume.","en":"False. In V = πr²H, r is squared, so the volume is multiplied by 2² = 4. Only when the height doubles does the volume double."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Houtmodel van 'n vuurpyl bestaan uit 'n silinder (middellyn 4 cm, hoogte 10 cm) met 'n keël (dieselfde middellyn, loodregte hoogte 3 cm) bo-op. Wat is die totale volume?","en":"A wooden model of a rocket consists of a cylinder (diameter 4 cm, height 10 cm) with a cone (same diameter, perpendicular height 3 cm) on top. What is the total volume?"},"options":[{"af":"125,66 cm³","en":"125.66 cm³"},{"af":"163,36 cm³","en":"163.36 cm³"},{"af":"138,23 cm³","en":"138.23 cm³"},{"af":"552,92 cm³","en":"552.92 cm³"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"r = 2 cm. Silinder: π × 2² × 10 = 40π. Keël: ⅓ × π × 2² × 3 = 4π. Totaal = 44π = 138,23 cm³. 163,36 vergeet die ⅓, 125,66 vergeet die keël, en 552,92 gebruik die middellyn as radius.","en":"r = 2 cm. Cylinder: π × 2² × 10 = 40π. Cone: ⅓ × π × 2² × 3 = 4π. Total = 44π = 138.23 cm³. 163.36 forgets the ⅓, 125.66 forgets the cone, and 552.92 uses the diameter as the radius."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Kubus het 'n buiteoppervlakte van 54 cm². Elke sy word verdriedubbel. Die nuwe buiteoppervlakte is ___ cm².","en":"A cube has a surface area of 54 cm². Each side is tripled. The new surface area is ___ cm²."},"answers":{"af":["486","486 cm²"],"en":["486","486 cm²"]},"explain":{"af":"Alle afmetings × 3, dus buiteoppervlakte × 3² = 9: 54 × 9 = 486 cm². (Kontroleer: 6s² = 54 gee s = 3; nuwe s = 9; 6 × 81 = 486.)","en":"All dimensions × 3, so surface area × 3² = 9: 54 × 9 = 486 cm². (Check: 6s² = 54 gives s = 3; new s = 9; 6 × 81 = 486.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Halfsfeervormige bak het 'n binneradius van 9 cm. Hoeveel liter hou die bak as dit vol is?","en":"A hemispherical bowl has an inner radius of 9 cm. How many litres does the bowl hold when it is full?"},"options":[{"af":"3,05 ℓ","en":"3.05 ℓ"},{"af":"15,27 ℓ","en":"15.27 ℓ"},{"af":"1 526,81 ℓ","en":"1 526.81 ℓ"},{"af":"1,53 ℓ","en":"1.53 ℓ"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"V = ⅔πr³ = ⅔ × π × 9³ = 486π = 1 526,81 cm³. Deel deur 1 000: 1,53 ℓ. 3,05 ℓ is 'n hele sfeer, 15,27 ℓ deel deur 100 in plaas van 1 000, en 1 526,81 ℓ vergeet om om te skakel.","en":"V = ⅔πr³ = ⅔ × π × 9³ = 486π = 1 526.81 cm³. Divide by 1 000: 1.53 ℓ. 3.05 ℓ is a whole sphere, 15.27 ℓ divides by 100 instead of 1 000, and 1 526.81 ℓ forgets to convert."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Sitrusplaas naby Brits tap lemoensap uit 'n tenk van 500 ℓ in silindriese bottels met 'n binnemiddellyn van 6 cm en 'n hoogte van 15 cm. Hoeveel bottels kan heeltemal vol gemaak word?","en":"A citrus farm near Brits bottles orange juice from a 500 ℓ tank into cylindrical bottles with an inner diameter of 6 cm and a height of 15 cm. How many bottles can be filled completely?"},"options":[{"af":"1","en":"1"},{"af":"294","en":"294"},{"af":"1 178","en":"1 178"},{"af":"1 179","en":"1 179"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"r = 3 cm. Een bottel: V = π × 3² × 15 = 135π = 424,12 cm³. Tenk: 500 ℓ = 500 000 cm³. 500 000 ÷ 424,12 = 1 178,9, dus 1 178 vol bottels – rond áf, want die 1 179ste bottel word nie vol nie. 294 gebruik die middellyn as radius, en 1 vergeet om ℓ na cm³ om te skakel.","en":"r = 3 cm. One bottle: V = π × 3² × 15 = 135π = 424.12 cm³. Tank: 500 ℓ = 500 000 cm³. 500 000 ÷ 424.12 = 1 178.9, so 1 178 full bottles – round down, because the 1 179th bottle will not be full. 294 uses the diameter as the radius, and 1 forgets to convert ℓ to cm³."}}]},{"id":"w10-t4-waarskynlikheid","title":{"af":"Waarskynlikheid","en":"Probability"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal waarskynlikhede en relatiewe frekwensies kan bereken, die optelreël kan gebruik en Venn-diagramme met twee gebeurtenisse kan invul en lees.","en":"You will be able to calculate probabilities and relative frequencies, use the addition rule and fill in and read Venn diagrams with two events."},"summary":{"af":"## Basiese begrippe\n\n- **Eksperiment:** 'n handeling met 'n onsekere uitkoms, bv. om 'n dobbelsteen te gooi.\n- **Uitkoms:** een moontlike resultaat van die eksperiment.\n- **Steekproefruimte (S):** die versameling van álle moontlike uitkomste. n(S) is die aantal uitkomste. Vir een dobbelsteen is S = {1; 2; 3; 4; 5; 6} en n(S) = 6.\n- **Gebeurtenis (E):** 'n deelversameling van S. Bv. E = \"'n ewe getal\" = {2; 4; 6}, dus n(E) = 3.\n\n## Teoretiese waarskynlikheid\n\nAs al die uitkomste ewe waarskynlik is, is\n\nP(E) = [[n(E)/n(S)]]\n\n- 0 ≤ P(E) ≤ 1. P(E) = 0 beteken die gebeurtenis is onmoontlik; P(E) = 1 beteken dit is seker.\n- Jy kan die antwoord as 'n breuk, desimale getal of persentasie skryf: [[3/8]] = 0,375 = 37,5%.\n\n**Twee stappe:** 'n Draaiskyf met twee gelyke dele, rooi (R) en blou (B), word twee keer gedraai. S = {RR; RB; BR; BB}, dus n(S) = 4. RB en BR is **verskillende** uitkomste, daarom is P(een rooi en een blou) = [[2/4]] = [[1/2]], nie [[1/3]] nie.\n\n## Relatiewe frekwensie\n\nAs jy 'n eksperiment werklik uitvoer, bereken jy die **relatiewe frekwensie** (eksperimentele waarskynlikheid):\n\nRelatiewe frekwensie = [[aantal kere wat E plaasvind/totale aantal proewe]]\n\nHoe meer proewe jy doen, hoe nader kom die relatiewe frekwensie aan die teoretiese waarskynlikheid. As 'n muntstuk 50 keer opgegooi word en 28 keer kop land, is die relatiewe frekwensie [[28/50]] = 0,56, terwyl die teoretiese waarskynlikheid 0,5 is.\n\n## Onderling uitsluitende gebeurtenisse\n\nA en B is **onderling uitsluitend** as hulle nie gelyktydig kan plaasvind nie – hulle het geen gemeenskaplike uitkomste nie. Dan is P(A en B) = 0 en\n\nP(A of B) = P(A) + P(B)\n\nBv. by een dobbelsteen: A = {1; 2} en B = {5; 6}.\n\n## Komplementêre gebeurtenisse\n\nDie komplement van A is \"nie A\" (ook geskryf as A′): al die uitkomste in S wat nie in A is nie. A en nie A is onderling uitsluitend **en** saam vul hulle die hele steekproefruimte. Daarom is\n\nP(nie A) = 1 − P(A)\n\n> **Onthou!** Komplementêre gebeurtenisse is altyd onderling uitsluitend, maar onderling uitsluitende gebeurtenisse is nie altyd komplementêr nie. {1; 2} en {5; 6} is onderling uitsluitend, maar 3 en 4 val buite albei.\n\n## Die optelreël\n\nVir enige twee gebeurtenisse A en B geld:\n\nP(A of B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A en B)\n\n- \"A of B\" (A ∪ B) beteken A, of B, of albei.\n- \"A en B\" (A ∩ B) beteken albei gelyktydig.\n- Ons trek P(A en B) af omdat die oorvleueling in P(A) én in P(B) getel is – anders tel ons dit twee keer.\n\nAs drie van die vier waardes gegee is, kan jy die vierde bereken. As jy P(A en B) = 0 kry, is A en B onderling uitsluitend.\n\n## Venn-diagramme met twee gebeurtenisse\n\n'n Reghoek stel S voor, met twee oorvleuelende sirkels A en B binne-in. Daar is vier gebiede:\n\n| Gebied | Betekenis | Aantal |\n|---|---|---|\n| Oorvleueling | A en B | n(A en B) |\n| Slegs A | in A, maar nie in B nie | n(A) − n(A en B) |\n| Slegs B | in B, maar nie in A nie | n(B) − n(A en B) |\n| Buite albei sirkels | nie A nie en nie B nie | n(S) − n(A of B) |\n\n**Stappe om 'n Venn-diagram in te vul:**\n\n1. Begin altyd by die oorvleueling (A en B).\n2. Trek af om \"slegs A\" en \"slegs B\" te kry.\n3. Trek die som van die drie gebiede van n(S) af vir die gebied buite die sirkels.\n4. Kontroleer dat al vier gebiede saam n(S) gee (of 1 as jy met waarskynlikhede werk).\n5. As die oorvleueling onbekend is, noem dit x en stel 'n vergelyking op: som van al vier gebiede = n(S).\n\n'n Waarskynlikheid uit 'n Venn-diagram is P = [[aantal in die gebied/n(S)]].\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Om n(A) in die \"slegs A\"-gebied te skryf in plaas van n(A) − n(A en B).\n- Om die gebied buite albei sirkels te vergeet.\n- Om P(A) + P(B) te gebruik as A en B oorvleuel – dan tel jy die oorvleueling twee keer.\n- Om RB en BR as een uitkoms te tel.\n- 'n Waarskynlikheid groter as 1 of kleiner as 0 is altyd verkeerd – gaan terug en soek die fout.","en":"## Basic concepts\n\n- **Experiment:** an action with an uncertain outcome, e.g. rolling a die.\n- **Outcome:** one possible result of the experiment.\n- **Sample space (S):** the set of all possible outcomes. n(S) is the number of outcomes. For one die S = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6} and n(S) = 6.\n- **Event (E):** a subset of S. E.g. E = \"an even number\" = {2, 4, 6}, so n(E) = 3.\n\n## Theoretical probability\n\nIf all the outcomes are equally likely, then\n\nP(E) = [[n(E)/n(S)]]\n\n- 0 ≤ P(E) ≤ 1. P(E) = 0 means the event is impossible; P(E) = 1 means it is certain.\n- You can write the answer as a fraction, decimal or percentage: [[3/8]] = 0.375 = 37.5%.\n\n**Two steps:** A spinner with two equal parts, red (R) and blue (B), is spun twice. S = {RR, RB, BR, BB}, so n(S) = 4. RB and BR are **different** outcomes, so P(one red and one blue) = [[2/4]] = [[1/2]], not [[1/3]].\n\n## Relative frequency\n\nWhen you actually carry out an experiment, you calculate the **relative frequency** (experimental probability):\n\nRelative frequency = [[number of times E occurs/total number of trials]]\n\nThe more trials you do, the closer the relative frequency gets to the theoretical probability. If a coin is tossed 50 times and lands heads 28 times, the relative frequency is [[28/50]] = 0.56, while the theoretical probability is 0.5.\n\n## Mutually exclusive events\n\nA and B are **mutually exclusive** if they cannot happen at the same time – they have no outcomes in common. Then P(A and B) = 0 and\n\nP(A or B) = P(A) + P(B)\n\nE.g. for one die: A = {1, 2} and B = {5, 6}.\n\n## Complementary events\n\nThe complement of A is \"not A\" (also written A′): all the outcomes in S that are not in A. A and not A are mutually exclusive **and** together they fill the whole sample space. Therefore\n\nP(not A) = 1 − P(A)\n\n> **Remember!** Complementary events are always mutually exclusive, but mutually exclusive events are not always complementary. {1, 2} and {5, 6} are mutually exclusive, but 3 and 4 fall outside both.\n\n## The addition rule\n\nFor any two events A and B:\n\nP(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B)\n\n- \"A or B\" (A ∪ B) means A, or B, or both.\n- \"A and B\" (A ∩ B) means both at the same time.\n- We subtract P(A and B) because the overlap is counted in P(A) and in P(B) – otherwise we count it twice.\n\nIf three of the four values are given, you can calculate the fourth. If you get P(A and B) = 0, A and B are mutually exclusive.\n\n## Venn diagrams with two events\n\nA rectangle represents S, with two overlapping circles A and B inside it. There are four regions:\n\n| Region | Meaning | Number |\n|---|---|---|\n| Overlap | A and B | n(A and B) |\n| Only A | in A, but not in B | n(A) − n(A and B) |\n| Only B | in B, but not in A | n(B) − n(A and B) |\n| Outside both circles | not A and not B | n(S) − n(A or B) |\n\n**Steps to fill in a Venn diagram:**\n\n1. Always start with the overlap (A and B).\n2. Subtract to get \"only A\" and \"only B\".\n3. Subtract the sum of the three regions from n(S) for the region outside the circles.\n4. Check that all four regions together give n(S) (or 1 if you are working with probabilities).\n5. If the overlap is unknown, call it x and set up an equation: sum of all four regions = n(S).\n\nA probability from a Venn diagram is P = [[number in the region/n(S)]].\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Writing n(A) in the \"only A\" region instead of n(A) − n(A and B).\n- Forgetting the region outside both circles.\n- Using P(A) + P(B) when A and B overlap – then you count the overlap twice.\n- Counting RB and BR as one outcome.\n- A probability greater than 1 or less than 0 is always wrong – go back and find the mistake."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Steekproefruimte (S)","en":"Sample space (S)"},"def":{"af":"Die versameling van alle moontlike uitkomste van 'n eksperiment.","en":"The set of all possible outcomes of an experiment."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitkoms","en":"Outcome"},"def":{"af":"Een moontlike resultaat van 'n eksperiment.","en":"One possible result of an experiment."}},{"term":{"af":"Gebeurtenis","en":"Event"},"def":{"af":"'n Deelversameling van die steekproefruimte, bv. 'gooi 'n ewe getal'.","en":"A subset of the sample space, e.g. 'roll an even number'."}},{"term":{"af":"Teoretiese waarskynlikheid","en":"Theoretical probability"},"def":{"af":"P(E) = n(E)/n(S) as al die uitkomste ewe waarskynlik is.","en":"P(E) = n(E)/n(S) when all the outcomes are equally likely."}},{"term":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie","en":"Relative frequency"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal kere wat 'n gebeurtenis in 'n eksperiment plaasvind gedeel deur die totale aantal proewe.","en":"The number of times an event occurs in an experiment divided by the total number of trials."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend","en":"Mutually exclusive"},"def":{"af":"Gebeurtenisse wat nie gelyktydig kan plaasvind nie; P(A en B) = 0.","en":"Events that cannot happen at the same time; P(A and B) = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Komplementêre gebeurtenisse","en":"Complementary events"},"def":{"af":"Twee onderling uitsluitende gebeurtenisse wat saam die hele steekproefruimte vul; P(nie A) = 1 − P(A).","en":"Two mutually exclusive events that together fill the whole sample space; P(not A) = 1 − P(A)."}},{"term":{"af":"Venn-diagram","en":"Venn diagram"},"def":{"af":"'n Reghoek (die steekproefruimte) met sirkels wat gebeurtenisse en hul oorvleueling voorstel.","en":"A rectangle (the sample space) with circles that represent events and their overlap."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Eenvoudige en komplementêre waarskynlikheid","en":"Simple and complementary probability"},"problem":{"af":"'n Krat van 'n sitrusplaas naby Brits bevat 12 lemoene, 5 nartjies en 3 suurlemoene. Een vrug word lukraak uitgehaal. Bereken (a) P(lemoen), (b) P(nie 'n suurlemoen nie) en (c) P(nartjie of suurlemoen).","en":"A crate from a citrus farm near Brits contains 12 oranges, 5 naartjies and 3 lemons. One fruit is taken out at random. Calculate (a) P(orange), (b) P(not a lemon) and (c) P(naartjie or lemon)."},"steps":[{"af":"n(S) = 12 + 5 + 3 = 20","en":"n(S) = 12 + 5 + 3 = 20"},{"af":"(a) P(lemoen) = [[12/20]] = [[3/5]] = 0,6","en":"(a) P(orange) = [[12/20]] = [[3/5]] = 0.6"},{"af":"(b) P(suurlemoen) = [[3/20]], dus P(nie suurlemoen) = 1 − [[3/20]] = [[17/20]] = 0,85 (komplementêre gebeurtenisse)","en":"(b) P(lemon) = [[3/20]], so P(not lemon) = 1 − [[3/20]] = [[17/20]] = 0.85 (complementary events)"},{"af":"(c) 'n Vrug kan nie tegelyk 'n nartjie en 'n suurlemoen wees nie, dus is die gebeurtenisse onderling uitsluitend: P = [[5/20]] + [[3/20]] = [[8/20]] = [[2/5]] = 0,4","en":"(c) A fruit cannot be a naartjie and a lemon at the same time, so the events are mutually exclusive: P = [[5/20]] + [[3/20]] = [[8/20]] = [[2/5]] = 0.4"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0,6  (b) 0,85  (c) 0,4","en":"(a) 0.6  (b) 0.85  (c) 0.4"}},{"title":{"af":"Venn-diagram met 'n onbekende","en":"Venn diagram with an unknown"},"problem":{"af":"In 'n klas van 30 leerders in Brits speel 18 rugby (R) en 15 krieket (K). 4 leerders speel geen van die twee nie. Bereken hoeveel albei speel, en bepaal dan P(slegs rugby) en P(R of K).","en":"In a class of 30 learners in Brits, 18 play rugby (R) and 15 play cricket (K). 4 learners play neither. Calculate how many play both, then find P(only rugby) and P(R or K)."},"steps":[{"af":"Laat x = n(R en K). Dan is slegs R = 18 − x, slegs K = 15 − x en buite die sirkels = 4","en":"Let x = n(R and K). Then only R = 18 − x, only K = 15 − x and outside the circles = 4"},{"af":"Al vier gebiede tel op tot 30: (18 − x) + x + (15 − x) + 4 = 30, dus 37 − x = 30 en x = 7","en":"All four regions add up to 30: (18 − x) + x + (15 − x) + 4 = 30, so 37 − x = 30 and x = 7"},{"af":"Gebiede: slegs R = 11, albei = 7, slegs K = 8, geen = 4. Kontroleer: 11 + 7 + 8 + 4 = 30 ✓","en":"Regions: only R = 11, both = 7, only K = 8, neither = 4. Check: 11 + 7 + 8 + 4 = 30 ✓"},{"af":"P(slegs rugby) = [[11/30]]","en":"P(only rugby) = [[11/30]]"},{"af":"P(R of K) = [[11 + 7 + 8/30]] = [[26/30]] = [[13/15]]. Kontroleer met die optelreël: [[18/30]] + [[15/30]] − [[7/30]] = [[26/30]] ✓","en":"P(R or K) = [[11 + 7 + 8/30]] = [[26/30]] = [[13/15]]. Check with the addition rule: [[18/30]] + [[15/30]] − [[7/30]] = [[26/30]] ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"7 leerders speel albei; P(slegs rugby) = 11/30; P(R of K) = 13/15","en":"7 learners play both; P(only rugby) = 11/30; P(R or K) = 13/15"}},{"title":{"af":"Die optelreël","en":"The addition rule"},"problem":{"af":"P(A) = 0,45, P(B) = 0,3 en P(A of B) = 0,6. Bereken (a) P(A en B), (b) of A en B onderling uitsluitend is, (c) P(nie A nie en nie B nie) en (d) P(slegs A).","en":"P(A) = 0.45, P(B) = 0.3 and P(A or B) = 0.6. Calculate (a) P(A and B), (b) whether A and B are mutually exclusive, (c) P(not A and not B) and (d) P(only A)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) P(A of B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A en B), dus 0,6 = 0,45 + 0,3 − P(A en B)","en":"(a) P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B), so 0.6 = 0.45 + 0.3 − P(A and B)"},{"af":"P(A en B) = 0,75 − 0,6 = 0,15","en":"P(A and B) = 0.75 − 0.6 = 0.15"},{"af":"(b) P(A en B) = 0,15 ≠ 0, dus is A en B NIE onderling uitsluitend nie","en":"(b) P(A and B) = 0.15 ≠ 0, so A and B are NOT mutually exclusive"},{"af":"(c) P(nie A nie en nie B nie) = 1 − P(A of B) = 1 − 0,6 = 0,4","en":"(c) P(not A and not B) = 1 − P(A or B) = 1 − 0.6 = 0.4"},{"af":"(d) P(slegs A) = P(A) − P(A en B) = 0,45 − 0,15 = 0,3","en":"(d) P(only A) = P(A) − P(A and B) = 0.45 − 0.15 = 0.3"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0,15  (b) Nee  (c) 0,4  (d) 0,3","en":"(a) 0.15  (b) No  (c) 0.4  (d) 0.3"}},{"title":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie teenoor teoretiese waarskynlikheid","en":"Relative frequency versus theoretical probability"},"problem":{"af":"'n Dobbelsteen word 120 keer gegooi. Die resultate: 1 → 18 keer, 2 → 22, 3 → 17, 4 → 23, 5 → 19, 6 → 21. Bereken die relatiewe frekwensie van (a) 'n 6 en (b) 'n ewe getal, en vergelyk elkeen met die teoretiese waarskynlikheid.","en":"A die is rolled 120 times. The results: 1 → 18 times, 2 → 22, 3 → 17, 4 → 23, 5 → 19, 6 → 21. Calculate the relative frequency of (a) a 6 and (b) an even number, and compare each with the theoretical probability."},"steps":[{"af":"Kontroleer die totaal: 18 + 22 + 17 + 23 + 19 + 21 = 120 ✓","en":"Check the total: 18 + 22 + 17 + 23 + 19 + 21 = 120 ✓"},{"af":"(a) Relatiewe frekwensie van 'n 6 = [[21/120]] = 0,175. Teoreties: P(6) = [[1/6]] ≈ 0,17","en":"(a) Relative frequency of a 6 = [[21/120]] = 0.175. Theoretical: P(6) = [[1/6]] ≈ 0.17"},{"af":"(b) Ewe getalle: 22 + 23 + 21 = 66, dus relatiewe frekwensie = [[66/120]] = 0,55","en":"(b) Even numbers: 22 + 23 + 21 = 66, so relative frequency = [[66/120]] = 0.55"},{"af":"Teoreties: P(ewe) = [[3/6]] = 0,5","en":"Theoretical: P(even) = [[3/6]] = 0.5"},{"af":"Die waardes is naby aan mekaar, maar nie gelyk nie. Met meer gooie sal die relatiewe frekwensies nader aan die teoretiese waarskynlikhede kom.","en":"The values are close, but not equal. With more rolls the relative frequencies will get closer to the theoretical probabilities."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0,175 teenoor ≈ 0,17  (b) 0,55 teenoor 0,5","en":"(a) 0.175 versus ≈ 0.17  (b) 0.55 versus 0.5"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Draaiskyf met twee gelyke dele, rooi (R) en blou (B), word twee keer gedraai. Wat is die steekproefruimte?","en":"A spinner with two equal parts, red (R) and blue (B), is spun twice. What is the sample space?"},"options":[{"af":"{RR; RB; BB}","en":"{RR, RB, BB}"},{"af":"{R; B}","en":"{R, B}"},{"af":"{RR; RB; BR; BB}","en":"{RR, RB, BR, BB}"},{"af":"{RB; BR}","en":"{RB, BR}"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Eers rooi dan blou (RB) en eers blou dan rooi (BR) is twee verskillende uitkomste, dus is n(S) = 4. {RR; RB; BB} is die klassieke fout wat RB en BR as een tel.","en":"First red then blue (RB) and first blue then red (BR) are two different outcomes, so n(S) = 4. {RR, RB, BB} is the classic mistake that counts RB and BR as one."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die waarskynlikheid van enige gebeurtenis lê tussen 0 en 1 (0 en 1 ingesluit).","en":"The probability of any event lies between 0 and 1 (0 and 1 included)."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 0 beteken onmoontlik en 1 beteken seker. 'n Antwoord soos 1,2 of −0,3 wys dat jy 'n fout gemaak het.","en":"True. 0 means impossible and 1 means certain. An answer such as 1.2 or −0.3 shows that you made a mistake."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each term to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Steekproefruimte","en":"Sample space"},"r":{"af":"Die versameling van alle moontlike uitkomste","en":"The set of all possible outcomes"}},{"l":{"af":"Gebeurtenis","en":"Event"},"r":{"af":"'n Deelversameling van die steekproefruimte","en":"A subset of the sample space"}},{"l":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend","en":"Mutually exclusive"},"r":{"af":"Die gebeurtenisse kan nie gelyktydig plaasvind nie","en":"The events cannot happen at the same time"}},{"l":{"af":"Komplementêre gebeurtenisse","en":"Complementary events"},"r":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend, en saam vul hulle die hele steekproefruimte","en":"Mutually exclusive, and together they fill the whole sample space"}},{"l":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie","en":"Relative frequency"},"r":{"af":"Aantal kere wat die gebeurtenis plaasvind ÷ totale aantal proewe","en":"Number of times the event occurs ÷ total number of trials"}}],"explain":{"af":"Let op die verskil: komplementêre gebeurtenisse is onderling uitsluitend én dek saam die hele steekproefruimte.","en":"Note the difference: complementary events are mutually exclusive and together cover the whole sample space."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,35. Dan is P(nie A) = ___.","en":"P(A) = 0.35. Then P(not A) = ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,65","0.65","65%","13/20"],"en":["0.65","0,65","65%","13/20"]},"explain":{"af":"A en nie A is komplementêr: P(nie A) = 1 − P(A) = 1 − 0,35 = 0,65.","en":"A and not A are complementary: P(not A) = 1 − P(A) = 1 − 0.35 = 0.65."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die letters van die woord MADIBENG word elkeen op 'n kaartjie geskryf, en een kaartjie word lukraak getrek. Wat is die waarskynlikheid dat dit 'n klinker is?","en":"The letters of the word MADIBENG are each written on a card, and one card is drawn at random. What is the probability that it is a vowel?"},"options":[{"af":"5/8","en":"5/8"},{"af":"3/5","en":"3/5"},{"af":"1/8","en":"1/8"},{"af":"3/8","en":"3/8"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"n(S) = 8 letters. Die klinkers is A, I en E, dus n(E) = 3 en P = 3/8. 5/8 is die medeklinkers, en 3/5 vergelyk klinkers met medeklinkers in plaas van met al die letters.","en":"n(S) = 8 letters. The vowels are A, I and E, so n(E) = 3 and P = 3/8. 5/8 is the consonants, and 3/5 compares vowels with consonants instead of with all the letters."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Losskakel by 'n rugbyklub in Madibeng oefen 40 doelskoppe en slaag met 32 daarvan. Die relatiewe frekwensie van 'n suksesvolle doelskop is ___.","en":"A flyhalf at a rugby club in Madibeng practises 40 conversion kicks and succeeds with 32 of them. The relative frequency of a successful kick is ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,8","0,80","0.8","4/5","80%","32/40"],"en":["0.8","0.80","0,8","4/5","80%","32/40"]},"explain":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie = aantal suksesse ÷ aantal proewe = 32/40 = 0,8.","en":"Relative frequency = number of successes ÷ number of trials = 32/40 = 0.8."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"A en B is onderling uitsluitend, met P(A) = 0,4 en P(B) = 0,35. Wat is P(A of B)?","en":"A and B are mutually exclusive, with P(A) = 0.4 and P(B) = 0.35. What is P(A or B)?"},"options":[{"af":"0,14","en":"0.14"},{"af":"0,75","en":"0.75"},{"af":"0,05","en":"0.05"},{"af":"0,25","en":"0.25"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend beteken P(A en B) = 0, dus P(A of B) = 0,4 + 0,35 = 0,75. 0,14 vermenigvuldig, 0,05 trek af, en 0,25 is P(nie A nie en nie B nie).","en":"Mutually exclusive means P(A and B) = 0, so P(A or B) = 0.4 + 0.35 = 0.75. 0.14 multiplies, 0.05 subtracts, and 0.25 is P(not A and not B)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,6, P(B) = 0,25 en P(A en B) = 0,15. Dan is P(A of B) = ___.","en":"P(A) = 0.6, P(B) = 0.25 and P(A and B) = 0.15. Then P(A or B) = ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,7","0,70","0.7","7/10","70%"],"en":["0.7","0.70","0,7","7/10","70%"]},"explain":{"af":"P(A of B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A en B) = 0,6 + 0,25 − 0,15 = 0,7. As jy net optel (0,85), tel jy die oorvleueling twee keer.","en":"P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B) = 0.6 + 0.25 − 0.15 = 0.7. If you only add (0.85), you count the overlap twice."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n Venn-diagram is n(S) = 40, n(A) = 22, n(B) = 15 en n(A en B) = 6. Hoeveel elemente lê buite albei sirkels?","en":"In a Venn diagram, n(S) = 40, n(A) = 22, n(B) = 15 and n(A and B) = 6. How many elements lie outside both circles?"},"options":[{"af":"9","en":"9"},{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"31","en":"31"},{"af":"37","en":"37"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"n(A of B) = 22 + 15 − 6 = 31, dus buite = 40 − 31 = 9. 3 vergeet om die oorvleueling af te trek (40 − 37), en 31 is n(A of B) self.","en":"n(A or B) = 22 + 15 − 6 = 31, so outside = 40 − 31 = 9. 3 forgets to subtract the overlap (40 − 37), and 31 is n(A or B) itself."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,6 en P(B) = 0,5. Dit is moontlik dat A en B onderling uitsluitend is.","en":"P(A) = 0.6 and P(B) = 0.5. It is possible that A and B are mutually exclusive."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. As hulle onderling uitsluitend was, sou P(A of B) = 0,6 + 0,5 = 1,1 wees – groter as 1, wat onmoontlik is. Hulle móét dus oorvleuel, met P(A en B) ≥ 0,1.","en":"False. If they were mutually exclusive, P(A or B) would be 0.6 + 0.5 = 1.1 – greater than 1, which is impossible. So they must overlap, with P(A and B) ≥ 0.1."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,52, P(B) = 0,38 en P(A of B) = 0,7. Dan is P(slegs A) = ___.","en":"P(A) = 0.52, P(B) = 0.38 and P(A or B) = 0.7. Then P(only A) = ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,32","0.32","32%","8/25"],"en":["0.32","0,32","32%","8/25"]},"explain":{"af":"Eers die oorvleueling: P(A en B) = 0,52 + 0,38 − 0,7 = 0,2. Dan P(slegs A) = P(A) − P(A en B) = 0,52 − 0,2 = 0,32.","en":"First the overlap: P(A and B) = 0.52 + 0.38 − 0.7 = 0.2. Then P(only A) = P(A) − P(A and B) = 0.52 − 0.2 = 0.32."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kaartjies genommer 1 tot 20 lê in 'n sak. Een kaartjie word lukraak getrek. Wat is die waarskynlikheid dat die getal 'n veelvoud van 3 óf 'n veelvoud van 4 is?","en":"Cards numbered 1 to 20 are in a bag. One card is drawn at random. What is the probability that the number is a multiple of 3 or a multiple of 4?"},"options":[{"af":"11/20","en":"11/20"},{"af":"3/10","en":"3/10"},{"af":"1/2","en":"1/2"},{"af":"1/20","en":"1/20"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Veelvoude van 3: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18 (6). Veelvoude van 4: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20 (5). Albei: 12 (1). P = 6/20 + 5/20 − 1/20 = 10/20 = 1/2. 11/20 tel 12 twee keer.","en":"Multiples of 3: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18 (6). Multiples of 4: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20 (5). Both: 12 (1). P = 6/20 + 5/20 − 1/20 = 10/20 = 1/2. 11/20 counts 12 twice."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n opname onder 50 leerders in Madibeng gebruik 28 netwerk V vir selfoondata, 20 gebruik netwerk M, en 8 gebruik nie een van die twee nie. Hoeveel leerders gebruik albei netwerke?","en":"In a survey of 50 learners in Madibeng, 28 use network V for cellphone data, 20 use network M, and 8 use neither. How many learners use both networks?"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"14","en":"14"},{"af":"48","en":"48"},{"af":"6","en":"6"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"n(V of M) = 50 − 8 = 42. Optelreël: 42 = 28 + 20 − n(albei), dus n(albei) = 48 − 42 = 6. 2 ignoreer die 8 wat geen netwerk gebruik nie (50 − 28 − 20), en 48 tel net op.","en":"n(V or M) = 50 − 8 = 42. Addition rule: 42 = 28 + 20 − n(both), so n(both) = 48 − 42 = 6. 2 ignores the 8 who use neither network (50 − 28 − 20), and 48 just adds."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Sak bevat 12 groen balle en 'n aantal geel balle. As een bal lukraak getrek word, is P(groen) = 3/8. Hoeveel geel balle is in die sak?","en":"A bag contains 12 green balls and some yellow balls. If one ball is drawn at random, P(green) = 3/8. How many yellow balls are in the bag?"},"options":[{"af":"20","en":"20"},{"af":"32","en":"32"},{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"4,5","en":"4.5"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"12/n(S) = 3/8, dus 3 × n(S) = 96 en n(S) = 32 balle altesaam. Geel = 32 − 12 = 20. 32 is die totaal, 5 gebruik die breuk se getalle as aantalle (8 − 3), en 4,5 is 12 × 3/8.","en":"12/n(S) = 3/8, so 3 × n(S) = 96 and n(S) = 32 balls in total. Yellow = 32 − 12 = 20. 32 is the total, 5 uses the fraction's numbers as counts (8 − 3), and 4.5 is 12 × 3/8."}}]}]}]},"fisiese-wetenskappe":{"id":"fisiese-wetenskappe","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Fisiese Wetenskappe","en":"Physical Sciences"},"short":{"af":"Fis Wet","en":"Phys Sci"},"icon":"⚛️","color":"#7c3aed","intro":{"af":"Fisiese Wetenskappe bestaan uit Fisika (beweging, golwe, elektrisiteit, energie) en Chemie (materie, die atoom, binding en chemiese reaksies). In November skryf jy twee vraestelle – Vraestel 1 Fisika en Vraestel 2 Chemie – wat die hele jaar se werk dek. Definisies, formules met eenhede en netjiese berekeninge is die sleutel.","en":"Physical Sciences consists of Physics (motion, waves, electricity, energy) and Chemistry (matter, the atom, bonding and chemical reactions). In November you write two papers – Paper 1 Physics and Paper 2 Chemistry – covering the whole year's work. Definitions, formulae with units and neat calculations are the key."},"examTips":[{"af":"Wys ALTYD jou bewerkings: formule → vervanging → antwoord met eenheid. Metodepunte red jou as die finale antwoord verkeerd is.","en":"ALWAYS show your working: formula → substitution → answer with unit. Method marks save you if the final answer is wrong."},{"af":"Kyk na die punte langs elke vraag: dit sê hoeveel stappe of feite die nasiener soek. Bestee ongeveer 1 minuut per punt.","en":"Look at the marks next to each question: they tell you how many steps or facts the marker wants. Spend about 1 minute per mark."},{"af":"Leer die DBE-definisies woord vir woord – die memo soek spesifieke sleutelwoorde, bv. 'verandering in posisie' vir verplasing.","en":"Learn the DBE definitions word for word – the memo looks for specific key words, e.g. 'change in position' for displacement."},{"af":"Skakel eers alle eenhede om na SI (km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹, g → kg, cm³ → dm³) voordat jy in 'n formule vervang.","en":"Convert all units to SI first (km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹, g → kg, cm³ → dm³) before substituting into a formula."},{"af":"Gee by vektore altyd die rigting saam met die grootte, bv. 12 m·s⁻¹ oos of 3 m noord.","en":"For vectors always give the direction with the magnitude, e.g. 12 m·s⁻¹ east or 3 m north."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: Alles Wetenskap Graad 10 (Afrikaans)","en":"Siyavula: Everything Science Grade 10 (Afrikaans)"},"url":"https://wcedeportal.co.za/eresource/76266","note":{"af":"Gratis, volledige CAPS-handboek vir Fisiese Wetenskappe met uitgewerkte voorbeelde.","en":"Free, complete CAPS Physical Sciences textbook with worked examples."}},{"title":{"af":"Noordwes Onderwysdepartement: vraestelle en memo's","en":"North West Department of Education: papers and memos"},"url":"https://education.nwpg.gov.za/?page_id=4644","note":{"af":"Provinsiale Graad 10-Novembervraestelle (ook Fisiese Wetenskappe V1 in Afrikaans) met memorandums.","en":"Provincial Grade 10 November papers (incl. Physical Sciences P1 in Afrikaans) with memos."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Fisiese Wetenskappe: twee vraestelle\n\n**Vraestel 1 (Fisika) en Vraestel 2 (Chemie): 100 punte elk, 2 uur elk** volgens die nuutste DBE-riglyne (*sommige skole gebruik nog 150 punte – bevestig met die 2026-afbakening*). Elke vraestel begin met **meervoudige keuse**, gevolg deur gestruktureerde vrae. Jy kry 'n gegewensblad en mag 'n sakrekenaar gebruik.\n\n| Vraestel 1: Fisika | ±Punte | Vraestel 2: Chemie | ±Punte |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Meganika (vektore, beweging, bewegingsvergelykings) | 45 | Materie en materiale (klassifikasie, KMT, atoom, periodieke tabel, binding) | 50 |\n| Golwe, klank en lig | 25 | Chemiese verandering (fisies/chemies, vergelykings, waterige oplossings, molbegrip) | 50 |\n| Elektrisiteit en magnetisme | 30 | | |\n\n### Wenke vir hierdie vraestelle\n\n1. Definisies is maklike punte – leer dit presies.\n2. Skryf by elke berekening die formule, die vervanging en die antwoord **met eenheid**.\n3. Lees grafiekvrae twee keer: vra hulle die gradiënt of die oppervlakte onder die grafiek?\n4. By meervoudige keuse: elimineer eers die duidelik verkeerde opsies.","en":"## Physical Sciences: two papers\n\n**Paper 1 (Physics) and Paper 2 (Chemistry): 100 marks each, 2 hours each** according to the latest DBE guidelines (*some schools still use 150 marks – confirm with the 2026 scope*). Each paper starts with **multiple choice**, followed by structured questions. You get a data sheet and may use a calculator.\n\n| Paper 1: Physics | ±Marks | Paper 2: Chemistry | ±Marks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Mechanics (vectors, motion, equations of motion) | 45 | Matter and materials (classification, KMT, atom, periodic table, bonding) | 50 |\n| Waves, sound and light | 25 | Chemical change (physical/chemical, equations, aqueous solutions, mole concept) | 50 |\n| Electricity and magnetism | 30 | | |\n\n### Tips for these papers\n\n1. Definitions are easy marks – learn them exactly.\n2. For every calculation write the formula, the substitution and the answer **with its unit**.\n3. Read graph questions twice: do they ask for the gradient or the area under the graph?\n4. In multiple choice: first eliminate the clearly wrong options."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Materie en materiale; golwe, klank en lig","en":"Matter and materials; waves, sound and light"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t1-klassifikasie-materie","title":{"af":"Klassifikasie van materie","en":"Classification of matter"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal materie as mengsels of suiwer stowwe kan klassifiseer, name en formules van verbindings kan skryf, stowwe volgens hul eienskappe kan groepeer en die regte skeidingsmetode kan kies.","en":"You will be able to classify matter as mixtures or pure substances, write names and formulae of compounds, group substances by their properties and choose the right separation method."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is materie?\n\n**Materie** is enigiets wat massa het en ruimte (volume) beslaan. Alles om jou – die water in Hartbeespoortdam, die lug, jou rugbybal – is materie en bestaan uit klein deeltjies (atome, molekules of ione). Ons klassifiseer materie volgens sy **samestelling** en sy **eienskappe**.\n\n## Mengsels en suiwer stowwe\n\n| Materie | Soorte | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mengsel | homogeen, heterogeen | lug, soutwater, sand en water |\n| Suiwer stof | element, verbinding | koper (Cu), water (H_{2}O) |\n\n- **Mengsel:** 'n kombinasie van twee of meer stowwe wat nie chemies aan mekaar gebind is nie. Die samestelling kan wissel, elke komponent behou sy eie eienskappe, en die komponente kan met **fisiese metodes** geskei word.\n- **Heterogene mengsel:** nie eenvormig nie; die verskillende komponente kan gesien word, bv. sand en water, olie en water, modderwater uit die Krokodilrivier.\n- **Homogene mengsel:** eenvormig deurgaans; die komponente kan nie gesien word nie, bv. soutwater, lug, koeldrank en **legerings** soos geelkoper (koper + sink) en staal. 'n **Oplossing** is 'n homogene mengsel van 'n opgeloste stof in 'n oplosmiddel.\n- **Suiwer stof:** materie wat nie deur enige fisiese proses in ander soorte materie geskei kan word nie. Dit het 'n vaste samestelling en 'n skerp, vaste smelt- en kookpunt. ('n Mengsel smelt oor 'n temperatuurgebied.)\n- **Element:** 'n stof wat nie deur chemiese metodes in eenvoudiger stowwe afgebreek kan word nie. Dit bestaan uit net een soort atoom, bv. Fe, Cu, O_{2}, N_{2}. Daar is 118 elemente op die periodieke tabel.\n- **Verbinding:** 'n stof wat uit twee of meer verskillende elemente bestaan wat in 'n vaste verhouding chemies gebind is, bv. H_{2}O, NaCl, CO_{2}. Dit kan net met **chemiese metodes** geskei word (bv. elektrolise van water).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** O_{2} is 'n **element** (net suurstofatome), nie 'n verbinding nie. Lug is 'n **mengsel**. Kraanwater is 'n homogene mengsel (opgeloste soute en chloor); net suiwer, gedistilleerde water is 'n verbinding. Moenie Co (kobalt, element) en CO (koolstofmonoksied, verbinding) verwar nie.\n\n## Name en formules\n\n1. Die metaal (positiewe ioon) word eerste genoem: NaCl = natriumchloried.\n2. 'n Enkel nie-metaal-ioon kry die uitgang **-ied**: oksied (O^{2−}), chloried (Cl^{−}), sulfied (S^{2−}).\n3. By twee nie-metale wys voorvoegsels die aantal atome (mono-, di-, tri-, tetra-): CO = koolstofmonoksied, CO_{2} = koolstofdioksied, SO_{3} = swaweltrioksied.\n4. By oorgangsmetale wys 'n Romeinse syfer die lading: Fe_{2}O_{3} = yster(III)oksied, CuSO_{4} = koper(II)sulfaat.\n\n| Ioon | Formule | Ioon | Formule |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ammonium | NH_{4}^{+} | karbonaat | CO_{3}^{2−} |\n| hidroksied | OH^{−} | sulfaat | SO_{4}^{2−} |\n| nitraat | NO_{3}^{−} | fosfaat | PO_{4}^{3−} |\n\nAl hierdie -aat-ione bevat suurstof. Let op: hidroksied eindig op -ied, maar is 'n saamgestelde ioon.\n\n**Formule skryf:** balanseer die ladings sodat die totaal nul is. Aluminiumsulfaat: Al^{3+} en SO_{4}^{2−} → 2 × (+3) = +6 en 3 × (−2) = −6, dus Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}. Sit hakies om 'n saamgestelde ioon as daar meer as een is: Ca(OH)_{2}, nie CaOH_{2} nie. Die getal buite die hakie vermenigvuldig alles binne: Ca(NO_{3})_{2} bevat 1 Ca, 2 N en 6 O = 9 atome.\n\nKen ook: NH_{3} (ammoniak), CH_{4} (metaan), HCl (waterstofchloried), H_{2}SO_{4} (swawelsuur), NaOH (natriumhidroksied), CaCO_{3} (kalsiumkarbonaat).\n\n## Metale, nie-metale en metalloïede\n\n- **Metale** (links en in die middel van die periodieke tabel): blink, goeie geleiers van elektrisiteit en hitte, smeebaar (kan plat geslaan word) en rekbaar (kan in drade getrek word). Almal is vaste stowwe by kamertemperatuur, behalwe kwik.\n- **Nie-metale** (regs): meestal dof, swak geleiers (isolators), bros as vaste stof; baie is gasse. Uitsondering: **grafiet** (koolstof) gelei elektrisiteit.\n- **Metalloïede** (langs die trapvormige lyn, bv. B, Si, Ge, As): lyk dikwels blink soos 'n metaal, maar is bros. Hulle is **halfgeleiers** – hul elektriese geleidingsvermoë **neem toe** as die temperatuur styg (by metale neem dit af). Silikon word in rekenaarskyfies en sonpanele gebruik.\n\n## Geleiers, isolators en magnetisme\n\n- **Elektriese geleier:** laat 'n elektriese stroom deur, bv. koper, yster, grafiet, soutwater. **Elektriese isolator:** laat nie stroom deur nie, bv. plastiek, rubber, hout, glas. Daarom is koperdrade met plastiek bedek. Toets: plaas die materiaal in 'n stroombaan met 'n sel en 'n gloeilamp – brand die gloeilamp, is dit 'n geleier.\n- **Termiese geleier:** gelei hitte goed (metale: braairooster, kastrol). **Termiese isolator:** gelei hitte swak (hout, plastiek, wol, lug, polistireen) – daarom het 'n braaitang hout- of plastiekhandvatsels.\n- **Magnetiese materiale** word deur 'n magneet aangetrek: yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt. Die meeste ander metale (koper, aluminium, sink, goud, silwer) is **nie-magneties**.\n\n## Skeidingsmetodes (fisies)\n\n| Metode | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filtrasie | onoplosbare vaste stof uit 'n vloeistof | sand uit water (sand = **residu**, vloeistof = **filtraat**) |\n| Verdamping | opgeloste vaste stof terugkry | sout uit seewater |\n| Distillasie | vloeistof uit 'n oplossing, of vloeistowwe met verskillende kookpunte | suiwer water uit seewater |\n| Kristallisasie | kristalle uit 'n versadigde oplossing | suikerkristalle |\n| Magnetiese skeiding | magnetiese van nie-magnetiese stof | ystervylsels uit swawel |\n| Skeitregter | vloeistowwe wat nie meng nie | olie en water |\n| Papierchromatografie | opgeloste kleurstowwe | kleure in ink |\n\n> **Wenk:** Kies die metode volgens die eienskap wat verskil: deeltjiegrootte, oplosbaarheid, kookpunt of magnetisme.","en":"## What is matter?\n\n**Matter** is anything that has mass and takes up space (volume). Everything around you – the water in Hartbeespoort Dam, the air, your rugby ball – is matter and is made of tiny particles (atoms, molecules or ions). We classify matter according to its **composition** and its **properties**.\n\n## Mixtures and pure substances\n\n| Matter | Kinds | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mixture | homogeneous, heterogeneous | air, salt water, sand and water |\n| Pure substance | element, compound | copper (Cu), water (H_{2}O) |\n\n- **Mixture:** a combination of two or more substances that are not chemically bonded to each other. The composition can vary, each component keeps its own properties, and the components can be separated by **physical methods**.\n- **Heterogeneous mixture:** not uniform; the different components can be seen, e.g. sand and water, oil and water, muddy water from the Crocodile River.\n- **Homogeneous mixture:** uniform throughout; the components cannot be seen, e.g. salt water, air, cool drink and **alloys** such as brass (copper + zinc) and steel. A **solution** is a homogeneous mixture of a solute dissolved in a solvent.\n- **Pure substance:** matter that cannot be separated into other kinds of matter by any physical process. It has a fixed composition and a sharp, fixed melting and boiling point. (A mixture melts over a range of temperatures.)\n- **Element:** a substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means. It consists of only one kind of atom, e.g. Fe, Cu, O_{2}, N_{2}. There are 118 elements on the periodic table.\n- **Compound:** a substance made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded in a fixed ratio, e.g. H_{2}O, NaCl, CO_{2}. It can only be separated by **chemical methods** (e.g. electrolysis of water).\n\n> **Common mistake:** O_{2} is an **element** (only oxygen atoms), not a compound. Air is a **mixture**. Tap water is a homogeneous mixture (dissolved salts and chlorine); only pure, distilled water is a compound. Do not confuse Co (cobalt, element) with CO (carbon monoxide, compound).\n\n## Names and formulae\n\n1. The metal (positive ion) is named first: NaCl = sodium chloride.\n2. A single non-metal ion gets the ending **-ide**: oxide (O^{2−}), chloride (Cl^{−}), sulfide (S^{2−}).\n3. For two non-metals, prefixes show the number of atoms (mono-, di-, tri-, tetra-): CO = carbon monoxide, CO_{2} = carbon dioxide, SO_{3} = sulfur trioxide.\n4. For transition metals, a Roman numeral shows the charge: Fe_{2}O_{3} = iron(III) oxide, CuSO_{4} = copper(II) sulfate.\n\n| Ion | Formula | Ion | Formula |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ammonium | NH_{4}^{+} | carbonate | CO_{3}^{2−} |\n| hydroxide | OH^{−} | sulfate | SO_{4}^{2−} |\n| nitrate | NO_{3}^{−} | phosphate | PO_{4}^{3−} |\n\nAll these -ate ions contain oxygen. Note: hydroxide ends in -ide, but it is a polyatomic ion.\n\n**Writing a formula:** balance the charges so that the total is zero. Aluminium sulfate: Al^{3+} and SO_{4}^{2−} → 2 × (+3) = +6 and 3 × (−2) = −6, so Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}. Put brackets around a polyatomic ion when there is more than one: Ca(OH)_{2}, not CaOH_{2}. The number outside the bracket multiplies everything inside: Ca(NO_{3})_{2} contains 1 Ca, 2 N and 6 O = 9 atoms.\n\nAlso know: NH_{3} (ammonia), CH_{4} (methane), HCl (hydrogen chloride), H_{2}SO_{4} (sulfuric acid), NaOH (sodium hydroxide), CaCO_{3} (calcium carbonate).\n\n## Metals, non-metals and metalloids\n\n- **Metals** (left and middle of the periodic table): shiny, good conductors of electricity and heat, malleable (can be hammered flat) and ductile (can be drawn into wires). All are solids at room temperature, except mercury.\n- **Non-metals** (right): mostly dull, poor conductors (insulators), brittle as solids; many are gases. Exception: **graphite** (carbon) conducts electricity.\n- **Metalloids** (along the staircase line, e.g. B, Si, Ge, As): often look shiny like a metal, but are brittle. They are **semiconductors** – their electrical conductivity **increases** as the temperature rises (in metals it decreases). Silicon is used in computer chips and solar panels.\n\n## Conductors, insulators and magnetism\n\n- **Electrical conductor:** allows an electric current to pass through, e.g. copper, iron, graphite, salt water. **Electrical insulator:** does not allow current through, e.g. plastic, rubber, wood, glass. That is why copper wires are covered in plastic. Test: put the material in a circuit with a cell and a light bulb – if the bulb glows, it is a conductor.\n- **Thermal conductor:** conducts heat well (metals: braai grid, pot). **Thermal insulator:** conducts heat poorly (wood, plastic, wool, air, polystyrene) – that is why braai tongs have wooden or plastic handles.\n- **Magnetic materials** are attracted by a magnet: iron, steel, nickel and cobalt. Most other metals (copper, aluminium, zinc, gold, silver) are **non-magnetic**.\n\n## Separation methods (physical)\n\n| Method | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filtration | insoluble solid from a liquid | sand from water (sand = **residue**, liquid = **filtrate**) |\n| Evaporation | recover a dissolved solid | salt from sea water |\n| Distillation | liquid from a solution, or liquids with different boiling points | pure water from sea water |\n| Crystallisation | crystals from a saturated solution | sugar crystals |\n| Magnetic separation | magnetic from non-magnetic substance | iron filings from sulfur |\n| Separating funnel | liquids that do not mix | oil and water |\n| Paper chromatography | dissolved dyes | colours in ink |\n\n> **Tip:** Choose the method according to the property that differs: particle size, solubility, boiling point or magnetism."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Mengsel","en":"Mixture"},"def":{"af":"'n Kombinasie van twee of meer stowwe wat nie chemies aan mekaar gebind is nie; dit kan met fisiese metodes geskei word.","en":"A combination of two or more substances that are not chemically bonded to each other; it can be separated by physical methods."}},{"term":{"af":"Heterogene mengsel","en":"Heterogeneous mixture"},"def":{"af":"'n Mengsel wat nie eenvormig is nie en waarin die verskillende komponente gesien kan word.","en":"A mixture that is not uniform and in which the different components can be seen."}},{"term":{"af":"Homogene mengsel","en":"Homogeneous mixture"},"def":{"af":"'n Mengsel wat eenvormig is deurgaans en waarin die verskillende komponente nie gesien kan word nie.","en":"A mixture that is uniform throughout and in which the different components cannot be seen."}},{"term":{"af":"Suiwer stof","en":"Pure substance"},"def":{"af":"Materie wat nie deur enige fisiese proses in ander soorte materie geskei kan word nie.","en":"Matter that cannot be separated into other kinds of matter by any physical process."}},{"term":{"af":"Element","en":"Element"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat nie deur chemiese metodes in eenvoudiger stowwe afgebreek kan word nie.","en":"A substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbinding","en":"Compound"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat uit twee of meer verskillende elemente bestaan wat in 'n vaste verhouding chemies gebind is.","en":"A substance made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded in a fixed ratio."}},{"term":{"af":"Metalloïed","en":"Metalloid"},"def":{"af":"'n Element met eienskappe van sowel metale as nie-metale; 'n halfgeleier waarvan die elektriese geleidingsvermoë toeneem as die temperatuur styg.","en":"An element with properties of both metals and non-metals; a semiconductor whose electrical conductivity increases as the temperature rises."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektriese geleier","en":"Electrical conductor"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat 'n elektriese stroom deur hom laat vloei, bv. koper of grafiet.","en":"A substance that allows an electric current to flow through it, e.g. copper or graphite."}},{"term":{"af":"Termiese isolator","en":"Thermal insulator"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat nie toelaat dat hitte maklik deur hom oorgedra word nie, bv. hout, plastiek of lug.","en":"A substance that does not allow heat to be transferred through it easily, e.g. wood, plastic or air."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetiese materiaal","en":"Magnetic material"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal wat deur 'n magneet aangetrek word, bv. yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt.","en":"A material that is attracted by a magnet, e.g. iron, steel, nickel and cobalt."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer stowwe","en":"Classify substances"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elk van die volgende as 'n element, 'n verbinding, 'n homogene mengsel of 'n heterogene mengsel: (a) koper, (b) gedistilleerde water, (c) lug, (d) geelkoper, (e) modderwater uit die Krokodilrivier, (f) koolstofdioksied.","en":"Classify each of the following as an element, a compound, a homogeneous mixture or a heterogeneous mixture: (a) copper, (b) distilled water, (c) air, (d) brass, (e) muddy water from the Crocodile River, (f) carbon dioxide."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra eers: is dit een stof met 'n vaste samestelling (suiwer stof), of meer as een stof wat nie chemies gebind is nie (mengsel)?","en":"First ask: is it one substance with a fixed composition (pure substance), or more than one substance that is not chemically bonded (mixture)?"},{"af":"(a) Koper (Cu) bestaan net uit koperatome → **element**. (b) Gedistilleerde water (H_{2}O) en (f) koolstofdioksied (CO_{2}) bestaan elk uit twee elemente wat in 'n vaste verhouding chemies gebind is → **verbindings**.","en":"(a) Copper (Cu) consists only of copper atoms → **element**. (b) Distilled water (H_{2}O) and (f) carbon dioxide (CO_{2}) each consist of two elements chemically bonded in a fixed ratio → **compounds**."},{"af":"(c) Lug is stikstof, suurstof, argon, koolstofdioksied en waterdamp wat nie chemies gebind is nie, en jy kan die komponente nie sien nie → **homogene mengsel**. (d) Geelkoper is 'n legering van koper en sink wat eenvormig deurgaans is → **homogene mengsel**.","en":"(c) Air is nitrogen, oxygen, argon, carbon dioxide and water vapour that are not chemically bonded, and you cannot see the components → **homogeneous mixture**. (d) Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc that is uniform throughout → **homogeneous mixture**."},{"af":"(e) In modderwater sien jy die gronddeeltjies, en hulle sak later uit – dit is nie eenvormig nie → **heterogene mengsel**.","en":"(e) In muddy water you can see the soil particles, and they settle out later – it is not uniform → **heterogeneous mixture**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) element (b) verbinding (c) homogene mengsel (d) homogene mengsel (e) heterogene mengsel (f) verbinding","en":"(a) element (b) compound (c) homogeneous mixture (d) homogeneous mixture (e) heterogeneous mixture (f) compound"}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf formules en name","en":"Write formulae and names"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die chemiese formule van (a) kalsiumnitraat, (b) aluminiumsulfaat en (c) ammoniumkarbonaat. Gee dan (d) die naam van Na₂SO₄.","en":"Write the chemical formula of (a) calcium nitrate, (b) aluminium sulfate and (c) ammonium carbonate. Then give (d) the name of Na₂SO₄."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ione: Ca^{2+} en NO_{3}^{−}. Twee NO_{3}^{−} (totaal −2) balanseer een Ca^{2+} (+2), en die nitraat kry hakies → Ca(NO_{3})_{2}","en":"(a) Ions: Ca^{2+} and NO_{3}^{−}. Two NO_{3}^{−} (total −2) balance one Ca^{2+} (+2), and the nitrate gets brackets → Ca(NO_{3})_{2}"},{"af":"(b) Ione: Al^{3+} en SO_{4}^{2−}. Die KGV van 3 en 2 is 6: 2 × (+3) = +6 en 3 × (−2) = −6 → Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}","en":"(b) Ions: Al^{3+} and SO_{4}^{2−}. The LCM of 3 and 2 is 6: 2 × (+3) = +6 and 3 × (−2) = −6 → Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}"},{"af":"(c) Ione: NH_{4}^{+} en CO_{3}^{2−}. Twee NH_{4}^{+} (+2) balanseer een CO_{3}^{2−} (−2) → (NH_{4})_{2}CO_{3}","en":"(c) Ions: NH_{4}^{+} and CO_{3}^{2−}. Two NH_{4}^{+} (+2) balance one CO_{3}^{2−} (−2) → (NH_{4})_{2}CO_{3}"},{"af":"(d) Na_{2}SO_{4} bevat Na^{+} en SO_{4}^{2−}. Noem die metaal eerste en behou die naam van die saamgestelde ioon → natriumsulfaat","en":"(d) Na_{2}SO_{4} contains Na^{+} and SO_{4}^{2−}. Name the metal first and keep the name of the polyatomic ion → sodium sulfate"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Ca(NO₃)₂ (b) Al₂(SO₄)₃ (c) (NH₄)₂CO₃ (d) natriumsulfaat","en":"(a) Ca(NO₃)₂ (b) Al₂(SO₄)₃ (c) (NH₄)₂CO₃ (d) sodium sulfate"}},{"title":{"af":"Skei 'n mengsel van drie stowwe","en":"Separate a mixture of three substances"},"problem":{"af":"'n Leerder mors sand, sout en ystervylsels in een bak. Beskryf, met redes, hoe sy al drie stowwe afsonderlik kan terugkry.","en":"A learner spills sand, salt and iron filings into one bowl. Describe, with reasons, how she can recover all three substances separately."},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik 'n **magneet**: ystervylsels is magneties en word uitgetrek. Sand en sout is nie-magneties en bly agter.","en":"Use a **magnet**: iron filings are magnetic and are pulled out. Sand and salt are non-magnetic and stay behind."},{"af":"Gooi water by die sand-en-sout en roer: die sout **los op**, maar die sand los nie op nie.","en":"Add water to the sand and salt and stir: the salt **dissolves**, but the sand does not."},{"af":"**Filtreer** die mengsel: die sand bly as **residu** in die filtreerpapier, en die soutoplossing loop deur as **filtraat**.","en":"**Filter** the mixture: the sand stays behind as the **residue** in the filter paper, and the salt solution runs through as the **filtrate**."},{"af":"**Verdamp** die filtraat in 'n verdampingsbak: die water verdamp en die sout bly agter.","en":"**Evaporate** the filtrate in an evaporating dish: the water evaporates and the salt stays behind."}],"answer":{"af":"Magneet (yster) → oplos in water → filtrasie (sand) → verdamping (sout)","en":"Magnet (iron) → dissolve in water → filtration (sand) → evaporation (salt)"}},{"title":{"af":"Ondersoek: geleiers en isolators","en":"Investigation: conductors and insulators"},"problem":{"af":"Leerders bou 'n stroombaan met 'n sel, 'n gloeilamp en twee krokodilknippies. Hulle plaas ewe lang stawe van koper, yster, glas, hout en grafiet (potloodlood) een vir een tussen die knippies. Die gloeilamp brand by koper, yster en grafiet, maar nie by glas en hout nie. (a) Noem die onafhanklike en afhanklike veranderlike. (b) Klassifiseer die materiale. (c) Watter resultaat is verrassend, en hoekom?","en":"Learners build a circuit with a cell, a light bulb and two crocodile clips. They place rods of equal length made of copper, iron, glass, wood and graphite (pencil lead) one at a time between the clips. The bulb glows for copper, iron and graphite, but not for glass and wood. (a) Name the independent and dependent variable. (b) Classify the materials. (c) Which result is surprising, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die **onafhanklike veranderlike** is wat die leerders self verander: die tipe materiaal. Die **afhanklike veranderlike** is wat hulle waarneem: of die gloeilamp brand (die elektriese geleidingsvermoë). Gekontroleerd: dieselfde sel, gloeilamp en staaflengte.","en":"(a) The **independent variable** is what the learners change themselves: the type of material. The **dependent variable** is what they observe: whether the bulb glows (the electrical conductivity). Controlled: the same cell, bulb and rod length."},{"af":"(b) Gloeilamp brand → stroom vloei → **geleiers**: koper, yster en grafiet. Gloeilamp brand nie → **isolators**: glas en hout.","en":"(b) Bulb glows → current flows → **conductors**: copper, iron and graphite. Bulb does not glow → **insulators**: glass and wood."},{"af":"(c) **Grafiet** is koolstof, 'n nie-metaal, maar dit gelei tog elektrisiteit. Dit is die bekende uitsondering op die reël dat nie-metale isolators is.","en":"(c) **Graphite** is carbon, a non-metal, yet it conducts electricity. It is the well-known exception to the rule that non-metals are insulators."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Onafhanklik: tipe materiaal; afhanklik: of die gloeilamp brand. (b) Geleiers: koper, yster, grafiet; isolators: glas, hout. (c) Grafiet – 'n nie-metaal wat gelei.","en":"(a) Independent: type of material; dependent: whether the bulb glows. (b) Conductors: copper, iron, graphite; insulators: glass, wood. (c) Graphite – a non-metal that conducts."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n heterogene mengsel?","en":"Which one of the following is a heterogeneous mixture?"},"options":[{"af":"Sand en water","en":"Sand and water"},{"af":"Soutwater","en":"Salt water"},{"af":"Lug","en":"Air"},{"af":"Geelkoper","en":"Brass"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In sand en water kan jy die twee komponente sien, en die sand sak uit – dit is nie eenvormig nie. Soutwater, lug en geelkoper (koper + sink) is eenvormig deurgaans: dit is homogene mengsels.","en":"In sand and water you can see the two components, and the sand settles out – it is not uniform. Salt water, air and brass (copper + zinc) are uniform throughout: they are homogeneous mixtures."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Lug is 'n verbinding van stikstof en suurstof.","en":"Air is a compound of nitrogen and oxygen."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Lug is 'n homogene mengsel: die gasse (hoofsaaklik N₂ en O₂, met bietjie Ar, CO₂ en waterdamp) is nie chemies gebind nie, en die samestelling kan wissel.","en":"False. Air is a homogeneous mixture: the gases (mainly N₂ and O₂, with a little Ar, CO₂ and water vapour) are not chemically bonded, and the composition can vary."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ioon CO₃²⁻ word die ___-ioon genoem.","en":"The ion CO₃²⁻ is called the ___ ion."},"answers":{"af":["karbonaat","karbonaatioon","karbonaat-ioon"],"en":["carbonate","carbonate ion","carbonate-ion"]},"explain":{"af":"CO₃²⁻ is die karbonaat-ioon. Dit bevat suurstof, daarom eindig die naam op -aat, bv. kalsiumkarbonaat (CaCO₃, kalksteen).","en":"CO₃²⁻ is the carbonate ion. It contains oxygen, which is why the name ends in -ate, e.g. calcium carbonate (CaCO₃, limestone)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke ioon by sy formule.","en":"Match each ion to its formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ammonium","en":"Ammonium"},"r":{"af":"NH₄⁺","en":"NH₄⁺"}},{"l":{"af":"Hidroksied","en":"Hydroxide"},"r":{"af":"OH⁻","en":"OH⁻"}},{"l":{"af":"Nitraat","en":"Nitrate"},"r":{"af":"NO₃⁻","en":"NO₃⁻"}},{"l":{"af":"Sulfaat","en":"Sulfate"},"r":{"af":"SO₄²⁻","en":"SO₄²⁻"}},{"l":{"af":"Fosfaat","en":"Phosphate"},"r":{"af":"PO₄³⁻","en":"PO₄³⁻"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ammonium NH₄⁺ is die enigste positiewe saamgestelde ioon hier. Hidroksied OH⁻ en nitraat NO₃⁻ het 'n lading van −1, sulfaat SO₄²⁻ −2 en fosfaat PO₄³⁻ −3.","en":"Ammonium NH₄⁺ is the only positive polyatomic ion here. Hydroxide OH⁻ and nitrate NO₃⁻ have a charge of −1, sulfate SO₄²⁻ −2 and phosphate PO₄³⁻ −3."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Grafiet is 'n nie-metaal wat elektrisiteit gelei.","en":"Graphite is a non-metal that conducts electricity."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Grafiet is 'n vorm van koolstof ('n nie-metaal), maar dit gelei elektrisiteit – die bekende uitsondering op die reël dat nie-metale isolators is. Daarom kan potloodlood 'n gloeilamp laat brand.","en":"True. Graphite is a form of carbon (a non-metal), yet it conducts electricity – the well-known exception to the rule that non-metals are insulators. That is why pencil lead can make a bulb glow."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom het 'n braaitang gewoonlik hout- of plastiekhandvatsels?","en":"Why do braai tongs usually have wooden or plastic handles?"},"options":[{"af":"Hout en plastiek is goeie termiese geleiers.","en":"Wood and plastic are good thermal conductors."},{"af":"Hout en plastiek is nie-magneties.","en":"Wood and plastic are non-magnetic."},{"af":"Hout en plastiek is termiese isolators, so hitte bereik nie maklik jou hand nie.","en":"Wood and plastic are thermal insulators, so heat does not easily reach your hand."},{"af":"Hout en plastiek is elektriese geleiers.","en":"Wood and plastic are electrical conductors."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die metaal van die tang word warm, want metale is goeie termiese geleiers. Hout en plastiek is termiese isolators: hulle gelei hitte swak, so jou hand bly koel. Magnetisme en elektriese geleiding het niks hiermee te doen nie.","en":"The metal of the tongs gets hot, because metals are good thermal conductors. Wood and plastic are thermal insulators: they conduct heat poorly, so your hand stays cool. Magnetism and electrical conduction have nothing to do with it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter metode gebruik jy om suiwer drinkwater uit seewater te kry?","en":"Which method do you use to obtain pure drinking water from sea water?"},"options":[{"af":"Filtrasie","en":"Filtration"},{"af":"Verdamping","en":"Evaporation"},{"af":"Papierchromatografie","en":"Paper chromatography"},{"af":"Distillasie","en":"Distillation"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By distillasie kook jy die seewater; die waterdamp kondenseer in 'n koeler en jy vang suiwer water op, terwyl die sout agterbly. Filtrasie werk nie, want die sout is opgelos en loop deur die filtreerpapier. Verdamping gee jou die sout, maar die water gaan verlore in die lug.","en":"In distillation you boil the sea water; the water vapour condenses in a condenser and you collect pure water, while the salt stays behind. Filtration does not work, because the salt is dissolved and passes through the filter paper. Evaporation gives you the salt, but the water is lost to the air."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die chemiese formule van kalsiumhidroksied: ___","en":"Write the chemical formula of calcium hydroxide: ___"},"answers":{"af":["Ca(OH)2","Ca(OH)₂"],"en":["Ca(OH)2","Ca(OH)₂"]},"explain":{"af":"Ca²⁺ het 'n lading van +2 en OH⁻ 'n lading van −1, dus is twee OH⁻-ione nodig: Ca(OH)₂. Die hakies is nodig – CaOH₂ sou beteken net een O en twee H.","en":"Ca²⁺ has a charge of +2 and OH⁻ a charge of −1, so two OH⁻ ions are needed: Ca(OH)₂. The brackets are necessary – CaOH₂ would mean only one O and two H."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die korrekte formule van aluminiumsulfaat?","en":"What is the correct formula of aluminium sulfate?"},"options":[{"af":"AlSO₄","en":"AlSO₄"},{"af":"Al₂(SO₄)₃","en":"Al₂(SO₄)₃"},{"af":"Al₃(SO₄)₂","en":"Al₃(SO₄)₂"},{"af":"Al₂SO₄","en":"Al₂SO₄"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Al³⁺ en SO₄²⁻: 2 × (+3) = +6 en 3 × (−2) = −6, dus is die totaal nul: Al₂(SO₄)₃. AlSO₄ ignoreer die ladings, Al₃(SO₄)₂ ruil die getalle verkeerd om, en Al₂SO₄ is nie neutraal nie (+6 − 2 = +4).","en":"Al³⁺ and SO₄²⁻: 2 × (+3) = +6 and 3 × (−2) = −6, so the total is zero: Al₂(SO₄)₃. AlSO₄ ignores the charges, Al₃(SO₄)₂ swaps the numbers the wrong way round, and Al₂SO₄ is not neutral (+6 − 2 = +4)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gee die chemiese naam van Mg(NO₃)₂: ___","en":"Give the chemical name of Mg(NO₃)₂: ___"},"answers":{"af":["magnesiumnitraat","magnesium nitraat","magnesium-nitraat"],"en":["magnesium nitrate","magnesiumnitrate","magnesium-nitrate"]},"explain":{"af":"Die metaal (magnesium, Mg²⁺) word eerste genoem, gevolg deur die naam van die saamgestelde ioon (nitraat, NO₃⁻): magnesiumnitraat. Twee NO₃⁻-ione balanseer die +2-lading.","en":"The metal (magnesium, Mg²⁺) is named first, followed by the name of the polyatomic ion (nitrate, NO₃⁻): magnesium nitrate. Two NO₃⁻ ions balance the +2 charge."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel atome in totaal is daar in een formule-eenheid ammoniumkarbonaat, (NH₄)₂CO₃? ___","en":"How many atoms in total are there in one formula unit of ammonium carbonate, (NH₄)₂CO₃? ___"},"answers":{"af":["14","14 atome"],"en":["14","14 atoms"]},"explain":{"af":"Die 2 buite die hakie vermenigvuldig alles binne: 2 N en 2 × 4 = 8 H. Daarby kom 1 C en 3 O. Totaal: 2 + 8 + 1 + 3 = 14 atome. 'n Algemene fout is om net 1 N en 4 H te tel (9 atome).","en":"The 2 outside the bracket multiplies everything inside: 2 N and 2 × 4 = 8 H. Add 1 C and 3 O. Total: 2 + 8 + 1 + 3 = 14 atoms. A common mistake is to count only 1 N and 4 H (9 atoms)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee wit vaste stowwe word stadig verhit. Stof P smelt presies by 801 °C. Stof Q begin by 150 °C smelt en is eers by 180 °C heeltemal gesmelt. Watter gevolgtrekking is korrek?","en":"Two white solids are heated slowly. Substance P melts at exactly 801 °C. Substance Q starts melting at 150 °C and has only melted completely at 180 °C. Which conclusion is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"P is 'n mengsel en Q is 'n suiwer stof.","en":"P is a mixture and Q is a pure substance."},{"af":"Albei is suiwer stowwe, want albei smelt.","en":"Both are pure substances, because both melt."},{"af":"Albei is mengsels, want albei is wit vaste stowwe.","en":"Both are mixtures, because both are white solids."},{"af":"P is 'n suiwer stof en Q is 'n mengsel.","en":"P is a pure substance and Q is a mixture."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Suiwer stof het 'n skerp, vaste smeltpunt (P: presies 801 °C – dit is die smeltpunt van suiwer natriumchloried). 'n Mengsel smelt oor 'n temperatuurgebied (Q: 150–180 °C). Die kleur sê niks oor suiwerheid nie.","en":"A pure substance has a sharp, fixed melting point (P: exactly 801 °C – the melting point of pure sodium chloride). A mixture melts over a range of temperatures (Q: 150–180 °C). The colour tells you nothing about purity."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Element X is 'n blink, bros vaste stof. Sy elektriese geleidingsvermoë neem toe wanneer dit verhit word. Watter element is X waarskynlik?","en":"Element X is a shiny, brittle solid. Its electrical conductivity increases when it is heated. Which element is X most likely?"},"options":[{"af":"Silikon","en":"Silicon"},{"af":"Koper","en":"Copper"},{"af":"Swawel","en":"Sulfur"},{"af":"Yster","en":"Iron"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Silikon is 'n metalloïed: dit lyk blink, maar is bros, en as halfgeleier neem sy geleidingsvermoë toe met temperatuur. Koper en yster is metale: smeebaar (nie bros nie), en hul geleidingsvermoë neem áf as hulle warmer word. Swawel is 'n dowwe nie-metaal en 'n isolator.","en":"Silicon is a metalloid: it looks shiny but is brittle, and as a semiconductor its conductivity increases with temperature. Copper and iron are metals: malleable (not brittle), and their conductivity decreases as they get hotter. Sulfur is a dull non-metal and an insulator."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo sê: \"Die kraanwater in ons huis in Brits is 'n suiwer stof, want dit is helder en jy kan niks anders daarin sien nie.\" Watter stelling evalueer sy bewering die beste?","en":"Thabo says: \"The tap water in our house in Brits is a pure substance, because it is clear and you cannot see anything else in it.\" Which statement best evaluates his claim?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: as jy niks anders kan sien nie, is dit suiwer.","en":"He is right: if you cannot see anything else, it is pure."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: kraanwater bevat opgeloste soute en chloor, dus is dit 'n homogene mengsel.","en":"He is wrong: tap water contains dissolved salts and chlorine, so it is a homogeneous mixture."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: kraanwater is 'n heterogene mengsel, want dit bevat opgeloste stowwe.","en":"He is wrong: tap water is a heterogeneous mixture, because it contains dissolved substances."},{"af":"Hy is reg: water is 'n verbinding, dus is alle water 'n suiwer stof.","en":"He is right: water is a compound, so all water is a pure substance."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Helder beteken net dat die mengsel eenvormig is – opgeloste stowwe is onsigbaar. Kraanwater bevat opgeloste soute (ione) en chloor wat by die suiweringsaanleg bygevoeg word, dus is dit 'n homogene (nie heterogene) mengsel. Net gedistilleerde water is suiwer H₂O.","en":"Clear only means the mixture is uniform – dissolved substances are invisible. Tap water contains dissolved salts (ions) and chlorine added at the purification plant, so it is a homogeneous (not heterogeneous) mixture. Only distilled water is pure H₂O."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-toestande-kmt","title":{"af":"Toestande van materie en die kinetiese molekulêre teorie","en":"States of matter and the kinetic molecular theory"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die drie toestande van materie en faseveranderinge met die kinetiese molekulêre teorie kan verduidelik, verhittings- en afkoelingskurwes kan interpreteer, en diffusie en Brownbeweging kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to explain the three states of matter and phase changes with the kinetic molecular theory, interpret heating and cooling curves, and describe diffusion and Brownian motion."},"summary":{"af":"## Die drie toestande van materie\n\n| | Vaste stof | Vloeistof | Gas |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Vorm en volume | vaste vorm en volume | vaste volume; neem die vorm van die houer aan | geen vaste vorm of volume nie; vul die houer |\n| Rangskikking | dig gepak in 'n reëlmatige patroon | naby mekaar, maar ongeorden | ver uitmekaar, lukraak |\n| Beweging | vibreer om vaste posisies | gly by mekaar verby | beweeg vinnig in alle rigtings |\n| Kragte tussen deeltjies | sterk | swakker | baie swak |\n| Saamdrukbaar? | nee | amper nie | ja, maklik |\n\n## Die kinetiese molekulêre teorie (KMT)\n\nDie KMT verduidelik die eienskappe van materie met die beweging van deeltjies:\n\n1. Materie bestaan uit klein deeltjies (atome, molekules of ione) wat **voortdurend beweeg**.\n2. Daar is **ruimtes** tussen die deeltjies.\n3. Daar is **aantrekkingskragte** tussen die deeltjies; hulle is sterker hoe nader die deeltjies aan mekaar is.\n4. Alle deeltjies het energie. Deeltjies in 'n vaste stof het die minste energie en dié in 'n gas die meeste.\n5. Die **temperatuur** van 'n stof is 'n maatstaf van die **gemiddelde kinetiese energie** van sy deeltjies.\n6. 'n **Faseverandering** kan plaasvind wanneer die energie van die deeltjies verander.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Deeltjies word nie groter as 'n stof verhit word nie – hulle beweeg vinniger en die ruimtes tussen hulle word groter. Deeltjies in 'n vaste stof staan ook nie stil nie; hulle vibreer.\n\n## Faseveranderinge\n\n| Proses | Verandering | Energie |\n|---|---|---|\n| Smelt | vaste stof → vloeistof | geabsorbeer |\n| Verdamping / kook | vloeistof → gas | geabsorbeer |\n| Sublimasie | vaste stof → gas (direk) | geabsorbeer |\n| Vries (stolling) | vloeistof → vaste stof | vrygestel |\n| Kondensasie | gas → vloeistof | vrygestel |\n| Afsetting (resublimasie) | gas → vaste stof (direk) | vrygestel |\n\nVoorbeelde van sublimasie: jodium, droë ys (vaste CO_{2}) en mottebolle. Ryp op die gras is afsetting.\n\n- **Smeltpunt:** die temperatuur waarby 'n vaste stof van fase verander om 'n vloeistof te word. Vir 'n suiwer stof is die **vriespunt** dieselfde temperatuur.\n- **Kookpunt:** die temperatuur waarby 'n vloeistof van fase verander om 'n gas te word.\n- **Verdamping teenoor kook:** verdamping gebeur by **enige** temperatuur, net aan die **oppervlak** – die vinnigste deeltjies ontsnap. Daarom koel sweet jou af. Kook gebeur by die kookpunt, **deur die hele vloeistof** (borrels vorm).\n- Hoe sterker die kragte tussen die deeltjies, hoe hoër die smelt- en kookpunt.\n\n**Toestand by 'n gegewe temperatuur T:** T laer as die smeltpunt → vaste stof; T tussen die smelt- en kookpunt → vloeistof; T hoër as die kookpunt → gas. Etanol (smeltpunt −114 °C, kookpunt 78 °C) is dus 'n vloeistof by 25 °C.\n\n## Die verhittingskurwe van water (in woorde)\n\nYs by −20 °C word teen 'n konstante tempo verhit, en die temperatuur word teen die tyd geplot:\n\n1. **Skuins lyn (−20 °C → 0 °C):** net ys. Die deeltjies vibreer vinniger; E_{k} en temperatuur styg.\n2. **Eerste plato (horisontaal by 0 °C):** die ys **smelt** – ys en water is saam teenwoordig. Die temperatuur bly konstant, want al die energie word gebruik om die **aantrekkingskragte tussen die deeltjies te oorkom**, nie om E_{k} te verhoog nie.\n3. **Skuins lyn (0 °C → 100 °C):** net vloeibare water; E_{k} styg.\n4. **Tweede plato (horisontaal by 100 °C):** die water **kook** – water en stoom is saam teenwoordig. Hierdie plato is baie **langer** as die eerste, want baie meer energie is nodig om die deeltjies heeltemal van mekaar te skei (gas) as om hulle net los te maak (vloeistof).\n5. **Skuins lyn bo 100 °C:** net stoom.\n\nDie **afkoelingskurwe** is die omgekeerde: plato's by 100 °C (kondensasie) en 0 °C (vries). Op 'n plato bly die temperatuur konstant omdat energie **vrygestel** word terwyl aantrekkingskragte tussen die deeltjies vorm; dit vervang die hitte wat na die omgewing verlore gaan.\n\n> **Onthou!** Op 'n plato is die temperatuur (en dus die gemiddelde E_{k}) konstant, al absorbeer of verloor die stof steeds energie. 'n Mengsel het nie 'n skerp plato nie; dit smelt oor 'n temperatuurgebied.\n\n## Diffusie en Brownbeweging – bewyse dat deeltjies beweeg\n\n- **Diffusie:** die beweging van deeltjies vanaf 'n gebied met 'n hoë konsentrasie na 'n gebied met 'n lae konsentrasie. Jy ruik die boerewors op die buurman se braai omdat die geurdeeltjies deur die lug diffundeer. 'n Kaliumpermanganaatkristal in water kleur stadig die hele beker pers. Diffusie is vinniger in gasse as in vloeistowwe, en vinniger by hoër temperature (die deeltjies beweeg vinniger).\n- **Brownbeweging:** die lukrake sigsagbeweging van klein deeltjies (bv. rookdeeltjies in lug of stuifmeeldeeltjies in water) wat veroorsaak word deur botsings met die onsigbare, vinnig bewegende deeltjies van die gas of vloeistof. Robert Brown het dit in 1827 waargeneem.","en":"## The three states of matter\n\n| | Solid | Liquid | Gas |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Shape and volume | fixed shape and volume | fixed volume; takes the shape of the container | no fixed shape or volume; fills the container |\n| Arrangement | closely packed in a regular pattern | close together, but disordered | far apart, random |\n| Movement | vibrate about fixed positions | slide past each other | move fast in all directions |\n| Forces between particles | strong | weaker | very weak |\n| Compressible? | no | hardly | yes, easily |\n\n## The kinetic molecular theory (KMT)\n\nThe KMT explains the properties of matter in terms of the movement of particles:\n\n1. Matter is made up of tiny particles (atoms, molecules or ions) that are **constantly moving**.\n2. There are **spaces** between the particles.\n3. There are **attractive forces** between the particles; they are stronger the closer the particles are to each other.\n4. All particles have energy. Particles in a solid have the least energy and those in a gas the most.\n5. The **temperature** of a substance is a measure of the **average kinetic energy** of its particles.\n6. A **phase change** can take place when the energy of the particles changes.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Particles do not get bigger when a substance is heated – they move faster and the spaces between them get bigger. Particles in a solid are also not standing still; they vibrate.\n\n## Phase changes\n\n| Process | Change | Energy |\n|---|---|---|\n| Melting | solid → liquid | absorbed |\n| Evaporation / boiling | liquid → gas | absorbed |\n| Sublimation | solid → gas (directly) | absorbed |\n| Freezing (solidification) | liquid → solid | released |\n| Condensation | gas → liquid | released |\n| Deposition (resublimation) | gas → solid (directly) | released |\n\nExamples of sublimation: iodine, dry ice (solid CO_{2}) and mothballs. Frost on the grass is deposition.\n\n- **Melting point:** the temperature at which a solid changes its phase to become a liquid. For a pure substance the **freezing point** is the same temperature.\n- **Boiling point:** the temperature at which a liquid changes its phase to become a gas.\n- **Evaporation versus boiling:** evaporation happens at **any** temperature, only at the **surface** – the fastest particles escape. That is why sweat cools you down. Boiling happens at the boiling point, **throughout the liquid** (bubbles form).\n- The stronger the forces between the particles, the higher the melting and boiling point.\n\n**State at a given temperature T:** T below the melting point → solid; T between the melting and boiling point → liquid; T above the boiling point → gas. Ethanol (melting point −114 °C, boiling point 78 °C) is therefore a liquid at 25 °C.\n\n## The heating curve of water (in words)\n\nIce at −20 °C is heated at a constant rate, and the temperature is plotted against time:\n\n1. **Sloping line (−20 °C → 0 °C):** only ice. The particles vibrate faster; E_{k} and temperature rise.\n2. **First plateau (horizontal at 0 °C):** the ice **melts** – ice and water are present together. The temperature stays constant, because all the energy is used to **overcome the attractive forces between the particles**, not to increase E_{k}.\n3. **Sloping line (0 °C → 100 °C):** only liquid water; E_{k} rises.\n4. **Second plateau (horizontal at 100 °C):** the water **boils** – water and steam are present together. This plateau is much **longer** than the first, because much more energy is needed to separate the particles completely (gas) than to just loosen them (liquid).\n5. **Sloping line above 100 °C:** only steam.\n\nThe **cooling curve** is the reverse: plateaus at 100 °C (condensation) and 0 °C (freezing). On a plateau the temperature stays constant because energy is **released** as attractive forces form between the particles; this replaces the heat lost to the surroundings.\n\n> **Remember!** On a plateau the temperature (and therefore the average E_{k}) is constant, even though the substance is still absorbing or losing energy. A mixture does not have a sharp plateau; it melts over a range of temperatures.\n\n## Diffusion and Brownian motion – evidence that particles move\n\n- **Diffusion:** the movement of particles from a region of high concentration to a region of low concentration. You smell the boerewors on the neighbour's braai because the smell particles diffuse through the air. A potassium permanganate crystal in water slowly colours the whole beaker purple. Diffusion is faster in gases than in liquids, and faster at higher temperatures (the particles move faster).\n- **Brownian motion:** the random zigzag movement of small particles (e.g. smoke particles in air or pollen particles in water) caused by collisions with the invisible, fast-moving particles of the gas or liquid. Robert Brown observed it in 1827."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kinetiese molekulêre teorie","en":"Kinetic molecular theory"},"def":{"af":"Die teorie dat materie uit deeltjies bestaan wat voortdurend beweeg, met ruimtes en aantrekkingskragte tussen hulle; die energie van die deeltjies bepaal die toestand van die stof.","en":"The theory that matter consists of particles that are constantly moving, with spaces and attractive forces between them; the energy of the particles determines the state of the substance."}},{"term":{"af":"Temperatuur","en":"Temperature"},"def":{"af":"'n Maatstaf van die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies in 'n stof.","en":"A measure of the average kinetic energy of the particles in a substance."}},{"term":{"af":"Smeltpunt","en":"Melting point"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vaste stof van fase verander om 'n vloeistof te word.","en":"The temperature at which a solid changes its phase to become a liquid."}},{"term":{"af":"Kookpunt","en":"Boiling point"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vloeistof van fase verander om 'n gas te word.","en":"The temperature at which a liquid changes its phase to become a gas."}},{"term":{"af":"Vriespunt","en":"Freezing point"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vloeistof van fase verander om 'n vaste stof te word; vir 'n suiwer stof is dit gelyk aan die smeltpunt.","en":"The temperature at which a liquid changes its phase to become a solid; for a pure substance it equals the melting point."}},{"term":{"af":"Verdamping","en":"Evaporation"},"def":{"af":"Die faseverandering van vloeistof na gas; dit vind by enige temperatuur aan die oppervlak van 'n vloeistof plaas.","en":"The phase change from liquid to gas; it takes place at any temperature at the surface of a liquid."}},{"term":{"af":"Kondensasie","en":"Condensation"},"def":{"af":"Die faseverandering van gas na vloeistof; energie word vrygestel.","en":"The phase change from gas to liquid; energy is released."}},{"term":{"af":"Sublimasie","en":"Sublimation"},"def":{"af":"Die faseverandering waar 'n vaste stof direk in 'n gas verander sonder om eers 'n vloeistof te word.","en":"The phase change in which a solid changes directly into a gas without first becoming a liquid."}},{"term":{"af":"Diffusie","en":"Diffusion"},"def":{"af":"Die beweging van deeltjies vanaf 'n gebied met 'n hoë konsentrasie na 'n gebied met 'n lae konsentrasie.","en":"The movement of particles from a region of high concentration to a region of low concentration."}},{"term":{"af":"Brownbeweging","en":"Brownian motion"},"def":{"af":"Die lukrake beweging van klein deeltjies in 'n vloeistof of gas, veroorsaak deur botsings met die vinnig bewegende deeltjies van die vloeistof of gas.","en":"The random movement of small particles in a liquid or gas, caused by collisions with the fast-moving particles of the liquid or gas."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer die verhittingskurwe van water","en":"Interpret the heating curve of water"},"problem":{"af":"Ys by −20 °C word in 'n beker teen 'n konstante tempo verhit totdat dit stoom by 110 °C is. Die temperatuur-teen-tyd-grafiek het vyf dele: AB styg van −20 °C tot 0 °C; BC is horisontaal by 0 °C; CD styg van 0 °C tot 100 °C; DE is horisontaal by 100 °C en baie langer as BC; EF styg van 100 °C tot 110 °C. (a) Watter fases is in BC en in DE teenwoordig? (b) Verduidelik waarom die temperatuur in BC konstant bly hoewel daar steeds verhit word. (c) Wat gebeur met die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies in DE? (d) Waarom is DE langer as BC?","en":"Ice at −20 °C in a beaker is heated at a constant rate until it is steam at 110 °C. The temperature-versus-time graph has five parts: AB rises from −20 °C to 0 °C; BC is horizontal at 0 °C; CD rises from 0 °C to 100 °C; DE is horizontal at 100 °C and much longer than BC; EF rises from 100 °C to 110 °C. (a) Which phases are present in BC and in DE? (b) Explain why the temperature stays constant in BC although heating continues. (c) What happens to the average kinetic energy of the particles in DE? (d) Why is DE longer than BC?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) BC is die smeltplato: **vaste stof (ys) en vloeistof (water)** is saam teenwoordig. DE is die kookplato: **vloeistof (water) en gas (stoom)**.","en":"(a) BC is the melting plateau: **solid (ice) and liquid (water)** are present together. DE is the boiling plateau: **liquid (water) and gas (steam)**."},{"af":"(b) Die energie wat geabsorbeer word, word gebruik om die **aantrekkingskragte tussen die watermolekules te oorkom** (die potensiële energie neem toe), en nie om die kinetiese energie te verhoog nie. Daarom bly die temperatuur by 0 °C.","en":"(b) The energy absorbed is used to **overcome the attractive forces between the water molecules** (the potential energy increases), not to increase the kinetic energy. That is why the temperature stays at 0 °C."},{"af":"(c) Die temperatuur bly 100 °C, en temperatuur is 'n maatstaf van die gemiddelde kinetiese energie – dus bly die gemiddelde E_{k} **konstant**.","en":"(c) The temperature stays at 100 °C, and temperature is a measure of the average kinetic energy – so the average E_{k} stays **constant**."},{"af":"(d) Om 'n vloeistof in 'n gas te verander, moet die deeltjies **heeltemal van mekaar geskei** word. Tydens smelt word hulle net losgemaak sodat hulle by mekaar kan verbygly. Kook vra dus baie meer energie, en teen dieselfde verhittingstempo duur dit langer.","en":"(d) To change a liquid into a gas, the particles must be **separated from each other completely**. During melting they are only loosened so that they can slide past each other. Boiling therefore needs much more energy, and at the same heating rate it takes longer."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) BC: ys + water; DE: water + stoom (b) energie oorkom die aantrekkingskragte (c) bly konstant (d) meer energie nodig om deeltjies heeltemal te skei","en":"(a) BC: ice + water; DE: water + steam (b) energy overcomes the attractive forces (c) stays constant (d) more energy needed to separate particles completely"}},{"title":{"af":"Toestand uit smelt- en kookpunt","en":"State from melting and boiling point"},"problem":{"af":"Vier stowwe het die volgende smelt- en kookpunte. A: −219 °C en −183 °C. B: −39 °C en 357 °C. C: 44 °C en 280 °C. D: 1 538 °C en 2 862 °C. (a) Gee die toestand van elke stof by kamertemperatuur (25 °C). (b) Watter stof het die sterkste kragte tussen sy deeltjies? (c) In watter toestand is C by 100 °C?","en":"Four substances have the following melting and boiling points. A: −219 °C and −183 °C. B: −39 °C and 357 °C. C: 44 °C and 280 °C. D: 1 538 °C and 2 862 °C. (a) Give the state of each substance at room temperature (25 °C). (b) Which substance has the strongest forces between its particles? (c) In which state is C at 100 °C?"},"steps":[{"af":"Reël: T < smeltpunt → vaste stof; smeltpunt < T < kookpunt → vloeistof; T > kookpunt → gas.","en":"Rule: T < melting point → solid; melting point < T < boiling point → liquid; T > boiling point → gas."},{"af":"(a) A: 25 °C > −183 °C → **gas**. B: −39 °C < 25 °C < 357 °C → **vloeistof**. C: 25 °C < 44 °C → **vaste stof**. D: 25 °C < 1 538 °C → **vaste stof**.","en":"(a) A: 25 °C > −183 °C → **gas**. B: −39 °C < 25 °C < 357 °C → **liquid**. C: 25 °C < 44 °C → **solid**. D: 25 °C < 1 538 °C → **solid**."},{"af":"(b) Hoe sterker die kragte tussen die deeltjies, hoe meer energie is nodig om hulle te skei, en hoe hoër die smelt- en kookpunt. D het die hoogste smelt- en kookpunt → **D**.","en":"(b) The stronger the forces between the particles, the more energy is needed to separate them, and the higher the melting and boiling point. D has the highest melting and boiling point → **D**."},{"af":"(c) 44 °C < 100 °C < 280 °C → C is 'n **vloeistof** by 100 °C.","en":"(c) 44 °C < 100 °C < 280 °C → C is a **liquid** at 100 °C."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) A gas, B vloeistof, C vaste stof, D vaste stof (b) D (c) vloeistof","en":"(a) A gas, B liquid, C solid, D solid (b) D (c) liquid"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik diffusie met die KMT","en":"Explain diffusion with the KMT"},"problem":{"af":"Pa braai boerewors in Brits, en binne 'n paar sekondes ruik die buurkinders dit oor die muur. (a) Noem die proses. (b) Verduidelik dit met die kinetiese molekulêre teorie. (c) 'n Leerder laat val 'n kaliumpermanganaatkristal in 'n beker koue water en een in 'n beker warm water. In watter beker versprei die pers kleur vinniger, en hoekom?","en":"Dad is cooking boerewors on the braai in Brits, and within a few seconds the neighbours' children smell it over the wall. (a) Name the process. (b) Explain it with the kinetic molecular theory. (c) A learner drops a potassium permanganate crystal into a beaker of cold water and one into a beaker of hot water. In which beaker does the purple colour spread faster, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Diffusie** – die beweging van deeltjies vanaf 'n gebied met 'n hoë konsentrasie na 'n gebied met 'n lae konsentrasie.","en":"(a) **Diffusion** – the movement of particles from a region of high concentration to a region of low concentration."},{"af":"(b) Volgens die KMT beweeg die geurdeeltjies voortdurend en lukraak, en daar is groot ruimtes tussen die lugdeeltjies. Die geurdeeltjies beweeg dus weg van die braaivleis (hoë konsentrasie) en versprei deur die lug na die buurkinders (lae konsentrasie).","en":"(b) According to the KMT the smell particles move constantly and randomly, and there are large spaces between the air particles. The smell particles therefore move away from the meat (high concentration) and spread through the air to the neighbours' children (low concentration)."},{"af":"(c) In die **warm** water. 'n Hoër temperatuur beteken 'n hoër gemiddelde kinetiese energie, dus beweeg die deeltjies vinniger en diffundeer die kleur vinniger.","en":"(c) In the **hot** water. A higher temperature means a higher average kinetic energy, so the particles move faster and the colour diffuses faster."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Diffusie (b) geurdeeltjies beweeg voortdurend en lukraak van hoë na lae konsentrasie (c) warm water – hoër gemiddelde Eₖ","en":"(a) Diffusion (b) smell particles move constantly and randomly from high to low concentration (c) hot water – higher average Eₖ"}},{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer 'n afkoelingskurwe","en":"Interpret a cooling curve"},"problem":{"af":"Vloeibare stof X by 90 °C word in 'n proefbuis gelaat om af te koel. Die temperatuur daal tot 69 °C, bly 'n ruk lank konstant by 69 °C en daal dan weer tot 40 °C. (a) Wat is die smeltpunt van X? (b) Watter fases is teenwoordig terwyl die temperatuur by 69 °C konstant bly? (c) Verduidelik waarom die temperatuur konstant bly hoewel X hitte aan die omgewing afgee. (d) Is X waarskynlik 'n suiwer stof? Gee 'n rede.","en":"Liquid substance X at 90 °C is left in a test tube to cool. The temperature drops to 69 °C, stays constant at 69 °C for a while and then drops again to 40 °C. (a) What is the melting point of X? (b) Which phases are present while the temperature stays constant at 69 °C? (c) Explain why the temperature stays constant although X gives off heat to the surroundings. (d) Is X probably a pure substance? Give a reason."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die plato is by 69 °C. Dit is die vriespunt, en vir 'n suiwer stof is die smeltpunt dieselfde → **69 °C**.","en":"(a) The plateau is at 69 °C. That is the freezing point, and for a pure substance the melting point is the same → **69 °C**."},{"af":"(b) Tydens die plato vries X: **vloeistof en vaste stof** is saam teenwoordig.","en":"(b) During the plateau X freezes: **liquid and solid** are present together."},{"af":"(c) Terwyl X vries, kom die deeltjies nader aan mekaar en vorm aantrekkingskragte. Daarby word **energie vrygestel**, wat die hitte vervang wat na die omgewing verlore gaan – dus bly die gemiddelde kinetiese energie, en dus die temperatuur, konstant.","en":"(c) While X freezes, the particles move closer together and attractive forces form. This **releases energy**, which replaces the heat lost to the surroundings – so the average kinetic energy, and therefore the temperature, stays constant."},{"af":"(d) **Ja**: X vries by een skerp, vaste temperatuur (een plato). 'n Mengsel sou oor 'n temperatuurgebied stol.","en":"(d) **Yes**: X freezes at one sharp, fixed temperature (one plateau). A mixture would solidify over a range of temperatures."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 69 °C (b) vloeistof en vaste stof (c) energie word vrygestel terwyl aantrekkingskragte vorm (d) ja – skerp vriespunt","en":"(a) 69 °C (b) liquid and solid (c) energy is released as attractive forces form (d) yes – sharp freezing point"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter toestand vibreer die deeltjies net om vaste posisies?","en":"In which state do the particles only vibrate about fixed positions?"},"options":[{"af":"Gas","en":"Gas"},{"af":"Vaste stof","en":"Solid"},{"af":"Vloeistof","en":"Liquid"},{"af":"In al drie toestande","en":"In all three states"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In 'n vaste stof is die deeltjies dig gepak en sterk aan mekaar gebind, so hulle kan net om vaste posisies vibreer. In 'n vloeistof gly hulle by mekaar verby, en in 'n gas beweeg hulle vinnig in alle rigtings.","en":"In a solid the particles are closely packed and strongly attracted to each other, so they can only vibrate about fixed positions. In a liquid they slide past each other, and in a gas they move fast in all directions."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Tydens kondensasie absorbeer 'n stof hitte-energie uit die omgewing.","en":"During condensation a substance absorbs heat energy from the surroundings."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Kondensasie (gas → vloeistof) stel energie vry, want aantrekkingskragte vorm tussen die deeltjies. Smelt, verdamping en sublimasie absorbeer energie.","en":"False. Condensation (gas → liquid) releases energy, because attractive forces form between the particles. Melting, evaporation and sublimation absorb energy."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vaste stof van fase verander om 'n vloeistof te word, word die ___ genoem.","en":"The temperature at which a solid changes its phase to become a liquid is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["smeltpunt","die smeltpunt"],"en":["melting point","the melting point","meltingpoint"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit is die definisie van die smeltpunt. Vir 'n suiwer stof is die vriespunt (vloeistof → vaste stof) by dieselfde temperatuur, bv. 0 °C vir water.","en":"This is the definition of the melting point. For a pure substance the freezing point (liquid → solid) is at the same temperature, e.g. 0 °C for water."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke proses by die faseverandering.","en":"Match each process to the phase change."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Smelt","en":"Melting"},"r":{"af":"vaste stof → vloeistof","en":"solid → liquid"}},{"l":{"af":"Vries","en":"Freezing"},"r":{"af":"vloeistof → vaste stof","en":"liquid → solid"}},{"l":{"af":"Kook","en":"Boiling"},"r":{"af":"vloeistof → gas","en":"liquid → gas"}},{"l":{"af":"Kondensasie","en":"Condensation"},"r":{"af":"gas → vloeistof","en":"gas → liquid"}},{"l":{"af":"Sublimasie","en":"Sublimation"},"r":{"af":"vaste stof → gas","en":"solid → gas"}}],"explain":{"af":"Smelt en vries is mekaar se omgekeerde, net soos kook en kondensasie. By sublimasie slaan die stof die vloeistoffase oor, bv. droë ys (vaste CO₂).","en":"Melting and freezing are each other's reverse, just like boiling and condensation. In sublimation the substance skips the liquid phase, e.g. dry ice (solid CO₂)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Volgens die kinetiese molekulêre teorie is die temperatuur van 'n stof 'n maatstaf van die …","en":"According to the kinetic molecular theory, the temperature of a substance is a measure of the …"},"options":[{"af":"totale energie van al die deeltjies.","en":"total energy of all the particles."},{"af":"grootte van die deeltjies.","en":"size of the particles."},{"af":"gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies.","en":"average kinetic energy of the particles."},{"af":"kragte tussen die deeltjies.","en":"forces between the particles."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Temperatuur meet die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies. Dit is nie die totale energie nie (dit sluit ook potensiële energie in), en deeltjies word nie groter as die temperatuur styg nie – hulle beweeg net vinniger.","en":"Temperature measures the average kinetic energy of the particles. It is not the total energy (that also includes potential energy), and particles do not get bigger as the temperature rises – they just move faster."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder kyk deur 'n mikroskoop na rookdeeltjies in lug. Die rookdeeltjies beweeg lukraak in 'n sigsagpatroon. Wat bewys hierdie Brownbeweging?","en":"A learner looks at smoke particles in air through a microscope. The smoke particles move randomly in a zigzag pattern. What does this Brownian motion prove?"},"options":[{"af":"Die lugdeeltjies beweeg voortdurend en lukraak en bots teen die rookdeeltjies.","en":"The air particles move constantly and randomly and collide with the smoke particles."},{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies is lewendig en beweeg uit hulle eie.","en":"The smoke particles are alive and move on their own."},{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies word groter omdat die lug warm is.","en":"The smoke particles get bigger because the air is warm."},{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies trek mekaar sterk aan.","en":"The smoke particles attract each other strongly."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies word van alle kante deur onsigbare, vinnig bewegende lugdeeltjies gestamp. Omdat die botsings lukraak is, skuif die rookdeeltjies in 'n sigsagpatroon. Dit is bewys dat die deeltjies van 'n gas voortdurend beweeg.","en":"The smoke particles are bumped from all sides by invisible, fast-moving air particles. Because the collisions are random, the smoke particles move in a zigzag pattern. This is evidence that the particles of a gas move constantly."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Diffusie vind vinniger plaas by 'n hoër temperatuur.","en":"Diffusion takes place faster at a higher temperature."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. By 'n hoër temperatuur is die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies hoër, dus beweeg hulle vinniger en versprei hulle vinniger – bv. kaliumpermanganaat versprei vinniger in warm water as in koue water.","en":"True. At a higher temperature the average kinetic energy of the particles is higher, so they move faster and spread faster – e.g. potassium permanganate spreads faster in hot water than in cold water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Terwyl ys smelt, bly die temperatuur by 0 °C, want die energie wat geabsorbeer word, word gebruik om die ___ tussen die deeltjies te oorkom.","en":"While ice melts, the temperature stays at 0 °C, because the energy absorbed is used to overcome the ___ between the particles."},"answers":{"af":["kragte","aantrekkingskragte","intermolekulêre kragte","intermolekulere kragte","aantrekkingskrag"],"en":["forces","attractive forces","intermolecular forces","forces of attraction"]},"explain":{"af":"Op die plato gaan die energie in die oorkoming van die aantrekkingskragte tussen die watermolekules, nie in die verhoging van hul kinetiese energie nie. Daarom bly die temperatuur konstant totdat al die ys gesmelt het.","en":"On the plateau the energy goes into overcoming the attractive forces between the water molecules, not into increasing their kinetic energy. That is why the temperature stays constant until all the ice has melted."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Suiwer asynsuur het 'n smeltpunt van 17 °C en 'n kookpunt van 118 °C. In watter toestand is dit op 'n winteroggend in Brits as die temperatuur 8 °C is?","en":"Pure acetic acid has a melting point of 17 °C and a boiling point of 118 °C. In which state is it on a winter morning in Brits when the temperature is 8 °C?"},"options":[{"af":"Vloeistof","en":"Liquid"},{"af":"Gas","en":"Gas"},{"af":"Vaste stof en vloeistof saam","en":"Solid and liquid together"},{"af":"Vaste stof","en":"Solid"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"8 °C is laer as die smeltpunt (17 °C), dus is die asynsuur 'n vaste stof. By kamertemperatuur (25 °C) sou dit 'n vloeistof wees – moenie outomaties 25 °C gebruik as die vraag 'n ander temperatuur gee nie. Vaste stof en vloeistof is net saam teenwoordig presies by die smeltpunt.","en":"8 °C is below the melting point (17 °C), so the acetic acid is a solid. At room temperature (25 °C) it would be a liquid – do not automatically use 25 °C when the question gives another temperature. Solid and liquid are only present together exactly at the melting point."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Stof het 'n smeltpunt van −23 °C en 'n kookpunt van 77 °C. By 90 °C is die stof 'n ___ (vaste stof, vloeistof of gas).","en":"A substance has a melting point of −23 °C and a boiling point of 77 °C. At 90 °C the substance is a ___ (solid, liquid or gas)."},"answers":{"af":["gas","'n gas","gasvormig"],"en":["gas","a gas","gaseous"]},"explain":{"af":"90 °C is hoër as die kookpunt (77 °C), dus het die stof reeds gekook en is dit 'n gas. Dit sou 'n vloeistof wees tussen −23 °C en 77 °C.","en":"90 °C is above the boiling point (77 °C), so the substance has already boiled and is a gas. It would be a liquid between −23 °C and 77 °C."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Suiwer vaste stof word teen 'n konstante tempo verhit. Die temperatuur styg van 20 °C tot 80 °C, bly dan 5 minute lank konstant by 80 °C en styg daarna weer. Watter stelling oor die 5 minute by 80 °C is korrek?","en":"A pure solid is heated at a constant rate. The temperature rises from 20 °C to 80 °C, then stays constant at 80 °C for 5 minutes and then rises again. Which statement about the 5 minutes at 80 °C is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die stof kook, en die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies neem toe.","en":"The substance boils, and the average kinetic energy of the particles increases."},{"af":"Die stof smelt; die energie oorkom die kragte tussen die deeltjies, en die gemiddelde kinetiese energie bly konstant.","en":"The substance melts; the energy overcomes the forces between the particles, and the average kinetic energy stays constant."},{"af":"Die stof smelt, en die deeltjies word groter.","en":"The substance melts, and the particles get bigger."},{"af":"Geen energie word geabsorbeer nie, want die temperatuur verander nie.","en":"No energy is absorbed, because the temperature does not change."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste plato van 'n vaste stof is die smeltplato (80 °C is die smeltpunt). Die stof absorbeer steeds energie, maar dit word gebruik om die kragte tussen die deeltjies te oorkom. Omdat die temperatuur konstant is, bly die gemiddelde Eₖ konstant. Deeltjies word nooit groter nie.","en":"The first plateau of a solid is the melting plateau (80 °C is the melting point). The substance still absorbs energy, but it is used to overcome the forces between the particles. Because the temperature is constant, the average Eₖ stays constant. Particles never get bigger."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Water word teen 'n konstante tempo van ys tot stoom verhit. Die plato by 100 °C is baie langer as die plato by 0 °C. Wat is die beste verduideliking?","en":"Water is heated at a constant rate from ice to steam. The plateau at 100 °C is much longer than the plateau at 0 °C. What is the best explanation?"},"options":[{"af":"Meer energie is nodig om die deeltjies heeltemal van mekaar te skei (gas) as om hulle net los te maak sodat hulle by mekaar kan verbygly (vloeistof).","en":"More energy is needed to separate the particles completely (gas) than to only loosen them so they can slide past each other (liquid)."},{"af":"100 °C is 'n hoër temperatuur as 0 °C, dus duur dit langer om dit te bereik.","en":"100 °C is a higher temperature than 0 °C, so it takes longer to reach it."},{"af":"Die kinetiese energie van die deeltjies neem tydens kook toe, maar nie tydens smelt nie.","en":"The kinetic energy of the particles increases during boiling, but not during melting."},{"af":"Stoom gelei hitte beter as ys.","en":"Steam conducts heat better than ice."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die lengte van 'n plato wys hoeveel energie die faseverandering nodig het. Om vloeistof in gas te verander, moet al die aantrekkingskragte oorkom word sodat die deeltjies ver uitmekaar kan beweeg; by smelt word hulle net losgemaak. Die tyd om 100 °C te bereik, is die skuins lyn, nie die plato nie, en op albei plato's bly Eₖ konstant.","en":"The length of a plateau shows how much energy the phase change needs. To change liquid into gas, all the attractive forces must be overcome so the particles can move far apart; in melting they are only loosened. The time to reach 100 °C is the sloping line, not the plateau, and on both plateaus Eₖ stays constant."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Op 'n koue wintersoggend by Hartbeespoortdam verander waterdamp in die lug direk in ys en vorm ryp op die gras. Hierdie faseverandering is die omgekeerde van ___.","en":"On a cold winter morning at Hartbeespoort Dam, water vapour in the air changes directly into ice and forms frost on the grass. This phase change is the reverse of ___."},"answers":{"af":["sublimasie"],"en":["sublimation"]},"explain":{"af":"Gas → vaste stof sonder 'n vloeistoffase is afsetting (resublimasie), die omgekeerde van sublimasie (vaste stof → gas direk). Dit is nie kondensasie nie, want daar vorm nie eers vloeibare water nie.","en":"Gas → solid without a liquid phase is deposition (resublimation), the reverse of sublimation (solid → gas directly). It is not condensation, because no liquid water forms first."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter sê: \"Water in 'n oop bakkie by kamertemperatuur kan nie verdamp nie, want dit is ver onder die kookpunt van 100 °C.\" Watter stelling evalueer sy bewering die beste?","en":"Pieter says: \"Water in an open bowl at room temperature cannot evaporate, because it is far below the boiling point of 100 °C.\" Which statement best evaluates his claim?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: water verdamp slegs by 100 °C.","en":"He is right: water only evaporates at 100 °C."},{"af":"Hy is reg: by kamertemperatuur het die waterdeeltjies geen kinetiese energie nie.","en":"He is right: at room temperature the water particles have no kinetic energy."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: verdamping vind by enige temperatuur aan die oppervlak plaas, want sommige deeltjies het genoeg kinetiese energie om te ontsnap; kook vind by die kookpunt deur die hele vloeistof plaas.","en":"He is wrong: evaporation takes place at any temperature at the surface, because some particles have enough kinetic energy to escape; boiling takes place at the boiling point throughout the liquid."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: water verdamp omdat die deeltjies by kamertemperatuur kleiner word.","en":"He is wrong: water evaporates because the particles get smaller at room temperature."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Hy verwar verdamping met kook. Die deeltjies het verskillende kinetiese energieë; die vinnigstes aan die oppervlak ontsnap by enige temperatuur – daarom droog wasgoed sonder om te kook. Deeltjies het altyd kinetiese energie en verander nie van grootte nie.","en":"He confuses evaporation with boiling. The particles have different kinetic energies; the fastest ones at the surface escape at any temperature – that is why washing dries without boiling. Particles always have kinetic energy and do not change size."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-atoom","title":{"af":"Die atoom","en":"The atom"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die ontwikkeling van die atoommodel kan beskryf, protone, neutrone en elektrone kan tel, die relatiewe atoommassa uit isotope kan bereken en elektronkonfigurasies tot Z = 20 kan skryf.","en":"You will be able to describe how the atomic model developed, count protons, neutrons and electrons, calculate relative atomic mass from isotopes and write electron configurations up to Z = 20."},"summary":{"af":"## Atoommodelle – hoe ons idee van die atoom ontwikkel het\n\n| Wetenskaplike | Model of ontdekking |\n|---|---|\n| Dalton (1803) | Materie bestaan uit klein, harde, **ondeelbare** atome (soos klein snoekerballe); alle atome van een element is dieselfde. |\n| Thomson (1897) | Ontdek die **elektron**. **Pruimpoedingmodel:** negatiewe elektrone is in 'n positief gelaaide bol versprei. |\n| Rutherford (1911) | **Alfadeeltjie-verstrooiing** (goudfoelie): die atoom is meestal leë ruimte met 'n klein, digte, **positiewe kern** wat byna al die massa bevat; elektrone beweeg om die kern (**kernmodel**). |\n| Bohr (1913) | Elektrone beweeg in **vaste energievlakke** om die kern. 'n Elektron wat energie absorbeer, spring na 'n hoër vlak; as dit terugval, straal die atoom lig met 'n spesifieke energie uit. |\n| Chadwick (1932) | Ontdek die **neutron**, 'n neutrale deeltjie in die kern. |\n\n**Rutherford se waarnemings:** die meeste alfadeeltjies het reguit deurgegaan → die atoom is meestal leë ruimte; party is afgebuig en baie min het teruggebons → 'n klein, digte, positiewe kern stoot die positiewe alfadeeltjies af. As 'n atoom so groot soos Loftus Versfeld was, sou die kern soos 'n ertjie op die middelkol wees.\n\n**Waarom Bohr?** Volgens Rutherford se model sou bewegende elektrone energie verloor en in die kern inspiraal. Vaste energievlakke verklaar waarom atome stabiel is en net sekere kleure lig uitstraal (bv. die geel lig van natriumstraatligte).\n\n## Die deeltjies in 'n atoom\n\n| Deeltjie | Lading | Relatiewe massa | Ligging |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Proton (p^{+}) | +1 | 1 | kern |\n| Neutron (n^{0}) | 0 | 1 | kern |\n| Elektron (e^{−}) | −1 | [[1/1836]] ≈ 0 | energievlakke om die kern |\n\nProtone en neutrone saam heet **nukleone**. 'n Neutrale atoom het ewe veel protone en elektrone.\n\n- **Atoomgetal (Z):** die aantal protone in 'n atoom van 'n element. Z bepaal watter element dit is.\n- **Massagetal (A):** die aantal protone plus neutrone in die kern van 'n atoom.\n- **Neutrone = A − Z.** Notasie: ^{A}_{Z}X, bv. ^{23}_{11}Na het 11 p, 12 n en 11 e.\n- **Ione:** elektrone = Z − lading. Na^{+} het 10 e (een verloor); Cl^{−} het 18 e (een bygekry). Die aantal protone verander nooit.\n\n## Isotope\n\n**Isotope** is atome van dieselfde element met dieselfde aantal protone, maar verskillende getalle neutrone (dus verskillende massagetalle), bv. C-12, C-13 en C-14, of Cl-35 en Cl-37. Isotope het dieselfde elektronkonfigurasie en dus **dieselfde chemiese eienskappe**, maar verskillende massas. Die SAFARI-1-reaktor by Pelindaba naby Hartbeespoortdam maak radio-isotope vir mediese gebruik.\n\n## Relatiewe atoommassa\n\nDie **relatiewe atoommassa** (A_{r}) is die gemiddelde massa van 'n element se atome, met inagneming van al sy isotope en hul persentasie voorkoms, op 'n skaal waarop 'n koolstof-12-atoom 'n massa van presies 12 het. Dit het **geen eenheid** nie.\n\n**A_{r} = (massagetal_{1} × %_{1} + massagetal_{2} × %_{2} + …) ÷ 100**\n\nChloor: 75 % Cl-35 en 25 % Cl-37 → A_{r} = (35 × 75 + 37 × 25) ÷ 100 = 35,5.\n\n**Omgekeerd:** as A_{r} gegee is, laat die een isotoop x % wees en die ander (100 − x) %, en los op vir x.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie net die massagetalle optel en deur 2 deel nie – (35 + 37) ÷ 2 = 36 is verkeerd, want die isotope kom nie ewe veel voor nie. A_{r} lê altyd naaste aan die isotoop wat die meeste voorkom.\n\n## Elektronkonfigurasie\n\nElektrone is in **energievlakke** (n = 1, 2, 3, 4) om die kern. Elke vlak het subvlakke met **orbitale**: 'n s-subvlak het een orbitaal en 'n p-subvlak drie. Elke orbitaal hou hoogstens 2 elektrone, dus hou s 2 en p 6 elektrone. Die maksimum per vlak is 2n^{2}: 2, 8, 18. Tot by Z = 20 word in vlak 3 net 3s en 3p (8 elektrone) gevul voordat 4s begin.\n\n**Drie reëls:**\n\n1. **Aufbau-beginsel:** elektrone vul eers die orbitale met die laagste energie. Volgorde: 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p → 4s. (4s het 'n laer energie as 3d, daarom kry K en Ca hul laaste elektrone in 4s.)\n2. **Hund se reël:** in 'n p-subvlak beset elektrone eers elke orbitaal enkel voordat hulle paar.\n3. **Pauli se uitsluitingsbeginsel:** 'n orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat, en hulle moet teenoorgestelde spin hê (↑↓).\n\n**sp-notasie:** O (Z = 8): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{4}; Na (Z = 11): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{1} = [Ne] 3s^{1}; K (Z = 19): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} 4s^{1}.\n\n**Aufbau-diagram (orbitaalblokdiagram):** elke orbitaal is 'n blokkie en elke elektron 'n pyltjie; die blokkies word van die laagste energie (onder) na die hoogste (bo) gerangskik. Suurstof: 1s [↑↓], 2s [↑↓], 2p [↑↓][↑][↑] – twee **ongepaarde** elektrone.\n\n**Valenselektrone** is die elektrone in die buitenste energievlak; hulle bepaal hoe 'n atoom reageer. Die res is **kernelektrone**. Cl: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{5} → 7 valenselektrone.\n\n**Ione:** Na^{+}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} en Cl^{−}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} – albei het 'n edelgaskonfigurasie.\n\n> **Wenk:** Tel die superskrifte op – die som moet gelyk wees aan die aantal elektrone.","en":"## Atomic models – how our idea of the atom developed\n\n| Scientist | Model or discovery |\n|---|---|\n| Dalton (1803) | Matter consists of tiny, hard, **indivisible** atoms (like tiny snooker balls); all atoms of one element are the same. |\n| Thomson (1897) | Discovered the **electron**. **Plum pudding model:** negative electrons are spread through a positively charged sphere. |\n| Rutherford (1911) | **Alpha particle scattering** (gold foil): the atom is mostly empty space with a small, dense, **positive nucleus** that contains almost all the mass; electrons move around the nucleus (**nuclear model**). |\n| Bohr (1913) | Electrons move in **fixed energy levels** around the nucleus. An electron that absorbs energy jumps to a higher level; when it falls back, the atom emits light of a specific energy. |\n| Chadwick (1932) | Discovered the **neutron**, a neutral particle in the nucleus. |\n\n**Rutherford's observations:** most alpha particles went straight through → the atom is mostly empty space; some were deflected and very few bounced back → a small, dense, positive nucleus repels the positive alpha particles. If an atom were as big as Loftus Versfeld, the nucleus would be like a pea on the centre spot.\n\n**Why Bohr?** According to Rutherford's model, moving electrons would lose energy and spiral into the nucleus. Fixed energy levels explain why atoms are stable and only emit certain colours of light (e.g. the yellow light of sodium street lights).\n\n## The particles in an atom\n\n| Particle | Charge | Relative mass | Location |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Proton (p^{+}) | +1 | 1 | nucleus |\n| Neutron (n^{0}) | 0 | 1 | nucleus |\n| Electron (e^{−}) | −1 | [[1/1836]] ≈ 0 | energy levels around the nucleus |\n\nProtons and neutrons together are called **nucleons**. A neutral atom has equal numbers of protons and electrons.\n\n- **Atomic number (Z):** the number of protons in an atom of an element. Z determines which element it is.\n- **Mass number (A):** the number of protons plus neutrons in the nucleus of an atom.\n- **Neutrons = A − Z.** Notation: ^{A}_{Z}X, e.g. ^{23}_{11}Na has 11 p, 12 n and 11 e.\n- **Ions:** electrons = Z − charge. Na^{+} has 10 e (lost one); Cl^{−} has 18 e (gained one). The number of protons never changes.\n\n## Isotopes\n\n**Isotopes** are atoms of the same element with the same number of protons, but different numbers of neutrons (therefore different mass numbers), e.g. C-12, C-13 and C-14, or Cl-35 and Cl-37. Isotopes have the same electron configuration and therefore **the same chemical properties**, but different masses. The SAFARI-1 reactor at Pelindaba near Hartbeespoort Dam makes radioisotopes for medical use.\n\n## Relative atomic mass\n\nThe **relative atomic mass** (A_{r}) is the average mass of an element's atoms, taking into account all its isotopes and their percentage abundance, on a scale on which a carbon-12 atom has a mass of exactly 12. It has **no unit**.\n\n**A_{r} = (mass number_{1} × %_{1} + mass number_{2} × %_{2} + …) ÷ 100**\n\nChlorine: 75 % Cl-35 and 25 % Cl-37 → A_{r} = (35 × 75 + 37 × 25) ÷ 100 = 35.5.\n\n**In reverse:** if A_{r} is given, let one isotope be x % and the other (100 − x) %, and solve for x.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not just add the mass numbers and divide by 2 – (35 + 37) ÷ 2 = 36 is wrong, because the isotopes are not equally abundant. A_{r} always lies closest to the most abundant isotope.\n\n## Electron configuration\n\nElectrons are in **energy levels** (n = 1, 2, 3, 4) around the nucleus. Each level has sublevels with **orbitals**: an s sublevel has one orbital and a p sublevel three. Each orbital holds at most 2 electrons, so s holds 2 and p holds 6 electrons. The maximum per level is 2n^{2}: 2, 8, 18. Up to Z = 20, only 3s and 3p (8 electrons) are filled in level 3 before 4s starts.\n\n**Three rules:**\n\n1. **Aufbau principle:** electrons fill the orbitals with the lowest energy first. Order: 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p → 4s. (4s has a lower energy than 3d, which is why K and Ca get their last electrons in 4s.)\n2. **Hund's rule:** in a p sublevel, electrons first occupy each orbital singly before they pair up.\n3. **Pauli's exclusion principle:** an orbital can hold at most two electrons, and they must have opposite spins (↑↓).\n\n**sp notation:** O (Z = 8): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{4}; Na (Z = 11): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{1} = [Ne] 3s^{1}; K (Z = 19): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} 4s^{1}.\n\n**Aufbau diagram (orbital box diagram):** each orbital is a box and each electron an arrow; the boxes are arranged from the lowest energy (bottom) to the highest (top). Oxygen: 1s [↑↓], 2s [↑↓], 2p [↑↓][↑][↑] – two **unpaired** electrons.\n\n**Valence electrons** are the electrons in the outermost energy level; they determine how an atom reacts. The rest are **core electrons**. Cl: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{5} → 7 valence electrons.\n\n**Ions:** Na^{+}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} and Cl^{−}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} – both have a noble gas configuration.\n\n> **Tip:** Add up the superscripts – the sum must equal the number of electrons."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Atoomgetal (Z)","en":"Atomic number (Z)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal protone in 'n atoom van 'n element.","en":"The number of protons in an atom of an element."}},{"term":{"af":"Massagetal (A)","en":"Mass number (A)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal protone en neutrone in die kern van 'n atoom.","en":"The number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom."}},{"term":{"af":"Isotoop","en":"Isotope"},"def":{"af":"Atome van dieselfde element met dieselfde aantal protone, maar verskillende getalle neutrone.","en":"Atoms of the same element with the same number of protons, but different numbers of neutrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Relatiewe atoommassa","en":"Relative atomic mass"},"def":{"af":"Die gemiddelde massa van 'n element se atome, met inagneming van sy isotope en hul persentasie voorkoms, op 'n skaal waarop koolstof-12 'n massa van 12 het; dit het geen eenheid nie.","en":"The average mass of an element's atoms, taking into account its isotopes and their percentage abundance, on a scale on which carbon-12 has a mass of 12; it has no unit."}},{"term":{"af":"Orbitaal","en":"Orbital"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied om die kern waar 'n elektron waarskynlik gevind word; elke orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat.","en":"A region around the nucleus where an electron is likely to be found; each orbital can hold at most two electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektronkonfigurasie","en":"Electron configuration"},"def":{"af":"Die rangskikking van die elektrone van 'n atoom in energievlakke en orbitale, bv. 1s² 2s² 2p⁴.","en":"The arrangement of an atom's electrons in energy levels and orbitals, e.g. 1s² 2s² 2p⁴."}},{"term":{"af":"Valenselektrone","en":"Valence electrons"},"def":{"af":"Die elektrone in die buitenste energievlak van 'n atoom.","en":"The electrons in the outermost energy level of an atom."}},{"term":{"af":"Aufbau-beginsel","en":"Aufbau principle"},"def":{"af":"Elektrone vul eers die orbitale met die laagste energie voordat hulle orbitale met 'n hoër energie beset.","en":"Electrons fill the orbitals with the lowest energy first before they occupy orbitals of higher energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Hund se reël","en":"Hund's rule"},"def":{"af":"Elektrone beset eers elke orbitaal in 'n subvlak enkel voordat hulle in dieselfde orbitaal paar.","en":"Electrons first occupy each orbital in a sublevel singly before they pair up in the same orbital."}},{"term":{"af":"Pauli se uitsluitingsbeginsel","en":"Pauli's exclusion principle"},"def":{"af":"'n Orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat, en die twee elektrone moet teenoorgestelde spin hê.","en":"An orbital can hold at most two electrons, and the two electrons must have opposite spins."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Rutherford se goudfoelie-eksperiment","en":"Rutherford's gold foil experiment"},"problem":{"af":"Rutherford het positief gelaaide alfadeeltjies op 'n baie dun goudfoelie geskiet. (a) Beskryf die waarnemings en wat elkeen oor die atoom bewys. (b) Waarom kon Thomson se pruimpoedingmodel nie die resultate verklaar nie?","en":"Rutherford fired positively charged alpha particles at a very thin gold foil. (a) Describe the observations and what each one shows about the atom. (b) Why could Thomson's plum pudding model not explain the results?"},"steps":[{"af":"Waarneming 1: die meeste alfadeeltjies het **reguit deurgegaan** → die atoom bestaan meestal uit **leë ruimte**.","en":"Observation 1: most alpha particles **went straight through** → the atom consists mostly of **empty space**."},{"af":"Waarneming 2: party is deur groot hoeke **afgebuig** → daar is 'n **positiewe** lading in die middel van die atoom wat die positiewe alfadeeltjies afstoot.","en":"Observation 2: some were **deflected** through large angles → there is a **positive** charge in the centre of the atom that repels the positive alpha particles."},{"af":"Waarneming 3: baie min het **teruggebons** → die positiewe lading en byna al die massa is in 'n baie **klein, digte kern** saamgepak.","en":"Observation 3: very few **bounced back** → the positive charge and almost all the mass are packed into a very **small, dense nucleus**."},{"af":"(b) In Thomson se model is die positiewe lading eweredig oor die hele atoom versprei. Dit sou die alfadeeltjies hoogstens effens afbuig, nooit laat terugbons nie. Rutherford het daarom die **kernmodel** voorgestel: 'n klein positiewe kern met elektrone wat daarom beweeg.","en":"(b) In Thomson's model the positive charge is spread evenly through the whole atom. It would deflect the alpha particles only slightly, never make them bounce back. Rutherford therefore proposed the **nuclear model**: a small positive nucleus with electrons moving around it."}],"answer":{"af":"Die atoom is meestal leë ruimte met 'n klein, digte, positiewe kern wat byna al die massa bevat; elektrone beweeg om die kern.","en":"The atom is mostly empty space with a small, dense, positive nucleus that contains almost all the mass; electrons move around the nucleus."}},{"title":{"af":"Tel protone, neutrone en elektrone","en":"Count protons, neutrons and electrons"},"problem":{"af":"Bepaal die aantal protone, neutrone en elektrone in (a) ²⁷₁₃Al, (b) ²⁷₁₃Al³⁺ en (c) ³²₁₆S²⁻.","en":"Determine the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in (a) ²⁷₁₃Al, (b) ²⁷₁₃Al³⁺ and (c) ³²₁₆S²⁻."},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik: protone = Z (onderste getal); neutrone = A − Z (A is die boonste getal); elektrone = Z − lading.","en":"Use: protons = Z (bottom number); neutrons = A − Z (A is the top number); electrons = Z − charge."},{"af":"(a) ^{27}_{13}Al: p = 13; n = 27 − 13 = 14; e = 13 (neutrale atoom).","en":"(a) ^{27}_{13}Al: p = 13; n = 27 − 13 = 14; e = 13 (neutral atom)."},{"af":"(b) Al^{3+}: p = 13; n = 14; e = 13 − 3 = 10 (die atoom het 3 elektrone verloor; die protone bly dieselfde).","en":"(b) Al^{3+}: p = 13; n = 14; e = 13 − 3 = 10 (the atom lost 3 electrons; the protons stay the same)."},{"af":"(c) S^{2−}: p = 16; n = 32 − 16 = 16; e = 16 − (−2) = 16 + 2 = 18 (die atoom het 2 elektrone bygekry).","en":"(c) S^{2−}: p = 16; n = 32 − 16 = 16; e = 16 − (−2) = 16 + 2 = 18 (the atom gained 2 electrons)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 13 p, 14 n, 13 e (b) 13 p, 14 n, 10 e (c) 16 p, 16 n, 18 e","en":"(a) 13 p, 14 n, 13 e (b) 13 p, 14 n, 10 e (c) 16 p, 16 n, 18 e"}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken die relatiewe atoommassa","en":"Calculate the relative atomic mass"},"problem":{"af":"Magnesium kom in die natuur voor as 79 % Mg-24, 10 % Mg-25 en 11 % Mg-26. Bereken die relatiewe atoommassa van magnesium.","en":"Magnesium occurs in nature as 79 % Mg-24, 10 % Mg-25 and 11 % Mg-26. Calculate the relative atomic mass of magnesium."},"steps":[{"af":"Formule: A_{r} = (massagetal_{1} × %_{1} + massagetal_{2} × %_{2} + massagetal_{3} × %_{3}) ÷ 100","en":"Formula: A_{r} = (mass number_{1} × %_{1} + mass number_{2} × %_{2} + mass number_{3} × %_{3}) ÷ 100"},{"af":"Vervang: A_{r} = (24 × 79 + 25 × 10 + 26 × 11) ÷ 100","en":"Substitute: A_{r} = (24 × 79 + 25 × 10 + 26 × 11) ÷ 100"},{"af":"= (1 896 + 250 + 286) ÷ 100 = 2 432 ÷ 100","en":"= (1 896 + 250 + 286) ÷ 100 = 2 432 ÷ 100"},{"af":"A_{r} = 24,32 (geen eenheid nie). Kontrole: die antwoord lê tussen 24 en 26, naaste aan 24, want Mg-24 kom die meeste voor.","en":"A_{r} = 24.32 (no unit). Check: the answer lies between 24 and 26, closest to 24, because Mg-24 is the most abundant."}],"answer":{"af":"Aᵣ(Mg) = 24,32","en":"Aᵣ(Mg) = 24.32"}},{"title":{"af":"Elektronkonfigurasie van fosfor","en":"Electron configuration of phosphorus"},"problem":{"af":"Vir fosfor (Z = 15): (a) skryf die elektronkonfigurasie in sp-notasie, (b) beskryf die Aufbau-diagram (orbitaalblokdiagram), en (c) bepaal die aantal valenselektrone en ongepaarde elektrone.","en":"For phosphorus (Z = 15): (a) write the electron configuration in sp notation, (b) describe the Aufbau diagram (orbital box diagram), and (c) determine the number of valence electrons and unpaired electrons."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n Neutrale P-atoom het 15 elektrone. Vul volgens die Aufbau-beginsel in die volgorde 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{3}. Kontrole: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 3 = 15.","en":"(a) A neutral P atom has 15 electrons. Fill according to the Aufbau principle in the order 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{3}. Check: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 3 = 15."},{"af":"(b) 1s, 2s en 3s het elk een blokkie met ↑↓; die drie 2p-blokkies is vol: [↑↓][↑↓][↑↓]. Volgens **Hund se reël** kry die drie 3p-blokkies elk een pyltjie: [↑][↑][↑] – die elektrone paar nie voordat elke blokkie een het nie.","en":"(b) 1s, 2s and 3s each have one box with ↑↓; the three 2p boxes are full: [↑↓][↑↓][↑↓]. According to **Hund's rule** the three 3p boxes each get one arrow: [↑][↑][↑] – the electrons do not pair before every box has one."},{"af":"(c) Valenselektrone = elektrone in die buitenste energievlak (n = 3): 3s^{2} 3p^{3} → 2 + 3 = **5**.","en":"(c) Valence electrons = electrons in the outermost energy level (n = 3): 3s^{2} 3p^{3} → 2 + 3 = **5**."},{"af":"Ongepaarde elektrone: die drie enkel elektrone in 3p → **3**. Elke gepaarde blokkie bevat twee pyltjies in teenoorgestelde rigtings (**Pauli**).","en":"Unpaired electrons: the three single electrons in 3p → **3**. Every paired box contains two arrows in opposite directions (**Pauli**)."}],"answer":{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p³; 5 valenselektrone; 3 ongepaarde elektrone","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p³; 5 valence electrons; 3 unpaired electrons"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter wetenskaplike het die neutron in 1932 ontdek?","en":"Which scientist discovered the neutron in 1932?"},"options":[{"af":"Thomson","en":"Thomson"},{"af":"Rutherford","en":"Rutherford"},{"af":"Bohr","en":"Bohr"},{"af":"Chadwick","en":"Chadwick"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Chadwick het in 1932 die neutron ontdek. Thomson het die elektron ontdek, Rutherford die kern, en Bohr het die model met vaste energievlakke voorgestel.","en":"Chadwick discovered the neutron in 1932. Thomson discovered the electron, Rutherford the nucleus, and Bohr proposed the model with fixed energy levels."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Volgens Bohr se model straal 'n atoom lig uit wanneer 'n elektron van 'n hoër na 'n laer energievlak val.","en":"According to Bohr's model, an atom emits light when an electron falls from a higher to a lower energy level."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 'n Elektron wat energie absorbeer, spring na 'n hoër vlak. As dit terugval, word die verskil in energie as lig uitgestraal – daarom straal elke element net sekere kleure uit.","en":"True. An electron that absorbs energy jumps to a higher level. When it falls back, the difference in energy is emitted as light – that is why each element emits only certain colours."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die atoomgetal (Z) van 'n element is die aantal ___ in 'n atoom van daardie element.","en":"The atomic number (Z) of an element is the number of ___ in an atom of that element."},"answers":{"af":["protone","proton"],"en":["protons","proton"]},"explain":{"af":"Z = die aantal protone. Dit bepaal watter element dit is: elke atoom met 6 protone is koolstof. Die massagetal (A) is protone plus neutrone.","en":"Z = the number of protons. It determines which element it is: every atom with 6 protons is carbon. The mass number (A) is protons plus neutrons."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke wetenskaplike by sy bydrae tot die atoommodel.","en":"Match each scientist to his contribution to the atomic model."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Dalton","en":"Dalton"},"r":{"af":"Atoom is 'n klein, harde, ondeelbare bol","en":"Atom is a tiny, hard, indivisible sphere"}},{"l":{"af":"Thomson","en":"Thomson"},"r":{"af":"Pruimpoedingmodel: elektrone in 'n positiewe bol","en":"Plum pudding model: electrons in a positive sphere"}},{"l":{"af":"Rutherford","en":"Rutherford"},"r":{"af":"Klein, digte, positiewe kern; meestal leë ruimte","en":"Small, dense, positive nucleus; mostly empty space"}},{"l":{"af":"Bohr","en":"Bohr"},"r":{"af":"Elektrone in vaste energievlakke","en":"Electrons in fixed energy levels"}},{"l":{"af":"Chadwick","en":"Chadwick"},"r":{"af":"Neutrale deeltjie in die kern","en":"Neutral particle in the nucleus"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die volgorde Dalton → Thomson → Rutherford → Bohr → Chadwick wys hoe elke nuwe eksperiment die vorige model verbeter het.","en":"The order Dalton → Thomson → Rutherford → Bohr → Chadwick shows how each new experiment improved the previous model."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In Rutherford se goudfoelie-eksperiment het die meeste alfadeeltjies reguit deur die foelie beweeg. Wat het hy hieruit afgelei?","en":"In Rutherford's gold foil experiment most alpha particles went straight through the foil. What did he conclude from this?"},"options":[{"af":"Die atoom bestaan meestal uit leë ruimte.","en":"The atom consists mostly of empty space."},{"af":"Die kern is negatief gelaai.","en":"The nucleus is negatively charged."},{"af":"Elektrone beweeg in vaste energievlakke.","en":"Electrons move in fixed energy levels."},{"af":"Die atoom is 'n harde, ondeelbare bol.","en":"The atom is a hard, indivisible sphere."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"As die meeste deeltjies ongehinderd deurgaan, is daar niks in hul pad nie: die atoom is meestal leë ruimte. Die kern is positief (dit stoot die positiewe alfadeeltjies af), energievlakke is Bohr se idee, en 'n harde bol is Dalton se model.","en":"If most particles pass through unhindered, there is nothing in their way: the atom is mostly empty space. The nucleus is positive (it repels the positive alpha particles), energy levels are Bohr's idea, and a hard sphere is Dalton's model."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Isotope van dieselfde element het verskillende atoomgetalle.","en":"Isotopes of the same element have different atomic numbers."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Isotope het dieselfde aantal protone, dus dieselfde atoomgetal (anders sou dit 'n ander element wees). Hulle verskil net in die aantal neutrone, dus in die massagetal.","en":"False. Isotopes have the same number of protons, therefore the same atomic number (otherwise it would be a different element). They differ only in the number of neutrons, therefore in the mass number."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is Pauli se uitsluitingsbeginsel?","en":"Which statement is Pauli's exclusion principle?"},"options":[{"af":"Elektrone vul eers die orbitale met die laagste energie.","en":"Electrons fill the orbitals with the lowest energy first."},{"af":"'n Orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat, en hulle moet teenoorgestelde spin hê.","en":"An orbital can hold at most two electrons, and they must have opposite spins."},{"af":"Elektrone beset eers elke orbitaal in 'n subvlak enkel voordat hulle paar.","en":"Electrons first occupy each orbital in a sublevel singly before they pair up."},{"af":"Elke energievlak kan hoogstens 8 elektrone bevat.","en":"Each energy level can hold at most 8 electrons."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Pauli: hoogstens twee elektrone per orbitaal, met teenoorgestelde spin (↑↓). Die eerste stelling is die Aufbau-beginsel en die derde is Hund se reël. Die laaste is vals: die maksimum per vlak is 2n², bv. 18 vir n = 3.","en":"Pauli: at most two electrons per orbital, with opposite spins (↑↓). The first statement is the Aufbau principle and the third is Hund's rule. The last is false: the maximum per level is 2n², e.g. 18 for n = 3."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel neutrone is daar in 'n atoom van ³⁹₁₉K? ___","en":"How many neutrons are there in an atom of ³⁹₁₉K? ___"},"answers":{"af":["20","20 neutrone"],"en":["20","20 neutrons"]},"explain":{"af":"Neutrone = A − Z = 39 − 19 = 20. Die boonste getal (39) is die massagetal en die onderste (19) die atoomgetal.","en":"Neutrons = A − Z = 39 − 19 = 20. The top number (39) is the mass number and the bottom one (19) the atomic number."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel elektrone het die oksiedioon, ¹⁶₈O²⁻?","en":"How many electrons does the oxide ion, ¹⁶₈O²⁻, have?"},"options":[{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"16","en":"16"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Elektrone = Z − lading = 8 − (−2) = 10. Die suurstofatoom het 2 elektrone bygekry. 6 is as jy die 2 aftrek in plaas van bytel, 8 is die neutrale atoom, en 16 is die massagetal.","en":"Electrons = Z − charge = 8 − (−2) = 10. The oxygen atom gained 2 electrons. 6 is if you subtract the 2 instead of adding it, 8 is the neutral atom, and 16 is the mass number."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die elektronkonfigurasie van kalsium (Z = 20)?","en":"What is the electron configuration of calcium (Z = 20)?"},"options":[{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 3d²","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 3d²"},{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s¹","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s¹"},{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁸","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁸"},{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s²","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ca het 20 elektrone. Ná 3p⁶ (18 elektrone) gaan die laaste twee na 4s, want 4s het 'n laer energie as 3d (Aufbau). 3d² ignoreer dit, 4s¹ het net 19 elektrone (dit is K), en 3p⁸ is onmoontlik – 'n p-subvlak hou hoogstens 6.","en":"Ca has 20 electrons. After 3p⁶ (18 electrons) the last two go into 4s, because 4s has a lower energy than 3d (Aufbau). 3d² ignores this, 4s¹ has only 19 electrons (that is K), and 3p⁸ is impossible – a p sublevel holds at most 6."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gallium bestaan uit 60,1 % Ga-69 en 39,9 % Ga-71. Bereken die relatiewe atoommassa van gallium (twee desimale plekke): ___","en":"Gallium consists of 60.1 % Ga-69 and 39.9 % Ga-71. Calculate the relative atomic mass of gallium (two decimal places): ___"},"answers":{"af":["69,80","69.80","69,8","69.8"],"en":["69.80","69,80","69.8","69,8"]},"explain":{"af":"Aᵣ = (69 × 60,1 + 71 × 39,9) ÷ 100 = (4 146,9 + 2 832,9) ÷ 100 = 6 979,8 ÷ 100 = 69,80. Geen eenheid nie. Die antwoord lê naaste aan 69, want Ga-69 kom die meeste voor.","en":"Aᵣ = (69 × 60.1 + 71 × 39.9) ÷ 100 = (4 146.9 + 2 832.9) ÷ 100 = 6 979.8 ÷ 100 = 69.80. No unit. The answer lies closest to 69, because Ga-69 is the most abundant."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Stikstof (Z = 7) het die konfigurasie 1s² 2s² 2p³. Watter beskrywing van die drie 2p-orbitaalblokkies is korrek?","en":"Nitrogen (Z = 7) has the configuration 1s² 2s² 2p³. Which description of the three 2p orbital boxes is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"[↑↓] [↑] [  ]","en":"[↑↓] [↑] [  ]"},{"af":"[↑↑] [↑] [  ]","en":"[↑↑] [↑] [  ]"},{"af":"[↑] [↑] [↑]","en":"[↑] [↑] [↑]"},{"af":"[↑↓↑] [  ] [  ]","en":"[↑↓↑] [  ] [  ]"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Hund se reël: elke 2p-orbitaal kry eers een elektron voordat enige paar, dus [↑] [↑] [↑] – drie ongepaarde elektrone. [↑↓] [↑] [  ] paar te vroeg (oortree Hund), [↑↑] het twee elektrone met dieselfde spin in een orbitaal, en [↑↓↑] het drie elektrone in een orbitaal (albei oortree Pauli).","en":"Hund's rule: each 2p orbital first gets one electron before any pair up, so [↑] [↑] [↑] – three unpaired electrons. [↑↓] [↑] [  ] pairs too early (breaks Hund), [↑↑] has two electrons with the same spin in one orbital, and [↑↓↑] has three electrons in one orbital (both break Pauli)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Chloor het 'n relatiewe atoommassa van 35,5 en bestaan uit net twee isotope, Cl-35 en Cl-37. Bereken die persentasie Cl-35: ___ %","en":"Chlorine has a relative atomic mass of 35.5 and consists of only two isotopes, Cl-35 and Cl-37. Calculate the percentage of Cl-35: ___ %"},"answers":{"af":["75","75 %","75%"],"en":["75","75 %","75%"]},"explain":{"af":"Laat Cl-35 = x % en Cl-37 = (100 − x) %. Dan 35x + 37(100 − x) = 35,5 × 100, dus 3 700 − 2x = 3 550, 2x = 150 en x = 75 %. Kontrole: 35,5 lê nader aan 35, so Cl-35 moet die meeste voorkom.","en":"Let Cl-35 = x % and Cl-37 = (100 − x) %. Then 35x + 37(100 − x) = 35.5 × 100, so 3 700 − 2x = 3 550, 2x = 150 and x = 75 %. Check: 35.5 lies closer to 35, so Cl-35 must be the most abundant."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder beweer: \"Cl-35 en Cl-37 reageer verskillend met natrium, want hulle het verskillende massas.\" Watter stelling evalueer die bewering die beste?","en":"A learner claims: \"Cl-35 and Cl-37 react differently with sodium, because they have different masses.\" Which statement best evaluates the claim?"},"options":[{"af":"Verkeerd: albei het 17 protone en 17 elektrone met dieselfde elektronkonfigurasie, dus het hulle dieselfde chemiese eienskappe.","en":"Wrong: both have 17 protons and 17 electrons with the same electron configuration, so they have the same chemical properties."},{"af":"Korrek: die swaarder isotoop het meer neutrone en reageer daarom heeltemal anders.","en":"Correct: the heavier isotope has more neutrons and therefore reacts completely differently."},{"af":"Verkeerd: Cl-37 het 2 ekstra elektrone, daarom reageer dit vinniger.","en":"Wrong: Cl-37 has 2 extra electrons, therefore it reacts faster."},{"af":"Korrek: isotope is verskillende elemente en het dus verskillende eienskappe.","en":"Correct: isotopes are different elements and therefore have different properties."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Chemiese eienskappe hang van die elektrone af, veral die valenselektrone. Isotope verskil net in die aantal neutrone (in die kern), dus het Cl-35 en Cl-37 dieselfde 17 elektrone, dieselfde konfigurasie en dieselfde chemiese eienskappe. Hulle is dieselfde element, en Cl-37 het 2 ekstra neutrone, nie elektrone nie.","en":"Chemical properties depend on the electrons, especially the valence electrons. Isotopes differ only in the number of neutrons (in the nucleus), so Cl-35 and Cl-37 have the same 17 electrons, the same configuration and the same chemical properties. They are the same element, and Cl-37 has 2 extra neutrons, not electrons."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-periodieke-tabel-binding","title":{"af":"Periodieke tabel en chemiese binding","en":"Periodic table and chemical bonding"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal tendense in die periodieke tabel met redes kan verduidelik, ione en formules kan skryf, en kovalente, ioniese en metaalbinding met Lewis-diagramme en eienskappe kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to explain trends in the periodic table with reasons, write ions and formulae, and describe covalent, ionic and metallic bonding with Lewis diagrams and properties."},"summary":{"af":"## Die periodieke tabel\n\nDie elemente is volgens **toenemende atoomgetal (Z)** gerangskik.\n\n- **Groep:** 'n vertikale kolom. Elemente in dieselfde groep het dieselfde aantal **valenselektrone** (elektrone in die buitenste energievlak) en daarom soortgelyke chemiese eienskappe.\n- **Periode:** 'n horisontale ry. Die periodenommer is gelyk aan die aantal energievlakke wat elektrone bevat.\n- **Metale** is links en in die middel (die oorgangsmetale, soos die platinum wat naby Brits gemyn word), **nie-metale** is regs, en **metalloïede** (bv. B en Si) lê op die trapvormige lyn tussen hulle.\n\n| Groep | Naam | Valenselektrone | Tipiese ioon |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | alkalimetale | 1 | Na⁺ (+1) |\n| 2 | aardalkalimetale | 2 | Mg²⁺ (+2) |\n| 13 | – | 3 | Al³⁺ (+3) |\n| 15 | – | 5 | N³⁻ (−3) |\n| 16 | – | 6 | O²⁻ (−2) |\n| 17 | halogene | 7 | Cl⁻ (−1) |\n| 18 | edelgasse | 8 (He: 2) | vorm nie ione nie |\n\n> **Wenk:** Vir groepe 13–18 is die aantal valenselektrone = groepnommer − 10. Uit die elektronkonfigurasie: Cl is 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁵, dus 3 energievlakke (periode 3) en 2 + 5 = 7 valenselektrone (groep 17).\n\nGroep 1-metale reageer heftig met water: 2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂. Hulle word **meer** reaktief laer af in die groep. Die halogene bestaan as diatomiese molekules (F₂, Cl₂) en word **minder** reaktief laer af. Edelgasse het 'n volle buitenste energievlak en is onreaktief.\n\n## Tendense en die redes\n\nTwee idees verklaar al die tendense:\n\n1. **Oor 'n periode (links → regs):** die kernlading (aantal protone) neem toe, maar die elektrone kom in **dieselfde** energievlak by. Die kern trek die buitenste elektrone sterker aan.\n2. **Af in 'n groep:** elke element het 'n **ekstra energievlak**. Die buitenste elektrone is verder van die kern en word deur die binneste elektrone afgeskerm, dus is die aantrekking swakker.\n\n| Eienskap | Definisie | Oor 'n periode → | Af in 'n groep ↓ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Atoomradius | die afstand van die middel van die kern tot by die buitenste elektrone | neem af | neem toe |\n| Eerste ionisasie-energie | die energie benodig per mol om die eerste elektron uit 'n atoom in die gasfase te verwyder | neem toe | neem af |\n| Elektronaffiniteit | die energie wat vrygestel word wanneer 'n elektron aan 'n atoom of molekuul geheg word om 'n negatiewe ioon te vorm | neem toe (in die algemeen) | neem af |\n| Elektronegatiwiteit | 'n maatstaf van die neiging van 'n atoom in 'n molekuul om bindingselektrone aan te trek | neem toe | neem af |\n\nFluoor is die mees elektronegatiewe element (4,0). 'n Lae ionisasie-energie beteken dat die atoom maklik 'n elektron verloor, wat tipies van metale is. Daarom is K meer reaktief as Na.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"Die atome word groter oor die periode, want daar is meer elektrone.\" Verkeerd! Die ekstra protone trek dieselfde energievlak nader, dus word die radius **kleiner**.\n\n## Chemiese binding\n\n'n **Chemiese binding** is 'n wedersydse aantrekking tussen twee atome as gevolg van die gelyktydige aantrekking tussen hul kerne en die buitenste elektrone. Atome bind om 'n stabiele **edelgaskonfigurasie** te kry: 8 valenselektrone (die **oktetreël**), of 2 vir H.\n\n### Kovalente binding: nie-metaal + nie-metaal\n\nDie **deel van elektrone** tussen twee atome om 'n molekuul te vorm. Een gedeelde elektronpaar is 'n enkelbinding (H–H), twee is 'n dubbelbinding (O=O) en drie is 'n drievoudige binding (N≡N). 'n Elektronpaar wat nie gedeel word nie, is 'n **alleenpaar** (nie-bindende paar).\n\n### Ioniese binding: metaal + nie-metaal\n\nDie **oordrag van elektrone**: die metaal verloor elektrone en vorm **katione** (positiewe ione); die nie-metaal kry elektrone en vorm **anione** (negatiewe ione). Die teenoorgesteld gelaaide ione trek mekaar elektrostaties aan en vorm 'n **kristalrooster**. Die eenvoudigste verhouding van die ione is 'n **formule-eenheid**, bv. NaCl (die sout op jou braaivleis). 'n Groot verskil in elektronegatiwiteit tussen die atome lei tot elektronoordrag.\n\n**Formules met die kruismetode:** skryf die ione neer, ruil die getalle van die ladings om en vereenvoudig. Die totale lading moet nul wees.\n\n- Mg²⁺ en Cl⁻ → MgCl₂\n- Al³⁺ en O²⁻ → Al₂O₃\n- Ca²⁺ en OH⁻ → Ca(OH)₂ (hakies om 'n saamgestelde ioon)\n\n### Metaalbinding: metaalatome\n\nDie binding tussen positiewe ione en 'n **see van gedelokaliseerde elektrone**. Die metaalatome gee hul valenselektrone af, en dié elektrone beweeg vrylik deur die hele metaal, bv. in die koperdrade van 'n kragkabel.\n\n## Lewis-diagramme (in woorde)\n\n'n Lewis-diagram toon die valenselektrone as kolletjies (of kruisies) om die simbool van die element.\n\n| Stof | Beskrywing van die Lewis-diagram |\n|---|---|\n| H₂O | O in die middel; 2 bindingspare (O–H) en 2 alleenpare op die O |\n| NH₃ | N in die middel; 3 bindingspare en 1 alleenpaar |\n| CH₄ | C in die middel; 4 bindingspare en geen alleenpare nie |\n| CO₂ | O=C=O: 2 dubbelbindings (4 bindingspare); elke O het 2 alleenpare |\n| NaCl | [Na]⁺ sonder kolletjies en [Cl]⁻ met 8 elektrone, elkeen in vierkantige hakies met sy lading |\n\n## Eienskappe\n\n| | Ionies (NaCl) | Kovalent molekulêr (H₂O, CO₂) | Metaal (Cu) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Smelt- en kookpunt | hoog: sterk aantrekking tussen ione oral in die rooster | laag: swak kragte tussen die molekules | meestal hoog |\n| Elektriese geleiding | slegs gesmelt of in water opgelos (die ione kan dan beweeg) | geen: geen vrye gelaaide deeltjies nie | ja, ook as vastestof (vrye elektrone) |\n| Ander | hard maar bros; baie los in water op | dikwels gasse of vloeistowwe by kamertemperatuur | smeebaar, rekbaar, blink (metaalglans), goeie hittegeleiers |\n\nKovalente **netwerkstrukture** (diamant, SiO₂) is anders: hulle is baie hard en het baie hoë smeltpunte.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Wanneer water kook, breek die O–H-bindings **nie**. Slegs die swak kragte tussen die molekules word oorkom.","en":"## The periodic table\n\nThe elements are arranged in order of **increasing atomic number (Z)**.\n\n- **Group:** a vertical column. Elements in the same group have the same number of **valence electrons** (electrons in the outermost energy level) and therefore similar chemical properties.\n- **Period:** a horizontal row. The period number equals the number of energy levels that contain electrons.\n- **Metals** are on the left and in the middle (the transition metals, such as the platinum mined near Brits), **non-metals** are on the right, and **metalloids** (e.g. B and Si) lie on the staircase line between them.\n\n| Group | Name | Valence electrons | Typical ion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | alkali metals | 1 | Na⁺ (+1) |\n| 2 | alkaline earth metals | 2 | Mg²⁺ (+2) |\n| 13 | – | 3 | Al³⁺ (+3) |\n| 15 | – | 5 | N³⁻ (−3) |\n| 16 | – | 6 | O²⁻ (−2) |\n| 17 | halogens | 7 | Cl⁻ (−1) |\n| 18 | noble gases | 8 (He: 2) | do not form ions |\n\n> **Tip:** For groups 13–18 the number of valence electrons = group number − 10. From the electron configuration: Cl is 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁵, so 3 energy levels (period 3) and 2 + 5 = 7 valence electrons (group 17).\n\nGroup 1 metals react vigorously with water: 2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂. They become **more** reactive further down the group. The halogens exist as diatomic molecules (F₂, Cl₂) and become **less** reactive further down. Noble gases have a full outer energy level and are unreactive.\n\n## Trends and the reasons\n\nTwo ideas explain all the trends:\n\n1. **Across a period (left → right):** the nuclear charge (number of protons) increases, but the electrons are added to the **same** energy level. The nucleus attracts the outer electrons more strongly.\n2. **Down a group:** each element has an **extra energy level**. The outer electrons are further from the nucleus and are shielded by the inner electrons, so the attraction is weaker.\n\n| Property | Definition | Across a period → | Down a group ↓ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Atomic radius | the distance from the centre of the nucleus to the outermost electrons | decreases | increases |\n| First ionisation energy | the energy needed per mole to remove the first electron from an atom in the gaseous phase | increases | decreases |\n| Electron affinity | the energy released when an electron is attached to an atom or molecule to form a negative ion | increases (in general) | decreases |\n| Electronegativity | a measure of the tendency of an atom in a molecule to attract bonding electrons | increases | decreases |\n\nFluorine is the most electronegative element (4.0). A low ionisation energy means the atom loses an electron easily, which is typical of metals. That is why K is more reactive than Na.\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"The atoms get bigger across the period because there are more electrons.\" Wrong! The extra protons pull the same energy level closer, so the radius becomes **smaller**.\n\n## Chemical bonding\n\nA **chemical bond** is a mutual attraction between two atoms resulting from the simultaneous attraction between their nuclei and the outer electrons. Atoms bond to obtain a stable **noble gas configuration**: 8 valence electrons (the **octet rule**), or 2 for H.\n\n### Covalent bonding: non-metal + non-metal\n\nThe **sharing of electrons** between two atoms to form a molecule. One shared electron pair is a single bond (H–H), two is a double bond (O=O) and three is a triple bond (N≡N). An electron pair that is not shared is a **lone pair** (non-bonding pair).\n\n### Ionic bonding: metal + non-metal\n\nThe **transfer of electrons**: the metal loses electrons and forms **cations** (positive ions); the non-metal gains electrons and forms **anions** (negative ions). The oppositely charged ions attract each other electrostatically and form a **crystal lattice**. The simplest ratio of the ions is a **formula unit**, e.g. NaCl (the salt on your braai meat). A large difference in electronegativity between the atoms leads to electron transfer.\n\n**Formulae with the criss-cross method:** write down the ions, swap the numbers of the charges and simplify. The total charge must be zero.\n\n- Mg²⁺ and Cl⁻ → MgCl₂\n- Al³⁺ and O²⁻ → Al₂O₃\n- Ca²⁺ and OH⁻ → Ca(OH)₂ (brackets around a compound ion)\n\n### Metallic bonding: metal atoms\n\nThe bond between positive ions and a **sea of delocalised electrons**. The metal atoms give up their valence electrons, and these electrons move freely through the whole metal, e.g. in the copper wires of a power cable.\n\n## Lewis diagrams (in words)\n\nA Lewis diagram shows the valence electrons as dots (or crosses) around the symbol of the element.\n\n| Substance | Description of the Lewis diagram |\n|---|---|\n| H₂O | O in the centre; 2 bonding pairs (O–H) and 2 lone pairs on the O |\n| NH₃ | N in the centre; 3 bonding pairs and 1 lone pair |\n| CH₄ | C in the centre; 4 bonding pairs and no lone pairs |\n| CO₂ | O=C=O: 2 double bonds (4 bonding pairs); each O has 2 lone pairs |\n| NaCl | [Na]⁺ with no dots and [Cl]⁻ with 8 electrons, each in square brackets with its charge |\n\n## Properties\n\n| | Ionic (NaCl) | Covalent molecular (H₂O, CO₂) | Metal (Cu) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Melting and boiling point | high: strong attraction between ions throughout the lattice | low: weak forces between the molecules | mostly high |\n| Electrical conduction | only when molten or dissolved in water (the ions can then move) | none: no free charged particles | yes, also as a solid (free electrons) |\n| Other | hard but brittle; many dissolve in water | often gases or liquids at room temperature | malleable, ductile, shiny (lustre), good conductors of heat |\n\nCovalent **network structures** (diamond, SiO₂) are different: they are very hard and have very high melting points.\n\n> **Common mistake:** When water boils, the O–H bonds do **not** break. Only the weak forces between the molecules are overcome."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Valenselektrone","en":"Valence electrons"},"def":{"af":"Die elektrone in die buitenste energievlak van 'n atoom. Hulle neem deel aan binding.","en":"The electrons in the outermost energy level of an atom. They take part in bonding."}},{"term":{"af":"Atoomradius","en":"Atomic radius"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand van die middel van die kern van 'n atoom tot by sy buitenste elektrone.","en":"The distance from the centre of the nucleus of an atom to its outermost electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Eerste ionisasie-energie","en":"First ionisation energy"},"def":{"af":"Die energie benodig per mol om die eerste elektron uit 'n atoom in die gasfase te verwyder.","en":"The energy needed per mole to remove the first electron from an atom in the gaseous phase."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektronaffiniteit","en":"Electron affinity"},"def":{"af":"Die energie wat vrygestel word wanneer 'n elektron aan 'n atoom of molekuul geheg word om 'n negatiewe ioon te vorm.","en":"The energy released when an electron is attached to an atom or molecule to form a negative ion."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektronegatiwiteit","en":"Electronegativity"},"def":{"af":"'n Maatstaf van die neiging van 'n atoom in 'n molekuul om bindingselektrone aan te trek.","en":"A measure of the tendency of an atom in a molecule to attract bonding electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Chemiese binding","en":"Chemical bond"},"def":{"af":"'n Wedersydse aantrekking tussen twee atome as gevolg van die gelyktydige aantrekking tussen hul kerne en die buitenste elektrone.","en":"A mutual attraction between two atoms resulting from the simultaneous attraction between their nuclei and the outer electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Kovalente binding","en":"Covalent bond"},"def":{"af":"Die deel van elektrone tussen twee atome om 'n molekuul te vorm.","en":"The sharing of electrons between two atoms to form a molecule."}},{"term":{"af":"Ioniese binding","en":"Ionic bond"},"def":{"af":"Die oordrag van elektrone om katione (positiewe ione) en anione (negatiewe ione) te vorm wat mekaar elektrostaties aantrek.","en":"The transfer of electrons to form cations (positive ions) and anions (negative ions) that attract each other electrostatically."}},{"term":{"af":"Metaalbinding","en":"Metallic bond"},"def":{"af":"Die binding tussen positiewe ione en 'n see van gedelokaliseerde elektrone.","en":"The bond between positive ions and a sea of delocalised electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Lewis-diagram","en":"Lewis diagram"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorstelling van 'n atoom, ioon of molekuul waarin die valenselektrone as kolletjies of kruisies om die simbool van die element geteken word.","en":"A representation of an atom, ion or molecule in which the valence electrons are drawn as dots or crosses around the symbol of the element."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Van elektronkonfigurasie na groep, periode en ioon","en":"From electron configuration to group, period and ion"},"problem":{"af":"Element X het atoomgetal 16. (a) Skryf die elektronkonfigurasie van X (sp-notasie). (b) In watter periode en groep is X? (c) Hoeveel valenselektrone het X, en watter ioon vorm dit? (d) Is X 'n metaal of 'n nie-metaal?","en":"Element X has atomic number 16. (a) Write the electron configuration of X (sp notation). (b) In which period and group is X? (c) How many valence electrons does X have, and which ion does it form? (d) Is X a metal or a non-metal?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n Neutrale atoom met Z = 16 het 16 elektrone: 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴. Kontroleer: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 4 = 16.","en":"(a) A neutral atom with Z = 16 has 16 electrons: 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴. Check: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 4 = 16."},{"af":"(b) Die hoogste energievlak is 3, dus is X in periode 3. Die buitenste energievlak (3s²3p⁴) bevat 6 elektrone, dus groep 6 + 10 = 16.","en":"(b) The highest energy level is 3, so X is in period 3. The outer energy level (3s²3p⁴) holds 6 electrons, so group 6 + 10 = 16."},{"af":"(c) X het 6 valenselektrone. Dit is makliker om 2 elektrone te kry as om 6 te verloor, dus vorm X 'n X²⁻-ioon met die edelgaskonfigurasie van Ar.","en":"(c) X has 6 valence electrons. It is easier to gain 2 electrons than to lose 6, so X forms an X²⁻ ion with the noble gas configuration of Ar."},{"af":"(d) X is swael (S). Dit lê regs in die periodieke tabel en kry elektrone, dus is dit 'n nie-metaal.","en":"(d) X is sulfur (S). It lies on the right of the periodic table and gains electrons, so it is a non-metal."}],"answer":{"af":"1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴; periode 3, groep 16; 6 valenselektrone, vorm S²⁻; nie-metaal (swael)","en":"1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴; period 3, group 16; 6 valence electrons, forms S²⁻; non-metal (sulfur)"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik 'n tendens","en":"Explain a trend"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Verduidelik waarom die atoomradius van natrium (Na) groter is as dié van chloor (Cl). (b) Verduidelik waarom kalium (K) heftiger met water reageer as natrium.","en":"(a) Explain why the atomic radius of sodium (Na) is larger than that of chlorine (Cl). (b) Explain why potassium (K) reacts more vigorously with water than sodium."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Na en Cl is albei in periode 3: hul buitenste elektrone is in dieselfde (derde) energievlak.","en":"(a) Na and Cl are both in period 3: their outer electrons are in the same (third) energy level."},{"af":"Cl het 17 protone en Na net 11. Die groter kernlading van Cl trek die buitenste elektrone sterker na die kern, dus is die Cl-atoom kleiner.","en":"Cl has 17 protons and Na only 11. The greater nuclear charge of Cl pulls the outer electrons more strongly towards the nucleus, so the Cl atom is smaller."},{"af":"(b) K (periode 4) het een energievlak meer as Na (periode 3). Sy valenselektron is verder van die kern en word meer deur die binneste elektrone afgeskerm.","en":"(b) K (period 4) has one more energy level than Na (period 3). Its valence electron is further from the nucleus and more shielded by the inner electrons."},{"af":"Die aantrekking op dié elektron is swakker, dus het K 'n laer ionisasie-energie. K verloor sy valenselektron makliker en reageer heftiger.","en":"The attraction on that electron is weaker, so K has a lower ionisation energy. K loses its valence electron more easily and reacts more vigorously."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Dieselfde aantal energievlakke, maar Cl het 'n groter kernlading wat die elektrone nader trek. (b) K se valenselektron is verder van die kern en meer afgeskerm, dus laer ionisasie-energie en hoër reaktiwiteit.","en":"(a) Same number of energy levels, but Cl has a greater nuclear charge that pulls the electrons closer. (b) K's valence electron is further from the nucleus and more shielded, so lower ionisation energy and higher reactivity."}},{"title":{"af":"Ioniese binding en formules","en":"Ionic bonding and formulae"},"problem":{"af":"Magnesium reageer met chloor. (a) Beskryf hoe die ione vorm. (b) Beskryf die Lewis-diagram van die produk in woorde. (c) Skryf die formule van die produk. (d) Gebruik die kruismetode om die formule van aluminiumoksied te skryf.","en":"Magnesium reacts with chlorine. (a) Describe how the ions form. (b) Describe the Lewis diagram of the product in words. (c) Write the formula of the product. (d) Use the criss-cross method to write the formula of aluminium oxide."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Mg (2 valenselektrone) verloor 2 elektrone en word Mg²⁺ met die konfigurasie van Ne. Elke Cl-atoom (7 valenselektrone) kry 1 elektron en word Cl⁻ met die konfigurasie van Ar. Een Mg-atoom gee dus een elektron aan elk van twee Cl-atome.","en":"(a) Mg (2 valence electrons) loses 2 electrons and becomes Mg²⁺ with the configuration of Ne. Each Cl atom (7 valence electrons) gains 1 electron and becomes Cl⁻ with the configuration of Ar. One Mg atom therefore gives one electron to each of two Cl atoms."},{"af":"(b) Lewis-diagram: [Mg]²⁺ sonder valenselektrone in vierkantige hakies, en twee [Cl]⁻-ione, elk met 8 elektrone (7 kolletjies en 1 kruisie van Mg) in vierkantige hakies met die lading.","en":"(b) Lewis diagram: [Mg]²⁺ with no valence electrons in square brackets, and two [Cl]⁻ ions, each with 8 electrons (7 dots and 1 cross from Mg) in square brackets with the charge."},{"af":"(c) Totale lading: (+2) + 2(−1) = 0, dus is die formule MgCl₂.","en":"(c) Total charge: (+2) + 2(−1) = 0, so the formula is MgCl₂."},{"af":"(d) Al³⁺ en O²⁻: ruil die getalle van die ladings om → Al₂O₃. Kontroleer: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = +6 − 6 = 0.","en":"(d) Al³⁺ and O²⁻: swap the numbers of the charges → Al₂O₃. Check: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = +6 − 6 = 0."}],"answer":{"af":"MgCl₂ (magnesiumchloried); Al₂O₃ (aluminiumoksied)","en":"MgCl₂ (magnesium chloride); Al₂O₃ (aluminium oxide)"}},{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die binding uit die eienskappe","en":"Identify the bonding from the properties"},"problem":{"af":"Drie vastestowwe word getoets. A smelt by 801 °C en gelei nie as vastestof nie, maar wel wanneer dit in water opgelos is. B smelt by 1 085 °C, gelei as vastestof en kan in draad uitgetrek word. C smelt reeds by 80 °C en gelei in geen toestand nie. Identifiseer die tipe binding in elke stof en verduidelik telkens.","en":"Three solids are tested. A melts at 801 °C and does not conduct as a solid, but does conduct when dissolved in water. B melts at 1 085 °C, conducts as a solid and can be drawn into a wire. C already melts at 80 °C and does not conduct in any state. Identify the type of bonding in each substance and explain each time."},"steps":[{"af":"A: hoë smeltpunt en gelei slegs in oplossing → ionies. In die vastestof sit die ione vas in die kristalrooster; in oplossing kan die ione vrylik beweeg en lading dra.","en":"A: high melting point and conducts only in solution → ionic. In the solid the ions are fixed in the crystal lattice; in solution the ions can move freely and carry charge."},{"af":"B: gelei as vastestof en is rekbaar → metaalbinding. Die gedelokaliseerde elektrone beweeg vrylik, en die lae positiewe ione kan oor mekaar gly sonder dat die metaal breek.","en":"B: conducts as a solid and is ductile → metallic bonding. The delocalised electrons move freely, and the layers of positive ions can slide over each other without the metal breaking."},{"af":"C: lae smeltpunt en gelei nooit → kovalent (molekulêr). Net swak kragte hou die molekules bymekaar, en daar is geen vrye gelaaide deeltjies nie.","en":"C: low melting point and never conducts → covalent (molecular). Only weak forces hold the molecules together, and there are no free charged particles."}],"answer":{"af":"A: ionies; B: metaalbinding; C: kovalent molekulêr","en":"A: ionic; B: metallic bonding; C: covalent molecular"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke groep in die periodieke tabel by sy naam.","en":"Match each group in the periodic table to its name."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Groep 1","en":"Group 1"},"r":{"af":"Alkalimetale","en":"Alkali metals"}},{"l":{"af":"Groep 2","en":"Group 2"},"r":{"af":"Aardalkalimetale","en":"Alkaline earth metals"}},{"l":{"af":"Groep 17","en":"Group 17"},"r":{"af":"Halogene","en":"Halogens"}},{"l":{"af":"Groep 18","en":"Group 18"},"r":{"af":"Edelgasse","en":"Noble gases"}}],"explain":{"af":"Groep 1: alkalimetale (1 valenselektron); groep 2: aardalkalimetale (2); groep 17: halogene (7); groep 18: edelgasse (volle buitenste energievlak).","en":"Group 1: alkali metals (1 valence electron); group 2: alkaline earth metals (2); group 17: halogens (7); group 18: noble gases (full outer energy level)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die definisie van elektronegatiwiteit?","en":"Which statement is the definition of electronegativity?"},"options":[{"af":"Die energie benodig per mol om die eerste elektron uit 'n atoom in die gasfase te verwyder","en":"The energy needed per mole to remove the first electron from an atom in the gaseous phase"},{"af":"Die energie wat vrygestel word wanneer 'n elektron aan 'n atoom geheg word om 'n negatiewe ioon te vorm","en":"The energy released when an electron is attached to an atom to form a negative ion"},{"af":"'n Maatstaf van die neiging van 'n atoom in 'n molekuul om bindingselektrone aan te trek","en":"A measure of the tendency of an atom in a molecule to attract bonding electrons"},{"af":"Die afstand van die middel van die kern tot by die buitenste elektrone","en":"The distance from the centre of the nucleus to the outermost electrons"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Elektronegatiwiteit gaan oor bindingselektrone in 'n molekuul. Die eerste opsie is ionisasie-energie, die tweede elektronaffiniteit en die laaste atoomradius.","en":"Electronegativity is about bonding electrons in a molecule. The first option is ionisation energy, the second electron affinity and the last atomic radius."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Fosfor (P) is in groep 15. Hoeveel valenselektrone het 'n fosforatoom? ___","en":"Phosphorus (P) is in group 15. How many valence electrons does a phosphorus atom have? ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf","5 valenselektrone","5 elektrone"],"en":["5","five","5 valence electrons","5 electrons"]},"explain":{"af":"Vir groepe 13–18: valenselektrone = groepnommer − 10 = 15 − 10 = 5 (konfigurasie 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p³: 2 + 3 = 5).","en":"For groups 13–18: valence electrons = group number − 10 = 15 − 10 = 5 (configuration 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p³: 2 + 3 = 5)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die atoomradius neem af van links na regs oor 'n periode.","en":"The atomic radius decreases from left to right across a period."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die kernlading neem toe terwyl die elektrone in dieselfde energievlak bykom, dus word die buitenste elektrone nader aan die kern getrek.","en":"True. The nuclear charge increases while the electrons are added to the same energy level, so the outer electrons are pulled closer to the nucleus."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van hierdie elemente het die hoogste eerste ionisasie-energie?","en":"Which of these elements has the highest first ionisation energy?"},"options":[{"af":"K","en":"K"},{"af":"Na","en":"Na"},{"af":"Mg","en":"Mg"},{"af":"Ar","en":"Ar"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ionisasie-energie neem toe oor 'n periode en af in 'n groep. Ar is 'n edelgas heel regs in periode 3 met 'n volle buitenste energievlak. K het die laagste, want dit is laer af in groep 1.","en":"Ionisation energy increases across a period and decreases down a group. Ar is a noble gas on the far right of period 3 with a full outer energy level. K has the lowest, because it is further down group 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vaste natriumchloried gelei elektrisiteit, want dit bestaan uit ione.","en":"Solid sodium chloride conducts electricity because it consists of ions."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. In die vastestof sit die ione vas in die kristalrooster en kan nie beweeg nie. NaCl gelei slegs wanneer dit gesmelt of in water opgelos is.","en":"False. In the solid the ions are fixed in the crystal lattice and cannot move. NaCl conducts only when it is molten or dissolved in water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stof bestaan uit 'n kristalrooster van positiewe en negatiewe ione?","en":"Which substance consists of a crystal lattice of positive and negative ions?"},"options":[{"af":"KBr","en":"KBr"},{"af":"Cu","en":"Cu"},{"af":"CO₂","en":"CO₂"},{"af":"H₂O","en":"H₂O"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"KBr is 'n metaal (K) plus 'n nie-metaal (Br): ioniese binding. Cu het metaalbinding (positiewe ione in 'n see van elektrone), en CO₂ en H₂O is kovalente molekules.","en":"KBr is a metal (K) plus a non-metal (Br): ionic bonding. Cu has metallic bonding (positive ions in a sea of electrons), and CO₂ and H₂O are covalent molecules."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel elektrone het 'n Ca²⁺-ioon? (Atoomgetal van Ca = 20) ___","en":"How many electrons does a Ca²⁺ ion have? (Atomic number of Ca = 20) ___"},"answers":{"af":["18","18 elektrone","agtien"],"en":["18","18 electrons","eighteen"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Ca-atoom het 20 elektrone. Die lading 2+ beteken dat dit 2 elektrone verloor het: 20 − 2 = 18. (22 is die algemene fout: die elektrone bytel.)","en":"A Ca atom has 20 electrons. The 2+ charge means it lost 2 electrons: 20 − 2 = 18. (22 is the common mistake: adding the electrons.)"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gebruik die kruismetode. Die formule van aluminiumoksied is ___.","en":"Use the criss-cross method. The formula of aluminium oxide is ___."},"answers":{"af":["Al₂O₃","Al2O3"],"en":["Al₂O₃","Al2O3"]},"explain":{"af":"Al³⁺ en O²⁻: ruil die getalle van die ladings om → Al₂O₃. Kontroleer: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = 0.","en":"Al³⁺ and O²⁻: swap the numbers of the charges → Al₂O₃. Check: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = 0."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Element X het die elektronkonfigurasie 1s²2s²2p⁶3s². Wat is die formule van die verbinding wat X met chloor vorm?","en":"Element X has the electron configuration 1s²2s²2p⁶3s². What is the formula of the compound that X forms with chlorine?"},"options":[{"af":"XCl","en":"XCl"},{"af":"X₂Cl","en":"X₂Cl"},{"af":"XCl₂","en":"XCl₂"},{"af":"XCl₃","en":"XCl₃"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"X het 2 valenselektrone (3s²), dus vorm dit X²⁺ (dit is Mg). Chloor vorm Cl⁻. Vir 'n totale lading van nul is twee Cl⁻ nodig: XCl₂. X₂Cl is die kruismetode verkeerd om gedoen.","en":"X has 2 valence electrons (3s²), so it forms X²⁺ (it is Mg). Chlorine forms Cl⁻. For a total charge of zero, two Cl⁻ are needed: XCl₂. X₂Cl is the criss-cross method done the wrong way round."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel alleenpare (nie-bindende elektronpare) is daar op die suurstofatoom in die Lewis-diagram van 'n watermolekuul (H₂O)? ___","en":"How many lone pairs (non-bonding electron pairs) are there on the oxygen atom in the Lewis diagram of a water molecule (H₂O)? ___"},"answers":{"af":["2","twee","2 alleenpare"],"en":["2","two","2 lone pairs"]},"explain":{"af":"O het 6 valenselektrone. Twee daarvan word met die twee H-atome gedeel (2 bindingspare), en die oorblywende 4 elektrone vorm 2 alleenpare. Nou het O 'n oktet.","en":"O has 6 valence electrons. Two of them are shared with the two H atoms (2 bonding pairs), and the remaining 4 electrons form 2 lone pairs. O now has an octet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel bindende elektronpare is daar altesaam in die Lewis-diagram van CO₂?","en":"How many bonding electron pairs are there in total in the Lewis diagram of CO₂?"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"8","en":"8"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"CO₂ is O=C=O: twee dubbelbindings, elk met 2 gedeelde pare, dus 4 bindende pare. Dit is 8 bindingselektrone, maar die vraag vra na pare. 2 sou wees as jy enkelbindings teken; dan het C nie 'n oktet nie.","en":"CO₂ is O=C=O: two double bonds, each with 2 shared pairs, so 4 bonding pairs. That is 8 bonding electrons, but the question asks for pairs. 2 would be if you drew single bonds; then C would not have an octet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is die atoomradius van kalium (K) groter as dié van natrium (Na)?","en":"Why is the atomic radius of potassium (K) larger than that of sodium (Na)?"},"options":[{"af":"K het meer protone, so die kern stoot die elektrone verder weg","en":"K has more protons, so the nucleus pushes the electrons further away"},{"af":"K het meer neutrone, wat die atoom groter maak","en":"K has more neutrons, which make the atom bigger"},{"af":"K het 'n hoër elektronegatiwiteit as Na","en":"K has a higher electronegativity than Na"},{"af":"K het 'n ekstra energievlak, dus is sy buitenste elektron verder van die kern","en":"K has an extra energy level, so its outer electron is further from the nucleus"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"K is in periode 4 en Na in periode 3. Die ekstra energievlak plaas die valenselektron verder van die kern, en die binneste elektrone skerm dit af. Protone trek elektrone aan (stoot nie), neutrone bepaal nie die grootte nie, en K se elektronegatiwiteit (0,8) is laer as Na s'n (0,9).","en":"K is in period 4 and Na in period 3. The extra energy level places the valence electron further from the nucleus, and the inner electrons shield it. Protons attract electrons (they do not repel them), neutrons do not determine the size, and K's electronegativity (0.8) is lower than Na's (0.9)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Metaan (CH₄) kook by −162 °C. 'n Leerder sê: \"Dit is omdat die C–H-bindings in metaan swak is en maklik breek.\" Watter evaluering van die stelling is korrek?","en":"Methane (CH₄) boils at −162 °C. A learner says: \"This is because the C–H bonds in methane are weak and break easily.\" Which evaluation of the statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Korrek: kovalente bindings is altyd swak","en":"Correct: covalent bonds are always weak"},{"af":"Verkeerd: tydens kook breek die C–H-bindings nie; slegs die swak kragte tussen die metaanmolekules word oorkom","en":"Wrong: during boiling the C–H bonds do not break; only the weak forces between the methane molecules are overcome"},{"af":"Verkeerd: metaan is 'n ioniese stof, en ione trek mekaar swak aan","en":"Wrong: methane is an ionic substance, and ions attract each other weakly"},{"af":"Korrek: tydens kook skei die H-atome van die C-atoom","en":"Correct: during boiling the H atoms separate from the C atom"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gasvormige metaan bestaan steeds uit CH₄-molekules, dus het die C–H-bindings nie gebreek nie. Die lae kookpunt kom van die swak kragte tussen die molekules. Kovalente bindings self is sterk, en C en H is albei nie-metale, dus is metaan kovalent, nie ionies nie.","en":"Gaseous methane still consists of CH₄ molecules, so the C–H bonds did not break. The low boiling point comes from the weak forces between the molecules. Covalent bonds themselves are strong, and C and H are both non-metals, so methane is covalent, not ionic."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-pulse-transversale-golwe","title":{"af":"Pulse en transversale golwe","en":"Pulses and transverse waves"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal pulse en transversale golwe kan beskryf, superposisie kan toepas en golfberekeninge met v = fλ en T = 1/f kan doen.","en":"You will be able to describe pulses and transverse waves, apply superposition and do wave calculations with v = fλ and T = 1/f."},"summary":{"af":"## Pulse\n\n'n **Puls** is 'n enkele versteuring in 'n medium. Swaai die punt van 'n lang tou een keer op en af, en 'n bult beweeg langs die tou. Die **medium** is die stof waardeur die puls beweeg, soos die tou of 'n veer.\n\n'n **Transversale puls** is 'n puls waar die deeltjies van die medium **loodreg** op die bewegingsrigting van die puls beweeg. Die puls beweeg horisontaal, maar elke stukkie tou beweeg net op en af en keer terug na sy **rus- (ewewigs)posisie**. 'n Puls dra **energie** oor, nie die medium self nie. Dink aan die Mexikaanse golf op Loftus: die toeskouers bly by hul sitplekke en staan net op en sit, maar die golf beweeg om die hele pawiljoen.\n\n- **Amplitude:** die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy rus- (ewewigs)posisie. Meet dit vanaf die ewewigsposisie, **nie** van bo tot onder nie.\n- **Pulslengte:** die horisontale lengte van die puls.\n- Die spoed van 'n puls hang slegs af van die **medium** (bv. hoe styf gespan en hoe dik die tou is), nie van die amplitude nie.\n\n## Superposisie en interferensie\n\nAs twee pulse mekaar ontmoet, tel hulle versteurings bymekaar. **Superposisie** is die algebraïese som van die amplitudes van twee pulse wat dieselfde ruimte op dieselfde tyd beset.\n\nKies \"op\" as positief en \"af\" as negatief:\n\n- **Konstruktiewe interferensie:** 'n kruin oorvleuel met 'n kruin (of 'n trog met 'n trog). Die resulterende amplitude is **groter**: 4 cm + 3 cm = 7 cm.\n- **Destruktiewe interferensie:** 'n kruin oorvleuel met 'n trog. Die resulterende amplitude is **kleiner**: 4 cm + (−3 cm) = 1 cm (bo die ewewigsposisie). As die twee amplitudes ewe groot is, is die resultaat nul: volledige destruktiewe interferensie.\n\nNá die ontmoeting beweeg elke puls **onveranderd** verder, met sy oorspronklike vorm, amplitude en rigting.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om by destruktiewe interferensie die groottes bymekaar te tel. Gebruik die tekens: 'n puls onder die ewewigsposisie is negatief.\n\n## Transversale golwe\n\n'n **Golf** is 'n opeenvolging van pulse. 'n **Transversale golf** is 'n golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium **loodreg** op die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.\n\n| Begrip | Definisie | Eenheid |\n|---|---|---|\n| Kruin | die hoogste punt op die golf (maksimum positiewe versteuring) | – |\n| Trog | die laagste punt op die golf (maksimum negatiewe versteuring) | – |\n| Amplitude | die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy ewewigsposisie | m |\n| Golflengte (λ) | die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase, bv. van kruin tot kruin | m |\n| Frekwensie (f) | die aantal golfpulse per sekonde | Hz (= s⁻¹) |\n| Periode (T) | die tyd wat dit neem vir een volledige golfpuls | s |\n\n### Punte in fase en uit fase\n\nPunte **in fase** is op presies dieselfde posisie in die siklus en beweeg in dieselfde rigting, bv. twee kruine of twee trôe. Hulle is 'n heelgetal golflengtes (1λ; 2λ; 3λ …) uitmekaar. Punte wat nie in fase is nie, is **uit fase**. 'n Kruin en die volgende trog is ½λ uitmekaar en is heeltemal uit fase.\n\n## Die formules\n\n- **T = [[1/f]]** en **f = [[1/T]]**: die periode en frekwensie is mekaar se omgekeerdes.\n- **v = fλ**: golfspoed (m·s⁻¹) = frekwensie (Hz) × golflengte (m).\n- Afstand wat die golf aflê: afstand = v × t.\n\n**Hoekom werk v = fλ?** In een periode T beweeg die golf presies een golflengte λ vorentoe, dus v = [[λ/T]] = fλ.\n\n- Die golfspoed hang van die **medium** af. In dieselfde medium bly v konstant: as f verdubbel, halveer λ.\n- Skakel eers om na SI-eenhede: cm → m (÷ 100), kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000).\n\n> **Wenk:** \"20 golwe gaan in 4 s verby\" beteken f = [[20/4]] = 5 Hz. \"Die afstand tussen 'n kruin en die volgende trog is 0,5 m\" beteken λ = 2 × 0,5 = 1 m.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die vertikale afstand van kruin tot trog as die amplitude te gebruik. Die amplitude is die **helfte** daarvan.\n\n## Grafieke in woorde\n\nOp 'n **verplasing-posisie-grafiek** (y-as: versteuring; x-as: afstand in m) lees jy die amplitude vertikaal af en die golflengte horisontaal, van kruin tot kruin. Op 'n **verplasing-tyd-grafiek** (x-as: tyd in s) is die tyd van kruin tot kruin die **periode T**, nie die golflengte nie.\n\n## Stappe vir berekeninge\n\n1. Lys die gegewe waardes en skakel om na SI-eenhede.\n2. Skryf die formule neer.\n3. Vervang en bereken.\n4. Gee die antwoord met die eenheid, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"## Pulses\n\nA **pulse** is a single disturbance in a medium. Flick the end of a long rope up and down once, and a bump travels along the rope. The **medium** is the substance through which the pulse travels, such as the rope or a spring.\n\nA **transverse pulse** is a pulse in which the particles of the medium move **perpendicular** to the direction of motion of the pulse. The pulse travels horizontally, but each piece of rope only moves up and down and returns to its **rest (equilibrium) position**. A pulse transfers **energy**, not the medium itself. Think of the Mexican wave at Loftus: the spectators stay at their seats and only stand up and sit down, but the wave moves around the whole stand.\n\n- **Amplitude:** the maximum disturbance of a particle from its rest (equilibrium) position. Measure it from the equilibrium position, **not** from top to bottom.\n- **Pulse length:** the horizontal length of the pulse.\n- The speed of a pulse depends only on the **medium** (e.g. how tightly stretched and how thick the rope is), not on the amplitude.\n\n## Superposition and interference\n\nWhen two pulses meet, their disturbances add up. **Superposition** is the algebraic sum of the amplitudes of two pulses that occupy the same space at the same time.\n\nChoose \"up\" as positive and \"down\" as negative:\n\n- **Constructive interference:** a crest overlaps with a crest (or a trough with a trough). The resultant amplitude is **larger**: 4 cm + 3 cm = 7 cm.\n- **Destructive interference:** a crest overlaps with a trough. The resultant amplitude is **smaller**: 4 cm + (−3 cm) = 1 cm (above the equilibrium position). If the two amplitudes are equal, the result is zero: complete destructive interference.\n\nAfter meeting, each pulse continues **unchanged**, with its original shape, amplitude and direction.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Adding the sizes in destructive interference. Use the signs: a pulse below the equilibrium position is negative.\n\n## Transverse waves\n\nA **wave** is a succession of pulses. A **transverse wave** is a wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate **perpendicular** to the direction of motion of the wave.\n\n| Concept | Definition | Unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Crest | the highest point on the wave (maximum positive disturbance) | – |\n| Trough | the lowest point on the wave (maximum negative disturbance) | – |\n| Amplitude | the maximum disturbance of a particle from its equilibrium position | m |\n| Wavelength (λ) | the distance between two successive points in phase, e.g. from crest to crest | m |\n| Frequency (f) | the number of wave pulses per second | Hz (= s⁻¹) |\n| Period (T) | the time taken for one complete wave pulse | s |\n\n### Points in phase and out of phase\n\nPoints **in phase** are at exactly the same position in the cycle and move in the same direction, e.g. two crests or two troughs. They are a whole number of wavelengths (1λ; 2λ; 3λ …) apart. Points that are not in phase are **out of phase**. A crest and the next trough are ½λ apart and are completely out of phase.\n\n## The formulae\n\n- **T = [[1/f]]** and **f = [[1/T]]**: period and frequency are each other's reciprocals.\n- **v = fλ**: wave speed (m·s⁻¹) = frequency (Hz) × wavelength (m).\n- Distance the wave covers: distance = v × t.\n\n**Why does v = fλ work?** In one period T the wave moves forward exactly one wavelength λ, so v = [[λ/T]] = fλ.\n\n- The wave speed depends on the **medium**. In the same medium v stays constant: if f doubles, λ halves.\n- First convert to SI units: cm → m (÷ 100), kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000).\n\n> **Tip:** \"20 waves pass in 4 s\" means f = [[20/4]] = 5 Hz. \"The distance between a crest and the next trough is 0.5 m\" means λ = 2 × 0.5 = 1 m.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Using the vertical distance from crest to trough as the amplitude. The amplitude is **half** of that.\n\n## Graphs in words\n\nOn a **displacement–position graph** (y-axis: disturbance; x-axis: distance in m) you read the amplitude vertically and the wavelength horizontally, from crest to crest. On a **displacement–time graph** (x-axis: time in s) the time from crest to crest is the **period T**, not the wavelength.\n\n## Steps for calculations\n\n1. List the given values and convert to SI units.\n2. Write down the formula.\n3. Substitute and calculate.\n4. Give the answer with the unit, rounded to two decimal places."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Puls","en":"Pulse"},"def":{"af":"'n Enkele versteuring in 'n medium.","en":"A single disturbance in a medium."}},{"term":{"af":"Transversale golf","en":"Transverse wave"},"def":{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium loodreg op die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate perpendicular to the direction of motion of the wave."}},{"term":{"af":"Amplitude","en":"Amplitude"},"def":{"af":"Die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy rus- (ewewigs)posisie.","en":"The maximum disturbance of a particle from its rest (equilibrium) position."}},{"term":{"af":"Superposisie","en":"Superposition"},"def":{"af":"Die algebraïese som van die amplitudes van twee pulse wat dieselfde ruimte op dieselfde tyd beset.","en":"The algebraic sum of the amplitudes of two pulses that occupy the same space at the same time."}},{"term":{"af":"Konstruktiewe interferensie","en":"Constructive interference"},"def":{"af":"Die verskynsel waar die kruin van een golf met die kruin van 'n ander golf oorvleuel om 'n golf met 'n groter amplitude te vorm.","en":"The phenomenon where the crest of one wave overlaps with the crest of another wave to produce a wave of increased amplitude."}},{"term":{"af":"Destruktiewe interferensie","en":"Destructive interference"},"def":{"af":"Die verskynsel waar die kruin van een golf met die trog van 'n ander golf oorvleuel, wat 'n golf met 'n kleiner amplitude tot gevolg het.","en":"The phenomenon where the crest of one wave overlaps with the trough of another wave, resulting in a wave of reduced amplitude."}},{"term":{"af":"Golflengte (λ)","en":"Wavelength (λ)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase. Eenheid: m.","en":"The distance between two successive points in phase. Unit: m."}},{"term":{"af":"Frekwensie (f)","en":"Frequency (f)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal golfpulse per sekonde. Eenheid: hertz (Hz).","en":"The number of wave pulses per second. Unit: hertz (Hz)."}},{"term":{"af":"Periode (T)","en":"Period (T)"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd wat dit neem vir een volledige golfpuls. Eenheid: s. T = 1/f.","en":"The time taken for one complete wave pulse. Unit: s. T = 1/f."}},{"term":{"af":"In fase","en":"In phase"},"def":{"af":"Punte wat op dieselfde posisie in die siklus is en in dieselfde rigting beweeg; hulle is 'n heelgetal golflengtes uitmekaar.","en":"Points at the same position in the cycle moving in the same direction; they are a whole number of wavelengths apart."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Superposisie van twee pulse","en":"Superposition of two pulses"},"problem":{"af":"Twee pulse beweeg op 'n tou na mekaar toe. Puls A het 'n amplitude van 4 cm bo die ewewigsposisie. (a) Puls B het 'n amplitude van 3 cm, ook bo die ewewigsposisie. Wat is die amplitude van die resulterende puls wanneer A en B presies oorvleuel? (b) Herhaal (a) as puls B 3 cm onder die ewewigsposisie is. (c) Beskryf die twee pulse nadat hulle by mekaar verby is.","en":"Two pulses move towards each other on a rope. Pulse A has an amplitude of 4 cm above the equilibrium position. (a) Pulse B has an amplitude of 3 cm, also above the equilibrium position. What is the amplitude of the resultant pulse when A and B overlap exactly? (b) Repeat (a) if pulse B is 3 cm below the equilibrium position. (c) Describe the two pulses after they have passed each other."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies op as positief: A = +4 cm.","en":"Choose up as positive: A = +4 cm."},{"af":"(a) B = +3 cm. Superposisie: (+4) + (+3) = +7 cm. Kruin op kruin: konstruktiewe interferensie.","en":"(a) B = +3 cm. Superposition: (+4) + (+3) = +7 cm. Crest on crest: constructive interference."},{"af":"(b) B = −3 cm. Superposisie: (+4) + (−3) = +1 cm, dus 1 cm bo die ewewigsposisie. Kruin op trog: destruktiewe interferensie.","en":"(b) B = −3 cm. Superposition: (+4) + (−3) = +1 cm, so 1 cm above the equilibrium position. Crest on trough: destructive interference."},{"af":"(c) Ná die ontmoeting beweeg A (4 cm) en B (3 cm) onveranderd verder in hul oorspronklike rigtings.","en":"(c) After meeting, A (4 cm) and B (3 cm) continue unchanged in their original directions."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 7 cm (konstruktief) (b) 1 cm bo die ewewigsposisie (destruktief) (c) Albei pulse beweeg onveranderd verder.","en":"(a) 7 cm (constructive) (b) 1 cm above the equilibrium position (destructive) (c) Both pulses continue unchanged."}},{"title":{"af":"Golflengte, frekwensie, periode en spoed","en":"Wavelength, frequency, period and speed"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo swaai by rugbyoefening 'n lang tou op en af. Die horisontale afstand tussen 'n kruin en die trog langsaan is 0,6 m, en 15 volledige golwe gaan in 6 s by 'n punt verby. Bereken (a) die golflengte, (b) die frekwensie, (c) die periode en (d) die golfspoed.","en":"At rugby practice Thabo swings a long rope up and down. The horizontal distance between a crest and the neighbouring trough is 0.6 m, and 15 complete waves pass a point in 6 s. Calculate (a) the wavelength, (b) the frequency, (c) the period and (d) the wave speed."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Van 'n kruin tot die volgende trog is ½λ, dus λ = 2 × 0,6 = 1,2 m.","en":"(a) From a crest to the next trough is ½λ, so λ = 2 × 0.6 = 1.2 m."},{"af":"(b) f = [[aantal golwe/tyd]] = [[15/6]] = 2,5 Hz","en":"(b) f = [[number of waves/time]] = [[15/6]] = 2.5 Hz"},{"af":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/2,5]] = 0,4 s","en":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/2.5]] = 0.4 s"},{"af":"(d) v = fλ = 2,5 × 1,2 = 3 m·s⁻¹","en":"(d) v = fλ = 2.5 × 1.2 = 3 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":{"af":"λ = 1,2 m; f = 2,5 Hz; T = 0,4 s; v = 3 m·s⁻¹","en":"λ = 1.2 m; f = 2.5 Hz; T = 0.4 s; v = 3 m·s⁻¹"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees 'n golf af van 'n grafiek (in woorde)","en":"Read a wave from a graph (in words)"},"problem":{"af":"'n Verplasing-posisie-grafiek van 'n transversale golf op 'n tou word so beskryf: die x-as loop van 0 tot 4,5 m, en presies 3 volledige golwe pas in daardie afstand. Die kruine is 0,2 m bo die ewewigsposisie en die trôe 0,2 m onder die ewewigsposisie. Die bron vibreer teen 4 Hz. Bepaal (a) die amplitude, (b) die golflengte en (c) die golfspoed. (d) Hoe ver beweeg die golf in 3 s?","en":"A displacement–position graph of a transverse wave on a rope is described as follows: the x-axis runs from 0 to 4.5 m, and exactly 3 complete waves fit into that distance. The crests are 0.2 m above the equilibrium position and the troughs 0.2 m below the equilibrium position. The source vibrates at 4 Hz. Determine (a) the amplitude, (b) the wavelength and (c) the wave speed. (d) How far does the wave travel in 3 s?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Amplitude = maksimum versteuring vanaf die ewewigsposisie = 0,2 m (nie 0,4 m van kruin tot trog nie).","en":"(a) Amplitude = maximum disturbance from the equilibrium position = 0.2 m (not 0.4 m from crest to trough)."},{"af":"(b) 3λ = 4,5 m, dus λ = [[4,5/3]] = 1,5 m","en":"(b) 3λ = 4.5 m, so λ = [[4.5/3]] = 1.5 m"},{"af":"(c) v = fλ = 4 × 1,5 = 6 m·s⁻¹","en":"(c) v = fλ = 4 × 1.5 = 6 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(d) afstand = v × t = 6 × 3 = 18 m","en":"(d) distance = v × t = 6 × 3 = 18 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Amplitude = 0,2 m; λ = 1,5 m; v = 6 m·s⁻¹; afstand = 18 m","en":"Amplitude = 0.2 m; λ = 1.5 m; v = 6 m·s⁻¹; distance = 18 m"}},{"title":{"af":"Punte in fase en 'n verandering in frekwensie","en":"Points in phase and a change in frequency"},"problem":{"af":"Op 'n transversale golf met 'n golflengte van 2 m lê punt A op 'n kruin. Punt B is 1 m regs van A, punt C is 2 m regs van A en punt D is 4 m regs van A. (a) Watter punte is in fase met A? (b) Beskryf die posisie van B. (c) Die frekwensie is 1,5 Hz. Die bron se frekwensie word nou verdubbel terwyl die golf in dieselfde tou bly. Bereken die nuwe golflengte.","en":"On a transverse wave with a wavelength of 2 m, point A lies on a crest. Point B is 1 m to the right of A, point C is 2 m to the right of A and point D is 4 m to the right of A. (a) Which points are in phase with A? (b) Describe the position of B. (c) The frequency is 1.5 Hz. The source's frequency is now doubled while the wave stays in the same rope. Calculate the new wavelength."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Punte in fase is 'n heelgetal golflengtes uitmekaar. C is 2 m = 1λ van A en D is 4 m = 2λ van A, dus is C en D in fase met A (albei op 'n kruin).","en":"(a) Points in phase are a whole number of wavelengths apart. C is 2 m = 1λ from A and D is 4 m = 2λ from A, so C and D are in phase with A (both on a crest)."},{"af":"(b) B is 1 m = ½λ van A, dus lê B op 'n trog en is heeltemal uit fase met A.","en":"(b) B is 1 m = ½λ from A, so B lies on a trough and is completely out of phase with A."},{"af":"(c) Oorspronklike spoed: v = fλ = 1,5 × 2 = 3 m·s⁻¹. Dieselfde medium, dus bly v = 3 m·s⁻¹.","en":"(c) Original speed: v = fλ = 1.5 × 2 = 3 m·s⁻¹. Same medium, so v stays 3 m·s⁻¹."},{"af":"Nuwe f = 2 × 1,5 = 3 Hz, dus λ = [[v/f]] = [[3/3]] = 1 m. Die frekwensie het verdubbel en die golflengte het gehalveer.","en":"New f = 2 × 1.5 = 3 Hz, so λ = [[v/f]] = [[3/3]] = 1 m. The frequency doubled and the wavelength halved."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) C en D (b) B lê op 'n trog en is uit fase met A (c) λ = 1 m","en":"(a) C and D (b) B lies on a trough and is out of phase with A (c) λ = 1 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n puls?","en":"What is a pulse?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Opeenvolging van pulse","en":"A succession of pulses"},{"af":"'n Enkele versteuring in 'n medium","en":"A single disturbance in a medium"},{"af":"Die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy ewewigsposisie","en":"The maximum disturbance of a particle from its equilibrium position"},{"af":"Die aantal golfpulse per sekonde","en":"The number of wave pulses per second"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Puls is 'n enkele versteuring in 'n medium. 'n Opeenvolging van pulse is 'n golf; die derde opsie is amplitude en die laaste frekwensie.","en":"A pulse is a single disturbance in a medium. A succession of pulses is a wave; the third option is amplitude and the last is frequency."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte definisie.","en":"Match each concept to the correct definition."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kruin","en":"Crest"},"r":{"af":"Die hoogste punt op 'n golf","en":"The highest point on a wave"}},{"l":{"af":"Trog","en":"Trough"},"r":{"af":"Die laagste punt op 'n golf","en":"The lowest point on a wave"}},{"l":{"af":"Golflengte","en":"Wavelength"},"r":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase","en":"The distance between two successive points in phase"}},{"l":{"af":"Periode","en":"Period"},"r":{"af":"Die tyd vir een volledige golfpuls","en":"The time for one complete wave pulse"}},{"l":{"af":"Frekwensie","en":"Frequency"},"r":{"af":"Die aantal golfpulse per sekonde","en":"The number of wave pulses per second"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kruin en trog is die hoogste en laagste punte. Golflengte is 'n afstand (m), periode 'n tyd (s) en frekwensie 'n aantal per sekonde (Hz).","en":"Crest and trough are the highest and lowest points. Wavelength is a distance (m), period a time (s) and frequency a number per second (Hz)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n transversale golf vibreer die deeltjies van die medium parallel aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf.","en":"In a transverse wave the particles of the medium vibrate parallel to the direction of motion of the wave."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. In 'n transversale golf vibreer die deeltjies loodreg op die bewegingsrigting van die golf. Parallel is 'n longitudinale golf.","en":"False. In a transverse wave the particles vibrate perpendicular to the direction of motion of the wave. Parallel is a longitudinal wave."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die SI-eenheid van frekwensie?","en":"What is the SI unit of frequency?"},"options":[{"af":"s","en":"s"},{"af":"m·s⁻¹","en":"m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"m","en":"m"},{"af":"Hz","en":"Hz"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Frekwensie word in hertz gemeet: 1 Hz = 1 s⁻¹ (een golfpuls per sekonde). s is die eenheid van periode, m van golflengte en m·s⁻¹ van golfspoed.","en":"Frequency is measured in hertz: 1 Hz = 1 s⁻¹ (one wave pulse per second). s is the unit of period, m of wavelength and m·s⁻¹ of wave speed."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Nadat twee pulse deur mekaar beweeg het, beweeg elkeen verder met sy oorspronklike vorm en amplitude.","en":"After two pulses have passed through each other, each continues with its original shape and amplitude."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Pulse beïnvloed mekaar net terwyl hulle oorvleuel (superposisie). Daarna beweeg elkeen onveranderd verder.","en":"True. Pulses affect each other only while they overlap (superposition). Afterwards each continues unchanged."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Eskom se wisselstroom het 'n frekwensie van 50 Hz. Die periode is ___ s.","en":"Eskom's alternating current has a frequency of 50 Hz. The period is ___ s."},"answers":{"af":["0,02","0.02","0,02 s","0.02 s","1/50","2 × 10⁻²"],"en":["0.02","0,02","0.02 s","0,02 s","1/50","2 × 10⁻²"]},"explain":{"af":"T = 1/f = 1/50 = 0,02 s.","en":"T = 1/f = 1/50 = 0.02 s."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vertikale afstand van die bokant van 'n kruin tot die onderkant van 'n trog is 30 cm. Die amplitude is ___ cm.","en":"The vertical distance from the top of a crest to the bottom of a trough is 30 cm. The amplitude is ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["15","15 cm","0,15 m","0.15 m"],"en":["15","15 cm","0.15 m","0,15 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Die amplitude word vanaf die ewewigsposisie gemeet, dus is dit die helfte van kruin tot trog: 30 ÷ 2 = 15 cm.","en":"The amplitude is measured from the equilibrium position, so it is half of crest to trough: 30 ÷ 2 = 15 cm."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Puls P (5 cm bo die ewewigsposisie) en puls Q (2 cm onder die ewewigsposisie) oorvleuel presies. Wat is die resulterende versteuring?","en":"Pulse P (5 cm above the equilibrium position) and pulse Q (2 cm below the equilibrium position) overlap exactly. What is the resultant disturbance?"},"options":[{"af":"7 cm bo die ewewigsposisie","en":"7 cm above the equilibrium position"},{"af":"3 cm onder die ewewigsposisie","en":"3 cm below the equilibrium position"},{"af":"3 cm bo die ewewigsposisie","en":"3 cm above the equilibrium position"},{"af":"2,5 cm bo die ewewigsposisie","en":"2.5 cm above the equilibrium position"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Op is positief: (+5) + (−2) = +3 cm, dus 3 cm bo die ewewigsposisie. Dit is destruktiewe interferensie. 7 cm kry jy as jy die tekens ignoreer.","en":"Up is positive: (+5) + (−2) = +3 cm, so 3 cm above the equilibrium position. This is destructive interference. You get 7 cm if you ignore the signs."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Golf het 'n frekwensie van 4 Hz en 'n golflengte van 0,75 m. Die golfspoed is ___ m·s⁻¹.","en":"A wave has a frequency of 4 Hz and a wavelength of 0.75 m. The wave speed is ___ m·s⁻¹."},"answers":{"af":["3","3,0","3,00","3.0","3 m·s⁻¹","3 m/s","3 m.s-1"],"en":["3","3.0","3.00","3,0","3 m·s⁻¹","3 m/s","3 m.s-1"]},"explain":{"af":"v = fλ = 4 × 0,75 = 3 m·s⁻¹.","en":"v = fλ = 4 × 0.75 = 3 m·s⁻¹."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"20 volledige golwe gaan in 4 s by 'n punt verby, en die golflengte is 0,5 m. Wat is die golfspoed?","en":"20 complete waves pass a point in 4 s, and the wavelength is 0.5 m. What is the wave speed?"},"options":[{"af":"2,5 m·s⁻¹","en":"2.5 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"10 m·s⁻¹","en":"10 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"0,1 m·s⁻¹","en":"0.1 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"40 m·s⁻¹","en":"40 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"f = 20 ÷ 4 = 5 Hz, dan v = fλ = 5 × 0,5 = 2,5 m·s⁻¹. 10 m·s⁻¹ kry jy as jy 20 as die frekwensie gebruik; 0,1 m·s⁻¹ as jy f = 4 ÷ 20 bereken.","en":"f = 20 ÷ 4 = 5 Hz, then v = fλ = 5 × 0.5 = 2.5 m·s⁻¹. You get 10 m·s⁻¹ if you use 20 as the frequency; 0.1 m·s⁻¹ if you calculate f = 4 ÷ 20."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Golf beweeg teen 6 m·s⁻¹ langs 'n tou en het 'n golflengte van 1,5 m. Die periode is ___ s.","en":"A wave travels at 6 m·s⁻¹ along a rope and has a wavelength of 1.5 m. The period is ___ s."},"answers":{"af":["0,25","0.25","0,25 s","0.25 s","1/4"],"en":["0.25","0,25","0.25 s","0,25 s","1/4"]},"explain":{"af":"f = v/λ = 6 ÷ 1,5 = 4 Hz, dan T = 1/f = 1/4 = 0,25 s.","en":"f = v/λ = 6 ÷ 1.5 = 4 Hz, then T = 1/f = 1/4 = 0.25 s."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Transversale golf het 'n golflengte van 0,8 m. Punt A lê op 'n kruin. Watter punt is in fase met A?","en":"A transverse wave has a wavelength of 0.8 m. Point A lies on a crest. Which point is in phase with A?"},"options":[{"af":"Die punt 0,4 m regs van A","en":"The point 0.4 m to the right of A"},{"af":"Die punt 0,2 m regs van A","en":"The point 0.2 m to the right of A"},{"af":"Die punt 1,0 m regs van A","en":"The point 1.0 m to the right of A"},{"af":"Die punt 1,6 m regs van A","en":"The point 1.6 m to the right of A"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Punte in fase is 'n heelgetal golflengtes uitmekaar: 1,6 m = 2 × 0,8 m = 2λ, dus is daardie punt ook op 'n kruin. 0,4 m = ½λ is 'n trog (heeltemal uit fase); 0,2 m = ¼λ en 1,0 m = 1¼λ is by die ewewigsposisie.","en":"Points in phase are a whole number of wavelengths apart: 1.6 m = 2 × 0.8 m = 2λ, so that point is also on a crest. 0.4 m = ½λ is a trough (completely out of phase); 0.2 m = ¼λ and 1.0 m = 1¼λ are at the equilibrium position."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Golf beweeg in dieselfde tou, maar die frekwensie van die bron word verdubbel. Wat gebeur met die golfspoed en die golflengte?","en":"A wave travels in the same rope, but the frequency of the source is doubled. What happens to the wave speed and the wavelength?"},"options":[{"af":"Die spoed verdubbel; die golflengte bly dieselfde","en":"The speed doubles; the wavelength stays the same"},{"af":"Die spoed bly dieselfde; die golflengte halveer","en":"The speed stays the same; the wavelength halves"},{"af":"Die spoed bly dieselfde; die golflengte verdubbel","en":"The speed stays the same; the wavelength doubles"},{"af":"Die spoed halveer; die golflengte verdubbel","en":"The speed halves; the wavelength doubles"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die golfspoed hang net van die medium af, en die tou bly dieselfde, dus bly v konstant. Uit v = fλ: as f verdubbel, moet λ halveer.","en":"The wave speed depends only on the medium, and the rope stays the same, so v stays constant. From v = fλ: if f doubles, λ must halve."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho sê: \"As ek die tou harder swaai sodat die amplitude groter is, beweeg die golf vinniger.\" Watter evaluering is korrek?","en":"Sipho says: \"If I swing the rope harder so that the amplitude is bigger, the wave travels faster.\" Which evaluation is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: meer energie beteken altyd 'n hoër spoed","en":"He is right: more energy always means a higher speed"},{"af":"Hy is reg: v = fλ, en die amplitude is deel van die golflengte","en":"He is right: v = fλ, and the amplitude is part of the wavelength"},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: die spoed hang net van die medium af; 'n groter amplitude dra meer energie oor, maar teen dieselfde spoed","en":"He is wrong: the speed depends only on the medium; a bigger amplitude transfers more energy, but at the same speed"},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: 'n groter amplitude maak die golf altyd stadiger","en":"He is wrong: a bigger amplitude always makes the wave slower"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die golfspoed word deur die medium bepaal (hoe styf gespan en hoe dik die tou is). Die amplitude is 'n vertikale versteuring en kom nie in v = fλ voor nie. 'n Groter amplitude beteken net dat meer energie oorgedra word.","en":"The wave speed is determined by the medium (how tightly stretched and how thick the rope is). The amplitude is a vertical disturbance and does not appear in v = fλ. A bigger amplitude only means that more energy is transferred."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-longitudinale-golwe-klank","title":{"af":"Longitudinale golwe en klank","en":"Longitudinal waves and sound"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal longitudinale golwe en klank kan beskryf, toonhoogte en luidheid aan frekwensie en amplitude kan koppel, en berekeninge met v = fλ en eggo's kan doen.","en":"You will be able to describe longitudinal waves and sound, link pitch and loudness to frequency and amplitude, and do calculations with v = fλ and echoes."},"summary":{"af":"## Longitudinale golwe\n\nDruk en trek die punt van 'n slinky-veer heen en weer in die lengte van die veer, en jy sien digte en oop gebiede wat langs die veer beweeg.\n\n'n **Longitudinale golf** is 'n golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium **parallel** aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.\n\n- **Kompressie:** 'n gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die naaste aan mekaar is (hoë druk).\n- **Verdunning:** 'n gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die verste van mekaar is (lae druk).\n- **Golflengte (λ):** die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende kompressies (of twee opeenvolgende verdunnings). Van 'n kompressie tot die volgende verdunning is ½λ.\n- **Amplitude:** die maksimum verplasing van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy ewewigsposisie.\n- Frekwensie, periode en golfspoed werk presies soos by transversale golwe: **v = fλ** en **T = [[1/f]]**.\n\n| | Transversale golf | Longitudinale golf |\n|---|---|---|\n| Deeltjies vibreer | loodreg op die golfrigting | parallel aan die golfrigting |\n| \"Hoë\" deel | kruin | kompressie |\n| \"Lae\" deel | trog | verdunning |\n| Voorbeeld | golf op 'n tou | klank; 'n slinky wat gedruk en getrek word |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"Die afstand van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie is 1,2 m, dus λ = [[1,2/5]].\" Verkeerd! Tel die **gapings**: van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie is 4λ, dus λ = [[1,2/4]] = 0,3 m.\n\n## Klank\n\nKlank word deur **vibrasies** gemaak: jou stembande, die membraan van 'n luidspreker of 'n kitaarsnaar. Die vibrerende voorwerp druk en trek die lugdeeltjies, sodat kompressies en verdunnings deur die lug beweeg. **Klank is 'n longitudinale, meganiese golf**: dit het 'n **medium** nodig en kan **nie deur 'n vakuum** beweeg nie. Daarom is dit doodstil in die ruimte.\n\n### Die spoed van klank\n\n| Medium | Spoed van klank (ongeveer) |\n|---|---|\n| lug | 340 m·s⁻¹ |\n| water | 1 500 m·s⁻¹ |\n| staal | 5 000 m·s⁻¹ |\n\nKlank beweeg die **vinnigste in vastestowwe** en die stadigste in gasse. In 'n vastestof is die deeltjies naby aan mekaar en sterk aan mekaar gebind, dus word die vibrasie vinnig van deeltjie na deeltjie oorgedra. As daar by 'n myn naby Brits geskiet word, voel jy die skok deur die grond voordat jy die knal deur die lug hoor. In lug beweeg klank ook vinniger as die temperatuur hoër is.\n\n### Toonhoogte, luidheid en kwaliteit\n\n| Eienskap | Hang af van | Betekenis |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Toonhoogte** | frekwensie | hoë frekwensie = hoë (skril) toon; lae frekwensie = lae (diep) toon |\n| **Luidheid** | amplitude | groter amplitude = harder klank (meer energie word oorgedra) |\n| **Kwaliteit (toonkleur)** | die vorm van die golf | dieselfde noot op 'n kitaar en 'n klavier klink verskillend |\n\n'n Taxi se skril toeter het 'n hoër frekwensie as 'n vragmotor se diep toeter. Die gejuig van die skare by 'n rugbywedstryd het 'n groter amplitude as 'n fluistering.\n\n## Menslike gehoor, infraklank en ultraklank\n\n- Mense hoor frekwensies van ongeveer **20 Hz tot 20 000 Hz** (20 kHz). Met ouderdom verloor mense eerste die vermoë om hoë frekwensies te hoor.\n- **Infraklank:** frekwensies laer as 20 Hz (olifante kommunikeer daarmee).\n- **Ultraklank:** klank met frekwensies **hoër as 20 kHz**, te hoog vir mense om te hoor. Vlermuise en dolfyne stuur ultraklank uit en gebruik die eggo's om prooi en hindernisse op te spoor (eggolokasie).\n\n### Gebruike van ultraklank\n\n- **Mediese beelde**, bv. 'n skandering van 'n ongebore baba of van organe. Ultraklankpulse word die liggaam ingestuur; by elke grens tussen verskillende weefsels word 'n deel van die klank teruggekaats. 'n Rekenaar gebruik die tyd en die sterkte van die eggo's om 'n beeld te bou.\n- Ultraklank is 'n meganiese golf en **nie ioniserend nie** (anders as X-strale), daarom is dit veilig vir ongebore babas.\n- Die hoë frekwensie gee 'n **kort golflengte**, sodat klein besonderhede gesien kan word.\n- **Sonar** meet die diepte van die see of vind visskole. Ultraklank word ook gebruik om juwele en instrumente skoon te maak en in fisioterapie.\n\n## Eggo's\n\n'n **Eggo** is 'n weerkaatste klank. Die klank beweeg **na** die voorwerp **en terug**, dus is die afstand na die voorwerp die helfte van die totale afstand wat die klank aflê:\n\n**afstand = [[v × t/2]]**, waar t die tyd is vandat die klank gemaak word totdat die eggo gehoor word.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om te vergeet om deur 2 te deel. Die gemete tyd is vir die heen-en-terug-reis.\n\n> **Wenk:** Skakel altyd eers om na SI-eenhede: kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000), cm → m (÷ 100). Die spoed van klank word in die vraag gegee; dit is nie op die gegewensblad nie.","en":"## Longitudinal waves\n\nPush and pull the end of a slinky spring back and forth along the length of the spring, and you see dense and open regions moving along the spring.\n\nA **longitudinal wave** is a wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate **parallel** to the direction of motion of the wave.\n\n- **Compression:** a region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are closest together (high pressure).\n- **Rarefaction:** a region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are furthest apart (low pressure).\n- **Wavelength (λ):** the distance between two successive compressions (or two successive rarefactions). From a compression to the next rarefaction is ½λ.\n- **Amplitude:** the maximum displacement of a particle from its equilibrium position.\n- Frequency, period and wave speed work exactly as for transverse waves: **v = fλ** and **T = [[1/f]]**.\n\n| | Transverse wave | Longitudinal wave |\n|---|---|---|\n| Particles vibrate | perpendicular to the wave direction | parallel to the wave direction |\n| \"High\" part | crest | compression |\n| \"Low\" part | trough | rarefaction |\n| Example | wave on a rope | sound; a slinky pushed and pulled |\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"The distance from the 1st to the 5th compression is 1.2 m, so λ = [[1.2/5]].\" Wrong! Count the **gaps**: from the 1st to the 5th compression is 4λ, so λ = [[1.2/4]] = 0.3 m.\n\n## Sound\n\nSound is made by **vibrations**: your vocal cords, the membrane of a loudspeaker or a guitar string. The vibrating object pushes and pulls the air particles, so that compressions and rarefactions travel through the air. **Sound is a longitudinal, mechanical wave**: it needs a **medium** and **cannot travel through a vacuum**. That is why space is completely silent.\n\n### The speed of sound\n\n| Medium | Speed of sound (approximately) |\n|---|---|\n| air | 340 m·s⁻¹ |\n| water | 1 500 m·s⁻¹ |\n| steel | 5 000 m·s⁻¹ |\n\nSound travels **fastest in solids** and slowest in gases. In a solid the particles are close together and strongly bonded, so the vibration is passed on quickly from particle to particle. When there is blasting at a mine near Brits, you feel the shock through the ground before you hear the bang through the air. In air, sound also travels faster when the temperature is higher.\n\n### Pitch, loudness and quality\n\n| Property | Depends on | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pitch** | frequency | high frequency = high (shrill) note; low frequency = low (deep) note |\n| **Loudness** | amplitude | bigger amplitude = louder sound (more energy is transferred) |\n| **Quality (timbre)** | the shape of the wave | the same note on a guitar and a piano sounds different |\n\nA taxi's shrill hooter has a higher frequency than a truck's deep hooter. The cheering of the crowd at a rugby match has a bigger amplitude than a whisper.\n\n## Human hearing, infrasound and ultrasound\n\n- Humans hear frequencies from about **20 Hz to 20 000 Hz** (20 kHz). With age, people first lose the ability to hear high frequencies.\n- **Infrasound:** frequencies lower than 20 Hz (elephants communicate with it).\n- **Ultrasound:** sound with frequencies **higher than 20 kHz**, too high for humans to hear. Bats and dolphins send out ultrasound and use the echoes to find prey and obstacles (echolocation).\n\n### Uses of ultrasound\n\n- **Medical imaging**, e.g. a scan of an unborn baby or of organs. Ultrasound pulses are sent into the body; at every boundary between different tissues part of the sound is reflected. A computer uses the time and the strength of the echoes to build an image.\n- Ultrasound is a mechanical wave and **not ionising** (unlike X-rays), which is why it is safe for unborn babies.\n- The high frequency gives a **short wavelength**, so small details can be seen.\n- **Sonar** measures the depth of the sea or finds shoals of fish. Ultrasound is also used to clean jewellery and instruments, and in physiotherapy.\n\n## Echoes\n\nAn **echo** is a reflected sound. The sound travels **to** the object **and back**, so the distance to the object is half of the total distance the sound covers:\n\n**distance = [[v × t/2]]**, where t is the time from when the sound is made until the echo is heard.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Forgetting to divide by 2. The measured time is for the round trip.\n\n> **Tip:** Always convert to SI units first: kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000), cm → m (÷ 100). The speed of sound is given in the question; it is not on the data sheet."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Longitudinale golf","en":"Longitudinal wave"},"def":{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium parallel aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate parallel to the direction of motion of the wave."}},{"term":{"af":"Kompressie","en":"Compression"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die naaste aan mekaar is (hoë druk).","en":"A region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are closest together (high pressure)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verdunning","en":"Rarefaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die verste van mekaar is (lae druk).","en":"A region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are furthest apart (low pressure)."}},{"term":{"af":"Golflengte (longitudinaal)","en":"Wavelength (longitudinal)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende kompressies of twee opeenvolgende verdunnings.","en":"The distance between two successive compressions or two successive rarefactions."}},{"term":{"af":"Meganiese golf","en":"Mechanical wave"},"def":{"af":"'n Golf wat 'n medium nodig het om deur te beweeg, bv. klank. Dit kan nie deur 'n vakuum beweeg nie.","en":"A wave that needs a medium to travel through, e.g. sound. It cannot travel through a vacuum."}},{"term":{"af":"Toonhoogte","en":"Pitch"},"def":{"af":"Hoe hoog of laag 'n klank klink. Dit word deur die frekwensie bepaal: hoe hoër die frekwensie, hoe hoër die toonhoogte.","en":"How high or low a sound is. It is determined by the frequency: the higher the frequency, the higher the pitch."}},{"term":{"af":"Luidheid","en":"Loudness"},"def":{"af":"Hoe hard of sag 'n klank is. Dit word deur die amplitude bepaal: hoe groter die amplitude, hoe harder die klank.","en":"How loud or soft a sound is. It is determined by the amplitude: the bigger the amplitude, the louder the sound."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwaliteit (toonkleur)","en":"Quality (timbre)"},"def":{"af":"Die eienskap wat dieselfde noot van verskillende instrumente anders laat klink; dit hang af van die vorm van die golf.","en":"The property that makes the same note from different instruments sound different; it depends on the shape of the wave."}},{"term":{"af":"Ultraklank","en":"Ultrasound"},"def":{"af":"Klank met frekwensies hoër as 20 kHz, bo die menslike gehoorgebied.","en":"Sound with frequencies higher than 20 kHz, above the human hearing range."}},{"term":{"af":"Eggo","en":"Echo"},"def":{"af":"'n Weerkaatste klank. Afstand na die weerkaatsende voorwerp = v × t ÷ 2.","en":"A reflected sound. Distance to the reflecting object = v × t ÷ 2."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Golflengte en spoed op 'n slinky","en":"Wavelength and speed on a slinky"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato druk en trek die punt van 'n slinky-veer heen en weer met 'n frekwensie van 5 Hz. Die afstand van die 1ste tot die 4de kompressie is 90 cm. Bereken (a) die golflengte, (b) die golfspoed en (c) die periode.","en":"Lerato pushes and pulls the end of a slinky spring back and forth with a frequency of 5 Hz. The distance from the 1st to the 4th compression is 90 cm. Calculate (a) the wavelength, (b) the wave speed and (c) the period."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Tel die gapings: van die 1ste tot die 4de kompressie is 3 golflengtes. 3λ = 90 cm = 0,9 m.","en":"(a) Count the gaps: from the 1st to the 4th compression is 3 wavelengths. 3λ = 90 cm = 0.9 m."},{"af":"λ = [[0,9/3]] = 0,3 m","en":"λ = [[0.9/3]] = 0.3 m"},{"af":"(b) v = fλ = 5 × 0,3 = 1,5 m·s⁻¹","en":"(b) v = fλ = 5 × 0.3 = 1.5 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/5]] = 0,2 s","en":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/5]] = 0.2 s"}],"answer":{"af":"λ = 0,3 m; v = 1,5 m·s⁻¹; T = 0,2 s","en":"λ = 0.3 m; v = 1.5 m·s⁻¹; T = 0.2 s"}},{"title":{"af":"'n Eggo in die Magaliesberg","en":"An echo in the Magaliesberg"},"problem":{"af":"Jan staan voor 'n krans in die Magaliesberg en klap sy hande. Hy hoor die eggo 1,5 s later. Die spoed van klank in lug is 340 m·s⁻¹. (a) Hoe ver is die krans van Jan af? (b) Jan stap nader totdat die krans 170 m weg is. Hoe lank ná die klap hoor hy nou die eggo?","en":"Jan stands in front of a cliff in the Magaliesberg and claps his hands. He hears the echo 1.5 s later. The speed of sound in air is 340 m·s⁻¹. (a) How far is the cliff from Jan? (b) Jan walks closer until the cliff is 170 m away. How long after the clap does he now hear the echo?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die klank beweeg na die krans en terug, dus afstand = [[v × t/2]].","en":"(a) The sound travels to the cliff and back, so distance = [[v × t/2]]."},{"af":"afstand = [[340 × 1,5/2]] = [[510/2]] = 255 m","en":"distance = [[340 × 1.5/2]] = [[510/2]] = 255 m"},{"af":"(b) Die klank moet heen en terug beweeg: totale afstand = 2 × 170 = 340 m.","en":"(b) The sound must travel there and back: total distance = 2 × 170 = 340 m."},{"af":"t = [[totale afstand/v]] = [[340/340]] = 1 s","en":"t = [[total distance/v]] = [[340/340]] = 1 s"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 255 m (b) 1 s","en":"(a) 255 m (b) 1 s"}},{"title":{"af":"Sonar en die golflengte van ultraklank","en":"Sonar and the wavelength of ultrasound"},"problem":{"af":"'n Vissersboot stuur 'n ultraklankpuls met 'n frekwensie van 50 kHz na die seebodem. Die eggo word 0,8 s later ontvang. Die spoed van klank in seewater is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Bereken (a) die diepte van die see en (b) die golflengte van die ultraklank in die water. (c) Kan die bemanning die puls hoor? Verduidelik.","en":"A fishing boat sends an ultrasound pulse with a frequency of 50 kHz to the sea floor. The echo is received 0.8 s later. The speed of sound in sea water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Calculate (a) the depth of the sea and (b) the wavelength of the ultrasound in the water. (c) Can the crew hear the pulse? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) diepte = [[v × t/2]] = [[1 500 × 0,8/2]] = [[1 200/2]] = 600 m","en":"(a) depth = [[v × t/2]] = [[1 500 × 0.8/2]] = [[1 200/2]] = 600 m"},{"af":"(b) Skakel eers om: f = 50 kHz = 50 × 1 000 = 50 000 Hz.","en":"(b) First convert: f = 50 kHz = 50 × 1 000 = 50 000 Hz."},{"af":"λ = [[v/f]] = [[1 500/50 000]] = 0,03 m (3 cm)","en":"λ = [[v/f]] = [[1 500/50 000]] = 0.03 m (3 cm)"},{"af":"(c) Nee. 50 kHz is hoër as 20 kHz, die boonste grens van menslike gehoor. Dit is ultraklank.","en":"(c) No. 50 kHz is higher than 20 kHz, the upper limit of human hearing. It is ultrasound."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 600 m (b) 0,03 m (c) Nee, 50 kHz is ultraklank (bo 20 kHz).","en":"(a) 600 m (b) 0.03 m (c) No, 50 kHz is ultrasound (above 20 kHz)."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk twee klankgolwe","en":"Compare two sound waves"},"problem":{"af":"Twee klankgolwe word as verplasing-tyd-grafieke op 'n ossilloskoop vertoon. Golf A: amplitude 2 blokkies, 5 volledige golwe in 0,01 s. Golf B: amplitude 1 blokkie, 10 volledige golwe in 0,01 s. (a) Bereken die frekwensie van elke golf. (b) Watter klank is die hardste? (c) Watter klank het die hoogste toonhoogte? (d) Bereken die golflengte van B in lug (spoed van klank = 340 m·s⁻¹).","en":"Two sound waves are shown as displacement–time graphs on an oscilloscope. Wave A: amplitude 2 blocks, 5 complete waves in 0.01 s. Wave B: amplitude 1 block, 10 complete waves in 0.01 s. (a) Calculate the frequency of each wave. (b) Which sound is the loudest? (c) Which sound has the highest pitch? (d) Calculate the wavelength of B in air (speed of sound = 340 m·s⁻¹)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) f_{A} = [[5/0,01]] = 500 Hz en f_{B} = [[10/0,01]] = 1 000 Hz","en":"(a) f_{A} = [[5/0.01]] = 500 Hz and f_{B} = [[10/0.01]] = 1 000 Hz"},{"af":"(b) Luidheid hang van die amplitude af. A het die groter amplitude (2 blokkies teenoor 1), dus is A die hardste.","en":"(b) Loudness depends on the amplitude. A has the bigger amplitude (2 blocks versus 1), so A is the loudest."},{"af":"(c) Toonhoogte hang van die frekwensie af. B het die hoër frekwensie (1 000 Hz), dus het B die hoogste toonhoogte.","en":"(c) Pitch depends on the frequency. B has the higher frequency (1 000 Hz), so B has the highest pitch."},{"af":"(d) λ_{B} = [[v/f]] = [[340/1 000]] = 0,34 m","en":"(d) λ_{B} = [[v/f]] = [[340/1 000]] = 0.34 m"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 500 Hz en 1 000 Hz (b) A (c) B (d) 0,34 m","en":"(a) 500 Hz and 1 000 Hz (b) A (c) B (d) 0.34 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n longitudinale golf?","en":"What is a longitudinal wave?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium loodreg op die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate perpendicular to the direction of motion of the wave"},{"af":"'n Enkele versteuring in 'n medium","en":"A single disturbance in a medium"},{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium parallel aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate parallel to the direction of motion of the wave"},{"af":"'n Golf wat sonder 'n medium deur 'n vakuum kan beweeg","en":"A wave that can travel through a vacuum without a medium"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In 'n longitudinale golf vibreer die deeltjies parallel aan die golfrigting. Loodreg is 'n transversale golf, en 'n enkele versteuring is 'n puls.","en":"In a longitudinal wave the particles vibrate parallel to the wave direction. Perpendicular is a transverse wave, and a single disturbance is a pulse."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kompressie","en":"Compression"},"r":{"af":"Gebied waar die deeltjies die naaste aan mekaar is","en":"Region where the particles are closest together"}},{"l":{"af":"Verdunning","en":"Rarefaction"},"r":{"af":"Gebied waar die deeltjies die verste van mekaar is","en":"Region where the particles are furthest apart"}},{"l":{"af":"Toonhoogte","en":"Pitch"},"r":{"af":"Word deur die frekwensie bepaal","en":"Determined by the frequency"}},{"l":{"af":"Luidheid","en":"Loudness"},"r":{"af":"Word deur die amplitude bepaal","en":"Determined by the amplitude"}},{"l":{"af":"Ultraklank","en":"Ultrasound"},"r":{"af":"Klank met 'n frekwensie hoër as 20 kHz","en":"Sound with a frequency higher than 20 kHz"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kompressie = deeltjies dig op mekaar (hoë druk); verdunning = deeltjies ver uitmekaar (lae druk). Toonhoogte hang van frekwensie af, luidheid van amplitude, en ultraklank is bo 20 kHz.","en":"Compression = particles packed closely (high pressure); rarefaction = particles far apart (low pressure). Pitch depends on frequency, loudness on amplitude, and ultrasound is above 20 kHz."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Klank kan deur 'n vakuum beweeg.","en":"Sound can travel through a vacuum."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Klank is 'n meganiese golf: dit het deeltjies ('n medium) nodig om die vibrasie oor te dra. In 'n vakuum is daar geen deeltjies nie.","en":"False. Sound is a mechanical wave: it needs particles (a medium) to pass on the vibration. In a vacuum there are no particles."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter medium beweeg klank die vinnigste?","en":"In which medium does sound travel fastest?"},"options":[{"af":"Vakuum","en":"Vacuum"},{"af":"Lug","en":"Air"},{"af":"Water","en":"Water"},{"af":"Staal","en":"Steel"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Klank beweeg die vinnigste in vastestowwe (staal ± 5 000 m·s⁻¹), stadiger in vloeistowwe (water ± 1 500 m·s⁻¹) en die stadigste in gasse (lug ± 340 m·s⁻¹). In 'n vakuum beweeg klank glad nie.","en":"Sound travels fastest in solids (steel ± 5 000 m·s⁻¹), slower in liquids (water ± 1 500 m·s⁻¹) and slowest in gases (air ± 340 m·s⁻¹). In a vacuum sound does not travel at all."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die boonste grens van die menslike gehoorgebied is ongeveer ___ Hz.","en":"The upper limit of the human hearing range is about ___ Hz."},"answers":{"af":["20 000","20000","20 000 Hz","20000 Hz","20 kHz"],"en":["20 000","20000","20 000 Hz","20000 Hz","20 kHz"]},"explain":{"af":"Mense hoor van ongeveer 20 Hz tot 20 000 Hz (20 kHz). Klank bo 20 kHz is ultraklank.","en":"Humans hear from about 20 Hz to 20 000 Hz (20 kHz). Sound above 20 kHz is ultrasound."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Hoe hoër die frekwensie van 'n klank, hoe hoër is die toonhoogte.","en":"The higher the frequency of a sound, the higher the pitch."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Toonhoogte word deur frekwensie bepaal: 'n taxi se skril toeter het 'n hoër frekwensie as 'n vragmotor se diep toeter.","en":"True. Pitch is determined by frequency: a taxi's shrill hooter has a higher frequency than a truck's deep hooter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder speel dieselfde noot harder op 'n kitaar. Wat verander aan die klankgolf?","en":"A learner plays the same note louder on a guitar. What changes in the sound wave?"},"options":[{"af":"Die frekwensie neem toe","en":"The frequency increases"},{"af":"Die amplitude neem toe, en die frekwensie bly dieselfde","en":"The amplitude increases, and the frequency stays the same"},{"af":"Die golflengte neem af","en":"The wavelength decreases"},{"af":"Die spoed van die klank in die lug neem toe","en":"The speed of the sound in the air increases"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Harder beteken 'n groter amplitude. Dit is dieselfde noot, dus bly die frekwensie (toonhoogte) dieselfde. Die spoed hang van die medium af, en met dieselfde v en f bly λ ook dieselfde.","en":"Louder means a bigger amplitude. It is the same note, so the frequency (pitch) stays the same. The speed depends on the medium, and with the same v and f, λ also stays the same."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Klank met 'n frekwensie van 680 Hz beweeg teen 340 m·s⁻¹ deur lug. Die golflengte is ___ m.","en":"A sound with a frequency of 680 Hz travels through air at 340 m·s⁻¹. The wavelength is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["0,5","0.5","0,50","0.50","0,5 m","0.5 m","50 cm"],"en":["0.5","0,5","0.50","0,50","0.5 m","0,5 m","50 cm"]},"explain":{"af":"λ = v/f = 340 ÷ 680 = 0,5 m.","en":"λ = v/f = 340 ÷ 680 = 0.5 m."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Jy skree voor 'n krans en hoor die eggo 2 s later. Die spoed van klank is 340 m·s⁻¹. Die krans is ___ m van jou af.","en":"You shout in front of a cliff and hear the echo 2 s later. The speed of sound is 340 m·s⁻¹. The cliff is ___ m away from you."},"answers":{"af":["340","340 m"],"en":["340","340 m"]},"explain":{"af":"afstand = v × t ÷ 2 = 340 × 2 ÷ 2 = 340 m. As jy vergeet om deur 2 te deel, kry jy 680 m: dit is die heen-en-terug-afstand.","en":"distance = v × t ÷ 2 = 340 × 2 ÷ 2 = 340 m. If you forget to divide by 2, you get 680 m: that is the round-trip distance."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die afstand van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie op 'n slinky is 1,2 m. Wat is die golflengte?","en":"The distance from the 1st to the 5th compression on a slinky is 1.2 m. What is the wavelength?"},"options":[{"af":"1,20 m","en":"1.20 m"},{"af":"0,60 m","en":"0.60 m"},{"af":"0,30 m","en":"0.30 m"},{"af":"0,24 m","en":"0.24 m"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie is daar 4 gapings, dus 4λ = 1,2 m en λ = 1,2 ÷ 4 = 0,30 m. 0,24 m kry jy as jy deur 5 deel (die kompressies tel in plaas van die gapings).","en":"From the 1st to the 5th compression there are 4 gaps, so 4λ = 1.2 m and λ = 1.2 ÷ 4 = 0.30 m. You get 0.24 m if you divide by 5 (counting the compressions instead of the gaps)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Dolfyn stuur ultraklank met 'n frekwensie van 150 kHz uit. Die spoed van klank in water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Die golflengte is ___ m.","en":"A dolphin sends out ultrasound with a frequency of 150 kHz. The speed of sound in water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. The wavelength is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["0,01","0.01","0,01 m","0.01 m","1 cm","1 × 10⁻²"],"en":["0.01","0,01","0.01 m","0,01 m","1 cm","1 × 10⁻²"]},"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers om: 150 kHz = 150 000 Hz. λ = v/f = 1 500 ÷ 150 000 = 0,01 m (1 cm). As jy vergeet om om te skakel, kry jy 10 m.","en":"First convert: 150 kHz = 150 000 Hz. λ = v/f = 1 500 ÷ 150 000 = 0.01 m (1 cm). If you forget to convert, you get 10 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Skip stuur 'n sonarpuls na die seebodem en ontvang die eggo 1,2 s later. Die spoed van klank in seewater is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Hoe diep is die see?","en":"A ship sends a sonar pulse to the sea floor and receives the echo 1.2 s later. The speed of sound in sea water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. How deep is the sea?"},"options":[{"af":"1 800 m","en":"1 800 m"},{"af":"900 m","en":"900 m"},{"af":"1 250 m","en":"1 250 m"},{"af":"450 m","en":"450 m"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"diepte = v × t ÷ 2 = 1 500 × 1,2 ÷ 2 = 900 m. 1 800 m is die heen-en-terug-afstand (vergeet om deur 2 te deel), en 1 250 m kom van v ÷ t.","en":"depth = v × t ÷ 2 = 1 500 × 1.2 ÷ 2 = 900 m. 1 800 m is the round-trip distance (forgetting to divide by 2), and 1 250 m comes from v ÷ t."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom beweeg klank vinniger deur staal as deur lug?","en":"Why does sound travel faster through steel than through air?"},"options":[{"af":"Die deeltjies in staal is nader aan mekaar en sterker aan mekaar gebind, dus word die vibrasie vinniger oorgedra","en":"The particles in steel are closer together and more strongly bonded, so the vibration is passed on faster"},{"af":"Klank is 'n transversale golf in staal, en transversale golwe is altyd vinniger","en":"Sound is a transverse wave in steel, and transverse waves are always faster"},{"af":"Klank kry 'n hoër frekwensie in staal, en 'n hoër frekwensie beteken 'n hoër spoed","en":"Sound gets a higher frequency in steel, and a higher frequency means a higher speed"},{"af":"Staal het minder deeltjies wat die klank in die pad staan","en":"Steel has fewer particles that get in the way of the sound"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Klank word van deeltjie na deeltjie oorgedra. In 'n vastestof is die deeltjies dig op mekaar en sterk gebind, dus beweeg die vibrasie vinnig. Klank bly longitudinaal, die frekwensie word deur die bron bepaal, en staal het juis méér deeltjies per volume as lug.","en":"Sound is passed on from particle to particle. In a solid the particles are packed closely and strongly bonded, so the vibration travels quickly. Sound stays longitudinal, the frequency is set by the source, and steel actually has more particles per volume than air."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder sê: \"Ultraklank is veiliger as X-strale vir 'n skandering van 'n ongebore baba, want ultraklank het 'n baie hoër frekwensie as X-strale.\" Watter evaluering is korrek?","en":"A learner says: \"Ultrasound is safer than X-rays for a scan of an unborn baby, because ultrasound has a much higher frequency than X-rays.\" Which evaluation is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Heeltemal korrek: die gevolgtrekking en die rede is albei reg","en":"Completely correct: the conclusion and the reason are both right"},{"af":"Heeltemal verkeerd: ultraklank is ook ioniserende straling en net so gevaarlik soos X-strale","en":"Completely wrong: ultrasound is also ionising radiation and just as dangerous as X-rays"},{"af":"Verkeerd: ultraklank kan nie deur die liggaam beweeg nie, so dit word nie vir skanderings gebruik nie","en":"Wrong: ultrasound cannot travel through the body, so it is not used for scans"},{"af":"Die gevolgtrekking is reg, maar die rede is verkeerd: ultraklank is 'n meganiese golf wat nie ioniserend is nie, terwyl X-strale ioniserende elektromagnetiese straling met 'n baie hoër frekwensie is","en":"The conclusion is right, but the reason is wrong: ultrasound is a mechanical wave that is not ionising, whereas X-rays are ionising electromagnetic radiation with a much higher frequency"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ultraklank word wel vir babaskanderings gebruik omdat dit veilig is, maar nie oor sy frekwensie nie. Dit is klank ('n meganiese golf, frekwensie net bo 20 kHz) en ioniseer nie. X-strale is elektromagnetiese straling met 'n veel hoër frekwensie wat selle kan beskadig.","en":"Ultrasound is indeed used for baby scans because it is safe, but not because of its frequency. It is sound (a mechanical wave, frequency just above 20 kHz) and does not ionise. X-rays are electromagnetic radiation with a much higher frequency that can damage cells."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-em-straling","title":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese straling","en":"Electromagnetic radiation"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die EM-spektrum in volgorde kan rangskik, gebruike en gevare kan noem, en met c = fλ en E = hf kan reken.","en":"You will be able to arrange the EM spectrum in order, name uses and dangers, and calculate with c = fλ and E = hf."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is elektromagnetiese straling?\n\n**Elektromagnetiese (EM) straling** is energie wat as golwe deur die ruimte beweeg. 'n EM-golf ontstaan wanneer 'n **gelaaide deeltjie versnel**. Die versnellende lading skep 'n ossillerende **elektriese veld**, wat 'n ossillerende **magneetveld** loodreg daarop opwek, wat weer 'n elektriese veld opwek, ensovoorts. Hierdie **wedersyds regenererende velde** is loodreg op mekaar én loodreg op die bewegingsrigting, daarom is EM-golwe **transversale golwe**.\n\n- EM-golwe het **geen medium** nodig nie: sonlig bereik ons deur die vakuum van die ruimte. (Klank kan nie deur 'n vakuum beweeg nie.)\n- Alle EM-golwe beweeg in 'n vakuum teen dieselfde spoed, die **spoed van lig**: c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. In lug is die spoed feitlik dieselfde.\n\n## Golf-deeltjie-dualiteit\n\nEM-straling het 'n **dubbele aard**. Sommige eienskappe word die beste met 'n **golfmodel** verklaar (bv. interferensie en diffraksie), ander die beste met 'n **deeltjiemodel** (bv. die foto-elektriese effek, waar lig elektrone uit 'n metaaloppervlak slaan). Die \"deeltjies\" van EM-straling heet **fotone**.\n\n> **Definisie:** 'n **Foton** is 'n kwantum (pakkie) energie.\n\n## Die EM-spektrum\n\nDie tipes is hier gerangskik van **lae frekwensie, lang golflengte en lae energie** (bo) na **hoë frekwensie, kort golflengte en hoë energie** (onder):\n\n| Tipe | Gebruike | Gevare |\n|---|---|---|\n| Radiogolwe | radio- en TV-uitsendings, tweerigtingradio's | geen bekende gevaar by normale vlakke |\n| Mikrogolwe | mikrogolfoonde, selfone, wi-fi, radar (spoedlokvalle), satelliet-TV | sterk bundels verhit liggaamsweefsel |\n| Infrarooi (IR) | TV-afstandbeheerders, nagsig- en hittekameras, hittelampe | brandwonde by hoë intensiteit |\n| Sigbare lig | sien, fotografie | baie helder lig (bv. die son) beskadig die oë |\n| Ultraviolet (UV) | sterilisering van water en toerusting, opsporing van vals banknote, vitamien D in die vel | sonbrand, velkanker, oogskade (katarakte) |\n| X-strale | beelde van bene, skandering van bagasie by lughawens | beskadig selle en DNS; kanker |\n| Gammastrale | radioterapie (kankerselle doodmaak), sterilisering van mediese toerusting en voedsel | die gevaarlikste: ernstige sel- en DNS-skade, kanker |\n\n**Sigbare lig** strek van ongeveer 700 nm (**rooi**, laagste energie) tot 400 nm (**violet**, hoogste energie): rooi, oranje, geel, groen, blou, indigo, violet.\n\n> **Wenk:** Leer die volgorde radio → mikro → infrarooi → sigbaar → UV → X → gamma uit jou kop. Vrae vra dikwels om 'n lys in volgorde van toenemende frekwensie of afnemende golflengte te rangskik (dit is dieselfde volgorde).\n\n## Formules\n\n**Golfvergelyking:** c = fλ\n- c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}; f in hertz (Hz); λ in meter (m).\n\n**Energie van 'n foton:** E = hf = [[hc/λ]]\n- E in joule (J); h = 6,63 × 10^{−34} J·s (Planck se konstante).\n- E is **direk eweredig** aan f: dubbel die frekwensie → dubbel die energie per foton.\n- E is **omgekeerd eweredig** aan λ: halveer die golflengte → dubbel die energie.\n\n| Eenheid | Omskakeling |\n|---|---|\n| 1 nm (nanometer) | 1 × 10^{−9} m |\n| 1 kHz | 1 × 10^{3} Hz |\n| 1 MHz | 1 × 10^{6} Hz |\n| 1 GHz | 1 × 10^{9} Hz |\n\n### Stappe vir 'n berekening\n1. Skryf die gegewe waardes neer en skakel om na SI-eenhede (nm → m, MHz → Hz).\n2. Skryf die formule neer.\n3. Vervang die waardes.\n4. Bereken en skryf die antwoord met die eenheid, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke (bv. 3,98 × 10^{−19} J).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om nm nie na m om te skakel nie, of om 340 m·s^{−1} (die spoed van klank) vir lig te gebruik. EM-golwe beweeg altyd teen c in 'n vakuum.\n\n## Deurdringingsvermoë en gevaar\n\nHoe **hoër die frekwensie**, hoe **meer energie** dra elke foton, en hoe **groter is die deurdringingsvermoë** van die straling. Neem die menslike liggaam as voorbeeld: dit straal infrarooi uit, dit weerkaats sigbare lig, UV dring net die vel binne, X-strale gaan deur sagte weefsel maar word deur bene geabsorbeer, en gammastrale gaan dwarsdeur; net dik lood of beton keer gammastrale effektief.\n\nDie fotone van **X-strale en gammastrale** (en hoë-energie UV) het genoeg energie om elektrone uit atome te slaan (**ioniserende straling**). **UV, X-strale en gammastrale** kan DNS beskadig, wat mutasies en **kanker** kan veroorsaak. Daarom:\n- smeer sonskerm en dra 'n hoed: Suid-Afrika, ook die Hoëveld rondom Brits, het baie hoë UV-vlakke;\n- staan 'n radiograaf agter 'n loodskerm en dra pasiënte 'n loodvoorskoot.\n\nSelfone (mikrogolwe) en kraglyne (baie lae frekwensie) straal lae-energie straling uit wat nie ioniserend is nie. Daar is geen duidelike bewys dat dit by normale gebruik skadelik is nie, maar navorsing gaan voort.\n\n> **Onthou!** 'n **Helderder** lig stuur **meer fotone** uit, nie fotone met meer energie nie. Die energie van **elke foton** hang net van f (of λ) af. Daarom kan swak UV jou vel verbrand, maar 'n helder rooi lamp nie.","en":"## What is electromagnetic radiation?\n\n**Electromagnetic (EM) radiation** is energy that travels through space as waves. An EM wave is produced when a **charged particle accelerates**. The accelerating charge creates an oscillating **electric field**, which generates an oscillating **magnetic field** perpendicular to it, which in turn generates an electric field, and so on. These **mutually regenerating fields** are perpendicular to each other and perpendicular to the direction of motion, so EM waves are **transverse waves**.\n\n- EM waves need **no medium**: sunlight reaches us through the vacuum of space. (Sound cannot travel through a vacuum.)\n- All EM waves travel at the same speed in a vacuum, the **speed of light**: c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. In air the speed is practically the same.\n\n## Wave–particle duality\n\nEM radiation has a **dual nature**. Some properties are best explained with a **wave model** (e.g. interference and diffraction), others best with a **particle model** (e.g. the photoelectric effect, where light knocks electrons out of a metal surface). The \"particles\" of EM radiation are called **photons**.\n\n> **Definition:** A **photon** is a quantum (packet) of energy.\n\n## The EM spectrum\n\nThe types are arranged here from **low frequency, long wavelength and low energy** (top) to **high frequency, short wavelength and high energy** (bottom):\n\n| Type | Uses | Dangers |\n|---|---|---|\n| Radio waves | radio and TV broadcasts, two-way radios | no known danger at normal levels |\n| Microwaves | microwave ovens, cellphones, wi-fi, radar (speed traps), satellite TV | strong beams heat body tissue |\n| Infrared (IR) | TV remote controls, night-vision and thermal cameras, heat lamps | burns at high intensity |\n| Visible light | seeing, photography | very bright light (e.g. the sun) damages the eyes |\n| Ultraviolet (UV) | sterilising water and equipment, detecting fake banknotes, vitamin D in the skin | sunburn, skin cancer, eye damage (cataracts) |\n| X-rays | images of bones, scanning luggage at airports | damage cells and DNA; cancer |\n| Gamma rays | radiotherapy (killing cancer cells), sterilising medical equipment and food | the most dangerous: serious cell and DNA damage, cancer |\n\n**Visible light** ranges from about 700 nm (**red**, lowest energy) to 400 nm (**violet**, highest energy): red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet.\n\n> **Tip:** Learn the order radio → micro → infrared → visible → UV → X → gamma by heart. Questions often ask you to arrange a list in order of increasing frequency or decreasing wavelength (that is the same order).\n\n## Formulae\n\n**Wave equation:** c = fλ\n- c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}; f in hertz (Hz); λ in metres (m).\n\n**Energy of a photon:** E = hf = [[hc/λ]]\n- E in joules (J); h = 6.63 × 10^{−34} J·s (Planck's constant).\n- E is **directly proportional** to f: double the frequency → double the energy per photon.\n- E is **inversely proportional** to λ: halve the wavelength → double the energy.\n\n| Unit | Conversion |\n|---|---|\n| 1 nm (nanometre) | 1 × 10^{−9} m |\n| 1 kHz | 1 × 10^{3} Hz |\n| 1 MHz | 1 × 10^{6} Hz |\n| 1 GHz | 1 × 10^{9} Hz |\n\n### Steps for a calculation\n1. Write down the given values and convert to SI units (nm → m, MHz → Hz).\n2. Write down the formula.\n3. Substitute the values.\n4. Calculate and write the answer with its unit, rounded to two decimal places (e.g. 3.98 × 10^{−19} J).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Not converting nm to m, or using 340 m·s^{−1} (the speed of sound) for light. EM waves always travel at c in a vacuum.\n\n## Penetrating ability and danger\n\nThe **higher the frequency**, the **more energy** each photon carries, and the **greater the penetrating ability** of the radiation. Take the human body as an example: it emits infrared, it reflects visible light, UV only penetrates the skin, X-rays pass through soft tissue but are absorbed by bones, and gamma rays go right through; only thick lead or concrete stops gamma rays effectively.\n\nThe photons of **X-rays and gamma rays** (and high-energy UV) have enough energy to knock electrons out of atoms (**ionising radiation**). **UV, X-rays and gamma rays** can damage DNA, which can cause mutations and **cancer**. That is why:\n- you wear sunscreen and a hat: South Africa, including the Highveld around Brits, has very high UV levels;\n- a radiographer stands behind a lead screen and patients wear a lead apron.\n\nCellphones (microwaves) and power lines (very low frequency) emit low-energy radiation that is not ionising. There is no clear proof that it is harmful during normal use, but research continues.\n\n> **Remember!** A **brighter** light sends out **more photons**, not photons with more energy. The energy of **each photon** depends only on f (or λ). That is why weak UV can burn your skin, but a bright red lamp cannot."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese straling","en":"Electromagnetic radiation"},"def":{"af":"Energie wat as transversale golwe van wedersyds regenererende, loodregte elektriese en magnetiese velde teen die spoed van lig deur die ruimte beweeg; dit word deur versnellende ladings veroorsaak.","en":"Energy that travels through space at the speed of light as transverse waves of mutually regenerating, perpendicular electric and magnetic fields; it is caused by accelerating charges."}},{"term":{"af":"Foton","en":"Photon"},"def":{"af":"'n Kwantum (pakkie) energie.","en":"A quantum (packet) of energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Golf-deeltjie-dualiteit","en":"Wave–particle duality"},"def":{"af":"EM-straling gedra soms soos 'n golf (bv. interferensie) en soms soos 'n stroom deeltjies, fotone (bv. die foto-elektriese effek).","en":"EM radiation sometimes behaves like a wave (e.g. interference) and sometimes like a stream of particles, photons (e.g. the photoelectric effect)."}},{"term":{"af":"Golflengte (λ)","en":"Wavelength (λ)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase, bv. twee opeenvolgende kruine. Eenheid: meter (m).","en":"The distance between two successive points in phase, e.g. two successive crests. Unit: metre (m)."}},{"term":{"af":"Frekwensie (f)","en":"Frequency (f)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal golwe wat per sekonde by 'n punt verbygaan. Eenheid: hertz (Hz).","en":"The number of waves that pass a point per second. Unit: hertz (Hz)."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese spektrum","en":"Electromagnetic spectrum"},"def":{"af":"Al die tipes EM-straling gerangskik volgens frekwensie of golflengte: radiogolwe, mikrogolwe, infrarooi, sigbare lig, UV, X-strale, gammastrale.","en":"All the types of EM radiation arranged according to frequency or wavelength: radio waves, microwaves, infrared, visible light, UV, X-rays, gamma rays."}},{"term":{"af":"Planck se konstante (h)","en":"Planck's constant (h)"},"def":{"af":"Die konstante h = 6,63 × 10⁻³⁴ J·s wat die energie van 'n foton aan sy frekwensie koppel: E = hf.","en":"The constant h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J·s that links the energy of a photon to its frequency: E = hf."}},{"term":{"af":"Deurdringingsvermoë","en":"Penetrating ability"},"def":{"af":"Hoe goed straling deur materiale kan beweeg; dit neem toe soos die frekwensie (en dus die energie per foton) toeneem.","en":"How well radiation can pass through materials; it increases as the frequency (and therefore the energy per photon) increases."}},{"term":{"af":"Ioniserende straling","en":"Ionising radiation"},"def":{"af":"Straling waarvan die fotone genoeg energie het om elektrone uit atome te slaan, bv. X-strale en gammastrale; dit kan selle en DNS beskadig.","en":"Radiation whose photons have enough energy to knock electrons out of atoms, e.g. X-rays and gamma rays; it can damage cells and DNA."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Frekwensie van 'n afstandbeheerder","en":"Frequency of a remote control"},"problem":{"af":"'n TV-afstandbeheerder stuur infrarooistraling met 'n golflengte van 940 nm uit. Bereken die frekwensie van die straling.","en":"A TV remote control emits infrared radiation with a wavelength of 940 nm. Calculate the frequency of the radiation."},"steps":[{"af":"Gegee: λ = 940 nm = 940 × 10^{−9} m = 9,4 × 10^{−7} m en c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. Skakel altyd eers nm na m om.","en":"Given: λ = 940 nm = 940 × 10^{−9} m = 9.4 × 10^{−7} m and c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. Always convert nm to m first."},{"af":"Formule: c = fλ, dus f = [[c/λ]]","en":"Formula: c = fλ, so f = [[c/λ]]"},{"af":"Vervang: f = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (9,4 × 10^{−7})","en":"Substitute: f = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (9.4 × 10^{−7})"},{"af":"f = 3,19 × 10^{14} Hz","en":"f = 3.19 × 10^{14} Hz"}],"answer":{"af":"f = 3,19 × 10¹⁴ Hz","en":"f = 3.19 × 10¹⁴ Hz"}},{"title":{"af":"Frekwensie en energie van 'n X-straalfoton","en":"Frequency and energy of an X-ray photon"},"problem":{"af":"'n Bundel X-strale het 'n golflengte van 1 × 10⁻¹⁰ m. Bereken (a) die frekwensie en (b) die energie van een X-straalfoton.","en":"A beam of X-rays has a wavelength of 1 × 10⁻¹⁰ m. Calculate (a) the frequency and (b) the energy of one X-ray photon."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) c = fλ, dus f = [[c/λ]] = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10})","en":"(a) c = fλ, so f = [[c/λ]] = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10})"},{"af":"f = 3 × 10^{18} Hz","en":"f = 3 × 10^{18} Hz"},{"af":"(b) E = hf = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{18})","en":"(b) E = hf = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{18})"},{"af":"E = 1,99 × 10^{−15} J. Kontrole met E = [[hc/λ]] = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10}) = 1,99 × 10^{−15} J ✔","en":"E = 1.99 × 10^{−15} J. Check with E = [[hc/λ]] = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10}) = 1.99 × 10^{−15} J ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) f = 3 × 10¹⁸ Hz  (b) E = 1,99 × 10⁻¹⁵ J","en":"(a) f = 3 × 10¹⁸ Hz  (b) E = 1.99 × 10⁻¹⁵ J"}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom UV jou vel verbrand, maar rooi lig nie","en":"Why UV burns your skin but red light does not"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken die energie van (a) 'n UV-foton met λ = 300 nm en (b) 'n rooi foton met λ = 700 nm. (c) Hoeveel keer meer energie het die UV-foton? (d) Verduidelik waarom jy op 'n somersdag by Hartbeespoortdam sonbrand kry, maar nie langs 'n helder rooi lamp nie.","en":"Calculate the energy of (a) a UV photon with λ = 300 nm and (b) a red photon with λ = 700 nm. (c) How many times more energy does the UV photon have? (d) Explain why you get sunburnt on a summer's day at Hartbeespoort Dam, but not next to a bright red lamp."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) E = [[hc/λ]] = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (300 × 10^{−9}) = 6,63 × 10^{−19} J","en":"(a) E = [[hc/λ]] = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (300 × 10^{−9}) = 6.63 × 10^{−19} J"},{"af":"(b) E = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (700 × 10^{−9}) = 2,84 × 10^{−19} J","en":"(b) E = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (700 × 10^{−9}) = 2.84 × 10^{−19} J"},{"af":"(c) E is omgekeerd eweredig aan λ: 700 ÷ 300 = 2,33. Die UV-foton het 2,33 keer soveel energie.","en":"(c) E is inversely proportional to λ: 700 ÷ 300 = 2.33. The UV photon has 2.33 times as much energy."},{"af":"(d) Skade aan velselle hang af van die energie van elke foton, nie van hoe helder die lig is nie. Elke UV-foton het genoeg energie om die DNS in velselle te beskadig (sonbrand, velkanker). 'n Helder rooi lamp stuur net meer fotone uit, maar elkeen het te min energie om selle te beskadig.","en":"(d) Damage to skin cells depends on the energy of each photon, not on how bright the light is. Each UV photon has enough energy to damage the DNA in skin cells (sunburn, skin cancer). A bright red lamp only sends out more photons, but each one has too little energy to damage cells."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 6,63 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (b) 2,84 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (c) 2,33 keer  (d) elke UV-foton het genoeg energie om selle te beskadig; helderheid verander net die aantal fotone.","en":"(a) 6.63 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (b) 2.84 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (c) 2.33 times  (d) each UV photon has enough energy to damage cells; brightness only changes the number of photons."}},{"title":{"af":"Rangskik en verduidelik: die radiograaf se loodskerm","en":"Arrange and explain: the radiographer's lead screen"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Rangskik die volgende in volgorde van toenemende frekwensie: X-strale, mikrogolwe, gammastrale, sigbare lig. (b) Verduidelik waarom 'n radiograaf agter 'n loodskerm staan terwyl sy 'n X-straalfoto neem, al word die pasiënt self aan die X-strale blootgestel.","en":"(a) Arrange the following in order of increasing frequency: X-rays, microwaves, gamma rays, visible light. (b) Explain why a radiographer stands behind a lead screen while she takes an X-ray, even though the patient is exposed to the X-rays."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Van lae na hoë frekwensie: mikrogolwe → sigbare lig → X-strale → gammastrale.","en":"(a) From low to high frequency: microwaves → visible light → X-rays → gamma rays."},{"af":"(b) X-strale het 'n hoë frekwensie, dus volgens E = hf 'n hoë energie per foton en 'n groot deurdringingsvermoë: hulle gaan deur sagte weefsel en kan selle en DNS beskadig (ioniserende straling).","en":"(b) X-rays have a high frequency, so according to E = hf a high energy per photon and a great penetrating ability: they pass through soft tissue and can damage cells and DNA (ionising radiation)."},{"af":"Lood is baie dig en absorbeer X-strale. Die radiograaf neem elke dag baie foto's, so sonder 'n skerm sou haar blootstelling opbou en die risiko vir kanker verhoog.","en":"Lead is very dense and absorbs X-rays. The radiographer takes many X-rays every day, so without a screen her exposure would build up and increase the risk of cancer."},{"af":"Die pasiënt kry net een klein dosis; die voordeel (bv. om 'n gebreekte been te sien) is groter as die klein risiko.","en":"The patient only gets one small dose; the benefit (e.g. seeing a broken bone) is greater than the small risk."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) mikrogolwe, sigbare lig, X-strale, gammastrale. (b) X-strale is hoë-energie, deurdringende, ioniserende straling; lood absorbeer dit en beskerm die radiograaf teen herhaalde blootstelling.","en":"(a) microwaves, visible light, X-rays, gamma rays. (b) X-rays are high-energy, penetrating, ionising radiation; lead absorbs them and protects the radiographer from repeated exposure."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter tipe elektromagnetiese straling het die langste golflengte?","en":"Which type of electromagnetic radiation has the longest wavelength?"},"options":[{"af":"Gammastrale","en":"Gamma rays"},{"af":"Ultravioletstraling","en":"Ultraviolet radiation"},{"af":"Radiogolwe","en":"Radio waves"},{"af":"X-strale","en":"X-rays"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Van lang na kort golflengte: radio → mikro → infrarooi → sigbaar → UV → X → gamma. Radiogolwe het die langste golflengte, en dus die laagste frekwensie en energie; gammastrale het die kortste.","en":"From long to short wavelength: radio → micro → infrared → visible → UV → X → gamma. Radio waves have the longest wavelength, and therefore the lowest frequency and energy; gamma rays have the shortest."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Alle tipes elektromagnetiese straling beweeg in 'n vakuum teen dieselfde spoed, 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹.","en":"All types of electromagnetic radiation travel at the same speed in a vacuum, 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Radiogolwe en gammastrale verskil in frekwensie en golflengte, maar in 'n vakuum beweeg alle EM-golwe teen c = 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹. Daarom kan jy c = fλ vir enige tipe gebruik.","en":"True. Radio waves and gamma rays differ in frequency and wavelength, but in a vacuum all EM waves travel at c = 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹. That is why you can use c = fλ for any type."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n foton?","en":"What is a photon?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Negatief gelaaide deeltjie wat om die kern van 'n atoom beweeg","en":"A negatively charged particle that moves around the nucleus of an atom"},{"af":"'n Kwantum (pakkie) energie","en":"A quantum (packet) of energy"},{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende kruine van 'n golf","en":"The distance between two successive crests of a wave"},{"af":"'n Gebied waar die deeltjies van 'n medium saamgedruk is","en":"A region where the particles of a medium are pressed together"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Foton is 'n kwantum (pakkie) energie: die 'deeltjie' van EM-straling. Die ander opsies beskryf 'n elektron, golflengte en 'n kompressie.","en":"A photon is a quantum (packet) of energy: the 'particle' of EM radiation. The other options describe an electron, wavelength and a compression."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke tipe EM-straling by 'n gebruik daarvan.","en":"Match each type of EM radiation to one of its uses."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Radiogolwe","en":"Radio waves"},"r":{"af":"Radio- en TV-uitsendings","en":"Radio and TV broadcasts"}},{"l":{"af":"Mikrogolwe","en":"Microwaves"},"r":{"af":"Selfoonseine en radar","en":"Cellphone signals and radar"}},{"l":{"af":"Infrarooi","en":"Infrared"},"r":{"af":"TV-afstandbeheerders en nagsigkameras","en":"TV remote controls and night-vision cameras"}},{"l":{"af":"X-strale","en":"X-rays"},"r":{"af":"'n Beeld van 'n gebreekte arm","en":"An image of a broken arm"}},{"l":{"af":"Gammastrale","en":"Gamma rays"},"r":{"af":"Kankerselle doodmaak (radioterapie)","en":"Killing cancer cells (radiotherapy)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Radio en TV gebruik radiogolwe; selfone en radar gebruik mikrogolwe; afstandbeheerders en nagsigkameras gebruik infrarooi; X-strale gaan deur sagte weefsel maar word deur been geabsorbeer; gammastrale het genoeg energie om kankerselle dood te maak.","en":"Radio and TV use radio waves; cellphones and radar use microwaves; remote controls and night-vision cameras use infrared; X-rays pass through soft tissue but are absorbed by bone; gamma rays have enough energy to kill cancer cells."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling beskryf 'n elektromagnetiese golf korrek?","en":"Which statement describes an electromagnetic wave correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is 'n longitudinale golf wat 'n medium soos lug nodig het.","en":"It is a longitudinal wave that needs a medium such as air."},{"af":"Dit bestaan uit 'n elektriese veld en 'n magneetveld wat ewewydig aan die bewegingsrigting ossilleer.","en":"It consists of an electric field and a magnetic field that oscillate parallel to the direction of motion."},{"af":"Dit bestaan net uit 'n ossillerende elektriese veld; die magneetveld bly konstant.","en":"It consists only of an oscillating electric field; the magnetic field stays constant."},{"af":"Dit bestaan uit 'n elektriese veld en 'n magneetveld wat loodreg op mekaar en op die bewegingsrigting ossilleer en mekaar wedersyds opwek.","en":"It consists of an electric field and a magnetic field that oscillate perpendicular to each other and to the direction of motion and mutually regenerate each other."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n EM-golf is 'n transversale golf: die ossillerende elektriese en magnetiese velde wek mekaar op, staan loodreg op mekaar en loodreg op die bewegingsrigting, en het geen medium nodig nie. 'n Longitudinale golf met 'n medium beskryf klank.","en":"An EM wave is a transverse wave: the oscillating electric and magnetic fields generate each other, are perpendicular to each other and to the direction of motion, and need no medium. A longitudinal wave with a medium describes sound."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese golwe het, net soos klank, 'n medium nodig om deur te beweeg.","en":"Electromagnetic waves, just like sound, need a medium to travel through."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. EM-golwe kan deur 'n vakuum beweeg: sonlig bereik die aarde deur die leë ruimte. Klank is 'n meganiese golf en het wel 'n medium nodig.","en":"False. EM waves can travel through a vacuum: sunlight reaches Earth through empty space. Sound is a mechanical wave and does need a medium."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is X-strale en gammastrale baie gevaarliker vir mense as radiogolwe?","en":"Why are X-rays and gamma rays much more dangerous to people than radio waves?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle het 'n hoër frekwensie, dus dra elke foton meer energie en kan dit selle en DNS beskadig.","en":"They have a higher frequency, so each photon carries more energy and can damage cells and DNA."},{"af":"Hulle beweeg vinniger as radiogolwe en tref die liggaam dus harder.","en":"They travel faster than radio waves and therefore hit the body harder."},{"af":"Hulle het 'n langer golflengte, dus dra elke foton meer energie.","en":"They have a longer wavelength, so each photon carries more energy."},{"af":"Hulle het altyd 'n groter amplitude as radiogolwe.","en":"They always have a larger amplitude than radio waves."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"E = hf: hoë frekwensie beteken hoë energie per foton en groot deurdringingsvermoë. Alle EM-golwe beweeg teen dieselfde spoed c, en X- en gammastrale het 'n KORTER golflengte, nie 'n langer een nie.","en":"E = hf: high frequency means high energy per photon and great penetrating ability. All EM waves travel at the same speed c, and X-rays and gamma rays have a SHORTER wavelength, not a longer one."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Radiostasie saai uit teen 'n frekwensie van 94,2 MHz. Bereken die golflengte van die radiogolwe, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: λ = ___ m","en":"A radio station broadcasts at a frequency of 94.2 MHz. Calculate the wavelength of the radio waves, rounded to two decimal places: λ = ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["3,18","3,18 m","3.18","3.18 m"],"en":["3,18","3,18 m","3.18","3.18 m"]},"explain":{"af":"94,2 MHz = 94,2 × 10⁶ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (94,2 × 10⁶) = 3,18 m.","en":"94.2 MHz = 94.2 × 10⁶ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (94.2 × 10⁶) = 3.18 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Mikrogolfoond werk teen 'n frekwensie van 2,45 GHz. Wat is die golflengte van die mikrogolwe?","en":"A microwave oven works at a frequency of 2.45 GHz. What is the wavelength of the microwaves?"},"options":[{"af":"122,45 m","en":"122.45 m"},{"af":"7,35 × 10¹⁷ m","en":"7.35 × 10¹⁷ m"},{"af":"1,39 × 10⁻⁷ m","en":"1.39 × 10⁻⁷ m"},{"af":"0,12 m","en":"0.12 m"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"2,45 GHz = 2,45 × 10⁹ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (2,45 × 10⁹) = 0,12 m. Jy kry 122,45 m as jy giga as 10⁶ (mega) neem, 7,35 × 10¹⁷ m as jy c en f vermenigvuldig, en 1,39 × 10⁻⁷ m as jy die spoed van klank (340 m·s⁻¹) gebruik.","en":"2.45 GHz = 2.45 × 10⁹ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (2.45 × 10⁹) = 0.12 m. You get 122.45 m if you take giga as 10⁶ (mega), 7.35 × 10¹⁷ m if you multiply c and f, and 1.39 × 10⁻⁷ m if you use the speed of sound (340 m·s⁻¹)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken die energie van 'n foton groen lig met 'n golflengte van 500 nm. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke: E = ___ × 10⁻¹⁹ J","en":"Calculate the energy of a photon of green light with a wavelength of 500 nm. Round to two decimal places: E = ___ × 10⁻¹⁹ J"},"answers":{"af":["3,98","3.98","3,98 × 10⁻¹⁹","3,98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J","3,98 x 10^-19","3.98 x 10^-19","3.98e-19"],"en":["3,98","3.98","3.98 × 10⁻¹⁹","3.98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J","3,98 x 10^-19","3.98 x 10^-19","3.98e-19"]},"explain":{"af":"λ = 500 nm = 500 × 10⁻⁹ m = 5 × 10⁻⁷ m. E = hc/λ = (6,63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (5 × 10⁻⁷) = 3,98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J.","en":"λ = 500 nm = 500 × 10⁻⁹ m = 5 × 10⁻⁷ m. E = hc/λ = (6.63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (5 × 10⁻⁷) = 3.98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken die energie van 'n X-straalfoton met 'n frekwensie van 4 × 10¹⁸ Hz.","en":"Calculate the energy of an X-ray photon with a frequency of 4 × 10¹⁸ Hz."},"options":[{"af":"8,84 × 10⁻²⁴ J","en":"8.84 × 10⁻²⁴ J"},{"af":"2,65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J","en":"2.65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J"},{"af":"1,66 × 10⁻⁵² J","en":"1.66 × 10⁻⁵² J"},{"af":"7,96 × 10⁻⁷ J","en":"7.96 × 10⁻⁷ J"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"E = hf = (6,63 × 10⁻³⁴)(4 × 10¹⁸) = 2,65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J. As f gegee is, het jy c nie nodig nie: hf/c gee 8,84 × 10⁻²⁴ J, h/f gee 1,66 × 10⁻⁵² J en hcf gee 7,96 × 10⁻⁷ J.","en":"E = hf = (6.63 × 10⁻³⁴)(4 × 10¹⁸) = 2.65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J. When f is given you do not need c: hf/c gives 8.84 × 10⁻²⁴ J, h/f gives 1.66 × 10⁻⁵² J and hcf gives 7.96 × 10⁻⁷ J."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Foton het 'n energie van 3,315 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Bereken die golflengte van die lig in nanometer: λ = ___ nm","en":"A photon has an energy of 3.315 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Calculate the wavelength of the light in nanometres: λ = ___ nm"},"answers":{"af":["600","600 nm","600,00","600,00 nm","600.00","600.00 nm"],"en":["600","600 nm","600,00","600,00 nm","600.00","600.00 nm"]},"explain":{"af":"E = hc/λ, dus λ = hc/E = (6,63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (3,315 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6 × 10⁻⁷ m. Omskakeling: 6 × 10⁻⁷ m ÷ 10⁻⁹ = 600 nm (oranje lig).","en":"E = hc/λ, so λ = hc/E = (6.63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (3.315 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6 × 10⁻⁷ m. Conversion: 6 × 10⁻⁷ m ÷ 10⁻⁹ = 600 nm (orange light)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Foton A (UV) het 'n golflengte van 200 nm en foton B 'n golflengte van 600 nm. Hoeveel keer groter is die energie van foton A as dié van foton B? ___","en":"Photon A (UV) has a wavelength of 200 nm and photon B a wavelength of 600 nm. How many times greater is the energy of photon A than that of photon B? ___"},"answers":{"af":["3","3 keer","drie","drie keer","3x","3×"],"en":["3","3 times","three","three times","3x","3×"]},"explain":{"af":"E = hc/λ, dus is E omgekeerd eweredig aan λ. λ_B ÷ λ_A = 600 ÷ 200 = 3, dus het foton A 3 keer soveel energie as foton B. Jy hoef nie die energieë self uit te werk nie.","en":"E = hc/λ, so E is inversely proportional to λ. λ_B ÷ λ_A = 600 ÷ 200 = 3, so photon A has 3 times as much energy as photon B. You do not need to work out the energies themselves."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo sê: “'n Baie helder rooi lamp is gevaarliker vir jou vel as 'n swak UV-lamp, want die helder lig dra meer energie.” Watter stelling evalueer sy bewering die beste?","en":"Thabo says: “A very bright red lamp is more dangerous to your skin than a weak UV lamp, because the bright light carries more energy.” Which statement evaluates his claim best?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: helderder lig beteken dat elke foton meer energie het.","en":"He is right: brighter light means that each photon has more energy."},{"af":"Hy is reg: rooi lig het 'n langer golflengte en dus meer energie per foton.","en":"He is right: red light has a longer wavelength and therefore more energy per photon."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: die helder lamp stuur net meer fotone uit; elke UV-foton het meer energie as 'n rooi foton (E = hf) en kan velselle beskadig, al is die UV-lamp swak.","en":"He is wrong: the bright lamp only sends out more photons; each UV photon has more energy than a red photon (E = hf) and can damage skin cells, even if the UV lamp is weak."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd, want rooi lig beweeg stadiger as UV-straling en tref die vel met minder energie.","en":"He is wrong, because red light travels slower than UV radiation and hits the skin with less energy."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Skade aan selle hang af van die energie van elke foton, en dit hang net van die frekwensie af (E = hf). UV het 'n hoër frekwensie as rooi lig. Helderheid bepaal net hoeveel fotone daar is. Alle EM-straling beweeg teen dieselfde spoed, en 'n langer golflengte beteken MINDER energie.","en":"Damage to cells depends on the energy of each photon, and that depends only on the frequency (E = hf). UV has a higher frequency than red light. Brightness only determines how many photons there are. All EM radiation travels at the same speed, and a longer wavelength means LESS energy."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Elektrisiteit en magnetisme; chemiese verandering","en":"Electricity and magnetism; chemical change"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t2-magnetisme","title":{"af":"Magnetisme","en":"Magnetism"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal magneetvelde in woorde kan beskryf, aantrekking en afstoting kan voorspel, en die aarde se magneetveld, die kompas en die magnetosfeer kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to describe magnetic fields in words, predict attraction and repulsion, and explain Earth's magnetic field, the compass and the magnetosphere."},"summary":{"af":"## Magnete en pole\n\n'n **Magneet** is 'n voorwerp met 'n paar teenoorgestelde pole: 'n **noordpool (N)** en 'n **suidpool (S)**. As 'n staafmagneet vrylik aan 'n tou hang, draai sy N-pool na die noorde; daarom word dit ook die *noordsoekende pool* genoem.\n\n- **Gelyke pole stoot mekaar af; ongelyke pole trek mekaar aan.**\n- Pole kom altyd in pare voor. Breek jy 'n magneet middeldeur, kry **elke stuk weer 'n N- en 'n S-pool**. 'n Magneet met net een pool bestaan nie.\n- Die magnetiese krag is 'n **nie-kontakkrag**: magnete werk op mekaar in sonder om te raak. Die krag is die sterkste naby die pole en word swakker hoe verder die magnete van mekaar af is.\n\n> **Wenk:** Net **afstoting** bewys dat 'n voorwerp 'n magneet is. 'n Magneet trek ook gewone, ongemagnetiseerde yster aan, so aantrekking bewys niks.\n\n## Ferromagnetiese materiale en domeine\n\n**Yster, kobalt en nikkel** (en allooie soos staal) is **ferromagneties**: hulle word sterk deur 'n magneet aangetrek en kan self gemagnetiseer word. Koper, aluminium, goud, plastiek en hout is nie ferromagneties nie. Nie alle metale is dus magneties nie!\n\nIn 'n ferromagnetiese materiaal gedra die atome soos klein magnetjies wat in groepies, **magnetiese domeine**, almal in dieselfde rigting wys. In 'n ongemagnetiseerde spyker wys die domeine lukraak in alle rigtings, sodat hul effekte mekaar uitkanselleer. As jy dit magnetiseer (bv. deur dit herhaaldelik in een rigting met 'n magneet te stryk), lyn die domeine op.\n\n- **Sagte yster** magnetiseer en demagnetiseer maklik: goed vir tydelike magnete en elektromagnete.\n- **Staal** behou sy magnetisme: goed vir permanente magnete.\n- Sterk **verhitting** of **hamer en laat val** krap die domeine weer deurmekaar en verswak die magneet.\n\n## Die magneetveld\n\n> **Definisie:** 'n **Magneetveld** is 'n gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind.\n\nOns stel die veld voor met **magneetveldlyne**. Jy kan die patroon sien deur **ystervylsels** om 'n magneet te strooi, of deur 'n klein **kompas** (self 'n magneetjie wat vrylik kan draai) van punt tot punt te skuif.\n\nReëls vir magneetveldlyne:\n1. **Rigting:** buite die magneet wys die lyne **van N na S**. Die rigting van die veld by 'n punt is die rigting waarin die **N-pool van 'n kompasnaald** daar wys.\n2. Veldlyne vorm **geslote lusse** (binne die magneet loop hulle van S na N).\n3. Veldlyne **kruis nooit** nie.\n4. Hoe **digter** die lyne, hoe **sterker** die veld. Die veld is die sterkste by die pole.\n\n### Veldpatrone in woorde\n- **Een staafmagneet:** die lyne kom by die N-pool uit, buig in boë aan albei kante van die magneet om en gaan by die S-pool in. Hulle is die digste by die twee pole.\n- **Ongelyke pole na mekaar (N … S):** die lyne loop reguit oor die gaping van N na S, dig en byna ewewydig. Die magnete **trek aan**.\n- **Gelyke pole na mekaar (N … N):** die lyne van albei pole buig weg van mekaar en loop sywaarts uit die gaping. Presies in die middel is 'n **neutrale punt** waar die twee velde mekaar uitkanselleer (veld = 0). Die magnete **stoot af**. By S … S is die patroon dieselfde, maar die pyltjies wys na die pole toe.\n\n## Die aarde se magneetveld\n\nDie aarde gedra asof daar 'n reuse-**staafmagneet** binne-in hom is. Die veld word waarskynlik veroorsaak deur **gesmelte yster wat in die vloeibare buitenste kern beweeg**.\n\n- Die **suidpool van hierdie \"staafmagneet\"** lê naby die **geografiese Noordpool**. Dit trek die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald aan (ongelyke pole trek aan), daarom wys 'n kompas oral op aarde, ook in Brits, noord.\n- Buite die aarde loop die veldlyne dus van die suidelike halfrond na die noordelike halfrond.\n\n| Eienskap | Geografiese Noordpool | Magnetiese noordpool |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wat is dit? | die punt waar die aarde se rotasie-as die oppervlak sny (ware noord) | die punt waarheen 'n kompas wys; die veldlyne gaan hier vertikaal die aarde in |\n| Beweeg dit? | nee | ja, stadig oor die jare (tans in die Arktiese gebied) |\n| Magneetpool? | nee | magneties gesproke 'n **suidpool** |\n\nDie hoek tussen ware (geografiese) noord en magnetiese noord is die **magnetiese deklinasie**. In Suid-Afrika wys 'n kompas etlike grade **wes** van ware noord, so 'n stapper in die Magaliesberg moet sy kompaslesing met die deklinasie op die kaart regstel.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"In die suidelike halfrond wys 'n kompas suid.\" Nee! Die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald wys oral op aarde na magnetiese noord.\n\n## Die magnetosfeer en die sonwind\n\nDie son stuur voortdurend 'n stroom **gelaaide deeltjies** (hoofsaaklik protone en elektrone) die ruimte in: die **sonwind**. Die **magnetosfeer** is die gebied rondom die aarde waar die aarde se magneetveld oorheers. Dit **buig die meeste van die sonwind om die aarde** en beskerm so lewende organismes en die atmosfeer teen hierdie hoë-energie deeltjies. (Die osoonlaag, nie die magnetosfeer nie, beskerm ons teen UV-straling.)\n\n- Sommige deeltjies word langs die veldlyne na die **pole** gelei. Daar bots hulle met gasatome in die boonste atmosfeer, wat dan gekleurde lig uitstraal: die **aurora** (Aurora Borealis of noorderlig in die noorde, Aurora Australis of suiderlig in die suide).\n- Groot uitbarstings op die son veroorsaak **magnetiese storms**. Dit kan satelliete beskadig, GPS en radiokommunikasie ontwrig, transformators in kragnetwerke beskadig en kompaslesings versteur.","en":"## Magnets and poles\n\nA **magnet** is an object with a pair of opposite poles: a **north pole (N)** and a **south pole (S)**. If a bar magnet hangs freely from a string, its N pole turns to the north; that is why it is also called the *north-seeking pole*.\n\n- **Like poles repel; unlike poles attract.**\n- Poles always occur in pairs. If you break a magnet in half, **each piece again has an N and an S pole**. A magnet with only one pole does not exist.\n- The magnetic force is a **non-contact force**: magnets act on each other without touching. The force is strongest near the poles and becomes weaker the further apart the magnets are.\n\n> **Tip:** Only **repulsion** proves that an object is a magnet. A magnet also attracts ordinary, unmagnetised iron, so attraction proves nothing.\n\n## Ferromagnetic materials and domains\n\n**Iron, cobalt and nickel** (and alloys such as steel) are **ferromagnetic**: they are strongly attracted by a magnet and can be magnetised themselves. Copper, aluminium, gold, plastic and wood are not ferromagnetic. So not all metals are magnetic!\n\nIn a ferromagnetic material the atoms behave like tiny magnets that, in groups called **magnetic domains**, all point in the same direction. In an unmagnetised nail the domains point randomly in all directions, so that their effects cancel. When you magnetise it (e.g. by stroking it repeatedly in one direction with a magnet), the domains line up.\n\n- **Soft iron** magnetises and demagnetises easily: good for temporary magnets and electromagnets.\n- **Steel** keeps its magnetism: good for permanent magnets.\n- Strong **heating** or **hammering and dropping** jumbles the domains again and weakens the magnet.\n\n## The magnetic field\n\n> **Definition:** A **magnetic field** is a region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force.\n\nWe represent the field with **magnetic field lines**. You can see the pattern by sprinkling **iron filings** around a magnet, or by moving a small **compass** (itself a tiny magnet that can turn freely) from point to point.\n\nRules for magnetic field lines:\n1. **Direction:** outside the magnet the lines point **from N to S**. The direction of the field at a point is the direction in which the **N pole of a compass needle** points there.\n2. Field lines form **closed loops** (inside the magnet they run from S to N).\n3. Field lines **never cross**.\n4. The **denser** the lines, the **stronger** the field. The field is strongest at the poles.\n\n### Field patterns in words\n- **One bar magnet:** the lines come out at the N pole, curve around in arcs on both sides of the magnet and go in at the S pole. They are densest at the two poles.\n- **Unlike poles facing (N … S):** the lines run straight across the gap from N to S, dense and almost parallel. The magnets **attract**.\n- **Like poles facing (N … N):** the lines from both poles bend away from each other and run sideways out of the gap. Exactly in the middle is a **neutral point** where the two fields cancel (field = 0). The magnets **repel**. For S … S the pattern is the same, but the arrows point towards the poles.\n\n## Earth's magnetic field\n\nEarth behaves as if there were a giant **bar magnet** inside it. The field is probably caused by **molten iron moving in the liquid outer core**.\n\n- The **south pole of this \"bar magnet\"** lies near the **geographic North Pole**. It attracts the N pole of a compass needle (unlike poles attract), which is why a compass points north everywhere on Earth, also in Brits.\n- Outside Earth the field lines therefore run from the southern hemisphere to the northern hemisphere.\n\n| Property | Geographic North Pole | Magnetic north pole |\n|---|---|---|\n| What is it? | the point where Earth's axis of rotation cuts the surface (true north) | the point a compass points to; the field lines go vertically into Earth here |\n| Does it move? | no | yes, slowly over the years (currently in the Arctic region) |\n| Magnetic pole? | no | magnetically speaking a **south pole** |\n\nThe angle between true (geographic) north and magnetic north is the **magnetic declination**. In South Africa a compass points several degrees **west** of true north, so a hiker in the Magaliesberg must correct his compass reading with the declination on the map.\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"In the southern hemisphere a compass points south.\" No! The N pole of a compass needle points to magnetic north everywhere on Earth.\n\n## The magnetosphere and the solar wind\n\nThe sun continuously sends a stream of **charged particles** (mainly protons and electrons) into space: the **solar wind**. The **magnetosphere** is the region around Earth where Earth's magnetic field dominates. It **deflects most of the solar wind around Earth** and so protects living organisms and the atmosphere from these high-energy particles. (The ozone layer, not the magnetosphere, protects us from UV radiation.)\n\n- Some particles are guided along the field lines to the **poles**. There they collide with gas atoms in the upper atmosphere, which then give off coloured light: the **aurora** (Aurora Borealis or northern lights in the north, Aurora Australis or southern lights in the south).\n- Large eruptions on the sun cause **magnetic storms**. These can damage satellites, disrupt GPS and radio communication, damage transformers in power grids and disturb compass readings."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Magneet","en":"Magnet"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp met 'n paar teenoorgestelde pole (noord en suid) wat 'n magneetveld om hom het.","en":"An object with a pair of opposite poles (north and south) that has a magnetic field around it."}},{"term":{"af":"Magneetveld","en":"Magnetic field"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind.","en":"A region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force."}},{"term":{"af":"Magneetveldlyne","en":"Magnetic field lines"},"def":{"af":"Denkbeeldige lyne wat die rigting en sterkte van 'n magneetveld aandui: buite die magneet van N na S, hulle kruis nooit, en hoe digter, hoe sterker die veld.","en":"Imaginary lines that show the direction and strength of a magnetic field: outside the magnet from N to S, they never cross, and the denser they are, the stronger the field."}},{"term":{"af":"Ferromagnetiese materiaal","en":"Ferromagnetic material"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal soos yster, kobalt, nikkel of hul allooie (bv. staal) wat sterk deur 'n magneet aangetrek word en self gemagnetiseer kan word.","en":"A material such as iron, cobalt, nickel or their alloys (e.g. steel) that is strongly attracted by a magnet and can be magnetised itself."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetiese domein","en":"Magnetic domain"},"def":{"af":"'n Klein gebied in 'n ferromagnetiese materiaal waarin die atoommagnetjies almal in dieselfde rigting wys.","en":"A small region in a ferromagnetic material in which the atomic magnets all point in the same direction."}},{"term":{"af":"Kompas","en":"Compass"},"def":{"af":"'n Klein magneet (naald) wat vrylik kan draai; sy N-pool wys in die rigting van die magneetveld.","en":"A small magnet (needle) that can turn freely; its N pole points in the direction of the magnetic field."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetiese noordpool","en":"Magnetic north pole"},"def":{"af":"Die punt in die Arktiese gebied waarheen 'n kompas wys. Magneties is dit 'n suidpool, en dit lê nie op dieselfde plek as die geografiese Noordpool nie.","en":"The point in the Arctic region to which a compass points. Magnetically it is a south pole, and it does not lie at the same place as the geographic North Pole."}},{"term":{"af":"Geografiese Noordpool","en":"Geographic North Pole"},"def":{"af":"Die punt waar die aarde se rotasie-as die oppervlak in die noorde sny (ware noord).","en":"The point where Earth's axis of rotation cuts the surface in the north (true north)."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetosfeer","en":"Magnetosphere"},"def":{"af":"Die gebied rondom die aarde waar die aarde se magneetveld oorheers; dit buig die meeste van die sonwind om die aarde.","en":"The region around Earth where Earth's magnetic field dominates; it deflects most of the solar wind around Earth."}},{"term":{"af":"Sonwind","en":"Solar wind"},"def":{"af":"'n Stroom gelaaide deeltjies (hoofsaaklik protone en elektrone) wat voortdurend van die son af uitvloei.","en":"A stream of charged particles (mainly protons and electrons) that continuously flows out from the sun."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Karteer die veld van 'n staafmagneet","en":"Map the field of a bar magnet"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf hoe jy met 'n klein kompas die magneetveld om 'n staafmagneet kan karteer, en beskryf die veldpatroon wat jy kry in woorde.","en":"Describe how you can map the magnetic field around a bar magnet with a small compass, and describe the field pattern you get in words."},"steps":[{"af":"Sit die magneet op 'n vel papier en trek sy buitelyn. Plaas die kompas naby die N-pool en merk die punt waarheen die N-pool van die kompasnaald wys.","en":"Put the magnet on a sheet of paper and trace its outline. Place the compass near the N pole and mark the point to which the N pole of the compass needle points."},{"af":"Skuif die kompas sodat die S-kant van die naald op die merk is, en merk weer waarheen die N-pool wys. Herhaal tot jy by die S-pool uitkom. Verbind die merke met 'n gladde kromme met pyltjies van N na S: dit is een veldlyn.","en":"Move the compass so that the S end of the needle is on the mark, and mark again where the N pole points. Repeat until you reach the S pole. Join the marks with a smooth curve with arrows from N to S: this is one field line."},{"af":"Herhaal vanaf ander beginpunte. Die lyne kom by die N-pool uit, buig in boë aan albei kante van die magneet om en gaan by die S-pool in.","en":"Repeat from other starting points. The lines come out at the N pole, curve around in arcs on both sides of the magnet and go in at the S pole."},{"af":"Die lyne kruis nooit, en hulle is die digste by die pole, waar die veld die sterkste is. By enige punt is die veldrigting die rigting waarin die kompas se N-pool wys.","en":"The lines never cross, and they are densest at the poles, where the field is strongest. At any point the field direction is the direction in which the compass's N pole points."}],"answer":{"af":"Veldlyne loop buite die magneet van N na S, vorm geslote lusse, kruis nooit en is die digste (sterkste veld) by die pole.","en":"Field lines run from N to S outside the magnet, form closed loops, never cross and are densest (strongest field) at the poles."}},{"title":{"af":"Die veld tussen twee magnete","en":"The field between two magnets"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf die magneetveld tussen twee staafmagnete wanneer (a) 'n N-pool en 'n S-pool na mekaar wys, en (b) twee N-pole na mekaar wys. Sê in elke geval of die magnete mekaar aantrek of afstoot.","en":"Describe the magnetic field between two bar magnets when (a) an N pole and an S pole face each other, and (b) two N poles face each other. In each case, say whether the magnets attract or repel each other."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) N … S: die veldlyne loop reguit oor die gaping van die N-pool na die S-pool. In die gaping is hulle dig en byna ewewydig, dus is die veld daar sterk en byna eenvormig.","en":"(a) N … S: the field lines run straight across the gap from the N pole to the S pole. In the gap they are dense and almost parallel, so the field there is strong and almost uniform."},{"af":"Ongelyke pole trek mekaar aan, dus trek die magnete aan.","en":"Unlike poles attract each other, so the magnets attract."},{"af":"(b) N … N: die veldlyne kom by albei N-pole uit en buig weg van mekaar, sywaarts uit die gaping. Geen lyn loop van die een N-pool na die ander nie.","en":"(b) N … N: the field lines come out at both N poles and bend away from each other, sideways out of the gap. No line runs from one N pole to the other."},{"af":"Presies in die middel is die twee velde ewe sterk en teenoorgesteld: hulle kanselleer uit, en dit is 'n neutrale punt (veld = 0). Gelyke pole stoot mekaar af, dus stoot die magnete af.","en":"Exactly in the middle the two fields are equally strong and opposite: they cancel, and this is a neutral point (field = 0). Like poles repel each other, so the magnets repel."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Reguit, digte lyne van N na S oor die gaping; aantrekking. (b) Lyne buig weg van mekaar met 'n neutrale punt in die middel; afstoting.","en":"(a) Straight, dense lines from N to S across the gap; attraction. (b) Lines bend away from each other with a neutral point in the middle; repulsion."}},{"title":{"af":"Kompas, magnetiese noord en ware noord","en":"Compass, magnetic north and true north"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik (a) waarom die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald in Brits na die noorde wys, (b) die verskil tussen die geografiese Noordpool en die magnetiese noordpool, en (c) wat 'n stapper in die Magaliesberg moet doen as sy met kaart en kompas ware noord wil volg.","en":"Explain (a) why the N pole of a compass needle in Brits points north, (b) the difference between the geographic North Pole and the magnetic north pole, and (c) what a hiker in the Magaliesberg must do if she wants to follow true north with a map and compass."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die aarde gedra soos 'n reuse-staafmagneet (waarskynlik weens bewegende gesmelte yster in die buitenste kern). Daardie magneet se S-pool lê naby die geografiese Noordpool. Ongelyke pole trek aan, dus word die N-pool van die naald na die noorde getrek, oral op aarde.","en":"(a) Earth behaves like a giant bar magnet (probably due to moving molten iron in the outer core). That magnet's S pole lies near the geographic North Pole. Unlike poles attract, so the N pole of the needle is pulled towards the north, everywhere on Earth."},{"af":"(b) Die geografiese Noordpool is die punt waar die aarde se rotasie-as die oppervlak sny; dit beweeg nie. Die magnetiese noordpool is die punt waarheen kompasse wys en waar die veldlyne vertikaal die aarde ingaan. Dit lê in die Arktiese gebied, nie op dieselfde plek nie, en beweeg stadig.","en":"(b) The geographic North Pole is the point where Earth's axis of rotation cuts the surface; it does not move. The magnetic north pole is the point compasses point to and where the field lines go vertically into Earth. It lies in the Arctic region, not at the same place, and moves slowly."},{"af":"(c) Die hoek tussen ware noord en magnetiese noord is die magnetiese deklinasie. In Suid-Afrika wys 'n kompas etlike grade wes van ware noord, dus moet sy die deklinasie wat op die kaart aangedui is, by haar kompaslesing in berekening bring.","en":"(c) The angle between true north and magnetic north is the magnetic declination. In South Africa a compass points several degrees west of true north, so she must take the declination shown on the map into account in her compass reading."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die aarde se magnetiese S-pool naby geografiese noord trek die naald se N-pool aan. (b) Geografies = rotasie-as, vas; magneties = waar kompasse wys, elders en beweeg. (c) Stel reg vir die deklinasie.","en":"(a) Earth's magnetic S pole near geographic north attracts the needle's N pole. (b) Geographic = axis of rotation, fixed; magnetic = where compasses point, elsewhere and moving. (c) Correct for the declination."}},{"title":{"af":"Sonstorms, die magnetosfeer en aurora's","en":"Solar storms, the magnetosphere and auroras"},"problem":{"af":"Tydens 'n sterk sonstorm word 'n groot wolk gelaaide deeltjies na die aarde geslinger. Verduidelik (a) hoe die magnetosfeer ons beskerm, (b) waarom aurora's hoofsaaklik naby die pole gesien word, en (c) watter skade so 'n magnetiese storm aan tegnologie kan doen.","en":"During a strong solar storm a large cloud of charged particles is flung towards Earth. Explain (a) how the magnetosphere protects us, (b) why auroras are mainly seen near the poles, and (c) what damage such a magnetic storm can do to technology."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die magnetosfeer is die gebied om die aarde waar die aarde se magneetveld oorheers. Gelaaide deeltjies wat deur 'n magneetveld beweeg, word afgebuig, dus word die meeste van die sonwind om die aarde gelei. Dit beskerm lewende organismes en die atmosfeer.","en":"(a) The magnetosphere is the region around Earth where Earth's magnetic field dominates. Charged particles moving through a magnetic field are deflected, so most of the solar wind is guided around Earth. This protects living organisms and the atmosphere."},{"af":"(b) Sommige deeltjies word langs die veldlyne na die pole gelei, waar die lyne die aarde ingaan. Daar bots hulle met gasatome in die boonste atmosfeer, wat dan gekleurde lig uitstraal: Aurora Borealis in die noorde en Aurora Australis in die suide.","en":"(b) Some particles are guided along the field lines to the poles, where the lines enter Earth. There they collide with gas atoms in the upper atmosphere, which then give off coloured light: Aurora Borealis in the north and Aurora Australis in the south."},{"af":"(c) 'n Magnetiese storm kan satelliete beskadig, GPS en radiokommunikasie ontwrig, groot strome in lang kraglyne veroorsaak wat transformators beskadig, en kompaslesings versteur.","en":"(c) A magnetic storm can damage satellites, disrupt GPS and radio communication, cause large currents in long power lines that damage transformers, and disturb compass readings."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die magneetveld buig die gelaaide deeltjies om die aarde. (b) Veldlyne lei deeltjies na die pole, waar hulle met gasatome bots en lig uitstraal. (c) Satelliete, GPS, radio, kragnetwerke en kompasse word geraak.","en":"(a) The magnetic field deflects the charged particles around Earth. (b) Field lines guide particles to the poles, where they collide with gas atoms that give off light. (c) Satellites, GPS, radio, power grids and compasses are affected."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende materiale is ferromagneties?","en":"Which one of the following materials is ferromagnetic?"},"options":[{"af":"Koper","en":"Copper"},{"af":"Aluminium","en":"Aluminium"},{"af":"Nikkel","en":"Nickel"},{"af":"Glas","en":"Glass"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Yster, kobalt en nikkel (en allooie soos staal) is ferromagneties. Koper en aluminium is metale wat elektrisiteit goed gelei, maar 'n magneet trek hulle nie aan nie: nie alle metale is magneties nie.","en":"Iron, cobalt and nickel (and alloys such as steel) are ferromagnetic. Copper and aluminium are metals that conduct electricity well, but a magnet does not attract them: not all metals are magnetic."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gelyke magneetpole stoot mekaar af en ongelyke magneetpole trek mekaar aan.","en":"Like magnetic poles repel each other and unlike magnetic poles attract each other."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. N en N (of S en S) stoot af; N en S trek aan.","en":"True. N and N (or S and S) repel; N and S attract."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die korrekte definisie van 'n magneetveld?","en":"Which statement is the correct definition of a magnetic field?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind.","en":"A region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force."},{"af":"'n Gebied in die ruimte waar 'n gelaaide voorwerp 'n elektrostatiese krag ondervind.","en":"A region in space where a charged object experiences an electrostatic force."},{"af":"Die krag wat twee magnete op mekaar uitoefen wanneer hulle aan mekaar raak.","en":"The force that two magnets exert on each other when they touch."},{"af":"Die lyne wat van die suidpool na die noordpool om 'n magneet getrek word.","en":"The lines that are drawn from the south pole to the north pole around a magnet."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Magneetveld is 'n gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind. Die tweede opsie beskryf 'n elektriese veld; die magnetiese krag werk sonder kontak; en veldlyne wys buite die magneet van N na S.","en":"A magnetic field is a region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force. The second option describes an electric field; the magnetic force acts without contact; and field lines point from N to S outside the magnet."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Buite 'n staafmagneet wys die magneetveldlyne van die ___ na die suidpool.","en":"Outside a bar magnet the magnetic field lines point from the ___ to the south pole."},"answers":{"af":["noordpool","noord","N","N-pool","N pool","die noordpool","noord-pool"],"en":["north pole","north","N","N pole","N-pole","the north pole"]},"explain":{"af":"Buite die magneet loop die veldlyne van die noordpool na die suidpool (binne die magneet van S na N, sodat hulle geslote lusse vorm).","en":"Outside the magnet the field lines run from the north pole to the south pole (inside the magnet from S to N, so that they form closed loops)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sonwind","en":"Solar wind"},"r":{"af":"'n Stroom gelaaide deeltjies wat van die son af uitvloei","en":"A stream of charged particles flowing out from the sun"}},{"l":{"af":"Aurora","en":"Aurora"},"r":{"af":"Gekleurde lig naby die pole wanneer gelaaide deeltjies met gasatome in die boonste atmosfeer bots","en":"Coloured light near the poles when charged particles collide with gas atoms in the upper atmosphere"}},{"l":{"af":"Magnetiese domein","en":"Magnetic domain"},"r":{"af":"'n Klein gebied in 'n ferromagnetiese materiaal waar die atoommagnetjies in dieselfde rigting wys","en":"A small region in a ferromagnetic material where the atomic magnets point in the same direction"}},{"l":{"af":"Kompas","en":"Compass"},"r":{"af":"'n Klein magneet wat vrylik kan draai en in die rigting van die magneetveld wys","en":"A small magnet that can turn freely and points in the direction of the magnetic field"}},{"l":{"af":"Ferromagnetiese materiaal","en":"Ferromagnetic material"},"r":{"af":"'n Stof soos yster wat sterk aangetrek word en gemagnetiseer kan word","en":"A substance such as iron that is strongly attracted and can be magnetised"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die sonwind bestaan uit gelaaide deeltjies van die son; dié wat na die pole gelei word, veroorsaak aurora's. Domeine is groepies opgelynde atoommagnetjies in ferromagnetiese stowwe soos yster. 'n Kompas is 'n vrydraaiende magneetjie.","en":"The solar wind consists of charged particles from the sun; those guided to the poles cause auroras. Domains are groups of lined-up atomic magnets in ferromagnetic substances such as iron. A compass is a freely turning small magnet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe beskerm die magnetosfeer lewe op aarde?","en":"How does the magnetosphere protect life on Earth?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit absorbeer die meeste van die son se UV-straling.","en":"It absorbs most of the sun's UV radiation."},{"af":"Dit hou die aarde warm deur hitte vas te vang.","en":"It keeps Earth warm by trapping heat."},{"af":"Dit trek meteoriete weg van die aarde af.","en":"It pulls meteorites away from Earth."},{"af":"Dit buig die meeste van die gelaaide deeltjies van die sonwind om die aarde.","en":"It deflects most of the charged particles of the solar wind around Earth."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die aarde se magneetveld buig die gelaaide deeltjies van die sonwind af, sodat die meeste nie die oppervlak bereik nie. Die osoonlaag (nie die magnetosfeer nie) absorbeer UV, en hitte word deur kweekhuisgasse vasgevang.","en":"Earth's magnetic field deflects the charged particles of the solar wind, so most of them do not reach the surface. The ozone layer (not the magnetosphere) absorbs UV, and heat is trapped by greenhouse gases."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar magneetveldlyne ver uitmekaar is, is die magneetveld die sterkste.","en":"Where magnetic field lines are far apart, the magnetic field is strongest."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Hoe digter die veldlyne, hoe sterker die veld. Die veld is die sterkste by die pole, waar die lyne die digste is.","en":"False. The denser the field lines, the stronger the field. The field is strongest at the poles, where the lines are densest."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter breek 'n staafmagneet presies in die middel in twee stukke. Wat is waar van die twee stukke?","en":"Pieter breaks a bar magnet exactly in the middle into two pieces. What is true of the two pieces?"},"options":[{"af":"Een stuk het net 'n noordpool en die ander stuk net 'n suidpool.","en":"One piece has only a north pole and the other piece only a south pole."},{"af":"Elke stuk is 'n kleiner magneet met sy eie noordpool en suidpool.","en":"Each piece is a smaller magnet with its own north pole and south pole."},{"af":"Albei stukke verloor hul magnetisme omdat die pole geskei is.","en":"Both pieces lose their magnetism because the poles have been separated."},{"af":"Elke stuk het twee noordpole.","en":"Each piece has two north poles."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Pole kom altyd in pare voor. Die domeine in elke stuk wys steeds in dieselfde rigting, dus vorm elke stuk 'n nuwe, kleiner magneet met 'n N- en 'n S-pool.","en":"Poles always occur in pairs. The domains in each piece still point in the same direction, so each piece forms a new, smaller magnet with an N and an S pole."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Staafmagneet lê op 'n tafel met sy N-pool na die ooste en sy S-pool na die weste. 'n Klein kompas word langs die middel van die magneet neergesit. Ignoreer die aarde se magneetveld. Die N-pool van die kompasnaald wys na die ___.","en":"A bar magnet lies on a table with its N pole to the east and its S pole to the west. A small compass is placed next to the middle of the magnet. Ignore Earth's magnetic field. The N pole of the compass needle points to the ___."},"answers":{"af":["weste","wes","die weste","W"],"en":["west","W","the west"]},"explain":{"af":"Buite die magneet loop die veldlyne van N na S. Langs die middel van die magneet loop hulle ewewydig aan die magneet, van die N-kant (ooste) na die S-kant (weste). Die kompas se N-pool wys in die rigting van die veld: na die weste.","en":"Outside the magnet the field lines run from N to S. Next to the middle of the magnet they run parallel to the magnet, from the N end (east) to the S end (west). The compass's N pole points in the direction of the field: to the west."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die S-pool van magneet A word naby kant X van magneet B gebring, en die twee stoot mekaar af. Watter pool is kant X? ___","en":"The S pole of magnet A is brought near end X of magnet B, and the two repel each other. Which pole is end X? ___"},"answers":{"af":["suidpool","suid","S","S-pool","S pool","'n suidpool","die suidpool"],"en":["south pole","south","S","S pole","S-pole","a south pole","the south pole"]},"explain":{"af":"Afstoting gebeur net tussen gelyke pole. Kant X stoot 'n S-pool af, dus is X ook 'n suidpool.","en":"Repulsion happens only between like poles. End X repels an S pole, so X is also a south pole."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika kry 'n onbekende metaalstaaf. Watter waarneming bewys dat die staaf 'n magneet is?","en":"Anika finds an unknown metal bar. Which observation proves that the bar is a magnet?"},"options":[{"af":"Een kant van die staaf trek die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald aan.","en":"One end of the bar attracts the N pole of a compass needle."},{"af":"Die staaf gelei elektrisiteit.","en":"The bar conducts electricity."},{"af":"Die staaf word deur 'n sterk magneet aangetrek.","en":"The bar is attracted by a strong magnet."},{"af":"Een kant van die staaf stoot die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald af.","en":"One end of the bar repels the N pole of a compass needle."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Aantrekking bewys niks, want 'n magneet trek ook gewone, ongemagnetiseerde yster aan. Afstoting gebeur net tussen gelyke pole van twee magnete, dus bewys dit dat die staaf 'n magneet is. Elektriese geleiding sê niks oor magnetisme nie.","en":"Attraction proves nothing, because a magnet also attracts ordinary, unmagnetised iron. Repulsion happens only between like poles of two magnets, so it proves that the bar is a magnet. Electrical conduction says nothing about magnetism."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee identiese staafmagnete lê in een lyn met hul N-pole 10 cm van mekaar af. Wat is waar by die punt presies in die middel tussen die twee N-pole?","en":"Two identical bar magnets lie in a line with their N poles 10 cm apart. What is true at the point exactly in the middle between the two N poles?"},"options":[{"af":"Die twee magneetvelde kanselleer mekaar uit, dus is die magneetveld daar nul ('n neutrale punt).","en":"The two magnetic fields cancel each other, so the magnetic field there is zero (a neutral point)."},{"af":"Die magneetveld is daar die sterkste, want twee pole wys na mekaar.","en":"The magnetic field is strongest there, because two poles face each other."},{"af":"Die veldlyne loop daar reguit van die een N-pool na die ander N-pool.","en":"The field lines there run straight from one N pole to the other N pole."},{"af":"Die magneetveld wys daar na die linkerkantste magneet toe.","en":"The magnetic field there points towards the magnet on the left."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By die middelpunt wys die veld van die linkermagneet se N-pool na regs (weg van die N-pool) en dié van die regtermagneet na links. Die magnete is identies en die punt is ewe ver, dus is die velde ewe sterk en teenoorgesteld: hulle kanselleer uit. Veldlyne loop nooit van N na N nie.","en":"At the midpoint the field of the left magnet's N pole points to the right (away from the N pole) and that of the right magnet to the left. The magnets are identical and the point is equally far, so the fields are equally strong and opposite: they cancel. Field lines never run from N to N."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald wys na die aarde se geografiese Noordpool. As jy die aarde as 'n reuse-staafmagneet beskou, watter pool van daardie staafmagneet lê naby die geografiese Noordpool? ___","en":"The N pole of a compass needle points to Earth's geographic North Pole. If you think of Earth as a giant bar magnet, which pole of that bar magnet lies near the geographic North Pole? ___"},"answers":{"af":["suidpool","suid","S","S-pool","S pool","'n suidpool","die suidpool"],"en":["south pole","south","S","S pole","S-pole","a south pole","the south pole"]},"explain":{"af":"Ongelyke pole trek mekaar aan. Die kompas se N-pool word na die noorde getrek, dus moet daar 'n magnetiese SUIDpool naby die geografiese Noordpool wees. Ons noem die plek 'magnetiese noordpool' omdat dit in die noorde lê, maar magneties gedra dit soos 'n suidpool.","en":"Unlike poles attract each other. The compass's N pole is pulled to the north, so there must be a magnetic SOUTH pole near the geographic North Pole. We call the place 'magnetic north pole' because it lies in the north, but magnetically it behaves like a south pole."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato stap in die Magaliesberg en wil met haar kaart presies na ware (geografiese) noord stap. Sy sê: “Ek volg net my kompasnaald; dit wys presies na die geografiese Noordpool.” Watter stelling evalueer haar plan die beste?","en":"Lerato is hiking in the Magaliesberg and wants to walk exactly to true (geographic) north with her map. She says: “I'll just follow my compass needle; it points exactly to the geographic North Pole.” Which statement evaluates her plan best?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy is reg, want die magnetiese noordpool en die geografiese Noordpool is presies dieselfde punt.","en":"She is right, because the magnetic north pole and the geographic North Pole are exactly the same point."},{"af":"Sy is nie heeltemal reg nie: die kompas wys na magnetiese noord, wat nie op dieselfde plek as geografiese noord lê nie, dus moet sy vir die hoek tussen hulle (die deklinasie) regstel.","en":"She is not completely right: the compass points to magnetic north, which is not at the same place as geographic north, so she must correct for the angle between them (the declination)."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd, want in die suidelike halfrond wys 'n kompasnaald se N-pool suid.","en":"She is wrong, because in the southern hemisphere the N pole of a compass needle points south."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd, want 'n kompas wys altyd na die son.","en":"She is wrong, because a compass always points to the sun."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Kompas wys oral op aarde (ook in Suid-Afrika) na magnetiese noord. Die magnetiese noordpool lê egter nie op die geografiese Noordpool nie en beweeg stadig, dus verskil die rigtings met die deklinasiehoek. In Suid-Afrika wys die kompas etlike grade wes van ware noord.","en":"A compass points to magnetic north everywhere on Earth (also in South Africa). However, the magnetic north pole does not lie at the geographic North Pole and moves slowly, so the directions differ by the declination angle. In South Africa the compass points several degrees west of true north."}}]},{"id":"f10-t2-elektrostatika","title":{"af":"Elektrostatika","en":"Electrostatics"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe voorwerpe gelaai word, die beginsels van behoud en kwantisering van lading toepas, en ladingsdeling en elektronoordrag tussen sfere bereken.","en":"You will be able to explain how objects become charged, apply the principles of conservation and quantisation of charge, and calculate charge sharing and electron transfer between spheres."},"summary":{"af":"## Twee soorte lading\n\nAlle materie bestaan uit atome met positiewe **protone** (in die kern) en negatiewe **elektrone** (om die kern). 'n **Neutrale** voorwerp het ewe veel protone en elektrone, dus is sy netto lading nul. Daar is **twee soorte lading: positief en negatief**.\n\n- 'n Voorwerp word **negatief** gelaai as dit **elektrone bykry**.\n- 'n Voorwerp word **positief** gelaai as dit **elektrone verloor**.\n- In vaste stowwe beweeg **slegs elektrone**; protone sit vas in die kern.\n- **Gelyke ladings stoot mekaar af; ongelyke ladings trek mekaar aan.** Die elektrostatiese krag is 'n nie-kontakkrag en word sterker hoe nader die ladings aan mekaar is.\n- Lading (Q) word in **coulomb (C)** gemeet. Die lading op een elektron is q_{e} = −1,6 × 10^{−19} C (data-blad). Voorvoegsels: 1 μC = 10^{−6} C; 1 nC = 10^{−9} C; 1 pC = 10^{−12} C.\n\n## Laai deur wrywing\n\nAs twee verskillende isolators teen mekaar gevryf word, word elektrone van die een na die ander oorgedra. Die een wat elektrone bykry, word negatief; die ander een word **ewe veel** positief.\n\n| Wat word gevryf? | Voorwerp word | Lap/materiaal word |\n|---|---|---|\n| glasstaaf met sy | positief (verloor elektrone) | negatief |\n| eboniet- of plastiekstaaf met pels of wol | negatief (kry elektrone by) | positief |\n| ballon teen jou hare | negatief | hare positief |\n\nAlledaags: jy kry 'n skok as jy ná 'n rit in 'n taxi aan die metaaldeur raak (jou klere het teen die sitplek gevryf), en weerlig tydens 'n Hoëveldse donderstorm is 'n reuse-ontlading tussen gelaaide wolke en die grond. As 'n gelaaide voorwerp met die grond verbind word (**aarding**), vloei elektrone na of van die aarde totdat die voorwerp neutraal is.\n\n## Behoud van lading\n\n> **Definisie (beginsel van behoud van lading):** Die netto lading van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant gedurende enige fisiese proses.\n\nLading word nie geskep of vernietig nie, net **oorgedra**. Kry 'n ebonietstaaf −5 nC, dan kry die pels presies +5 nC: die totaal bly 0.\n\n## Kwantisering van lading\n\n> **Definisie (beginsel van kwantisering van lading):** Alle ladings in die heelal bestaan uit 'n heelgetalveelvoud van die lading op een elektron, d.w.s. Q = nq_{e}.\n\n- n is die aantal elektrone wat bygekry of verloor is: altyd 'n **heelgetal**. Bereken dit met n = Q ÷ q_{e}.\n- 'n Negatiewe voorwerp het n **oortollige** elektrone; 'n positiewe voorwerp kort n elektrone.\n- 'n Lading van 2,4 × 10^{−19} C is **onmoontlik**: dit sou 1,5 elektrone beteken.\n\n## Identiese sfere wat aan mekaar raak\n\nAs twee **identiese, geleidende** sfere aan mekaar raak, vloei elektrone totdat die lading **eweredig gedeel** is. Ná skeiding het elkeen:\n\n**Q_{nuut} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]]**\n\n### Stappe\n1. Tel die ladings **met hul tekens** bymekaar en deel deur 2.\n2. Bereken die verandering in lading van een sfeer: ΔQ = Q_{nuut} − Q_{begin}.\n3. Skakel om na coulomb (μC → × 10^{−6}; nC → × 10^{−9}).\n4. Aantal elektrone oorgedra: n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}).\n5. Rigting: elektrone vloei **na** die sfeer wat negatiewer word (ΔQ negatief) en **weg van** die sfeer wat positiewer word.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die tekens te ignoreer. +6 μC en −2 μC gee [[6 + (−2)/2]] = +2 μC, nie [[6 + 2/2]] = +4 μC nie. Moenie ook vergeet om μC of nC na C om te skakel voordat jy n bereken nie.\n\n## Polarisasie: waarom 'n gelaaide voorwerp 'n neutrale voorwerp aantrek\n\nBring 'n negatief gelaaide staaf naby (sonder om te raak) 'n neutrale voorwerp:\n\n- **Geleier** (bv. aluminiumfoelie): die vrye elektrone word na die verste kant afgestoot. Die naaste kant word positief en die verste kant negatief: die lading word **geskei**.\n- **Isolator** (bv. papier of 'n muur): die elektrone kan nie deur die stof beweeg nie, maar die elektronwolk van elke molekuul skuif effens weg. Die molekules word **gepolariseer**: hul naaste kant is effens positief.\n\nDie teenoorgestelde lading is **nader** aan die staaf as die gelyke lading, dus is die aantrekking sterker as die afstoting: die neutrale voorwerp word **aangetrek**. Sy netto lading bly nul. Voorbeelde: 'n gelaaide kam tel papiersnippers op; 'n ballon wat teen jou hare gevryf is, kleef teen die muur; 'n gelaaide staaf buig 'n dun straaltjie water uit 'n kraan.\n\n> **Onthou!** Aantrekking bewys nie dat 'n voorwerp gelaai is nie, want dit kan neutraal wees. Net **afstoting** bewys dat albei voorwerpe gelaai is (met dieselfde soort lading).","en":"## Two kinds of charge\n\nAll matter consists of atoms with positive **protons** (in the nucleus) and negative **electrons** (around the nucleus). A **neutral** object has equal numbers of protons and electrons, so its net charge is zero. There are **two kinds of charge: positive and negative**.\n\n- An object becomes **negatively** charged when it **gains electrons**.\n- An object becomes **positively** charged when it **loses electrons**.\n- In solids **only electrons** move; protons are fixed in the nucleus.\n- **Like charges repel; unlike charges attract.** The electrostatic force is a non-contact force and becomes stronger the closer the charges are to each other.\n- Charge (Q) is measured in **coulombs (C)**. The charge on one electron is q_{e} = −1.6 × 10^{−19} C (data sheet). Prefixes: 1 μC = 10^{−6} C; 1 nC = 10^{−9} C; 1 pC = 10^{−12} C.\n\n## Charging by friction\n\nWhen two different insulators are rubbed together, electrons are transferred from one to the other. The one that gains electrons becomes negative; the other one becomes **equally** positive.\n\n| What is rubbed? | Object becomes | Cloth/material becomes |\n|---|---|---|\n| glass rod with silk | positive (loses electrons) | negative |\n| ebonite or plastic rod with fur or wool | negative (gains electrons) | positive |\n| balloon against your hair | negative | hair positive |\n\nEveryday: you get a shock when you touch the metal door after a ride in a taxi (your clothes rubbed against the seat), and lightning during a Highveld thunderstorm is a huge discharge between charged clouds and the ground. When a charged object is connected to the ground (**earthing**), electrons flow to or from the earth until the object is neutral.\n\n## Conservation of charge\n\n> **Definition (principle of conservation of charge):** The net charge of an isolated system remains constant during any physical process.\n\nCharge is not created or destroyed, only **transferred**. If an ebonite rod gets −5 nC, the fur gets exactly +5 nC: the total stays 0.\n\n## Quantisation of charge\n\n> **Definition (principle of charge quantisation):** All charges in the universe consist of an integer multiple of the charge on one electron, i.e. Q = nq_{e}.\n\n- n is the number of electrons gained or lost: always an **integer**. Calculate it with n = Q ÷ q_{e}.\n- A negative object has n **excess** electrons; a positive object is short of n electrons.\n- A charge of 2.4 × 10^{−19} C is **impossible**: it would mean 1.5 electrons.\n\n## Identical spheres that touch\n\nWhen two **identical, conducting** spheres touch, electrons flow until the charge is **shared equally**. After separation each has:\n\n**Q_{new} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]]**\n\n### Steps\n1. Add the charges **with their signs** and divide by 2.\n2. Calculate the change in charge of one sphere: ΔQ = Q_{new} − Q_{initial}.\n3. Convert to coulombs (μC → × 10^{−6}; nC → × 10^{−9}).\n4. Number of electrons transferred: n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}).\n5. Direction: electrons flow **to** the sphere that becomes more negative (ΔQ negative) and **away from** the sphere that becomes more positive.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Ignoring the signs. +6 μC and −2 μC give [[6 + (−2)/2]] = +2 μC, not [[6 + 2/2]] = +4 μC. Also do not forget to convert μC or nC to C before you calculate n.\n\n## Polarisation: why a charged object attracts a neutral object\n\nBring a negatively charged rod near (without touching) a neutral object:\n\n- **Conductor** (e.g. aluminium foil): the free electrons are repelled to the far side. The near side becomes positive and the far side negative: the charge is **separated**.\n- **Insulator** (e.g. paper or a wall): the electrons cannot move through the substance, but the electron cloud of each molecule shifts slightly away. The molecules become **polarised**: their near side is slightly positive.\n\nThe opposite charge is **closer** to the rod than the like charge, so the attraction is stronger than the repulsion: the neutral object is **attracted**. Its net charge stays zero. Examples: a charged comb picks up bits of paper; a balloon rubbed against your hair sticks to the wall; a charged rod bends a thin stream of water from a tap.\n\n> **Remember!** Attraction does not prove that an object is charged, because it may be neutral. Only **repulsion** proves that both objects are charged (with the same kind of charge)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Elektriese lading (Q)","en":"Electric charge (Q)"},"def":{"af":"'n Eienskap van deeltjies soos protone (positief) en elektrone (negatief); gelyke ladings stoot af en ongelyke ladings trek aan. Eenheid: coulomb (C).","en":"A property of particles such as protons (positive) and electrons (negative); like charges repel and unlike charges attract. Unit: coulomb (C)."}},{"term":{"af":"Lading op 'n elektron (qₑ)","en":"Charge on an electron (qₑ)"},"def":{"af":"Die kleinste vrye lading: qₑ = −1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.","en":"The smallest free charge: qₑ = −1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C."}},{"term":{"af":"Neutrale voorwerp","en":"Neutral object"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp met ewe veel protone en elektrone, sodat sy netto lading nul is.","en":"An object with equal numbers of protons and electrons, so that its net charge is zero."}},{"term":{"af":"Laai deur wrywing","en":"Charging by friction"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer twee verskillende materiale teen mekaar gevryf word en elektrone van die een na die ander oorgedra word; die een word negatief en die ander ewe veel positief.","en":"When two different materials are rubbed together and electrons are transferred from one to the other; one becomes negative and the other equally positive."}},{"term":{"af":"Beginsel van behoud van lading","en":"Principle of conservation of charge"},"def":{"af":"Die netto lading van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant gedurende enige fisiese proses.","en":"The net charge of an isolated system remains constant during any physical process."}},{"term":{"af":"Beginsel van kwantisering van lading","en":"Principle of charge quantisation"},"def":{"af":"Alle ladings in die heelal bestaan uit 'n heelgetalveelvoud van die lading op een elektron, d.w.s. Q = nqₑ.","en":"All charges in the universe consist of an integer multiple of the charge on one electron, i.e. Q = nqₑ."}},{"term":{"af":"Polarisasie","en":"Polarisation"},"def":{"af":"Die skeiding of herrangskikking van lading binne 'n neutrale voorwerp (of molekuul) as gevolg van 'n gelaaide voorwerp naby.","en":"The separation or rearrangement of charge within a neutral object (or molecule) due to a nearby charged object."}},{"term":{"af":"Geleier","en":"Conductor"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone vrylik kan beweeg, bv. koper en aluminium.","en":"A material in which electrons can move freely, e.g. copper and aluminium."}},{"term":{"af":"Isolator","en":"Insulator"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone nie vrylik kan beweeg nie, bv. plastiek, glas en rubber.","en":"A material in which electrons cannot move freely, e.g. plastic, glass and rubber."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Ballon teen jou hare","en":"Balloon against your hair"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho vryf 'n ballon teen sy hare. Die ballon kry 'n lading van −4,8 nC. (a) Watter deeltjies is oorgedra, en in watter rigting? (b) Wat is die lading op sy hare? (c) Hoeveel elektrone is oorgedra?","en":"Sipho rubs a balloon against his hair. The balloon gets a charge of −4.8 nC. (a) Which particles were transferred, and in which direction? (b) What is the charge on his hair? (c) How many electrons were transferred?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die ballon is negatief, dus het dit elektrone bygekry. Elektrone is van die hare na die ballon oorgedra; protone beweeg nie.","en":"(a) The balloon is negative, so it gained electrons. Electrons were transferred from the hair to the balloon; protons do not move."},{"af":"(b) Behoud van lading: voor die vryf was die totale lading 0. Ná die vryf: Q_{ballon} + Q_{hare} = 0, dus Q_{hare} = +4,8 nC.","en":"(b) Conservation of charge: before rubbing the total charge was 0. After rubbing: Q_{balloon} + Q_{hair} = 0, so Q_{hair} = +4.8 nC."},{"af":"(c) Q = nq_{e}, dus n = Q ÷ q_{e} = (−4,8 × 10^{−9}) ÷ (−1,6 × 10^{−19})","en":"(c) Q = nq_{e}, so n = Q ÷ q_{e} = (−4.8 × 10^{−9}) ÷ (−1.6 × 10^{−19})"},{"af":"n = 3 × 10^{10} elektrone","en":"n = 3 × 10^{10} electrons"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Elektrone, van die hare na die ballon. (b) +4,8 nC (c) 3 × 10¹⁰ elektrone","en":"(a) Electrons, from the hair to the balloon. (b) +4.8 nC (c) 3 × 10¹⁰ electrons"}},{"title":{"af":"Twee identiese sfere raak aan mekaar","en":"Two identical spheres touch"},"problem":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere op geïsoleerde staanders dra ladings van Q_A = −3 μC en Q_B = +9 μC. Hulle raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Bereken (a) die nuwe lading op elke sfeer en (b) die aantal elektrone wat oorgedra is, en sê in watter rigting.","en":"Two identical metal spheres on insulated stands carry charges of Q_A = −3 μC and Q_B = +9 μC. They touch and are then separated. Calculate (a) the new charge on each sphere and (b) the number of electrons transferred, and state in which direction."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Q_{nuut} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]] = [[(−3) + 9/2]] = +3 μC op elke sfeer.","en":"(a) Q_{new} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]] = [[(−3) + 9/2]] = +3 μC on each sphere."},{"af":"(b) Vir sfeer A: ΔQ = Q_{nuut} − Q_{begin} = +3 − (−3) = +6 μC = 6 × 10^{−6} C. A word positiewer, dus het A elektrone verloor.","en":"(b) For sphere A: ΔQ = Q_{new} − Q_{initial} = +3 − (−3) = +6 μC = 6 × 10^{−6} C. A becomes more positive, so A lost electrons."},{"af":"n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = (6 × 10^{−6}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 3,75 × 10^{13} elektrone","en":"n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = (6 × 10^{−6}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 3.75 × 10^{13} electrons"},{"af":"Die elektrone het van A na B beweeg. Kontrole: vir B is ΔQ = +3 − 9 = −6 μC, dus het B presies soveel elektrone bygekry ✔ (behoud van lading).","en":"The electrons moved from A to B. Check: for B, ΔQ = +3 − 9 = −6 μC, so B gained exactly as many electrons ✔ (conservation of charge)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) +3 μC elk  (b) 3,75 × 10¹³ elektrone, van A na B","en":"(a) +3 μC each  (b) 3.75 × 10¹³ electrons, from A to B"}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom 'n kam papier optel","en":"Why a comb picks up paper"},"problem":{"af":"Anika trek 'n plastiekkam deur haar droë hare en hou dit naby klein stukkies papier. Die papier spring na die kam, al is die papier neutraal. Verduidelik.","en":"Anika pulls a plastic comb through her dry hair and holds it near small bits of paper. The paper jumps to the comb, even though the paper is neutral. Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Die kam word deur wrywing gelaai: dit kry elektrone van die hare by en word negatief.","en":"The comb is charged by friction: it gains electrons from the hair and becomes negative."},{"af":"Papier is 'n isolator, dus kan elektrone nie deur die papier beweeg nie. In elke molekuul word die elektronwolk egter effens weg van die kam gestoot: die molekules word gepolariseer. Die kant van die papier naaste aan die kam word effens positief en die verste kant effens negatief.","en":"Paper is an insulator, so electrons cannot move through the paper. In each molecule, however, the electron cloud is pushed slightly away from the comb: the molecules become polarised. The side of the paper nearest the comb becomes slightly positive and the far side slightly negative."},{"af":"Die positiewe kant is nader aan die kam as die negatiewe kant. Die elektrostatiese krag is sterker hoe nader die ladings is, dus is die aantrekking groter as die afstoting.","en":"The positive side is closer to the comb than the negative side. The electrostatic force is stronger the closer the charges are, so the attraction is greater than the repulsion."},{"af":"Die netto krag is aantrekking en die ligte papier spring na die kam. Die papier se netto lading bly nul.","en":"The net force is attraction and the light paper jumps to the comb. The paper's net charge stays zero."}],"answer":{"af":"Die gelaaide kam polariseer die papier; die nabye teenoorgestelde lading word sterker aangetrek as wat die verder gelyke lading afgestoot word, dus word die neutrale papier aangetrek.","en":"The charged comb polarises the paper; the nearby opposite charge is attracted more strongly than the more distant like charge is repelled, so the neutral paper is attracted."}},{"title":{"af":"Is die lading moontlik?","en":"Is the charge possible?"},"problem":{"af":"Watter van die volgende ladings is moontlik? Gee 'n rede. (a) +4,8 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (b) −6,4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (c) +2,0 × 10⁻¹⁹ C","en":"Which of the following charges are possible? Give a reason. (a) +4.8 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (b) −6.4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (c) +2.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ C"},"steps":[{"af":"Volgens die beginsel van kwantisering van lading is Q = nq_{e}, dus moet n = |Q| ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) 'n heelgetal wees.","en":"According to the principle of charge quantisation Q = nq_{e}, so n = |Q| ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) must be an integer."},{"af":"(a) n = (4,8 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 3: moontlik (die voorwerp het 3 elektrone verloor).","en":"(a) n = (4.8 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 3: possible (the object lost 3 electrons)."},{"af":"(b) n = (6,4 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 4: moontlik (4 oortollige elektrone).","en":"(b) n = (6.4 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 4: possible (4 excess electrons)."},{"af":"(c) n = (2,0 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 1,25: nie 'n heelgetal nie, dus onmoontlik. 'n Voorwerp kan nie 'n deel van 'n elektron bykry of verloor nie.","en":"(c) n = (2.0 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 1.25: not an integer, so impossible. An object cannot gain or lose part of an electron."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) en (b) is moontlik (n = 3 en n = 4); (c) is onmoontlik (n = 1,25 is nie 'n heelgetal nie).","en":"(a) and (b) are possible (n = 3 and n = 4); (c) is impossible (n = 1.25 is not an integer)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die SI-eenheid van elektriese lading?","en":"What is the SI unit of electric charge?"},"options":[{"af":"Ampère (A)","en":"Ampere (A)"},{"af":"Volt (V)","en":"Volt (V)"},{"af":"Coulomb (C)","en":"Coulomb (C)"},{"af":"Newton (N)","en":"Newton (N)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Lading word in coulomb (C) gemeet. Die ampère is die eenheid van stroom, die volt van potensiaalverskil en die newton van krag.","en":"Charge is measured in coulombs (C). The ampere is the unit of current, the volt of potential difference and the newton of force."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter deeltjies word oorgedra wanneer twee voorwerpe deur wrywing gelaai word?","en":"Which particles are transferred when two objects are charged by friction?"},"options":[{"af":"Elektrone","en":"Electrons"},{"af":"Protone","en":"Protons"},{"af":"Neutrone","en":"Neutrons"},{"af":"Atoomkerne","en":"Atomic nuclei"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Slegs elektrone kan van een voorwerp na 'n ander beweeg. Protone en neutrone sit vas in die kern van die atoom.","en":"Only electrons can move from one object to another. Protons and neutrons are fixed in the nucleus of the atom."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Voorwerp word positief gelaai wanneer dit protone bykry.","en":"An object becomes positively charged when it gains protons."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Protone beweeg nie; 'n voorwerp word positief gelaai wanneer dit elektrone verloor, sodat daar meer protone as elektrone oorbly.","en":"False. Protons do not move; an object becomes positively charged when it loses electrons, so that more protons than electrons remain."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Behoud van lading","en":"Conservation of charge"},"r":{"af":"Die netto lading van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant gedurende enige fisiese proses","en":"The net charge of an isolated system remains constant during any physical process"}},{"l":{"af":"Kwantisering van lading","en":"Charge quantisation"},"r":{"af":"Alle ladings is 'n heelgetalveelvoud van die lading op een elektron","en":"All charges are an integer multiple of the charge on one electron"}},{"l":{"af":"Polarisasie","en":"Polarisation"},"r":{"af":"Die skeiding van lading in 'n neutrale voorwerp weens 'n gelaaide voorwerp naby","en":"The separation of charge in a neutral object due to a nearby charged object"}},{"l":{"af":"Geleier","en":"Conductor"},"r":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone vrylik kan beweeg, bv. koper","en":"A material in which electrons can move freely, e.g. copper"}},{"l":{"af":"Isolator","en":"Insulator"},"r":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone nie vrylik kan beweeg nie, bv. plastiek","en":"A material in which electrons cannot move freely, e.g. plastic"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leer die twee beginsels woordeliks: behoud (die totaal bly dieselfde) en kwantisering (Q = nqₑ met n 'n heelgetal). Polarisasie verklaar waarom gelaaide voorwerpe neutrale voorwerpe aantrek.","en":"Learn the two principles word for word: conservation (the total stays the same) and quantisation (Q = nqₑ with n an integer). Polarisation explains why charged objects attract neutral objects."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Ebonietstaaf word met 'n stuk pels gevryf en kry 'n lading van −5 nC. Wat is die lading op die pels daarna? (Geen lading gaan na die omgewing verlore nie.)","en":"An ebonite rod is rubbed with a piece of fur and gets a charge of −5 nC. What is the charge on the fur afterwards? (No charge is lost to the surroundings.)"},"options":[{"af":"0 nC (die pels bly neutraal)","en":"0 nC (the fur stays neutral)"},{"af":"+5 nC","en":"+5 nC"},{"af":"−5 nC","en":"−5 nC"},{"af":"+10 nC","en":"+10 nC"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Behoud van lading: voor die vryf was die totale lading 0, dus moet dit daarna ook 0 wees: −5 nC + Q_pels = 0, dus Q_pels = +5 nC. Die elektrone wat die staaf bygekry het, het van die pels af gekom.","en":"Conservation of charge: before rubbing the total charge was 0, so afterwards it must also be 0: −5 nC + Q_fur = 0, so Q_fur = +5 nC. The electrons the rod gained came from the fur."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Gelaaide ballon kan 'n neutrale muur aantrek.","en":"A charged balloon can attract a neutral wall."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die ballon polariseer die molekules in die muur: die kant naaste aan die ballon kry 'n effense teenoorgestelde lading, en omdat dit nader is, is die aantrekking sterker as die afstoting.","en":"True. The balloon polarises the molecules in the wall: the side nearest the balloon gets a slight opposite charge, and because it is closer, the attraction is stronger than the repulsion."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Negatief gelaaide plastiekstaaf word naby (sonder om te raak) 'n klein, neutrale aluminiumfoeliebal gebring wat aan 'n draad hang. Wat gebeur, en waarom?","en":"A negatively charged plastic rod is brought near (without touching) a small, neutral aluminium-foil ball hanging from a thread. What happens, and why?"},"options":[{"af":"Die bal word afgestoot, want dit word negatief gelaai.","en":"The ball is repelled, because it becomes negatively charged."},{"af":"Niks gebeur nie, want die bal is neutraal.","en":"Nothing happens, because the ball is neutral."},{"af":"Die bal word aangetrek, want protone vloei van die staaf na die bal.","en":"The ball is attracted, because protons flow from the rod to the ball."},{"af":"Die bal word aangetrek: elektrone in die bal word na die verste kant afgestoot, sodat die naaste kant positief is en sterker aangetrek word as wat die verder negatiewe kant afgestoot word.","en":"The ball is attracted: electrons in the ball are repelled to the far side, so the near side is positive and is attracted more strongly than the more distant negative side is repelled."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Aluminium is 'n geleier: die vrye elektrone beweeg weg van die negatiewe staaf. Die lading word geskei (polarisasie), maar die bal bly neutraal. Die nabye positiewe kant word sterker aangetrek as wat die verder negatiewe kant afgestoot word, dus word die bal aangetrek. Protone beweeg nie, en die staaf raak nie die bal nie.","en":"Aluminium is a conductor: the free electrons move away from the negative rod. The charge is separated (polarisation), but the ball stays neutral. The near positive side is attracted more strongly than the more distant negative side is repelled, so the ball is attracted. Protons do not move, and the rod does not touch the ball."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Voorwerp het 'n lading van −8 × 10⁻¹⁸ C. Hoeveel oortollige elektrone het die voorwerp? ___","en":"An object has a charge of −8 × 10⁻¹⁸ C. How many excess electrons does the object have? ___"},"answers":{"af":["50","50 elektrone","vyftig"],"en":["50","50 electrons","fifty"]},"explain":{"af":"Q = nqₑ, dus n = Q ÷ qₑ = (−8 × 10⁻¹⁸) ÷ (−1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 50 elektrone.","en":"Q = nqₑ, so n = Q ÷ qₑ = (−8 × 10⁻¹⁸) ÷ (−1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 50 electrons."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere met ladings van +8 nC en −2 nC raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Wat is die lading op elke sfeer?","en":"Two identical metal spheres with charges of +8 nC and −2 nC touch and are then separated. What is the charge on each sphere?"},"options":[{"af":"+5 nC","en":"+5 nC"},{"af":"+3 nC","en":"+3 nC"},{"af":"+6 nC","en":"+6 nC"},{"af":"−3 nC","en":"−3 nC"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Q_nuut = (Q₁ + Q₂)/2 = (8 + (−2))/2 = +3 nC. +5 nC kry jy as jy die teken van −2 ignoreer, +6 nC as jy vergeet om deur 2 te deel, en −3 nC het die verkeerde teken, want die totale lading (+6 nC) is positief.","en":"Q_new = (Q₁ + Q₂)/2 = (8 + (−2))/2 = +3 nC. You get +5 nC if you ignore the sign of −2, +6 nC if you forget to divide by 2, and −3 nC has the wrong sign, because the total charge (+6 nC) is positive."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Glasstaaf verloor 5 × 10¹⁰ elektrone wanneer dit met sy gevryf word. Wat is die lading op die glasstaaf? Q = ___ × 10⁻⁹ C","en":"A glass rod loses 5 × 10¹⁰ electrons when it is rubbed with silk. What is the charge on the glass rod? Q = ___ × 10⁻⁹ C"},"answers":{"af":["+8","8","+8,00","8,00","+8.00","8.00","+8 × 10⁻⁹","+8 × 10⁻⁹ C","8 × 10⁻⁹ C","+8 nC","8 nC","+8e-9","8e-9"],"en":["+8","8","+8.00","8.00","+8,00","8,00","+8 × 10⁻⁹","+8 × 10⁻⁹ C","8 × 10⁻⁹ C","+8 nC","8 nC","+8e-9","8e-9"]},"explain":{"af":"Die staaf verloor elektrone, dus is sy lading positief. Q = n × 1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = (5 × 10¹⁰)(1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = +8 × 10⁻⁹ C (+8 nC).","en":"The rod loses electrons, so its charge is positive. Q = n × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = (5 × 10¹⁰)(1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = +8 × 10⁻⁹ C (+8 nC)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere, A (−6 nC) en B (+2 nC), raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Hoeveel elektrone is van A na B oorgedra? ___ × 10¹⁰","en":"Two identical metal spheres, A (−6 nC) and B (+2 nC), touch and are then separated. How many electrons were transferred from A to B? ___ × 10¹⁰"},"answers":{"af":["2,5","2.5","2,50","2.50","2,5 × 10¹⁰","2.5 × 10¹⁰","2,5 x 10^10","2.5 x 10^10","2.5e10"],"en":["2.5","2,5","2.50","2,50","2.5 × 10¹⁰","2,5 × 10¹⁰","2.5 x 10^10","2,5 x 10^10","2.5e10"]},"explain":{"af":"Q_nuut = (−6 + 2)/2 = −2 nC. Vir A: ΔQ = −2 − (−6) = +4 nC = 4 × 10⁻⁹ C (A het elektrone verloor). n = (4 × 10⁻⁹) ÷ (1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2,5 × 10¹⁰ elektrone.","en":"Q_new = (−6 + 2)/2 = −2 nC. For A: ΔQ = −2 − (−6) = +4 nC = 4 × 10⁻⁹ C (A lost electrons). n = (4 × 10⁻⁹) ÷ (1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2.5 × 10¹⁰ electrons."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere, P (+4 μC) en Q (−8 μC), raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Watter stelling beskryf die ladingsoordrag korrek?","en":"Two identical metal spheres, P (+4 μC) and Q (−8 μC), touch and are then separated. Which statement describes the charge transfer correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Protone beweeg van P na Q.","en":"Protons move from P to Q."},{"af":"Elektrone beweeg van P na Q.","en":"Electrons move from P to Q."},{"af":"Elektrone beweeg van Q na P.","en":"Electrons move from Q to P."},{"af":"Geen lading word oorgedra nie, want die totale lading bly behoue.","en":"No charge is transferred, because the total charge is conserved."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Elkeen kry (4 + (−8))/2 = −2 μC. P verander van +4 μC na −2 μC: dit word negatiewer, dus het P elektrone bygekry, en dié het van Q af gekom. Protone beweeg nie. Behoud van lading beteken die totaal bly −4 μC, nie dat niks beweeg nie.","en":"Each gets (4 + (−8))/2 = −2 μC. P changes from +4 μC to −2 μC: it becomes more negative, so P gained electrons, and they came from Q. Protons do not move. Conservation of charge means the total stays −4 μC, not that nothing moves."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Drie identiese metaalsfere dra ladings van A = +9 nC, B = −3 nC en C = +5 nC. A raak aan B en hulle word geskei. Daarna raak B aan C en hulle word geskei. Wat is die finale lading op C? ___ nC","en":"Three identical metal spheres carry charges of A = +9 nC, B = −3 nC and C = +5 nC. A touches B and they are separated. Then B touches C and they are separated. What is the final charge on C? ___ nC"},"answers":{"af":["+4","+4 nC","4","4 nC","4,00","4,00 nC","4.00","4.00 nC"],"en":["+4","+4 nC","4","4 nC","4,00","4,00 nC","4.00","4.00 nC"]},"explain":{"af":"Stap 1: A en B: (9 + (−3))/2 = +3 nC elk. Stap 2: B (nou +3 nC) en C: (3 + 5)/2 = +4 nC elk. Gebruik altyd B se NUWE lading in die tweede stap.","en":"Step 1: A and B: (9 + (−3))/2 = +3 nC each. Step 2: B (now +3 nC) and C: (3 + 5)/2 = +4 nC each. Always use B's NEW charge in the second step."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato meet die lading op 'n klein oliedruppel en rapporteer 2,4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C. Watter stelling evalueer haar resultaat die beste?","en":"Lerato measures the charge on a small oil drop and reports 2.4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C. Which statement evaluates her result best?"},"options":[{"af":"Die resultaat is onmoontlik: (2,4 × 10⁻¹⁹) ÷ (1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 1,5, en 'n voorwerp kan nie 'n halwe elektron bykry of verloor nie; die meting moet foutief wees.","en":"The result is impossible: (2.4 × 10⁻¹⁹) ÷ (1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 1.5, and an object cannot gain or lose half an electron; the measurement must be wrong."},{"af":"Die resultaat is moontlik, want lading kan enige waarde hê.","en":"The result is possible, because charge can have any value."},{"af":"Die resultaat is moontlik, want 2,4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C is groter as die lading op een elektron.","en":"The result is possible, because 2.4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C is larger than the charge on one electron."},{"af":"Die resultaat is onmoontlik, want 'n lading moet altyd negatief wees.","en":"The result is impossible, because a charge must always be negative."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Volgens die beginsel van kwantisering van lading is Q = nqₑ met n 'n heelgetal. Hier is n = 1,5, dus kan die lading nie bestaan nie. Lading kan nie enige waarde hê nie, dit kan positief of negatief wees, en om groter as qₑ te wees, is nie genoeg nie: dit moet 'n heelgetalveelvoud wees.","en":"According to the principle of charge quantisation Q = nqₑ with n an integer. Here n = 1.5, so the charge cannot exist. Charge cannot have any value, it can be positive or negative, and being larger than qₑ is not enough: it must be an integer multiple."}}]},{"id":"f10-t2-elektriese-stroombane","title":{"af":"Elektriese stroombane","en":"Electric circuits"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal emk, potensiaalverskil, stroom en weerstand kan definieer en die ekwivalente weerstand, strome en spannings in serie-, parallel- en kombinasiestroombane kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to define emf, potential difference, current and resistance, and calculate the equivalent resistance, currents and voltages in series, parallel and combination circuits."},"summary":{"af":"## Potensiaalverskil en emk\n\n- **Potensiaalverskil (V)** is die arbeid verrig (of energie oorgedra) per eenheid positiewe lading wat tussen twee punte beweeg: V = [[W/Q]]. Eenheid: **volt (V)**; 1 V = 1 J·C^{−1}.\n- **Emk (ε)** is die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van 'n battery wanneer **geen stroom** deur die battery vloei nie. Dit is die maksimum energie wat die battery per coulomb lading verskaf.\n- **Terminale potensiaalverskil** is die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van die battery wanneer stroom **wel** vloei. Dit is effens kleiner as die emk, want 'n bietjie energie word binne-in die battery self in hitte omgeskakel.\n\n> **Wenk:** 'n Voltmeter oor die pole van die battery lees die **emk** as die skakelaar **oop** is, en die **terminale potensiaalverskil** as die skakelaar **toe** is.\n\n**Selle in serie:** Die positiewe pool van een sel word aan die negatiewe pool van die volgende gekoppel, en hulle emk'e **tel op**. Drie 1,5 V-selle in 'n flits gee 3 × 1,5 = 4,5 V. Identiese selle in **parallel** gee dieselfde emk as een sel, maar hou langer.\n\n## Stroom\n\n**Stroom (I)** is die tempo van vloei van lading: I = [[Q/Δt]]. Eenheid: **ampère (A)**; 1 A = 1 C·s^{−1}.\n\n- **Konvensionele stroom** vloei in die eksterne stroombaan van die **positiewe** pool na die **negatiewe** pool. Elektrone vloei in die teenoorgestelde rigting.\n- Die aantal elektrone wat verbybeweeg: n = [[Q/e]], met e = 1,6 × 10^{−19} C.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Δt moet in **sekondes** wees: 2 min = 120 s en 1 h = 3 600 s.\n\n## Weerstand\n\n**Weerstand (R)** is die teenstand teen die vloei van elektriese stroom. Dit is die verhouding van die potensiaalverskil oor 'n resistor tot die stroom daardeur: R = [[V/I]]. Eenheid: **ohm (Ω)**; 1 Ω = 1 V·A^{−1}.\n\n**Hoekom is daar weerstand?** Elektrone wat deur 'n metaal beweeg, bots met die metaalatome (positiewe ione) en dra van hulle kinetiese energie aan die atome oor. Daarom word 'n ketel se element warm en gloei 'n gloeilamp se filament.\n\n| Faktor | Effek op die weerstand van 'n metaaldraad |\n|---|---|\n| Langer draad | R neem toe (meer botsings) |\n| Dikker draad (groter deursnee-oppervlakte) | R neem af (meer ruimte vir elektrone) |\n| Hoër temperatuur | R neem toe (atome vibreer meer) |\n| Tipe materiaal | bv. koper het 'n baie laer R as nichroom |\n\n**'n Battery word pap** omdat sy chemiese potensiële energie na elektriese energie omgeskakel word, wat in die resistors na hitte en lig omgeskakel word. As die chemikalieë opgebruik is, kan dit nie meer energie aan die ladings gee nie.\n\n### Ohm se wet\n\n*Die potensiaalverskil oor 'n geleier is direk eweredig aan die stroom in die geleier by konstante temperatuur.* Dus is [[V/I]] = R konstant. 'n Grafiek van V (y-as) teenoor I (x-as) vir 'n ohmiese geleier is 'n reguit lyn deur die oorsprong; die gradiënt is R.\n\n## Meters\n\n- **Ammeter** – meet stroom; word in **serie** gekoppel; het 'n baie **lae** weerstand (ideaal nul), sodat dit die stroom nie verander nie.\n- **Voltmeter** – meet potensiaalverskil; word in **parallel** oor die komponent gekoppel; het 'n baie **hoë** weerstand (ideaal oneindig), sodat feitlik geen stroom daardeur vloei nie.\n\n## Resistors in serie en in parallel\n\n| | Serie (een pad) | Parallel (aparte takke) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stroom | dieselfde deur elke resistor: I_{T} = I_{1} = I_{2} | verdeel: I_{T} = I_{1} + I_{2} + I_{3} |\n| Potensiaalverskil | verdeel: V_{T} = V_{1} + V_{2} + V_{3} | dieselfde oor elke tak: V_{T} = V_{1} = V_{2} |\n| Ekwivalente weerstand | R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} | [[1/Rₚ]] = [[1/R₁]] + [[1/R₂]] + [[1/R₃]] |\n| Bynaam | spanningsverdeler | stroomverdeler |\n\n- In serie kry die **grootste** resistor die **grootste** deel van die potensiaalverskil.\n- In parallel vloei die **grootste** stroom deur die **kleinste** weerstand.\n- Vir **twee** resistors in parallel: R_{p} = [[R₁R₂/R₁ + R₂]] (produk oor som).\n- R_{p} is altyd **kleiner as die kleinste** resistor in die kombinasie. Hoe meer resistors in parallel, hoe kleiner die totale weerstand, want daar is meer paaie vir die stroom – soos 'n dikker draad.\n- Huisbedrading is in parallel: elke toestel kry die volle spanning, en as een lamp uitbrand, werk die res steeds.\n\n## Metode vir 'n kombinasiestroombaan\n\n1. Bereken R_{p} van die parallelle deel.\n2. Totale weerstand: R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p}.\n3. Hoofstroom: I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}.\n4. Potensiaalverskil oor die serie-resistor: V = I_{T} × R. Dan is V_{p} = V_{T} − V_{serie}.\n5. Takstroom: I = V_{p} ÷ R vir elke tak. Kontroleer dat die takstrome optel tot I_{T}.\n\n### Wat gebeur as ...? (battery met weglaatbare interne weerstand)\n\nRedeneer altyd in hierdie volgorde: R_{T} verander → I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} verander → V oor die serie-resistor verander → V oor die parallelle deel verander.\n\n- 'n Resistor word **in parallel bygevoeg** → R_{T} neem af → I_{T} neem toe.\n- 'n Tak word **verwyder** (bv. 'n gloeilamp brand uit) → R_{T} neem toe → I_{T} neem af.\n- 'n Gloeilamp brand helderder as die stroom deur hom (en die potensiaalverskil oor hom) groter is.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** [[1/Rₚ]] nie omkeer na R_{p} nie; parallelle resistors sommer optel; die battery se volle spanning oor een resistor in 'n serie-stroombaan gebruik.","en":"## Potential difference and emf\n\n- **Potential difference (V)** is the work done (or energy transferred) per unit positive charge moving between two points: V = [[W/Q]]. Unit: **volt (V)**; 1 V = 1 J·C^{−1}.\n- **Emf (ε)** is the potential difference across the terminals of a battery when **no current** flows through the battery. It is the maximum energy the battery provides per coulomb of charge.\n- **Terminal potential difference** is the potential difference across the terminals of the battery when current **does** flow. It is slightly less than the emf, because a little energy is converted to heat inside the battery itself.\n\n> **Tip:** A voltmeter across the battery terminals reads the **emf** when the switch is **open**, and the **terminal potential difference** when the switch is **closed**.\n\n**Cells in series:** The positive terminal of one cell is connected to the negative terminal of the next, and their emfs **add up**. Three 1.5 V cells in a torch give 3 × 1.5 = 4.5 V. Identical cells in **parallel** give the same emf as one cell, but last longer.\n\n## Current\n\n**Current (I)** is the rate of flow of charge: I = [[Q/Δt]]. Unit: **ampere (A)**; 1 A = 1 C·s^{−1}.\n\n- **Conventional current** flows in the external circuit from the **positive** terminal to the **negative** terminal. Electrons flow in the opposite direction.\n- The number of electrons passing: n = [[Q/e]], with e = 1.6 × 10^{−19} C.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Δt must be in **seconds**: 2 min = 120 s and 1 h = 3 600 s.\n\n## Resistance\n\n**Resistance (R)** is the opposition to the flow of electric current. It is the ratio of the potential difference across a resistor to the current through it: R = [[V/I]]. Unit: **ohm (Ω)**; 1 Ω = 1 V·A^{−1}.\n\n**Why is there resistance?** Electrons moving through a metal collide with the metal atoms (positive ions) and transfer some of their kinetic energy to the atoms. That is why a kettle's element gets hot and a light bulb's filament glows.\n\n| Factor | Effect on the resistance of a metal wire |\n|---|---|\n| Longer wire | R increases (more collisions) |\n| Thicker wire (larger cross-sectional area) | R decreases (more room for electrons) |\n| Higher temperature | R increases (atoms vibrate more) |\n| Type of material | e.g. copper has a much lower R than nichrome |\n\n**A battery goes flat** because its chemical potential energy is converted to electrical energy, which is converted to heat and light in the resistors. When the chemicals are used up, it can no longer give energy to the charges.\n\n### Ohm's law\n\n*The potential difference across a conductor is directly proportional to the current in the conductor at constant temperature.* So [[V/I]] = R is constant. A graph of V (y-axis) against I (x-axis) for an ohmic conductor is a straight line through the origin; the gradient is R.\n\n## Meters\n\n- **Ammeter** – measures current; connected in **series**; has a very **low** resistance (ideally zero) so that it does not change the current.\n- **Voltmeter** – measures potential difference; connected in **parallel** across the component; has a very **high** resistance (ideally infinite) so that almost no current flows through it.\n\n## Resistors in series and in parallel\n\n| | Series (one path) | Parallel (separate branches) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Current | the same through each resistor: I_{T} = I_{1} = I_{2} | divides: I_{T} = I_{1} + I_{2} + I_{3} |\n| Potential difference | divides: V_{T} = V_{1} + V_{2} + V_{3} | the same across each branch: V_{T} = V_{1} = V_{2} |\n| Equivalent resistance | R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} | [[1/Rₚ]] = [[1/R₁]] + [[1/R₂]] + [[1/R₃]] |\n| Also called | voltage divider | current divider |\n\n- In series the **largest** resistor gets the **largest** share of the potential difference.\n- In parallel the **largest** current flows through the **smallest** resistance.\n- For **two** resistors in parallel: R_{p} = [[R₁R₂/R₁ + R₂]] (product over sum).\n- R_{p} is always **smaller than the smallest** resistor in the combination. The more resistors in parallel, the smaller the total resistance, because there are more paths for the current – like a thicker wire.\n- House wiring is in parallel: every appliance gets the full voltage, and if one lamp blows, the rest still work.\n\n## Method for a combination circuit\n\n1. Calculate R_{p} of the parallel section.\n2. Total resistance: R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p}.\n3. Main current: I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}.\n4. Potential difference across the series resistor: V = I_{T} × R. Then V_{p} = V_{T} − V_{series}.\n5. Branch current: I = V_{p} ÷ R for each branch. Check that the branch currents add up to I_{T}.\n\n### What happens if ...? (battery with negligible internal resistance)\n\nAlways reason in this order: R_{T} changes → I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} changes → V across the series resistor changes → V across the parallel section changes.\n\n- A resistor is **added in parallel** → R_{T} decreases → I_{T} increases.\n- A branch is **removed** (e.g. a bulb blows) → R_{T} increases → I_{T} decreases.\n- A bulb glows brighter when the current through it (and the potential difference across it) is larger.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** not inverting [[1/Rₚ]] to get R_{p}; simply adding parallel resistors; using the battery's full voltage across one resistor in a series circuit."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Emk (ε)","en":"Emf (ε)"},"def":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van 'n battery wanneer geen stroom deur die battery vloei nie; die maksimum energie wat die battery per coulomb lading verskaf.","en":"The potential difference across the terminals of a battery when no current flows through the battery; the maximum energy the battery provides per coulomb of charge."}},{"term":{"af":"Terminale potensiaalverskil","en":"Terminal potential difference"},"def":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van 'n battery wanneer stroom in die stroombaan vloei. Dit is kleiner as die emk.","en":"The potential difference across the terminals of a battery when current flows in the circuit. It is less than the emf."}},{"term":{"af":"Potensiaalverskil (V)","en":"Potential difference (V)"},"def":{"af":"Die arbeid verrig (energie oorgedra) per eenheid positiewe lading tussen twee punte: V = W/Q. Eenheid: volt (V).","en":"The work done (energy transferred) per unit positive charge between two points: V = W/Q. Unit: volt (V)."}},{"term":{"af":"Stroom (I)","en":"Current (I)"},"def":{"af":"Die tempo van vloei van lading: I = Q/Δt. Eenheid: ampère (A); 1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹.","en":"The rate of flow of charge: I = Q/Δt. Unit: ampere (A); 1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Weerstand (R)","en":"Resistance (R)"},"def":{"af":"Die teenstand teen die vloei van elektriese stroom; die verhouding R = V/I. Eenheid: ohm (Ω); 1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹.","en":"The opposition to the flow of electric current; the ratio R = V/I. Unit: ohm (Ω); 1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Ohm se wet","en":"Ohm's law"},"def":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor 'n geleier is direk eweredig aan die stroom in die geleier by konstante temperatuur.","en":"The potential difference across a conductor is directly proportional to the current in the conductor at constant temperature."}},{"term":{"af":"Ekwivalente weerstand","en":"Equivalent resistance"},"def":{"af":"Die enkele weerstand wat 'n kombinasie van resistors kan vervang en by dieselfde potensiaalverskil dieselfde stroom sal deurlaat.","en":"The single resistance that can replace a combination of resistors and will allow the same current at the same potential difference."}},{"term":{"af":"Ammeter","en":"Ammeter"},"def":{"af":"'n Instrument wat stroom meet. Dit word in serie gekoppel en het 'n baie lae weerstand.","en":"An instrument that measures current. It is connected in series and has a very low resistance."}},{"term":{"af":"Voltmeter","en":"Voltmeter"},"def":{"af":"'n Instrument wat potensiaalverskil meet. Dit word in parallel oor 'n komponent gekoppel en het 'n baie hoë weerstand.","en":"An instrument that measures potential difference. It is connected in parallel across a component and has a very high resistance."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lading, stroom en aantal elektrone","en":"Charge, current and number of electrons"},"problem":{"af":"Tydens beurtkrag laai jy jou foon met 'n kragbank. Die kragbank lewer 'n konstante stroom van 2 A vir 30 minute. Bereken (a) die lading wat gevloei het en (b) die aantal elektrone wat gevloei het.","en":"During load-shedding you charge your phone with a power bank. The power bank delivers a constant current of 2 A for 30 minutes. Calculate (a) the charge that flowed and (b) the number of electrons that flowed."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel eers die tyd na sekondes om: Δt = 30 × 60 = 1 800 s.","en":"First convert the time to seconds: Δt = 30 × 60 = 1 800 s."},{"af":"(a) I = [[Q/Δt]], dus Q = IΔt = 2 × 1 800 = 3 600 C.","en":"(a) I = [[Q/Δt]], so Q = IΔt = 2 × 1 800 = 3 600 C."},{"af":"(b) Elke elektron dra 'n lading van 1,6 × 10^{−19} C: n = [[Q/e]] = 3 600 ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19})","en":"(b) Each electron carries a charge of 1.6 × 10^{−19} C: n = [[Q/e]] = 3 600 ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19})"},{"af":"n = 2,25 × 10^{22} elektrone","en":"n = 2.25 × 10^{22} electrons"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Q = 3 600 C; (b) n = 2,25 × 10²² elektrone","en":"(a) Q = 3 600 C; (b) n = 2.25 × 10²² electrons"}},{"title":{"af":"Resistors in serie","en":"Resistors in series"},"problem":{"af":"'n Battery met 'n emk van 12 V en weglaatbare interne weerstand is in serie gekoppel met drie resistors van 2 Ω, 4 Ω en 6 Ω. 'n Ammeter is in serie in die stroombaan en 'n voltmeter is oor die 6 Ω-resistor gekoppel. Bereken (a) die ekwivalente weerstand, (b) die ammeterlesing en (c) die voltmeterlesing.","en":"A battery with an emf of 12 V and negligible internal resistance is connected in series with three resistors of 2 Ω, 4 Ω and 6 Ω. An ammeter is in series in the circuit and a voltmeter is connected across the 6 Ω resistor. Calculate (a) the equivalent resistance, (b) the ammeter reading and (c) the voltmeter reading."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) In serie tel weerstande op: R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} = 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 Ω","en":"(a) In series resistances add up: R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} = 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 Ω"},{"af":"(b) R = [[V/I]], dus I = V ÷ R = 12 ÷ 12 = 1 A. In serie is die stroom oral dieselfde, so die ammeter lees 1 A.","en":"(b) R = [[V/I]], so I = V ÷ R = 12 ÷ 12 = 1 A. In series the current is the same everywhere, so the ammeter reads 1 A."},{"af":"(c) V = IR = 1 × 6 = 6 V oor die 6 Ω-resistor.","en":"(c) V = IR = 1 × 6 = 6 V across the 6 Ω resistor."},{"af":"Kontroleer: V oor 2 Ω = 2 V en oor 4 Ω = 4 V. 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 V = emk ✓ – 'n serie-stroombaan is 'n spanningsverdeler, en die grootste resistor kry die grootste deel.","en":"Check: V across 2 Ω = 2 V and across 4 Ω = 4 V. 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 V = emf ✓ – a series circuit is a voltage divider, and the largest resistor gets the largest share."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 12 Ω; (b) 1 A; (c) 6 V","en":"(a) 12 Ω; (b) 1 A; (c) 6 V"}},{"title":{"af":"Kombinasiestroombaan","en":"Combination circuit"},"problem":{"af":"'n Battery met 'n emk van 12 V en weglaatbare interne weerstand is gekoppel aan 'n 4 Ω-resistor in serie met 'n parallelle kombinasie van 'n 6 Ω- en 'n 3 Ω-resistor. Bereken (a) die totale weerstand, (b) die stroom deur die battery, (c) die potensiaalverskil oor die parallelle kombinasie en (d) die stroom deur die 6 Ω-resistor.","en":"A battery with an emf of 12 V and negligible internal resistance is connected to a 4 Ω resistor in series with a parallel combination of a 6 Ω and a 3 Ω resistor. Calculate (a) the total resistance, (b) the current through the battery, (c) the potential difference across the parallel combination and (d) the current through the 6 Ω resistor."},"steps":[{"af":"Parallelle deel eerste (produk oor som): R_{p} = [[6 × 3/6 + 3]] = [[18/9]] = 2 Ω","en":"Parallel section first (product over sum): R_{p} = [[6 × 3/6 + 3]] = [[18/9]] = 2 Ω"},{"af":"(a) R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p} = 4 + 2 = 6 Ω","en":"(a) R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p} = 4 + 2 = 6 Ω"},{"af":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} = 12 ÷ 6 = 2 A","en":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} = 12 ÷ 6 = 2 A"},{"af":"(c) V oor die 4 Ω-resistor = I_{T}R = 2 × 4 = 8 V. Dus V_{p} = 12 − 8 = 4 V (of V_{p} = I_{T}R_{p} = 2 × 2 = 4 V).","en":"(c) V across the 4 Ω resistor = I_{T}R = 2 × 4 = 8 V. So V_{p} = 12 − 8 = 4 V (or V_{p} = I_{T}R_{p} = 2 × 2 = 4 V)."},{"af":"(d) I_{6Ω} = V_{p} ÷ R = 4 ÷ 6 = 0,67 A. Kontroleer: I_{3Ω} = 4 ÷ 3 = 1,33 A en 0,67 + 1,33 = 2,00 A = I_{T} ✓","en":"(d) I_{6Ω} = V_{p} ÷ R = 4 ÷ 6 = 0.67 A. Check: I_{3Ω} = 4 ÷ 3 = 1.33 A and 0.67 + 1.33 = 2.00 A = I_{T} ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 6 Ω; (b) 2 A; (c) 4 V; (d) 0,67 A","en":"(a) 6 Ω; (b) 2 A; (c) 4 V; (d) 0.67 A"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik: 'n ekstra gloeilamp in parallel","en":"Explain: an extra bulb in parallel"},"problem":{"af":"Twee identiese gloeilampe is in parallel aan 'n battery met weglaatbare interne weerstand gekoppel. 'n Ammeter is in serie met die battery. 'n Derde identiese gloeilamp word in parallel bygevoeg. Wat gebeur met (a) die totale weerstand, (b) die ammeterlesing en (c) die helderheid van die oorspronklike twee gloeilampe? Verduidelik.","en":"Two identical bulbs are connected in parallel to a battery with negligible internal resistance. An ammeter is in series with the battery. A third identical bulb is added in parallel. What happens to (a) the total resistance, (b) the ammeter reading and (c) the brightness of the original two bulbs? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n Ekstra tak gee 'n ekstra pad vir die stroom, dus neem die totale weerstand **af**. As elke gloeilamp 'n weerstand R het, daal R_{p} van [[R/2]] na [[R/3]].","en":"(a) An extra branch gives an extra path for the current, so the total resistance **decreases**. If each bulb has resistance R, R_{p} drops from [[R/2]] to [[R/3]]."},{"af":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}. Die battery se potensiaalverskil bly dieselfde en R_{T} neem af, dus neem die ammeterlesing **toe** (dit word 1,5 keer groter).","en":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}. The battery's potential difference stays the same and R_{T} decreases, so the ammeter reading **increases** (it becomes 1.5 times larger)."},{"af":"(c) Elke gloeilamp is direk oor die battery gekoppel, dus bly die potensiaalverskil oor elkeen V. Die stroom deur elkeen, I = V ÷ R, bly dieselfde, so die helderheid **bly dieselfde**.","en":"(c) Each bulb is connected directly across the battery, so the potential difference across each stays V. The current through each, I = V ÷ R, stays the same, so the brightness **stays the same**."},{"af":"Daarom word huise in parallel bedraad: as jy 'n ekstra lamp aanskakel, word die ander nie dowwer nie – maar die totale stroom uit die battery of omsetter neem toe.","en":"That is why houses are wired in parallel: switching on an extra lamp does not make the others dimmer – but the total current from the battery or inverter increases."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Neem af; (b) neem toe; (c) bly dieselfde","en":"(a) Decreases; (b) increases; (c) stays the same"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die definisie van elektriese stroom?","en":"Which statement is the definition of electric current?"},"options":[{"af":"Die arbeid verrig per eenheid positiewe lading","en":"The work done per unit positive charge"},{"af":"Die tempo van vloei van lading","en":"The rate of flow of charge"},{"af":"Die teenstand teen die vloei van lading","en":"The opposition to the flow of charge"},{"af":"Die totale hoeveelheid lading wat deur 'n geleier vloei","en":"The total amount of charge that flows through a conductor"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Stroom is die tempo van vloei van lading: I = Q/Δt. Die eerste opsie beskryf potensiaalverskil, die derde beskryf weerstand en die laaste is net lading (Q) – stroom gaan oor hoeveel lading per sekonde vloei.","en":"Current is the rate of flow of charge: I = Q/Δt. The first option describes potential difference, the third describes resistance and the last is just charge (Q) – current is about how much charge flows per second."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke grootheid by sy SI-eenheid.","en":"Match each quantity to its SI unit."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Stroom","en":"Current"},"r":{"af":"ampère (A)","en":"ampere (A)"}},{"l":{"af":"Potensiaalverskil","en":"Potential difference"},"r":{"af":"volt (V)","en":"volt (V)"}},{"l":{"af":"Weerstand","en":"Resistance"},"r":{"af":"ohm (Ω)","en":"ohm (Ω)"}},{"l":{"af":"Lading","en":"Charge"},"r":{"af":"coulomb (C)","en":"coulomb (C)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Stroom: ampère (1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹); potensiaalverskil: volt (1 V = 1 J·C⁻¹); weerstand: ohm (1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹); lading: coulomb.","en":"Current: ampere (1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹); potential difference: volt (1 V = 1 J·C⁻¹); resistance: ohm (1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹); charge: coulomb."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om die stroom deur 'n resistor te meet, word 'n ammeter in parallel met die resistor gekoppel.","en":"To measure the current through a resistor, an ammeter is connected in parallel with the resistor."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Ammeter word in serie gekoppel sodat dieselfde stroom deur die ammeter en die resistor vloei. Die voltmeter is die meter wat in parallel gekoppel word.","en":"False. An ammeter is connected in series so that the same current flows through the ammeter and the resistor. The voltmeter is the meter that is connected in parallel."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Drie verskillende resistors is in serie aan 'n battery gekoppel. Watter stelling is korrek?","en":"Three different resistors are connected in series to a battery. Which statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor elke resistor is dieselfde.","en":"The potential difference across each resistor is the same."},{"af":"Die totale weerstand is kleiner as die kleinste resistor.","en":"The total resistance is smaller than the smallest resistor."},{"af":"Die stroom deur elke resistor is dieselfde.","en":"The current through each resistor is the same."},{"af":"Die stroom verdeel tussen die resistors.","en":"The current divides between the resistors."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In serie is daar net een pad, dus is die stroom oral dieselfde. Die potensiaalverskil verdeel (die grootste resistor kry die meeste), en R_s = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ is groter as enige van die resistors. Die ander drie opsies beskryf eienskappe van 'n parallelle stroombaan.","en":"In series there is only one path, so the current is the same everywhere. The potential difference divides (the largest resistor gets the most), and R_s = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ is larger than any of the resistors. The other three options describe properties of a parallel circuit."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter verandering sal die weerstand van 'n koperdraad VERLAAG?","en":"Which change will DECREASE the resistance of a copper wire?"},"options":[{"af":"Gebruik 'n dikker draad van dieselfde lengte.","en":"Use a thicker wire of the same length."},{"af":"Gebruik 'n langer draad van dieselfde dikte.","en":"Use a longer wire of the same thickness."},{"af":"Verhit die draad.","en":"Heat the wire."},{"af":"Gebruik 'n dunner draad van dieselfde lengte.","en":"Use a thinner wire of the same length."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Dikker draad het 'n groter deursnee-oppervlakte: daar is meer ruimte vir die elektrone om deur te beweeg, dus neem R af. 'n Langer draad gee meer botsings, en 'n warmer draad se atome vibreer meer – albei verhoog R. 'n Dunner draad verhoog ook R.","en":"A thicker wire has a larger cross-sectional area: there is more room for the electrons to move through, so R decreases. A longer wire gives more collisions, and in a hotter wire the atoms vibrate more – both increase R. A thinner wire also increases R."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Wanneer die skakelaar oop is en geen stroom vloei nie, lees 'n voltmeter wat oor die pole van 'n battery gekoppel is, die emk van die battery.","en":"When the switch is open and no current flows, a voltmeter connected across the terminals of a battery reads the emf of the battery."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Emk is per definisie die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van die battery wanneer geen stroom vloei nie. As die skakelaar toe is, lees die voltmeter die terminale potensiaalverskil, wat effens kleiner is.","en":"True. Emf is by definition the potential difference across the terminals of the battery when no current flows. With the switch closed, the voltmeter reads the terminal potential difference, which is slightly less."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n 4 Ω-, 'n 6 Ω- en 'n 10 Ω-resistor word in serie gekoppel. Die ekwivalente weerstand is ___ Ω.","en":"A 4 Ω, a 6 Ω and a 10 Ω resistor are connected in series. The equivalent resistance is ___ Ω."},"answers":{"af":["20","20 Ω","20Ω","20 ohm","20,0","20.0","20,00","20.00"],"en":["20","20 Ω","20Ω","20 ohm","20 ohms","20,0","20.0","20,00","20.00"]},"explain":{"af":"In serie tel die weerstande op: R_s = 4 + 6 + 10 = 20 Ω.","en":"In series the resistances add up: R_s = 4 + 6 + 10 = 20 Ω."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Lading van 90 C vloei in 1 minuut deur 'n gloeilamp. Die stroom deur die gloeilamp is ___ A.","en":"A charge of 90 C flows through a bulb in 1 minute. The current through the bulb is ___ A."},"answers":{"af":["1,5","1.5","1,5 A","1.5 A","1,5A","1.5A","1,50","1.50","1,50 A","1.50 A"],"en":["1,5","1.5","1,5 A","1.5 A","1,5A","1.5A","1,50","1.50","1,50 A","1.50 A"]},"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers om: Δt = 1 min = 60 s. I = Q/Δt = 90 ÷ 60 = 1,5 A. As jy vergeet om na sekondes om te skakel, kry jy die verkeerde antwoord van 90 A.","en":"Convert first: Δt = 1 min = 60 s. I = Q/Δt = 90 ÷ 60 = 1.5 A. If you forget to convert to seconds, you get the wrong answer of 90 A."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor 'n resistor is 6 V en die stroom daardeur is 0,4 A. Die weerstand van die resistor is ___ Ω.","en":"The potential difference across a resistor is 6 V and the current through it is 0.4 A. The resistance of the resistor is ___ Ω."},"answers":{"af":["15","15 Ω","15Ω","15 ohm","15,0","15.0","15,00","15.00"],"en":["15","15 Ω","15Ω","15 ohm","15 ohms","15,0","15.0","15,00","15.00"]},"explain":{"af":"R = V/I = 6 ÷ 0,4 = 15 Ω. Moenie V × I (= 2,4) bereken nie – weerstand is spanning gedeel deur stroom.","en":"R = V/I = 6 ÷ 0.4 = 15 Ω. Do not calculate V × I (= 2.4) – resistance is voltage divided by current."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n 6 Ω- en 'n 12 Ω-resistor word in parallel gekoppel. Wat is die ekwivalente weerstand?","en":"A 6 Ω and a 12 Ω resistor are connected in parallel. What is the equivalent resistance?"},"options":[{"af":"18 Ω","en":"18 Ω"},{"af":"0,25 Ω","en":"0.25 Ω"},{"af":"9 Ω","en":"9 Ω"},{"af":"4 Ω","en":"4 Ω"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/12 = 2/12 + 1/12 = 3/12, dus Rₚ = 12/3 = 4 Ω (of produk oor som: 72 ÷ 18 = 4 Ω). 18 Ω is die serie-antwoord, 0,25 Ω is 1/Rₚ wat nie omgekeer is nie, en 9 Ω is net die gemiddeld. Kontroleer: Rₚ moet kleiner as 6 Ω wees.","en":"1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/12 = 2/12 + 1/12 = 3/12, so Rₚ = 12/3 = 4 Ω (or product over sum: 72 ÷ 18 = 4 Ω). 18 Ω is the series answer, 0.25 Ω is 1/Rₚ not inverted, and 9 Ω is just the average. Check: Rₚ must be smaller than 6 Ω."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Drie identiese 1,5 V-selle word in serie aan 'n 9 Ω-resistor gekoppel. Ignoreer die selle se interne weerstand. Wat is die stroom in die stroombaan?","en":"Three identical 1.5 V cells are connected in series to a 9 Ω resistor. Ignore the internal resistance of the cells. What is the current in the circuit?"},"options":[{"af":"0,17 A","en":"0.17 A"},{"af":"0,5 A","en":"0.5 A"},{"af":"2 A","en":"2 A"},{"af":"40,5 A","en":"40.5 A"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Selle in serie: emk = 3 × 1,5 = 4,5 V. I = V ÷ R = 4,5 ÷ 9 = 0,5 A. 0,17 A gebruik net een sel (1,5 ÷ 9), 2 A is R ÷ V (omgekeer) en 40,5 A is V × R.","en":"Cells in series: emf = 3 × 1.5 = 4.5 V. I = V ÷ R = 4.5 ÷ 9 = 0.5 A. 0.17 A uses only one cell (1.5 ÷ 9), 2 A is R ÷ V (inverted) and 40.5 A is V × R."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n 2 Ω-resistor is in serie met 'n parallelle kombinasie van twee 4 Ω-resistors. Die stroombaan is gekoppel aan 'n battery met 'n emk van 8 V en weglaatbare interne weerstand. 'n Ammeter is in serie met die battery. Wat lees die ammeter?","en":"A 2 Ω resistor is in series with a parallel combination of two 4 Ω resistors. The circuit is connected to a battery with an emf of 8 V and negligible internal resistance. An ammeter is in series with the battery. What does the ammeter read?"},"options":[{"af":"2 A","en":"2 A"},{"af":"0,8 A","en":"0.8 A"},{"af":"4 A","en":"4 A"},{"af":"1 A","en":"1 A"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Rₚ = (4 × 4)/(4 + 4) = 2 Ω; R_T = 2 + 2 = 4 Ω; I = 8 ÷ 4 = 2 A. 0,8 A kry jy as jy al drie resistors in serie optel (8 ÷ 10), 4 A as jy die 2 Ω-serie-resistor vergeet (8 ÷ 2), en 1 A is die stroom in net een van die takke.","en":"Rₚ = (4 × 4)/(4 + 4) = 2 Ω; R_T = 2 + 2 = 4 Ω; I = 8 ÷ 4 = 2 A. You get 0.8 A if you add all three resistors in series (8 ÷ 10), 4 A if you forget the 2 Ω series resistor (8 ÷ 2), and 1 A is the current in just one of the branches."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n 3 Ω-resistor is in serie met 'n parallelle kombinasie van 'n 6 Ω-, 'n 3 Ω- en 'n 2 Ω-resistor. Die ekwivalente weerstand van al vier resistors saam is ___ Ω.","en":"A 3 Ω resistor is in series with a parallel combination of a 6 Ω, a 3 Ω and a 2 Ω resistor. The equivalent resistance of all four resistors together is ___ Ω."},"answers":{"af":["4","4 Ω","4Ω","4 ohm","4,0","4.0","4,00","4.00"],"en":["4","4 Ω","4Ω","4 ohm","4 ohms","4,0","4.0","4,00","4.00"]},"explain":{"af":"Parallel eerste: 1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/3 + 1/2 = 1/6 + 2/6 + 3/6 = 6/6 = 1, dus Rₚ = 1 Ω. Tel dan die serie-resistor by: R = 3 + 1 = 4 Ω. Produk oor som werk net vir twee resistors op 'n slag.","en":"Parallel first: 1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/3 + 1/2 = 1/6 + 2/6 + 3/6 = 6/6 = 1, so Rₚ = 1 Ω. Then add the series resistor: R = 3 + 1 = 4 Ω. Product over sum only works for two resistors at a time."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Drie identiese gloeilampe P, Q en R is aan 'n battery met weglaatbare interne weerstand gekoppel. Q en R is in parallel met mekaar, en hierdie parallelle kombinasie is in serie met P. Gloeilamp R brand uit (sy filament breek). Watter stelling beskryf die gevolg korrek?","en":"Three identical bulbs P, Q and R are connected to a battery with negligible internal resistance. Q and R are in parallel with each other, and this parallel combination is in series with P. Bulb R blows (its filament breaks). Which statement correctly describes the result?"},"options":[{"af":"P word helderder en Q word dowwer.","en":"P becomes brighter and Q becomes dimmer."},{"af":"P en Q word albei dowwer.","en":"P and Q both become dimmer."},{"af":"P word dowwer en Q word helderder.","en":"P becomes dimmer and Q becomes brighter."},{"af":"P word dowwer en Q gaan ook uit.","en":"P becomes dimmer and Q also goes out."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sonder R het die parallelle deel net een pad, dus neem sy weerstand toe (van ½R na R) en R_T neem toe (van 1,5R na 2R). I_T = V ÷ R_T neem af, dus word P dowwer en die potensiaalverskil oor P daal (van ⅔V na ½V). Die potensiaalverskil oor Q = V − V_P neem dus toe (van ⅓V na ½V), so Q word helderder. Q gaan nie uit nie – dit is steeds in 'n volledige stroombaan met P.","en":"Without R the parallel section has only one path, so its resistance increases (from ½R to R) and R_T increases (from 1.5R to 2R). I_T = V ÷ R_T decreases, so P becomes dimmer and the potential difference across P drops (from ⅔V to ½V). The potential difference across Q = V − V_P therefore increases (from ⅓V to ½V), so Q becomes brighter. Q does not go out – it is still in a complete circuit with P."}}]},{"id":"f10-t2-fisiese-chemiese-verandering","title":{"af":"Fisiese en chemiese verandering","en":"Physical and chemical change"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal fisiese en chemiese veranderinge op deeltjievlak kan onderskei, die behoudswette en die wet van konstante samestelling kan toepas en chemiese vergelykings met toestandsimbole kan balanseer.","en":"You will be able to distinguish physical and chemical changes at particle level, apply the conservation laws and the law of constant composition, and balance chemical equations with state symbols."},"summary":{"af":"## Fisiese verandering\n\n'n **Fisiese verandering** is 'n verandering waartydens **geen nuwe stowwe** gevorm word nie. Net die toestand, vorm of rangskikking van die deeltjies verander.\n\n- Die **molekules bly heel**: geen bindings binne-in die molekules word gebreek nie. Net die afstand tussen die molekules en hulle rangskikking verander.\n- Die **massa**, die aantal **atome** en die aantal **molekules** bly behoue.\n- Die **energieverandering is klein** – net die kragte tussen die molekules word oorkom.\n- Dit is gewoonlik maklik **omkeerbaar**.\n- Voorbeelde: ys smelt, water verdamp of kondenseer, was smelt, glas breek, 'n mengsel word deur filtrasie of distillasie geskei.\n\n## Chemiese verandering\n\n'n **Chemiese verandering** is 'n verandering waartydens **nuwe stowwe** met nuwe chemiese eienskappe gevorm word.\n\n- **Bindings word gebreek** in die reaktanse en **nuwe bindings word gevorm** in die produkte – die atome word **herrangskik**.\n- Die **massa** en die aantal en soort **atome** bly behoue, maar die aantal **molekules** kan verander.\n- Die **energieverandering is groot**: om bindings te breek kos energie, en wanneer bindings vorm, word energie vrygestel. 'n Reaksie wat energie vrystel (bv. die vuur by 'n braai) is **eksotermies**; een wat energie opneem, is **endotermies**.\n- Dit is gewoonlik moeilik omkeerbaar.\n- Tekens van 'n chemiese reaksie: 'n kleurverandering, gas word gevorm (borrels), 'n presipitaat (vaste stof) vorm, die temperatuur verander, of lig of klank word afgegee.\n- Voorbeelde: hout of gas brand, yster roes, kos verteer, kalksteen ontbind as dit verhit word.\n\n| | Fisiese verandering | Chemiese verandering |\n|---|---|---|\n| Nuwe stowwe? | nee | ja |\n| Molekules | bly heel | word opgebreek; atome herrangskik |\n| Energie | klein verandering | groot verandering |\n| Massa en atome | behoue | behoue |\n| Aantal molekules | behoue | kan verander |\n| Omkeerbaar? | maklik | moeilik |\n\n## Ontbinding en sintese\n\n- **Ontbindingsreaksie:** een verbinding breek op in twee of meer eenvoudiger stowwe. Bv. die elektrolise van water: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g), of waterstofperoksied: 2H_{2}O_{2}(aq) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ) + O_{2}(g).\n- **Sintesereaksie:** twee of meer stowwe verbind om **een** nuwe produk te vorm. Bv. yster en swael word saam verhit: Fe(s) + S(s) → FeS(s); of 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n## Behoud van atome en massa\n\n- **Wet van behoud van massa:** *Die massa van 'n geslote sisteem van stowwe bly konstant, ongeag die prosesse wat binne die sisteem plaasvind.* Tydens 'n reaksie is die totale massa van die reaktanse dus gelyk aan die totale massa van die produkte.\n- **Behoud van atome:** atome word nie geskep of vernietig nie, net herrangskik. Daarom moet elke chemiese vergelyking gebalanseer wees.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** In 'n **oop** houer lyk dit asof massa verander. As staalwol brand, is die produk swaarder (suurstof uit die lug het met die yster verbind). As kalksteen verhit word, word die vaste stof ligter (CO_{2}-gas ontsnap). In 'n geslote sisteem bly die totale massa presies dieselfde.\n\n## Wet van konstante samestelling\n\n*In enige gegewe chemiese verbinding verbind die elemente altyd in dieselfde massaverhouding met mekaar*, ongeag hoe die verbinding berei is of waar dit vandaan kom.\n\n- Water (H_{2}O): H : O = 2 × 1 : 16 = 2 : 16 = **1 : 8** volgens massa.\n- Koolstofdioksied (CO_{2}): C : O = 12 : 32 = **3 : 8**.\n- Waterstofperoksied (H_{2}O_{2}) is 'n *ander* verbinding: H : O = 2 : 32 = 1 : 16.\n\n## Reaksies in woorde en simbole\n\n- **Woordvergelyking:** magnesium + suurstof → magnesiumoksied\n- **Gebalanseerde chemiese vergelyking:** 2Mg(s) + O_{2}(g) → 2MgO(s)\n\n**Reaktanse** staan links van die pyl en **produkte** regs. Die **koëffisiënt** (groot getal voor 'n formule) gee die aantal deeltjies; die **onderskrif** (klein getal) is deel van die formule.\n\n**Toestandsimbole:** (s) vaste stof; (ℓ) vloeistof; (g) gas; (aq) waterige oplossing – opgelos in water.\n\n## Stappe om 'n vergelyking te balanseer\n\n1. Skryf die korrekte formules van al die reaktanse en produkte. Onthou die diatomiese elemente: H_{2}, N_{2}, O_{2}, F_{2}, Cl_{2}, Br_{2}, I_{2}.\n2. Tel die atome van elke element aan albei kante.\n3. Balanseer **slegs met koëffisiënte** – verander **nooit** 'n onderskrif nie (H_{2}O → H_{2}O_{2} is 'n heel ander stof!).\n4. Begin met die element wat in die minste formules voorkom en laat H en O vir laaste. Hanteer 'n poliatomiese ioon (bv. SO_{4}) as een eenheid as dit onveranderd aan albei kante voorkom.\n5. Kontroleer elke element en skryf die koëffisiënte in die kleinste heelgetalverhouding.\n\n**Voorbeeld:** CH_{4} + O_{2} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O. C: 1 = 1. H: 4 links, dus 2H_{2}O. O: regs 2 + 2 = 4, dus 2O_{2}. Antwoord: CH_{4}(g) + 2O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n> **Wenk – atome tel met hakies:** 3Ca(NO_{3})_{2} bevat 3 Ca-atome, 3 × 2 = 6 N-atome en 3 × 2 × 3 = 18 O-atome. Die koëffisiënt vermenigvuldig alles in die formule.","en":"## Physical change\n\nA **physical change** is a change in which **no new substances** are formed. Only the state, shape or arrangement of the particles changes.\n\n- The **molecules stay intact**: no bonds inside the molecules are broken. Only the distance between the molecules and their arrangement change.\n- The **mass**, the number of **atoms** and the number of **molecules** are conserved.\n- The **energy change is small** – only the forces between the molecules are overcome.\n- It is usually easily **reversible**.\n- Examples: ice melting, water evaporating or condensing, wax melting, glass breaking, a mixture being separated by filtration or distillation.\n\n## Chemical change\n\nA **chemical change** is a change in which **new substances** with new chemical properties are formed.\n\n- **Bonds are broken** in the reactants and **new bonds are formed** in the products – the atoms are **rearranged**.\n- The **mass** and the number and type of **atoms** are conserved, but the number of **molecules** can change.\n- The **energy change is large**: breaking bonds costs energy, and when bonds form, energy is released. A reaction that releases energy (e.g. the fire at a braai) is **exothermic**; one that absorbs energy is **endothermic**.\n- It is usually difficult to reverse.\n- Signs of a chemical reaction: a colour change, a gas forms (bubbles), a precipitate (solid) forms, the temperature changes, or light or sound is given off.\n- Examples: wood or gas burning, iron rusting, food being digested, limestone decomposing when heated.\n\n| | Physical change | Chemical change |\n|---|---|---|\n| New substances? | no | yes |\n| Molecules | stay intact | are broken up; atoms rearranged |\n| Energy | small change | large change |\n| Mass and atoms | conserved | conserved |\n| Number of molecules | conserved | can change |\n| Reversible? | easily | with difficulty |\n\n## Decomposition and synthesis\n\n- **Decomposition reaction:** one compound breaks up into two or more simpler substances. E.g. the electrolysis of water: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g), or hydrogen peroxide: 2H_{2}O_{2}(aq) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ) + O_{2}(g).\n- **Synthesis reaction:** two or more substances combine to form **one** new product. E.g. iron and sulfur heated together: Fe(s) + S(s) → FeS(s); or 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n## Conservation of atoms and mass\n\n- **Law of conservation of mass:** *The mass of a closed system of substances will remain constant, regardless of the processes acting inside the system.* So during a reaction the total mass of the reactants equals the total mass of the products.\n- **Conservation of atoms:** atoms are not created or destroyed, only rearranged. That is why every chemical equation must be balanced.\n\n> **Common mistake:** In an **open** container it looks as if mass changes. When steel wool burns, the product is heavier (oxygen from the air combined with the iron). When limestone is heated, the solid becomes lighter (CO_{2} gas escapes). In a closed system the total mass stays exactly the same.\n\n## Law of constant composition\n\n*In any given chemical compound, the elements always combine in the same proportion by mass with each other*, regardless of how the compound was prepared or where it comes from.\n\n- Water (H_{2}O): H : O = 2 × 1 : 16 = 2 : 16 = **1 : 8** by mass.\n- Carbon dioxide (CO_{2}): C : O = 12 : 32 = **3 : 8**.\n- Hydrogen peroxide (H_{2}O_{2}) is a *different* compound: H : O = 2 : 32 = 1 : 16.\n\n## Reactions in words and symbols\n\n- **Word equation:** magnesium + oxygen → magnesium oxide\n- **Balanced chemical equation:** 2Mg(s) + O_{2}(g) → 2MgO(s)\n\n**Reactants** are on the left of the arrow and **products** on the right. The **coefficient** (large number in front of a formula) gives the number of particles; the **subscript** (small number) is part of the formula.\n\n**State symbols:** (s) solid; (ℓ) liquid; (g) gas; (aq) aqueous solution – dissolved in water.\n\n## Steps to balance an equation\n\n1. Write the correct formulae of all the reactants and products. Remember the diatomic elements: H_{2}, N_{2}, O_{2}, F_{2}, Cl_{2}, Br_{2}, I_{2}.\n2. Count the atoms of each element on both sides.\n3. Balance **only with coefficients** – **never** change a subscript (H_{2}O → H_{2}O_{2} is a completely different substance!).\n4. Start with the element that appears in the fewest formulae and leave H and O for last. Treat a polyatomic ion (e.g. SO_{4}) as one unit if it appears unchanged on both sides.\n5. Check every element and write the coefficients in the smallest whole-number ratio.\n\n**Example:** CH_{4} + O_{2} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O. C: 1 = 1. H: 4 on the left, so 2H_{2}O. O: on the right 2 + 2 = 4, so 2O_{2}. Answer: CH_{4}(g) + 2O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n> **Tip – counting atoms with brackets:** 3Ca(NO_{3})_{2} contains 3 Ca atoms, 3 × 2 = 6 N atoms and 3 × 2 × 3 = 18 O atoms. The coefficient multiplies everything in the formula."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Fisiese verandering","en":"Physical change"},"def":{"af":"'n Verandering waartydens geen nuwe stowwe gevorm word nie; die molekules bly heel en net hulle rangskikking verander.","en":"A change in which no new substances are formed; the molecules stay intact and only their arrangement changes."}},{"term":{"af":"Chemiese verandering","en":"Chemical change"},"def":{"af":"'n Verandering waartydens nuwe stowwe met nuwe eienskappe gevorm word; bindings word gebreek en nuwe bindings word gevorm.","en":"A change in which new substances with new properties are formed; bonds are broken and new bonds are formed."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontbindingsreaksie","en":"Decomposition reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin een verbinding in twee of meer eenvoudiger stowwe opbreek, bv. 2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂.","en":"A reaction in which one compound breaks up into two or more simpler substances, e.g. 2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂."}},{"term":{"af":"Sintesereaksie","en":"Synthesis reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin twee of meer stowwe verbind om een nuwe produk te vorm, bv. Fe + S → FeS.","en":"A reaction in which two or more substances combine to form one new product, e.g. Fe + S → FeS."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van behoud van massa","en":"Law of conservation of mass"},"def":{"af":"Die massa van 'n geslote sisteem van stowwe bly konstant, ongeag die prosesse wat binne die sisteem plaasvind.","en":"The mass of a closed system of substances will remain constant, regardless of the processes acting inside the system."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van konstante samestelling","en":"Law of constant composition"},"def":{"af":"In enige gegewe chemiese verbinding verbind die elemente altyd in dieselfde massaverhouding met mekaar.","en":"In any given chemical compound, the elements always combine in the same proportion by mass with each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Gebalanseerde chemiese vergelyking","en":"Balanced chemical equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking met dieselfde aantal atome van elke element aan die reaktant- en die produkkant.","en":"An equation with the same number of atoms of each element on the reactant side and the product side."}},{"term":{"af":"Koëffisiënt","en":"Coefficient"},"def":{"af":"Die getal voor 'n formule in 'n chemiese vergelyking wat die aantal deeltjies aandui; dit word gebruik om te balanseer.","en":"The number in front of a formula in a chemical equation that shows the number of particles; it is used to balance."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksotermiese reaksie","en":"Exothermic reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie wat energie (hitte) aan die omgewing vrystel, bv. die verbranding van hout.","en":"A reaction that releases energy (heat) to the surroundings, e.g. the burning of wood."}},{"term":{"af":"Endotermiese reaksie","en":"Endothermic reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie wat energie uit die omgewing opneem, bv. die ontbinding van kalksteen wanneer dit verhit word.","en":"A reaction that absorbs energy from the surroundings, e.g. the decomposition of limestone when it is heated."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Fisies of chemies? Verduidelik op deeltjievlak","en":"Physical or chemical? Explain at particle level"},"problem":{"af":"Vergelyk wat met die watermolekules gebeur wanneer (a) water in 'n ketel kook en (b) water deur elektrolise in waterstof en suurstof ontbind word. Verwys na die molekules, die energie en die massa.","en":"Compare what happens to the water molecules when (a) water boils in a kettle and (b) water is decomposed into hydrogen and oxygen by electrolysis. Refer to the molecules, the energy and the mass."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Kook: die watermolekules bly H_{2}O; hulle beweeg net verder uitmekaar (vloeistof → gas). Geen nuwe stof vorm nie, dus is dit 'n **fisiese verandering**.","en":"(a) Boiling: the water molecules stay H_{2}O; they just move further apart (liquid → gas). No new substance forms, so it is a **physical change**."},{"af":"(a) Net die kragte tussen die molekules word oorkom, dus is die energieverandering relatief klein. Die massa en die aantal molekules bly dieselfde.","en":"(a) Only the forces between the molecules are overcome, so the energy change is relatively small. The mass and the number of molecules stay the same."},{"af":"(b) Elektrolise: die bindings binne-in die watermolekules word gebreek en die atome word herrangskik in H_{2}- en O_{2}-molekules: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g). Nuwe stowwe vorm, dus is dit 'n **chemiese verandering** ('n ontbindingsreaksie).","en":"(b) Electrolysis: the bonds inside the water molecules are broken and the atoms are rearranged into H_{2} and O_{2} molecules: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g). New substances form, so it is a **chemical change** (a decomposition reaction)."},{"af":"(b) Baie elektriese energie is nodig om die bindings te breek – 'n groot energieverandering. Daar is 4 H- en 2 O-atome aan albei kante, dus is die massa behoue, maar 2 molekules word 3 molekules.","en":"(b) A lot of electrical energy is needed to break the bonds – a large energy change. There are 4 H and 2 O atoms on both sides, so mass is conserved, but 2 molecules become 3 molecules."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Fisiese verandering; (b) chemiese verandering (ontbinding)","en":"(a) Physical change; (b) chemical change (decomposition)"}},{"title":{"af":"Balanseer 'n verbrandingsreaksie","en":"Balance a combustion reaction"},"problem":{"af":"Tydens beurtkrag kook baie gesinne in Brits op 'n gasstoof. Propaan (C₃H₈) brand in suurstof en vorm koolstofdioksied en waterdamp. Skryf 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking met toestandsimbole.","en":"During load-shedding many families in Brits cook on a gas stove. Propane (C₃H₈) burns in oxygen and forms carbon dioxide and water vapour. Write a balanced equation with state symbols."},"steps":[{"af":"Ongebalanseerd: C_{3}H_{8}(g) + O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(g)","en":"Unbalanced: C_{3}H_{8}(g) + O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(g)"},{"af":"C: 3 atome links, dus 3CO_{2} regs.","en":"C: 3 atoms on the left, so 3CO_{2} on the right."},{"af":"H: 8 atome links, dus 4H_{2}O regs (4 × 2 = 8).","en":"H: 8 atoms on the left, so 4H_{2}O on the right (4 × 2 = 8)."},{"af":"O laaste: regs is daar 3 × 2 + 4 × 1 = 10 O-atome, dus 5O_{2} links (5 × 2 = 10).","en":"O last: on the right there are 3 × 2 + 4 × 1 = 10 O atoms, so 5O_{2} on the left (5 × 2 = 10)."},{"af":"Kontroleer: C 3 = 3; H 8 = 8; O 10 = 10 ✓","en":"Check: C 3 = 3; H 8 = 8; O 10 = 10 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(g)","en":"C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(g)"}},{"title":{"af":"Van 'n woordvergelyking na simbole","en":"From a word equation to symbols"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 'n gebalanseerde chemiese vergelyking met toestandsimbole vir: aluminium + suurstof → aluminiumoksied (vaste stof). Watter tipe reaksie is dit?","en":"Write a balanced chemical equation with state symbols for: aluminium + oxygen → aluminium oxide (solid). What type of reaction is this?"},"steps":[{"af":"Formules: aluminium is 'n metaal (Al); suurstofgas is diatomies (O_{2}); aluminiumoksied bestaan uit Al^{3+}- en O^{2−}-ione, dus Al_{2}O_{3}.","en":"Formulae: aluminium is a metal (Al); oxygen gas is diatomic (O_{2}); aluminium oxide consists of Al^{3+} and O^{2−} ions, so Al_{2}O_{3}."},{"af":"Ongebalanseerd: Al(s) + O_{2}(g) → Al_{2}O_{3}(s)","en":"Unbalanced: Al(s) + O_{2}(g) → Al_{2}O_{3}(s)"},{"af":"O: 2 links en 3 regs. Die KGV van 2 en 3 is 6, dus 3O_{2} en 2Al_{2}O_{3}.","en":"O: 2 on the left and 3 on the right. The LCM of 2 and 3 is 6, so 3O_{2} and 2Al_{2}O_{3}."},{"af":"Al: regs is daar nou 2 × 2 = 4 Al-atome, dus 4Al links.","en":"Al: on the right there are now 2 × 2 = 4 Al atoms, so 4Al on the left."},{"af":"Kontroleer: Al 4 = 4; O 6 = 6 ✓. Twee stowwe vorm een produk, dus is dit 'n **sintesereaksie**.","en":"Check: Al 4 = 4; O 6 = 6 ✓. Two substances form one product, so it is a **synthesis reaction**."}],"answer":{"af":"4Al(s) + 3O₂(g) → 2Al₂O₃(s); sintesereaksie","en":"4Al(s) + 3O₂(g) → 2Al₂O₃(s); synthesis reaction"}},{"title":{"af":"Behoud van massa en konstante samestelling","en":"Conservation of mass and constant composition"},"problem":{"af":"Kalk (CaO), wat in die mynbedryf en vir sement gebruik word, word gemaak deur kalksteen sterk te verhit: CaCO₃(s) → CaO(s) + CO₂(g). 'n Leerder verhit 10 g CaCO₃ in 'n oop proefbuis totdat dit volledig ontbind, en 5,6 g vaste stof bly oor. (a) Bereken die massa CO₂ wat gevorm het. (b) Die leerder sê massa het verlore gegaan. Evalueer sy stelling. (c) Watter massa CaO sal 25 g CaCO₃ lewer?","en":"Lime (CaO), which is used in mining and for cement, is made by strongly heating limestone: CaCO₃(s) → CaO(s) + CO₂(g). A learner heats 10 g CaCO₃ in an open test tube until it decomposes completely, and 5.6 g of solid remains. (a) Calculate the mass of CO₂ that formed. (b) The learner says mass was lost. Evaluate his statement. (c) What mass of CaO will 25 g CaCO₃ produce?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Behoud van massa: m(CaCO_{3}) = m(CaO) + m(CO_{2})","en":"(a) Conservation of mass: m(CaCO_{3}) = m(CaO) + m(CO_{2})"},{"af":"m(CO_{2}) = 10 − 5,6 = 4,4 g","en":"m(CO_{2}) = 10 − 5.6 = 4.4 g"},{"af":"(b) Massa het nie verlore gegaan nie: die 4,4 g CO_{2} is 'n gas wat uit die oop proefbuis ontsnap het. In 'n geslote sisteem sou die totale massa 10 g gebly het.","en":"(b) Mass was not lost: the 4.4 g CO_{2} is a gas that escaped from the open test tube. In a closed system the total mass would have stayed 10 g."},{"af":"(c) CaCO_{3} het 'n konstante samestelling, dus lewer dit altyd dieselfde massafraksie CaO: 10 g gee 5,6 g. Vir 25 g: m(CaO) = 25 × [[5,6/10]] = 14 g","en":"(c) CaCO_{3} has a constant composition, so it always produces the same mass fraction of CaO: 10 g gives 5.6 g. For 25 g: m(CaO) = 25 × [[5.6/10]] = 14 g"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 4,4 g CO₂; (b) die CO₂-gas het ontsnap – massa is behoue in 'n geslote sisteem; (c) 14 g CaO","en":"(a) 4.4 g CO₂; (b) the CO₂ gas escaped – mass is conserved in a closed system; (c) 14 g CaO"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n chemiese verandering?","en":"Which one of the following is a chemical change?"},"options":[{"af":"Ys smelt in 'n koelhouer.","en":"Ice melts in a cooler box."},{"af":"Suiker word fyngemaak.","en":"Sugar is crushed."},{"af":"'n Spyker roes buite in die reën.","en":"A nail rusts outside in the rain."},{"af":"Water kook in 'n ketel.","en":"Water boils in a kettle."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Roes is 'n nuwe stof (ysteroksied) wat vorm wanneer yster met suurstof en water reageer. Smelt, fynmaak en kook verander net die toestand of vorm van die stof – geen nuwe stof vorm nie.","en":"Rust is a new substance (iron oxide) that forms when iron reacts with oxygen and water. Melting, crushing and boiling only change the state or shape of the substance – no new substance forms."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke toestandsimbool by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each state symbol to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"(s)","en":"(s)"},"r":{"af":"vaste stof","en":"solid"}},{"l":{"af":"(ℓ)","en":"(ℓ)"},"r":{"af":"vloeistof","en":"liquid"}},{"l":{"af":"(g)","en":"(g)"},"r":{"af":"gas","en":"gas"}},{"l":{"af":"(aq)","en":"(aq)"},"r":{"af":"opgelos in water (waterige oplossing)","en":"dissolved in water (aqueous solution)"}}],"explain":{"af":"(s) = vaste stof, (ℓ) = vloeistof, (g) = gas en (aq) = waterige oplossing. Let op: (ℓ) beteken 'n suiwer vloeistof soos water, terwyl (aq) beteken dat die stof in water opgelos is.","en":"(s) = solid, (ℓ) = liquid, (g) = gas and (aq) = aqueous solution. Note: (ℓ) means a pure liquid such as water, while (aq) means the substance is dissolved in water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die reaksie 2H₂O₂(aq) → 2H₂O(ℓ) + O₂(g) is 'n voorbeeld van ...","en":"The reaction 2H₂O₂(aq) → 2H₂O(ℓ) + O₂(g) is an example of ..."},"options":[{"af":"'n sintesereaksie.","en":"a synthesis reaction."},{"af":"'n ontbindingsreaksie.","en":"a decomposition reaction."},{"af":"'n fisiese verandering.","en":"a physical change."},{"af":"'n presipitasiereaksie.","en":"a precipitation reaction."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Een verbinding (H₂O₂) breek op in twee eenvoudiger stowwe (H₂O en O₂) – dit is ontbinding. By sintese verbind stowwe juis om een produk te vorm. Dit is chemies (nuwe stowwe vorm), en geen onoplosbare vaste stof vorm nie, dus is dit nie presipitasie nie.","en":"One compound (H₂O₂) breaks up into two simpler substances (H₂O and O₂) – that is decomposition. In synthesis, substances combine to form one product. It is chemical (new substances form), and no insoluble solid forms, so it is not precipitation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling beskryf 'n fisiese verandering op deeltjievlak die beste?","en":"Which statement best describes a physical change at particle level?"},"options":[{"af":"Bindings binne-in die molekules word gebreek en nuwe bindings word gevorm.","en":"Bonds inside the molecules are broken and new bonds are formed."},{"af":"Atome word vernietig en nuwe atome word gevorm.","en":"Atoms are destroyed and new atoms are formed."},{"af":"Die aantal molekules verander, maar die massa bly dieselfde.","en":"The number of molecules changes, but the mass stays the same."},{"af":"Die molekules bly heel; net hulle rangskikking en die afstand tussen hulle verander.","en":"The molecules stay intact; only their arrangement and the distance between them change."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By 'n fisiese verandering bly die molekules heel – net die rangskikking en spasiëring verander. Bindings breek en vorm, en die aantal molekules verander, by 'n chemiese verandering. Atome word nooit vernietig of geskep nie.","en":"In a physical change the molecules stay intact – only the arrangement and spacing change. Bonds breaking and forming, and the number of molecules changing, happen in a chemical change. Atoms are never destroyed or created."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Tydens 'n chemiese reaksie bly die aantal molekules altyd dieselfde.","en":"During a chemical reaction the number of molecules always stays the same."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die aantal en soort atome bly behoue, maar die aantal molekules kan verander. In 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O word 3 molekules 2 molekules, terwyl daar 4 H- en 2 O-atome aan albei kante is.","en":"False. The number and type of atoms are conserved, but the number of molecules can change. In 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, 3 molecules become 2 molecules, while there are 4 H and 2 O atoms on both sides."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Volgens die wet van konstante samestelling bevat suiwer water altyd waterstof en suurstof in die massaverhouding 1 : 8, ongeag waar die water vandaan kom.","en":"According to the law of constant composition, pure water always contains hydrogen and oxygen in the mass ratio 1 : 8, regardless of where the water comes from."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. H₂O bevat 2 × 1 = 2 g waterstof vir elke 16 g suurstof, dus H : O = 2 : 16 = 1 : 8. Suiwer water uit 'n dam of uit 'n laboratorium het presies dieselfde samestelling.","en":"True. H₂O contains 2 × 1 = 2 g hydrogen for every 16 g oxygen, so H : O = 2 : 16 = 1 : 8. Pure water from a dam or from a laboratory has exactly the same composition."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer 'n kers brand, smelt die was eers, en dan brand die wasdamp in die vlam. Watter stelling is korrek?","en":"When a candle burns, the wax first melts, and then the wax vapour burns in the flame. Which statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die smelt is 'n fisiese verandering en die brand is 'n chemiese verandering.","en":"The melting is a physical change and the burning is a chemical change."},{"af":"Albei is fisiese veranderinge.","en":"Both are physical changes."},{"af":"Albei is chemiese veranderinge.","en":"Both are chemical changes."},{"af":"Die smelt is 'n chemiese verandering en die brand is 'n fisiese verandering.","en":"The melting is a chemical change and the burning is a physical change."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Gesmelte was is steeds was (dieselfde molekules) – 'n fisiese verandering. Wanneer die wasdamp brand, reageer dit met suurstof en vorm nuwe stowwe (CO₂ en H₂O) met 'n groot energievrystelling (hitte en lig) – 'n chemiese verandering.","en":"Melted wax is still wax (the same molecules) – a physical change. When the wax vapour burns, it reacts with oxygen and forms new substances (CO₂ and H₂O) with a large release of energy (heat and light) – a chemical change."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Balanseer die vergelyking vir die vorming van ammoniak: N₂(g) + ___H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g)","en":"Balance the equation for the formation of ammonia: N₂(g) + ___H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g)"},"answers":{"af":["3","3H2","3H₂","drie"],"en":["3","3H2","3H₂","three"]},"explain":{"af":"Regs is daar 2 × 3 = 6 H-atome. Links het elke H₂-molekule 2 H-atome, dus is 3H₂ nodig (3 × 2 = 6). N: 2 = 2 ✓.","en":"On the right there are 2 × 3 = 6 H atoms. On the left each H₂ molecule has 2 H atoms, so 3H₂ is needed (3 × 2 = 6). N: 2 = 2 ✓."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel suurstofatome word deur 2Al₂(SO₄)₃ voorgestel? ___","en":"How many oxygen atoms are represented by 2Al₂(SO₄)₃? ___"},"answers":{"af":["24","24 atome","24 O-atome","24 O"],"en":["24","24 atoms","24 O atoms","24 O"]},"explain":{"af":"Elke SO₄ het 4 O-atome; die hakie word met 3 vermenigvuldig (12 O per Al₂(SO₄)₃), en die koëffisiënt 2 verdubbel alles: 2 × 3 × 4 = 24.","en":"Each SO₄ has 4 O atoms; the bracket is multiplied by 3 (12 O per Al₂(SO₄)₃), and the coefficient 2 doubles everything: 2 × 3 × 4 = 24."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer 2,4 g magnesium volledig in suurstof brand, vorm 4,0 g magnesiumoksied. Die massa suurstof wat gereageer het, is ___ g.","en":"When 2.4 g of magnesium burns completely in oxygen, 4.0 g of magnesium oxide forms. The mass of oxygen that reacted is ___ g."},"answers":{"af":["1,6","1.6","1,6 g","1.6 g","1,6g","1.6g","1,60","1.60","1,60 g","1.60 g"],"en":["1,6","1.6","1,6 g","1.6 g","1,6g","1.6g","1,60","1.60","1,60 g","1.60 g"]},"explain":{"af":"Behoud van massa: m(Mg) + m(O₂) = m(MgO), dus m(O₂) = 4,0 − 2,4 = 1,6 g. Die produk is swaarder as die magnesium omdat die suurstof nou deel daarvan is.","en":"Conservation of mass: m(Mg) + m(O₂) = m(MgO), so m(O₂) = 4.0 − 2.4 = 1.6 g. The product is heavier than the magnesium because the oxygen is now part of it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is die korrekte, gebalanseerde vergelyking vir magnesium wat in suurstofgas brand?","en":"Which one is the correct, balanced equation for magnesium burning in oxygen gas?"},"options":[{"af":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → MgO(s)","en":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → MgO(s)"},{"af":"Mg(s) + O(g) → MgO(s)","en":"Mg(s) + O(g) → MgO(s)"},{"af":"2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)","en":"2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)"},{"af":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)","en":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO: Mg 2 = 2 en O 2 = 2 ✓. Die eerste opsie het 2 O links en net 1 regs. Die tweede skryf suurstofgas as O, maar suurstofgas is diatomies (O₂). Die laaste het 1 Mg links en 2 regs.","en":"2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO: Mg 2 = 2 and O 2 = 2 ✓. The first option has 2 O on the left and only 1 on the right. The second writes oxygen gas as O, but oxygen gas is diatomic (O₂). The last has 1 Mg on the left and 2 on the right."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n hoogoond word ystererts met koolstofmonoksied gereduseer: _Fe₂O₃ + _CO → _Fe + _CO₂. Watter stel koëffisiënte (in volgorde) balanseer die vergelyking?","en":"In a blast furnace iron ore is reduced with carbon monoxide: _Fe₂O₃ + _CO → _Fe + _CO₂. Which set of coefficients (in order) balances the equation?"},"options":[{"af":"1; 1; 2; 1","en":"1; 1; 2; 1"},{"af":"2; 3; 4; 3","en":"2; 3; 4; 3"},{"af":"1; 3; 2; 2","en":"1; 3; 2; 2"},{"af":"1; 3; 2; 3","en":"1; 3; 2; 3"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂: Fe 2 = 2; C 3 = 3; O 3 + 3 = 6 links en 3 × 2 = 6 regs ✓. Met 1; 1; 2; 1 is O 4 teen 2; met 2; 3; 4; 3 is O 9 teen 6; met 1; 3; 2; 2 is C 3 teen 2.","en":"Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂: Fe 2 = 2; C 3 = 3; O 3 + 3 = 6 on the left and 3 × 2 = 6 on the right ✓. With 1; 1; 2; 1, O is 4 vs 2; with 2; 3; 4; 3, O is 9 vs 6; with 1; 3; 2; 2, C is 3 vs 2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Suiwer water bevat altyd waterstof en suurstof in die massaverhouding 1 : 8. Hoeveel gram suurstof is in 45 g suiwer water? ___ g","en":"Pure water always contains hydrogen and oxygen in the mass ratio 1 : 8. How many grams of oxygen are in 45 g of pure water? ___ g"},"answers":{"af":["40","40 g","40g","40,0","40.0","40,00","40.00"],"en":["40","40 g","40g","40,0","40.0","40,00","40.00"]},"explain":{"af":"Die verhouding 1 : 8 beteken 9 dele altesaam, waarvan 8 dele suurstof is. m(O) = 45 × 8/9 = 40 g (en m(H) = 5 g). As jy 45 × 8 of 45 ÷ 8 bereken, het jy vergeet dat die totaal 9 dele is.","en":"The ratio 1 : 8 means 9 parts in total, of which 8 parts are oxygen. m(O) = 45 × 8/9 = 40 g (and m(H) = 5 g). If you calculate 45 × 8 or 45 ÷ 8, you forgot that the total is 9 parts."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo weeg 5,0 g staalwol (yster), verbrand dit in 'n oop porseleinbakkie en vind dat die produk swaarder as 5,0 g is. Hy sê dit bewys dat die wet van behoud van massa nie altyd geld nie. Watter evaluering van sy stelling is korrek?","en":"Thabo weighs 5.0 g of steel wool (iron), burns it in an open porcelain dish and finds that the product is heavier than 5.0 g. He says this proves that the law of conservation of mass does not always hold. Which evaluation of his statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: suurstof uit die lug het met die yster verbind, en die massa van daardie suurstof is nou deel van die produk.","en":"He is wrong: oxygen from the air combined with the iron, and the mass of that oxygen is now part of the product."},{"af":"Hy is reg: die hitte van die vlam het ekstra massa geskep.","en":"He is right: the heat of the flame created extra mass."},{"af":"Hy is reg: die wet geld net vir fisiese veranderinge.","en":"He is right: the law only applies to physical changes."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: sy skaal moet foutief wees, want die massa moes presies 5,0 g gebly het.","en":"He is wrong: his scale must be faulty, because the mass should have stayed exactly 5.0 g."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die bakkie was oop, dus was dit nie 'n geslote sisteem nie. Yster het met suurstof uit die lug gereageer (Fe + O₂ → ysteroksied), en die massa van die suurstof is bygevoeg. As jy die massa van die suurstof wat gereageer het, saam met die yster tel, is die massa behoue. Massa word nooit deur hitte geskep nie, en die wet geld ook vir chemiese veranderinge.","en":"The dish was open, so it was not a closed system. Iron reacted with oxygen from the air (Fe + O₂ → iron oxide), and the mass of the oxygen was added. If you count the mass of the oxygen that reacted together with the iron, mass is conserved. Mass is never created by heat, and the law also applies to chemical changes."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Chemiese reaksies en meganika","en":"Chemical reactions and mechanics"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t3-waterige-oplossings","title":{"af":"Reaksies in waterige oplossings","en":"Reactions in aqueous solution"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe stowwe in water oplos en gelei, presipitasiereaksies en ioontoetse kan uitvoer en interpreteer, en presipitasie-, suur-basis- en redoksreaksies kan herken.","en":"You will be able to explain how substances dissolve in water and conduct, carry out and interpret precipitation reactions and ion tests, and recognise precipitation, acid–base and redox reactions."},"summary":{"af":"## Water as polêre oplosmiddel\n\n- In 'n watermolekule is suurstof meer **elektronegatief** as waterstof, dus word die gedeelde elektrone nader aan die O-atoom getrek. O kry 'n **gedeeltelike negatiewe lading (δ−)** en elke H 'n **gedeeltelike positiewe lading (δ+)**.\n- Die molekule is **hoekig (gebuig)**, dus kanselleer die ladings nie uit nie: water is 'n **polêre molekule**.\n- Daarom los ioniese en polêre stowwe goed in water op.\n\n## Oplos: dissosiasie en ionisasie\n\n**Dissosiasie** is die proses waartydens 'n ioniese verbinding in ione opbreek.\n\n1. Die δ−-kant (O) van die watermolekules trek die **positiewe ione** aan; die δ+-kant (H) trek die **negatiewe ione** aan.\n2. Die ione word uit die kristalrooster losgetrek.\n3. Elke ioon word deur watermolekules omring (**hidrasie**).\n\n- NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)\n- Na_{2}SO_{4}(s) → 2Na^{+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) – 1 mol Na_{2}SO_{4} lewer 3 mol ione.\n\n**Ionisasie** is die proses waartydens ione tydens 'n chemiese reaksie gevorm word, bv. wanneer 'n kovalente stof met water reageer: HCl(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ) → H_{3}O^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq).\n\nNie alle ioniese verbindings is oplosbaar nie. **Onoplosbaar:** AgCl, AgBr, AgI, BaSO_{4}, BaCO_{3}, CaCO_{3}, PbI_{2}. **Oplosbaar:** alle nitrate en alle natrium-, kalium- en ammoniumsoute.\n\n## Elektroliete en geleidingsvermoë\n\n'n **Elektroliet** is 'n stof wat in water oplos en ione vorm, sodat die oplossing elektrisiteit gelei. Die stroom word deur **bewegende ione** gedra, nie deur elektrone nie.\n\n| Tipe | Ione in oplossing | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sterk elektroliet | dissosieer/ioniseer **volledig** – baie ione | NaCl, CuSO_{4}, HCl |\n| Swak elektroliet | ioniseer **gedeeltelik** – min ione | asynsuur (CH_{3}COOH) in asyn |\n| Nie-elektroliet | **geen** ione nie | suiker (sukrose), etanol |\n\nDie **geleidingsvermoë** van 'n oplossing neem toe met 'n hoër **konsentrasie** ione, 'n sterker elektroliet (**tipe stof**) en 'n hoër **temperatuur**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Gedistilleerde water gelei feitlik nie, want dit bevat byna geen ione nie. Kraanwater en damwater gelei wel, want opgeloste soute vorm ione – daarom is 'n haardroër naby die bad so gevaarlik.\n\n## Presipitasiereaksies\n\n'n **Presipitaat** is 'n onoplosbare vaste stof wat vorm wanneer twee oplossings gemeng word. Die ione ruil maats.\n\n- Volledige vergelyking: AgNO_{3}(aq) + NaCl(aq) → AgCl(s) + NaNO_{3}(aq)\n- Netto ioniese vergelyking: Ag^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq) → AgCl(s)\n- **Toeskouerione** (hier Na^{+} en NO_{3}^{−}) bly opgelos en neem nie aan die reaksie deel nie. Hulle word uit die netto ioniese vergelyking weggelaat.\n\n## Toetse vir anione\n\n| Ioon | Voeg by | Positiewe toets |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cl^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **wit** presipitaat (AgCl) wat nie in die suur oplos nie |\n| Br^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **roomkleurige (liggeel)** presipitaat (AgBr) wat nie oplos nie |\n| I^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **geel** presipitaat (AgI) wat nie oplos nie |\n| SO_{4}^{2−} | BaCl_{2}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **wit** presipitaat (BaSO_{4}) wat nie in die suur oplos nie |\n| CO_{3}^{2−} | verdunde suur (HCl of HNO_{3}) | **borrels** CO_{2}-gas wat **helder kalkwater melkerig** maak |\n\n- Ba^{2+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) → BaSO_{4}(s)\n- CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) + 2H^{+}(aq) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ)\n- Karbonate vorm **ook** 'n presipitaat met AgNO_{3} en met BaCl_{2} (bv. wit BaCO_{3}). Daarom voeg ons **salpetersuur** by: 'n karbonaatpresipitaat **los op en borrel** (CO_{2}), maar AgCl, AgBr, AgI en BaSO_{4} los **nie** op nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie HCl by die silwernitraattoets gebruik nie. HCl voeg self Cl^{−}-ione by, dus sal 'n wit AgCl-presipitaat vorm al was daar geen chloried in die monster nie.\n\n## Suur-basis- en redoksreaksies\n\n- **Suur-basis-reaksie:** 'n **proton (H^{+})** word van die suur na die basis oorgedra. Suur + basis → sout + water (**neutralisasie**): HCl(aq) + NaOH(aq) → NaCl(aq) + H_{2}O(ℓ); netto: H^{+}(aq) + OH^{−}(aq) → H_{2}O(ℓ). Suur + karbonaat → sout + water + CO_{2} is ook 'n suur-basis-reaksie. Voorbeelde: 'n teensuurmiddel neutraliseer oortollige maagsuur, en boere strooi landboukalk op suur grond.\n- **Redoksreaksie:** **elektrone** word oorgedra. **Oksidasie** is 'n verlies aan elektrone; **reduksie** is 'n wins aan elektrone. Bv. Zn(s) + Cu^{2+}(aq) → Zn^{2+}(aq) + Cu(s): Zn verloor 2 elektrone (word geoksideer) en Cu^{2+} wen 2 elektrone (word gereduseer). 'n Sinkstrook in blou kopersulfaatoplossing word met rooibruin koper bedek en die blou kleur verbleik.\n\n### Hoe herken jy die reaksietipe?\n\n| Tipe | Wat word oorgedra? | Kenteken |\n|---|---|---|\n| Presipitasie | niks – ione ruil maats | twee oplossings (aq) → onoplosbare vaste stof (s) |\n| Suur-basis | H^{+} (protone) | suur + basis → sout + water |\n| Redoks | elektrone | 'n ongebonde element (lading 0) word 'n ioon, of 'n ioon word 'n element |\n\n> **Wenk:** 'n Vaste stof as produk beteken nie outomaties presipitasie nie. In Zn + CuSO_{4} vorm vaste koper omdat Cu^{2+} elektrone wen – dit is redoks.","en":"## Water as a polar solvent\n\n- In a water molecule oxygen is more **electronegative** than hydrogen, so the shared electrons are pulled closer to the O atom. O gets a **partial negative charge (δ−)** and each H a **partial positive charge (δ+)**.\n- The molecule is **angular (bent)**, so the charges do not cancel out: water is a **polar molecule**.\n- That is why ionic and polar substances dissolve well in water.\n\n## Dissolving: dissociation and ionisation\n\n**Dissociation** is the process in which an ionic compound splits into ions.\n\n1. The δ− side (O) of the water molecules attracts the **positive ions**; the δ+ side (H) attracts the **negative ions**.\n2. The ions are pulled out of the crystal lattice.\n3. Each ion is surrounded by water molecules (**hydration**).\n\n- NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)\n- Na_{2}SO_{4}(s) → 2Na^{+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) – 1 mol Na_{2}SO_{4} gives 3 mol of ions.\n\n**Ionisation** is the process in which ions are formed during a chemical reaction, e.g. when a covalent substance reacts with water: HCl(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ) → H_{3}O^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq).\n\nNot all ionic compounds are soluble. **Insoluble:** AgCl, AgBr, AgI, BaSO_{4}, BaCO_{3}, CaCO_{3}, PbI_{2}. **Soluble:** all nitrates and all sodium, potassium and ammonium salts.\n\n## Electrolytes and conductivity\n\nAn **electrolyte** is a substance that dissolves in water and forms ions, so that the solution conducts electricity. The current is carried by **moving ions**, not by electrons.\n\n| Type | Ions in solution | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Strong electrolyte | dissociates/ionises **completely** – many ions | NaCl, CuSO_{4}, HCl |\n| Weak electrolyte | ionises **partially** – few ions | acetic acid (CH_{3}COOH) in vinegar |\n| Non-electrolyte | **no** ions | sugar (sucrose), ethanol |\n\nThe **conductivity** of a solution increases with a higher **concentration** of ions, a stronger electrolyte (**type of substance**) and a higher **temperature**.\n\n> **Remember:** Distilled water hardly conducts, because it contains almost no ions. Tap water and dam water do conduct, because dissolved salts form ions – that is why a hairdryer near the bath is so dangerous.\n\n## Precipitation reactions\n\nA **precipitate** is an insoluble solid that forms when two solutions are mixed. The ions swap partners.\n\n- Full equation: AgNO_{3}(aq) + NaCl(aq) → AgCl(s) + NaNO_{3}(aq)\n- Net ionic equation: Ag^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq) → AgCl(s)\n- **Spectator ions** (here Na^{+} and NO_{3}^{−}) stay dissolved and do not take part in the reaction. They are left out of the net ionic equation.\n\n## Tests for anions\n\n| Ion | Add | Positive test |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cl^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **white** precipitate (AgCl) that does not dissolve in the acid |\n| Br^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **cream (light yellow)** precipitate (AgBr) that does not dissolve |\n| I^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **yellow** precipitate (AgI) that does not dissolve |\n| SO_{4}^{2−} | BaCl_{2}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **white** precipitate (BaSO_{4}) that does not dissolve in the acid |\n| CO_{3}^{2−} | dilute acid (HCl or HNO_{3}) | **bubbles** of CO_{2} gas that turn **clear limewater milky** |\n\n- Ba^{2+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) → BaSO_{4}(s)\n- CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) + 2H^{+}(aq) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ)\n- Carbonates **also** form a precipitate with AgNO_{3} and with BaCl_{2} (e.g. white BaCO_{3}). That is why we add **nitric acid**: a carbonate precipitate **dissolves and fizzes** (CO_{2}), but AgCl, AgBr, AgI and BaSO_{4} do **not** dissolve.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not use HCl in the silver nitrate test. HCl adds Cl^{−} ions itself, so a white AgCl precipitate will form even if there was no chloride in the sample.\n\n## Acid–base and redox reactions\n\n- **Acid–base reaction:** a **proton (H^{+})** is transferred from the acid to the base. Acid + base → salt + water (**neutralisation**): HCl(aq) + NaOH(aq) → NaCl(aq) + H_{2}O(ℓ); net: H^{+}(aq) + OH^{−}(aq) → H_{2}O(ℓ). Acid + carbonate → salt + water + CO_{2} is also an acid–base reaction. Examples: an antacid neutralises excess stomach acid, and farmers spread agricultural lime on acidic soil.\n- **Redox reaction:** **electrons** are transferred. **Oxidation** is a loss of electrons; **reduction** is a gain of electrons. E.g. Zn(s) + Cu^{2+}(aq) → Zn^{2+}(aq) + Cu(s): Zn loses 2 electrons (is oxidised) and Cu^{2+} gains 2 electrons (is reduced). A zinc strip in blue copper sulfate solution becomes coated with red-brown copper and the blue colour fades.\n\n### How do you recognise the reaction type?\n\n| Type | What is transferred? | Clue |\n|---|---|---|\n| Precipitation | nothing – ions swap partners | two solutions (aq) → insoluble solid (s) |\n| Acid–base | H^{+} (protons) | acid + base → salt + water |\n| Redox | electrons | an uncombined element (charge 0) becomes an ion, or an ion becomes an element |\n\n> **Tip:** A solid product does not automatically mean precipitation. In Zn + CuSO_{4} solid copper forms because Cu^{2+} gains electrons – that is redox."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Polêre molekule","en":"Polar molecule"},"def":{"af":"'n Molekule met 'n ongelyke ladingsverspreiding: een kant is gedeeltelik negatief (δ−) en die ander kant gedeeltelik positief (δ+), bv. H₂O.","en":"A molecule with an unequal charge distribution: one side is partially negative (δ−) and the other side partially positive (δ+), e.g. H₂O."}},{"term":{"af":"Dissosiasie","en":"Dissociation"},"def":{"af":"Die proses waartydens 'n ioniese verbinding in ione opbreek, bv. NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq).","en":"The process in which an ionic compound splits into ions, e.g. NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq)."}},{"term":{"af":"Ionisasie","en":"Ionisation"},"def":{"af":"Die proses waartydens ione tydens 'n chemiese reaksie gevorm word, bv. wanneer HCl-gas met water reageer om H₃O⁺ en Cl⁻ te vorm.","en":"The process in which ions are formed during a chemical reaction, e.g. when HCl gas reacts with water to form H₃O⁺ and Cl⁻."}},{"term":{"af":"Hidrasie","en":"Hydration"},"def":{"af":"Die proses waartydens opgeloste ione deur watermolekules omring word.","en":"The process in which dissolved ions are surrounded by water molecules."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektroliet","en":"Electrolyte"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat in water oplos en ione vorm, sodat die oplossing elektrisiteit gelei.","en":"A substance that dissolves in water and forms ions, so that the solution conducts electricity."}},{"term":{"af":"Presipitaat","en":"Precipitate"},"def":{"af":"'n Onoplosbare vaste stof wat vorm wanneer twee oplossings gemeng word.","en":"An insoluble solid that forms when two solutions are mixed."}},{"term":{"af":"Toeskouerione","en":"Spectator ions"},"def":{"af":"Ione wat in die oplossing teenwoordig is maar nie aan die reaksie deelneem nie; hulle word uit die netto ioniese vergelyking weggelaat.","en":"Ions that are present in the solution but do not take part in the reaction; they are left out of the net ionic equation."}},{"term":{"af":"Suur-basis-reaksie","en":"Acid–base reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin protone (H⁺-ione) van 'n suur na 'n basis oorgedra word; suur + basis → sout + water.","en":"A reaction in which protons (H⁺ ions) are transferred from an acid to a base; acid + base → salt + water."}},{"term":{"af":"Redoksreaksie","en":"Redox reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin elektrone van een stof na 'n ander oorgedra word.","en":"A reaction in which electrons are transferred from one substance to another."}},{"term":{"af":"Oksidasie en reduksie","en":"Oxidation and reduction"},"def":{"af":"Oksidasie is 'n verlies aan elektrone; reduksie is 'n wins aan elektrone.","en":"Oxidation is a loss of electrons; reduction is a gain of electrons."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Sout los in water op","en":"Salt dissolves in water"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik, met verwysing na die watermolekules, wat gebeur wanneer natriumchloried (tafelsout) in water oplos. Skryf 'n vergelyking en verduidelik waarom die oplossing elektrisiteit gelei, terwyl vaste NaCl dit nie doen nie.","en":"Explain, with reference to the water molecules, what happens when sodium chloride (table salt) dissolves in water. Write an equation and explain why the solution conducts electricity, while solid NaCl does not."},"steps":[{"af":"Water is polêr: die O-atoom is δ− en die H-atome is δ+, en die molekule is hoekig.","en":"Water is polar: the O atom is δ− and the H atoms are δ+, and the molecule is angular."},{"af":"Die δ−-O-kante van watermolekules trek die Na^{+}-ione aan, en die δ+-H-kante trek die Cl^{−}-ione aan. Die ione word uit die kristalrooster getrek – dit is **dissosiasie**.","en":"The δ− O sides of water molecules attract the Na^{+} ions, and the δ+ H sides attract the Cl^{−} ions. The ions are pulled out of the crystal lattice – this is **dissociation**."},{"af":"Elke ioon word deur watermolekules omring (hidrasie): NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)","en":"Each ion is surrounded by water molecules (hydration): NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)"},{"af":"In vaste NaCl sit die ione vas in die rooster en kan nie beweeg nie. In die oplossing beweeg die ione vrylik en dra lading, dus gelei die oplossing – NaCl is 'n sterk elektroliet.","en":"In solid NaCl the ions are fixed in the lattice and cannot move. In the solution the ions move freely and carry charge, so the solution conducts – NaCl is a strong electrolyte."}],"answer":{"af":"Die ione dissosieer en word gehidreer: NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq). Die vrye, bewegende ione gelei die stroom.","en":"The ions dissociate and are hydrated: NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq). The free, moving ions conduct the current."}},{"title":{"af":"Presipitasie en die netto ioniese vergelyking","en":"Precipitation and the net ionic equation"},"problem":{"af":"Wanneer kleurlose lood(II)nitraatoplossing, Pb(NO₃)₂(aq), by kleurlose kaliumjodiedoplossing, KI(aq), gevoeg word, vorm 'n helder geel presipitaat van lood(II)jodied. (a) Skryf 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking met toestandsimbole. (b) Skryf die netto ioniese vergelyking. (c) Noem die toeskouerione.","en":"When colourless lead(II) nitrate solution, Pb(NO₃)₂(aq), is added to colourless potassium iodide solution, KI(aq), a bright yellow precipitate of lead(II) iodide forms. (a) Write a balanced equation with state symbols. (b) Write the net ionic equation. (c) Name the spectator ions."},"steps":[{"af":"Die ione ruil maats: Pb^{2+} verbind met I^{−} tot PbI_{2} (twee I^{−} vir elke Pb^{2+}), en K^{+} bly by NO_{3}^{−} as KNO_{3}.","en":"The ions swap partners: Pb^{2+} combines with I^{−} to form PbI_{2} (two I^{−} for each Pb^{2+}), and K^{+} stays with NO_{3}^{−} as KNO_{3}."},{"af":"(a) Pb(NO_{3})_{2}(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI_{2}(s) + 2KNO_{3}(aq). Kontroleer: Pb 1 = 1; N 2 = 2; O 6 = 6; K 2 = 2; I 2 = 2 ✓","en":"(a) Pb(NO_{3})_{2}(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI_{2}(s) + 2KNO_{3}(aq). Check: Pb 1 = 1; N 2 = 2; O 6 = 6; K 2 = 2; I 2 = 2 ✓"},{"af":"(b) Laat die ione wat onveranderd opgelos bly, weg: Pb^{2+}(aq) + 2I^{−}(aq) → PbI_{2}(s). Lading links: +2 + 2(−1) = 0 = lading regs ✓","en":"(b) Leave out the ions that stay dissolved unchanged: Pb^{2+}(aq) + 2I^{−}(aq) → PbI_{2}(s). Charge on the left: +2 + 2(−1) = 0 = charge on the right ✓"},{"af":"(c) K^{+} en NO_{3}^{−} bly opgelos (alle kalium- en nitraatsoute is oplosbaar) – dit is die toeskouerione.","en":"(c) K^{+} and NO_{3}^{−} stay dissolved (all potassium and nitrate salts are soluble) – they are the spectator ions."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Pb(NO₃)₂(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI₂(s) + 2KNO₃(aq); (b) Pb²⁺(aq) + 2I⁻(aq) → PbI₂(s); (c) K⁺ en NO₃⁻","en":"(a) Pb(NO₃)₂(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI₂(s) + 2KNO₃(aq); (b) Pb²⁺(aq) + 2I⁻(aq) → PbI₂(s); (c) K⁺ and NO₃⁻"}},{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer drie onbekende oplossings","en":"Identify three unknown solutions"},"problem":{"af":"Drie bottels sonder etikette bevat NaCl(aq), Na₂SO₄(aq) en Na₂CO₃(aq). Jy het verdunde salpetersuur (HNO₃), bariumchloriedoplossing (BaCl₂(aq)) en silwernitraatoplossing (AgNO₃(aq)). Beskryf hoe jy elke oplossing sal identifiseer.","en":"Three unlabelled bottles contain NaCl(aq), Na₂SO₄(aq) and Na₂CO₃(aq). You have dilute nitric acid (HNO₃), barium chloride solution (BaCl₂(aq)) and silver nitrate solution (AgNO₃(aq)). Describe how you would identify each solution."},"steps":[{"af":"Voeg verdunde HNO_{3} by 'n monster van elke oplossing. Die een wat **borrel** (CO_{2}-gas wat kalkwater melkerig maak), is Na_{2}CO_{3}: CO_{3}^{2−} + 2H^{+} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O","en":"Add dilute HNO_{3} to a sample of each solution. The one that **fizzes** (CO_{2} gas that turns limewater milky) is Na_{2}CO_{3}: CO_{3}^{2−} + 2H^{+} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O"},{"af":"Voeg BaCl_{2}(aq) by nuwe monsters van die oorblywende twee. Die een wat 'n **wit presipitaat** gee wat nie in HNO_{3} oplos nie (BaSO_{4}), is Na_{2}SO_{4}.","en":"Add BaCl_{2}(aq) to fresh samples of the remaining two. The one that gives a **white precipitate** that does not dissolve in HNO_{3} (BaSO_{4}) is Na_{2}SO_{4}."},{"af":"Voeg AgNO_{3}(aq) by die laaste oplossing. 'n **Wit presipitaat** (AgCl) wat nie in verdunde HNO_{3} oplos nie, bevestig NaCl: Ag^{+} + Cl^{−} → AgCl(s)","en":"Add AgNO_{3}(aq) to the last solution. A **white precipitate** (AgCl) that does not dissolve in dilute HNO_{3} confirms NaCl: Ag^{+} + Cl^{−} → AgCl(s)"},{"af":"Hoekom die karbonaat eerste? Karbonaat sou ook 'n wit presipitaat met BaCl_{2} en met AgNO_{3} gee. Deur dit eers met suur uit te skakel, voorkom jy verwarring.","en":"Why the carbonate first? Carbonate would also give a white precipitate with BaCl_{2} and with AgNO_{3}. By ruling it out with acid first, you avoid confusion."}],"answer":{"af":"Borrels met suur → Na₂CO₃; wit presipitaat met BaCl₂ → Na₂SO₄; wit presipitaat met AgNO₃ → NaCl","en":"Fizzing with acid → Na₂CO₃; white precipitate with BaCl₂ → Na₂SO₄; white precipitate with AgNO₃ → NaCl"}},{"title":{"af":"Herken die reaksietipe","en":"Recognise the reaction type"},"problem":{"af":"Identifiseer elke reaksie as presipitasie, suur-basis of redoks, en gee 'n rede. (a) Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g); (b) H₂SO₄(aq) + 2KOH(aq) → K₂SO₄(aq) + 2H₂O(ℓ); (c) CaCl₂(aq) + Na₂CO₃(aq) → CaCO₃(s) + 2NaCl(aq)","en":"Identify each reaction as precipitation, acid–base or redox, and give a reason. (a) Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g); (b) H₂SO₄(aq) + 2KOH(aq) → K₂SO₄(aq) + 2H₂O(ℓ); (c) CaCl₂(aq) + Na₂CO₃(aq) → CaCO₃(s) + 2NaCl(aq)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Mg is 'n ongebonde element (lading 0) wat Mg^{2+} word: Mg → Mg^{2+} + 2e^{−} (oksidasie). H^{+} wen elektrone en word H_{2}: 2H^{+} + 2e^{−} → H_{2} (reduksie). Elektrone word oorgedra → **redoks**.","en":"(a) Mg is an uncombined element (charge 0) that becomes Mg^{2+}: Mg → Mg^{2+} + 2e^{−} (oxidation). H^{+} gains electrons and becomes H_{2}: 2H^{+} + 2e^{−} → H_{2} (reduction). Electrons are transferred → **redox**."},{"af":"(b) 'n Suur (H_{2}SO_{4}) en 'n basis (KOH) vorm 'n sout en water. H^{+} word aan OH^{−} oorgedra: H^{+} + OH^{−} → H_{2}O → **suur-basis** (neutralisasie).","en":"(b) An acid (H_{2}SO_{4}) and a base (KOH) form a salt and water. H^{+} is transferred to OH^{−}: H^{+} + OH^{−} → H_{2}O → **acid–base** (neutralisation)."},{"af":"(c) Twee oplossings word gemeng en die ione ruil maats om die onoplosbare CaCO_{3}(s) te vorm: Ca^{2+}(aq) + CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) → CaCO_{3}(s). Geen elektrone of protone word oorgedra nie → **presipitasie**.","en":"(c) Two solutions are mixed and the ions swap partners to form the insoluble CaCO_{3}(s): Ca^{2+}(aq) + CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) → CaCO_{3}(s). No electrons or protons are transferred → **precipitation**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Redoks; (b) suur-basis; (c) presipitasie","en":"(a) Redox; (b) acid–base; (c) precipitation"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is water 'n polêre molekule?","en":"Why is water a polar molecule?"},"options":[{"af":"Waterstof is meer elektronegatief as suurstof, dus is die H-kante negatief.","en":"Hydrogen is more electronegative than oxygen, so the H sides are negative."},{"af":"Water bestaan uit H⁺- en O²⁻-ione.","en":"Water consists of H⁺ and O²⁻ ions."},{"af":"Suurstof is meer elektronegatief as waterstof en die molekule is hoekig, dus is die O-kant δ− en die H-kante δ+.","en":"Oxygen is more electronegative than hydrogen and the molecule is angular, so the O side is δ− and the H sides are δ+."},{"af":"Die molekule is lineêr en die elektrone word eweredig gedeel.","en":"The molecule is linear and the electrons are shared equally."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Suurstof trek die gedeelde elektrone sterker aan (hoër elektronegatiwiteit), dus is O δ− en H δ+. Omdat die molekule hoekig is, kanselleer hierdie ladings nie uit nie. Water is kovalent – dit bestaan nie uit ione nie.","en":"Oxygen attracts the shared electrons more strongly (higher electronegativity), so O is δ− and H is δ+. Because the molecule is angular, these charges do not cancel out. Water is covalent – it does not consist of ions."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke ioon by sy positiewe toets.","en":"Match each ion to its positive test."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Cl⁻","en":"Cl⁻"},"r":{"af":"Wit presipitaat met AgNO₃(aq) wat nie in HNO₃ oplos nie","en":"White precipitate with AgNO₃(aq) that does not dissolve in HNO₃"}},{"l":{"af":"I⁻","en":"I⁻"},"r":{"af":"Geel presipitaat met AgNO₃(aq)","en":"Yellow precipitate with AgNO₃(aq)"}},{"l":{"af":"SO₄²⁻","en":"SO₄²⁻"},"r":{"af":"Wit presipitaat met BaCl₂(aq) wat nie in HNO₃ oplos nie","en":"White precipitate with BaCl₂(aq) that does not dissolve in HNO₃"}},{"l":{"af":"CO₃²⁻","en":"CO₃²⁻"},"r":{"af":"Borrels met verdunde suur; die gas maak kalkwater melkerig","en":"Bubbles with dilute acid; the gas turns limewater milky"}}],"explain":{"af":"Halogeniede gee presipitate met silwernitraat (AgCl wit, AgBr roomkleurig, AgI geel); sulfaat gee wit BaSO₄ met bariumchloried; karbonaat gee CO₂-gas met suur, en CO₂ maak kalkwater melkerig.","en":"Halides give precipitates with silver nitrate (AgCl white, AgBr cream, AgI yellow); sulfate gives white BaSO₄ with barium chloride; carbonate gives CO₂ gas with acid, and CO₂ turns limewater milky."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gedistilleerde water is 'n goeie geleier van elektrisiteit.","en":"Distilled water is a good conductor of electricity."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gedistilleerde water bevat byna geen ione nie, dus gelei dit feitlik nie. Kraanwater gelei wel, omdat opgeloste soute ione vorm.","en":"False. Distilled water contains almost no ions, so it hardly conducts. Tap water does conduct, because dissolved salts form ions."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat gebeur wanneer kaliumnitraat (KNO₃) in water oplos?","en":"What happens when potassium nitrate (KNO₃) dissolves in water?"},"options":[{"af":"Die KNO₃-molekules versprei tussen die watermolekules.","en":"The KNO₃ molecules spread out between the water molecules."},{"af":"Die K-, N- en O-atome skei van mekaar.","en":"The K, N and O atoms separate from each other."},{"af":"Die verbinding reageer met water om KOH en HNO₃ te vorm.","en":"The compound reacts with water to form KOH and HNO₃."},{"af":"Die K⁺- en NO₃⁻-ione skei en word deur watermolekules omring.","en":"The K⁺ and NO₃⁻ ions separate and are surrounded by water molecules."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"KNO₃ is 'n ioniese verbinding, dus dissosieer dit: KNO₃(s) → K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq), en die ione word gehidreer. Ioniese verbindings bestaan nie uit molekules nie, die nitraatioon (NO₃⁻) bly as een eenheid bymekaar, en daar vorm geen nuwe stowwe nie.","en":"KNO₃ is an ionic compound, so it dissociates: KNO₃(s) → K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq), and the ions are hydrated. Ionic compounds do not consist of molecules, the nitrate ion (NO₃⁻) stays together as one unit, and no new substances form."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kant van 'n watermolekule word na 'n Cl⁻-ioon in oplossing aangetrek?","en":"Which side of a water molecule is attracted to a Cl⁻ ion in solution?"},"options":[{"af":"Die waterstofkant (δ+)","en":"The hydrogen side (δ+)"},{"af":"Die suurstofkant (δ−)","en":"The oxygen side (δ−)"},{"af":"Albei kante ewe veel","en":"Both sides equally"},{"af":"Geen kant nie, want water is nie-polêr","en":"Neither side, because water is non-polar"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Teenoorgestelde ladings trek mekaar aan: die negatiewe Cl⁻-ioon trek die gedeeltelik positiewe (δ+) H-kant van die watermolekule aan. Die δ−-O-kant word na positiewe ione soos Na⁺ aangetrek.","en":"Opposite charges attract: the negative Cl⁻ ion attracts the partially positive (δ+) H side of the water molecule. The δ− O side is attracted to positive ions such as Na⁺."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Suiker (sukrose) los in water op, maar die oplossing gelei nie elektrisiteit nie, omdat suiker nie ione in water vorm nie.","en":"Sugar (sucrose) dissolves in water, but the solution does not conduct electricity, because sugar does not form ions in water."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Suiker is 'n kovalente stof wat as heel molekules oplos – dit dissosieer of ioniseer nie. Sonder vrye ione kan die oplossing nie gelei nie, dus is suiker 'n nie-elektroliet.","en":"True. Sugar is a covalent substance that dissolves as whole molecules – it does not dissociate or ionise. Without free ions the solution cannot conduct, so sugar is a non-electrolyte."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vier oplossings het almal dieselfde konsentrasie en temperatuur. Watter een gelei elektrisiteit die swakste?","en":"Four solutions all have the same concentration and temperature. Which one conducts electricity the worst?"},"options":[{"af":"NaCl(aq)","en":"NaCl(aq)"},{"af":"CH₃COOH(aq) (asynsuur)","en":"CH₃COOH(aq) (acetic acid)"},{"af":"HCl(aq)","en":"HCl(aq)"},{"af":"CuSO₄(aq)","en":"CuSO₄(aq)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Asynsuur is 'n swak elektroliet: dit ioniseer net gedeeltelik, dus is daar die minste ione in oplossing. NaCl en CuSO₄ dissosieer volledig en HCl ioniseer volledig – dit is sterk elektroliete.","en":"Acetic acid is a weak electrolyte: it ionises only partially, so there are the fewest ions in solution. NaCl and CuSO₄ dissociate completely and HCl ionises completely – they are strong electrolytes."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Silwernitraatoplossing word by kaliumbromiedoplossing gevoeg. Die chemiese formule van die roomkleurige presipitaat is ___.","en":"Silver nitrate solution is added to potassium bromide solution. The chemical formula of the cream-coloured precipitate is ___."},"answers":{"af":["AgBr","AgBr(s)","silwerbromied"],"en":["AgBr","AgBr(s)","silver bromide"]},"explain":{"af":"Die ione ruil maats: Ag⁺ + Br⁻ → AgBr(s). KNO₃ bly opgelos, want alle kalium- en nitraatsoute is oplosbaar.","en":"The ions swap partners: Ag⁺ + Br⁻ → AgBr(s). KNO₃ stays dissolved, because all potassium and nitrate salts are soluble."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"1 mol CaCl₂ dissosieer volledig in water. Hoeveel mol ione word gevorm? ___ mol","en":"1 mol of CaCl₂ dissociates completely in water. How many moles of ions are formed? ___ mol"},"answers":{"af":["3","3 mol","drie"],"en":["3","3 mol","three"]},"explain":{"af":"CaCl₂(s) → Ca²⁺(aq) + 2Cl⁻(aq): 1 mol Ca²⁺ + 2 mol Cl⁻ = 3 mol ione. Onthou die 2 voor Cl⁻ – die onderskrif in CaCl₂ beteken twee chloriedione.","en":"CaCl₂(s) → Ca²⁺(aq) + 2Cl⁻(aq): 1 mol Ca²⁺ + 2 mol Cl⁻ = 3 mol of ions. Remember the 2 in front of Cl⁻ – the subscript in CaCl₂ means two chloride ions."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die netto ioniese vergelyking vir die reaksie AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)?","en":"What is the net ionic equation for the reaction AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)?"},"options":[{"af":"K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq) → KNO₃(s)","en":"K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq) → KNO₃(s)"},{"af":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(aq)","en":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(aq)"},{"af":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(s)","en":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(s)"},{"af":"AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)","en":"AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Net die ione wat die presipitaat vorm, verskyn in die netto ioniese vergelyking, en die presipitaat kry (s). K⁺ en NO₃⁻ is toeskouerione – KNO₃ is oplosbaar. AgI(aq) is verkeerd, want AgI is 'n onoplosbare vaste stof, en die laaste opsie is die volledige vergelyking, nie die netto ioniese vergelyking nie.","en":"Only the ions that form the precipitate appear in the net ionic equation, and the precipitate gets (s). K⁺ and NO₃⁻ are spectator ions – KNO₃ is soluble. AgI(aq) is wrong, because AgI is an insoluble solid, and the last option is the full equation, not the net ionic equation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die reaksie BaCl₂(aq) + K₂SO₄(aq) → BaSO₄(s) + 2KCl(aq) is die toeskouerione K⁺ en ___.","en":"In the reaction BaCl₂(aq) + K₂SO₄(aq) → BaSO₄(s) + 2KCl(aq) the spectator ions are K⁺ and ___."},"answers":{"af":["Cl⁻","Cl-","Cl−","Cl","chloried","chloriedioon","chloriedione"],"en":["Cl⁻","Cl-","Cl−","Cl","chloride","chloride ion","chloride ions"]},"explain":{"af":"Ba²⁺ en SO₄²⁻ vorm die presipitaat BaSO₄(s): Ba²⁺(aq) + SO₄²⁻(aq) → BaSO₄(s). K⁺ en Cl⁻ bly opgelos as KCl(aq) en neem nie deel nie – hulle is die toeskouerione.","en":"Ba²⁺ and SO₄²⁻ form the precipitate BaSO₄(s): Ba²⁺(aq) + SO₄²⁻(aq) → BaSO₄(s). K⁺ and Cl⁻ stay dissolved as KCl(aq) and do not take part – they are the spectator ions."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die reaksie Fe(s) + CuSO₄(aq) → FeSO₄(aq) + Cu(s) is 'n voorbeeld van ...","en":"The reaction Fe(s) + CuSO₄(aq) → FeSO₄(aq) + Cu(s) is an example of ..."},"options":[{"af":"'n presipitasiereaksie, omdat 'n vaste stof vorm.","en":"a precipitation reaction, because a solid forms."},{"af":"'n redoksreaksie, omdat Fe elektrone verloor en Cu²⁺ elektrone wen.","en":"a redox reaction, because Fe loses electrons and Cu²⁺ gains electrons."},{"af":"'n suur-basis-reaksie, omdat 'n sout vorm.","en":"an acid–base reaction, because a salt forms."},{"af":"'n ontbindingsreaksie, omdat CuSO₄ opbreek.","en":"a decomposition reaction, because CuSO₄ breaks up."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Fe (lading 0) word Fe²⁺: Fe → Fe²⁺ + 2e⁻ (oksidasie). Cu²⁺ word Cu (lading 0): Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu (reduksie). Elektrone word oorgedra, dus is dit redoks. Die vaste koper vorm nie deur ione wat maats ruil nie, en geen protone word oorgedra nie.","en":"Fe (charge 0) becomes Fe²⁺: Fe → Fe²⁺ + 2e⁻ (oxidation). Cu²⁺ becomes Cu (charge 0): Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu (reduction). Electrons are transferred, so it is redox. The solid copper does not form by ions swapping partners, and no protons are transferred."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Kleurlose oplossing gee 'n wit presipitaat met BaCl₂(aq). Wanneer verdunde HNO₃ bygevoeg word, los die presipitaat op en borrels vorm. Die oplossing bevat ___-ione.","en":"A colourless solution gives a white precipitate with BaCl₂(aq). When dilute HNO₃ is added, the precipitate dissolves and bubbles form. The solution contains ___ ions."},"answers":{"af":["karbonaat","karbonaatione","karbonaatioon","CO₃²⁻","CO3 2-","CO32-","CO3^2-","CO₃","CO3","carbonate"],"en":["carbonate","carbonate ions","carbonate ion","CO₃²⁻","CO3 2-","CO32-","CO3^2-","CO₃","CO3","karbonaat"]},"explain":{"af":"Sulfaat én karbonaat gee albei 'n wit presipitaat met BaCl₂. BaSO₄ los nie in salpetersuur op nie, maar BaCO₃ los op en vorm CO₂-borrels: BaCO₃(s) + 2H⁺(aq) → Ba²⁺(aq) + CO₂(g) + H₂O(ℓ). Dus is dit karbonaat.","en":"Sulfate and carbonate both give a white precipitate with BaCl₂. BaSO₄ does not dissolve in nitric acid, but BaCO₃ dissolves and forms CO₂ bubbles: BaCO₃(s) + 2H⁺(aq) → Ba²⁺(aq) + CO₂(g) + H₂O(ℓ). So it is carbonate."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder toets 'n onbekende oplossing vir chloriedione. Sy voeg AgNO₃(aq) by en kry 'n wit presipitaat. Om seker te maak dat dit nie 'n karbonaat is nie, voeg sy daarna verdunde soutsuur (HCl) in plaas van salpetersuur by. Watter evaluering van haar metode is korrek?","en":"A learner tests an unknown solution for chloride ions. She adds AgNO₃(aq) and gets a white precipitate. To make sure it is not a carbonate, she then adds dilute hydrochloric acid (HCl) instead of nitric acid. Which evaluation of her method is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die metode is geldig, want enige suur sal 'n karbonaatpresipitaat oplos.","en":"The method is valid, because any acid will dissolve a carbonate precipitate."},{"af":"Die metode is ongeldig, want HCl los AgCl op.","en":"The method is invalid, because HCl dissolves AgCl."},{"af":"Die metode is geldig, want HCl is 'n sterker suur en gee duideliker resultate.","en":"The method is valid, because HCl is a stronger acid and gives clearer results."},{"af":"Die metode is ongeldig, want HCl voeg self Cl⁻-ione by, sodat AgCl in elk geval vorm en 'n wit presipitaat niks bewys nie.","en":"The method is invalid, because HCl adds Cl⁻ ions itself, so AgCl forms anyway and a white precipitate proves nothing."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die Cl⁻-ione uit die HCl reageer met die oortollige Ag⁺ en vorm wit AgCl, selfs al het die monster geen chloried bevat nie (bv. as dit 'n karbonaat was). Die toets moet met salpetersuur gedoen word, want nitrate is oplosbaar en voeg geen ione by wat 'n presipitaat met Ag⁺ vorm nie. AgCl los nie in HCl op nie.","en":"The Cl⁻ ions from the HCl react with the excess Ag⁺ and form white AgCl, even if the sample contained no chloride (e.g. if it was a carbonate). The test must be done with nitric acid, because nitrates are soluble and add no ions that form a precipitate with Ag⁺. AgCl does not dissolve in HCl."}}]},{"id":"f10-t3-molbegrip","title":{"af":"Kwantitatiewe aspekte van chemiese verandering","en":"Quantitative aspects of chemical change"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal met die mol kan reken: massa, aantal deeltjies, gasvolume en konsentrasie omskakel, empiriese formules en kristalwater bepaal en molverhoudings in reaksies gebruik.","en":"You will be able to calculate with the mole: convert between mass, number of particles, gas volume and concentration, determine empirical formulae and water of crystallisation, and use mole ratios in reactions."},"summary":{"af":"## Die mol en Avogadro se getal\n\nChemici kan nie atome een vir een tel nie – hulle is te klein en daar is te veel. Daarom tel ons deeltjies in \"pakke\" van 6,02 × 10²³, net soos eiers in dosyne.\n\n- Die **mol** is die SI-eenheid vir **hoeveelheid stof** (simbool n).\n- **Een mol** van 'n stof is die hoeveelheid stof wat dieselfde aantal deeltjies bevat as wat daar atome in 12 g koolstof-12 is.\n- Daardie getal is **Avogadro se getal**: N_{A} = 6,02 × 10²³ deeltjies per mol.\n- Die deeltjies kan atome, molekules of ione wees – sê altyd watter een jy bedoel.\n\n> **Wenk:** As jy elke sekonde een deeltjie tel, sal dit jou ongeveer 1,9 × 10¹⁶ jaar neem om een mol te tel – meer as 'n miljoen keer die ouderdom van die heelal!\n\n## Molêre massa\n\n**Molêre massa (M)** is die massa van een mol van 'n stof, gemeet in g·mol⁻¹. Die relatiewe atoommassa op die periodieke tabel, in gram, is een mol atome: 12 g C en 24 g Mg bevat elk 6,02 × 10²³ atome.\n\nTel die relatiewe atoommassas volgens die formule bymekaar:\n\n- M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CaCO₃) = 40 + 12 + 3(16) = 100 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CuSO₄·5H₂O) = 63,5 + 32 + 4(16) + 5(18) = 249,5 g·mol⁻¹\n\nVir molekules (kovalente stowwe) praat ons van **relatiewe molekulêre massa** en vir ioniese verbindings van **relatiewe formulemassa**. Dit het geen eenheid nie. Molêre massa het dieselfde getalwaarde, maar met die eenheid g·mol⁻¹.\n\n## Die formules wat jy moet ken\n\n| Formule | Gebruik | Eenhede |\n|---|---|---|\n| n = [[m/M]] | massa ↔ mol | m in g, M in g·mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[N/N_{A}]] | aantal deeltjies ↔ mol | N_{A} = 6,02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[V/V_{m}]] | gasvolume by STD ↔ mol | V in dm³, V_{m} = 22,4 dm³·mol⁻¹ |\n| c = [[n/V]] = [[m/MV]] | konsentrasie | c in mol·dm⁻³, V in dm³ |\n\n### Molêre gasvolume\n\nEen mol van **enige gas** beslaan 22,4 dm³ by STD (standaardtemperatuur en -druk: 0 °C of 273 K en 101,3 kPa). Dit geld **net vir gasse** – nie vir vloeistowwe of vaste stowwe nie.\n\n### Konsentrasie\n\n**Konsentrasie** is die hoeveelheid opgeloste stof per kubieke desimeter (liter) oplossing. Die volume moet in dm³ wees: 1 dm³ = 1 L = 1 000 cm³, dus deel cm³ deur 1 000.\n\n## Persentasiesamestelling\n\n% element = [[aantal atome × A_{r}/M van verbinding]] × 100\n\nVoorbeeld: % O in H₂O = [[16/18]] × 100 = 88,89 %.\n\n## Empiriese en molekulêre formule\n\n- **Empiriese formule:** die eenvoudigste positiewe heelgetalverhouding van atome in 'n verbinding.\n- **Molekulêre formule:** die werklike aantal atome van elke soort in 'n molekuul.\n\nGlukose het die molekulêre formule C₆H₁₂O₆ en die empiriese formule CH₂O.\n\n**Metode (van persentasies):**\n\n1. Neem 100 g aan, sodat elke persentasie 'n massa in gram word.\n2. Bereken n = [[m/M]] vir elke element.\n3. Deel almal deur die kleinste n.\n4. Kry jy iets soos 1,5 of 1,33? Vermenigvuldig almal met 2 of 3 tot jy heelgetalle het.\n5. Molekulêre formule: faktor = [[M(molekulêr)/M(empiries)]]; vermenigvuldig elke onderskrif met die faktor.\n\n## Kristalwater\n\nSommige soute bevat watermolekules in hul kristalstruktuur – dit is **kristalwater**. Blou kopersulfaat, CuSO₄·5H₂O, word met verhitting wit, watervrye CuSO₄ as die water verdamp.\n\nOm x in 'n gehidreerde sout (sout·xH₂O) te bepaal:\n\n1. m(water) = m(gehidreerde sout) − m(watervrye sout)\n2. n(watervrye sout) = [[m/M]] en n(H₂O) = [[m/18]]\n3. x = [[n(H₂O)/n(sout)]]\n\n## Stoïgiometrie: berekeninge met molverhoudings\n\nDie koëffisiënte in 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking gee die **molverhouding**, nie die massaverhouding nie. In 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO reageer 2 mol Mg met 1 mol O₂ om 2 mol MgO te vorm.\n\n1. Skryf die gebalanseerde vergelyking.\n2. Skakel die gegewe hoeveelheid om na mol.\n3. Gebruik die molverhouding om die mol van die gevraagde stof te kry.\n4. Skakel om na wat gevra word (massa, gasvolume, aantal deeltjies of konsentrasie).\n\n> **Algemene foute:** cm³ nie na dm³ omgeskakel nie; molekules en atome verwar (1 mol H₂O bevat 3 mol atome); 22,4 dm³·mol⁻¹ vir 'n vloeistof of vaste stof gebruik; massas in plaas van mol met die molverhouding vermenigvuldig; 1,5 in 'n empiriese formule na 2 afgerond in plaas daarvan om met 2 te vermenigvuldig.","en":"## The mole and Avogadro's number\n\nChemists cannot count atoms one by one – they are too small and there are too many. So we count particles in \"packs\" of 6.02 × 10²³, just like eggs in dozens.\n\n- The **mole** is the SI unit for **amount of substance** (symbol n).\n- **One mole** of a substance is the amount of substance having the same number of particles as there are atoms in 12 g carbon-12.\n- That number is **Avogadro's number**: N_{A} = 6.02 × 10²³ particles per mole.\n- The particles can be atoms, molecules or ions – always say which one you mean.\n\n> **Tip:** If you counted one particle every second, it would take you about 1.9 × 10¹⁶ years to count one mole – more than a million times the age of the universe!\n\n## Molar mass\n\n**Molar mass (M)** is the mass of one mole of a substance, measured in g·mol⁻¹. The relative atomic mass on the periodic table, in grams, is one mole of atoms: 12 g C and 24 g Mg each contain 6.02 × 10²³ atoms.\n\nAdd up the relative atomic masses according to the formula:\n\n- M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CaCO₃) = 40 + 12 + 3(16) = 100 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CuSO₄·5H₂O) = 63.5 + 32 + 4(16) + 5(18) = 249.5 g·mol⁻¹\n\nFor molecules (covalent substances) we speak of **relative molecular mass** and for ionic compounds of **relative formula mass**. These have no unit. Molar mass has the same numerical value, but with the unit g·mol⁻¹.\n\n## The formulae you must know\n\n| Formula | Use | Units |\n|---|---|---|\n| n = [[m/M]] | mass ↔ moles | m in g, M in g·mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[N/N_{A}]] | number of particles ↔ moles | N_{A} = 6.02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[V/V_{m}]] | gas volume at STP ↔ moles | V in dm³, V_{m} = 22.4 dm³·mol⁻¹ |\n| c = [[n/V]] = [[m/MV]] | concentration | c in mol·dm⁻³, V in dm³ |\n\n### Molar gas volume\n\nOne mole of **any gas** occupies 22.4 dm³ at STP (standard temperature and pressure: 0 °C or 273 K and 101.3 kPa). This applies **only to gases** – not to liquids or solids.\n\n### Concentration\n\n**Concentration** is the amount of solute per cubic decimetre (litre) of solution. The volume must be in dm³: 1 dm³ = 1 L = 1 000 cm³, so divide cm³ by 1 000.\n\n## Percentage composition\n\n% element = [[number of atoms × A_{r}/M of compound]] × 100\n\nExample: % O in H₂O = [[16/18]] × 100 = 88.89 %.\n\n## Empirical and molecular formula\n\n- **Empirical formula:** the simplest positive integer ratio of atoms present in a compound.\n- **Molecular formula:** the actual number of atoms of each type in a molecule.\n\nGlucose has the molecular formula C₆H₁₂O₆ and the empirical formula CH₂O.\n\n**Method (from percentages):**\n\n1. Assume 100 g, so that each percentage becomes a mass in grams.\n2. Calculate n = [[m/M]] for each element.\n3. Divide all of them by the smallest n.\n4. Do you get something like 1.5 or 1.33? Multiply all of them by 2 or 3 until you have whole numbers.\n5. Molecular formula: factor = [[M(molecular)/M(empirical)]]; multiply every subscript by the factor.\n\n## Water of crystallisation\n\nSome salts contain water molecules in their crystal structure – this is **water of crystallisation**. Blue copper sulfate, CuSO₄·5H₂O, turns into white, anhydrous CuSO₄ when heated as the water evaporates.\n\nTo determine x in a hydrated salt (salt·xH₂O):\n\n1. m(water) = m(hydrated salt) − m(anhydrous salt)\n2. n(anhydrous salt) = [[m/M]] and n(H₂O) = [[m/18]]\n3. x = [[n(H₂O)/n(salt)]]\n\n## Stoichiometry: calculations with mole ratios\n\nThe coefficients in a balanced equation give the **mole ratio**, not the mass ratio. In 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO, 2 mol Mg reacts with 1 mol O₂ to form 2 mol MgO.\n\n1. Write the balanced equation.\n2. Convert the given quantity to moles.\n3. Use the mole ratio to get the moles of the substance asked for.\n4. Convert to what is asked (mass, gas volume, number of particles or concentration).\n\n> **Common mistakes:** not converting cm³ to dm³; confusing molecules and atoms (1 mol H₂O contains 3 mol atoms); using 22.4 dm³·mol⁻¹ for a liquid or solid; multiplying masses instead of moles by the mole ratio; rounding 1.5 in an empirical formula to 2 instead of multiplying by 2."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Mol","en":"Mole"},"def":{"af":"Die SI-eenheid vir hoeveelheid stof. Een mol is die hoeveelheid stof wat dieselfde aantal deeltjies bevat as wat daar atome in 12 g koolstof-12 is.","en":"The SI unit for amount of substance. One mole is the amount of substance having the same number of particles as there are atoms in 12 g carbon-12."}},{"term":{"af":"Avogadro se getal (N_A)","en":"Avogadro's number (N_A)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal deeltjies in een mol van 'n stof: 6,02 × 10²³ deeltjies per mol.","en":"The number of particles in one mole of a substance: 6.02 × 10²³ particles per mole."}},{"term":{"af":"Molêre massa (M)","en":"Molar mass (M)"},"def":{"af":"Die massa van een mol van 'n stof, gemeet in g·mol⁻¹.","en":"The mass of one mole of a substance, measured in g·mol⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Molêre gasvolume (V_m)","en":"Molar gas volume (V_m)"},"def":{"af":"Die volume wat een mol van enige gas beslaan: 22,4 dm³ by STD (0 °C / 273 K en 101,3 kPa).","en":"The volume occupied by one mole of any gas: 22.4 dm³ at STP (0 °C / 273 K and 101.3 kPa)."}},{"term":{"af":"Konsentrasie (c)","en":"Concentration (c)"},"def":{"af":"Die hoeveelheid opgeloste stof per kubieke desimeter (liter) oplossing: c = n/V, in mol·dm⁻³.","en":"The amount of solute per cubic decimetre (litre) of solution: c = n/V, in mol·dm⁻³."}},{"term":{"af":"Persentasiesamestelling","en":"Percentage composition"},"def":{"af":"Die persentasie van die massa van 'n verbinding wat deur elke element bygedra word.","en":"The percentage of the mass of a compound contributed by each element."}},{"term":{"af":"Empiriese formule","en":"Empirical formula"},"def":{"af":"Die eenvoudigste positiewe heelgetalverhouding van atome in 'n verbinding.","en":"The simplest positive integer ratio of atoms present in a compound."}},{"term":{"af":"Molekulêre formule","en":"Molecular formula"},"def":{"af":"Die werklike aantal atome van elke soort in 'n molekuul.","en":"The actual number of atoms of each type in a molecule."}},{"term":{"af":"Kristalwater","en":"Water of crystallisation"},"def":{"af":"Watermolekules wat deel van die kristalstruktuur van 'n sout is, bv. die 5H₂O in CuSO₄·5H₂O.","en":"Water molecules that form part of the crystal structure of a salt, e.g. the 5H₂O in CuSO₄·5H₂O."}},{"term":{"af":"Molverhouding","en":"Mole ratio"},"def":{"af":"Die verhouding waarin stowwe in mol reageer en vorm, gegee deur die koëffisiënte in 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking.","en":"The ratio in moles in which substances react and form, given by the coefficients in a balanced equation."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Van massa na mol, molekules en atome","en":"From mass to moles, molecules and atoms"},"problem":{"af":"Na rugbyoefening drink jy 'n sluk water van 9 g. Bereken (a) die hoeveelheid stof (mol) water, (b) die aantal watermolekules en (c) die totale aantal atome in die sluk.","en":"After rugby practice you drink a sip of water of 9 g. Calculate (a) the amount of substance (moles) of water, (b) the number of water molecules and (c) the total number of atoms in the sip."},"steps":[{"af":"Molêre massa: M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹","en":"Molar mass: M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹"},{"af":"(a) n = [[m/M]] = [[9/18]] = 0,5 mol","en":"(a) n = [[m/M]] = [[9/18]] = 0.5 mol"},{"af":"(b) N = n × N_{A} = 0,5 × 6,02 × 10²³ = 3,01 × 10²³ molekules","en":"(b) N = n × N_{A} = 0.5 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 3.01 × 10²³ molecules"},{"af":"(c) Elke H₂O-molekule bevat 3 atome (2 H + 1 O), dus is die aantal atome = 3 × 3,01 × 10²³ = 9,03 × 10²³ atome","en":"(c) Each H₂O molecule contains 3 atoms (2 H + 1 O), so the number of atoms = 3 × 3.01 × 10²³ = 9.03 × 10²³ atoms"}],"answer":{"af":"n = 0,5 mol; 3,01 × 10²³ molekules; 9,03 × 10²³ atome","en":"n = 0.5 mol; 3.01 × 10²³ molecules; 9.03 × 10²³ atoms"}},{"title":{"af":"Konsentrasie, molverhouding en gasvolume","en":"Concentration, mole ratio and gas volume"},"problem":{"af":"Magnesiumlint reageer met 100 cm³ soutsuur met 'n konsentrasie van 0,5 mol·dm⁻³ volgens: Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g). Al die suur reageer. Bereken (a) die hoeveelheid stof HCl, (b) die volume H₂-gas wat by STD vorm en (c) die massa magnesium wat reageer.","en":"Magnesium ribbon reacts with 100 cm³ of hydrochloric acid with a concentration of 0.5 mol·dm⁻³ according to: Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g). All the acid reacts. Calculate (a) the amount of substance of HCl, (b) the volume of H₂ gas formed at STP and (c) the mass of magnesium that reacts."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel die volume om na dm³: V = [[100/1 000]] = 0,1 dm³","en":"Convert the volume to dm³: V = [[100/1 000]] = 0.1 dm³"},{"af":"(a) n(HCl) = c × V = 0,5 × 0,1 = 0,05 mol","en":"(a) n(HCl) = c × V = 0.5 × 0.1 = 0.05 mol"},{"af":"(b) Molverhouding HCl : H₂ = 2 : 1, dus n(H₂) = [[0,05/2]] = 0,025 mol. V = n × V_{m} = 0,025 × 22,4 = 0,56 dm³","en":"(b) Mole ratio HCl : H₂ = 2 : 1, so n(H₂) = [[0.05/2]] = 0.025 mol. V = n × V_{m} = 0.025 × 22.4 = 0.56 dm³"},{"af":"(c) Molverhouding Mg : HCl = 1 : 2, dus n(Mg) = 0,025 mol. m = n × M = 0,025 × 24 = 0,6 g","en":"(c) Mole ratio Mg : HCl = 1 : 2, so n(Mg) = 0.025 mol. m = n × M = 0.025 × 24 = 0.6 g"}],"answer":{"af":"n(HCl) = 0,05 mol; V(H₂) = 0,56 dm³; m(Mg) = 0,6 g","en":"n(HCl) = 0.05 mol; V(H₂) = 0.56 dm³; m(Mg) = 0.6 g"}},{"title":{"af":"Empiriese en molekulêre formule","en":"Empirical and molecular formula"},"problem":{"af":"Die suiker in druiwe bestaan uit 40 % koolstof, 6,67 % waterstof en 53,33 % suurstof (volgens massa). Die molêre massa is 180 g·mol⁻¹. Bepaal (a) die empiriese formule en (b) die molekulêre formule.","en":"The sugar in grapes consists of 40% carbon, 6.67% hydrogen and 53.33% oxygen (by mass). The molar mass is 180 g·mol⁻¹. Determine (a) the empirical formula and (b) the molecular formula."},"steps":[{"af":"Neem 100 g aan: m(C) = 40 g, m(H) = 6,67 g, m(O) = 53,33 g","en":"Assume 100 g: m(C) = 40 g, m(H) = 6.67 g, m(O) = 53.33 g"},{"af":"n(C) = [[40/12]] = 3,33 mol; n(H) = [[6,67/1]] = 6,67 mol; n(O) = [[53,33/16]] = 3,33 mol","en":"n(C) = [[40/12]] = 3.33 mol; n(H) = [[6.67/1]] = 6.67 mol; n(O) = [[53.33/16]] = 3.33 mol"},{"af":"Deel deur die kleinste (3,33): C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1. (a) Empiriese formule = CH₂O","en":"Divide by the smallest (3.33): C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1. (a) Empirical formula = CH₂O"},{"af":"M(CH₂O) = 12 + 2(1) + 16 = 30 g·mol⁻¹. Faktor = [[180/30]] = 6","en":"M(CH₂O) = 12 + 2(1) + 16 = 30 g·mol⁻¹. Factor = [[180/30]] = 6"},{"af":"(b) Vermenigvuldig elke onderskrif met 6: molekulêre formule = C₆H₁₂O₆ (glukose)","en":"(b) Multiply every subscript by 6: molecular formula = C₆H₁₂O₆ (glucose)"}],"answer":{"af":"Empiriese formule CH₂O; molekulêre formule C₆H₁₂O₆","en":"Empirical formula CH₂O; molecular formula C₆H₁₂O₆"}},{"title":{"af":"Kristalwater in Engelse sout","en":"Water of crystallisation in Epsom salt"},"problem":{"af":"Engelse sout (MgSO₄·xH₂O) word gebruik om seer spiere ná 'n rugbywedstryd in te week. 'n Leerder verhit 4,92 g van die gehidreerde sout totdat al die kristalwater verdamp het. 2,40 g watervrye MgSO₄ bly oor. Bepaal die waarde van x.","en":"Epsom salt (MgSO₄·xH₂O) is used to soak sore muscles after a rugby match. A learner heats 4.92 g of the hydrated salt until all the water of crystallisation has evaporated. 2.40 g of anhydrous MgSO₄ remains. Determine the value of x."},"steps":[{"af":"m(H₂O) = m(gehidreerd) − m(watervry) = 4,92 − 2,40 = 2,52 g","en":"m(H₂O) = m(hydrated) − m(anhydrous) = 4.92 − 2.40 = 2.52 g"},{"af":"M(MgSO₄) = 24 + 32 + 4(16) = 120 g·mol⁻¹, dus n(MgSO₄) = [[2,40/120]] = 0,02 mol","en":"M(MgSO₄) = 24 + 32 + 4(16) = 120 g·mol⁻¹, so n(MgSO₄) = [[2.40/120]] = 0.02 mol"},{"af":"n(H₂O) = [[2,52/18]] = 0,14 mol","en":"n(H₂O) = [[2.52/18]] = 0.14 mol"},{"af":"x = [[n(H₂O)/n(MgSO₄)]] = [[0,14/0,02]] = 7, dus is die formule MgSO₄·7H₂O","en":"x = [[n(H₂O)/n(MgSO₄)]] = [[0.14/0.02]] = 7, so the formula is MgSO₄·7H₂O"}],"answer":{"af":"x = 7 (MgSO₄·7H₂O)","en":"x = 7 (MgSO₄·7H₂O)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die SI-eenheid vir hoeveelheid stof?","en":"What is the SI unit for amount of substance?"},"options":[{"af":"kilogram (kg)","en":"kilogram (kg)"},{"af":"gram per mol (g·mol⁻¹)","en":"gram per mole (g·mol⁻¹)"},{"af":"mol","en":"mole (mol)"},{"af":"kubieke desimeter (dm³)","en":"cubic decimetre (dm³)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die mol is die SI-eenheid vir hoeveelheid stof (n). Kilogram is die eenheid van massa, g·mol⁻¹ is die eenheid van molêre massa en dm³ is 'n volume-eenheid.","en":"The mole is the SI unit for amount of substance (n). Kilogram is the unit of mass, g·mol⁻¹ is the unit of molar mass and dm³ is a unit of volume."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke grootheid by sy eenheid.","en":"Match each quantity to its unit."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Molêre massa","en":"Molar mass"},"r":{"af":"g·mol⁻¹","en":"g·mol⁻¹"}},{"l":{"af":"Konsentrasie","en":"Concentration"},"r":{"af":"mol·dm⁻³","en":"mol·dm⁻³"}},{"l":{"af":"Molêre gasvolume","en":"Molar gas volume"},"r":{"af":"dm³·mol⁻¹","en":"dm³·mol⁻¹"}},{"l":{"af":"Hoeveelheid stof","en":"Amount of substance"},"r":{"af":"mol","en":"mol"}}],"explain":{"af":"Molêre massa is gram per mol (g·mol⁻¹); konsentrasie is mol per dm³ oplossing (mol·dm⁻³); molêre gasvolume is dm³ per mol (dm³·mol⁻¹); hoeveelheid stof word in mol gemeet.","en":"Molar mass is grams per mole (g·mol⁻¹); concentration is moles per dm³ of solution (mol·dm⁻³); molar gas volume is dm³ per mole (dm³·mol⁻¹); amount of substance is measured in moles."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Een mol van enige stof, ook vloeibare water en yster, beslaan 22,4 dm³ by STD.","en":"One mole of any substance, including liquid water and iron, occupies 22.4 dm³ at STP."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. 22,4 dm³·mol⁻¹ geld net vir gasse by STD. In vloeistowwe en vaste stowwe is die deeltjies baie nader aan mekaar: een mol vloeibare water (18 g) beslaan net sowat 18 cm³.","en":"False. 22.4 dm³·mol⁻¹ applies only to gases at STP. In liquids and solids the particles are much closer together: one mole of liquid water (18 g) occupies only about 18 cm³."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken die hoeveelheid stof in 11 g koolstofdioksied (CO₂). n = ___ mol","en":"Calculate the amount of substance in 11 g of carbon dioxide (CO₂). n = ___ mol"},"answers":{"af":["0,25","0.25","0,25 mol","0.25 mol","n = 0,25","n = 0.25","n = 0,25 mol","n = 0.25 mol"],"en":["0.25","0,25","0.25 mol","0,25 mol","n = 0.25","n = 0,25","n = 0.25 mol","n = 0,25 mol"]},"explain":{"af":"M(CO₂) = 12 + 2(16) = 44 g·mol⁻¹. n = m/M = 11/44 = 0,25 mol.","en":"M(CO₂) = 12 + 2(16) = 44 g·mol⁻¹. n = m/M = 11/44 = 0.25 mol."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling oor 1 mol waterstofgas (H₂) en 1 mol suurstofgas (O₂) is korrek?","en":"Which statement about 1 mol of hydrogen gas (H₂) and 1 mol of oxygen gas (O₂) is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle het dieselfde massa.","en":"They have the same mass."},{"af":"Die O₂ bevat meer molekules, want dit is swaarder.","en":"The O₂ contains more molecules, because it is heavier."},{"af":"Die H₂ bevat meer molekules, want H-atome is kleiner.","en":"The H₂ contains more molecules, because H atoms are smaller."},{"af":"Hulle bevat dieselfde aantal molekules, maar die O₂ het 'n groter massa.","en":"They contain the same number of molecules, but the O₂ has a greater mass."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Een mol van enige stof bevat 6,02 × 10²³ deeltjies, dus is die aantal molekules gelyk. Die massas verskil: M(H₂) = 2 g·mol⁻¹ en M(O₂) = 32 g·mol⁻¹, dus weeg 1 mol O₂ 32 g en 1 mol H₂ net 2 g.","en":"One mole of any substance contains 6.02 × 10²³ particles, so the number of molecules is equal. The masses differ: M(H₂) = 2 g·mol⁻¹ and M(O₂) = 32 g·mol⁻¹, so 1 mol O₂ has a mass of 32 g and 1 mol H₂ only 2 g."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die empiriese formule van glukose (C₆H₁₂O₆) is CH₂O.","en":"The empirical formula of glucose (C₆H₁₂O₆) is CH₂O."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Deel al die onderskrifte deur 6 (die grootste gemene faktor): C₆H₁₂O₆ → CH₂O. Dit is die eenvoudigste heelgetalverhouding C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1.","en":"True. Divide all the subscripts by 6 (the highest common factor): C₆H₁₂O₆ → CH₂O. This is the simplest whole-number ratio C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ammoniak vir kunsmis word gemaak volgens: N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g). As 2 mol N₂ volledig reageer, vorm ___ mol NH₃.","en":"Ammonia for fertiliser is made according to: N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g). If 2 mol N₂ reacts completely, ___ mol NH₃ forms."},"answers":{"af":["4","4 mol"],"en":["4","4 mol"]},"explain":{"af":"Die molverhouding N₂ : NH₃ = 1 : 2. Dus vorm 2 mol N₂ → 2 × 2 = 4 mol NH₃.","en":"The mole ratio N₂ : NH₃ = 1 : 2. So 2 mol N₂ → 2 × 2 = 4 mol NH₃."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel NH₃-molekules is daar in 3,4 g ammoniak?","en":"How many NH₃ molecules are there in 3.4 g of ammonia?"},"options":[{"af":"1,20 × 10²³","en":"1.20 × 10²³"},{"af":"4,82 × 10²³","en":"4.82 × 10²³"},{"af":"2,05 × 10²⁴","en":"2.05 × 10²⁴"},{"af":"0,20","en":"0.20"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"M(NH₃) = 14 + 3(1) = 17 g·mol⁻¹; n = 3,4/17 = 0,2 mol; N = 0,2 × 6,02 × 10²³ = 1,20 × 10²³ molekules. 4,82 × 10²³ is die aantal atome (4 per molekule), 2,05 × 10²⁴ kom van die massa direk met N_A te vermenigvuldig, en 0,20 is die aantal mol, nie molekules nie.","en":"M(NH₃) = 14 + 3(1) = 17 g·mol⁻¹; n = 3.4/17 = 0.2 mol; N = 0.2 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 1.20 × 10²³ molecules. 4.82 × 10²³ is the number of atoms (4 per molecule), 2.05 × 10²⁴ comes from multiplying the mass directly by N_A, and 0.20 is the number of moles, not molecules."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"4 g natriumhidroksied (NaOH) word in water opgelos om 250 cm³ oplossing te maak. Die konsentrasie van die oplossing is ___ mol·dm⁻³.","en":"4 g of sodium hydroxide (NaOH) is dissolved in water to make 250 cm³ of solution. The concentration of the solution is ___ mol·dm⁻³."},"answers":{"af":["0,4","0.4","0,40","0.40","0,4 mol·dm⁻³","0.4 mol·dm⁻³","0,4 mol/dm³","0.4 mol/dm³","0,4 mol.dm-3","0.4 mol.dm-3","0,4 mol/dm3","0.4 mol/dm3"],"en":["0.4","0,4","0.40","0,40","0.4 mol·dm⁻³","0,4 mol·dm⁻³","0.4 mol/dm³","0,4 mol/dm³","0.4 mol.dm-3","0,4 mol.dm-3","0.4 mol/dm3","0,4 mol/dm3"]},"explain":{"af":"M(NaOH) = 23 + 16 + 1 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; n = 4/40 = 0,1 mol. V = 250 cm³ = 0,25 dm³. c = n/V = 0,1/0,25 = 0,4 mol·dm⁻³. As jy vergeet om cm³ na dm³ om te skakel, kry jy die verkeerde 0,0004.","en":"M(NaOH) = 23 + 16 + 1 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; n = 4/40 = 0.1 mol. V = 250 cm³ = 0.25 dm³. c = n/V = 0.1/0.25 = 0.4 mol·dm⁻³. If you forget to convert cm³ to dm³, you get the wrong 0.0004."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Boere naby Brits gebruik ammoniumnitraat (NH₄NO₃) as kunsmis. Wat is die persentasie stikstof (volgens massa) in NH₄NO₃?","en":"Farmers near Brits use ammonium nitrate (NH₄NO₃) as fertiliser. What is the percentage of nitrogen (by mass) in NH₄NO₃?"},"options":[{"af":"17,5 %","en":"17.5%"},{"af":"60 %","en":"60%"},{"af":"58,33 %","en":"58.33%"},{"af":"35 %","en":"35%"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"M(NH₄NO₃) = 2(14) + 4(1) + 3(16) = 80 g·mol⁻¹. Daar is 2 N-atome: % N = (2 × 14)/80 × 100 = 35 %. 17,5 % tel net een N-atoom, 60 % is die persentasie suurstof, en 58,33 % kom van die O net een keer te tel (28/48).","en":"M(NH₄NO₃) = 2(14) + 4(1) + 3(16) = 80 g·mol⁻¹. There are 2 N atoms: % N = (2 × 14)/80 × 100 = 35%. 17.5% counts only one N atom, 60% is the percentage of oxygen, and 58.33% comes from counting the O only once (28/48)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Magnesium brand met 'n helder wit vlam: 2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s). Watter massa MgO vorm as 6 g Mg volledig reageer?","en":"Magnesium burns with a bright white flame: 2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s). What mass of MgO forms when 6 g Mg reacts completely?"},"options":[{"af":"5 g","en":"5 g"},{"af":"10 g","en":"10 g"},{"af":"20 g","en":"20 g"},{"af":"6 g","en":"6 g"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"n(Mg) = 6/24 = 0,25 mol. Molverhouding Mg : MgO = 2 : 2 = 1 : 1, dus n(MgO) = 0,25 mol. M(MgO) = 24 + 16 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; m = 0,25 × 40 = 10 g. 5 g en 20 g gebruik die verhouding verkeerd, en 6 g vergeet dat die suurstof ook massa byvoeg.","en":"n(Mg) = 6/24 = 0.25 mol. Mole ratio Mg : MgO = 2 : 2 = 1 : 1, so n(MgO) = 0.25 mol. M(MgO) = 24 + 16 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; m = 0.25 × 40 = 10 g. 5 g and 20 g use the ratio incorrectly, and 6 g forgets that the oxygen also adds mass."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Propaan (C₃H₈) is 'n hoofbestanddeel van die gas in braaigasbottels: C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(ℓ). As 22 g propaan volledig verbrand, watter volume CO₂ vorm by STD? V = ___ dm³","en":"Propane (C₃H₈) is a main component of the gas in braai gas bottles: C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(ℓ). If 22 g of propane burns completely, what volume of CO₂ forms at STP? V = ___ dm³"},"answers":{"af":["33,6","33.6","33,6 dm³","33.6 dm³","33,6 dm3","33.6 dm3","V = 33,6","V = 33.6","V = 33,6 dm³","V = 33.6 dm³"],"en":["33.6","33,6","33.6 dm³","33,6 dm³","33.6 dm3","33,6 dm3","V = 33.6","V = 33,6","V = 33.6 dm³","V = 33,6 dm³"]},"explain":{"af":"M(C₃H₈) = 3(12) + 8(1) = 44 g·mol⁻¹; n = 22/44 = 0,5 mol. Molverhouding C₃H₈ : CO₂ = 1 : 3, dus n(CO₂) = 1,5 mol. V = n × V_m = 1,5 × 22,4 = 33,6 dm³.","en":"M(C₃H₈) = 3(12) + 8(1) = 44 g·mol⁻¹; n = 22/44 = 0.5 mol. Mole ratio C₃H₈ : CO₂ = 1 : 3, so n(CO₂) = 1.5 mol. V = n × V_m = 1.5 × 22.4 = 33.6 dm³."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hematiet is 'n ystererts met 70 % yster en 30 % suurstof (volgens massa). Anel kry die molverhouding Fe : O = 1,25 : 1,875 = 1 : 1,5 en skryf die empiriese formule as FeO₂ (sy rond 1,5 op na 2). Johan skryf Fe₂O₃. Wie is korrek?","en":"Haematite is an iron ore with 70% iron and 30% oxygen (by mass). Anel gets the mole ratio Fe : O = 1.25 : 1.875 = 1 : 1.5 and writes the empirical formula as FeO₂ (she rounds 1.5 up to 2). Johan writes Fe₂O₃. Who is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Anel, want 'n molverhouding word altyd na die naaste heelgetal afgerond.","en":"Anel, because a mole ratio is always rounded to the nearest whole number."},{"af":"Geeneen nie; die formule is FeO, want 1,5 moet na 1 afgerond word.","en":"Neither; the formula is FeO, because 1.5 must be rounded down to 1."},{"af":"Johan, want 'n verhouding van 1 : 1,5 moet met 2 vermenigvuldig word om die heelgetalle 2 : 3 te kry.","en":"Johan, because a ratio of 1 : 1.5 must be multiplied by 2 to get the whole numbers 2 : 3."},{"af":"Albei, want FeO₂ en Fe₂O₃ het dieselfde persentasie yster.","en":"Both, because FeO₂ and Fe₂O₃ have the same percentage of iron."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Johan is korrek. 1,5 is nie naby 'n heelgetal nie, dus mag jy nie afrond nie – vermenigvuldig met 2: 1 : 1,5 → 2 : 3, dus Fe₂O₃. Kontroleer: % Fe in Fe₂O₃ = 112/160 × 100 = 70 %, maar in FeO₂ is dit 56/88 × 100 = 63,64 %, so Anel se formule pas nie by die data nie.","en":"Johan is correct. 1.5 is not close to a whole number, so you may not round – multiply by 2: 1 : 1.5 → 2 : 3, so Fe₂O₃. Check: % Fe in Fe₂O₃ = 112/160 × 100 = 70%, but in FeO₂ it is 56/88 × 100 = 63.64%, so Anel's formula does not fit the data."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder verhit blou kopersulfaat (CuSO₄·xH₂O) om x te bepaal, maar stop te gou: die oorblyfsel is nog effens blou. Hoe beïnvloed dit die berekende waarde van x?","en":"A learner heats blue copper sulfate (CuSO₄·xH₂O) to determine x, but stops too soon: the residue is still slightly blue. How does this affect the calculated value of x?"},"options":[{"af":"x sal te klein wees, want minder water is verwyder as wat werklik in die kristal was.","en":"x will be too small, because less water was removed than was actually in the crystal."},{"af":"x sal te groot wees, want die oorblyfsel is swaarder.","en":"x will be too large, because the residue is heavier."},{"af":"x sal korrek wees, want die molverhouding verander nie.","en":"x will be correct, because the mole ratio does not change."},{"af":"x kan glad nie bereken word nie, want watervrye kopersulfaat is wit.","en":"x cannot be calculated at all, because anhydrous copper sulfate is white."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die blou kleur wys daar is nog kristalwater in die oorblyfsel. Die berekende massa water (gehidreerd − oorblyfsel) is dus te klein, en die 'watervrye' massa is te groot. n(H₂O) is te klein en n(CuSO₄) te groot, dus is x = n(H₂O)/n(CuSO₄) te klein. Verhit tot die oorblyfsel heeltemal wit is en die massa nie meer verander nie.","en":"The blue colour shows there is still water of crystallisation in the residue. The calculated mass of water (hydrated − residue) is therefore too small, and the 'anhydrous' mass is too large. n(H₂O) is too small and n(CuSO₄) too large, so x = n(H₂O)/n(CuSO₄) is too small. Heat until the residue is completely white and the mass no longer changes."}}]},{"id":"f10-t3-vektore-beweging","title":{"af":"Vektore, skalare en beweging in een dimensie","en":"Vectors, scalars and motion in one dimension"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal vektore en skalare kan onderskei, resultante kan bepaal en beweging met woorde, berekeninge en x–t-, v–t- en a–t-grafieke kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to distinguish between vectors and scalars, determine resultants and describe motion with words, calculations and x–t, v–t and a–t graphs."},"summary":{"af":"## Skalare en vektore\n\n- **Skalaar:** 'n fisiese hoeveelheid met slegs grootte. Voorbeelde: massa, tyd, afstand, spoed, energie, temperatuur.\n- **Vektor:** 'n fisiese hoeveelheid met grootte én rigting. Voorbeelde: verplasing, snelheid, versnelling, krag, gewig.\n\n'n Vektor word as 'n pyl geteken: die **lengte** van die pyl stel die grootte voor en die **pylpunt** wys die rigting. Gee 'n vektorantwoord altyd met 'n rigting, bv. 250 m oos of +250 m.\n\n## Resultant van vektore in een dimensie\n\nDie **resultante vektor** is die enkele vektor wat dieselfde effek het as twee of meer vektore saam. Vir vektore op een reguit lyn:\n\n1. Kies 'n positiewe rigting (bv. oos = +, wes = −).\n2. Gee elke vektor die regte teken.\n3. Tel die vektore algebraïes bymekaar.\n4. Gee die grootte én die rigting: + is die positiewe rigting, − die teenoorgestelde rigting.\n\nVektore in dieselfde rigting tel op; vektore in teenoorgestelde rigtings trek van mekaar af. As jy hulle kop-aan-stert teken, loop die resultant van die stert van die eerste pyl na die kop van die laaste pyl.\n\n## Verwysingsraamwerk, posisie, afstand en verplasing\n\n- **Eendimensionele beweging:** beweging langs 'n reguit lyn.\n- **Verwysingsraamwerk:** 'n verwysingspunt (oorsprong) gekombineer met 'n stel rigtings, bv. die Brits-taxistaanplek as 0 m met oos as positief.\n- **Posisie (x):** waar 'n voorwerp relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt is. Posisie kan positief of negatief wees.\n- **Afstand:** die lengte van die pad wat afgelê is. Afstand is 'n skalaar en altyd positief.\n- **Verplasing (Δx):** verandering in posisie: Δx = x_{f} − x_{i}. Dit is 'n vektor wat van die beginposisie na die eindposisie wys.\n\n> **Onthou!** Hardloop jy een rondte van 400 m op die atletiekbaan, is jou afstand 400 m maar jou verplasing **nul**, want jy eindig waar jy begin het.\n\n## Spoed, snelheid en versnelling\n\n| Hoeveelheid | Definisie | Formule | Eenheid |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Gemiddelde spoed (skalaar) | totale afstand gedeel deur totale tyd | [[afstand/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Gemiddelde snelheid (vektor) | tempo van verandering van posisie (totale verplasing gedeel deur totale tyd) | v = [[Δx/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Versnelling (vektor) | tempo van verandering van snelheid | a = [[Δv/Δt]] = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] | m·s⁻² |\n\n- **Oombliklike snelheid:** die verplasing gedeel deur 'n baie klein (infinitesimale) tydinterval – die snelheid op 'n spesifieke oomblik.\n- **Oombliklike spoed:** die grootte van die oombliklike snelheid. 'n Motor se spoedmeter wys oombliklike spoed – dit wys nie die rigting nie.\n- **Omskakeling:** 1 km·h⁻¹ = [[1 000 m/3 600 s]], dus km·h⁻¹ ÷ 3,6 = m·s⁻¹ en m·s⁻¹ × 3,6 = km·h⁻¹.\n\n### Positiewe en negatiewe versnelling\n\nDie teken van a gee net sy **rigting**. Of 'n voorwerp vinniger of stadiger gaan, hang van a én v saam af:\n\n- a en v in **dieselfde** rigting → die spoed neem toe.\n- a en v in **teenoorgestelde** rigtings → die spoed neem af; die voorwerp **vertraag**.\n\n'n Negatiewe versnelling beteken dus nie altyd vertraging nie: 'n motor wat wes (−) ry en al vinniger gaan, het 'n negatiewe snelheid én 'n negatiewe versnelling.\n\n## Beweging in grafieke\n\n| Beweging | x–t-grafiek | v–t-grafiek | a–t-grafiek |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stilstaande voorwerp | horisontale lyn (x konstant) | lyn op die t-as (v = 0) | lyn op die t-as (a = 0) |\n| Konstante snelheid | reguit skuins lyn | horisontale lyn by v ≠ 0 | lyn op die t-as (a = 0) |\n| Konstante versnelling uit rus | kromme wat al steiler word | reguit skuins lyn deur die oorsprong | horisontale lyn by a ≠ 0 |\n\n**Wat jy uit 'n grafiek kry:**\n\n- **Gradiënt van die x–t-grafiek** = snelheid. Hoe steiler, hoe vinniger; 'n lyn wat afwaarts loop, beteken beweging in die negatiewe rigting. By 'n kromme gee die gradiënt van die **raaklyn** die oombliklike snelheid.\n- **Gradiënt van die v–t-grafiek** = versnelling.\n- **Oppervlakte onder die v–t-grafiek** = verplasing. Gebruik reghoeke (l × b), driehoeke (½ × basis × hoogte) en trapesiums. Oppervlakte onder die t-as is 'n negatiewe verplasing.\n- **Oppervlakte onder die a–t-grafiek** = verandering in snelheid (Δv).\n\nOp 'n **tikkerband** (bewegingsdiagram) beteken gelyke spasies tussen die kolletjies konstante snelheid. Spasies wat groter word, beteken die spoed neem toe; spasies wat kleiner word, beteken die voorwerp vertraag.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** afstand en verplasing verwar; die rigting by 'n vektorantwoord vergeet; km·h⁻¹ nie na m·s⁻¹ omgeskakel nie; dink dat a = 0 as v = 0 (by die draaipunt is v = 0, maar a is nie nul nie); die y-waarde van 'n x–t-grafiek as die snelheid lees in plaas van die gradiënt te bereken.","en":"## Scalars and vectors\n\n- **Scalar:** a physical quantity having magnitude only. Examples: mass, time, distance, speed, energy, temperature.\n- **Vector:** a physical quantity having both magnitude and direction. Examples: displacement, velocity, acceleration, force, weight.\n\nA vector is drawn as an arrow: the **length** of the arrow represents the magnitude and the **arrowhead** shows the direction. Always give a vector answer with a direction, e.g. 250 m east or +250 m.\n\n## Resultant of vectors in one dimension\n\nThe **resultant vector** is the single vector having the same effect as two or more vectors together. For vectors on one straight line:\n\n1. Choose a positive direction (e.g. east = +, west = −).\n2. Give each vector the correct sign.\n3. Add the vectors algebraically.\n4. Give the magnitude and the direction: + is the positive direction, − the opposite direction.\n\nVectors in the same direction add up; vectors in opposite directions subtract from each other. If you draw them head-to-tail, the resultant runs from the tail of the first arrow to the head of the last arrow.\n\n## Frame of reference, position, distance and displacement\n\n- **One-dimensional motion:** motion along a straight line.\n- **Frame of reference:** a reference point (origin) combined with a set of directions, e.g. the Brits taxi rank as 0 m with east as positive.\n- **Position (x):** where an object is relative to a reference point. Position can be positive or negative.\n- **Distance:** the length of the path travelled. Distance is a scalar and always positive.\n- **Displacement (Δx):** change in position: Δx = x_{f} − x_{i}. It is a vector pointing from the initial position to the final position.\n\n> **Remember!** If you run one 400 m lap on the athletics track, your distance is 400 m but your displacement is **zero**, because you end where you started.\n\n## Speed, velocity and acceleration\n\n| Quantity | Definition | Formula | Unit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Average speed (scalar) | total distance divided by total time | [[distance/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Average velocity (vector) | rate of change of position (total displacement divided by total time) | v = [[Δx/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Acceleration (vector) | rate of change of velocity | a = [[Δv/Δt]] = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] | m·s⁻² |\n\n- **Instantaneous velocity:** the displacement divided by a very small (infinitesimal) time interval – the velocity at a specific moment.\n- **Instantaneous speed:** the magnitude of the instantaneous velocity. A car's speedometer shows instantaneous speed – it does not show the direction.\n- **Conversion:** 1 km·h⁻¹ = [[1 000 m/3 600 s]], so km·h⁻¹ ÷ 3.6 = m·s⁻¹ and m·s⁻¹ × 3.6 = km·h⁻¹.\n\n### Positive and negative acceleration\n\nThe sign of a only gives its **direction**. Whether an object goes faster or slower depends on a and v together:\n\n- a and v in the **same** direction → the speed increases.\n- a and v in **opposite** directions → the speed decreases; the object **decelerates**.\n\nSo a negative acceleration does not always mean deceleration: a car driving west (−) and going faster and faster has a negative velocity and a negative acceleration.\n\n## Motion in graphs\n\n| Motion | x–t graph | v–t graph | a–t graph |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stationary object | horizontal line (x constant) | line on the t-axis (v = 0) | line on the t-axis (a = 0) |\n| Constant velocity | straight sloping line | horizontal line at v ≠ 0 | line on the t-axis (a = 0) |\n| Constant acceleration from rest | curve that gets steeper and steeper | straight sloping line through the origin | horizontal line at a ≠ 0 |\n\n**What you get from a graph:**\n\n- **Gradient of the x–t graph** = velocity. The steeper, the faster; a line running downwards means motion in the negative direction. For a curve, the gradient of the **tangent** gives the instantaneous velocity.\n- **Gradient of the v–t graph** = acceleration.\n- **Area under the v–t graph** = displacement. Use rectangles (l × b), triangles (½ × base × height) and trapeziums. Area below the t-axis is a negative displacement.\n- **Area under the a–t graph** = change in velocity (Δv).\n\nOn a **ticker tape** (motion diagram), equal spaces between the dots mean constant velocity. Spaces that get bigger mean the speed is increasing; spaces that get smaller mean the object is slowing down.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** confusing distance and displacement; forgetting the direction in a vector answer; not converting km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹; thinking that a = 0 when v = 0 (at the turning point v = 0, but a is not zero); reading the y-value of an x–t graph as the velocity instead of calculating the gradient."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Skalaar","en":"Scalar"},"def":{"af":"'n Fisiese hoeveelheid met slegs grootte, bv. massa, tyd, afstand en spoed.","en":"A physical quantity having magnitude only, e.g. mass, time, distance and speed."}},{"term":{"af":"Vektor","en":"Vector"},"def":{"af":"'n Fisiese hoeveelheid met grootte én rigting, bv. verplasing, snelheid, versnelling en krag.","en":"A physical quantity having both magnitude and direction, e.g. displacement, velocity, acceleration and force."}},{"term":{"af":"Resultante vektor","en":"Resultant vector"},"def":{"af":"Die enkele vektor wat dieselfde effek het as twee of meer vektore saam.","en":"The single vector having the same effect as two or more vectors together."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwysingsraamwerk","en":"Frame of reference"},"def":{"af":"'n Verwysingspunt (oorsprong) gekombineer met 'n stel rigtings.","en":"A reference point (origin) combined with a set of directions."}},{"term":{"af":"Afstand","en":"Distance"},"def":{"af":"Die lengte van die pad wat afgelê is (skalaar).","en":"The length of the path travelled (scalar)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verplasing","en":"Displacement"},"def":{"af":"Verandering in posisie: Δx = x_f − x_i (vektor).","en":"Change in position: Δx = x_f − x_i (vector)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemiddelde spoed","en":"Average speed"},"def":{"af":"Die totale afstand afgelê gedeel deur die totale tyd geneem (skalaar).","en":"The total distance travelled divided by the total time taken (scalar)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemiddelde snelheid","en":"Average velocity"},"def":{"af":"Die tempo van verandering van posisie: totale verplasing gedeel deur totale tyd (vektor).","en":"The rate of change of position: total displacement divided by total time (vector)."}},{"term":{"af":"Oombliklike snelheid","en":"Instantaneous velocity"},"def":{"af":"Die verplasing gedeel deur 'n baie klein (infinitesimale) tydinterval; die snelheid op 'n spesifieke oomblik.","en":"The displacement divided by a very small (infinitesimal) time interval; the velocity at a specific moment."}},{"term":{"af":"Versnelling","en":"Acceleration"},"def":{"af":"Die tempo van verandering van snelheid: a = Δv/Δt, in m·s⁻² (vektor).","en":"The rate of change of velocity: a = Δv/Δt, in m·s⁻² (vector)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Afstand, verplasing, spoed en snelheid","en":"Distance, displacement, speed and velocity"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo stap van sy huis in Brits 400 m oos na die kafee en dan 150 m wes na sy vriend se huis, langs dieselfde reguit straat. Die hele staptog duur 5 minute. Bereken (a) die afstand, (b) die verplasing, (c) die gemiddelde spoed en (d) die gemiddelde snelheid.","en":"Thabo walks from his house in Brits 400 m east to the café and then 150 m west to his friend's house, along the same straight street. The whole walk takes 5 minutes. Calculate (a) the distance, (b) the displacement, (c) the average speed and (d) the average velocity."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies oos as positief. (a) Afstand = 400 + 150 = 550 m","en":"Choose east as positive. (a) Distance = 400 + 150 = 550 m"},{"af":"(b) Δx = (+400) + (−150) = +250 m, dus 250 m oos","en":"(b) Δx = (+400) + (−150) = +250 m, so 250 m east"},{"af":"Skakel die tyd om na sekondes: Δt = 5 × 60 = 300 s. (c) Gemiddelde spoed = [[afstand/Δt]] = [[550/300]] = 1,83 m·s⁻¹","en":"Convert the time to seconds: Δt = 5 × 60 = 300 s. (c) Average speed = [[distance/Δt]] = [[550/300]] = 1.83 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(d) Gemiddelde snelheid = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[250/300]] = 0,83 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"(d) Average velocity = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[250/300]] = 0.83 m·s⁻¹ east"}],"answer":{"af":"Afstand 550 m; verplasing 250 m oos; gemiddelde spoed 1,83 m·s⁻¹; gemiddelde snelheid 0,83 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"Distance 550 m; displacement 250 m east; average speed 1.83 m·s⁻¹; average velocity 0.83 m·s⁻¹ east"}},{"title":{"af":"Resultant van saamlynige vektore","en":"Resultant of collinear vectors"},"problem":{"af":"By die skool se sportdag trek twee spanne toutrek. Aan die westekant trek Pieter met 350 N en Sipho met 400 N. Aan die oostekant trek Johan met 380 N en Kagiso met 420 N. Al die kragte is langs dieselfde reguit lyn. Bepaal die resultante krag op die tou.","en":"At the school's sports day two teams play tug-of-war. On the west side Pieter pulls with 350 N and Sipho with 400 N. On the east side Johan pulls with 380 N and Kagiso with 420 N. All the forces are along the same straight line. Determine the resultant force on the rope."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies oos as positief. Wes-kragte kry 'n negatiewe teken: −350 N en −400 N. Oos-kragte: +380 N en +420 N","en":"Choose east as positive. West forces get a negative sign: −350 N and −400 N. East forces: +380 N and +420 N"},{"af":"F_{R} = (+380) + (+420) + (−350) + (−400)","en":"F_{R} = (+380) + (+420) + (−350) + (−400)"},{"af":"F_{R} = +800 − 750 = +50 N","en":"F_{R} = +800 − 750 = +50 N"},{"af":"Die positiewe teken beteken oos: die resultante krag is 50 N oos, dus trek die oostelike span die sterkste","en":"The positive sign means east: the resultant force is 50 N east, so the eastern team pulls the hardest"}],"answer":{"af":"F_R = 50 N oos","en":"F_R = 50 N east"}},{"title":{"af":"Versnelling en vertraging van 'n taxi","en":"Acceleration and deceleration of a taxi"},"problem":{"af":"'n Minibustaxi trek by 'n robot in Brits weg en bereik 72 km·h⁻¹ in 8 s, terwyl dit in 'n reguit lyn oos ry. By die volgende robot rem die taxi eenvormig van 20 m·s⁻¹ tot stilstand in 4 s. Bereken die versnelling (a) terwyl die taxi wegtrek en (b) terwyl dit rem.","en":"A minibus taxi pulls away at a robot in Brits and reaches 72 km·h⁻¹ in 8 s while driving in a straight line east. At the next robot the taxi brakes uniformly from 20 m·s⁻¹ to a standstill in 4 s. Calculate the acceleration (a) while the taxi pulls away and (b) while it brakes."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies oos as positief. Skakel om: v_{f} = 72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹","en":"Choose east as positive. Convert: v_{f} = 72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(a) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[20 − 0/8]] = 2,5 m·s⁻², dus 2,5 m·s⁻² oos","en":"(a) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[20 − 0/8]] = 2.5 m·s⁻², so 2.5 m·s⁻² east"},{"af":"(b) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[0 − 20/4]] = −5 m·s⁻²","en":"(b) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[0 − 20/4]] = −5 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"Die negatiewe teken beteken wes. Die versnelling is teenoor die snelheid (oos), dus vertraag die taxi: a = 5 m·s⁻² wes","en":"The negative sign means west. The acceleration is opposite to the velocity (east), so the taxi decelerates: a = 5 m·s⁻² west"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 2,5 m·s⁻² oos; (b) 5 m·s⁻² wes (die taxi vertraag)","en":"(a) 2.5 m·s⁻² east; (b) 5 m·s⁻² west (the taxi decelerates)"}},{"title":{"af":"Gradiënt en oppervlakte van 'n v–t-grafiek","en":"Gradient and area of a v–t graph"},"problem":{"af":"'n Motor ry langs 'n reguit pad na Hartbeespoortdam (oos is positief). Die v–t-grafiek word so beskryf: die snelheid neem eenvormig toe van 0 m·s⁻¹ by t = 0 s tot 12 m·s⁻¹ by t = 4 s; dit bly konstant op 12 m·s⁻¹ tot t = 10 s; dan neem dit eenvormig af tot 0 m·s⁻¹ by t = 13 s. Bereken (a) die versnelling in elke deel, (b) die totale verplasing en (c) die gemiddelde snelheid vir die 13 s.","en":"A car drives along a straight road to Hartbeespoort Dam (east is positive). The v–t graph is described as follows: the velocity increases uniformly from 0 m·s⁻¹ at t = 0 s to 12 m·s⁻¹ at t = 4 s; it stays constant at 12 m·s⁻¹ until t = 10 s; then it decreases uniformly to 0 m·s⁻¹ at t = 13 s. Calculate (a) the acceleration in each part, (b) the total displacement and (c) the average velocity for the 13 s."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Versnelling = gradiënt. 0–4 s: a = [[12 − 0/4 − 0]] = 3 m·s⁻² oos; 4–10 s: horisontale lyn, dus a = 0 m·s⁻²; 10–13 s: a = [[0 − 12/13 − 10]] = −4 m·s⁻², dus 4 m·s⁻² wes","en":"(a) Acceleration = gradient. 0–4 s: a = [[12 − 0/4 − 0]] = 3 m·s⁻² east; 4–10 s: horizontal line, so a = 0 m·s⁻²; 10–13 s: a = [[0 − 12/13 − 10]] = −4 m·s⁻², so 4 m·s⁻² west"},{"af":"(b) Verplasing = oppervlakte onder die grafiek: driehoek [[1/2]] × 4 × 12 = 24 m; reghoek 6 × 12 = 72 m; driehoek [[1/2]] × 3 × 12 = 18 m","en":"(b) Displacement = area under the graph: triangle [[1/2]] × 4 × 12 = 24 m; rectangle 6 × 12 = 72 m; triangle [[1/2]] × 3 × 12 = 18 m"},{"af":"Totale Δx = 24 + 72 + 18 = 114 m oos","en":"Total Δx = 24 + 72 + 18 = 114 m east"},{"af":"(c) Gemiddelde snelheid = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[114/13]] = 8,77 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"(c) Average velocity = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[114/13]] = 8.77 m·s⁻¹ east"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 3 m·s⁻² oos; 0 m·s⁻²; 4 m·s⁻² wes. (b) 114 m oos. (c) 8,77 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"(a) 3 m·s⁻² east; 0 m·s⁻²; 4 m·s⁻² west. (b) 114 m east. (c) 8.77 m·s⁻¹ east"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n vektorhoeveelheid?","en":"Which one of the following is a vector quantity?"},"options":[{"af":"Massa","en":"Mass"},{"af":"Spoed","en":"Speed"},{"af":"Afstand","en":"Distance"},{"af":"Verplasing","en":"Displacement"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Verplasing het grootte én rigting (bv. 250 m oos), dus is dit 'n vektor. Massa, spoed en afstand het net grootte – hulle is skalare. Spoed is die lokval: snelheid is die vektor, spoed die skalaar.","en":"Displacement has magnitude and direction (e.g. 250 m east), so it is a vector. Mass, speed and distance have magnitude only – they are scalars. Speed is the trap: velocity is the vector, speed the scalar."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by die regte definisie.","en":"Match each term to the correct definition."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Afstand","en":"Distance"},"r":{"af":"Die lengte van die pad afgelê","en":"The length of the path travelled"}},{"l":{"af":"Verplasing","en":"Displacement"},"r":{"af":"Verandering in posisie","en":"Change in position"}},{"l":{"af":"Spoed","en":"Speed"},"r":{"af":"Tempo van verandering van afstand","en":"Rate of change of distance"}},{"l":{"af":"Snelheid","en":"Velocity"},"r":{"af":"Tempo van verandering van posisie","en":"Rate of change of position"}},{"l":{"af":"Versnelling","en":"Acceleration"},"r":{"af":"Tempo van verandering van snelheid","en":"Rate of change of velocity"}}],"explain":{"af":"Afstand en spoed is skalare (pad en tempo langs die pad). Verplasing, snelheid en versnelling is vektore: verplasing is die verandering in posisie, snelheid die tempo waarteen posisie verander, en versnelling die tempo waarteen snelheid verander.","en":"Distance and speed are scalars (path and rate along the path). Displacement, velocity and acceleration are vectors: displacement is the change in position, velocity the rate at which position changes, and acceleration the rate at which velocity changes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Atleet hardloop een volle rondte van 400 m op die skool se atletiekbaan en eindig presies waar sy begin het. Haar verplasing is nul, al het sy 'n afstand van 400 m afgelê.","en":"An athlete runs one full 400 m lap on the school's athletics track and ends exactly where she started. Her displacement is zero, even though she covered a distance of 400 m."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Verplasing is die verandering in posisie: begin- en eindposisie is dieselfde, dus Δx = 0. Afstand is die lengte van die pad, en dit is 400 m.","en":"True. Displacement is the change in position: the initial and final positions are the same, so Δx = 0. Distance is the length of the path, and that is 400 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Voorwerp beweeg met 'n konstante snelheid in die positiewe rigting. Watter beskrywing van sy grafieke is korrek?","en":"An object moves with a constant velocity in the positive direction. Which description of its graphs is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die x–t-grafiek is 'n horisontale lyn.","en":"The x–t graph is a horizontal line."},{"af":"Die x–t-grafiek is 'n reguit lyn met 'n konstante positiewe gradiënt.","en":"The x–t graph is a straight line with a constant positive gradient."},{"af":"Die v–t-grafiek is 'n reguit lyn met 'n positiewe gradiënt.","en":"The v–t graph is a straight line with a positive gradient."},{"af":"Die a–t-grafiek is 'n horisontale lyn bo die t-as.","en":"The a–t graph is a horizontal line above the t-axis."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Konstante snelheid beteken die posisie verander elke sekonde ewe veel, dus is die x–t-grafiek 'n reguit skuins lyn (gradiënt = snelheid). 'n Horisontale x–t-lyn is 'n stilstaande voorwerp. 'n Skuins v–t-lyn en 'n a–t-lyn bo die t-as beskryf konstante versnelling – by konstante snelheid is a = 0.","en":"Constant velocity means the position changes by the same amount every second, so the x–t graph is a straight sloping line (gradient = velocity). A horizontal x–t line is a stationary object. A sloping v–t line and an a–t line above the t-axis describe constant acceleration – at constant velocity a = 0."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die spoedgrens op 'n Suid-Afrikaanse snelweg is 120 km·h⁻¹. Skakel dit om na m·s⁻¹ (rond af tot twee desimale plekke): ___ m·s⁻¹","en":"The speed limit on a South African freeway is 120 km·h⁻¹. Convert it to m·s⁻¹ (round off to two decimal places): ___ m·s⁻¹"},"answers":{"af":["33,33","33,33 m·s⁻¹","33,33 m/s","33,33 m.s-1","33,33 m·s-1","33,33 ms-1","33,33 m s^-1","33.33","33.33 m·s⁻¹","33.33 m/s","33.33 m.s-1","33.33 m·s-1","33.33 ms-1","33.33 m s^-1"],"en":["33.33","33.33 m·s⁻¹","33.33 m/s","33.33 m.s-1","33.33 m·s-1","33.33 ms-1","33.33 m s^-1","33,33","33,33 m·s⁻¹","33,33 m/s","33,33 m.s-1","33,33 m·s-1","33,33 ms-1","33,33 m s^-1"]},"explain":{"af":"Deel deur 3,6: 120 ÷ 3,6 = 33,33 m·s⁻¹. Dit is omdat 1 km = 1 000 m en 1 h = 3 600 s, dus 120 × 1 000 ÷ 3 600 = 33,33 m·s⁻¹.","en":"Divide by 3.6: 120 ÷ 3.6 = 33.33 m·s⁻¹. This is because 1 km = 1 000 m and 1 h = 3 600 s, so 120 × 1 000 ÷ 3 600 = 33.33 m·s⁻¹."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Negatiewe versnelling beteken altyd dat 'n voorwerp stadiger beweeg.","en":"Negative acceleration always means that an object is slowing down."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. Die teken van a gee net die rigting. 'n Voorwerp vertraag net as a en v in teenoorgestelde rigtings is. 'n Motor wat in die negatiewe rigting ry en al vinniger gaan, het 'n negatiewe versnelling, maar sy spoed neem toe.","en":"False. The sign of a only gives the direction. An object slows down only if a and v are in opposite directions. A car driving in the negative direction and going faster and faster has a negative acceleration, but its speed increases."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Taxi se spoedmeter wys 60 km·h⁻¹. Watter hoeveelheid lees die spoedmeter af?","en":"A taxi's speedometer shows 60 km·h⁻¹. Which quantity does the speedometer read?"},"options":[{"af":"Oombliklike spoed","en":"Instantaneous speed"},{"af":"Gemiddelde spoed","en":"Average speed"},{"af":"Oombliklike snelheid","en":"Instantaneous velocity"},{"af":"Gemiddelde snelheid","en":"Average velocity"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die spoedmeter wys hoe vinnig die taxi op daardie oomblik ry (oombliklik), maar nie in watter rigting nie. Sonder rigting is dit 'n skalaar: oombliklike spoed, nie snelheid nie. Gemiddelde spoed sou die totale afstand gedeel deur die totale tyd vir die hele rit wees.","en":"The speedometer shows how fast the taxi is moving at that moment (instantaneous), but not in which direction. Without direction it is a scalar: instantaneous speed, not velocity. Average speed would be the total distance divided by the total time for the whole trip."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Fietsryer ry langs 'n reguit pad 12 km noord, dan 5 km suid en dan 3 km noord. Die resultante verplasing is ___ km noord.","en":"A cyclist rides along a straight road 12 km north, then 5 km south and then 3 km north. The resultant displacement is ___ km north."},"answers":{"af":["10","10 km","10 km noord","10 km N"],"en":["10","10 km","10 km north","10 km N"]},"explain":{"af":"Kies noord as positief: Δx = (+12) + (−5) + (+3) = +10 km, dus 10 km noord. Die afstand is 12 + 5 + 3 = 20 km, maar die vraag vra die verplasing.","en":"Choose north as positive: Δx = (+12) + (−5) + (+3) = +10 km, so 10 km north. The distance is 12 + 5 + 3 = 20 km, but the question asks for the displacement."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Hond op 'n plaas naby Brits hardloop 30 m oos in 6 s, draai om en hardloop 10 m wes in 4 s. Wat is die hond se gemiddelde snelheid vir die hele 10 s?","en":"A dog on a farm near Brits runs 30 m east in 6 s, turns around and runs 10 m west in 4 s. What is the dog's average velocity for the whole 10 s?"},"options":[{"af":"4 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"4 m·s⁻¹ east"},{"af":"3,75 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"3.75 m·s⁻¹ east"},{"af":"2 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"2 m·s⁻¹ east"},{"af":"2 m·s⁻¹ wes","en":"2 m·s⁻¹ west"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kies oos as positief. Δx = (+30) + (−10) = +20 m; Δt = 6 + 4 = 10 s. v = Δx/Δt = 20/10 = 2 m·s⁻¹ oos. 4 m·s⁻¹ is die gemiddelde spoed (40 m/10 s), 3,75 m·s⁻¹ is die gemiddeld van die twee spoede (5 en 2,5), en wes is die verkeerde rigting.","en":"Choose east as positive. Δx = (+30) + (−10) = +20 m; Δt = 6 + 4 = 10 s. v = Δx/Δt = 20/10 = 2 m·s⁻¹ east. 4 m·s⁻¹ is the average speed (40 m/10 s), 3.75 m·s⁻¹ is the average of the two speeds (5 and 2.5), and west is the wrong direction."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Motor op 'n reguit pad buite Brits versnel eenvormig van 5 m·s⁻¹ tot 25 m·s⁻¹ in 4 s. Die grootte van die versnelling is ___ m·s⁻².","en":"A car on a straight road outside Brits accelerates uniformly from 5 m·s⁻¹ to 25 m·s⁻¹ in 4 s. The magnitude of the acceleration is ___ m·s⁻²."},"answers":{"af":["5","5 m·s⁻²","5 m/s²","5 m/s^2","5 m.s-2","5 m·s-2","5 ms-2","5 m s^-2"],"en":["5","5 m·s⁻²","5 m/s²","5 m/s^2","5 m.s-2","5 m·s-2","5 ms-2","5 m s^-2"]},"explain":{"af":"a = (v_f − v_i)/Δt = (25 − 5)/4 = 20/4 = 5 m·s⁻². 'n Algemene fout is om 25/4 = 6,25 te bereken en die beginsnelheid te vergeet.","en":"a = (v_f − v_i)/Δt = (25 − 5)/4 = 20/4 = 5 m·s⁻². A common mistake is to calculate 25/4 = 6.25 and forget the initial velocity."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die x–t-grafiek van 'n taxi is 'n reguit lyn van x = 10 m by t = 0 s tot x = 40 m by t = 6 s. Wat is die taxi se snelheid?","en":"The x–t graph of a taxi is a straight line from x = 10 m at t = 0 s to x = 40 m at t = 6 s. What is the taxi's velocity?"},"options":[{"af":"5 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"5 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"},{"af":"6,67 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"6.67 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"},{"af":"1,67 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"1.67 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"},{"af":"0,2 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"0.2 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Snelheid = gradiënt van die x–t-grafiek = Δx/Δt = (40 − 10)/(6 − 0) = 30/6 = 5 m·s⁻¹. 6,67 kom van 40/6 (die beginposisie vergeet), 1,67 van 10/6, en 0,2 van Δt/Δx (die gradiënt omgekeer).","en":"Velocity = gradient of the x–t graph = Δx/Δt = (40 − 10)/(6 − 0) = 30/6 = 5 m·s⁻¹. 6.67 comes from 40/6 (forgetting the initial position), 1.67 from 10/6, and 0.2 from Δt/Δx (the gradient upside down)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n v–t-grafiek is 'n reguit lyn van 4 m·s⁻¹ by t = 0 s tot 16 m·s⁻¹ by t = 6 s (positiewe rigting). Die verplasing in hierdie 6 s is ___ m.","en":"A v–t graph is a straight line from 4 m·s⁻¹ at t = 0 s to 16 m·s⁻¹ at t = 6 s (positive direction). The displacement in these 6 s is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["60","60 m","Δx = 60","Δx = 60 m","+60","+60 m"],"en":["60","60 m","Δx = 60","Δx = 60 m","+60","+60 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Verplasing = oppervlakte onder die v–t-grafiek. Die vorm is 'n trapesium: ½(4 + 16) × 6 = 60 m. Of: reghoek 4 × 6 = 24 m plus driehoek ½ × 6 × 12 = 36 m, saam 60 m. 96 m (16 × 6) of 36 m (net die driehoek) is algemene foute.","en":"Displacement = area under the v–t graph. The shape is a trapezium: ½(4 + 16) × 6 = 60 m. Or: rectangle 4 × 6 = 24 m plus triangle ½ × 6 × 12 = 36 m, together 60 m. 96 m (16 × 6) or 36 m (only the triangle) are common mistakes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die v–t-grafiek van 'n motor (oos is positief) is 'n reguit lyn van 20 m·s⁻¹ by t = 0 s tot −10 m·s⁻¹ by t = 7,5 s; dit sny die t-as by t = 5 s. Lerato sê: \"By t = 5 s staan die motor stil, dus is sy versnelling daar nul.\" Evalueer haar stelling.","en":"The v–t graph of a car (east is positive) is a straight line from 20 m·s⁻¹ at t = 0 s to −10 m·s⁻¹ at t = 7.5 s; it cuts the t-axis at t = 5 s. Lerato says: \"At t = 5 s the car is stationary, so its acceleration there is zero.\" Evaluate her statement."},"options":[{"af":"Sy is korrek: as v = 0 is, moet a ook 0 wees.","en":"She is correct: if v = 0, a must also be 0."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd: die gradiënt van die v–t-grafiek is oral −4 m·s⁻², dus is a = 4 m·s⁻² wes, ook by t = 5 s.","en":"She is wrong: the gradient of the v–t graph is −4 m·s⁻² everywhere, so a = 4 m·s⁻² west, also at t = 5 s."},{"af":"Sy is korrek: die grafiek sny die t-as by t = 5 s, en daar is die gradiënt nul.","en":"She is correct: the graph cuts the t-axis at t = 5 s, and there the gradient is zero."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd: by t = 5 s is a = 4 m·s⁻² oos, want die motor draai om.","en":"She is wrong: at t = 5 s, a = 4 m·s⁻² east, because the car turns around."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Versnelling is die gradiënt, nie die waarde van v nie. Gradiënt = (−10 − 20)/7,5 = −4 m·s⁻², dieselfde oral op die reguit lyn. By t = 5 s is v = 0 (die draaipunt), maar a is steeds 4 m·s⁻² wes. Die motor vertraag terwyl dit oos ry, en versnel dan wes.","en":"Acceleration is the gradient, not the value of v. Gradient = (−10 − 20)/7.5 = −4 m·s⁻², the same everywhere on the straight line. At t = 5 s, v = 0 (the turning point), but a is still 4 m·s⁻² west. The car slows down while driving east, and then speeds up westwards."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Taxi ry van die Brits-taxistaanplek na Hartbeespoort en terug na dieselfde staanplek. Die odometer wys dat die taxi altesaam 50 km gery het, en die rit het 1 h geduur. Leerder 1 sê die gemiddelde snelheid was 50 km·h⁻¹. Leerder 2 sê die gemiddelde snelheid was 0 km·h⁻¹, maar die gemiddelde spoed was 50 km·h⁻¹. Wie is korrek?","en":"A taxi drives from the Brits taxi rank to Hartbeespoort and back to the same rank. The odometer shows that the taxi travelled 50 km in total, and the trip took 1 h. Learner 1 says the average velocity was 50 km·h⁻¹. Learner 2 says the average velocity was 0 km·h⁻¹, but the average speed was 50 km·h⁻¹. Who is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Leerder 1, want spoed en snelheid is dieselfde ding.","en":"Learner 1, because speed and velocity are the same thing."},{"af":"Leerder 1, want die taxi het die hele tyd beweeg.","en":"Learner 1, because the taxi was moving the whole time."},{"af":"Geeneen nie: die gemiddelde snelheid is 25 km·h⁻¹, want die taxi was net 25 km van die staanplek af.","en":"Neither: the average velocity is 25 km·h⁻¹, because the taxi was only 25 km from the rank."},{"af":"Leerder 2, want die verplasing is nul (die taxi eindig waar hy begin het), terwyl die afstand 50 km is.","en":"Learner 2, because the displacement is zero (the taxi ends where it started), while the distance is 50 km."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Gemiddelde snelheid = verplasing/tyd = 0 km/1 h = 0 km·h⁻¹, want die begin- en eindposisie is dieselfde. Gemiddelde spoed = afstand/tyd = 50 km/1 h = 50 km·h⁻¹. Leerder 1 verwar spoed (skalaar) met snelheid (vektor), en 25 km is 'n posisie halfpad, nie die verplasing vir die hele rit nie.","en":"Average velocity = displacement/time = 0 km/1 h = 0 km·h⁻¹, because the initial and final positions are the same. Average speed = distance/time = 50 km/1 h = 50 km·h⁻¹. Learner 1 confuses speed (scalar) with velocity (vector), and 25 km is a position halfway, not the displacement for the whole trip."}}]},{"id":"f10-t3-bewegingsvergelykings","title":{"af":"Bewegingsvergelykings","en":"Equations of motion"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die vier bewegingsvergelykings kan kies en gebruik om snelheid, versnelling, verplasing en tyd vir eenvormig versnelde beweging te bereken – ook in probleme met meer as een stadium.","en":"You will be able to choose and use the four equations of motion to calculate velocity, acceleration, displacement and time for uniformly accelerated motion – also in multi-stage problems."},"summary":{"af":"## Wanneer gebruik jy die bewegingsvergelykings?\n\nDie vier bewegingsvergelykings beskryf beweging in 'n reguit lyn met **konstante (eenvormige) versnelling**. As die versnelling verander (bv. 'n taxi wat stop-en-gaan ry), mag jy dit nie oor die hele beweging gebruik nie – breek die beweging dan op in stadiums waarin a konstant is.\n\n| Simbool | Grootheid | SI-eenheid |\n|---|---|---|\n| v_{i} | beginsnelheid | m·s⁻¹ |\n| v_{f} | eindsnelheid | m·s⁻¹ |\n| a | versnelling | m·s⁻² |\n| Δt | tydsinterval | s |\n| Δx | verplasing | m |\n\n## Die vier vergelykings (gegewensblad)\n\n1. **v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt** – bevat nie Δx nie\n2. **Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2}** – bevat nie v_{f} nie\n3. **v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx** – bevat nie Δt nie\n4. **Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt** – bevat nie a nie (gemiddelde snelheid × tyd)\n\nElke vergelyking bevat vier van die vyf groothede. As jy **drie** ken, kan jy die vierde bereken.\n\n### Hoe kies jy die regte vergelyking?\n\nSkryf die gegewe groothede en die onbekende neer. Soek die grootheid wat **nie gegee is nie en ook nie gevra word nie** – kies dan die vergelyking waarin dié grootheid **ontbreek**. Bv. gegee v_{i}, a en Δx, gevra v_{f}: Δt speel geen rol nie, dus gebruik v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n\n### Versteekte inligting in woorde\n\n- \"begin uit rus\" / \"vertrek van stilstand\" → v_{i} = 0\n- \"kom tot stilstand\" / \"stop\" → v_{f} = 0\n- \"konstante snelheid\" → a = 0 (dan is Δx = vΔt)\n- \"rem\" / \"vertraag\" → a is teenoor die bewegingsrigting (negatief as die bewegingsrigting positief gekies is)\n\n## Tekenkonvensie\n\nSnelheid, versnelling en verplasing is **vektore**. Kies eers 'n positiewe rigting (bv. vorentoe of oos = positief) en hou daarby vir die hele probleem.\n\n- 'n Voorwerp wat **vinniger** word: a en v het **dieselfde** teken.\n- 'n Voorwerp wat **stadiger** word: a en v het **teenoorgestelde** tekens.\n- 'n Negatiewe versnelling beteken **nie altyd** stadiger nie – as die voorwerp in die negatiewe rigting beweeg, word dit vinniger.\n- Gee 'n vektor-antwoord altyd met 'n **rigting**, bv. 12 m·s⁻¹ oos.\n\n## Omskakeling: km·h⁻¹ ↔ m·s⁻¹\n\n1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s, dus:\n\n- km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹: **deel deur 3,6** (72 km·h⁻¹ = 20 m·s⁻¹)\n- m·s⁻¹ → km·h⁻¹: **maal met 3,6** (25 m·s⁻¹ = 90 km·h⁻¹)\n\nSkakel ook cm na m en minute na sekondes om **voordat** jy vervang.\n\n## Probleme met meer as een stadium\n\nAs die beweging verander (bv. 'n taxi trek by 'n robot weg en ry dan teen konstante snelheid), werk elke stadium apart uit:\n\n- Die **eindsnelheid van stadium 1 is die beginsnelheid van stadium 2**.\n- Totale verplasing = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2}.\n\n### Stopafstand by 'n robot\n\n'n Bestuurder sien die robot rooi word, maar reageer nie dadelik nie.\n\n1. **Reaksietyd:** die motor ry nog teen **konstante snelheid**, dus reaksie-afstand = v × reaksietyd.\n2. **Remafstand:** die motor vertraag eenvormig tot v_{f} = 0; gebruik v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n3. **Stopafstand = reaksie-afstand + remafstand.**\n\nMet v_{f} = 0 gee die derde vergelyking remafstand = v_{i}^{2} ÷ (2 × grootte van a). Die remafstand is dus eweredig aan v_{i}^{2}: ry jy **twee keer** so vinnig, is die remafstand **vier keer** so lank.\n\n## Stappe vir enige berekening\n\n1. Kies 'n positiewe rigting.\n2. Lys die gegewe en die onbekende met tekens en SI-eenhede.\n3. Kies die vergelyking (die een sonder die ontbrekende grootheid).\n4. Skryf die formule, vervang en bereken.\n5. Gee die antwoord met eenheid (en rigting vir vektore), afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** km·h⁻¹ nie na m·s⁻¹ omgeskakel nie; die minusteken van 'n remmende versnelling vergeet; afstand in plaas van verplasing gebruik; in ½aΔt^{2} net Δt kwadreer (nie aΔt nie); by v_{f}^{2} vergeet om die vierkantswortel te trek.\n\n> **Wenk:** Kontroleer jou antwoord met 'n v-t-grafiek in jou kop: die **gradiënt** is die versnelling en die **oppervlakte onder die grafiek** is die verplasing.","en":"## When do you use the equations of motion?\n\nThe four equations of motion describe motion in a straight line with **constant (uniform) acceleration**. If the acceleration changes (e.g. a taxi driving stop-start), you may not use them for the whole motion – split the motion into stages in which a is constant.\n\n| Symbol | Quantity | SI unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| v_{i} | initial velocity | m·s⁻¹ |\n| v_{f} | final velocity | m·s⁻¹ |\n| a | acceleration | m·s⁻² |\n| Δt | time interval | s |\n| Δx | displacement | m |\n\n## The four equations (data sheet)\n\n1. **v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt** – contains no Δx\n2. **Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2}** – contains no v_{f}\n3. **v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx** – contains no Δt\n4. **Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt** – contains no a (average velocity × time)\n\nEach equation contains four of the five quantities. If you know **three**, you can calculate the fourth.\n\n### How do you choose the right equation?\n\nWrite down the given quantities and the unknown. Find the quantity that is **neither given nor asked for** – then choose the equation in which that quantity is **missing**. E.g. given v_{i}, a and Δx, asked v_{f}: Δt plays no role, so use v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n\n### Hidden information in words\n\n- \"starts from rest\" / \"departs from standstill\" → v_{i} = 0\n- \"comes to rest\" / \"stops\" → v_{f} = 0\n- \"constant velocity\" → a = 0 (then Δx = vΔt)\n- \"brakes\" / \"slows down\" → a is opposite to the direction of motion (negative if the direction of motion is chosen as positive)\n\n## Sign convention\n\nVelocity, acceleration and displacement are **vectors**. First choose a positive direction (e.g. forward or east = positive) and stick to it for the whole problem.\n\n- An object that **speeds up**: a and v have the **same** sign.\n- An object that **slows down**: a and v have **opposite** signs.\n- A negative acceleration does **not always** mean slowing down – if the object moves in the negative direction, it speeds up.\n- Always give a vector answer with a **direction**, e.g. 12 m·s⁻¹ east.\n\n## Converting: km·h⁻¹ ↔ m·s⁻¹\n\n1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s, so:\n\n- km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹: **divide by 3.6** (72 km·h⁻¹ = 20 m·s⁻¹)\n- m·s⁻¹ → km·h⁻¹: **multiply by 3.6** (25 m·s⁻¹ = 90 km·h⁻¹)\n\nAlso convert cm to m and minutes to seconds **before** you substitute.\n\n## Multi-stage problems\n\nIf the motion changes (e.g. a taxi pulls away at a robot and then drives at constant velocity), work out each stage separately:\n\n- The **final velocity of stage 1 is the initial velocity of stage 2**.\n- Total displacement = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2}.\n\n### Stopping distance at a robot\n\nA driver sees the robot turn red but does not react immediately.\n\n1. **Reaction time:** the car still moves at **constant velocity**, so reaction distance = v × reaction time.\n2. **Braking distance:** the car slows down uniformly to v_{f} = 0; use v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n3. **Stopping distance = reaction distance + braking distance.**\n\nWith v_{f} = 0 the third equation gives braking distance = v_{i}^{2} ÷ (2 × magnitude of a). The braking distance is therefore proportional to v_{i}^{2}: drive **twice** as fast and the braking distance is **four times** as long.\n\n## Steps for any calculation\n\n1. Choose a positive direction.\n2. List the given and the unknown with signs and SI units.\n3. Choose the equation (the one without the missing quantity).\n4. Write the formula, substitute and calculate.\n5. Give the answer with a unit (and a direction for vectors), rounded to two decimal places.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** not converting km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹; forgetting the minus sign of a braking acceleration; using distance instead of displacement; in ½aΔt^{2} squaring only Δt (not aΔt); forgetting to take the square root with v_{f}^{2}.\n\n> **Tip:** Check your answer with a v-t graph in your head: the **gradient** is the acceleration and the **area under the graph** is the displacement."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Verplasing (Δx)","en":"Displacement (Δx)"},"def":{"af":"Verplasing is die verandering in posisie van 'n voorwerp. Dit is 'n vektor: dit het grootte en rigting.","en":"Displacement is the change in position of an object. It is a vector: it has magnitude and direction."}},{"term":{"af":"Snelheid (v)","en":"Velocity (v)"},"def":{"af":"Snelheid is die tempo van verandering van posisie. Dit is 'n vektor, gemeet in m·s⁻¹.","en":"Velocity is the rate of change of position. It is a vector, measured in m·s⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Versnelling (a)","en":"Acceleration (a)"},"def":{"af":"Versnelling is die tempo van verandering van snelheid. Dit is 'n vektor, gemeet in m·s⁻².","en":"Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity. It is a vector, measured in m·s⁻²."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenvormige versnelling","en":"Uniform acceleration"},"def":{"af":"Versnelling wat konstant bly: die snelheid verander elke sekonde met dieselfde hoeveelheid. Slegs dan mag die bewegingsvergelykings gebruik word.","en":"Acceleration that stays constant: the velocity changes by the same amount every second. Only then may the equations of motion be used."}},{"term":{"af":"Beginsnelheid (v_i)","en":"Initial velocity (v_i)"},"def":{"af":"Die snelheid van 'n voorwerp aan die begin van die tydsinterval wat bestudeer word. \"Begin uit rus\" beteken v_i = 0.","en":"The velocity of an object at the start of the time interval being studied. \"Starts from rest\" means v_i = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Eindsnelheid (v_f)","en":"Final velocity (v_f)"},"def":{"af":"Die snelheid van 'n voorwerp aan die einde van die tydsinterval wat bestudeer word. \"Kom tot stilstand\" beteken v_f = 0.","en":"The velocity of an object at the end of the time interval being studied. \"Comes to rest\" means v_f = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Reaksietyd","en":"Reaction time"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd tussen die oomblik wat 'n bestuurder 'n gevaar sien en die oomblik wat hy begin rem. Die motor beweeg intussen teen konstante snelheid.","en":"The time between the moment a driver sees a hazard and the moment he starts braking. The car moves at constant velocity during this time."}},{"term":{"af":"Stopafstand","en":"Stopping distance"},"def":{"af":"Die totale afstand wat 'n voertuig aflê vandat die bestuurder die gevaar sien totdat dit stilstaan: reaksie-afstand + remafstand.","en":"The total distance a vehicle covers from the moment the driver sees the hazard until it stops: reaction distance + braking distance."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Taxi trek by 'n robot weg","en":"Taxi pulls away at a robot"},"problem":{"af":"'n Taxi staan stil by 'n robot in Brits. Toe die lig groen word, versnel dit eenvormig teen 1,5 m·s⁻² vir 8 s. Bereken (a) die taxi se snelheid na 8 s en (b) die taxi se verplasing in hierdie 8 s.","en":"A taxi is stationary at a robot in Brits. When the light turns green, it accelerates uniformly at 1.5 m·s⁻² for 8 s. Calculate (a) the taxi's velocity after 8 s and (b) the taxi's displacement in these 8 s."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief. Gegee: v_{i} = 0 (begin uit rus), a = +1,5 m·s⁻², Δt = 8 s.","en":"Choose the direction of motion as positive. Given: v_{i} = 0 (starts from rest), a = +1.5 m·s⁻², Δt = 8 s."},{"af":"(a) Δx is nie nodig nie, dus: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt = 0 + (1,5)(8) = 12 m·s⁻¹ in die bewegingsrigting","en":"(a) Δx is not needed, so: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt = 0 + (1.5)(8) = 12 m·s⁻¹ in the direction of motion"},{"af":"(b) Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2} = (0)(8) + ½(1,5)(8)^{2} = ½(1,5)(64)","en":"(b) Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2} = (0)(8) + ½(1.5)(8)^{2} = ½(1.5)(64)"},{"af":"Δx = 48 m in die bewegingsrigting. Kontrole: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(0 + 12)(8) = 48 m ✔","en":"Δx = 48 m in the direction of motion. Check: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(0 + 12)(8) = 48 m ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 12 m·s⁻¹ in die bewegingsrigting (b) 48 m in die bewegingsrigting","en":"(a) 12 m·s⁻¹ in the direction of motion (b) 48 m in the direction of motion"}},{"title":{"af":"Remmende motor met omskakeling van eenhede","en":"Braking car with unit conversion"},"problem":{"af":"'n Motor ry teen 72 km·h⁻¹ op die R511 naby Hartbeespoortdam. Die bestuurder trap rem en die motor kom eenvormig tot stilstand oor 'n afstand van 40 m. Bereken (a) die versnelling van die motor en (b) hoe lank dit neem om te stop.","en":"A car travels at 72 km·h⁻¹ on the R511 near Hartbeespoort Dam. The driver brakes and the car comes to rest uniformly over a distance of 40 m. Calculate (a) the acceleration of the car and (b) how long it takes to stop."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel eers om: v_{i} = 72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief. v_{f} = 0 (kom tot stilstand), Δx = +40 m.","en":"Convert first: v_{i} = 72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Choose the direction of motion as positive. v_{f} = 0 (comes to rest), Δx = +40 m."},{"af":"(a) Δt is nie gegee nie en word nie gevra nie, dus: v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0^{2} = (20)^{2} + 2a(40)","en":"(a) Δt is not given and not asked for, so: v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0^{2} = (20)^{2} + 2a(40)"},{"af":"0 = 400 + 80a → a = −400 ÷ 80 = −5 m·s⁻², d.w.s. 5 m·s⁻² teenoor die bewegingsrigting","en":"0 = 400 + 80a → a = −400 ÷ 80 = −5 m·s⁻², i.e. 5 m·s⁻² opposite to the direction of motion"},{"af":"(b) v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 0 = 20 + (−5)Δt → 5Δt = 20 → Δt = 4 s","en":"(b) v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 0 = 20 + (−5)Δt → 5Δt = 20 → Δt = 4 s"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) a = −5 m·s⁻² (5 m·s⁻² teenoor die bewegingsrigting) (b) Δt = 4 s","en":"(a) a = −5 m·s⁻² (5 m·s⁻² opposite to the direction of motion) (b) Δt = 4 s"}},{"title":{"af":"Stopafstand met reaksietyd (twee stadiums)","en":"Stopping distance with reaction time (two stages)"},"problem":{"af":"'n Bestuurder ry teen 90 km·h⁻¹ toe hy 'n robot 75 m voor hom rooi sien word. Sy reaksietyd is 0,8 s. Daarna rem hy en die motor vertraag eenvormig teen 6 m·s⁻² tot stilstand. Bereken die totale stopafstand en bepaal of die motor voor die stopstreep stilhou.","en":"A driver travels at 90 km·h⁻¹ when he sees a robot 75 m ahead turn red. His reaction time is 0.8 s. Then he brakes and the car slows down uniformly at 6 m·s⁻² until it stops. Calculate the total stopping distance and determine whether the car stops before the stop line."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel om: v = 90 ÷ 3,6 = 25 m·s⁻¹. Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief.","en":"Convert: v = 90 ÷ 3.6 = 25 m·s⁻¹. Choose the direction of motion as positive."},{"af":"Stadium 1 (reaksietyd, konstante snelheid, a = 0): Δx_{1} = vΔt = (25)(0,8) = 20 m","en":"Stage 1 (reaction time, constant velocity, a = 0): Δx_{1} = vΔt = (25)(0.8) = 20 m"},{"af":"Stadium 2 (rem): v_{i} = 25 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 0, a = −6 m·s⁻². v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0 = 625 + 2(−6)Δx_{2} → Δx_{2} = 625 ÷ 12 = 52,08 m","en":"Stage 2 (braking): v_{i} = 25 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 0, a = −6 m·s⁻². v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0 = 625 + 2(−6)Δx_{2} → Δx_{2} = 625 ÷ 12 = 52.08 m"},{"af":"Stopafstand = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2} = 20 + 52,08 = 72,08 m. Dit is minder as 75 m, dus stop die motor 75 − 72,08 = 2,92 m voor die stopstreep.","en":"Stopping distance = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2} = 20 + 52.08 = 72.08 m. This is less than 75 m, so the car stops 75 − 72.08 = 2.92 m before the stop line."}],"answer":{"af":"Stopafstand = 72,08 m; die motor stop 2,92 m voor die stopstreep.","en":"Stopping distance = 72.08 m; the car stops 2.92 m before the stop line."}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte vergelyking","en":"Choose the right equation"},"problem":{"af":"'n Fietsryer in die Magaliesberg ry teen 8 m·s⁻¹ en vertraag eenvormig tot 2 m·s⁻¹ in 5 s terwyl hy teen 'n steilte uitry. Bereken (a) die afstand wat hy in hierdie 5 s aflê en (b) sy versnelling. Verduidelik telkens waarom jy die vergelyking gekies het.","en":"A cyclist in the Magaliesberg travels at 8 m·s⁻¹ and slows down uniformly to 2 m·s⁻¹ in 5 s while riding up a steep slope. Calculate (a) the distance he covers in these 5 s and (b) his acceleration. Explain each time why you chose the equation."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief. Gegee: v_{i} = 8 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 2 m·s⁻¹, Δt = 5 s.","en":"Choose the direction of motion as positive. Given: v_{i} = 8 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 2 m·s⁻¹, Δt = 5 s."},{"af":"(a) a is nie gegee nie en word nie gevra nie, dus gebruik die vergelyking sonder a: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(8 + 2)(5) = 25 m","en":"(a) a is not given and not asked for, so use the equation without a: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(8 + 2)(5) = 25 m"},{"af":"(b) Δx is nie nodig nie, dus gebruik die vergelyking sonder Δx: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 2 = 8 + a(5)","en":"(b) Δx is not needed, so use the equation without Δx: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 2 = 8 + a(5)"},{"af":"a = (2 − 8) ÷ 5 = −1,2 m·s⁻². Die negatiewe teken wys dat die versnelling teenoor die bewegingsrigting is – die fietsryer vertraag.","en":"a = (2 − 8) ÷ 5 = −1.2 m·s⁻². The negative sign shows that the acceleration is opposite to the direction of motion – the cyclist slows down."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 25 m (b) a = −1,2 m·s⁻² (1,2 m·s⁻² teenoor die bewegingsrigting)","en":"(a) 25 m (b) a = −1.2 m·s⁻² (1.2 m·s⁻² opposite to the direction of motion)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter bewegingsvergelyking bevat NIE die tydsinterval Δt nie?","en":"Which equation of motion does NOT contain the time interval Δt?"},"options":[{"af":"v_f = v_i + aΔt","en":"v_f = v_i + aΔt"},{"af":"Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt²","en":"Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt²"},{"af":"Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt","en":"Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt"},{"af":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx","en":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx is die enigste vergelyking sonder Δt. Gebruik dit wanneer die tyd nie gegee is nie en ook nie gevra word nie.","en":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx is the only equation without Δt. Use it when the time is neither given nor asked for."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die bewegingsvergelykings mag slegs gebruik word as die versnelling konstant (eenvormig) is.","en":"The equations of motion may only be used if the acceleration is constant (uniform)."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die vergelykings geld net vir eenvormige versnelling. As a verander, breek die beweging op in stadiums waarin a konstant is.","en":"True. The equations only hold for uniform acceleration. If a changes, split the motion into stages in which a is constant."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skakel 54 km·h⁻¹ om na m·s⁻¹: ___ m·s⁻¹","en":"Convert 54 km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹: ___ m·s⁻¹"},"answers":{"af":["15","15 m·s⁻¹","15 m/s","15 m.s-1","15 m s-1","15 ms-1","15 m·s-1"],"en":["15","15 m·s⁻¹","15 m/s","15 m.s-1","15 m s-1","15 ms-1","15 m·s-1"]},"explain":{"af":"Deel deur 3,6: 54 ÷ 3,6 = 15 m·s⁻¹ (want 1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s).","en":"Divide by 3.6: 54 ÷ 3.6 = 15 m·s⁻¹ (because 1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke frase in 'n vraag by die versteekte inligting wat dit gee (bewegingsrigting = positief).","en":"Match each phrase in a question to the hidden information it gives (direction of motion = positive)."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"begin uit rus","en":"starts from rest"},"r":{"af":"v_i = 0","en":"v_i = 0"}},{"l":{"af":"kom tot stilstand","en":"comes to rest"},"r":{"af":"v_f = 0","en":"v_f = 0"}},{"l":{"af":"beweeg teen konstante snelheid","en":"moves at constant velocity"},"r":{"af":"a = 0","en":"a = 0"}},{"l":{"af":"rem eenvormig","en":"brakes uniformly"},"r":{"af":"a is negatief","en":"a is negative"}}],"explain":{"af":"Uit rus → v_i = 0; tot stilstand → v_f = 0; konstante snelheid → geen versnelling nie; rem → a is teenoor die beweging, dus negatief.","en":"From rest → v_i = 0; to rest → v_f = 0; constant velocity → no acceleration; braking → a is opposite to the motion, so negative."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motor ry oos en rem. Oos word as positief gekies. Watter tekens het die snelheid en die versnelling terwyl die motor rem?","en":"A car travels east and brakes. East is chosen as positive. What signs do the velocity and the acceleration have while the car is braking?"},"options":[{"af":"v positief, a positief","en":"v positive, a positive"},{"af":"v negatief, a negatief","en":"v negative, a negative"},{"af":"v positief, a negatief","en":"v positive, a negative"},{"af":"v negatief, a positief","en":"v negative, a positive"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die motor beweeg nog oos, dus is v positief. Dit word stadiger, dus is a teenoor die beweging (wes): negatief. 'n Algemene fout is om te dink die snelheid word ook negatief sodra die motor rem.","en":"The car is still moving east, so v is positive. It is slowing down, so a is opposite to the motion (west): negative. A common mistake is to think the velocity also becomes negative as soon as the car brakes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Negatiewe versnelling beteken altyd dat 'n voorwerp stadiger beweeg.","en":"A negative acceleration always means that an object is slowing down."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die teken wys net die rigting. As 'n voorwerp in die negatiewe rigting beweeg en a ook negatief is, wys v en a in dieselfde rigting en word die voorwerp vinniger.","en":"False. The sign only shows the direction. If an object moves in the negative direction and a is also negative, v and a point the same way and the object speeds up."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Taxi begin uit rus en versnel eenvormig teen 2,5 m·s⁻² vir 4 s. Wat is sy snelheid na 4 s?","en":"A taxi starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 2.5 m·s⁻² for 4 s. What is its velocity after 4 s?"},"options":[{"af":"1,6 m·s⁻¹","en":"1.6 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"10 m·s⁻¹","en":"10 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"6,5 m·s⁻¹","en":"6.5 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"20 m·s⁻¹","en":"20 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"v_f = v_i + aΔt = 0 + (2,5)(4) = 10 m·s⁻¹. Die 20 is die verplasing in meter (½aΔt² = ½(2,5)(16)), nie die snelheid nie.","en":"v_f = v_i + aΔt = 0 + (2.5)(4) = 10 m·s⁻¹. The 20 is the displacement in metres (½aΔt² = ½(2.5)(16)), not the velocity."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Fietsryer begin uit rus en versnel eenvormig teen 1,5 m·s⁻² vir 6 s. Sy verplasing in hierdie tyd is ___ m.","en":"A cyclist starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 1.5 m·s⁻² for 6 s. His displacement in this time is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["27","27 m"],"en":["27","27 m"]},"explain":{"af":"v_f is nie nodig nie: Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt² = 0 + ½(1,5)(6)² = ½(1,5)(36) = 27 m.","en":"v_f is not needed: Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt² = 0 + ½(1.5)(6)² = ½(1.5)(36) = 27 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motor ry teen 20 m·s⁻¹ en rem eenvormig tot stilstand in 5 s. Wat is sy versnelling? (Neem die bewegingsrigting as positief.)","en":"A car travels at 20 m·s⁻¹ and brakes uniformly to rest in 5 s. What is its acceleration? (Take the direction of motion as positive.)"},"options":[{"af":"4 m·s⁻²","en":"4 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"−0,25 m·s⁻²","en":"−0.25 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"−100 m·s⁻²","en":"−100 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"−4 m·s⁻²","en":"−4 m·s⁻²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"v_f = v_i + aΔt → 0 = 20 + a(5) → a = −4 m·s⁻². Die minusteken wys dat die versnelling teenoor die beweging is; +4 m·s⁻² vergeet die teken.","en":"v_f = v_i + aΔt → 0 = 20 + a(5) → a = −4 m·s⁻². The minus sign shows that the acceleration is opposite to the motion; +4 m·s⁻² forgets the sign."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Motor ry teen 30 m·s⁻¹ en rem met 'n versnelling van −5 m·s⁻² tot stilstand. Die remafstand is ___ m.","en":"A car travels at 30 m·s⁻¹ and brakes to rest with an acceleration of −5 m·s⁻². The braking distance is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["90","90 m"],"en":["90","90 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Δt is nie bekend nie: v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx → 0 = 30² + 2(−5)Δx → 0 = 900 − 10Δx → Δx = 90 m.","en":"Δt is not known: v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx → 0 = 30² + 2(−5)Δx → 0 = 900 − 10Δx → Δx = 90 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motorfiets versnel eenvormig van 10 m·s⁻¹ tot 30 m·s⁻¹ oor 'n afstand van 100 m. Hoe lank neem dit?","en":"A motorbike accelerates uniformly from 10 m·s⁻¹ to 30 m·s⁻¹ over a distance of 100 m. How long does it take?"},"options":[{"af":"5 s","en":"5 s"},{"af":"2,5 s","en":"2.5 s"},{"af":"10 s","en":"10 s"},{"af":"3,33 s","en":"3.33 s"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"a is onbekend en word nie gevra nie, dus Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt → 100 = ½(10 + 30)Δt = 20Δt → Δt = 5 s. 2,5 s kry jy as jy die ½ vergeet; 10 s as jy die snelhede aftrek in plaas van optel.","en":"a is unknown and not asked for, so Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt → 100 = ½(10 + 30)Δt = 20Δt → Δt = 5 s. You get 2.5 s if you forget the ½; 10 s if you subtract the velocities instead of adding them."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Taxi begin uit rus, versnel eenvormig teen 2 m·s⁻² vir 5 s en ry dan 10 s lank teen konstante snelheid. Die totale verplasing is ___ m.","en":"A taxi starts from rest, accelerates uniformly at 2 m·s⁻² for 5 s and then drives at constant velocity for 10 s. The total displacement is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["125","125 m"],"en":["125","125 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Stadium 1: Δx₁ = ½(2)(5)² = 25 m en v_f = 0 + (2)(5) = 10 m·s⁻¹. Stadium 2 (a = 0): Δx₂ = (10)(10) = 100 m. Totaal: 25 + 100 = 125 m.","en":"Stage 1: Δx₁ = ½(2)(5)² = 25 m and v_f = 0 + (2)(5) = 10 m·s⁻¹. Stage 2 (a = 0): Δx₂ = (10)(10) = 100 m. Total: 25 + 100 = 125 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Bestuurder ry teen 72 km·h⁻¹ toe 'n robot 50 m voor hom rooi word. Sy reaksietyd is 0,75 s, en daarna vertraag die motor eenvormig teen 5 m·s⁻² tot stilstand. Stop die motor voor die stopstreep?","en":"A driver travels at 72 km·h⁻¹ when a robot 50 m ahead turns red. His reaction time is 0.75 s, after which the car slows down uniformly at 5 m·s⁻² until it stops. Does the car stop before the stop line?"},"options":[{"af":"Ja – die remafstand is 40 m, dus stop dit 10 m voor die streep.","en":"Yes – the braking distance is 40 m, so it stops 10 m before the line."},{"af":"Ja – die totale stopafstand is net 17 m.","en":"Yes – the total stopping distance is only 17 m."},{"af":"Nee – die totale stopafstand is 55 m, dus stop dit 5 m oor die streep.","en":"No – the total stopping distance is 55 m, so it stops 5 m past the line."},{"af":"Nee – die totale stopafstand is 95 m.","en":"No – the total stopping distance is 95 m."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Reaksie-afstand = (20)(0,75) = 15 m. Remafstand: 0 = 20² + 2(−5)Δx → Δx = 40 m. Stopafstand = 15 + 40 = 55 m > 50 m. 'Ja, 40 m' vergeet die reaksie-afstand; 95 m vergeet die 2 in 2aΔx.","en":"72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Reaction distance = (20)(0.75) = 15 m. Braking distance: 0 = 20² + 2(−5)Δx → Δx = 40 m. Stopping distance = 15 + 40 = 55 m > 50 m. 'Yes, 40 m' forgets the reaction distance; 95 m forgets the 2 in 2aΔx."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo sê: \"As jy twee keer so vinnig ry, is jou remafstand twee keer so lank (met dieselfde remvertraging).\" Evalueer sy stelling.","en":"Thabo says: \"If you drive twice as fast, your braking distance is twice as long (with the same braking deceleration).\" Evaluate his statement."},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg – die remafstand is direk eweredig aan die spoed.","en":"He is right – the braking distance is directly proportional to the speed."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd – die remafstand word vier keer so lank, want remafstand = v_i² ÷ (2 × grootte van a).","en":"He is wrong – the braking distance becomes four times as long, because braking distance = v_i² ÷ (2 × magnitude of a)."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd – die remafstand bly dieselfde, want die remme is dieselfde.","en":"He is wrong – the braking distance stays the same, because the brakes are the same."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd – die remafstand halveer, want die motor stop vinniger.","en":"He is wrong – the braking distance halves, because the car stops faster."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Met v_f = 0: 0 = v_i² + 2aΔx, dus is die remafstand eweredig aan v_i². Verdubbel v_i → remafstand × 4. Bv. 20 m·s⁻¹ en a = −5 m·s⁻² gee 40 m; 40 m·s⁻¹ gee 160 m. Daarom is spoed so gevaarlik.","en":"With v_f = 0: 0 = v_i² + 2aΔx, so the braking distance is proportional to v_i². Double v_i → braking distance × 4. E.g. 20 m·s⁻¹ and a = −5 m·s⁻² gives 40 m; 40 m·s⁻¹ gives 160 m. That is why speeding is so dangerous."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Energie en die hidrosfeer","en":"Energy and the hydrosphere"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t4-energie","title":{"af":"Energie","en":"Energy"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal swaartekragpotensiële, kinetiese en meganiese energie kan bereken en die wet van behoud van meganiese energie kan toepas op vallende voorwerpe, tuimeltreine en slingers.","en":"You will be able to calculate gravitational potential, kinetic and mechanical energy and apply the law of conservation of mechanical energy to falling objects, roller coasters and pendulums."},"summary":{"af":"## Energie\n\n**Energie** is die vermoë om arbeid te verrig. Energie is 'n **skalaar** (dit het geen rigting nie) en word in **joule (J)** gemeet: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻². In hierdie onderwerp werk ons met twee vorme van energie wat saam meganiese energie vorm.\n\n## Swaartekragpotensiële energie (E_{p})\n\n**Definisie:** Swaartekragpotensiële energie (gravitasionele potensiële energie) is die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy posisie in die gravitasieveld relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt.\n\n**E_{p} = mgh**\n\n| Simbool | Betekenis | Eenheid |\n|---|---|---|\n| m | massa | kg |\n| g | gravitasieversnelling = 9,8 m·s⁻² | m·s⁻² |\n| h | hoogte bo die verwysingspunt | m |\n\n- By die verwysingspunt (gewoonlik die grond of die laagste punt) is h = 0, dus E_{p} = 0.\n- E_{p} is eweredig aan h: twee keer so hoog → twee keer soveel E_{p}.\n- 'n Rots bo-op 'n krans in die Magaliesberg het meer E_{p} as dieselfde rots onder by die pad.\n\n## Kinetiese energie (E_{k})\n\n**Definisie:** Kinetiese energie is die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy beweging.\n\n**E_{k} = ½mv^{2}** (m in kg, v in m·s⁻¹)\n\n- E_{k} is eweredig aan m: verdubbel die massa → verdubbel E_{k}.\n- E_{k} is eweredig aan v^{2}: verdubbel die spoed → **vier keer** soveel E_{k}. Daarom is 'n botsing teen 120 km·h⁻¹ soveel erger as een teen 60 km·h⁻¹.\n- 'n Voorwerp in rus het E_{k} = 0.\n\n## Meganiese energie (E_{M})\n\n**Definisie:** Meganiese energie is die som van die swaartekragpotensiële energie en die kinetiese energie van 'n voorwerp.\n\n**E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = mgh + ½mv^{2}**\n\n## Behoud van energie\n\n**Wet van behoud van energie:** Energie kan nie geskep of vernietig word nie; dit kan slegs van een vorm na 'n ander omgeskakel word.\n\n**Wet van behoud van meganiese energie:** Die totale meganiese energie van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant. 'n Sisteem is geïsoleerd as daar **geen wrywing of lugweerstand** (geen eksterne kragte) is nie.\n\nWat 'n voorwerp aan E_{p} verloor, wen dit aan E_{k} – en andersom:\n\n**E_{M} (begin) = E_{M} (einde)** → mgh_{1} + ½mv_{1}^{2} = mgh_{2} + ½mv_{2}^{2}\n\n### Toepassings\n\n- **Vallende voorwerp** (uit rus, geen lugweerstand): bo is al die energie E_{p}; net voor die grond is al die energie E_{k}. mgh = ½mv^{2} → **v = √(2gh)**. Die massa kanselleer, dus tref 'n swaar en 'n ligte klip die grond met dieselfde spoed.\n- **Tuimeltrein (roller coaster):** die karretjie is die vinnigste by die laagste punt. As dit uit rus begin, kan dit (sonder wrywing) nooit hoër as die beginhoogte kom nie.\n- **Slinger:** by die hoogste punte (die draaipunte) is v = 0, dus E_{k} = 0 en E_{p} maksimum. By die laagste punt is E_{p} minimum (kies dit as h = 0) en E_{k} en die spoed maksimum.\n\n### As daar wel wrywing is\n\nMet wrywing of lugweerstand word meganiese energie **nie** behou nie: 'n deel word na **hitte (termiese energie) en klank** omgeskakel. Die **totale** energie bly steeds behoue: omgeskakelde energie = E_{M} (begin) − E_{M} (einde). Daarom swaai 'n slinger in die werklikheid al laer en stop dit uiteindelik.\n\n## Stappe vir 'n behoud-berekening\n\n1. Kies die verwysingspunt (h = 0) – gewoonlik die laagste punt.\n2. Skryf: E_{M} by die beginpunt = E_{M} by die eindpunt.\n3. Vervang mgh en ½mv^{2} aan albei kante (E_{k} = 0 waar die voorwerp in rus is; E_{p} = 0 by h = 0).\n4. Los op vir die onbekende en gee die eenheid. Rond eers aan die einde af tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** massa in gram gebruik (deel deur 1 000 om kg te kry); hoogte in cm gebruik (deel deur 100); km·h⁻¹ nie na m·s⁻¹ omgeskakel nie; E_{k} = mv^{2} sonder die ½; die vierkantswortel vergeet as jy v bereken; die beginhoogte gebruik in plaas van die hoogte wat die voorwerp gedaal het.\n\n> **Onthou!** Energie is 'n skalaar – moet nooit 'n rigting by 'n energie-antwoord skryf nie. Gebruik altyd g = 9,8 m·s⁻².","en":"## Energy\n\n**Energy** is the ability to do work. Energy is a **scalar** (it has no direction) and is measured in **joules (J)**: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻². In this topic we work with two forms of energy that together make up mechanical energy.\n\n## Gravitational potential energy (E_{p})\n\n**Definition:** Gravitational potential energy is the energy an object possesses due to its position in the gravitational field relative to a reference point.\n\n**E_{p} = mgh**\n\n| Symbol | Meaning | Unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| m | mass | kg |\n| g | gravitational acceleration = 9.8 m·s⁻² | m·s⁻² |\n| h | height above the reference point | m |\n\n- At the reference point (usually the ground or the lowest point) h = 0, so E_{p} = 0.\n- E_{p} is proportional to h: twice as high → twice as much E_{p}.\n- A rock on top of a cliff in the Magaliesberg has more E_{p} than the same rock down by the road.\n\n## Kinetic energy (E_{k})\n\n**Definition:** Kinetic energy is the energy an object possesses as a result of its motion.\n\n**E_{k} = ½mv^{2}** (m in kg, v in m·s⁻¹)\n\n- E_{k} is proportional to m: double the mass → double E_{k}.\n- E_{k} is proportional to v^{2}: double the speed → **four times** as much E_{k}. That is why a crash at 120 km·h⁻¹ is so much worse than one at 60 km·h⁻¹.\n- An object at rest has E_{k} = 0.\n\n## Mechanical energy (E_{M})\n\n**Definition:** Mechanical energy is the sum of the gravitational potential energy and the kinetic energy of an object.\n\n**E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = mgh + ½mv^{2}**\n\n## Conservation of energy\n\n**Law of conservation of energy:** Energy cannot be created or destroyed; it can only be changed from one form into another.\n\n**Law of conservation of mechanical energy:** The total mechanical energy of an isolated system remains constant. A system is isolated if there is **no friction or air resistance** (no external forces).\n\nWhat an object loses in E_{p}, it gains in E_{k} – and vice versa:\n\n**E_{M} (start) = E_{M} (end)** → mgh_{1} + ½mv_{1}^{2} = mgh_{2} + ½mv_{2}^{2}\n\n### Applications\n\n- **Falling object** (from rest, no air resistance): at the top all the energy is E_{p}; just before the ground all the energy is E_{k}. mgh = ½mv^{2} → **v = √(2gh)**. The mass cancels, so a heavy and a light stone hit the ground with the same speed.\n- **Roller coaster:** the cart is fastest at the lowest point. If it starts from rest, it can (without friction) never get higher than its starting height.\n- **Pendulum:** at the highest points (the turning points) v = 0, so E_{k} = 0 and E_{p} is maximum. At the lowest point E_{p} is minimum (choose it as h = 0) and E_{k} and the speed are maximum.\n\n### When there is friction\n\nWith friction or air resistance, mechanical energy is **not** conserved: part of it is converted into **heat (thermal energy) and sound**. The **total** energy is still conserved: energy converted = E_{M} (start) − E_{M} (end). That is why a real pendulum swings lower and lower and eventually stops.\n\n## Steps for a conservation calculation\n\n1. Choose the reference point (h = 0) – usually the lowest point.\n2. Write: E_{M} at the starting point = E_{M} at the end point.\n3. Substitute mgh and ½mv^{2} on both sides (E_{k} = 0 where the object is at rest; E_{p} = 0 at h = 0).\n4. Solve for the unknown and give the unit. Only round off at the end, to two decimal places.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** using mass in grams (divide by 1 000 to get kg); using height in cm (divide by 100); not converting km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹; E_{k} = mv^{2} without the ½; forgetting the square root when you calculate v; using the starting height instead of the height the object has dropped.\n\n> **Remember!** Energy is a scalar – never write a direction with an energy answer. Always use g = 9.8 m·s⁻²."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Energie","en":"Energy"},"def":{"af":"Die vermoë om arbeid te verrig. Energie is 'n skalaar en word in joule (J) gemeet.","en":"The ability to do work. Energy is a scalar and is measured in joules (J)."}},{"term":{"af":"Swaartekragpotensiële energie (E_p)","en":"Gravitational potential energy (E_p)"},"def":{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy posisie in die gravitasieveld relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt. E_p = mgh.","en":"The energy an object possesses due to its position in the gravitational field relative to a reference point. E_p = mgh."}},{"term":{"af":"Kinetiese energie (E_k)","en":"Kinetic energy (E_k)"},"def":{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy beweging. E_k = ½mv².","en":"The energy an object possesses as a result of its motion. E_k = ½mv²."}},{"term":{"af":"Meganiese energie (E_M)","en":"Mechanical energy (E_M)"},"def":{"af":"Die som van die swaartekragpotensiële energie en die kinetiese energie van 'n voorwerp. E_M = E_p + E_k.","en":"The sum of the gravitational potential energy and the kinetic energy of an object. E_M = E_p + E_k."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van behoud van energie","en":"Law of conservation of energy"},"def":{"af":"Energie kan nie geskep of vernietig word nie; dit kan slegs van een vorm na 'n ander omgeskakel word.","en":"Energy cannot be created or destroyed; it can only be changed from one form into another."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van behoud van meganiese energie","en":"Law of conservation of mechanical energy"},"def":{"af":"Die totale meganiese energie van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem (geen wrywing of lugweerstand nie) bly konstant.","en":"The total mechanical energy of an isolated system (no friction or air resistance) remains constant."}},{"term":{"af":"Geïsoleerde sisteem","en":"Isolated system"},"def":{"af":"'n Sisteem waarop geen eksterne kragte soos wrywing of lugweerstand inwerk nie, sodat die meganiese energie behoue bly.","en":"A system on which no external forces such as friction or air resistance act, so that mechanical energy is conserved."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwysingspunt","en":"Reference point"},"def":{"af":"Die gekose posisie waar h = 0 en dus E_p = 0 – gewoonlik die grond of die laagste punt van die beweging.","en":"The chosen position where h = 0 and therefore E_p = 0 – usually the ground or the lowest point of the motion."}},{"term":{"af":"Joule (J)","en":"Joule (J)"},"def":{"af":"Die SI-eenheid van energie: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻².","en":"The SI unit of energy: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻²."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Potensiële, kinetiese en meganiese energie","en":"Potential, kinetic and mechanical energy"},"problem":{"af":"'n Witkruisarend met 'n massa van 4 kg sweef 50 m bo die grond langs die Magaliesberg teen 'n spoed van 10 m·s⁻¹. Neem die grond as verwysingspunt en bereken die arend se (a) swaartekragpotensiële energie, (b) kinetiese energie en (c) meganiese energie.","en":"A Verreaux's (black) eagle with a mass of 4 kg glides 50 m above the ground along the Magaliesberg at a speed of 10 m·s⁻¹. Take the ground as reference point and calculate the eagle's (a) gravitational potential energy, (b) kinetic energy and (c) mechanical energy."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) E_{p} = mgh = (4)(9,8)(50) = 1 960 J","en":"(a) E_{p} = mgh = (4)(9.8)(50) = 1 960 J"},{"af":"(b) E_{k} = ½mv^{2} = ½(4)(10)^{2} = ½(4)(100) = 200 J – kwadreer net die spoed.","en":"(b) E_{k} = ½mv^{2} = ½(4)(10)^{2} = ½(4)(100) = 200 J – square only the speed."},{"af":"(c) E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = 1 960 + 200 = 2 160 J","en":"(c) E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = 1 960 + 200 = 2 160 J"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 1 960 J (b) 200 J (c) 2 160 J","en":"(a) 1 960 J (b) 200 J (c) 2 160 J"}},{"title":{"af":"Vallende klip","en":"Falling stone"},"problem":{"af":"'n Klip van 200 g word uit rus van 'n brug 20 m bo die water van die Krokodilrivier laat val. Ignoreer lugweerstand. Bereken (a) die klip se meganiese energie bo-op die brug en (b) sy spoed net voordat hy die water tref.","en":"A 200 g stone is dropped from rest from a bridge 20 m above the water of the Crocodile River. Ignore air resistance. Calculate (a) the stone's mechanical energy at the top of the bridge and (b) its speed just before it hits the water."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel om: m = 200 g = 0,2 kg. Kies die wateroppervlak as verwysingspunt (h = 0).","en":"Convert: m = 200 g = 0.2 kg. Choose the water surface as reference point (h = 0)."},{"af":"(a) Bo is v = 0, dus E_{k} = 0. E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (0,2)(9,8)(20) = 39,2 J","en":"(a) At the top v = 0, so E_{k} = 0. E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (0.2)(9.8)(20) = 39.2 J"},{"af":"(b) Geen lugweerstand nie, dus word E_{M} behou: E_{M} bo = E_{M} onder → 39,2 = 0 + ½(0,2)v^{2}","en":"(b) No air resistance, so E_{M} is conserved: E_{M} top = E_{M} bottom → 39.2 = 0 + ½(0.2)v^{2}"},{"af":"v^{2} = 39,2 ÷ 0,1 = 392 → v = √392 = 19,80 m·s⁻¹","en":"v^{2} = 39.2 ÷ 0.1 = 392 → v = √392 = 19.80 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"Kontrole: v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9,8 × 20) = 19,80 m·s⁻¹ – die massa kanselleer.","en":"Check: v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9.8 × 20) = 19.80 m·s⁻¹ – the mass cancels."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 39,2 J (b) 19,80 m·s⁻¹","en":"(a) 39.2 J (b) 19.80 m·s⁻¹"}},{"title":{"af":"Tuimeltrein","en":"Roller coaster"},"problem":{"af":"'n Tuimeltrein-karretjie met passasiers het 'n totale massa van 600 kg. Dit begin uit rus by punt A, 30 m bo die grond, rol af na punt B (5 m bo die grond) en klim dan na punt C (18 m bo die grond). Ignoreer wrywing. Bereken die spoed by B en by C.","en":"A roller-coaster cart with passengers has a total mass of 600 kg. It starts from rest at point A, 30 m above the ground, rolls down to point B (5 m above the ground) and then climbs to point C (18 m above the ground). Ignore friction. Calculate the speed at B and at C."},"steps":[{"af":"Verwysingspunt: die grond. By A is v = 0, dus E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (600)(9,8)(30) = 176 400 J. Sonder wrywing bly E_{M} oral 176 400 J.","en":"Reference point: the ground. At A v = 0, so E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (600)(9.8)(30) = 176 400 J. Without friction E_{M} stays 176 400 J everywhere."},{"af":"By B: E_{p} = (600)(9,8)(5) = 29 400 J, dus E_{k} = E_{M} − E_{p} = 176 400 − 29 400 = 147 000 J","en":"At B: E_{p} = (600)(9.8)(5) = 29 400 J, so E_{k} = E_{M} − E_{p} = 176 400 − 29 400 = 147 000 J"},{"af":"½(600)v_{B}^{2} = 147 000 → v_{B}^{2} = 490 → v_{B} = 22,14 m·s⁻¹","en":"½(600)v_{B}^{2} = 147 000 → v_{B}^{2} = 490 → v_{B} = 22.14 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"By C: E_{p} = (600)(9,8)(18) = 105 840 J, dus E_{k} = 176 400 − 105 840 = 70 560 J","en":"At C: E_{p} = (600)(9.8)(18) = 105 840 J, so E_{k} = 176 400 − 105 840 = 70 560 J"},{"af":"½(600)v_{C}^{2} = 70 560 → v_{C}^{2} = 235,2 → v_{C} = 15,34 m·s⁻¹. (C is hoër as B, dus is die karretjie daar stadiger.)","en":"½(600)v_{C}^{2} = 70 560 → v_{C}^{2} = 235.2 → v_{C} = 15.34 m·s⁻¹. (C is higher than B, so the cart is slower there.)"}],"answer":{"af":"v_{B} = 22,14 m·s⁻¹; v_{C} = 15,34 m·s⁻¹","en":"v_{B} = 22.14 m·s⁻¹; v_{C} = 15.34 m·s⁻¹"}},{"title":{"af":"Slinger","en":"Pendulum"},"problem":{"af":"'n Slinger se gewig (massa 0,5 kg) word opgetrek tot 0,2 m bo sy laagste punt en uit rus gelos. Ignoreer lugweerstand. (a) Waar is die gewig se spoed die grootste? Verduidelik. (b) Bereken die maksimum spoed. (c) In die werklikheid swaai die slinger al laer en stop dit uiteindelik. Verduidelik waarom.","en":"A pendulum bob (mass 0.5 kg) is pulled up to 0.2 m above its lowest point and released from rest. Ignore air resistance. (a) Where is the bob's speed the greatest? Explain. (b) Calculate the maximum speed. (c) In reality the pendulum swings lower and lower and eventually stops. Explain why."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) By die laagste punt. Daar is E_{p} die kleinste (h = 0). Omdat E_{M} konstant bly, is E_{k} – en dus die spoed – daar die grootste.","en":"(a) At the lowest point. There E_{p} is the smallest (h = 0). Because E_{M} stays constant, E_{k} – and therefore the speed – is the greatest there."},{"af":"(b) By die hoogste punt: E_{k} = 0 en E_{p} = mgh = (0,5)(9,8)(0,2) = 0,98 J, dus E_{M} = 0,98 J","en":"(b) At the highest point: E_{k} = 0 and E_{p} = mgh = (0.5)(9.8)(0.2) = 0.98 J, so E_{M} = 0.98 J"},{"af":"By die laagste punt: E_{p} = 0, dus E_{k} = 0,98 J → ½(0,5)v^{2} = 0,98 → v^{2} = 3,92 → v = 1,98 m·s⁻¹","en":"At the lowest point: E_{p} = 0, so E_{k} = 0.98 J → ½(0.5)v^{2} = 0.98 → v^{2} = 3.92 → v = 1.98 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(c) Lugweerstand (en wrywing by die ophangpunt) werk teen die beweging. 'n Deel van die meganiese energie word na hitte en klank omgeskakel, dus neem E_{M} af en bereik die gewig elke swaai 'n laer hoogte. Die totale energie bly wel behoue.","en":"(c) Air resistance (and friction at the pivot) acts against the motion. Part of the mechanical energy is converted into heat and sound, so E_{M} decreases and the bob reaches a lower height with every swing. The total energy is still conserved."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) By die laagste punt (b) 1,98 m·s⁻¹ (c) Lugweerstand en wrywing skakel meganiese energie na hitte en klank om.","en":"(a) At the lowest point (b) 1.98 m·s⁻¹ (c) Air resistance and friction convert mechanical energy into heat and sound."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die definisie van kinetiese energie?","en":"Which statement is the definition of kinetic energy?"},"options":[{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy posisie relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt.","en":"The energy an object possesses due to its position relative to a reference point."},{"af":"Die som van die swaartekragpotensiële en kinetiese energie van 'n voorwerp.","en":"The sum of the gravitational potential and kinetic energy of an object."},{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy beweging.","en":"The energy an object possesses as a result of its motion."},{"af":"Die energie wat in die chemiese bindings van 'n stof gestoor is.","en":"The energy stored in the chemical bonds of a substance."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kinetiese energie is bewegingsenergie. Die eerste opsie is die definisie van swaartekragpotensiële energie en die tweede dié van meganiese energie.","en":"Kinetic energy is energy of motion. The first option is the definition of gravitational potential energy and the second that of mechanical energy."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke grootheid by die regte formule of eenheid.","en":"Match each quantity to the correct formula or unit."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Swaartekragpotensiële energie","en":"Gravitational potential energy"},"r":{"af":"mgh","en":"mgh"}},{"l":{"af":"Kinetiese energie","en":"Kinetic energy"},"r":{"af":"½mv²","en":"½mv²"}},{"l":{"af":"Meganiese energie","en":"Mechanical energy"},"r":{"af":"E_p + E_k","en":"E_p + E_k"}},{"l":{"af":"Eenheid van energie","en":"Unit of energy"},"r":{"af":"joule (J) = kg·m²·s⁻²","en":"joule (J) = kg·m²·s⁻²"}}],"explain":{"af":"E_p = mgh, E_k = ½mv², E_M = E_p + E_k, en alle vorme van energie word in joule gemeet.","en":"E_p = mgh, E_k = ½mv², E_M = E_p + E_k, and all forms of energy are measured in joules."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Boks van 5 kg staan op 'n rak 2 m bo die vloer. Sy swaartekragpotensiële energie relatief tot die vloer is ___ J.","en":"A 5 kg box stands on a shelf 2 m above the floor. Its gravitational potential energy relative to the floor is ___ J."},"answers":{"af":["98","98 J","98 joule"],"en":["98","98 J","98 joule"]},"explain":{"af":"E_p = mgh = (5)(9,8)(2) = 98 J.","en":"E_p = mgh = (5)(9.8)(2) = 98 J."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Slinger het sy grootste kinetiese energie by sy hoogste punt.","en":"A pendulum has its greatest kinetic energy at its highest point."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. By die hoogste punt staan die gewig vir 'n oomblik stil: v = 0, dus E_k = 0 en E_p is maksimum. E_k is die grootste by die laagste punt.","en":"False. At the highest point the bob is momentarily at rest: v = 0, so E_k = 0 and E_p is maximum. E_k is greatest at the lowest point."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"As die spoed van 'n motor verdubbel, wat gebeur met sy kinetiese energie?","en":"If the speed of a car doubles, what happens to its kinetic energy?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit verdubbel.","en":"It doubles."},{"af":"Dit word vier keer groter.","en":"It becomes four times greater."},{"af":"Dit halveer.","en":"It halves."},{"af":"Dit bly dieselfde, want die massa het nie verander nie.","en":"It stays the same, because the mass has not changed."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"E_k = ½mv²: die spoed word gekwadreer, dus (2)² = 4. Verdubbel die spoed → vier keer soveel E_k. 'Dit verdubbel' geld vir die massa, nie die spoed nie.","en":"E_k = ½mv²: the speed is squared, so (2)² = 4. Double the speed → four times as much E_k. 'It doubles' applies to the mass, not the speed."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Swaar klip en 'n ligte klip word uit rus van dieselfde hoogte laat val. Sonder lugweerstand tref hulle die grond met dieselfde spoed.","en":"A heavy stone and a light stone are dropped from rest from the same height. Without air resistance they hit the ground with the same speed."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh): die massa kanselleer. Die swaar klip het wel meer E_k, maar dieselfde spoed.","en":"True. mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh): the mass cancels. The heavy stone does have more E_k, but the same speed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motor van 1 200 kg ry teen 72 km·h⁻¹. Wat is sy kinetiese energie?","en":"A 1 200 kg car travels at 72 km·h⁻¹. What is its kinetic energy?"},"options":[{"af":"240 000 J","en":"240 000 J"},{"af":"3 110 400 J","en":"3 110 400 J"},{"af":"12 000 J","en":"12 000 J"},{"af":"480 000 J","en":"480 000 J"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers om: 72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. E_k = ½(1 200)(20)² = 240 000 J. 3 110 400 J gebruik 72 sonder omskakeling, 12 000 J vergeet om te kwadreer en 480 000 J vergeet die ½.","en":"Convert first: 72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. E_k = ½(1 200)(20)² = 240 000 J. 3 110 400 J uses 72 without converting, 12 000 J forgets to square and 480 000 J forgets the ½."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Rugbybal van 450 g word teen 20 m·s⁻¹ geskop. Die bal se kinetiese energie is ___ J.","en":"A 450 g rugby ball is kicked at 20 m·s⁻¹. The ball's kinetic energy is ___ J."},"answers":{"af":["90","90 J","90 joule"],"en":["90","90 J","90 joule"]},"explain":{"af":"m = 450 g = 0,45 kg. E_k = ½mv² = ½(0,45)(20)² = ½(0,45)(400) = 90 J.","en":"m = 450 g = 0.45 kg. E_k = ½mv² = ½(0.45)(20)² = ½(0.45)(400) = 90 J."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Kolgans van 2 kg vlieg 10 m bo die grond teen 3 m·s⁻¹. Wat is sy meganiese energie relatief tot die grond?","en":"An Egyptian goose of 2 kg flies 10 m above the ground at 3 m·s⁻¹. What is its mechanical energy relative to the ground?"},"options":[{"af":"196 J","en":"196 J"},{"af":"187 J","en":"187 J"},{"af":"199 J","en":"199 J"},{"af":"205 J","en":"205 J"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"E_p = (2)(9,8)(10) = 196 J en E_k = ½(2)(3)² = 9 J, dus E_M = 196 + 9 = 205 J. 196 J is net E_p; 199 J vergeet om v te kwadreer; 187 J trek af in plaas van optel.","en":"E_p = (2)(9.8)(10) = 196 J and E_k = ½(2)(3)² = 9 J, so E_M = 196 + 9 = 205 J. 196 J is only E_p; 199 J forgets to square v; 187 J subtracts instead of adding."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Klip word uit rus van 'n hoogte van 5 m laat val. Ignoreer lugweerstand. Sy spoed net voordat hy die grond tref, is ___ m·s⁻¹.","en":"A stone is dropped from rest from a height of 5 m. Ignore air resistance. Its speed just before it hits the ground is ___ m·s⁻¹."},"answers":{"af":["9,90","9.90","9,90 m·s⁻¹","9.90 m·s⁻¹","9,90 m/s","9.90 m/s","9,90 m.s-1","9.90 m.s-1","9,90 m s-1","9.90 m s-1","9,90 ms-1","9.90 ms-1","9,90 m·s-1","9.90 m·s-1","9,9","9.9","9,9 m·s⁻¹","9.9 m·s⁻¹","9,9 m/s","9.9 m/s","9,9 m.s-1","9.9 m.s-1","9,9 m s-1","9.9 m s-1","9,9 ms-1","9.9 ms-1","9,9 m·s-1","9.9 m·s-1"],"en":["9,90","9.90","9,90 m·s⁻¹","9.90 m·s⁻¹","9,90 m/s","9.90 m/s","9,90 m.s-1","9.90 m.s-1","9,90 m s-1","9.90 m s-1","9,90 ms-1","9.90 ms-1","9,90 m·s-1","9.90 m·s-1","9,9","9.9","9,9 m·s⁻¹","9.9 m·s⁻¹","9,9 m/s","9.9 m/s","9,9 m.s-1","9.9 m.s-1","9,9 m s-1","9.9 m s-1","9,9 ms-1","9.9 ms-1","9,9 m·s-1","9.9 m·s-1"]},"explain":{"af":"E_M bo = E_M onder: mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9,8 × 5) = √98 = 9,90 m·s⁻¹. Die massa is nie nodig nie.","en":"E_M top = E_M bottom: mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9.8 × 5) = √98 = 9.90 m·s⁻¹. The mass is not needed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Tuimeltrein-karretjie begin uit rus by 'n punt 20 m bo die grond. Wat is sy spoed by 'n punt 8 m bo die grond? Ignoreer wrywing.","en":"A roller-coaster cart starts from rest at a point 20 m above the ground. What is its speed at a point 8 m above the ground? Ignore friction."},"options":[{"af":"12,52 m·s⁻¹","en":"12.52 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"15,34 m·s⁻¹","en":"15.34 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"19,80 m·s⁻¹","en":"19.80 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"235,2 m·s⁻¹","en":"235.2 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"mgh₁ = mgh₂ + ½mv² → ½v² = g(h₁ − h₂) = 9,8 × 12 → v² = 235,2 → v = 15,34 m·s⁻¹. Die karretjie het 12 m gedaal, nie 8 m of 20 m nie; 235,2 vergeet die vierkantswortel.","en":"mgh₁ = mgh₂ + ½mv² → ½v² = g(h₁ − h₂) = 9.8 × 12 → v² = 235.2 → v = 15.34 m·s⁻¹. The cart dropped 12 m, not 8 m or 20 m; 235.2 forgets the square root."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Blok gly teen 4 m·s⁻¹ oor 'n wrywinglose horisontale oppervlak en dan teen 'n wrywinglose helling op. Die maksimum hoogte wat die blok bereik, is ___ m.","en":"A block slides at 4 m·s⁻¹ across a frictionless horizontal surface and then up a frictionless slope. The maximum height the block reaches is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["0,82","0.82","0,82 m","0.82 m"],"en":["0,82","0.82","0,82 m","0.82 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Onder: E_k = ½mv²; bo (v = 0): E_p = mgh. ½mv² = mgh → h = v² ÷ 2g = 16 ÷ 19,6 = 0,82 m.","en":"At the bottom: E_k = ½mv²; at the top (v = 0): E_p = mgh. ½mv² = mgh → h = v² ÷ 2g = 16 ÷ 19.6 = 0.82 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Slinger word uit rus 0,3 m bo sy laagste punt gelos. Lerato sê die gewig se spoed is die helfte van die maksimum spoed wanneer dit 0,15 m bo die laagste punt is. Johan sê dit is by 0,225 m. Wie is reg?","en":"A pendulum is released from rest 0.3 m above its lowest point. Lerato says the bob's speed is half the maximum speed when it is 0.15 m above the lowest point. Johan says it is at 0.225 m. Who is right?"},"options":[{"af":"Johan – by halwe spoed is E_k net ¼ van die maksimum, dus is ¾ van die energie nog E_p: h = ¾ × 0,3 = 0,225 m.","en":"Johan – at half speed E_k is only ¼ of the maximum, so ¾ of the energy is still E_p: h = ¾ × 0.3 = 0.225 m."},{"af":"Lerato – halwe spoed beteken halwe energie, dus h = ½ × 0,3 = 0,15 m.","en":"Lerato – half speed means half the energy, so h = ½ × 0.3 = 0.15 m."},{"af":"Albei is verkeerd – die hoogte is ¼ × 0,3 = 0,075 m.","en":"Both are wrong – the height is ¼ × 0.3 = 0.075 m."},{"af":"Albei is verkeerd – die hoogte hang van die massa af, wat nie gegee is nie.","en":"Both are wrong – the height depends on the mass, which is not given."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"E_k is eweredig aan v²: (½)² = ¼. By halwe spoed is E_k = ¼E_M, dus E_p = ¾E_M en h = ¾ × 0,3 = 0,225 m. Die massa kanselleer. Lerato neem verkeerdelik aan dat E_k eweredig aan v is.","en":"E_k is proportional to v²: (½)² = ¼. At half speed E_k = ¼E_M, so E_p = ¾E_M and h = ¾ × 0.3 = 0.225 m. The mass cancels. Lerato wrongly assumes that E_k is proportional to v."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder van 60 kg gly uit rus van die bopunt van 'n 4 m hoë waterglybaan af en bereik die onderkant teen 7 m·s⁻¹. Watter gevolgtrekking is korrek?","en":"A 60 kg learner slides from rest from the top of a 4 m high water slide and reaches the bottom at 7 m·s⁻¹. Which conclusion is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Meganiese energie is behou, want E_k onder is gelyk aan E_p bo.","en":"Mechanical energy is conserved, because E_k at the bottom equals E_p at the top."},{"af":"Meganiese energie is nie behou nie: 882 J is deur wrywing vernietig.","en":"Mechanical energy is not conserved: 882 J was destroyed by friction."},{"af":"Meganiese energie is nie behou nie: 882 J is deur wrywing na hitte en klank omgeskakel.","en":"Mechanical energy is not conserved: 882 J was converted into heat and sound by friction."},{"af":"Meganiese energie is behou, want die leerder se massa het nie verander nie.","en":"Mechanical energy is conserved, because the learner's mass did not change."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Bo: E_M = E_p = (60)(9,8)(4) = 2 352 J. Onder: E_M = E_k = ½(60)(7)² = 1 470 J. Die verskil van 882 J is nie 'vernietig' nie (energie kan nie vernietig word nie) – wrywing het dit na hitte en klank omgeskakel.","en":"Top: E_M = E_p = (60)(9.8)(4) = 2 352 J. Bottom: E_M = E_k = ½(60)(7)² = 1 470 J. The difference of 882 J was not 'destroyed' (energy cannot be destroyed) – friction converted it into heat and sound."}}]},{"id":"f10-t4-hidrosfeer","title":{"af":"Die hidrosfeer","en":"The hydrosphere"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die samestelling van die hidrosfeer, sy wisselwerking met ander globale sisteme, die waterkringloop, besoedeling, suiwering en die toetsing van watergehalte kan verduidelik – en waarom waterbewaring in Suid-Afrika so belangrik is.","en":"You will be able to explain the composition of the hydrosphere, its interaction with other global systems, the water cycle, pollution, purification and water-quality testing – and why water conservation is so important in South Africa."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is die hidrosfeer?\n\nDie **hidrosfeer** is al die water op, onder en bo die aarde se oppervlak, in al drie toestande: oseane en seë, riviere, mere en damme, grondwater (bv. boorgate), ys (gletsers en poolyskappe), waterdamp in die atmosfeer en selfs die water in lewende organismes.\n\n- Ongeveer **97,5 %** van alle water is **soutwater**, meestal in die oseane.\n- Net ongeveer **2,5 %** is **varswater**, en die meeste daarvan is gevries in ys of lê diep onder die grond.\n- **Minder as 1 %** van al die water op aarde is varswater wat ons maklik kan gebruik.\n\n### Hoekom is water so spesiaal?\n\n- Water is 'n **polêre** molekule en los baie stowwe op. Daarom is water in die natuur **nooit suiwer nie** – dit bevat altyd opgeloste ione en gasse.\n- Water het 'n hoë **spesifieke warmtekapasiteit**: die oseane warm stadig op en koel stadig af en reguleer so die aarde se klimaat.\n\n## Wisselwerking met ander globale sisteme\n\n| Sisteem | Wisselwerking met die hidrosfeer |\n|---|---|\n| Atmosfeer (lug) | verdamping en neerslag; O_{2} en CO_{2} los in water op; die beweging van water en energie dryf die weer |\n| Litosfeer (rotse en grond) | water verweer en erodeer rotse; dit los minerale (ione) uit rotse en grond op; grondwater word in rotse gestoor |\n| Biosfeer (lewende dinge) | plante neem water op vir fotosintese en gee waterdamp af (transpirasie); water is 'n habitat; alle selle bevat water |\n\n## Die waterkringloop\n\nDie **son** se energie dryf die kringloop; **swaartekrag** laat reën val en water afloop.\n\n1. **Verdamping:** water uit oseane, damme en riviere word waterdamp.\n2. **Transpirasie:** plante gee waterdamp deur hul blare af.\n3. **Kondensasie:** waterdamp styg, koel af en kondenseer tot druppeltjies wat wolke vorm.\n4. **Neerslag:** water val as reën, hael of sneeu.\n5. **Afloop en infiltrasie:** water vloei oor die oppervlak na riviere en damme, of sypel in die grond in en word **grondwater**.\n\n## Water as hulpbron in Suid-Afrika\n\nSuid-Afrika is 'n **waterskaars** land – een van die 30 droogste lande ter wêreld. Ons gemiddelde reënval is ongeveer 500 mm per jaar, teenoor 'n wêreldgemiddeld van ongeveer 860 mm. **Landbou** (besproeiing) gebruik die meeste water (ongeveer 60 %). Gauteng kry deel van sy water via die Lesotho-Hooglandwaterprojek en die Vaalrivier. Tydens beurtkrag staan pompe stil, wat tot wateronderbrekings lei.\n\n## Besoedeling\n\n| Besoedelstof | Bron | Gevolg |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rioolwater | swak bestuurde rioolwerke | bakterieë (bv. *E. coli*, cholera) → siektes |\n| Kunsmis (nitrate, fosfate) | plase, rioolwater | eutrofikasie |\n| Suur mynwater | ou goud- en steenkoolmyne | lae pH, swaar metale, sulfate |\n| Swaar metale (lood, kwik) | nywerhede | giftig; hoop in voedselkettings op |\n| Plastiek en rommel | mense | versmoor diere, verstop riviere |\n| Warm water (termiese besoedeling) | kragstasies, fabrieke | warm water hou minder suurstof op |\n\n**Eutrofikasie:** te veel voedingstowwe (nitrate en fosfate) → alge en waterplante (bv. waterhiasint) groei explosief → hulle blok sonlig, en wanneer hulle vrek, gebruik **bakterieë** wat die dooie materiaal afbreek die **opgeloste suurstof** op → visse vrek. Hartbeespoortdam is 'n bekende voorbeeld: afvalwater van rioolwerke stroomop in Gauteng bring baie fosfate in die dam.\n\n## Ione in water\n\nWater los ione uit rotse en grond op, bv. Na^{+}, Ca^{2+}, Mg^{2+}, Cl^{−}, SO_{4}^{2−}, HCO_{3}^{−} en NO_{3}^{−}. Klein hoeveelhede is onskadelik; hoë vlakke maak water onveilig.\n\n- **Harde water** bevat baie **Ca^{2+}- en Mg^{2+}-ione**. Dit vorm moeilik skuim met seep en laat **ketelsteen** in ketels en geisers.\n- **Sagte water** bevat min van hierdie ione.\n\n## Watergehalte toets\n\n- **pH:** pH < 7 is suur, pH = 7 is neutraal en pH > 7 is basies. Drinkwater is naby neutraal (ongeveer 6,5–8,5). Meet met universele indikator, pH-papier of 'n pH-meter. Suur mynwater het 'n baie lae pH.\n- **Elektriese geleidingsvermoë:** suiwer (gedistilleerde) water gelei elektrisiteit baie swak. Hoe meer **opgeloste ione**, hoe beter gelei die water. Hoë geleidingsvermoë = baie opgeloste soute (bv. seewater, suur mynwater).\n- **Opgeloste suurstof** (lae vlakke dui op besoedeling), **troebelheid** en **bakterieë** (*E. coli* dui op rioolbesoedeling).\n- **Ione:** silwernitraat gee 'n wit presipitaat met Cl^{−}; bariumchloried gee 'n wit presipitaat met SO_{4}^{2−}.\n\n## Watersuiwering\n\n'n Munisipale suiweringsaanleg suiwer water in stappe:\n\n1. **Siwwing:** groot voorwerpe (takke, plastiek) word uitgesif.\n2. **Koagulasie en flokkulasie:** aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) word bygevoeg sodat klein swewende deeltjies saamklont tot groter vlokke.\n3. **Sedimentasie (besinking):** die vlokke sak na die bodem.\n4. **Filtrasie:** water vloei deur sand- en gruisfilters.\n5. **Disinfeksie (chlorinering):** chloor maak bakterieë en ander mikroörganismes dood.\n\nDie pH word ook aangepas (bv. met kalk). Tuis kan jy water **kook** (minstens 1 minuut) of 'n paar druppels huishoudelike bleikmiddel byvoeg om kieme dood te maak – dit verwyder egter **nie** opgeloste soute of swaar metale nie.\n\n## Waterbewaring\n\n- Herstel lekkende krane en toilette; stort kort in plaas van bad.\n- Vang reënwater in tenks op en hergebruik gryswater in die tuin.\n- Plant inheemse, waterwyse plante en lei water in die koel deel van die dag nat.\n- Boere: drupbesproeiing in plaas van sprinkelbesproeiing.\n- Moenie olie, chemikalieë of medisyne in die drein gooi nie.\n\n> **Onthou!** \"Helder\" beteken nie \"veilig\" nie – bakterieë en opgeloste gifstowwe is onsigbaar.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Chloor verwyder nie vuilheid nie – dit **maak kieme dood**. Vaste deeltjies word deur flokkulasie, sedimentasie en filtrasie verwyder.","en":"## What is the hydrosphere?\n\nThe **hydrosphere** is all the water on, below and above the Earth's surface, in all three states: oceans and seas, rivers, lakes and dams, groundwater (e.g. boreholes), ice (glaciers and polar ice caps), water vapour in the atmosphere and even the water in living organisms.\n\n- About **97.5%** of all water is **salt water**, mostly in the oceans.\n- Only about **2.5%** is **fresh water**, and most of it is frozen as ice or lies deep underground.\n- **Less than 1%** of all the water on Earth is fresh water that we can use easily.\n\n### Why is water so special?\n\n- Water is a **polar** molecule and dissolves many substances. That is why water in nature is **never pure** – it always contains dissolved ions and gases.\n- Water has a high **specific heat capacity**: the oceans warm up and cool down slowly and so regulate the Earth's climate.\n\n## Interaction with other global systems\n\n| System | Interaction with the hydrosphere |\n|---|---|\n| Atmosphere (air) | evaporation and precipitation; O_{2} and CO_{2} dissolve in water; the movement of water and energy drives the weather |\n| Lithosphere (rocks and soil) | water weathers and erodes rocks; it dissolves minerals (ions) from rocks and soil; groundwater is stored in rocks |\n| Biosphere (living things) | plants take up water for photosynthesis and release water vapour (transpiration); water is a habitat; all cells contain water |\n\n## The water cycle\n\nThe **sun's** energy drives the cycle; **gravity** makes rain fall and water run off.\n\n1. **Evaporation:** water from oceans, dams and rivers becomes water vapour.\n2. **Transpiration:** plants release water vapour through their leaves.\n3. **Condensation:** water vapour rises, cools and condenses into droplets that form clouds.\n4. **Precipitation:** water falls as rain, hail or snow.\n5. **Run-off and infiltration:** water flows over the surface to rivers and dams, or seeps into the ground and becomes **groundwater**.\n\n## Water as a resource in South Africa\n\nSouth Africa is a **water-scarce** country – one of the 30 driest countries in the world. Our average rainfall is about 500 mm per year, compared to a world average of about 860 mm. **Agriculture** (irrigation) uses the most water (about 60%). Gauteng gets part of its water via the Lesotho Highlands Water Project and the Vaal River. During load-shedding pumps stop, which leads to water outages.\n\n## Pollution\n\n| Pollutant | Source | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sewage | poorly managed sewage works | bacteria (e.g. *E. coli*, cholera) → disease |\n| Fertiliser (nitrates, phosphates) | farms, sewage | eutrophication |\n| Acid mine drainage | old gold and coal mines | low pH, heavy metals, sulfates |\n| Heavy metals (lead, mercury) | industry | toxic; build up in food chains |\n| Plastic and litter | people | suffocates animals, blocks rivers |\n| Warm water (thermal pollution) | power stations, factories | warm water holds less oxygen |\n\n**Eutrophication:** too many nutrients (nitrates and phosphates) → algae and water plants (e.g. water hyacinth) grow explosively → they block sunlight, and when they die, **bacteria** that break down the dead material use up the **dissolved oxygen** → fish die. Hartbeespoort Dam is a well-known example: waste water from sewage works upstream in Gauteng brings large amounts of phosphates into the dam.\n\n## Ions in water\n\nWater dissolves ions from rocks and soil, e.g. Na^{+}, Ca^{2+}, Mg^{2+}, Cl^{−}, SO_{4}^{2−}, HCO_{3}^{−} and NO_{3}^{−}. Small amounts are harmless; high levels make water unsafe.\n\n- **Hard water** contains many **Ca^{2+} and Mg^{2+} ions**. It does not lather easily with soap and leaves **scale** in kettles and geysers.\n- **Soft water** contains few of these ions.\n\n## Testing water quality\n\n- **pH:** pH < 7 is acidic, pH = 7 is neutral and pH > 7 is basic. Drinking water is close to neutral (about 6.5–8.5). Measure with universal indicator, pH paper or a pH meter. Acid mine drainage has a very low pH.\n- **Electrical conductivity:** pure (distilled) water conducts electricity very poorly. The more **dissolved ions**, the better the water conducts. High conductivity = many dissolved salts (e.g. sea water, acid mine drainage).\n- **Dissolved oxygen** (low levels indicate pollution), **turbidity** and **bacteria** (*E. coli* indicates sewage pollution).\n- **Ions:** silver nitrate gives a white precipitate with Cl^{−}; barium chloride gives a white precipitate with SO_{4}^{2−}.\n\n## Water purification\n\nA municipal purification plant purifies water in steps:\n\n1. **Screening:** large objects (branches, plastic) are sieved out.\n2. **Coagulation and flocculation:** aluminium sulfate (alum) is added so that small suspended particles clump together into larger flocs.\n3. **Sedimentation (settling):** the flocs sink to the bottom.\n4. **Filtration:** water flows through sand and gravel filters.\n5. **Disinfection (chlorination):** chlorine kills bacteria and other micro-organisms.\n\nThe pH is also adjusted (e.g. with lime). At home you can **boil** water (at least 1 minute) or add a few drops of household bleach to kill germs – but this does **not** remove dissolved salts or heavy metals.\n\n## Water conservation\n\n- Fix leaking taps and toilets; take short showers instead of baths.\n- Collect rainwater in tanks and reuse grey water in the garden.\n- Plant indigenous, water-wise plants and water them in the cool part of the day.\n- Farmers: drip irrigation instead of sprinkler irrigation.\n- Do not pour oil, chemicals or medicine down the drain.\n\n> **Remember!** \"Clear\" does not mean \"safe\" – bacteria and dissolved toxins are invisible.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Chlorine does not remove dirt – it **kills germs**. Solid particles are removed by flocculation, sedimentation and filtration."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hidrosfeer","en":"Hydrosphere"},"def":{"af":"Al die water op, onder en bo die aarde se oppervlak in al drie toestande: oseane, riviere, damme, grondwater, ys, waterdamp en die water in organismes.","en":"All the water on, below and above the Earth's surface in all three states: oceans, rivers, dams, groundwater, ice, water vapour and the water in organisms."}},{"term":{"af":"Waterkringloop","en":"Water cycle"},"def":{"af":"Die deurlopende beweging van water tussen die hidrosfeer, atmosfeer, litosfeer en biosfeer deur verdamping, transpirasie, kondensasie, neerslag, afloop en infiltrasie; aangedryf deur die son se energie.","en":"The continuous movement of water between the hydrosphere, atmosphere, lithosphere and biosphere through evaporation, transpiration, condensation, precipitation, run-off and infiltration; driven by the sun's energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Transpirasie","en":"Transpiration"},"def":{"af":"Die verdamping van water uit die blare van plante na die atmosfeer.","en":"The evaporation of water from the leaves of plants into the atmosphere."}},{"term":{"af":"Grondwater","en":"Groundwater"},"def":{"af":"Water wat in die grond insypel en ondergronds in porieë en krake in rotse gestoor word; dit word deur boorgate onttrek.","en":"Water that seeps into the ground and is stored underground in pores and cracks in rocks; it is extracted through boreholes."}},{"term":{"af":"Eutrofikasie","en":"Eutrophication"},"def":{"af":"Die verryking van water met voedingstowwe (nitrate en fosfate) wat oormatige groei van alge en waterplante veroorsaak; wanneer dit afsterf, gebruik bakterieë die opgeloste suurstof op en visse vrek.","en":"The enrichment of water with nutrients (nitrates and phosphates) that causes excessive growth of algae and water plants; when these die, bacteria use up the dissolved oxygen and fish die."}},{"term":{"af":"Harde water","en":"Hard water"},"def":{"af":"Water met 'n hoë konsentrasie Ca²⁺- en Mg²⁺-ione; dit vorm moeilik skuim met seep en laat ketelsteen.","en":"Water with a high concentration of Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺ ions; it does not lather easily with soap and leaves scale."}},{"term":{"af":"Suur mynwater","en":"Acid mine drainage"},"def":{"af":"Suur water met 'n lae pH en baie opgeloste swaar metale en sulfate wat uit (ou) myne vloei en riviere besoedel.","en":"Acidic water with a low pH and many dissolved heavy metals and sulfates that flows out of (old) mines and pollutes rivers."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektriese geleidingsvermoë","en":"Electrical conductivity"},"def":{"af":"'n Maatstaf van hoe goed water elektrisiteit gelei; dit neem toe namate die hoeveelheid opgeloste ione toeneem.","en":"A measure of how well water conducts electricity; it increases as the amount of dissolved ions increases."}},{"term":{"af":"pH","en":"pH"},"def":{"af":"'n Skaal (0–14) wat aandui hoe suur of basies 'n oplossing is: onder 7 suur, 7 neutraal, bo 7 basies.","en":"A scale (0–14) that shows how acidic or basic a solution is: below 7 acidic, 7 neutral, above 7 basic."}},{"term":{"af":"Flokkulasie","en":"Flocculation"},"def":{"af":"Die stap in watersuiwering waar 'n chemikalie soos aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) bygevoeg word sodat klein swewende deeltjies saamklont tot vlokke wat kan besink.","en":"The step in water purification where a chemical such as aluminium sulfate (alum) is added so that small suspended particles clump together into flocs that can settle."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die waterkringloop","en":"The water cycle"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf hoe water wat uit Hartbeespoortdam verdamp, weer in die dam kan beland. Noem elke proses in die waterkringloop en die energiebron wat die kringloop dryf.","en":"Describe how water that evaporates from Hartbeespoort Dam can end up in the dam again. Name each process in the water cycle and the energy source that drives the cycle."},"steps":[{"af":"Verdamping: die son se energie verhit die damwater en water op die oppervlak word waterdamp in die atmosfeer. (Plante rondom die dam gee ook waterdamp af deur transpirasie.)","en":"Evaporation: the sun's energy heats the dam water and water at the surface becomes water vapour in the atmosphere. (Plants around the dam also release water vapour through transpiration.)"},{"af":"Kondensasie: die warm, klam lug styg en koel af, en die waterdamp kondenseer tot klein druppeltjies wat wolke vorm.","en":"Condensation: the warm, moist air rises and cools, and the water vapour condenses into tiny droplets that form clouds."},{"af":"Neerslag: die druppels groei, word te swaar en val as reën (of hael) oor die opvanggebied van die dam, bv. in Gauteng.","en":"Precipitation: the droplets grow, become too heavy and fall as rain (or hail) over the dam's catchment area, e.g. in Gauteng."},{"af":"Afloop en infiltrasie: 'n deel van die reënwater vloei oor die oppervlak na strome en die Krokodilrivier, wat in die dam invloei; 'n deel sypel in die grond in en word grondwater.","en":"Run-off and infiltration: part of the rainwater flows over the surface to streams and the Crocodile River, which flows into the dam; part seeps into the ground and becomes groundwater."},{"af":"Die son is die energiebron wat die kringloop dryf; swaartekrag laat die reën val en die water afvloei.","en":"The sun is the energy source that drives the cycle; gravity makes the rain fall and the water run off."}],"answer":{"af":"Verdamping (en transpirasie) → kondensasie → neerslag → afloop (en infiltrasie) terug na die dam; die son dryf die kringloop.","en":"Evaporation (and transpiration) → condensation → precipitation → run-off (and infiltration) back to the dam; the sun drives the cycle."}},{"title":{"af":"Eutrofikasie in Hartbeespoortdam","en":"Eutrophication in Hartbeespoort Dam"},"problem":{"af":"Hartbeespoortdam is dikwels met 'n groen laag alge en waterhiasint bedek, en soms vrek baie visse. Verduidelik stap vir stap hoe besoedeling dit veroorsaak en stel twee maatreëls voor om dit te verminder.","en":"Hartbeespoort Dam is often covered with a green layer of algae and water hyacinth, and sometimes many fish die. Explain step by step how pollution causes this and suggest two measures to reduce it."},"steps":[{"af":"Bron: afvalwater van rioolwerke en kunsmis wat van plase afspoel, bevat baie nitrate en fosfate – voedingstowwe vir plante.","en":"Source: waste water from sewage works and fertiliser washed off farms contain lots of nitrates and phosphates – nutrients for plants."},{"af":"Die oormaat voedingstowwe laat alge en waterplante soos waterhiasint baie vinnig groei. Dit word eutrofikasie genoem.","en":"The excess nutrients make algae and water plants such as water hyacinth grow very fast. This is called eutrophication."},{"af":"Die digte laag blok sonlig, sodat plante onder die oppervlak nie kan fotosintetiseer nie en vrek; later vrek die alge self ook.","en":"The dense layer blocks sunlight, so plants below the surface cannot photosynthesise and die; later the algae themselves die too."},{"af":"Bakterieë breek die dooie plantmateriaal af en gebruik daarvoor die opgeloste suurstof in die water. Die suurstofvlak daal so laag dat visse versmoor en vrek.","en":"Bacteria break down the dead plant material and use the dissolved oxygen in the water to do so. The oxygen level drops so low that fish suffocate and die."},{"af":"Maatreëls: (1) rioolwerke stroomop opgradeer sodat minder fosfate in die riviere beland; (2) kunsmis spaarsamer gebruik en nie naby riviere nie. (Om die waterhiasint uit te haal, help net tydelik – dit behandel die simptoom, nie die oorsaak nie.)","en":"Measures: (1) upgrade sewage works upstream so that fewer phosphates end up in the rivers; (2) use fertiliser sparingly and not close to rivers. (Removing the water hyacinth only helps temporarily – it treats the symptom, not the cause.)"}],"answer":{"af":"Oormaat nitrate en fosfate → eutrofikasie → plante vrek → bakterieë gebruik die suurstof op → visse vrek. Maatreëls: beter rioolsuiwering en minder kunsmisafloop.","en":"Excess nitrates and phosphates → eutrophication → plants die → bacteria use up the oxygen → fish die. Measures: better sewage treatment and less fertiliser run-off."}},{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer watertoetse","en":"Interpret water tests"},"problem":{"af":"Leerders toets drie watermonsters. Monster A (kraanwater): pH 7,4; lae geleidingsvermoë; helder. Monster B (stroompie langs 'n ou goudmyn): pH 3,2; baie hoë geleidingsvermoë; oranjebruin. Monster C (boorgatwater): pH 7,9; hoë geleidingsvermoë; laat ketelsteen in die ketel. (a) Watter monster is waarskynlik deur suur mynwater besoedel? Gee twee redes. (b) Waarom laat monster C ketelsteen? (c) Silwernitraatoplossing word by A gevoeg: 'n wit presipitaat vorm wat nie oplos wanneer verdunde salpetersuur bygevoeg word nie. Wat bewys dit?","en":"Learners test three water samples. Sample A (tap water): pH 7.4; low conductivity; clear. Sample B (stream next to an old gold mine): pH 3.2; very high conductivity; orange-brown. Sample C (borehole water): pH 7.9; high conductivity; leaves scale in the kettle. (a) Which sample is probably polluted by acid mine drainage? Give two reasons. (b) Why does sample C leave scale? (c) Silver nitrate solution is added to A: a white precipitate forms that does not dissolve when dilute nitric acid is added. What does this prove?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Monster B. Rede 1: die pH van 3,2 is baie laag – die water is suur, soos suur mynwater. Rede 2: die baie hoë geleidingsvermoë wys daar is baie opgeloste ione (bv. sulfaat- en metaalione).","en":"(a) Sample B. Reason 1: the pH of 3.2 is very low – the water is acidic, like acid mine drainage. Reason 2: the very high conductivity shows there are many dissolved ions (e.g. sulfate and metal ions)."},{"af":"Die oranjebruin kleur kom van opgeloste ysterverbindings – nog 'n teken van suur mynwater.","en":"The orange-brown colour comes from dissolved iron compounds – another sign of acid mine drainage."},{"af":"(b) Monster C is harde water: dit bevat baie Ca^{2+}- en Mg^{2+}-ione (wat ook die hoë geleidingsvermoë verklaar). Wanneer die water verhit word, slaan kalsium- en magnesiumverbindings as ketelsteen neer.","en":"(b) Sample C is hard water: it contains many Ca^{2+} and Mg^{2+} ions (which also explains the high conductivity). When the water is heated, calcium and magnesium compounds precipitate as scale."},{"af":"(c) 'n Wit presipitaat met silwernitraat wat nie in verdunde salpetersuur oplos nie, is silwerchloried (AgCl). Die kraanwater bevat dus chloriedione (Cl^{−}) – water is nooit suiwer nie.","en":"(c) A white precipitate with silver nitrate that does not dissolve in dilute nitric acid is silver chloride (AgCl). The tap water therefore contains chloride ions (Cl^{−}) – water is never pure."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) B – lae pH en baie hoë geleidingsvermoë (b) harde water met baie Ca²⁺- en Mg²⁺-ione (c) chloriedione (Cl⁻) is teenwoordig.","en":"(a) B – low pH and very high conductivity (b) hard water with many Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺ ions (c) chloride ions (Cl⁻) are present."}},{"title":{"af":"Watersuiwering","en":"Water purification"},"problem":{"af":"Rou water uit 'n rivier word by 'n munisipale aanleg gesuiwer. (a) Rangskik die stappe filtrasie, chlorinering, siwwing, sedimentasie en flokkulasie in die regte volgorde en gee die doel van elk. (b) Tydens 'n wateronderbreking het 'n gesin net onbehandelde rivierwater. Hoe kan hulle dit veiliger maak om te drink, en wat sal hul metode nie verwyder nie?","en":"Raw river water is purified at a municipal plant. (a) Arrange the steps filtration, chlorination, screening, sedimentation and flocculation in the correct order and give the purpose of each. (b) During a water outage a family only has untreated river water. How can they make it safer to drink, and what will their method not remove?"},"steps":[{"af":"1. Siwwing: groot voorwerpe soos takke, blare en plastiek word met skerms uitgesif.","en":"1. Screening: large objects such as branches, leaves and plastic are sieved out with screens."},{"af":"2. Flokkulasie (en koagulasie): aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) word bygevoeg; klein swewende deeltjies klont saam tot groter vlokke. 3. Sedimentasie: die swaar vlokke sak in groot tenks na die bodem.","en":"2. Flocculation (and coagulation): aluminium sulfate (alum) is added; small suspended particles clump together into larger flocs. 3. Sedimentation: the heavy flocs sink to the bottom in large tanks."},{"af":"4. Filtrasie: die water vloei deur lae sand en gruis wat die oorblywende fyn deeltjies vasvang.","en":"4. Filtration: the water flows through layers of sand and gravel that trap the remaining fine particles."},{"af":"5. Chlorinering: chloor word laaste bygevoeg om bakterieë en ander mikroörganismes dood te maak; 'n bietjie bly in die water sodat dit in die pype veilig bly.","en":"5. Chlorination: chlorine is added last to kill bacteria and other micro-organisms; a little stays in the water so that it remains safe in the pipes."},{"af":"(b) Kook die water (minstens 1 minuut) of voeg 'n paar druppels huishoudelike bleikmiddel by om kieme dood te maak. Dit verwyder nie opgeloste soute, swaar metale of ander chemikalieë nie.","en":"(b) Boil the water (at least 1 minute) or add a few drops of household bleach to kill germs. This does not remove dissolved salts, heavy metals or other chemicals."}],"answer":{"af":"Siwwing → flokkulasie → sedimentasie → filtrasie → chlorinering; kook of bleikmiddel maak kieme dood, maar verwyder nie opgeloste stowwe nie.","en":"Screening → flocculation → sedimentation → filtration → chlorination; boiling or bleach kills germs but does not remove dissolved substances."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter beskrywing pas die beste by die hidrosfeer?","en":"Which description best fits the hydrosphere?"},"options":[{"af":"Net die water in die oseane en seë","en":"Only the water in the oceans and seas"},{"af":"Die laag gasse wat die aarde omring","en":"The layer of gases that surrounds the Earth"},{"af":"Net die varswater in riviere, mere en damme","en":"Only the fresh water in rivers, lakes and dams"},{"af":"Al die water op, onder en bo die aarde se oppervlak – vloeibaar, ys en waterdamp","en":"All the water on, below and above the Earth's surface – liquid, ice and water vapour"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die hidrosfeer sluit ALLE water in: oseane, varswater, grondwater, ys, waterdamp en water in organismes. Die laag gasse is die atmosfeer.","en":"The hydrosphere includes ALL water: oceans, fresh water, groundwater, ice, water vapour and water in organisms. The layer of gases is the atmosphere."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die proses waardeur plante waterdamp deur hul blare aan die atmosfeer afgee, word ___ genoem.","en":"The process by which plants release water vapour through their leaves into the atmosphere is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["transpirasie","transpiration"],"en":["transpiration","transpirasie"]},"explain":{"af":"Transpirasie is die verdamping van water uit plante se blare. Dit verbind die biosfeer met die atmosfeer.","en":"Transpiration is the evaporation of water from plants' leaves. It links the biosphere to the atmosphere."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke proses in die waterkringloop by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each process in the water cycle to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Verdamping","en":"Evaporation"},"r":{"af":"Vloeibare water word waterdamp deur die son se energie.","en":"Liquid water becomes water vapour due to the sun's energy."}},{"l":{"af":"Kondensasie","en":"Condensation"},"r":{"af":"Waterdamp koel af en vorm druppeltjies in wolke.","en":"Water vapour cools and forms droplets in clouds."}},{"l":{"af":"Neerslag","en":"Precipitation"},"r":{"af":"Water val as reën, hael of sneeu.","en":"Water falls as rain, hail or snow."}},{"l":{"af":"Infiltrasie","en":"Infiltration"},"r":{"af":"Water sypel in die grond in en word grondwater.","en":"Water seeps into the ground and becomes groundwater."}}],"explain":{"af":"Verdamping: vloeistof → gas; kondensasie: gas → vloeistof (wolke); neerslag: water val uit wolke; infiltrasie: water sypel in die grond in.","en":"Evaporation: liquid → gas; condensation: gas → liquid (clouds); precipitation: water falls from clouds; infiltration: water seeps into the ground."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Suiwer (gedistilleerde) water is 'n goeie geleier van elektrisiteit.","en":"Pure (distilled) water is a good conductor of electricity."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gedistilleerde water bevat byna geen ione nie en gelei baie swak. Kraan-, rivier- en seewater gelei omdat daar opgeloste ione in is.","en":"False. Distilled water contains almost no ions and conducts very poorly. Tap, river and sea water conduct because they contain dissolved ions."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Reënwater los minerale uit rotse op en dra die ione na 'n rivier. Dit is 'n voorbeeld van wisselwerking tussen die hidrosfeer en die …","en":"Rainwater dissolves minerals from rocks and carries the ions to a river. This is an example of interaction between the hydrosphere and the …"},"options":[{"af":"atmosfeer","en":"atmosphere"},{"af":"litosfeer","en":"lithosphere"},{"af":"biosfeer","en":"biosphere"},{"af":"magnetosfeer","en":"magnetosphere"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rotse en grond vorm die litosfeer. Water verweer rotse en los minerale (ione) daaruit op – daarom bevat natuurlike water altyd ione.","en":"Rocks and soil make up the lithosphere. Water weathers rocks and dissolves minerals (ions) from them – that is why natural water always contains ions."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Harde water bevat 'n hoë konsentrasie magnesiumione en ___-ione.","en":"Hard water contains a high concentration of magnesium ions and ___ ions."},"answers":{"af":["kalsium","Ca²⁺","Ca2+","Ca","kalsiumione","calcium"],"en":["calcium","Ca²⁺","Ca2+","Ca","calcium ions","kalsium"]},"explain":{"af":"Harde water bevat baie Ca²⁺- en Mg²⁺-ione. Dit vorm moeilik skuim met seep en laat ketelsteen in ketels.","en":"Hard water contains many Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺ ions. It does not lather easily with soap and leaves scale in kettles."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die doel daarvan om aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) by 'n watersuiweringsaanleg by te voeg?","en":"What is the purpose of adding aluminium sulfate (alum) at a water purification plant?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit maak bakterieë dood.","en":"It kills bacteria."},{"af":"Dit verwyder opgeloste soute soos NaCl.","en":"It removes dissolved salts such as NaCl."},{"af":"Dit laat klein swewende deeltjies saamklont sodat hulle kan besink.","en":"It makes small suspended particles clump together so that they can settle."},{"af":"Dit maak die water sag deur Ca²⁺-ione te verwyder.","en":"It softens the water by removing Ca²⁺ ions."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Aluin veroorsaak flokkulasie: klein deeltjies klont saam tot vlokke wat in die sedimentasietenks besink. Bakterieë word deur chloor doodgemaak, nie deur aluin nie.","en":"Alum causes flocculation: small particles clump together into flocs that settle in the sedimentation tanks. Bacteria are killed by chlorine, not by alum."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Water wat helder lyk, is altyd veilig om te drink.","en":"Water that looks clear is always safe to drink."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Bakterieë (bv. E. coli), virusse en opgeloste gifstowwe soos swaar metale is onsigbaar. Helder water kan steeds besoedel wees.","en":"False. Bacteria (e.g. E. coli), viruses and dissolved toxins such as heavy metals are invisible. Clear water can still be polluted."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter volgorde word rou water in 'n munisipale aanleg gesuiwer?","en":"In which order is raw water purified at a municipal plant?"},"options":[{"af":"siwwing → flokkulasie → sedimentasie → filtrasie → chlorinering","en":"screening → flocculation → sedimentation → filtration → chlorination"},{"af":"chlorinering → siwwing → filtrasie → flokkulasie → sedimentasie","en":"chlorination → screening → filtration → flocculation → sedimentation"},{"af":"siwwing → filtrasie → flokkulasie → chlorinering → sedimentasie","en":"screening → filtration → flocculation → chlorination → sedimentation"},{"af":"siwwing → sedimentasie → flokkulasie → filtrasie → chlorinering","en":"screening → sedimentation → flocculation → filtration → chlorination"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Eers word groot voorwerpe uitgesif, dan laat aluin deeltjies saamklont (flokkulasie) sodat hulle kan besink (sedimentasie). Filtrasie vang die fyn deeltjies vas, en chloor word laaste bygevoeg om kieme dood te maak. Flokkulasie moet vóór sedimentasie kom.","en":"First large objects are screened out, then alum makes particles clump together (flocculation) so that they can settle (sedimentation). Filtration traps the fine particles, and chlorine is added last to kill germs. Flocculation must come before sedimentation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Watermonster uit 'n stroom by 'n ou myn het 'n pH van 3,5. Die water is ___ (suur, neutraal of basies).","en":"A water sample from a stream near an old mine has a pH of 3.5. The water is ___ (acidic, neutral or basic)."},"answers":{"af":["suur","acidic","suur water"],"en":["acidic","suur","acid"]},"explain":{"af":"pH < 7 is suur. 'n pH van 3,5 is baie suur – tipies van suur mynwater.","en":"pH < 7 is acidic. A pH of 3.5 is very acidic – typical of acid mine drainage."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Stort gebruik 10 L water per minuut. Elkeen in 'n gesin van 4 verkort sy daaglikse stort van 10 minute na 4 minute. Hoeveel water spaar die gesin per dag? ___ L","en":"A shower uses 10 L of water per minute. Each person in a family of 4 shortens their daily shower from 10 minutes to 4 minutes. How much water does the family save per day? ___ L"},"answers":{"af":["240","240 L","240 ℓ","240 liter","240 dm³","240 dm3"],"en":["240","240 L","240 ℓ","240 litres","240 liters","240 dm³","240 dm3"]},"explain":{"af":"Elke persoon spaar 10 − 4 = 6 minute × 10 L per minuut = 60 L. Vir 4 mense: 4 × 60 = 240 L per dag (meer as 87 000 L per jaar!).","en":"Each person saves 10 − 4 = 6 minutes × 10 L per minute = 60 L. For 4 people: 4 × 60 = 240 L per day (more than 87 000 L per year!)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Leerders toets vier watermonsters. Watter monster kom waarskynlik uit 'n stroom wat deur suur mynwater besoedel is?","en":"Learners test four water samples. Which sample most likely comes from a stream polluted by acid mine drainage?"},"options":[{"af":"Monster P: pH 7,2; lae geleidingsvermoë","en":"Sample P: pH 7.2; low conductivity"},{"af":"Monster Q: pH 3,1; baie hoë geleidingsvermoë","en":"Sample Q: pH 3.1; very high conductivity"},{"af":"Monster R: pH 8,9; matige geleidingsvermoë","en":"Sample R: pH 8.9; moderate conductivity"},{"af":"Monster S: pH 7,0; byna geen geleidingsvermoë nie","en":"Sample S: pH 7.0; almost no conductivity"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Suur mynwater is suur (lae pH) en bevat baie opgeloste ione (sulfate en metaalione), dus het dit 'n hoë geleidingsvermoë. S lyk soos gedistilleerde water; R is basies.","en":"Acid mine drainage is acidic (low pH) and contains many dissolved ions (sulfates and metal ions), so it has a high conductivity. S looks like distilled water; R is basic."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Na 'n algeblom in Hartbeespoortdam vrek baie visse. Wat is die hoofrede?","en":"After an algal bloom in Hartbeespoort Dam many fish die. What is the main reason?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kunsmis in die water is direk giftig vir die visse.","en":"The fertiliser in the water is directly poisonous to the fish."},{"af":"Die alge gebruik al die koolstofdioksied in die water op.","en":"The algae use up all the carbon dioxide in the water."},{"af":"Die alge maak die water te koud omdat hulle die son blok.","en":"The algae make the water too cold because they block the sun."},{"af":"Bakterieë wat die dooie alge en plante afbreek, gebruik die opgeloste suurstof op.","en":"Bacteria that break down the dead algae and plants use up the dissolved oxygen."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By eutrofikasie vrek die alge en plante later. Bakterieë breek die dooie materiaal af en gebruik daarvoor die opgeloste suurstof, sodat die visse versmoor.","en":"In eutrophication the algae and plants die later. Bacteria break down the dead material and use up the dissolved oxygen to do so, so the fish suffocate."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die munisipaliteit wil die eutrofikasie in Hartbeespoortdam op die lang termyn verminder. Watter maatreël sal die doeltreffendste wees?","en":"The municipality wants to reduce the eutrophication in Hartbeespoort Dam in the long term. Which measure will be the most effective?"},"options":[{"af":"Gooi meer chloor in die dam om die alge dood te maak.","en":"Add more chlorine to the dam to kill the algae."},{"af":"Haal die waterhiasint een keer per jaar uit.","en":"Remove the water hyacinth once a year."},{"af":"Gradeer rioolwerke stroomop op en beperk kunsmisafloop sodat minder fosfate en nitrate die dam bereik.","en":"Upgrade sewage works upstream and limit fertiliser run-off so that fewer phosphates and nitrates reach the dam."},{"af":"Bou nog 'n dam stroomaf om die water op te vang.","en":"Build another dam downstream to catch the water."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die oorsaak is te veel voedingstowwe (fosfate en nitrate). Net om die bron aan te pak, los die probleem op die lang termyn op. Chloor sou alle waterlewe skade aandoen, die hiasint uithaal behandel net die simptoom, en 'n dam stroomaf help nie die dam stroomop nie.","en":"The cause is too many nutrients (phosphates and nitrates). Only tackling the source solves the problem in the long term. Chlorine would harm all aquatic life, removing the hyacinth only treats the symptom, and a dam downstream does not help the dam upstream."}}]}]}]}}};